** {{desc|hy|հապալաս|lbor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ar|🂡}}
Ultimately from {{der|ar|la|as}}, likely through {{bor|ar|fr|as}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|آس|m|pl=آسَات}}

# {{senseid|ar|ace}} [[ace]] {{lb|ar|card games|dice|etc.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|آس|pl=sfp}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|ar|👨‍⚕️}}
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|אָסְיָא}} / {{m|syc|ܐܵܣܝܵܐ|t=physician, healer|tr=ʾāsyā}}, from {{der|ar|akk|asûm|𒀀𒍪|ts=asû|tr=A.ZU|t=physician, healer}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒀀𒍪|ts=azu|tr=A.ZU|t=physician, healer}}. This term has merged with the native root {{ar-root|ء س و}} having originally the meanings “to grieve”, “to hurt”, and developed additional forms, this noun being reinterpreted as an active participle of the {{ar-form|I|nocap=1}} verb, the same happening in {{cog|arc|-}}. It has also engendered additional forms in {{cog|arc|-}}, {{cog|he|-}}, {{cog|sem-eth|-}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|آسٍ|cons=آسِي|m|pl=آسُونَ|pl2=أُسَاة|pl3=إِسَاء|f=آسِيَة}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{senseid|ar|healer}} [[physician]], [[healer]], one who knows [[medicine]]
#: {{synonyms|ar|طَبِيب}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 965|author=w:Al-Mutanabbi|title={{l|ar||فِي الْخَدِّ أَنْ عَزَمَ الْخَلِيطُ رَحِيلًا}}|passage=يَطَأُ الثَّرَى مُتَرَفِّقًا مِنْ تَيْهِهِ // فَكَأَنَّهُ '''آسٍ''' يَجُسُّ عَلِيلَا}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|آسٍ|f=آسِيَة|pl=آسُونَ|pl2=أُسَاة|pl3=إِسَاء|fpl=sfp|fpl2=أَوَاسٍ:diin}}

