Page 128 أ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أ}}
'''Combined with [[fatha]]:'''
{{lang|ar|أَ}} :
* {{ar-IPA|أَ}}
'''Combined with [[damma]]:'''
{{lang|ar|أُ}} :
* {{ar-IPA|أُ}}

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|head=أ / ‍أ|tr=ʔ}}

# The first letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet is the small [[hamza]] ({{l|ar|ء|tr=-}}) that sits on top of {{l|ar|أ|tr=-}}, and the tall column is its bearer. The composite letter is called {{l|ar|أَلِف}} and the hamza represents a [[glottal stop]] ({{IPAchar|/ʔ/}}). (See also {{l|ar|ا}}.) It is followed by {{l|ar|ب}}.

====See also====
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* {{l|ar|ا}}, {{l|ar|إ}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/أ|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|أ}}]]

===Etymology 2===
From former {{m|ar|هَـ}}, from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ha}}. Cognate to {{cog|he|הֲ־|tr=hă-}}.

====Particle====
{{ar-particle|أَ|tr=ʔa-}}

# {{non-gloss definition|introduces a positive yes-no question}}
#: {{syn|ar|هَل}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|96|9-12|passage='''أَ'''رَأَيْتَ الَّذِي يَنْهَىٰ (9) عَبْدًا إِذَا صَلَّىٰ (10) '''أَ'''رَأَيْتَ إِن كَانَ عَلَى الْهُدَىٰ (11) أَوْ أَمَرَ بِالتَّقْوَىٰ (12)|t=9 Hast thou seen the one who scoldeth 10 this worshipper when he prayeth? 11 Hast thou looked at whether he is rightly guided, 12 or whether he preacheth righteousness?}}
# {{non-gloss definition|introduces a negative yes-no question}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|89|6-8|passage='''أَ'''لَمْ تَرَ كَيْفَ فَعَلَ رَبُّكَ بِعَادٍ (6) إِرَمَ ذَاتِ الْعِمَادِ (7) الَّتِي لَمْ يُخْلَقْ مِثْلُهَا فِي الْبِلَادِ (8)|t=6 Hast thou not seen what thy Lord did to ʿĀd? 7 ʾIram, with its pillars, 8 the like of which had never been created before!}}
# {{non-gloss definition|indicates an '''exclusive''' disjunction with {{m|ar|أَمْ|t=or}}, as in alternative questions}}
#: {{syn|ar|هَل|q1=sometimes proscribed}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|21|109|passage=وَإِنْ أَدْرِي '''أَ'''قَرِيبٌ أَم بَعِيدٌ مَّا تُوعَدُونَ|subst=وَإِنْ/وَ-إِنْ,'''أَ'''قَرِيبٌ/'''أَ'''-قَرِيبٌ|t=I know not '''whether''' nigh or far is that which ye are promised.}}
# {{non-gloss definition|indicates an '''inclusive''' disjunction with {{m|ar|أَمْ|t=or}} that denotes sameness, indistinguishability, unimportance, insignificance, or indifference}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|63|6|passage=سَوَاءٌ عَلَيْهِمْ '''أَ'''سْتَغْفَرْتَ لَهُمْ أَمْ لَمْ تَسْتَغْفِرْ لَهُمْ لَن يَغْفِرَ ٱللّٰهُ لَهُمْ|t=It is the same '''whether''' thou prayest for their forgiveness or not: Allah will not forgive them.|subst='''أَ'''/'''أَ-'''}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Unlike {{m|ar|هَلْ}}, {{m|ar|أَ}} precedes {{m|ar|وَ}}, {{m|ar|فَـ}}, and {{m|ar|ثُمَّ}}:
*: {{RQ:Qur'an|23|115|passage='''أَ'''فَحَسِبْتُمْ أَنَّمَا خَلَقْنَاكُمْ عَبَثًا وَأَنَّكُمْ إِلَيْنَا لَا تُرْجَعُونَ|subst='''أَ'''فَحَسِبْتُمْ/'''أَ'''-فَ-حَسِبْتُمْ,وَأَنَّكُمْ/وَ-أَنَّكُمْ|translation=Then '''did ye''' think that We created you uselessly and that to Us ye would not be returned?}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|آ||used before {{m|ar|اَلْ}}}}

====References====
* {{R:sem-pro:FS Militarev|page=200}}

