Page 211 أبى: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ء ب ي}}

===Etymology===
Supposedly from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔabay-}}; according to unifying theory, the meaning of wanting is the original, but came to be always used with negation, such that this is the bulk of attestation of {{cog|hbo|אָבָה|tr=ʔāḇā}}, and the dialects which standard Arabic has been based on have dropped the negating particle while other dialects continue the older situation. The alternative view assumes mutilated {{m|ar|بَغَى|t=to desire}}, well-known, behind the nonstandard meanings.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.pass.vn:إِبَاء,إِبَاءَة}}

# to [[reject]], to [[refuse]]
# to have an [[aversion]] for
# {{lb|ar|non-standard}} to [[will]], to [[desire]]
# {{lb|ar|non-standard}} to [[demand]], to [[ask for]]
# {{lb|ar|non-standard}} to be in [[lack]], to be [[necessary]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.pass.vn:إِبَاء,إِبَاءَة}}

