Page 245 أثل: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Starr-161213-0424-Tamarix aphylla-looking unhealthy-Uprange-Kahoolawe (32422919586).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|أَثْل}}]]
{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ء|ث|ل}} meaning to be strong rooted, well-founded, deeply and firmly connected, tied with many roots; cognates with {{cog|arc|אַתְלָא|}}, {{cog|xsa|𐩱𐩻𐩡|tr=ʾṯl}}, {{cog|he|אֵשֶׁל|}}. Theoretically from {{der|ar|afa-pro|*ʔčl|t=tamarisk, strong rooted tree}} with correspondence to {{cog|egy|jzr|t=tamarisk}}. Alternatively, if not rooted in a common ancestor, one may be a loan derived from the other.

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|collective}} {{ar-IPA|أَثْل}}
* {{q|singulative}} {{ar-IPA|أَثْلَة}}
* {{q|paucal}} {{ar-IPA|أَثَلَات}}
* {{q|plural}} {{ar-IPA|أُثُول}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|أَثْل|m|sing=أَثْلَة|pauc=أَثَلَات|pl=أُثُول}}

