Page 319 أحسن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
{{ar-rootbox|ح س ن}}
Causative to {{m|ar|حَسُنَ|t=to be right}}: to make something a good result.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَحْسَنَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|IV}}

# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to [[do]] or [[act]] [[well]], to do or act [[right]]; to do or act [[good]]
#: {{ant|ar|أَسَاءَ|t=to do wrong; to do evil, to offend}}
#: {{ux|ar|أَحْسَنَ إِلَيْكَ سَعْدٌ '''بَيْنَمَا''' أَنْتَ أَسَأْتَ إِلَيْهِ|t=Saad treated you well, whereas you treated him badly}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[do]] [[well]], to do [[right]]; to [[know]] ([[how]] to do {{non-gloss|or}} how to [[use]]), to [[be able]] to, to have [[command]] of, to [[master]], to be [[proficient]] in
#: {{syn|ar|أَجَادَ|t=to excel in}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''تُحْسِنُ''' هِيَ ٱللُّغَةَ ٱلْعَرَبِيَّةَ|She '''masters''' the Arabic language.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:{{w|lang=ar|وجدي الأهدل|وَجْدِيّ الْأَهْدَل}}|title=ar:أرض المؤامرات السعيدة|year=2018|isbn=978-614-469-069-7|publisher=Nawfal / Hachette Antoine|location=Bayrūt|page=156|passage=سألتني إن كنت '''أُحسن''' الطبخ، فقلت لها: «لو لم أكن صحافياً لكنت طبّاخاً».|t=She asked me whether I '''had proficiency''' in the art of cooking, and I said to her: “Were I not a journalist, I would be a cook!“}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|IV}}

===Etymology 1.2===
{{ar-rootbox|ح س ن}}
{{ar-elative}} of {{m|ar|حَسَن|t=good}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَحْسَن}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|أَحْسَن|f=حُسْنَى|pl=أَحْسَنُونَ|pl2=أَحَاسِن|fpl=حُسْنَيَات|fpl2=حُسَن}}

# {{gloss|{{infl of|ar|حَسَن||elad}}}} {{lb|ar|broadly}} [[better]], [[best]], [[nicer]], [[nicest]], more [[excellent]], most [[excellent]] (for example, more [[suitable]], most [[suitable]], more [[befit|befitting]], most [[befit|befitting]]; more [[beautiful]], most [[beautiful]], [[prettier]], [[prettiest]])
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|41|34|text=وَلَا تَسْتَوِي الْحَسَنَةُ وَلَا السَّيِّئَةُ ۚ ادْفَعْ بِالَّتِي هِيَ '''أَحْسَنُ''' فَإِذَا الَّذِي بَيْنَكَ وَبَيْنَهُ عَدَاوَةٌ كَأَنَّهُ وَلِيٌّ حَمِيمٌ|subst=السَّيِّئَةُ ۚ ادْفَعْ/السَّيِّئَةُ. اِدْفَعْ,وَلَا/وَ-لَا,فَإِذَا/فَ-إِذَا,وَبَيْنَهُ/وَ-بَيْنَهُ|t=And the good deed does not equal the bad: repel by that which is '''better''', whereupon he who is inimical to you will be as if he were a devoted friend.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|أَحْسَن|f=حُسْنَى|pl=أَحْسَنُونَ|pl2=أَحَاسِن|fpl=حُسْنَيَات|fpl2=حُسَن}}

