===Etymology===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʾaḫ-}}, from the root {{ar-root|ء|خ|و}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|אח|tr=akh}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَخ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-أخ.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أَخ|m|cons=أَخُو|d=أَخَوَان|pl=إِخْوَة|pl2=إِخْوَان|f=أُخْت}}

# [[brother]]

====Usage notes====
* {{lang|ar|أخ}} is used literally as well as figuratively. Moreover, {{lang|ar|أخ}} includes both full brothers and [[half brother]]s. The synonym {{m|ar|شَقِيق}} refers to full brothers exclusively.

