===Etymology 1.1===
{{ar-rootbox|ء خ ذ}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔaḫaḏ-}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|אָחַז|tr=aḥáz}}, {{cog|arc|ܐܚܕ|tr=ʾeḥaḏ}}, {{cog|xsa|𐩱𐩭𐩹|tr=ʾḵḏ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَخَذَ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-أخذ.ogg}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:أَخْذ,مَأْخَذ}}

# to [[take]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|154
|passage=وَلَمَّا سَكَتَ عَنْ مُوسَى الْغَضَبُ أَخَذَ الأَلْوَاحَ{{...}}
|translation=When Moses’ anger subsided, he took up the tablets...}}
# to [[take]] along
# to [[get]], to [[receive]], to [[obtain]]
# to [[seize]], to [[grab]], to [[take hold]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|150
|passage={{…}}وَأَخَذَ بِرَأْسِ أَخِيهِ يَجُرُّهُ إِلَيْهِ{{...}}
|translation=And he (Moses) threw down the Tablets and seized his brother (Aaron) by [the hair of] his head, pulling him toward him.}}
# to [[capture]], to [[seize]], to take [[captive]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|9|5
|passage=فَإِذَا ٱنْسَلَخَ الْأَشْهُرُ الْحُرُمُ فَاقْتُلُوا الْمُشْرِكِينَ حَيْثُ وَجَدتُّمُوهُمْ '''وَخُذُوهُمْ''' وَاحْصُرُوهُمْ وَاقْعُدُوا لَهُمْ كُلَّ مَرْصَدٍ{{…}}
|translation=But once the Sacred Months have passed, kill the polytheists ˹who violated their treaties and fought˺ wherever you find them, capture them, besiege them, and lie in wait for them on every way.}}
# to [[perceive]], to [[notice]]
# to [[gather]], to [[understand]], to [[infer]], to [[deduce]]
# to [[grip]], to [[captivate]], to [[spellbind]]
# to [[keep]], to [[observe]], to [[adopt]], to [[embrace]], to [[follow]]
#: {{usex|ar|أَخَذَ بِرَأْيِ صَدِيقِهِ|He took his friend's advice.}}
# to [[accept]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3|81
|passage={{…}}قَالَ أَأَقْرَرْتُمْ وَ'''أَخَذْتُمْ''' عَلَىٰ ذَٰلِكُمْ إِصْرِي قَالُوا أَقْرَرْنَا{{…}}
|translation=[God] said, “Do you affirm and accept upon that My Burden (i.e. Allah’s Covenant)?” They [the prophets] said, “We affirm.”}}
# to [[admonish]], to [[urge]], to [[drive]]
# to [[enjoin]], to [[impose]]
# to [[strip]], to [[deprive]], to [[cut off]], to [[bar]]
# to [[reproach]], to [[blame]], to [[criticize]]
#: {{usex|ar|أَخَذَ عَلَى الْمُؤَلِّفِ إِهْمَالَهُ المَصَادِرَ|The author was reproached for his neglect of the sources.}}
# to [[obligate]]
# to [[learn]], to [[study]]
# to [[begin]], to [[start]], to [[prepare]] to, to [[set out]] to, to be [[about to]], to [[get ready]] to {{qualifier|followed by a non-past verb}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''أَخَذْتُ''' أَبْكِي|t='''I began''' to cry|inline=t}}

