Page 399 أداف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Seemingly {{m|ar|أَضَافَ|t=to add; to admix}} borrowed into {{bor|ar|arc|-}} and then back with also the variants {{alter|ar|دَافَ|أَذَافَ}}, as there is even [[begadkefat]], and originally wine-drinking met Arabs as a practice of the more urban Aramaic culture, marking various loans in the vinicultural fields such as {{m|ar|نَاجُود|t=beaker}} and {{m|ar|تَاجِر|t=wine-merchant}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَدَافَ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|IV.II:و}} {{tlb|ar|archaic}}

# to [[mix]], to [[dilute]], to [[crush]]
#: {{syn|ar|شَجَّ|خَفَّفَ}}
#* {{R:ar:FAH|6II|page=336 Nr. 589|passage=وَيَقُولُونَ شَرَابٌ مُذَافٌ بِٱلذَّالِ ٱلْمُعْجَمَةِ. وَٱلصَّوَابُ مَدُوفٌ بِدَالٍ غَيْرَ مُعْجَمَةٍ. وَقَدْ دُفْتُ ٱلشَّيْءَ بِغَيْرِهِ أَدُوفُهُ دَوْفًا إِِذَا خَلَطْتَهُ.|t=They say ''muḏāf'' wine with the dotted ḏal but the correct is ''madūf'' with undotted dāl. I diluted the thing in the base stem, I dilute it into a dilution when you have mixed it well.}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1226|ar|author=ar:{{w|Muhammad bin Hasan al-Baghdadi|محمد بن الحسن بن محمد بن الكريم الكاتب البغدادي}}<t:Muḥammad bin al-Ḥasan bin Muḥammad bin al-Karīm al-Baḡdādīy>|title=كتاب الطبيخ ومعجم المآكل الدمشقية|chapter=ar:الباب التاسع في ذكر الحلاوات وأصنافها|chapterurl=https://www.hindawi.org/books/93091736/9/|page=75|year_published=2018|isbn=978-1-5273-1569-3|publisher=[[w:ar:مؤسسة هنداوي|Hindawi Foundation]]|passage=مُكَفَّن<br/>يُؤْخَذُ رَطْلُ سُكَّرٍ وَثُلُثُ رَطْلِ لَوْزٍ أَوْ فُسْتُقٍ، فَيُدَقُّ ٱلْجَمِيعُ نَاعِمًا، وَيُعْجَنُ بِمَاءِ ٱلْوَرْدِ عَجْنًا قَوِيًّا، ثُمَّ يُطْرَحُ فِي ٱلدَّسْتِ أُوقِيَّةَ شَيْرَجٍ، وَيُحَلُّ نِصْفُ رَطْلِ سُكَّرٍ فَيُعْمَلُ جُلَّابًا، فَإِذَا غَلَى ٱلشَّيْرَجُ طُرِحَ عَلَيْهِ ثُلُثَ ٱلْجُلَّابِ، وَيُوَاصَلُ تَحْرِيكُهُ، ثُمَّ يُطْرَحُ عَلَيْهِ أُوقِيَّةَ نَشًا '''مُدَافًا''' بِمَاءٍ، وَلَا يَزَالُ يُحَرَّكُ حَتَّى يَنْعَقِدَ، ثُمَّ يُطْرَحُ عَلَى بَلَاطَةٍ نَاعِمَةٍ حَتَّى يُبَرَّدُ، وَيُبْسَطُ قِطَعًا صِغَارًا مُرَبَّعَةً قَدْرَ ٱلْكَفِّ، ثُمَّ يُجْعَلُ عَلَيْهِ شَيْءٌ مِنْ ذَٰلِكَ ٱلسُّكَّرِ وَٱللَّوْزِ وَٱلْمَعْجُونِ، وَيُلَفُّ عَلَى هَيْئَةِ ٱلْأَوْسَاطِ، ثُمَّ يُذَرُّ عَلَيْهِ ٱلسُّكَّرُ ٱلْمُطَيَّبُ وَيُرْفَعُ.|t=Mukaffan<br/>One takes a rottol of sugar and a third of a rottol of almond and pistachio, then pounds all fine, and kneads with rosewater heartily, then throws an ounce of sesame oil in a kettle, and dissolves half a rottol of sugar, and produces rosewater syrup, and when the sesame oil boils a third of the rosewater syrup is thrown upon it, connected by working it in a bit, then one throws upon it an ounce of starch '''diluted''' with water, then one continues to work it in until it becomes a slop, then on casts it upon a thin slate until it cools off, then it is spread into small strands quadrupled after the size of the handpalm, then one applies upon it some of that sugar and the almond and the dough and rolls in around the centres, then one scatters upon it the seasoned sugar and finishes.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 1333|author={{w|Al-Nuwayri|an-Nuwayrīy}}|title=ar:نِهَايَةُ ٱلْأَرَبِ فِي فُنُونِ ٱلْأَدَبِ|url=http://www.alwaraq.net/Core/SearchServlet/searchone?docid=101&searchtext=2KfZhNi32YbYrNmK2LE=&option=1&offset=6&WordForm=1&exactpage=1274&totalpages=7&AllOffset=1|passage=(…) فَٱسْحَقْ لَهُ لِكُلِّ رَطْلٍ مِنَ ٱلْمَاءِ مِثْقَالًا مِنْ مِسْكٍ، وَمِثْقَالًا مِنْ عَنْبَرٍ شِحْرِيٍّ '''مُدَافٍ''' (…)|t=(…) And crush there for every rottol of water a miṯqāl of musk, and a miṯqāl of '''diluted''' {{w|Al-Shihr|šiḥrī}} ambergris (…)}}

