Page 498 أردماني: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-etym-nisba|أُرْدَمَان}}, from {{bor|ar|la|Lordmanni}} (by way of {{w|re-bracketing}} the [[lateral]] as the definite article ''al-''), variant of {{m|la|Nordmanni}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|non|norðmaðr}}.

===Adjective===
{{ar-nisba|أُرْدَمَانِيّ}}

# {{lb|ar|rare|historical|_|or|_|obsolete}} [[Norse]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|أُرْدَمَانِيّ|pl=sp}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun-nisba|أُرْدَمَانِيّ}}

# {{lb|ar|rare|historical|_|or|_|obsolete}} a [[Northman]]; a [[Norseman]]
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:المُقْتَبَس<t:The Excerpts>
|author=ar:ابْن حَيَّان الْقُرْطُبِيّ<t:ʾIbn Ḥayyān al-Qurṭubī>
|text=
وَٱحْتَلَّ بِسَاحِلٍ مِنْ سَوَاحِلِ ثُغُورِنَا مَرَاكِبُ لِقَوْمٍ مِنَ ٱلْمَجُوسِ، يُقَالُ لَهُمُ '''الْأُرْدَمَانِيُّونَ'''. أَقْبَلُوا مِنْ بَلَدِهِمْ فِي ٱلْبَحْرِ إِلَى أَرْضِ إِفْرَنْجَةٍ، وَخَرَجُوا عَلَى سَاحِلِهِمْ، فَقَتَلُوا رِجَالَهُمْ، وَأَصَابُوا ذَرَارِيهِمْ، وَغَنَمُوا أَمْوَالَهُمْ، وَأَقَامُوا بِبَلَدِهِمْ يَعِيثُونَ فِيهِمْ، وَيَقْتُلُونَ مَنْ ظَفَرُوا بِهِ مِنْهُمْ.
|t=And then, somewhere along our shores, the longships of a nation of Mazdeans came in, who are called the '''''ʾUrdamāniyyūn'''''. They had journeyed forth from their homeland by sea to the land of the Franks, and then they filed out on their shoreline, slew their men, seized their children, and looted their wealth, and thereafter they lingered around in their country marauding in it and slaying whomever they could catch from among them.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:المُقْتَبَس<t:The Excerpts>
|author=ar:ابْن حَيَّان الْقُرْطُبِيّ<t:ʾIbn Ḥayyān al-Qurṭubī>
|text=
يقولون إنَّ '''الأُرْدَمَانِينَ''' أقبَلُوا / فقلتُ إذا شاؤُوا رضِيتُ لهم نصرَا<br>لقد أيقنَ الإسلامُ أنَّ سيوفَه / ستحمي حماهُ بل ستصطلمُ الكفَرَا
|t=“The '''Northmen''' have arrived!” they shout and cry!<br>“Ah, well,” said I, “So let them taste a victory,<br>Islam just knows his strongholds are secure,<br>His swords, to faithless men, excisory.”}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أُرْدَمَانِيّ|pl=sp}}
-------- end text --------
Page 499 أردمون: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|grc|ἀρτέμων}}. Also found as {{cog|syc|ܐܰܪܛܶܡܘܿܢܳܐ|tr=arṭemōnā}} and {{cog|la|artemōn}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَرْدَمُون}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أَرْدَمُون|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[foresail]] at the [[mizzenmast]]
#* {{ante|608}}, [https://www.aldiwan.net/poem25036.html by] [[w:Zuhayr bin Abi Sulma|{{l|ar||زُهَيْرُ بْنُ أَبِي سُلْمَى}}]]
#*: {{quote|ar|إِذَا تَرَامَت بِهَا الدَيْمُومَةُ الْجَدَدُ / عَوْمَ الْقَوَادِسِ قَفَّى الْأَرْدَمُونَ بِهَا / إِذَا تَرَامَى بِهَا الْمُغْلَوْلِبُ الزَبِدُ / بِفِتْيَةٍ كَسُيُوفِ الْهِنْدِ يَبْعَثُهُم|subst=بِهَا/بِ-هَا,يَبْعَثُهُم/يَبْعَثُ-هُم,بِفِتْيَةٍ/بِ-فِتْيَةٍ,كَسُيُوفِ/كَ-سُيُوفِ|When the wasteland of the hard soil was reached / by floating in the barges, they put up behind them the foresail / And when the luxuriance of foam / hit the young men, it sent them forth like Indian swords.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَرْدَمُون}}

===References===
