Page 504 أرز: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Réserve des cèdres de Tannourine au Liban-Nord S73F2380.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|أَرْز}} – {{taxlink|Cedrus libani subsp. libani|subspecies}}|upright=1.15]]
{{swp|lang=ar|أرز (شجرة)}}

===Etymology 1===
The tree is native to the region north of [[Israel]] and [[Judea]]. Borrowed into Arabic and {{cog|gez|አርዝ}} and before {{w|Segolate|the pertinent vowel change}} into {{cog|he|אֶרֶז|tr=ʾérez|t=cedar}} from {{bor|ar|arc|אַרְזָא}} / {{m|syc|ܐܪܙܐ|tr=ʾarzā|t=cedar}}, also found in {{cog|uga|𐎀𐎗𐎇|t=cedar}}, continuing {{der|ar|akk|𒂞|𒄑𒂞|ts=erēnu, erinnu|tr=<sup>GIŠ</sup>ERIN}} from {{der|ar|sux|𒂞|𒄑𒂞|ts=eren|tr=<sup>GIŠ</sup>ERIN}}, which also passed into {{cog|hit|𒂞|𒄑𒂞|tr=<sup>GIŠ</sup>ERIN|ts=herin(a)-|t=cedar}} and also {{cog|xhu|𒂊𒊑𒅎𒁉|𒄑𒂊𒊑𒅎𒁉|tr={{sup|GIŠ}}e-ri-im-bi|ts=erimbi}}, {{m|xhu|𒂊𒊑𒁉|𒄑𒂊𒊑𒁉|tr={{sup|GIŠ}}e-ri-bi|ts=eribi|t=cedar}} and thence back into a {{cog|hit|-}} alternative form. While Rabin argues for a {{der|ar|hit|-}} origin of the word, the form ''ʾarz'' recalls {{cog|ira-pro|*hampr̥sā|t=juniper}}, which is not remote in meaning – {{cog|grc|κέδρος}} also means both cedar and juniper.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَرْز}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|أَرْز|sing=أَرْزَة}}

# [[cedar]] ({{taxfmt|Cedrus|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#* {{RQ:Awwam|7|22|volume=1|page=287|passage=وأما غراسة '''الأرز''' وهو الذي يسمى السرول<br/>قال هو نوعان أحدهما يشبه الطرفاء والآخر يشبه العرعر|translation=About the planting of the '''cedar''' which is called cypress<br/>there are two kinds, one resembles the tamarisk and the other resembles the juniper.}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|34|6|volume=2|pages=721–722|passage=وقال غيره يتخذ لها الخلايا من خشب '''الأرز''' ومن طين طيب الريح وتطين الخلايا من خارجها برماد وأخثاء البقر مدقوق معجون بالماء ويتخذ لها بعض الناس الخلايا من قشور الشبر وتسميه العامة «جناحا»|translation=And another author said that for beehives '''cedar''' wood and clay of good smell is taken and the beehives are daubed from the outside with ash and cow dung powdered and kneaded with water, and some people take for beehives the barks of the cork oak, generally called “wings”.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|أَرْز|sing=أَرْزَة}}

