Page 528 أرضي شوكي: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}
[[File:Carciofo spinoso 1.JPG|thumb|180px|أرضي شوكي]]

===Etymology===
{{psm|ar|en|artichoke}}, based on the native words {{m|ar|أَرْضِيّ||earthly, terrestrial, of ground}} and {{m|ar|شَوْكِيّ||thorny, prickly}} (i.e. “growing in earth and thorny”), the [[nisba]] forms of {{m|ar|أَرْض||earth}} and {{m|ar|شَوْك||thorn}}, respectively.

English {{m|en|artichoke}} is in turn of {{der|ar|ar|-}} origin, ultimately from {{m|ar|خرشوف|الْخُرْشُوف|artichoke}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَرْضِيّ شَوْكِيّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|[[أَرْضِيّ]] [[شَوْكِيّ]]|m|head2=[[أَرْضِي]] [[شُوكِيّ]]|tr2=ʾarḍī šōkiyy}}

# {{lb|ar|Levantine|collective}} [[artichoke]]
#: {{syn|ar|خُرْشُوف}}

====Declension====
{{i|can also be indeclinable}}
