Page 532 أرطى: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|أرطاة|أَرْطَى|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|ar}}, associated as a natively coined term, developing into the roots {{ar-root|ر ط ي}} and {{ar-root|ء ر ط}}, dealing with topics of its color and ability to grow in the most inhospitable ground, providing shelter and edible fruit. Potential distant connections to {{cog|akk|𒌑𒌨𒂅𒌋|tr={{sup|U{{sub|2}}}}ur-ṭu-u|ts=urṭû|t=a plant like a tamarisk but red; a dye}}, also used as a dye for hides and compared to a tamarisk in Arabic culture.

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|أَرْطًى|head2=أَرْطَى|m|g2=f|cons=أَرْطَى|sing=أَرْطَاة|pl=أَرَاطٍ|plcons=أَرَاطِي}}

# {{taxlink|Calligonum|genus}} gen. et spp.
#: {{syn|ar|عَبَل|q1=in the southern half of the Arabian peninsula}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|أَرْطًى|head2=أَرْطَى|sing=أَرْطَاة|pl=أَرَاطٍ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=27}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=49}}
* {{R:ar:Mandaville|B}}

{{C|ar|Buckwheat family plants|Woods}}
