# {{tlb|ar|obsolete}} [[honey]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:إبراهيم بن قيس بن سليمان أبو إسحاق الهمداني الحضرمي|year=a. 1082|title=poetized|passage=وخذها كمثل الأري والأري مثلها … يتيه بها نشادها في المحافل|t=And her cheek is like honey and honey like her … her attending suitor will well be starkers}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَرْي}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|ar|stabl}}
Given the distinction between desert-dwellers and stationary animal husbandmen, and the original form claimed {{m|ar||*آرُويٌ}}, probably a borrowing from {{bor|ar|arc|-}} attested as {{m|arc|אוריא}} / {{m|syc|ܐܘܪܝܐ|tr=ʾoryā}}.{{dercat|ar|akk}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|إِْرْي|آرِيّ|أَرِيّة|آرِيَّة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|أَرِيّ|m|pl=أَوَارٍ|pl2=أَوَرِيّ}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# a place of [[confinement]] of a [[beast]], a [[manger]], [[trough]], or [[cot]], [[sty]], [[stable]], or the [[rope]] or [[post]], [[attachment]] by which it is tied

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَرِيّ|pl=أَوَارٍ|pl2=أَوَرِيّ:di}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|أَرَى|t=to place in the same stable}}
* {{l|ar|أَرَّى|t=to make a manger for; to make firm, to establish}}
* {{l|ar|آرَى|t=to tie in the same stable, to join at the manger}}
* {{l|ar|تَأَرَّى|t=to remain or stay confined}}
* {{l|ar|اِئْتَرَى|t=to stay at}}

===Etymology 4===
{{etymid|ar|foc}}
In view of the suspicious sound plural of {{m|ar|إِرَة|t=fire; place of fire; roast-meat}} {{m|ar|إِرُون}}, probably from that and it from {{bor|ar|arc|איאר}} / {{m|arc|איירא}} / {{m|arc|איירה}} / {{m|syc|ܐܝܪܐ|tr=ʾīrā|t=pot, cauldron}}, even though {{m|ar|أُوَار|t=blaze}} be considered unborrowed.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I.III:ي.nopass.vn:أَرْي,أَرِيّ}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete|rare}}

# to [[burnt]] or [[sooten]]ed at the bottom, to be [[inflame]]d {{lb|ar|also|figuratively}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I.III:ي.nopass.vn:أَرْي,أَرِيّ}}

