===Etymology===
{{unknown|ar}}, suggested as {{bor|ar|ira}}, comparing with {{cog|fa-cls|اورنگ|tr=awrang|t=throne}}, but this is difficult. A native origin would connect the Arabic only to {{m|ar|أَرَاك|t=[[toothbrush tree]]}}, or perhaps an obsolete {{m|ar|أَرَكَ|t=to persevere, to bide}}, because it is a place of abode, which however likely derives from the plant name, as these trees are inviting for camels, goats, and humans to eat.

