Page 597 أس: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إِسّ}}

===Etymology===
The Arabic root {{ar-root|ء س س}} is weakly developed; thus is concluded that all other words in it are denominal from this noun and this noun is, similarly to other architectural terms, borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|אוּשָּׁא|tr=ʾūšā|t=foundation}}, from {{der|ar|akk|uššu⁠m|𒀳|ts=uššu|t=foundation}}, whereas in reference to remains of ashes and hence campsite, or in bedouin rather than urban signification, it can be comprehended as inherited from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔiš-|t=fire}}, quod vide.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أُسّ|m|head2=أَسّ|pl=إِسَاس|pl2=آسَاس}}

# [[foundation]], [[groundwork]], [[basis]]
# {{lb|ar|mathematics}} [[power]], [[exponent]]
# {{lb|ar|classical}} [[remain]], [[relic]], [[trace]], [[vestige]], [[mark]] [[left]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أُسّ|head2=أَسّ|pl=إِسَاس|pl2=آسَاس}}

====Descendants====
