# {{infl of|ar|شَاقّ||elad}}; [[tough]]est, most [[wearisome]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|أَشَقّ:el}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|أَشَقّ|f=شَقَّاء|pl=شُقّ}}

# of [[inclinate]]d [[gait]] in such a manner that a [[gap]] is left between the legs, long-footed

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|أَشَقّ:cd}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|ar|pal||tr=wšʾk|ts=wašak|sc=Phlv}}, {{m|pal|tr=wšk|ts=wašak|sc=Phlv}}, attested at least thrice in {{w|Book Pahlavi}} and once in {{cog|syc|ܘܣܩܐ|tr=wasqā}}, once in {{cog|myz|ࡀࡅࡎࡒࡀ|tr=wasqā}},<ref name="Henning">{{cite-journal|last=Henning|first=Walter Bruno|journal=Bulletin of the School of Oriental and African Studies|volume=17|issue=3|title=The Middle-Persian Word for ‘Beer’|year=1955|pages=603–604|doi=10.1017/S0041977X00112480}}</ref> denoting in each case a kind of ceremonial drink employed by [[Zoroastrian]]s in place of wine, which matches gum ammoniac as this was employed in antiquity for its emollient, swelling-atoning and limb-pain-relieving effect,<ref>See for example {{cite-web|es|work=Dioscórides Interactivo|title=σίλφιον – ''Ferula tingitana''|url=http://dioscorides.usal.es/p2.php?numero=483|year={{#time:o}}}} which probably related to {{taxlink|Ferula tingitana|species}} however {{taxlink|Dorema ammoniacum|species}} was used the same by the Hellenes and the Arabic translators of Greek identified the former with the latter – so also {{R:Steiger-Voces|page=56}}.</ref> and apparently the drink was called after ammoniacum it was composed of,<ref name="Henning"/> as the later {{cog|fa-cls|وشه|tr=wuša}} and {{m|fa|اشه|tr=oša}} and the Arabic are known to mean gum ammoniac, and one finds a {{cog|gkm|οὐσάκ}} glossed as ammoniacum.<ref name="Löw">{{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=3|page=457}}</ref><br/>
The measure of the Arabic word is also <var>K</var>a<var>L</var>a<var>M</var>, not only <var>K</var>u<var>LL</var>a<var>M</var>.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|وُشَّق|أُشَّج|وُشَّج}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|أُشَّق|m}}

# {{taxlink|Ferula marmarica|species}} (in Africa)
# {{taxlink|Ferula ammoniacum|species}} syn. {{taxlink|Dorema ammoniacum|species}} (in Eastern Iran, Afghanistan, Turkistan)
# {{taxlink|Ferula aucheri|species}} syn. {{taxlink|Dorema aucheri|species}} (in Western Persia)
# [[gum ammoniac]], [[ammoniacum]], obtained from the said plants

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أُشَّق}}

=====Descendants=====
