{{ar-decl-adj|أَشَلّ:cd|fd=شَلَّاوَانِ}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|ar|arc|אַשְׁלָא|tr=ašlā|t=rope}} ({{cog|syc|ܐܻܝܫܠܴܐ|tr=ʾīšlā|t=rope}}), in {{der|ar|arc-imp|𐡀𐡔𐡋|t=a surface measure}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒌑𒌃|ts=ašlu|tr=<sup>Ú</sup>NINNI<sub>5</sub>|t=rush; [[towrope|tow-rope]]; [[measuring]] [[rope]]; a linear measure of about 60 meters; a surface measure}}. {{doublet|ar|أَسَل|t1=long and slender twigs; rush; spear}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَشْل}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|أَشْل|m|pl=أُشُول}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[rope]]
# a [[linear measure]] of sixty [[cubit]]s ({{m|ar|ذِرَاع}})
#* {{RQ:Mafatih-Vloten|page=66 line 8}}

