Page 781 أصلح: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ص ل ح}}
Cognate with {{cog|he|הִצְלִיחַ||succeed|tr=hitslíakh}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|IV.pass}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to make (something bad) [[better]]; to [[mend]]
#: {{syn|ar|حَسَّنَ|t=to make (something) better; to refine}}
#: {{ant|ar|أَفْسَدَ|t=to make (something good) bad; to vitiate; to spoil; to corrupt; to pervert}}
## to [[repair]] (something malfunctioning, such as a machine or a device); to [[fix]]
##: {{ant|ar|أَفْسَدَ|أَتْلَفَ|خَرَّبَ|كَسَرَ|حَطَّمَ|عَطَّلَ|t2=to damage; to mar|t3=to ruin; to vandalize; to sabotage|t4=to break; to break up|t5=to crash; to wreck|t6=to render nonfunctional; to corrupt}}
##: {{usex|ar|هٰذَا الرَّجُلُ يُجِيدُ '''إِصْلَاحَ''' الْأَجْهِزَةِ الْمُتَعَطِّلَة.|This man excels at '''repairing''' nonfunctional machines and devices.}}
## to [[reform]] (something); to [[improve]]
##: {{usex|ar|'''اَلْإِصْلَاحُ''' الْبُرُوتِسْتَانْتِيّ|The Protestant '''Reformation'''}}
##: {{usex|ar|حِزْبُ الْإِصْلَاح|The '''Reform''' Party}}
##: {{usex|ar|جَمَاعَةُ '''إِصْلَاحِ''' مَالِيزِيَا|The '''Reform''' of Malaysia Organization}}
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|11-12
|passage=وَإِذَا قِيلَ لَهُمْ لَا تُفْسِدُوا فِي الْأَرْضِ قَالُوا إِنَّمَا نَحْنُ '''مُصْلِحُونَ''' أَلَا إِنَّهُمْ هُمُ الْمُفْسِدُونَ وَلَٰكِن لَّا يَشْعُرُونَ.
|translation=And when it is said to them, "Do not spread corruption on the earth!" they say, "We are but '''reformers'''!" They are the corrupters, but they are senseless!}}
## to [[better]] (something or someone) [[moral]]ly; to [[moralize]]; to [[uplift]]; to [[correct]]
##: {{syn|ar|أَدَّبَ|t=to better (someone) morally especially by beating or reproach; to castigate; to discipline}}
##: {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:الجامع لأحكام القرآن
|trans-title=The Collection of the Ordainments of the Qur'an
|author=w:al-Qurṭubī
|text=
وَمِنْ مَنَافِعِ الْعَصَا ضَرْبُ الرَّجُلِ نِسَاءَهُ بِهَا فِيمَا '''يُصْلِحُهُمْ''' وَيُصْلِحُ''' حَالَهُ وَحَالَهُمْ مَعَهُ
|t=Among the benefits of the stick is beating one's women with it to '''improve them and to improve''' [with it] one's life and theirs too.}}
# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to [[fix]] [[relation]]s {{+obj|ar|:بَيْنَ<between>}}, to [[make peace]], to [[reconcile]]; to [[harmonize]]
#: {{syn|ar|وَفَّقَ|t=to make agree or compatible; to match; to harmonize}}
#: {{ant|ar|أَلَّبَ|هَيَّجَ|نَفَّرَ|أَفْسَدَ|t1=to incite; to stir up|t2=to rouse; to inflame; to provoke|t3=to drive away as from hate or disgust; to repel|t4=to spread corruption and falsehood so as to agitate and fuel sedition}}
#: {{usex|ar|'''أَصْلَحَ''' بَيْنَ الْمُتَخَاصِمَيْنِ|t='''He reconciled''' between the two squabblers.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|4|128
|passage=وَإِنِ ٱمْرَأَةٌ خَافَتْ مِن بَعْلِهَا نُشُوزًا أَوْ إِعْرَاضًا فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا أَن '''يُصْلِحَا''' بَيْنَهُمَا صُلْحًا وَٱلصُّلْحُ خَيْرٌ
|translation=And if a woman fears from her husbans any inharmony or rebuffing, there is no blame on them if they '''reconcile'''. Indeed, reconciliation is good!}}

