Page 799 أضحى: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{m|ar|ضَحَّى|gloss=sacrifice, immolate}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|أَضْحَى|sing=أَضْحَاة}}

# sacrificial animal, [[victim]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَضْحًى}}

====See also====
* {{l|ar|عِيد الْأَضْحَى}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|ar|ضَحْوَة|t=[[morning]]}}, from the root {{ar-root|ض ح و}}. Sense of “become” resembles other verbs of similar meaning derived from different times of day; compare {{m|ar|أَصْبَحَ}}, {{m|ar|بَاتَ}}, {{m|ar|أَمْسَى}}, all meaning "become."

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|IV}}

# {{lb|ar|copulative}} to [[become]]
#: {{syn|ar|Thesaurus:صار}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''أَضْحَى''' الطَّالِبُ نَشِيطًا|The student '''became''' hardworking.}}
# to make [[visible]]
# to [[set out]] (to do something), to [[commence]] (doing something)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|IV}}
