Page 948 أفاويه: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|أَفْوَاه}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|gez|አፈው|t=scent, fragrance}}, pl. {{m|gez|አፈዋት}}, if not from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}. But also with parallels in {{der|ar|cus}}. The singular {{m|ar|فُوه}} is back-formed and possibly invented by medieval dictionary authors to place the word under a “root”. Doublet of {{m|ar|فَوْعَة}}, {{m|ar|فاح|فَوْح}}, {{m|ar|فاخ|فَوْخ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَفَاوِيه}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أَفَاوِيه|p}} {{tlb|ar|plural only}}

# what [[diffuse]]s [[fragrance]], [[odoriferous]] [[substance]]s, [[aromatic]] [[ingredient]]s, [[fragrant]]s
# [[spice]]s, [[seasoning]]s, [[condiment]]s
#: {{syn|ar|تَابِل|بَهَار|أَبْزَار|أَبَازِير}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|فُوه|pl=أَفَاوِيه|pl2=أَفْوَاه|lemma=أَفَاوِيه}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa|bor=1|فوه|tr=fuh|t=fragrant}}
* {{desc|bor=1|pt|alefanginas|alefangínias}}
* {{desc|es|alefanginas|bor=1}}

