Page 950 أفتى: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܐܦܬܝ|tr=ʾap̄tī|t=to expand; to propagate (orthodoxy)}},<ref>{{R:syc:Brockelmann 1995|page=615b}}</ref> which is a causative to {{der|ar|sem-wes-pro|*pataw-|t=to penetrate}}, perhaps also encompassing idioms such as {{der|ar|akk|uznam petûm|𒊻𒉆 𒉿𒌅𒌑𒌝|tr=uznam petûm}}, {{m|akk||𒊻𒉆 𒁍𒌓𒌅𒌝|tr=uznam puttûm|lit=to open an ear}},<ref>{{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=946}}</ref> from the related {{m|sem-pro|*pataḥ-|t=to open}}, so it would be equivalent to {{m+|ar||فَتَحَ أُذْنًا}}.

The corresponding noun {{m|ar|فَتْوَى|t=formal opinion}} has its patterning reflecting {{bor|ar|syc|ܦܬܘܐ|tr=peṯwā|t=spinning out, breadth (of words)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَفْتَى}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|IV}} {{tlb|ar|transitive}}

# {{lb|ar|law}} to [[deliver]] a [[formal]] [[opinion]] to (someone)
## {{lb|ar|Islam}} to [[deliver]] a [[fatwa]]
# to [[furnish]] (someone) with [[information]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|IV}}

===References===
<references/>
-------- end text --------
