Page 1013 أقام: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ق|و|م}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|הֵקִים|tr=hekím}}.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|IV.II:و.pass.vn:+,إِقَام,مُقَام}}

# to [[raise]], to [[lift]]
#: {{ux|ar|أقامَ يَسُوع أشخاصًا  خَسِروا حَياتَهُم،‏ ذُكورًا وإناثًا وكِبارًا وصِغارًا.|Jesus raised people who had lost their lives, male and female, old and young.}}
# to [[set up]], to [[erect]]
# to [[establish]], to [[found]]
#: {{ux|ar|وَأَقِيمُوا الصَّلَاةَ وَآتُوا الزَّكَاةَ وَارْكَعُوا مَعَ الرَّاكِعِينَ.|And establish prayer and give zakah and bow with those who bow.}}
# to [[appoint]], to [[nominate]] {{+obj|ar|acc<someone> + acc<as someone>}}
# to [[put]] [[in charge]] {{+obj|ar|acc<someone> + :عَلَى<of something>}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[awaken]]
# to [[resurrect]], to [[raise]] from the [[dead]]
# to [[stay]], to [[reside]], to [[abide]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<somewhere>}}
# to [[hold]] (a meeting, a celebration, a competition, a reception, etc.)
# to [[celebrate]] (a festival)
# to [[persist]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<in something>}}
# to [[sustain]] (someone) {{q|of food}}
# to [[perform]] (an action)
# to [[engage in]](?)
#: {{ux|ar|وأقامت علاقات جنسية كثيرة قبل الزواج.|She engaged in many sexual relationships before marriage.}}
# to [[observe]] (a prayer)

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|IV.II:و.pass.vn:+,إِقَام,مُقَام}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|قوم}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=2995}}
