{{ar-noun|أَكَّار|m|pl=أَكَّارُون|pl2=أَكَرَة}} {{term-label|ar|obsolete}}

# [[farmer]], [[tiller]], [[cultivator]] of [[land]]
#: {{syn|ar|زَرَّاع|زَارِع|حَرَّاث|فَلَّاح|كَافِر|بَرْدَزْبَة}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{w|Al-Akhtal al-Taghlibi|{{lang|ar|الأخطل}}}} [[https://www.aldiwan.net/poem6081.html ''al-ʾaḵṭal'']]|year=a. 710|title=la:Delectus veterum carminum arabicorum|page=54|pageurl=https://menadoc.bibliothek.uni-halle.de/ssg/content/pageview/551971|location=Berlin|publisher=H. Reuther’s Verlagsbuchhandlung|year_published=1890|editors={{w|Theodor Nöldeke}}; {{w|August Müller (orientalist)|August Müller}}|passage=إِنَّ الفَوَارِسَ يَعْرِفُونَ ظُهُورَكُم، أَوْلَادَ كُلِّ مُقَبَّحٍ أَكّارِ!|t=Indeed the nomads know your backs, children of every disdained boor!}}
#* {{quote-book|1=ar|author=w:Al-Jāḥiẓ|chapter=قِصَّةُ ابْنِ العَقَدِيِّ|trans-chapter=The Story of Ibn Al-Aqadiyy|editor=Muḥammad Fatḥī ʾAbū Bakr|title=Al-Buḵalāʾ|edition=5th|genre=|publisher=[[w:en:Egyptian-Lebanese Publishing House|Al Dar Al Masriah Al Lubnaniah]]|year=a. 869|year_published=2021|location=Cairo, Egypt|isbn=978-977-795-035-0|page=256|passage=قَالَ: «يَشْتَرِي لَنَا أَرُزًّا بِقِشْرِهِ وَيَحْمِلُهُ مَعَهُ، لَيْسَ مَعَهُ شَيْءٌ مِمَّا خَلَقَ اللّٰهُ إِلَّا ذٰلِكَ الْأَرُزّ. فَإِذَا صِرْنَا إِلَى أَرْضِهِ كَلَّفَ '''أَكَّارَهُ''' أَنْ يَجُشَّهُ فِي مِجَشَّةٍ لَهُ،{{…}}»}}

