Page 1144 ألوة: -------- begin text --------
[[File:കറ്റാർവാഴകൾ.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|أَلْوَة}}|upright=1.15]]
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
Apparently from one of the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} forms from which are already from {{der|ar|grc|ἀλόη}}, as Nöldeke<ref>{{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=43}}</ref> recognizes in view of the first variant being {{m|ar|أَلْوًى}}, whereafter the obsolete language also affords {{m-self|ar|أُلْوَة}}, {{m-self|ar|أُلُوَّة}}, {{m-self|ar|أَلُوَّة}}, {{m|ar|آلُوَّة}}, {{m|ar|أُولُوَّة}}, {{m|ar|لُوَّة}}, {{m|ar|لَيَّة}}, {{m|ar|لِيَّة}}, {{m|ar|أُلُوّ}}, {{m|ar|إِلِيَّة}}, though Greppin<ref>{{R:arc:Greppin:1988|page=34}}</ref> later assumed the view that Arabic and {{cog|sem-eth|-}} directly acquired from a {{der|ar|dra|-}} language; the {{cog|gez|ዐልዋ}}, {{m|gez|ዓልው}}, {{m|gez|ዓልዋ}}, {{m|gez|አለው}}, {{m|gez|አልው}} are, following Nöldeke, instead from the original non-Greek-derived Aramaic forms represented by {{cog|syc|ܥܠܘܝ|tr=ʕalway, ʕelway}}, {{cog|arc-cpa|ܥܠܘܐ}}, {{m|arc|ܥܠܘܝܬܐ}}, {{cog|myz|ࡏࡋࡅࡀࡉࡀ|tr=ʕluaia}}, {{m|myz|ࡀࡋࡅࡀࡉ|tr=ʔluai}}, which are directly from Indian languages. Compare the latter half of the compounds {{cog|ta|கற்றாழை|t=aloe vera}}, {{cog|ml|കറ്റാർവാഴ|t=aloe vera}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَلْوَة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|أَلْوَة|f|pl=أَلُوَّة|pl2=أُلُوَّة}}

# {{C|ar|Asparagales order plants|Succulents}} [[aloe]]
#: {{syn|ar|صَبِر|مَقْر}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَلْوَة|pl=أَلُوَّة|pl2=أُلُوَّة}}

=====Descendants=====
