Page 1168 أما: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{univerbation|ar|أَن|مَا|t1=that|pos2=relative}}, the original thought being “that this matter be touched”, “be it that”, or just a dialectal variant of disjunctive {{m|ar|إِمَّا|t=be it that}} as {{m|ar|أَمَّا}} can well be used for positing two alternatives.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَمَّا}}

====Conjunction====
{{head|ar|conjunction|head=أَمَّا}}

# [[as for]]; {{non-gloss definition|followed by a noun or pronoun, itself followed by the particle {{m|ar|فَـ}}}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|92|4-10
|passage=إِنَّ سَعْيَكُمْ لَشَتَّى <br> فَ'''أَمَّا''' مَنْ أَعْطَى وَٱتَّقَى <br> وَصَدَّقَ بِٱلْحُسْنَى <br> فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُ لِلْيُسْرَى <br> وَ'''أَمَّا''' مَن بَخِلَ وَٱسْتَغْنَى <br> وَكَذَّبَ بِٱلْحُسْنَى <br> فَسَنُيَسِّرُهُ لِلْعُسْرَى
|translation=Indeed, your efforts are diverse.<br>'''As for''' he who gives and fears Allah<br>And believes in the best [reward],<br>We will ease him toward ease.<br>But '''as for''' he who withholds and considers himself free of need<br>And denies the best [reward],<br>We will ease him toward difficulty.
|subst=وَ/وَ-,فَ/فَ-,لِلْ/لِ-ٱلْ}}
#* {{quote-text|ar|passage=وَلَمْ أَرَ كَٱلمَعْرُوفِ؛ '''أَمَّا''' مَذَاقُهُ / فَحُلْوٌ، وَ'''أَمَّا''' وَجْهُهُ فَجَمِيلُ|subst=وَلَمْ/وَ-لَمْ,كَٱلمَعْرُوفِ/كَ-لْ-مَعْرُوفِ,فَحُلْوٌ/فَ-حُلْوٌ,وَ'''أَمَّا'''/وَ-'''أَمَّا''',فَجَمِيلُ/فَ-جَمِيلُ}}

=====Usage notes=====
* It doesn't affect the case of the noun that follows:
* {{uxi|ar|'''أَمَّا''' ٱلرَّجُلُ '''فَ'''هُوَ فَقِيرٌ.|As for the man, he is poor.}}
* {{uxi|ar|'''أَمَّا''' ٱلرَّجُلَ ٱلْفَقِيرَ '''فَ'''لَا تَقْهَرْ!|As for the poor man, don't oppress him!}}

