Page 1202 أمسوخ: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|أَمْصُوخ|أُمْصُوخ}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|ar}}, too rare a word, perhaps from the root {{ar-root|م س خ}}, maybe an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing related to {{cog|syc|ܐܡܫܐ|tr=ʾamšā|t=flow, spurt}}, {{m|syc|ܐܡܝܫܐ|tr=ʾāmīšā|t=swamp; wetland edge of a river}} in reference to where it grows.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَمْصُوخ|أُمْسُوخ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أَمْسُوخ|m|head2=أُمْسُوخ}}

# {{tlb|ar|obsolete|rare}} [[horsetail]] ({{taxfmt|Equisetum|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|ذَنَب الْخَيْل|كِنْبَاث}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 1210|author={{lang|ar|{{w|ابن الأثير أبو السعادات|lang=ar}}}}|title=ar:النهاية في غريب الحديث والأثر|url=http://www.alwaraq.net/Core/SearchServlet/searchone?docid=246&searchtext=Itin2YTYo9mF2LXZiNiuIg==&option=1&offset=1&WordForm=1&exactpage=811&totalpages=1&AllOffset=1|passage=لو ضربك بأُمْصوخِ عيشومةٍ لقتلك الأمصوخُ خُوصُ الثُّمام وهو أضعف ما يكون.|t=If you get beaten by dry horsetail it gets you killed, it is the frond of panicgrass, though it be the weakest there is.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَمْسُوخ|head2=أُمْسُوخ}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|bor=1|axm|ամսուս|ումսուհ}}, {{q|possibly}} {{l|axm|ամվաճ}}

{{C|ar|Spore plants}}
