Page 1240 أن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
Probably identical to {{m|ar|هَمّ|t=concern}} from the root {{ar-root|ه م م}}, with sound changes typical to Arabic, as e.g. in {{m|ar|إن}}. Note also the noun {{m|ar|هَن|t=thing; self, ''synonym of {{m|ar|نَفْس}}''}}, often mentioned in grammars as one of [[:Category:Arabic nouns with long construct singular|“the six nouns” also known as “five nouns“]], which became obsolete due to often referring to genitalia.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَنْ}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|أَنْ}}

# {{ngd|introduces a verb clause in place of the definite verbal noun}}
#: {{synonyms|ar|مَا}}
## [[to]], [[that]]; {{ngd|introduces a subjunctive verb}} {{q|often corresponding to the English infinitive}}
##: {{ux|ar|سَيَنْتَخِبُ الشَّعْبُ رَئِيسًا جَدِيدًا '''بَعْدَ أَنْ يُكْتَبَ''' الدُّسْتُور.|t=The people will elect a new president '''after''' the constitution '''is written'''.|lit=...after '''[that]''' the constitution be written}}
##: {{ux|ar|أُرِيدُ '''أَنْ''' آكُلَ.|t=I want '''to''' eat.|lit=I want '''that''' I eat.}}
##: {{ux|ar|أُرِيدُ '''أَنْ''' يَأْكُلَ.|t=I want him '''to''' eat.|lit=I want '''that''' he eats.}}
## [[that]]; {{ngd|introduces a past-tense verb}}
<!-- Translating the below as "so" rather than "that" in order to avoid confusion with the bolded term -->
##: {{ux|ar|سَبَقَ '''أَنْ''' قُلْتُ لَكَ ذٰلِكَ|t=I already told you so.|lit=it has passed '''that''' I told you so.}}
##: {{ux|ar|اِنْتَخَبَ الشَّعْبُ رَئِيسًا جَدِيدًا '''بَعْدَ أَنْ كُتِبَ''' الدُّسْتُور.|t=The people elected a new president '''after''' the constitution '''was written'''.|lit=...after '''[that]''' the constitution was written}}
# {{lb|ar|literary}} {{ngd|introduces reported speech}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|44|passage=وَنَادَىٰ أَصْحَابُ الْجَنَّةِ أَصْحَابَ النَّارِ أَن قَدْ وَجَدْنَا مَا وَعَدَنَا رَبُّنَا حَقًّا فَهَلْ وَجَدتُّم مَّا وَعَدَ رَبُّكُمْ حَقًّا ۖ قَالُوا نَعَمْ ۚ فَأَذَّنَ مُؤَذِّنٌ بَيْنَهُمْ أَن لَّعْنَةُ اللَّهِ عَلَى الظَّالِمِينَ}}And the Companions of the Garden shall cry out to the Companions of the Fire '''[literally "that"]''' "We have found true what our Lord promised us. So did ye find true what your Lord promised you?" They shall say, "Yes", then an announcer shall announce between them '''[literally "that"]''' "God's curse is on the evildoers!"
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|117
|passage=وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَى مُوسَى '''أَنْ''' أَلْقِ عَصَاكَ
|translation=And we intimated to Moses, “throw your staff!”
|lit=and we intimated to Moses '''that''' throw your staff
|subst=وَ/وَ-}}
# {{form of|ar|Form|أَنَّ}}
#: {{ux|ar|أَشْهَدُ '''أَنْ''' لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللّٰهُ.|t=I bear witness '''that''' there is no god except Allah.}}
#: {{ux|ar|عَلِمْتُ '''أَنْ''' سَيُسَافِرُ زُهَيْرٌ|t=I knew '''that''' Zuhayr would travel}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|10|10
|passage=وَآخِرُ دَعْوَاهُمْ أَنِ ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَالَمِينَ
|translation=And the last of their call will be '''[that]''' "Praise to Allah, Lord of the worlds!"
|subst=وَآخِرُ/وَ-آخِرُ,لِلَّهِ/لِ-لَّهِ}}
# [[lest]]
#*: {{RQ:Qur'an|7|172
|passage=وَإِذْ أَخَذَ رَبُّكَ مِنۢ بَنِىٓ ءَادَمَ مِن ظُهُورِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَأَشْهَدَهُمْ عَلَىٰٓ أَنفُسِهِمْ أَلَسْتُ بِرَبِّكُمْ ۖ قَالُوا۟ بَلَىٰ ۛ شَهِدْنَآ ۛ أَن تَقُولُوا۟ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَـٰمَةِ إِنَّا كُنَّا عَنْ هَـٰذَا غَـٰفِلِينَ
|translation=And (remember) when your Lord brought forth from the Children of Adam, from their loins, their seed (or from Adam's loin his offspring) and made them testify as to themselves (saying): "Am I not your Lord?" They said: "Yes! We testify," '''lest''' you should say on the Day of Resurrection: "Verily, we have been unaware of this." }}

=====Usage notes=====
* In sense 1.2, if {{m-self|ar|أَنْ}} and the clause it introduces pertain to a verb, then they are syntactically its ''subject''. However, this clause is never allowed to precede the verb: Arabic does not accept the phrasing {{m|ar||*'''أَنْ''' قُلْتُ لَكَ ذٰلِكَ سَبَقَ|lit='''that''' I told you so has passed}}.
** If the verb phrase inside the clause is relatively short, this can serve to distinguish an {{lang|ar|أَنْ}}-phrase from the equivalent verbal noun. A sentence like {{m|ar||سَبَقَ '''أَنْ''' تَعَامَلْنَا|t=we have already done business together}} is perfectly fine being reworded to {{m|ar||تَعَامُلُنَا سَبَقَ}} instead of {{m|ar||سَبَقَ تَعَامُلُنَا}}, but {{m|ar||*'''أَنْ''' تَعَامَلْنَا سَبَقَ}} is ungrammatical.
* Notice that sense 1 is twice shown introducing the complement of prepositions like {{m|ar|قَبْلَ|t=before}} and {{m|ar|بَعْدَ|t=after}}; this also includes phrasal ones like {{m|ar|بِمُجَرَّدِ|tr=bi-mujarradi|t=as soon as|pos={{m|ar|بِـ|t=with}} + {{m|ar|مُجَرَّد|t=merely}}}}. If this preposition is in a past context, then the verb inside the clause can in fact be either past ''or'' nonpast: the overall meaning will be past-tense either way. Compare the example above that translates to "the people elected...", which shows the use of a past-tense verb with {{m|ar||بَعْدَ أَن}}, to the following:
*: {{ux|ar|مَرِضَ قَبْلَ '''أَنْ''' يُسَافِرَ|t=He fell sick before he traveled.|lit=he fell sick before '''[that]''' he travel}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|أَلَّا}}
* {{l|ar|أَلَّن}}
* {{l|ar|أَلَّو}}
* {{l|ar|لِأَنْ}}
* {{l|ar|لِئَلَّا}}
* {{l|ar|لِئَلَّن}}
* {{l|ar|أَن التَّفْسِيرِيَّة}}

===Etymology 1.2===
{{adverbial accusative|ar}} of the noun underlying the former conjunction.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَنَّ}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|أَنَّ}}

# [[that]] {{q|introduces an equational clause or a verb phrase}}
#: {{ux|ar|هَلْ تَعْلَمُ '''أَنَّ'''نِي أَطْوَلُ مِنْكَ؟|t=Do you know '''that''' I'm taller than you?}}
#: {{ux|ar|أَعْرِفُ '''أَنَّ''' ٱبْنَكَ سَرَقَ سَيَّارَتِي.|t=I know '''that''' your son stole my car.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* If pertaining to a verb, {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} and the clause it introduces are syntactically its ''object''. This distinguishes {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} from {{m-self|ar|أَنْ}}, especially in the case outlined in the usage note above.
* {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} must be followed immediately by the subject of the clause it introduces, in the accusative case. An attached object pronoun can satisfy this condition.
** The sole exception is in the relevant sense of {{m-self|ar|أَنْ}} above. In that case, such a subject ''can'' appear and cause the {{m-self|ar|أَنَّ}} pronunciation to resurface, but it is only optional. Compare the following alternative phrasing: {{ux|ar|أَشْهَدُ '''أَنَّهُ''' لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا اللَّهُ|t=I bear witness '''that''' there is no god except Allah.}}

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|أَنَّ||1s=[[أَنِّي]] / [[أَنَّنِي]]|1p=[[أَنَّنَا]] / [[أَنَّا]]}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{l|ar|إِنَّ}} {{q|after certain verbs}}

=====Derived terms=====
{{col2|ar|لِأَنَّ|أَنَّمَا}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:ʾinna and her sisters/ar}}

===Etymology 2.1===
From the root {{ar-root|ء|ن|ن}}, probably also related to the root {{ar-root|ه م م}} connected to the idea of worry, affect. Compare {{m|ar|هَنَاة|t=misfortune, accident}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَنَّ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.ipass.vn:أَنّ,أَنِين,تَأْنَان}}

# to [[moan]], to [[groan]], to [[complain]] {{+obj|ar|:مِن<of something>/:أَنَّ(clause)<that ...>}}
#* {{quote|ar|كُلَّمَا '''أَنَّ''' بِالْعِرَاقِ جَرِيحٌ / لَمَسَ الشَّرْقُ جَنْبَهُ فِي عُمَانِهِ}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.ipass.vn:أَنّ,أَنِين,تَأْنَان}}

===Etymology 2.2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَنّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|أَنّ|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|أَنَّ|form=I}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَنّ}}

===References===
* {{R:sem-pro:FS Militarev|page=207–209}}

