Page 1304 أنس: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ء ن س}}

===Etymology 1.1===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i,u.pass.vn:أُنْس,أَنَس,إِنْس}}<br />
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.pass.vn:أُنْس,أَنَس,إِنْس}}<br />
{{ar-verb|I/u~u.pass.vn:أُنْس,أَنَس,إِنْس}}<br />

# {{lb|ar|intransitive|or|transitive}} to become [[used to]], to be [[comfortable]] with {{+obj|ar|:بِ/:إِلَى/acc<something>}}
#: {{syn|ar|اِعْتَادَ}}
# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to [[enjoy]], to be [[happy]] with {{+obj|ar|:بِ/:ل}}
#: {{syn|ar|أَلِفَ}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[know]], to be [[familiar]] with (an issue)
#: {{syn|ar|سلَّى}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[comfort]] [[psychological]]ly; to [[solace]]
#: {{syn|ar|سلَّى}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[sense]] or [[make out]] ([[visual]]ly, [[auditory|auditorily]], or [[mental]]ly)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i,u.pass.vn:أُنْس,أَنَس,إِنْس}}<br />
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.pass.vn:أُنْس,أَنَس,إِنْس}}<br />
{{ar-conj|I/u~u.pass.vn:أُنْس,أَنَس,إِنْس}}

===Etymology 1.2===
Morphologically from the root {{ar-root|ء|ن|س}}, with some senses influenced by or deriving directly from {{m|ar|إِنْس|t=humans}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[comfort]] [[psychological]]ly; to [[amuse]]
#: {{syn|ar|لَاطَفَ}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[humanize]], to [[anthropomorphize]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَنْسَنَ|جَسَّمَ}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[treat]] like a [[human]]
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[perceive]] or [[discern]] ([[visual]]ly, [[auditory|auditorily]], or [[mental]]ly)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 1.3===

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|أَنَس|m}}

# {{given name|ar|male}}

