-------- end text --------
Page 1359 أنوق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unk|ar}}. Maybe from the root {{ar-root|ء ن ق}}, maybe natively from {{m|ar|نَاقَة|t=female camel}} or [http://cal.huc.edu/oneentry.php?lemma=nqy%20N&cits=all via] a [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only witnessed by borrowings|lost]] [http://cal.huc.edu/oneentry.php?lemma=ynqh%20N&cits=all Aramaic] term as in {{m|la|struthiocamelus|t=ostrich}}, but this is less likely since old dictionaries understand the word as {{m|ar|[[ذَكَر]] ال[[رَّخَم]]|t=male of the [[Egyptian vulture]]}}, maybe from {{ar-root|ع ن ق|nocat=1}} as in another name of a long-necked bird {{m|ar|عَنْقَاء}}, the form of a {{ar-color/defect adjective|nocat=1|lc=1}}, compared to {{bor|ar|arc|אִינְקָא|tr=ʾinqā}} for a large bird, however regularly compared to {{bor|ar|gez|አንቄ}}, {{m|gez|አንቄት}}, maybe a borrowing from a regional form of it, since in {{cog|sem-eth|-}} the Proto-Semitic pattern ''KaLīM'' shifted to ''KaLūM''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَنُوق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أَنُوق|m}}

# [[vulture]], [[kite]] (bird)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَنُوق}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=66a}}
* {{R:ar:Baranov}}
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:arc:Levy|volume=1|page=43a|entry=אִינְקָא}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=2|page=9–10 Nr. 6|entry=*ˀan(V)ḳ-|e=364}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-3}}

{{C|ar|Vultures}}
