# {{place|ar|city|p/East Azerbaijan Province|c/Iran|t1=Ahar}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|instead=1|lang=ar|page=374 ''m''–''u''|section=web [http://islamport.com/w/bld/Web/451/136.htm 1/136]|passage=وأما أرمينية فإنها كورة جليلة رسمها أرميني بن كنظر بن يافث بن نوح ومنها ترتفع الستور والزلاليُّ الرفيعة كثيرة الخصائص قصبتها دَبِيل ومن مدنها: بَدْلِيس، خِلَاط، أَرْجِيش، بَرْكَرِي، خُوَيُّ، سَلَمَاس، أُرْمِيَة، دَاخَرَّقَان، مَرَاغَة، '''أَهْرُ'''، مَرَنْد، سَِنْجَان، قالِيقَلَا، قندرية، قَلْعَة يُونِس، نورين.|t=Concerning Armenia, it is a revered region of Armenian tradition, a son like the son of Japhet, the son of Noah, and from it hail draperies and fine rugs of lots of peculiarities the filament of which is like that of Dwin, and of its towns are: [a list of settlements follows].}}
# {{place|ar|county|p/East Azerbaijan Province|c/Iran|t1=Ahar County}} {{gloss|{{l|ar|مُقَاطَعَة أَهْر|tr=muqāṭaʕa ʔahr}}}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَهْر:di|state=ind-def}}

===Etymology 2===
Causative to {{m|ar|هَرَّ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|أَهَرَّ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|IV}}

# to cause to [[purr]], [[whirr]], [[bray]], [[grumble]], [[snarl]], or [[howl]]
# to call to the [[water]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|IV}}
-------- end text --------
Page 1376 أهل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ء ه ل}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔahl-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{audio|ar|Ar-أهل.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|أَهْل|m|g2=p|pl=أَهْلُونَ|pl2=أَهَالٍ|plcons=أَهَالِي}}

# [[family]], [[household]]; [[people]], [[kinfolk]], [[relations]]
#: {{syn|ar|أُسْرَة|آل}}
# {{lb|ar|dated}} [[wife]]
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:جامع البيان في تأويل القرآن
|trans-title=The Compilation of Qur'anic Interpretations
|author=w:al-Ṭabarī
|text=
عن ابن عباس، في قوله: ﴿لِيَسْتَأْذِنْكُمُ الَّذِينَ مَلَكَتْ أَيْمَانُكُمْ﴾ يقول: إذا خلا الرجل '''بأهله''' بعد صلاة العشاء، فلا يدخل عليه خادم ولا صبيّ إلا بإذن حتى يصلي الغداة، فإذا خلا '''بأهله''' عند صلاة الظهر فمثل ذلك.
|t=[It was related] that Ibn Abbas said this regarding the verse "And those whom your right hand possesses must ask for your permission [to enter]": "If the man retires '''with his wife''' after the night prayer, no servant or young boy may enter till he finishes the prayer of dawn, and also when he is alone '''with his wife''' during the time of the noon prayer.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:الجامع لأحكام القرآن
|trans-title=The Collection of the Ordainments of the Qur'an
|author=w:al-Qurṭubī
|text=
قال مالك: (ومن بعد صلاة العشاء) فالله سماها صلاة العشاء فأحب النبي - صلى الله عليه وسلم - أن تسمى بما سماها الله تعالى به ويعلمها الإنسان '''أهله''' وولده
|t=Mālik said, "'And after the night prayer' [shows that] Allah called it 'the night prayer', and so the Prophet, may Allah bless him and grant him peace, liked it to be called what Allah called it and [liked] the man to teach it [thus] to '''his wife''' and children.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:تفسير القرآن العظيم
|trans-title=The Interpretation of the Great Qur'an
|author=w:Ibn Kaṯīr
|text=
(وحين تضعون ثيابكم من الظهيرة) أي: في وقت القيلولة؛ لأن الإنسان قد يضع ثيابه في تلك الحال مع '''أهله'''، (ومن بعد صلاة العشاء) لأنه وقت النوم، فيؤمر الخدم والأطفال ألا يهجموا على أهل البيت في هذه الأحوال، لما يُخشى من أن يكون الرجل على '''أهله''' ونحو ذلك من الأعمال
|t="And when you put off your clothes from noon," that is, nap time, since the man could take off his clothes [when] with '''his wife''', "and after the night prayer" because it is sleeping time, so [all] servants and children are ordered not to burst in on the people of the house at those times in case the man is with [literally "on"] '''his wife''' or something like that.}}
# [[people]], [[membership]] {{gloss|body of members}}, [[followership]] {{gloss|group of followers}} {{+obj|ar|gen<of>}}
## [[adherents]] {{+obj|ar|gen<of>}}
##: {{coi|ar|أَهْل الْحَدِيث|t=the adherents of traditions}}
##: {{coi|ar|أَهْل الْكِتَاب|t=the adherents of the Book}}
## [[experts]] {{+obj|ar|gen<in>}}
##: {{coi|ar|أَهْل الطِّب|t=medical experts}}
# [[inhabitant]]s
#: {{coi|ar|أَهْل الْقَرْيَة|t=the inhabitants of the village}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|29|31|passage=وَلَمَّا جَاءَتْ رُسُلُنَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ بِالْبُشْرَىٰ قَالُوا إِنَّا مُهْلِكُو '''أَهْلِ''' هَٰذِهِ الْقَرْيَةِ{{nbsp}}ۖ إِنَّ '''أَهْلَهَا''' كَانُوا ظَالِمِينَ|subst=الْقَرْيَةِ{{nbsp}}ۖ /الْقَرْيَةِ|translation=And when Our messengers brought Abraham the good news, they said: Lo! we are about to destroy the '''people''' of that township, for '''its people''' are wrong-doers.|footer=<small>Translated by [[w:en:Marmaduke Pickthall|Marmaduke Pickthall]]</small>}}

