===Etymology===
Shortening of longer phrase {{m|ar|لَقَدْ صَادَفْتُمْ أَهْلًا وَوَطِئْتُمْ سَهْلًا|tr=laqad ṣādaftum ʔahlan wa-waṭiʔtum sahlan||You have come across your own people and you have trodden on even ground}}.<ref name="classicidioms">[https://archive.org/details/ALearnersDictionaryOfClassicalArabicIdioms_201703/page/n1/mode/2up A Learner's Dictionary Of Classical Arabic Idioms] Page 138. Entry 941.</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَهْلًا وَسَهْلًا}}

===Interjection===
{{ar-interj|[[أَهْلًا]] [[وَ]][[سَهْلًا]]}}

# [[welcome]]

