Page 1393 أو: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʔaw}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|אוֹ|tr=’o}}, {{cog|uga|𐎜|ts=ʾō}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَوْ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-أو.ogg}}

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|أَوْ}}

# {{non-gloss definition|indicates an inclusive disjunction}}
#: {{ux|ar|كُلِ التَّمْرَ الْهِنْدِيَّ '''أَوِ''' ٱشْرَبِ الْبُرْتُقَالَ.|t=Eat the tamarind! '''Or''' drink the orange-juice!}}
# {{lb|ar|only in declaratives}} {{non-gloss definition|indicates an exclusive disjunction}}
#: {{ux|ar|كُلُّ شَيْءٍ إِمَّا مَوْجُودٌ '''أَوْ''' غَيْرُ مَوْجُودٍ.|t=Every object is either existent '''or''' inexistent.}}
#: {{ux|ar|لَا أَدْرِي هَلْ صَاحِبُكَ شَقِيٌّ '''أَوْ''' سَعِيدٌ.|t=I do not know whether your friend is happy '''or''' downhearted.}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|ar|أَمْ}} is used in questions where only one option is correct, possible or needed, and {{m|ar|أَوْ}} is used if more options may be correct.
#: {{ux|ar|هَلْ سَيَأْتِي أَبُوكَ أَوْ أُمُّكَ؟|Will your mother  or your father come? (will anyone of them come?)}}
#: {{ux|ar|هَلْ سَيَأْتِي أَبُوكَ أَمْ أُمُّكَ؟|Will your mother  or your father come? (which one will come?)}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|أَمْ}}
* {{l|ar|إِمَّا}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|sw|au|bor=1}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|أو}}

-------- end text --------
