Page 1435 أورشليم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܐܘܪܫܠܡ|tr=ʾūrišlēm, ʾōrēšlim}}, a pre-[[Hebrew]] form. Compare {{m|akk|Urušalim|𒌑𒊒𒊓𒅆𒆠|tr=Urušalim}} in the [[w:Amarna letters|Armana letters]] (14th century B.C.).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أُورُشَلِيم}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|أُورُشَلِيم|f}}

# {{lb|ar|Christianity|Israel}} {{place|ar|the claimed (and de-facto) <<capital city>> of <<c/Israel>>|;|the claimed <<capital city>> of <<c/Palestine>>|t1=Jerusalem}}

====Usage notes====
Because of its common origin with Hebrew {{m|he|ירושלים}}, the Arabic {{m|ar||أُورُشَلِيم}} is used in official Arabic documents of the Israeli government. It is also used in Christian liturgical Arabic. Outside of these two contexts, the name is seldom used and {{m|ar|الْقُدْس}} is preferred.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أُورُشَلِيمُ|state=ind-def}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|اَلْقُدْس}}
* {{l|ar|بَيْت اَلْمَقْدِس}}
