Page 1514 أيدع: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Dracaena cinnabari (50078807432).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|أَيْدَع}} – {{taxlink|Dracaena cinnabari|species}}|upright=1.15]]
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Anciently borrowed from {{bor|ar|sem-sar|-}},<ref>{{R:ar:FAH|34|page=298b|instead=1}}</ref> the three quality grades of dragon's blood being called in {{cog|sqt|-}} for high quality {{m|sqt|ʔəmṣɔ́loh}}, medium quality '''{{m|sqt|ʔəʔī́daʕ}}''', low quality {{m|sqt|fṣɔṣ}}, the tree {{m|sqt|ʔaʕarhī́yəb}}.<ref>{{cite-journal|volume=2|work=New Arabian Studies|page=189|pages=186–198|year=1994|publisher=University of Exeter Press|last=Simeone-Senelle|pageurl=https://www.google.de/books/edition/New_Arabian_Studies/29yk1ddLaDoC?hl=de&gbpv=1&dq=%22a%27arhiy%C7%9Db%22&pg=PA189&printsec=frontcover|first=Marie-Claude|title=Aloe and Dragon's Blood, some Medicinal and Traditional Uses on the Island of Socotra}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|أَيْدَع}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|أَيْدَع|m}}

# [[dragon's blood]] ({{taxlink|Dracaena cinnabari|species}}, and other ''[[Dracaena]]'' species, and {{taxlink|Calamus draco|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|دَم الْأَخَوَيْن|دَم التِنِّين|دَم الثُعْبَان|عَنْدَم}}
#: {{rfquotek|ar|Abū Ḥanīfa ad-Dīnawarī}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أَيْدَع}}

