Page 1563 إبرهم: -------- begin text --------

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|إِبْرَٰهِـۧم|tr=ʾibrāhīm|m}}

# {{obsolete spelling of|ar|إِبْرَاهِيم}}

====Usage notes====
This spelling is found in the [[Qur'an]] alongside the normal classical spelling {{m|ar|إِبْرَٰهِيم}}. In the influential [[w:History of the Quran#1924 Cairo edition|Cairo edition]], it is only found in Surat {{w|Al-Baqara}} (where it is used exclusively), but usage is more mixed in early manuscripts. The reading {{m|ar|إِبْرٰهٰم}} is used in some reading traditions, notably that of [[w:ar:هشام عن ابن عامر|Hisham ibn Ammar]], for this spelling, based on the scribal tradition.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِبْرَٰهِـۧم/ʾibrāhīm:di|state=ind-def}}

===References===
* van Putten, Marijn (2020), "Hišām's ''ʾIbrāhām'': Evidence for a Canonical Quranic Reading Based on the ''Rasm''", ''Journal of the Royal Asiatic Society'' Vol. 30, Issue 2, pp. 231-250.
-------- end text --------
