Page 1569 إبزيم: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إِبْزَام|إِبْزِين}}

===Etymology===
Superficially of the root {{ar-root|ب ز م}}, however a borrowing of {{bor|ar|fa|ابزین|tr=abzin}}, {{m|fa|اوزین|tr=avzin|t=ring; buckle}}, which is maybe a suffixation of the same word as {{m|fa|بز|tr=baz|t=high ground, hill, summit of a mountain}}, and easily {{m|ar|بَزِيم|t=a [[shoot]] of a [[plant]] or [[frond]] used to bind [[vegetable]] [[bundle]]s and the [[bundle]] itself}}, {{m|ar|وَزِيم|t=bundle of vegetables}} are all the same word rather via a meaning of binding or surrounding, then meanings {{m|ar|بَزَمَ|t=to take with two fingers}} denominal. Also in {{cog|tmr|אבזיינא|tr=ʾaḇzyēnā}}, {{m|arc|אפזיינא|tr=ʾap̄zyēnā|t=buckle}}, {{m|arc|בזיינא|tr=bazyēnā|t=buckle, clasp}}, Jewish Neo-Aramaic {{m|arc|אבזונא|tr=ʾaḇzūnā}}, {{cog|kmr|avzûm}}, {{m|kmr|avzûn|t=buckle}}, {{cog|ckb|ئاوزوونە}}, {{m|ckb|ئاوزینە|t=buckle}}, {{cog|ka|აბზინდა|t=buckle}}, and in the {{cog|hy|-}} invented language Ṙuštuni {{m|hy||աբզէդոն|t=girdle}}. The sound change of trailing {{m|ar||ـنٌ}} to {{m|ar|ـمٌ}} having happened in Arabic is evidenced by {{m|ar|مِيجَم|t=fuller’s beetle}} and {{m|ar|كرزن|كَرْزَم|t=one-sided axe}}, see their forms on their pages.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِبْزِيم}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِبْزِيم|m|pl=إِبْزِيمَات|pl2=أَبَازِيم}}

# {{C|ar|Fasteners|Clothing|Horse tack}} [[clasp]], [[buckle]] (of a belt or shoe or [[surcingle]] etc.)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِبْزِيم|pl=sfp|pl2=أَبَازِيم}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa|ابزیم|tr=abzim|bor=1}}
* {{desc|he|אבזם|tr=avzam|bor=1}}

