Page 1572 إبط: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
No cognates are {{unk|ar|title=known}}. Maybe irregularly from {{ar-root|ع ب ط|nocat=1}} or even {{ar-root|غ ب ط|nocat=1}} or {{m|ar|بَطَّ}}, but probably {{ar-root|ه ب ط}} with the armpit understood as the part of the arm where “declivity” or “emaciation” has its place and the regular sound change of the initial consonant known from grammatical elements {{m|ar|إِن}}, {{m|ar|أَن}}, {{m|ar|أَ}}, {{ar-form|IV|nocap=1}} etc. but also found in e.g. {{m|ar|إِبِل}} and {{m|ar|أُهْبَة}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِبْط}}

===Noun===
