Page 1576 إبل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The root {{ar-root|ء ب ل}} else but contains terms plausibly denominative from this word for camels; the animal name, as well as the raincloud-name reminiscing {{m|ar|وَبْل|t=heavy-dropped rain}}, must be connected to {{der|ar|sem-pro|*wabal-|t=to carry, to bear}} also of restricted Arabic use in the root formula {{ar-root|و ب ل}}, with glottal stop as {{m|ar|أُهْبَة|t=gear, accoutrement}}. In {{cog|syc|-}} one finds {{m|syc|ܐܒܠܬܐ|tr=ʾabbāltā, ʾebbaltā, ʾebbāltā|t=a herd or caravan of camels}}, accounting for its vocalism probably a separate derivation of this sense, whereas the Arabic unusual measure of {{m|ar|إِبِل}} is inflated by a prop vowel<ref>{{R:ar:EALL|volume=4|page=174|entry=Semitic Languages|author=Voigt, Rainer}}</ref> from an original pattern as in animal names like {{m|ar|عِجْل}} and {{m|ar|حِسْل}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِبِل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|إِبِل|f|pl=آبَال}}

# {{lb|ar|collective}} [[camel]]s
# {{lb|ar|collective|obsolete}} [[rain cloud]]s
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|88|17-19|passage=أَفَلَا يَنْظُرُونَ إِلَى '''ٱلْإِبِلِ''' كَيْفَ خُلِقَتْ<br/>وَإِلَى ٱلسَّمَآءِ كَيْفَ رُفِعَتْ<br/>وَإِلَى ٱلْجِبَالِ كَيْفَ نُصِبَتْ|translation=Then do they not look unto the '''rainy clouds'''<ref>{{cite-web|last=Drissner|first=Gerald|title=Camels or rain clouds? The intriguing word {{lang|ar|إبل}} in the Qur’an|date=2023-10-27|url=https://arabic-for-nerds.com/islam/camel-or-rain-cloud-quran/|work=Arabic for Nerds}}</ref> – how they are created? And the sky, how it has been raised? And the mountains how they have been set up?}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِبِل|pl=آبَال}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|akk|𒄿𒁉𒇻|tr=i-bi-lu|ts=ibilu|bor=1}}<ref>{{cite-book|last=Forbes|first=Robert James|title=Studies in ancient technology|volume=II|year=1993|edition=3rd|publisher=E. J. Brill|location=Leiden|page=209|isbn=978-90-04-00622-5|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=4Oi70BovgoQC&pg=PA209}}</ref>

====See also====
