Page 1580 إبليس: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Theorised to come from {{der|ar|grc|διάβολος||[[devil]], [[accuser]], [[slanderer]]}}. Alternatively, it has been maintained to originate from the trilateral root {{ar-root|ب|ل|س}} with the meaning of "despairing [of God's mercy] or confounded [and unable to see the right course]" from the verb {{m|ar|أَبْلَسَ}}. This would, however, require the trilateral root to take the form ''if'īl'' which, excepting [[إحليل]], is usually associated with words of non-Arabic origin (see [[إدريس]], [[إكليل]], [[إنجيل]], [[إبريز]], and [[إبريق]]).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِبْلِيس}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|إِبْلِيس|m}}

# {{lb|ar|religion}} [[Iblis]], [[Satan]]; the [[Devil]].
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|34
|passage=وَإِذْ قُلْنَا لِلْمَلَائِكَةِ ٱسْجُدُوا لِآدَمَ فَسَجَدُوا إِلَّا '''إِبْلِيسَ''' أَبَى وَٱسْتَكْبَرَ وَكَانَ مِنَ الْكَافِرِينَ
|translation=And [mention] when We said to the angels, "Prostrate before Adam"; so they prostrated, except for '''Iblees'''. He refused and was arrogant and became of the disbelievers.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِبْلِيسُ|state=ind-def}}

