Page 1669 إذ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{clipping|ar|إِذَا}} used to underscore a particular point in time, perhaps analogical to the relations of other conjunctions like {{m|ar|إِمَّا}} and {{m|ar|إِن}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِذْ}}

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|إِذْ}}

# and [[then]]
# [[as]], [[when]]
# [[since]], [[because]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=13th century|author=Ibn Malik|url=https://archive.org/details/alfiyyah-ibn-maalik/123219776-Alfiya-Ibn-Malik/mode/1up|title=[[w:Alfiya|Alfiyyah]]
|passage=وَعَوْدُ خَافِضٍ لَدَى عَطْفٍ عَلَى / ضَمِيرِ خَفْضٍ لَازِمًا قَدْ جُعِلَا / وَلَيْسَ عِنْدِي لَازِمًا '''إِذْ''' قَدْ أَتَى / فِي ٱلنَّظْمِ وَٱلنَّثْرِ الصَّحِيحِ مُثْبَتَا
|translation=And the return of a preposition when conjoined to a genitive pronoun, / It is made necessary with a genitive pronoun, / But it is not necessary in my opinion, '''because''' it has come, / In both authentic, sound poetry and prose, it is established.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 2001|author=w:al-Uthaymin|url=https://shamela.ws/book/36954/573|page=573 (page 14 in-book online)|chapter=Part 52 - The conjunction with a genitive pronoun|title=Sharh (Explanation of) Alfiyyah Ibn Malik
|passage=[العطف على الضمير المخفوض] - قال المؤلف رحمه الله: «وعود خافض لدى عطف على ضمير خفض لازماً قد جعلا وليس عندي لازماً '''إذ''' قد أتى في النظم والنثر الصحيح مثبتا» - (عودُ): مبتدأ خبره جملة: (قد جُعل). - (ولازماً) المفعول الثاني لجُعل مقدم، ونائب الفاعل في جُعل مستتر هو المفعول الأول.
|translation=[Section: The conjunction with a genitive pronoun] - The author [Ibn Malik], may Allah have mercy on him, said: {{highlight|"Returning the preposition when conjoining to a genitive pronoun is obligatory. However, in my opinion, it is not obligatory '''because''' it has been confirmed in both poetry and prose."|lightblue}} - ‘(عودُ):’ A subject, with its predicate being the clause: ‘(قد جُعل)’. - The term '(ولازماً)' is the second object of 'جُعل' and is advanced, while the hidden subject of 'جُعل' is the first object.}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|إذ}}

===Further reading===
* {{pedia|lang=ar}}
-------- end text --------
Page 1670 إذا: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
Equivalent to a {{univerbation|ar|إِن|t1=if, ''introduces protasis''|ذَا|t2=this, ''demonstrative pronoun''|nocap=1}}. A retroactively added<!--nachgeschobene--> protasis may be instead understood by the hearer as a new main clause, therefore “when” became “then”. Like in {{noncog|la|-}}—well-known—relative pronouns are used as proximal demonstrative pronouns indistinctly: [[quod erat demonstrandum]].

Compare to {{cog|he|אָז|t=so, therefore, then|tr=ʾāz}}, {{cog|he|אַזַי}}, {{cog|arc|אֱדַיִן|t=then, at that time|tr=ʾĕḏáyin}}, which may in lack of attestations of conjunctional use instead parallel {{m|ar|هٰذَا}} however.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|إِذَا}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-إذا.ogg}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|إِذَا}} {{+obj|ar|past/jussive}}

# [[when]], [[when]] it is [[that]]; [[as soon as]]; [[if]]
#: {{syn|ar|إِذ|لَمَّا|حِينَ|t1=when|q1=dated|t2=when; once|t3=(at) the moment that}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''إِذَا''' جِئْتَ فَاتَّصِلْ بِي|t='''As soon as''' you arrive, call me.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|4|6
|passage=وَٱبْتَلُوا ٱلْيَتَامَى حَتَّى إِذَا بَلَغُوا ٱلنِّكَاحَ فَإِنْ آنَسْتُم مِّنْهُمْ رُشْدًا فَٱدْفَعُوا إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوَالَهُمْ وَلَا تَأْكُلُوهَا إِسْرَافًا وَبِدَارًا أَن يَكْبَرُوا وَمَن كَانَ غَنِيًّا فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ وَمَن كَانَ فَقِيرًا فَلْيَأْكُلْ بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ فَ'''إِذَا''' دَفَعْتُمْ إِلَيْهِمْ أَمْوَالَهُمْ فَأَشْهِدُوا عَلَيْهِمْ وَكَفَى بِٱللَّهِ حَسِيبًا
|t=And examine the orphans till they seem able to bear intercourse. If you sense prudence from them, pass their money to them, and do not eat it extravangantly nor hastily before their growing up. Whoever is rich should abstain, and whoever is poor may eat [from it] as is custom. And '''when''' you pass them the money, summon someone to be a witness against them. It is Allah who is the Reckoner [and who counts your deeds].
|subst=وَٱبْتَلُوا/وَ-ٱبْتَلُوا,فَإِنْ/فَ-إِنْ,فَٱدْفَعُوا/فَ-ٱدْفَعُوا,وَلَا/وَ-لَا,وَبِدَارًا/وَ-بِدَارًا,وَمَن/وَ-مَن,فَلْيَسْتَعْفِفْ/فَلْ-يَسْتَعْفِفْ,فَلْيَأْكُلْ/فَلْ-يَأْكُلْ,بِٱلْمَعْرُوفِ/بِ-ٱلْمَعْرُوفِ,فَ'''إِذَا'''/فَ-'''إِذَا''',فَأَشْهِدُوا/فَ-أَشْهِدُوا,وَكَفَى/وَ-كَفَى,بِٱللَّهِ/بِ-لَّهِ}}
#* {{quote-song|ar
|lyricist=أَبُو ٱلْقَاسِمِ ٱلشَّابِيّ;مُصْطَفَى صَادِق الرَّافِعِي
|composer=مُحَمَّد عَبْدُ ٱلْوَهَّاب
|title=حُمَاةَ ٱلْحِمَى
|year=1930s
|passage='''إِذَا''' الشَّعْبُ يَوْمًا أَرَادَ الْحَيَاة / فَلَا بُدَّ أَنْ يَسْتَجِيبَ الْقَدَر
|t=When a prideful people wills to live, / Destiny itself will grant their wish.
|subst=فَلَا/فَ-لَا}}
# {{lb|ar|indicates perception, as of a sudden or concurrent action}} {{qualifier|with {{m|ar|فَ|t=then}}}} [[and]] [[then]], [[and]]; [[thereupon]], [[whereupon]]; [[when]] [[behold]], [[then]] [[behold]]
#: {{ux|ar|خَرَجْتُ فَ'''إِذَا''' الْمَطَرُ يَنْهَمِرُ|t=I went out, '''and''' the rain was pouring.|subst=فَ'''إِذَا'''/فَ-'''إِذَا'''}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|117
|passage=وَأَوْحَيْنَا إِلَى مُوسَى أَنْ أَلْقِ عَصَاكَ فَ'''إِذَا''' هِيَ تَلْقَفُ مَا يَأْفِكُونَ
|t=And We inspired Moses [and said,] "Cast your staff", '''whereupon''' it devoured what they were forging.
|subst=وَ/وَ-,فَ/فَ-}}

=====Usage notes=====
* When ''iḏā'' is used as the conditional particle in a conditional clause, it may be followed by a past-tense verb regardless of natural time-reference.
* As a particle of surprise the verb that follows is typically found in the present/non-past tense despite having a past-tense sense; most often used in storytelling or relating events, announcing an event or occurrence that follows after another, a sequence.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|إِذَا مَا|t=when; whenever}}

