Page 1714 إزار: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Spiridon louis.jpg|thumb|right|{{senseno|ar|skirt}}]]
[[File:Achan-dhoti-tipu-sultan-fort.jpg|thumb|right|{{senseno|ar|skirt}}]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إِزَارَة}}

===Etymology===
Similar to the root {{ar-root|ء س ر|nocat=1}}, whence also {{m|ar|إِسَار|t=strap}}, but perhaps more closely via {{bor|ar|arc|אזרא|tr=ʾizārā}}, {{m|arc|איזרא}} / {{m|syc|ܐܝܙܪܐ|tr=ʾīzārā|t=a kind of wide belt as a garment}} from a root cognate to {{cog|ar|عَزَرَ|t=to withhold, to restrain}}, as it derives best in {{der|ar|he|אָזַר|tr=ʾāzar|t=to press, to trouble; to be a pressing pain to, to wound, to besiege etc.; to bind, to gird}}, forming {{cog|he|אֵיזֹור}}, {{m|he|אֵזֹור|tr=ʾēzōr|t=girdle, belt}}, in which shape it has been borrowed into {{cog|jpa|אֵיזֹורא}}, {{m|he|אֵזֹורא|tr=ʾēzōrā|t=girdle, belt}}. Hardly thus another clothing term from {{cog|hyx-pro|-}} but more likely coincidentally similar to {{noncog|xcl|եզր|t=edge of a cloth, end}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِزَار}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِزَار|m|g2=f|pl=أُزُر|pl2=آزِرَة}}

# {{senseid|ar|skirt}} an [[item]] of [[menswear]] [[make up|made up]] of a [[piece]] of [[cloth]] that is [[wrap]]ped around the [[lower]] [[body]]; a [[man|men]]'s [[skirt]] (such as a [[kilt]] or a [[sarong]])
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|20|25-35|
passage=قَالَ رَبِّ ٱشْرَحْ لِي صَدْرِي 25 وَيَسِّرْ لِي أَمْرِي 26 وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِنْ لِسَانِي 27 يَفْقَهُوا قَوْلِي 28 وَاجْعَلْ لِي وَزِيرًا مِنْ أَهْلِي 29 هَارُونَ أَخِي 30 اُشْدُدْ بِهِ '''أَزْرِي''' 31 وَأَشْرِكْهُ فِي أَمْرِي 32 كَيْ نُسَبِّحَكَ كَثِيرًا 33 وَنَذْكُرَكَ كَثِيرًا 34 إِنَّكَ كُنْتَ بِنَا بَصِيرًا 35
|t=25 He said, "My Lord, clear out my chest, 26 and ease my affairs, 27 and loosen the knot in my tongue 28 so that they may understand my words, 29 and name a councilor for me, from my own people: 30 Aaron, my brother. 31 Fasten up '''my skirt''' with him, 32 and split up my powers with him 33 so that we can praise You, again and again, 34 and remember and speak of You, again and again. 35 You have been ever-watchful of us."}}
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} [[robe]]s
#: {{syn|ar|جِلْبَاب|مِلْحَفَة}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِزَار|pl=أُزُر|pl2=آزِرَة}}

