Page 1777 إسكدنيا: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إِسْكِيدُنْيَا|إِكِّدُنْيَا|أَكِدُنْيَا|إِيكِّيدُنْيَا|إِكِّيدُنْيَا}}, and written apart

===Etymology===
Paradoxically, it is not called in {{cog|tr||**eski dünya}} but {{m|tr|yeni dünya}} / {{m|ota|یڭی دنیا}} (a meaning also widespread in the {{noncog|ar|يَنْكِي دُنْيَا|tr=yangī dunyā}} by the middle of the twentieth century). In {{m|ar|إِسْكِدُنْيَا}}, the first half is in fact the {{der|ar|fa|-}} borrowing {{m|ota|ازگیل}} / {{m|tr|ezgil|t=medlar}}. And the second half also, {{m|ota|دنیا}} / {{m|tr|dünya|t=world}} being a reinterpretation of {{m|ota|دنگل|tr=döngel, düngel|t=medlar}}, which is the same word blended with the stem of {{m|ota|دونمك}} / {{m|tr|dönmek|t=to turn around}} based on the fruit’s round form.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِسْكِدُنْيَا|f}}

# [[medlar]], [[loquat]] and what looks like it of fruits and fruit-trees
#: {{syn|ar|مُشْمُلَة}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِسْكِدُنْيَا}}

[[Category:Iraqi Arabic]]
[[Category:Syrian Arabic]]
{{C|ar|Pome fruits}}
-------- end text --------
