Page 1800 إشبين: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|شَبِين|شِبِين}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܫܰܘܫܒܺܝܢܳܐ|tr=šawšəḇīnā}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒋢𒊓𒁉𒉡|ts=susapinnu|t=paranymph, friend of the bridegroom in a wedding ceremony}}, also a foreign word, structure suggesting Anatolian, but strangely attested in {{noncog|hit|-}} as an {{l|en|Akkadogram}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِشْبِين}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِشْبِين|m|pl=أَشَابِين|f=إِشْبِينَة}} <!-- is إِشْبِين f also? Example إِشْبِين is Queen Victoria -->

# somebody who is adduced as a witness to a [[baptism]], [[godfather]], [[baptismal]] [[sponsor]]
# somebody who is adduced as a witness to a [[wedding]], [[bridesman]], [[groomsman]], [[paranymph]]
#* {{quote-web|ar|title=ar:من بينهم كلبها.. المرشحون للقيام بدور أشبين لميغان ماركل|date=2018-05-17|work=BBC Arabic|url=http://www.bbc.com/arabic/world-44156692|passage=إنها الملكة فيكتوريا التي قامت بدور الإشبين لاثنتين من بناتها الأميرة هيلينا عام 1866 والأميرة بياتريس عام 1885 عقب وفاة زوجها الأمير ألبرت.|t=It was the Queen Victoria who slipped into the role of a bridesmaid for her two daughters Princesses Helena in the year 1866 and Beatrice in the year 1885 after the death of her husband Prince Albert.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|إِشْبِين|pl=أَشَابِين}}

