===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܫܰܘܫܒܺܝܢܬܴܐ|tr=šawšəḇīntā}}, developed as the feminine form of {{bor|ar|syc|ܫܰܘܫܒܺܝܢܳܐ|tr=šawšəḇīnā}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒋢𒊓𒁉𒉡|ts=susapinnu|t=paranymph, friend of the bridegroom in a wedding ceremony}}, not attested with feminine equivalent. Ultimately a foreign word, structure suggesting Anatolian, but strangely attested in {{noncog|hit|-}} as an {{l|en|Akkadogram}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِشْبِينَة}}

===Noun===
