Page 1813 إشقيل: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إسْقِيل}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|grc|σκίλλα}}. Perhaps more often rendered by {{m|ar|ش}} in Arabic, otherwise rare in Greek borrowings save for historical {{w|Laminal consonant|laminal}} {{IPAchar|/s/}} pronunciation in {{cog|VL.|-}} or {{cog|roa|-}} engendering it, because in {{bor|ar|syc|-}} in which the word had spread earlier it had {{m|syc|ܣ|tr=s}} which corresponds in inherited cognates to {{noncog|sem-pro||*ś}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إشْقِيل|m}}

# [[squill]] ({{taxfmt|Drimia maritima|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|عُنْصُل|بَصَل الفَأْر}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إشْقِيل}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|he-med|אישקיל|bor=1|tr=ʾišqī́l}}

===References===
* {{RQ:Ibn Janāḥ:2020|page=242|section=35 (fol. 6r,10–13)|lang=en|instead=1}} say that as the Syriac forms all have {{bor|ar|syc|ܣ|tr=s}}, the form {{m|ar|إسْقِيل}} is “more correct”, which only makes sense if one grants that it was assumed from Syriac by {{w|Graeco-Arabic translation movement|Syriac medicine truchmen}}.
* {{R:ar:Maimonides|page=33 Nr. 60}}

{{C|ar|Asparagus family plants}}
