From {{bor|ar|arc|אַקְלִידָא}} / {{m|syc|ܐܩܠܝܕܐ|tr=ʾaqlīdā|t=key}} from {{der|ar|grc|κλεῖδα}}, accusative singular of {{m|grc|κλείς|t=key}}, from {{der|ar|ine-pro|*kleh₂us|t=nail, pin, hook – instruments of old use for locking doors}}, from the root {{m|ine-pro|*(s)kleh₂w-}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِقْلِيد|m|pl=أَقَالِيد}} {{tlb|ar|Ḥaḍramawt}}

# [[key]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|64|86
|passage=فَدَخَلْتُ فَكَمَنْتُ، فَلَمَّا دَخَلَ النَّاسُ أَغْلَقَ الْبَابَ، ثُمَّ عَلَّقَ الأَغَالِيقَ عَلَى وَتَدٍ قَالَ فَقُمْتُ إِلَى الأَقَالِيدِ، فَأَخَذْتُهَا فَفَتَحْتُ الْبَابَ.
|translation=So I went in (the castle) and hid myself. When the people got inside, the gate-keeper closed the gate and hung the keys on a fixed wooden peg. I got up and took the keys and opened the gate.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِقْلِيد|pl=أَقَالِيد}}

