Page 1943 إلا: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|Illa (Arabic)|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|gez|አላ|tr=ʾälla}}, {{cog|he|אֶלָּא|tr=ʾellā}}.

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|إِلَّا}}

# {{lb|ar|in affirmatives and rhetorical questions}} [[except]] ([[except for|for]]), [[save]] ([[save for|for]]), [[but]] ([[but for|for]]), [[bar]]ring; [[other than]], [[besides]], [[apart from]]
#: {{ux|ar|رَأَيْتُهُمْ جَمِيعًا '''إِلّا''' إِيَّاكَ.|t=I could see them all '''except''' you.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|21|22|passage=لَوْ كَانَ فِيهِمَا ءَالِهَةٌ '''إِلَّا''' ٱللَّهُ لَفَسَدَتَا فَسُبْحَـٰنَ ٱللَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَرْشِ عَمَّا يَصِفُونَ|t=Had there been within them [i.e., the heavens and earth] any gods '''besides''' Allāh, they both would have been ruined. So exalted is Allāh, the Lord of the Throne, above what they describe.}}
# {{lb|ar|in negatives}} no more than; nothing more than; nothing but or no one but; [[only]], [[but]]
#: {{ux|ar|[[صحة|الصِّحَّةُ]] [[تَاجٌ]] [[عَلَى]] [[رأس|رُؤُوسِ]] [[صحيح|الْأَصِحَّاءِ]] [[لَا]] [[رأى|يَرَاهُ]] '''إِلَّا''' [[مريض|الْمَرْضَى]].|Health is a crown that is on the heads of the healthy, which '''only''' the ill can see.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|81|27|passage=إِنْ هُوَ إِلاَّ ذِكْرٌ لِّلْعَالَمِينَ 27 لِمَن شَاء مِنكُمْ أَن يَسْتَقِيمَ 28 وَمَا تَشَاؤُونَ إِلاَّ أَن يَشَاء اللَّهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِينَ 29|t=27 This is '''but''' a reminder to the worlds, 28 to those of you who wish to straighten out themselves, 29 and you never wish it '''except''' when God wishes it, the Lord of the Worlds.}}

====Usage notes====
When the sentence is positive, the excluded noun is always accusative.
#: {{ux|ar|نَجَحَ ٱلطُّلَّابُ '''إِلَّا''' ٱلْكَسْلَانَ.|The students succeeded '''except for''' the lazy ones.}}
When the sentence is negative, the excluded noun can be accusative or it can follow the declension of the included noun as it behaves as a substitute for it.
#: {{ux|ar|مَا فَشِلَ ٱلطُّلَّابُ '''إِلَّا''' ٱلْكَسْلَانَ / ٱلْكَسْلَانُ.|The students didn't fail '''except for''' the lazy ones.}}
#: {{ux|ar|لَا آكُلُ ٱلْفَوَاكِهَ '''إِلَّا''' تُفَّاحًا.|I don't eat fruit '''except for''' apples.}}
#: {{ux|ar|لَنْ أَذْهَبَ لِأَيِّ أَصْدِقَاءٍ '''إِلَّا''' مُحَمَّدًا / مُحَمَّدٍ.|I won't get to any friends '''except for''' Muhammad.}}
When the excluded noun isn't a member of the included group, it's always accusative.
#: {{ux|ar|جَاءَ ٱلْمُسَافِرُونَ '''إِلَّا''' حَقَائِبَهُمْ.|The passengers arrived '''without''' their luggage.}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا حَضَرَ ٱللَّاعِبُونَ '''إِلَّا''' ٱلْمُدَرِّبَ.|The players didn't come but their trainer did.}}
In negative sentences, the included noun can sometimes be omitted. Then the noun following {{m|ar|إِلَّا}} has to be in the case that the included noun would have had if it had been mentioned, as it behaves as a substitute for it.
#: {{ux|ar|مَا كَتَبَ ٱلْوَاجِبَ '''إِلَّا''' طَالِبٌ.|Nobody wrote the homework except for one student.}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا كَتَبَ ٱلطَّالِبُ '''إِلَّا''' وَاجِبَهُ.|The student wrote nothing except for his homework.}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا كَتَبَ ٱلطَّالِبُ '''إِلَّا''' بِقَلَمِهِ.|The student wrote with nothing except for his pen.}}
If we mention the included noun, the excluded noun can follow its declension or it can be accusative.
#: {{ux|ar|مَا كَتَبَ ٱلْوَاجِبَ أَيُّ طُلَّابٍ '''إِلَّا''' طَالِبٌ / '''إِلَّا''' طَالِبًا.|No student wrote the homework except for one.}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا كَتَبَ ٱلطَّالِبُ أَيَّ وَاجِبٍ '''إِلَّا''' وَاجِبَهُ.|The student wrote no homework except for his one.}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا كَتَبَ ٱلطَّالِبُ بِأَيِّ قَلَمٍ '''إِلَّا''' بِقَلَمِهِ / '''إِلَّا''' قَلَمَهُ.|The student wrote with no pen except for his one.}}

====Derived terms====
