===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إِلَاه}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ʾil-}} with a vocative suffix {{m|ar|ـَاه}} which is else only sporadically attested in Arabic but has left its trace in the -ā vocatives of {{m|ar|أَب|t=father}}, {{m|ar|أَخ|t=brother}}, {{m|ar|حَم|t=father-in-law}}. Forms a root {{ar-root|ء|ل|ه}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِلَاهْ}}
** Egypt: {{IPA|ar|[ʔeˈlæːh]}}
** Levant: {{IPA|ar|[ʔɪˈlaːh]}}
** Central Arabia: {{IPA|ar|[ʔɪˈlæːh]}}
** Hijazi: {{IPA|acw|[ʔɪˈlaːh]}}
** Persian Gulf: {{IPA|ar|[ʔɪˈlɑːh]}}
** Tunisia: {{IPA|ar|[ʔiˈlɛːh]}}
** Algeria: {{IPA|ar|[ʔiˈlæːh]}}
** Morocco: {{IPA|ar|[ʔiˈlæːh]}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|إِلٰه|m|f=إِلٰهَة|pl=آلِهَة}} {{tlb|ar|countable}}

# the [[God]], the [[Deity]], the [[Divinity]]
#: {{syn|ar|رَبّ|t=Lord; Master}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|28|88|text=وَلَا تَدْعُ مَعَ اللَّٰهِ '''إِلَٰهًا''' آخَرَ&nbsp;ۘ لَا '''إِلَٰهَ''' إِلَّا هُوَ|subst=آخَرَ&nbsp;ۘ لَا/آخَرَ لَا|t=And do not call upon another '''God''' beside Allah: there is no '''God''' but He.}}

