Page 1998 إمر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|yl}}
From {{bor|ar|arc|אִימְּרָא}} / {{m|arc|אִמְּרָא|tr=ʾimmərā}} / {{m|syc|ܐܶܡܪܳܐ|tr=ʾemmərā|t=lamb}}, absolute state {{m|arc|אִימַּר}} / {{m|arc|אִמַּר|tr=ʾimmar}} / {{m|syc|ܐܶܡܱܪ|tr=ʾemmar}}, from {{der|ar|akk|immerum|𒇻|tr=immerum|t=sheep}}. Note also an Aramaic diminutive having been borrowed as {{m+|ar|عَمْرُوسَة|t=small lamb}}, and the transferred semantics being mirrored in {{cog|xcl|յիմար|t=foolish}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|إِمَّر|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{C|ar|Baby animals|Sheep}} [[lamb]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|إِمَّر}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|إِمَّر}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[simple-minded]], [[stupid]]
#: {{synonyms|ar|إِمَّع|إِمَّعَة}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|إِمَّر|f=إِمَّر|pl=إِمَّر|fpl=إِمَّر|d=إِمَّر:tri|fd=إِمَّر:tri}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|إِمَّرَة}}

====References====
{{rel-top|click to expand}}
* {{R:ar:BehnstedtWoidich|WA1|pages=255–263}}, survey that the word survives in no dialect, shewing its peripheral origin.
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=58b}}
* {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|page=237}}, declares it Aramaic due to the form and supposed lacking of the word in old sources.
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=2|pages=7–9, Nr. 5|entry=*ˀimmar-|id=363}}, reconstruct with little extra-Semitic cognates {{noncog|afa-pro|-}}, themselves noting that {{cog|phn|𐤀𐤌𐤓}} occurs but in a text “showing a number of features often regarded as Aramaic”, and that {{cog|uga|𐎛𐎎𐎗}} is “poetic”. {{cog|he|אׅמַּר|tr=ʾimmar}} or {{m|he|אׅמֵּר|tr=ʾimmēr}} referenced on a dozen of places in Koehler-Baumgartner with left-open vocalization may or may not occur, having a lot of homonyms, but the tendency of transmission to corrupt any occurrence would be evidence that it is another “poetic” word unknown to the {{cog|hbo|-}} vernacular, i.e. an educated Aramaic borrowing into Hebrew. Lastly, the loan permeation may be illustrated by {{cog|eu|umerri|t=lamb}}.
* {{R:sem:Nöldeke:1879|pages=1261–1262}}, declares it native due to a place-name {{m|ar|إِمَّرَة}} and the occurrence in {{w|Imru' al-Qais|Imruʾ al-Qays}} (of whose poems lots of forgeries exist).
* {{R:Nöldeke:Beitr.|page=83}}
* {{R:akk:Zimmern|page=50}}
{{rel-bottom}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ar|affl}}
{{ar-rootbox|ء م ر}}

