Page 2010 إن شاء الرب وعشنا: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Literally: “If the Lord wills it and we’re in life”, based on [[w:Epistle of James|James]] 4:15.

===Interjection===
{{head|ar|interjection|head=[[إنْ]] [[شاءَ]] اَل[[رَّبُّ]] وَ[[عِشْنَا]]}}

# {{lb|ar|Christianity}} [[God willing]]

====Usage notes====
* This phrase is markedly religious, unlike {{m|ar|إنْ شاءَ اللهُ}}, which is commonly used by all Arabic speakers regardless of their beliefs.
-------- end text --------
Page 2011 إن شاء الله: -------- begin text --------
{{phrasebook|ar}}
{{wikipedia|insha'Allah}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|إِنْ شَاءَ ٱللٰه|إِنْ شَاءَ ٱللٰهُ}}

===Interjection===
{{ar-interj|[[إِنْ]] [[شَاءَ]] [[ٱللّٰهُ]]}}

# [[God willing]]; [[inshallah]], if it is God’s will (literally, “if God has willed [it]”)
#: {{ux|ar|سَأَزُوْرُ أَقَارِبِي فِي مَدِينَةِ الرِّيَاضِ هَذَا الصَّيْفَ، '''إِنْ شَاءَ اللَّهُ'''.|I will visit my relatives in Riyadh this summer, '''God willing'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|37|102|passage=فَلَمَّا بَلَغَ مَعَهُ ٱلسَّعْيَ قَالَ يَا بُنَيَّ إِنِّي أَرَى فِي ٱلْمَنَامِ أَنِّي أَذْبَحُكَ فَٱنْظُرْ مَاذَا تَرَى قَالَ يَا أَبَتِ ٱفْعَلْ مَا تُؤْمَرُ سَتَجِدُنِي '''إِنْ شَاءَ اللّٰهُ''' مِنَ ٱلصَّابِرِينَ|t=When he was old enough to assist in his endeavour, he said, "My son! I see in dreams that I am sacrificing you. See what you think." He said, "Father! Do whatever you have been commanded. '''If God wishes''', you will find me to be patient."}}
# it is to be hoped; I hope; we hope so; [[hopefully]]

====Related terms====
