Page 2145 ا: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{ar-IPA|أَلِفْ}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{ar-IPA|أ}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ا''' / '''‍ا'''|tr=ʔalif}}
[[File:1 ﺍ 'álif.svg|thumb]]

# Although usually considered to be the first letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet, the small [[hamza]] ({{l|ar|ء}}) that sits on top of {{l|ar|أ}} is really the first letter of the Arabic alphabet, and the tall column is its bearer. This entry only deals with the lower part, the bearer, which is called {{l|ar|أَلِف}} and, without the hamza, is used to lengthen a preceding [[a]].

====Descendants====
* {{desc|nqo|ߊ|sc=Nkoo}}

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|tr=ʔalif}}

# The first letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is followed by {{l|ar|ب}}.
{{ArabForm2}}

===Pronunciation===
'''After [[fatha]]:'''
{{lang|ar|ـَا}} — {{IPA|ar|/aː/}}
:* {{l|ar|عَار|gloss=[[shame]]}}

'''Combined with [[fatha]]:'''
{{lang|ar|اَ}} — {{IPA|ar|/ʔa/}}
:* {{l|ar|اَلْيَوْمَ|gloss=[[today]]}}

'''Combined with [[kasra]]:'''
{{lang|ar|اِ}} — {{IPA|ar|/ʔi/}}
:* {{l|ar|اِبْن|gloss=[[son]]}}

'''Combined with [[damma]]:'''
{{lang|ar|اُ}} — {{IPA|ar|/ʔu/}}
:* {{l|ar|اُكْتُبْ|gloss=[[write]]}}

