Page 3008 اصطخم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ص خ م}} related to scorching by sun, see {{m|ar|صَخَمَ}}. Classical Arabic dictionaries define it as "to stand upright", also adding "silent as if angry", and Lane cites them.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|اِصْطَخَمَ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|VIII.nopass}} {{tlb|ar|classical|obsolete}}

# {{def-uncertain|ar}}
## to be [[burnt]] by the sun, to take [[sunbath]]
##: {{quote-book|ar|year=c. 7th century|author=Kaʿb bin Zuhair|title=Qasīdat al-Burdah (Bānat Suʿād), some versions|text=يَوْماً يَظَلُّ بِهِ الحِرْبَاءُ مُصْطَخِماً // كَأَنَّ ضَاحِيَهُ بِالنَارِ مَمْلُول|t=The day a chameleon gets ''muṣṭaḵim'' // as if his sunward side is burnt by fire}}
#: {{syn|ar|اِصْطَخَدَ|q=used in other versions of this line}}
## to [[stand]] [[upright]] ''(and [[silent]], as if [[angry]])''
##: {{quote-book|ar|year=c. 7th century|author=Al-ʿUdayl bin Al-Farḵ Al-ʿIjliyy|title=A-lā man lihammin|text=إِذَا مَا تَوَقَّلَ حِرْبَاؤُهَا // عَلَى الْجِذْلِ ثُمَّ نَمَا وَاصْطَخَمْ}}
