Page 3210 الأردن: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From [[w:Jund_al-Urdunn|{{l|ar||جُنْد الْأُرْدُنّ}}]], “the military district of Jordan”, probably straight out borrowed from the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} isolect spoken there at the time, attested by the written {{cog|tmr|-}} and {{cog|arc-jla|-}} as {{m|arc|יֹורְדְּנא|tr=yordənā}} and {{m|arc|יַרְדְּנא|tr=yardənā}}. Both forms give the present Arabic one regularly: The [[emphatic state]] ending was rendered by the Arabic article, and the distinction of the onset consonants {{IPAchar|/j/}}, {{IPAchar|/ʔ/}} and {{IPAchar|/ʕ/}} either had already little [[functional load]], in the same fashion as the etyma of {{m|ar|هُود}}, {{m|ar|يَافُوخ}}, {{m|ar|يَلَب}}, {{m|ar|الْعِرَاق}} etc., or the onset {{m|ar||يُـ}} or the pattern of {{m|ar||*يَرْدُن}} or {{m|ar||*أَرْدُن}} in Arabic was hardly admissible and had to be regularized, that is classicized. See {{cog|he|יַרְדֵּן|tr=yardén}} for the ultimate derivation of the toponym.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الْأُرْدُن|الْأُرْدُنّ}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|الْأُرْدُن|head2=الْأُرْدُنّ|m}}

# {{transclude sense|ar|Jordan|id=Q810}}
#: {{ux|ar|الْأُرْدُنُ مُحَاطَةٌ مِنَ الشَّمَالِ بِسُورِيَا، مِنَ الْغَرْبِ بِفِلَسْطِينَ، وَمِنَ الشَّرْقِ بِالْعِرَاقِ، وَمِنَ الشَّرْقِ وَالْجَنُوبِ بِالْمَمْلَكَةِ الْعَرَبِيَّةِ السُّعُودِيَّةِ.|Jordan is surrounded from the north by Syria, from the west by Palestine, from the east by Iraq, and from the east and south by the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.}}
# {{transclude sense|ar|Jordan|id=Q40059}}
#* {{quote-song|ar
|title=زَهْرَة الْمَدَائِن
|trans-title={{w|Zahrat al-Mada'en|Flower of Cities}}
|year=1967
|artist=w:Fairuz
|lyricist=w:Said Akl
|composer=w:Rahbani brothers
|text=وَسَتَغْسِلُ يَا نَهْرَ '''ٱلْأُرْدُنِ''' وَجْهِي بِمِيَاهٍ قُدْسِيَّة<br/>وَسَتَمْحُو يَا نَهْرَ '''ٱلْأُرْدُنِ''' آثَارَ ٱلْقَدَمِ ٱلْهَمَجِيَّة
|t=And ye, o '''Jordan''' river, will wash my face with water of holiness;<br/>And ye, o '''Jordan''' river, will erase the traces of the barbaric feet.
|url=https://youtu.be/XryCNk6q4KM}}<!---translation based on Stone, Christopher (2008), "Fayruz, the Rahbani Brothers, Jerusalem, and the Leba-stinian song" in Jerusalem: Idea and Reality Mayer & Mourad (eds.), p. 159-160--->

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|أُرْدُن|head2=أُرْدُنّ|state=def}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|ar|أُرْدُنِيّ//أُرْدُنِّيّ}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|أردن}}
* {{R:CAL|yrdn|N}}
* {{R:CAL|ywrdnn|N}}

