Page 3322 الجزائر: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
The broken plural of {{m|ar|جَزِيرَة||island}} has come to be the proper name for Algeria, its capital, and the islands in its bay, as there were once several small islands in the Bay of Algiers. Most of these islands are now connected to the shore or have been removed. {{m|ar|جزائر|الْجَزَائِر}} is itself a truncated form of the city's older name of {{m|ar|جَزَائِر بَنِي مَزْغَنَّى||the islands of (the tribe) Ait Mazghanna}}, which was used by early medieval geographers such as {{w|Muhammad al-Idrisi}} and {{w|Yaqut al-Hamawi}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الْجَزَائِر}}
** {{IPA|arq|/(ɪ)d.dzaː.jir/|a=Algerian}}
** {{a|ar|Moroccan}} {{ary-IPA|(e)l.jazāʔir|(e)l.jazāyir}}
* {{audio|ar|LL-Q13955 (ara)-Reda Kerbouche-الجزائر.wav}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|الْجَزَائِر|f-p}}

# {{tcl|ar|Algeria|id=Q262}}
# {{tcl|ar|Algiers|id=Q3561}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَزَائِر|state=def}}

