===Etymology===
{{bor|ar|gez|ሐበሠት}}, only attested in [[Aksumite]] inscriptions, later replaced with e.g. {{m|gez|ብሔረ ግዕዝ|tr=bəḥerä gəʿz}}, {{m|gez|ብሔረ አግዓዝ}} and the {{cog|grc|-}} [[exonym]] {{m|gez|ኢትዮጵያ}}; originally also meaning both sides of the Red Sea (which {{w|Kingdom of Aksum|Aksum}} colonized). To its dominion then {{bor|ar|sem-srb|𐩢𐩨𐩦𐩩|tr=ḥbs²t}} referred. In {{der|ar|egy|-}} the inhabitants of [[Punt]] were repeatedly called {{m|egy|ḫbzty|ḫbztyw}}, {{m|egy|ḫbsty|ḫbstyw}}, interpreted as from {{m|egy|ḫbs}}, {{m|egy|ḫbz}}, {{m|egy|ḫbzwt|t=beard}}, however the moniker’s status as an actual [[demonym]] instead of just meaning literally “bearded ones” is doubtful, as well as the capability of the Egyptians to impose their term upon Aksum to be her endonym, for it to become the copiously attested {{cog|xsa|𐩢𐩨𐩦𐩩|ts=ḥabaśatu}} and {{m|xsa|𐩱𐩢𐩨𐩦|ts=ʾaḥbūśu|t=Abyssinians}} too. Possibly originally referring to an emigrated Yemenite tribe, reflected in the (now Saudi) toponyms {{m|ar|وَادِي حَبُوش}} and {{m|ar|جَبَل حُبَيْش}} as well as {{m|ar|جَبَل حَبَشِيّ}} whose residents are called {{m|ar|الْأَحْبُش}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|اَلْحَبَشَة}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|اَلْحَبَشَة|f}}

# {{lb|ar|historical}} [[Abyssinia]] {{gloss|former name of Ethiopia}}
#: {{syn|ar|إِثْيُوبْيَا}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَبَشَة|state=def}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|حَبَشِيّ}}
* {{l|ar|حَبَشَ|t=to earn, to obtain for the household}}
* {{l|ar|دِيك الْحَبَش|t=turkey}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|gez|ሐበሽ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ms|Habsyah|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|حَبَشه|tr=habaše|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:egy:Breyer:2016|pages=530 seqq.}}
* {{R:egy:Cooper:2020|pages=77 seqq.}}
-------- end text --------
