Page 3378 الذي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
An innovation in Arabic, formed from {{af|ar|اَل|لَ|ذِي|t1=the|t2=truly|t3=this}}. Compare {{cog|hbo|הלזה|tr=hallāze|t=this, that}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|اَلَّذِي}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-الذي.ogg}}

===Pronoun===
{{ar-pron|اَلَّذِي|m|f=اَلَّتِي}}

# {{lb|ar|relative pronoun}} [[who]], [[that]], [[which]]
#* {{Q|ar|year=10th century|[[w:Al-Mutanabbi|Al-Mutanabbi]]|quote=أَنَا '''الَّذِي''' نَظَرَ الْأَعْمَى إِلَى أَدَبِي <br> وَأَسْمَعَتْ كَلِمَاتِي مَنْ بِهِ صَمَمُ|t=I am '''he''' whose set-down verse the blind have seen, <br> whose words and rhymes have echoed in unhearing ears!|subst=وَ//وَ-}}

====Usage notes====
Although used similarly to the relative pronouns of the modern Germanic and Romance languages, it may be worth noting that "relative clauses" in Arabic are structurally identical to [[w:Nominal sentence|"nominal" (or zero-copula) sentences]] and "verbal" sentences with fronted nouns. Thus, when the relative pronoun is the object of a verb or a preposition, a pronominal clitic that references and agrees with the "relative pronoun" in gender and number is added '''after''' the respective verb or preposition while the relative pronoun itself remains at the beginning of the clause, though the addition of clitics after verbs and participles is optional (just as when nouns in verbal sentences are fronted).

# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا هُوَ الرَّجُلُ الَّذِي رَأَيْتُ|This is the man I saw.|lit=This is the man that I saw}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا هُوَ الرَّجُلُ الَّذِي رَأَيْتُهُ|This is the man I saw.|lit=This is the man that I saw him}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا هُوَ الصُّنْدُوقُ الَّذِي فِيهِ الْكِتَابُ|This is the box that the book is in.|lit=This is the box that in it is the book}}
# {{uxi|ar|تِلْكَ هِيَ الْوَرَقَةُ الَّتِي كَتَبْتُ عَلَيْهَا|This is the paper on which I wrote.|lit=This is the paper that I wrote on it}}

This is also the case in fused (or nominal) relative clauses.

# {{uxi|ar|فَٱقْضِ مَا أَنْتَ قَاضٍ|So judge as you will.|lit=So ordain what[ever] you [are] ordaining|subst=فَٱقْضِ/فَ-ٱقْضِ}}

Syntactically, this differs from, for example, English, where relative pronouns replace nouns (as in [[that]], [[which]], [[who]], and [[whom]]) and determiners (as in [[whose]] and [[which]]) in the relative clause. Hence, relative pronouns are classified in traditional Arabic grammar as a subcategory of nouns. In linguistics, such a clitic is often termed a {{m|en|resumptive pronoun}}, whose addition in the relative clause is also a feature of Hebrew (for which see the usage notes in the entry for {{m|he|אשר}}).

If the antecedent is indefinite, the relative pronoun is obligatorily omitted, regardless of the structure of the relative clause.

# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا هُوَ الرَّجُلُ الَّذِي يَبِيعُ كُتُبًا كَثِيرَةً|This is the man who sells a lot of books.|lit=This is the man that sells many books}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا رَجُلٌ يَبِيعُ كُتُبًا كَثِيرَةً|This is a man who sells a lot of books.|lit=This [is] a man sells many books}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا هُوَ الرَّجُلُ الَّذِي شَعْرُهُ طَوِيلٌ|This is the man whose hair is long.|lit=This is the man that his hair [is] long}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰذَا رَجُلٌ شَعْرُهُ طَوِيلٌ|This is a man whose hair is long.|lit=This [is] a man his hair [is] long}}

If the relative clause includes a predicative adjective qualifying an attribute of the antecedent or another referent related to or associated with it, the adjective may be moved to the front of the clause, in which case the relative pronoun is obligatorily omitted. The adjective also becomes perpetually in the singular unless the attribute or related referent is a broken plural, in which case the adjective may be pluralized, though this is relatively uncommon and some traditional grammarians criticize it. In its new position, the adjective agrees with the '''antecedent''' in '''case''' and '''definiteness''' and with the '''noun denoting the attribute or associated referent''' in '''gender'''.

# {{uxi|ar|رَأَيْتُ رَجُلًا طَوِيلًا شَعْرُهُ|I saw a man whose hair is long.|lit=I saw a man long {{q|{{abbr|indef|indefinite}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|acc|accusative}}}} [is] his hair}}
# {{uxi|ar|رَأَيْتُ الرَّجُلَ الطَّوِيلَ شَعْرُهُ|I saw the man whose hair is long.|lit=I saw the man long {{q|{{abbr|def|definite}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|acc|accusative}}}} [is] his hair}}
# {{uxi|ar|رَأَيْتُ ٱمْرَأَةً طَوِيلًا شَعْرُهَا|I saw a woman whose hair is long.|lit=I saw a woman long {{q|{{abbr|indef|indefinite}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|acc|accusative}}}} [is] her hair}}
# {{uxi|ar|رَأَيْتُ الْمَرْأَةَ الطَّوِيلَ شَعْرُهَا|I saw the woman whose hair is long.|lit=I saw the woman long {{q|{{abbr|def|definite}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|acc|accusative}}}} [is] her hair}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰؤُلَاءِ رِجَالٌ طَوِيلٌ شَعْرُهُمْ|These are men with long hair.|lit=These [are] men long {{q|{{abbr|indef|indefinite}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|nom|nominative}}}} [is] their hair}}
# {{uxi|ar|هٰؤُلَاءِ نِسَاءٌ طَوِيلٌ شَعْرُهُنَّ|These are women with long hair.|lit=These [are] women long {{q|{{abbr|indef|indefinite}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|nom|nominative}}}} [is] their hair}}
# {{uxi|ar|وَقَفَ الْعُصْفُورُ عَلَى شَجَرَةٍ عَظِيمَةٍ أَغْصَانُهَا|The bird stood on a tree with great branches.|lit=The bird stood on a tree great {{q|{{abbr|indef|indefinite}} {{abbr|f|feminine}} {{abbr|sg|singular}} {{abbr|gen|genitive}}}} [are] its branches {{q|{{abbr|inan|inanimate}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|pl|plural}}}}}}
# {{uxi|ar|وَقَفَ الْعُصْفُورُ عَلَى شَجَرَةٍ عِظَامٍ أَغْصَانُهَا|The bird stood on a tree with great branches.|lit=The bird stood on a tree great {{q|{{abbr|indef|indefinite}} {{abbr|c|common}} {{abbr|pl|plural}} {{abbr|gen|genitive}}}} [are] its branches {{q|{{abbr|inan|inanimate}} {{abbr|m|masculine}} {{abbr|pl|plural}}}}}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|اَلَّذِي:inv|f=اَلَّتِي:inv|pl=اَلَّذِينَ:inv|fpl=اَللَّاتِي:inv|fpl2=اَللَّائِي:inv|fpl3=اَللَّوَاتِي:inv
|cpl=اَلْأُلَى|d=اَللَّذَان|fd=اَللَّتَان
|state=def|omitarticle=yes|pos=pronoun|noirreg=yes}}

