Page 3396 الزهرة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Related to {{m|ar|زُهْرَة|t=brilliance, brightness, radiance, beauty}}; Venus is the brightest object in the night sky (except the moon).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الزُّهَرَة}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|الزُّهَرَة|f}}

# {{senseid|ar|Q313}}{{lb|ar|astronomy}} [[Venus]] (planet)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|زُهَرَةُ|state=def}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|أَعَزّ|عُزَّايَان|tr=|t=}}, {{l|ar|أَعَزّ|العُزَّى|tr=|t=the most powerful, strongest, highest in glory; most dear, highest esteemed, most loved}}
* {{l|ar|كَوْكَبَة|الكَوْكَبَة|tr=|t=the star, the planet, the prominent astronomical body}}
* {{l|ar|w:Athtar|عَثْتَر|tr=|t=one that makes herbage flourish, bringer of rain water; the morning or evening star}}
* {{l|ar|زُهْرَة|ذَات زُهْرَان|tr=|t=one that possesses or has brilliance or radiance}}
* {{l|ar|سَعْد|السَعْدَانِ|tr=|t=the two good fortunes}}, paired with Mercury or in other traditions Jupiter, contrasted with Mars and Saturn
* {{l|ar|سَعْد|السَعْد الأَصْغَر|tr=|t=the lesser good fortune}}, contrasted with Jupiter the greater

====Descendants====
* {{desc|chg|زهرة|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|زهره|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ms|Zuhrah|bor=1}}, {{desc|ms|Zuhrat|bor=1}}, {{desc|ms|Zuhara|bor=1}}, {{desc|ms|Zuharah|bor=1}}, {{desc|ms|زهرة|bor=1}}, {{desc|ms|زهره|bor=1}}, {{desc|ms|زهراء|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|Zuhura|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tr|Zöhre|bor=1}}, {{l|tr|Zühre}}

