Page 3397 السبت: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|س ب ت}}
Definite state of the {{ar-verbal noun|lc=1}} of {{m|ar|سَبَتَ}}  meaning “to {{l|en|rest}} or {{l|en|hibernate}}”, “to {{l|en|cease}}”, “to {{l|en|stop}} or be {{l|en|still}}”, “to be {{l|en|motionless}}”, “to be {{l|en|quiet}}” as a {{psm|ar|syc|nocap=1|ܫܒܬܐ|tr=šabbəṯā|t=Saturday}} used in the emphatic state; the religious sense likely being borrowed from the {{bor|ar|he|שַׁבָּת|tr=šabbā́ṯ|t=weekly day of rest}}. Ultimately stemming from {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ṯabat-|t=to be still, fixed, or staying}}, doublet of the native {{m|ar|ثَبَتَ}}. Related to {{der|ar|akk|𒋛𒁍𒌅|tr=se-bu-tu|ts=sebûtu|t=seventh day of the month}}, a holiday term that is paired with {{der|ar|akk|𒌓𒌋𒐊𒄰|tr=UD.15.KAM|ts=šapattu, šabattu|lit=a day of the cessation|t=two-week duration, the new and full moon}}.<ref>"[http://www.livius.org/sources/content/anet/104-106-the-epic-of-atrahasis/#end The Epic of Atraḥasis]" from Livius.org, © 1995–2017 adapted from B.R. Foster's translation; see especially 221 where the term appears.</ref> {{displaced|ar|شِيَار|sl=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|السَّبْت}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|السَّبْت|m}}

# [[Saturday]], the [[cessation]] or [[last]] [[day]] of the [[week]]
#: {{ux|ar|'''السَّبْتُ''' لَدَى ٱلْيَهُودِ يَوْمٌ مُهِمٌّ.|'''Saturday''' is an important day for the Jews.}}
# the [[Sabbath]]
# the [[duration]] of a [[week]], [[seven]]-[[day]] [[cycle]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَبْت|state=def|}}
{{ar-decl-noun|سَبْت|pl=سُبُوت}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|يَوْم السَّبْت}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|aa|sábti|bor=1}}
* {{desc|mg|asabotsy|bor=1}}
* {{desc|so|sábti|bor=1}}
* {{desc|id|Sabtu|bor=1}}

====See also====
* {{list:days of the week/ar}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Lane|سبت|pages=1287-1289}}
* [http://www.assyrianlanguages.org/akkadian/dosearch.php?searchkey=%C5%A1abattu&language=rawakkadian šabattu], © Association Assyrophile de France, last updated 2017.
* [https://archive.org/stream/AConsiceDictionaryAkkadian/CDA_w_corr#page/n175/mode/1up sebe] in {{R:akk:CDA|page=319}}
<references/>

-------- end text --------
