Page 3411 السودان: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Historically, the term was used to refer to Black Africa (Sub-Saharan region) in general, as the root word {{m|ar|سُود}} means "Blacks". It's one of the Arabic country names, which requires the definite article {{m|ar|ال}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|السُّودَان}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|السُّودَان|m}}

# {{place|ar|country|cont/Africa|t=Sudan}}

====Usage notes====
* Unlike the majority of country names {{m-self|ar|السُّودَان}} is a masculine.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سُودَان|state=def}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|سُودَانِيّ}}

