Page 3457 العراق: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ع ر ق}}
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Medieval Arabic geographic understanding of this toponym included the areas in the south and center of modern Iraq. This may be understood as the definite form of {{m|ar|عِرَاق|t=shore, coast, any region or area (of a whole country or a mere rivulet in a garden) adjacent to water as opposed to another one}}, contradistinguished from {{m|ar|جزيرة|الْجَزِيرَة|t=the Arabian Peninsula}}, respectively, in {{noncog|syc|-}} {{m|syc|ܓܙܺܝܪܬܴ݁ܐ|tr=gəzīrtā|t=Mesopotamia}}, but it is tempting to connect it with {{der|ar|pal||tr=ˀyrg|ts=ērag}} or {{m|pal||tr=ˀl'k'|ts=erāg|t=lowlands}},<ref>{{R:ar:Shapira-IA|page=163}}</ref> like {{m|pal|𐭠𐭩𐭥𐭠𐭭|tr=ʾyrʾn|ts=ērān|t=Iran}}, with diminutive suffix from {{m|pal|𐭠𐭩𐭫|tr=ʾyl|ts=ēr|t=Iranian}}, referring to historic rule from Iraq’s plateau-situated neighbor, [[Persia]]. The former Pahlavi form is more closely reflected in a {{cog|tmr|-}} incantation bowl; together with the neighboring region, this marks it as {{m|arc|אירג|tr=ʔyrg|ts=*ērag}}, being the oldest extant witness of the country name.<ref>See the Aramaic entry for the locus and the literature on it.</ref> The {{bor|ar|arc|-}} language continuum may have had a pharyngealized byform of the other vocalization, as also seen in {{m|ar|عِرْنَاس|t=distaff}} and {{m|ar|عَمْرُوسَة|t=small lamb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الْعِرَاق}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|الْعِرَاق|m|g2=f}}

# {{place|ar|country|cont/Asia|t=Iraq}}
<!--# Origin-->

====Usage notes====
* The definite article {{m|ar|ال}} is indispensable.
* Unlike the majority of country names, {{m|ar|الْعِرَاق}} is usually a masculine noun.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عِرَاق|state=def}}

====Related terms====
