Page 3530 الله أبهى: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|Alláh-u-Abhá}}

===Interjection===
{{ar-interj|[[الله|اللّٰهُ]] [[أبهى]]|tr=allāhu ʔabhā}}

# [[God]] is most glorious; used by [[Baháʼí]]s as a greeting crosslinguistically
-------- end text --------
Page 3531 الله أعلم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Literally “God knows best” or “God knows better”.

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=[[اَللّٰهُ]] [[أَعْلَم]]}}

# [[God knows]]

====Usage notes====
Used when responding to a question to which one does not know the answer or thinks they may be wrong. Also used to express that a human can never claim to be all-knowing, which is an attribute only belonging to God.

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa|الله اعلم|tr=allâho a'lam|bor=1}}
-------- end text --------
Page 3532 الله أكبر: -------- begin text --------
{{phrasebook|ar}}
[[Image:Flag of Waziristan resistance (1930s).svg|thumb|Flag of 1930s [[Waziristan|Waziristan (Pakistan)]] resistance movement: {{lang|ar|'''الله أكبر'''}}]]
[[Image:Flag of Iraq.svg|thumb|Flag of Iraq: {{lang|ar|'''اللّٰه أكبر'''}}]]

===Etymology===
{{m|ar|اللّٰه||God, Allah}} + {{m|ar|أَكْبَر}}, the [[elative]] of {{m|ar|كَبِير||big, great, powerful}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|اَلّٰهُ أَكْبَر}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-eg-الله أكبر.oga|a=Egypt}}

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=[[اللّٰهُ]] [[اكبر|أَكْبَر]]}}

# [[God]] is greater
# [[oh my God]]

