Page 3558 المريخ: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|م|ر|خ|}}, meaning "to rub", "to leak sap (especially flammable oils)", "to anoint or cover in oil", "to rub together flammable branches"; stemming from the red color of the planet being associated with fire, a conception found in archaic synonyms as well.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|اَلْمِرِّيخ}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|اَلْمِرِّيخ|m}}

# {{lb|ar|astronomy}} the planet [[Mars]]
#: {{ux|ar|''' اَلْمِرِّيخُ''' هُوَ ٱلْكَوْكَبُ ٱلرَّابِعُ فِي ٱلْبُعْدِ عَنِ ٱلشَّمْسِ فِي ٱلنِّظَامِ ٱلشَّمْسِيِّ وَهُوَ ٱلْجَارُ ٱلْخَارِجِيُّ لِلْأَرْضِ وَيُصَنَّفُ كَوْكَبًا صَخْرِيًّا، مِنْ مَجْمُوعَةِ ٱلْكَوَاكِبِ ٱلْأَرْضِيَّةِ.|'''Mars''' is the fourth planet in distance from the Sun in the Solar System and it is Earth's external neighbor and is classified as a rocky planet from the group of the Terrestrial Planets.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِرِّيخ|state=def}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|[[حَرِّق|المُحَرِّق]]|tr=|t=the burner, the burning one}}
* {{l|ar|[[عزيز|عَزِيزَان]]|tr=|t=the most powerful, strongest, the most intense}}
* {{l|ar|أَحْمَر|الأَحْمَر|tr=|t=the red one}}
* {{l|ar|نَحْس|النَحْسَانِ|tr=|t=the two misfortunes}}, paired with Saturn, contrasted with Venus and Mercury, or Venus and Jupiter in another tradition
* {{l|ar|نَحْس|النَحْس الأَصْغَر|tr=|t=the lesser misfortune}}, contrasted with Saturn the greater

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|مِرِّيخِيّ}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ajp|المريخ|tr=il-marrīḵ}}
* {{desc|syc|ܡܰܪܪܻܝܟ|tr=marrīḵ|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|fa|مریخ|tr=merrix|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|Mirihi|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tt|Merih|bor=1}}

===See also===
* {{list:planets of the Solar System/ar}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=4|page=167}}

{{C|ar|Planets of the Solar System}}
