Page 3559 المسجد الأقصى: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{lit|the far/furthermost [[mosque]] (from the perspective of pre-[[Hegira]] Mecca)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|المَسْجِد الأَقْصَى}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|[[مسجد|المَسْجِد]] [[أقصى|الأَقْصَى]]|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} a [[reference]] to the [[Temple in Jerusalem]] or the general area of the site thereof, hence the [[Temple Mount]]/[[Haram al-Sharif]]
#: {{syn|ar|بَيْت المَقْدِس|الحَرَم الشَّرِيف}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|17|1|passage=سُبْحَٰنَ ٱلَّذِي أَسْرَىٰ بِعَبْدِهِ لَيْلًا مِّنَ ٱلْمَسْجِدِ ٱلْحَرَامِ إِلَىٰ '''ٱلْمَسْجِدِ ٱلْأَقْصَىٰ''' ٱلَّذِي بَٰرَكْنَا حَوْلَهُ لِنُرِيَهُ مِنْ ءَايَٰتِنَا إِنَّهُ هُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْبَصِيرُ|t=Glorified be He Who transported His servant (Muhammad) by night from the Sacred Mosque to '''the Far Mosque (in Jerusalem)''', whose environ (that is, Jerusalem) We blessed, so that We show him Our signs; it is indeed He, the All-Hearing All-Seeing One.}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|60|97|passage={{...}}عَنْ أَبِي ذَرٍّ - رَضِيَ اللهُ عَنْهُ - قَالَ قُلْتُ يَا رَسُولَ اللهِ، أَيُّ مَسْجِدٍ وُضِعَ أَوَّلُ قَالَ " الْمَسْجِدُ الْحَرَامُ ". قُلْتُ ثُمَّ أَيُّ قَالَ " '''الْمَسْجِدُ الْأَقْصَىٰ''' ". قُلْتُ كَمْ كَانَ بَيْنَهُمَا قَالَ " أَرْبَعُونَ ". ثُمَّ قَالَ " حَيْثُمَا أَدْرَكَتْكَ الصَّلاَةُ فَصَلِّ، وَالأَرْضُ لَكَ مَسْجِدٌ ".|t={{...}}On the authority of ʾAbū Ḏarr — ''God be pleased with him'': He said: I said, "O Apostle of God! Which mosque was laid down first?" He said, "The Sacred Mosque (in Mecca)." I said, "Then which?" He said, "'''The Far Mosque (in Jerusalem)'''." I said, "How much is [the time] between the two of them?" He said, "Forty (years)." Then he said, "Wherever [the time of] prayer catches up to you, pray then [and there] for the earth is mosque for you."}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=12th century {{CE}}|title=Kitāb al-Qabas fī Šarḥ Muwaṭṭaʾ Mālik bin ʾAnas|trans-title=The Book of Spark in the Exposition of the ''Muwaṭṭaʾ'' of Mālik bin ʾAnas|author={{w|Abu Bakr ibn al-Arabi|ʾAbū Bakr ʾibn al-ʿArabī}}|text={{...}}صخرة بيت المقدس من عجائب الله تعالى فإنها صخرة قائمة شعثاء في وسط '''المسجد الأقصى'''{{...}}|t={{...}}The rock of Jerusalem is from the wonders of God, He be exalted, and it is indeed the conspicuous craggy rock in the midst of the '''Temple Mount'''{{...}}}}
# {{lb|ar|by extension}} the {{w|Al-Aqsa Mosque}} (on the [[Temple Mount]]/[[Haram al-Sharif]])
#: {{syn|ar|جَامِع الأَقْصَى|المُصَلَّى القِبْلِي}}
#* {{quote-journal|ar|date=23 May 1938|author=Professor Muhammad Saeed Al-Arian|title=أسبوع في فلسطين|trans-title=A Week in Palestine|journal=w:Arrissalah|text={{...}}فزرت '''المسجد الأقصى'''، وقبة الصخرة ومصلى عمر، وكنيسة القيامة، ومصعد المسيح، وبيت لحم، والمتحف الإسلامي، وكلية الروضة، والنادي المصري؛|t={{...}}I visited '''Al-Aqsa Mosque''', the Dome of the Rock, Omar’s prayer hall (Mosque of Omar), the Church of the Holy Sepulchre, the Christ’s place of ascension (Chapel of the Ascension), Bethlehem, the Islamic Museum, Al-Rawdah College, and the Egyptian Club.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|المَسْجِد|mod=أَقْصَى|idafa=def}}

{{C|ar|Buildings|Palestine}}

-------- end text --------
Page 3560 المسجد الحرام: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{lit|the sacred/inviolable [[mosque]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الْمَسْجِد الْحَرَام}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|[[مسجد|الْمَسْجِد]] [[حرام|الْحَرَام]]|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} a [[reference]] to the [[Kaaba]] or the general area of the site thereof, hence the [[Great Mosque of Mecca]]/[[Masjid al-Haram]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|144|passage={{...}}فَوَلِّ وَجْهَكَ شَطْرَ '''ٱلْمَسْجِدِ ٱلْحَرَامِ''' وَحَيْثُ مَا كُنْتُمْ فَوَلُّوا وُجُوهَكُمْ شَطْرَهُ{{...}}|t={{...}}so turn your face (in prayer) in the direction of '''the Sacred Mosque (in Mecca)''', and wherever you are turn your faces in its direction;{{...}}|subst=فَوَلِّ/فَ-وَلِّ}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|ibnmajah|5|608|text= " لَا تُشَدُّ الرِّحَالُ إِلَّا إِلَىٰ ثَلَاثَةِ مَسَاجِدَ إِلَىٰ '''الْمَسْجِدِ الْحَرَامِ''' وَإِلَىٰ الْمَسْجِدِ الأَقْصَىٰ وَإِلَىٰ مَسْجِدِي هَٰذَا ".|t="Bind not the camels' saddles (i.e., go not on a [pilgrim's] journey) but to three mosques: to '''the Sacred Mosque (in Mecca)''' and to the Far Mosque (in Jerusalem) and to this mosque of mine."}}
#* {{quote-web|ar|date=20 July 2013|author=Haya Al-Sahli|title=توسعات ضخمة للحرم المكي|work=[[Al Jazeera]]|url=https://www.aljazeera.net/news/2013/7/20/%D8%AA%D9%88%D8%B3%D8%B9%D8%A7%D8%AA-%D8%B6%D8%AE%D9%85%D8%A9-%D9%84%D9%84%D8%AD%D8%B1%D9%85-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%83%D9%8A|trans-title=Huge Expansions of Al Haram of Mecca|text=تعمل الجهات المعنية في السعودية على قدم وساق لتوسعة صحن الطواف في '''المسجد الحرام''' بمكة المكرمة، ورفع طاقته الاستيعابية من 48 ألف طائف في الساعة إلى 105 آلاف طائف، والانتهاء من مراحل المشروع الثلاث قبل نهاية حج 2015.|t=The concerned authorities in Saudi Arabia are working in full swing to expand the circumambulation hall in '''the Great Mosque''' in Mecca, and to raise its capacity from 48 thousand pilgrims per hour to 105 thousand, and to complete the three phases of the project before the end of the 2015 hajj.|archiveurl=|archivedate=}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْجِد|state=def|mod=حَرَام}}

{{C|ar|Buildings|Saudi Arabia}}
-------- end text --------
Page 3561 المسيح: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Definite form of {{l|ar|مَسِيح}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الْمَسِيح}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|الْمَسِيح|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Christianity|Islam}} [[Christ]]; the [[Messiah]] {{gloss|Jesus of Nazareth}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3|45
|passage=إِنَّ اللَّهَ يُبَشِّرُكِ بِكَلِمَةٍ مِنْهُ اسْمُهُ '''ٱلْمَسِيحُ''' عِيسَى ابْنُ مَرْيَمَ
|translation=...of a Word from Him, his name will be '''the Messiah''', Jesus, son of Mary; honoured in this world and the Hereafter, and he will be one of those nearest to Allah.}}
# {{lb|ar|Judaism}} the awaited [[Messiah]]

====Usage notes====
* Since Jesus is called {{m|ar|يَسُوع}} by Christians and {{m|ar|عِيسَى}} by Muslims, just {{m|ar|اَلْمَسِيح}} is often used wherever a neutral term accepted by both religions is intended.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسِيح|state=def}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|مَسِيحِيّ}}
-------- end text --------
Page 3562 المشتري: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Jupiter (39832023884).jpg|300px|thumb|{{lang|ar|اَلْمُشْتَرِي}}]]

===Etymology===
* From {{m|ar|مُشْتَرٍ|gloss=buyer, seller}}, from the root {{ar-root|ش|ر|ي}} with the original semantic sense of bringing of goods or commodities (to be exchanged). This renders the title to mean "the bringer of goods", "provider of commodities", or "supplier of fortunes"; parallel with the planet's other names also denoting fortune and its auspicious nature.
* Alternatively from the root {{ar-root|ش|ر|ي}} in the sense of "being persistent", "to be reliable"; possibly parallel with the title {{m|ar|صَدِيق}} and {{cog|he|צֶדֶק‬|tr=tzédek|}}, which however can also be interpreted as "charitable", "giving", or "honoring".
**Possible distant relation to {{cog|akk|𒀭𒈪𒁲𒊑|tr=mīšāru|t=uprightness; god personifying justice}} and {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎌𐎗|tr=|t=righteousness}}, cognate with {{cog|he|יָשָׁר|tr=yashár|t=upright, right, correct}} and {{m|ar|يَسْر|tr=|t=}}. The root {{ar-root|ي|س|ر}} also however denotes "to procure goods easily", "to be or grow rich", "to live in affluence or ease", "to have good fortune".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|الْمُشْتَرِي}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|الْمُشْتَرِي|m}}

# {{lb|ar|astronomy}} [[Jupiter]] (planet)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مُشْتَرٍ|state=def}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|[[جَدّ|الجَدّ]]|tr=|t=the good fortune}}<ref>[http://www.jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/6456-gad Gad] Jewish Encyclopedia ©2002-2011, JewishEncyclopedia.com. All rights reserved</ref><ref>[https://www.jstor.org/stable/10.7817/jameroriesoci.139.2.0307 The god Gad] by Ryan Thomas in Journal of the American Oriental Society
Vol. 139, No. 2 (April-June 2019), pp. 307-316</ref>
* {{l|ar|أَحْوَر|الأَحْوَر|tr=|t=the clear, distinguished, intense, bright among darkness}}<ref>Term ḤWR_19, under entry: [https://www2.hf.uio.no/polyglotta/index.php?page=record&view=record&vid=626&mid=1218146&level=2 ḤWR] Etymological Dictionary of Arabic, University of Oslo Faculty of Humanities</ref>
* {{l|ar|سَعْد|السَعْد الأَكْبَر|tr=|t=the greater good fortune}}<ref>Stefano Carboni, Following the Stars: Images of the Zodiac in Islamic Art, 1997, Jupiter, pg. 19</ref> contrasted with Venus the lesser

====Descendants====
* {{desc|az|Müştəri|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ms|Musytari|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|axm|մուշթարի|մուշտարի}}
* {{desc|fa|مشتری|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|Mshtarii|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tr|Müşteri|bor=1|qq=archaic}}

====See also====
* {{list:planets of the Solar System/ar}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Lane|حور|page=666}}
* {{w|Wilhelm Gesenius}}, ''Hebrew Lexicon'' (1852), "גד", pg. 177
<references/>

{{C|ar|Planets of the Solar System}}
