[[Category:Arabic abbreviations]]

-------- end text --------
Page 3914 ب ت ل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|he|ב-ט-ל|tr=b-ṭ-l}}.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[cutting-off]], [[severing]]

====Derived terms====
{{ar-verb forms|a|I-vn-head=بَتْل|I-vn=cut; distinction|I=to [[cut]]; to [[cut-off]], to sever; to; to settle, make final and conclusive [[clinch]]; to [[devote]] one self's to God and sever relations with the [[mundane]]; to be [[pious]], [[chaste]], and self-denying; to live in [[chastity]]|V=to devote one's self to God; to not marry in life|I-pp=forsaken, abandoned, deserted|V-pp=A person who cuts himself off of people in order to worship God; a person who does not want to get married; a palm whose branches have come down}}

* {{l|ar|بَتُول|t=chaste, virgin}}; also a female given name
** {{l|ar|بَتُولِي|t=virginal}}
** {{l|ar|بَتُولِيَّة|t=virginity}}
* {{l|ar|مُبَتَّل|t=ascetic, recluse; pious, godly man}}
* {{l|ar|بَتِيل|t=a palm branch severed from the rest of the tree; the flow of water under a mountain}}
* {{l|ar|بَتِيلَة|t=a body part that's perfect and distinguishable from the others}}
* {{l|ar|مُبَتَّل|t=having a perfectly-created body, in which every part (cut) of the body is beautiful on its own; someone who severs himself from society to worship God}}
* {{l|ar|مُبْتِل|t=a palm tree with numerous branches}}
* {{l|ar|تَبْتِيل|t=worshiping and Devotion to God; perfection in the body in which every part is gorgeous}}
* {{l|ar|مَبْتَل|t=location of a cut}}

;Onomastics
* {{l|ar|اَلْبَتُول|t=[[Virgin Mary]]; [[w:Fatima bint Muhammad|Faṭima Az-Zahraʾ]]}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|بَتُولَا|t=birch tree}}

