# concerning concepts related to "trumpets" or "a sudden loud blast of sound"; hence the meaning of "a sudden striking calamity" and by extension "an evil" or "wrongful conduct". Ultimately related to the root {{ar-root|ب|ق|ق}}, meaning "the buzzing of insects", "to be loud or noisy", "to be obnoxiously talkative", with likely {{psm|ar|grc|βούκινο|nocap=1}} or {{noncog|la|būcina}}, borrowed itself as {{noncog|syc|ܒܘܩ̈ܝܢܐܣ|tr=bwqynʾ|t=būqīnā}}. Compare {{noncog|en|bugle}}, an ox or bovid horn.

