Page 3980 باب: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Porte traditionnelle Sidi Ammar Sayada.JPG|thumb|right|{{l-self|ar|بَاب|tr=-}}]]
{{ar-rootbox|ب و ب}}

===Etymology===
Usually considered a borrowing from {{bor|ar|arc|בָּבָא|tr=bāḇā||gate}}, from {{der|ar|akk|bābum|𒆍|tr=bābum|t=gate}}, particularly since the Arabs, living in tents, did not need doors. However, Hans Bauer considers all of these words native, explaining the formation as an ancient {{univerbation|ar|nocap=1}} of etyma equivalent to {{cog|ar|بَاءَ}} {{m|ar|بِ}} “he has entered into (the house)”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَاب}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-باب.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَاب|m|pl=أَبْوَاب|pl2=بِيبَان}}

# [[door]], [[gate]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|58
|passage= وَادْخُلُوا '''الْبَابَ''' سُجَّدًا وَقُولُوا حِطَّةٌ
|translation= [And] enter '''the gate''' with humility [...]}}
# [[opening]], [[gateway]]
# [[entrance]]
# {{C|ar|Animal body parts}} [[gullet]], [[weasand]]
#* {{RQ:Ibn al-ʿawwām|33|10|volume=2|page=677 line 6|passage=وقد تخرج للدابة من حنكها ويسمي التحنيك وصفة العمل في ذلك إذا أحنكت الدابة فأفتح لها من الدرجة الثالثة والرابعة ولا تفتح لها قرب '''الباب''' لأن الدم ربما عسر إمساكه فتلف الدابة.|t=One may extract the blood from the jaw of a beast and it is called ''taḥnīk'' and the operation consists in that you have bound the beast with a chinstrap and now cut it open to the third or fourth degree but don’t open it close the '''throat''' as it may be difficult to contain the blood and the beast will succumb.}}
# [[opportunity]], a [[chance]], [[opening]]
# [[military]] [[tactic]], [[maneuver]], an [[opening]] to use a [[strategy]]
# [[chapter]], [[section]], [[column]]
# [[group]], [[class]], [[category]]
# {{lb|ar|astronomy}} [[appearance]] of an [[astronomical]] [[body]], a [[juncture]], an [[opening]] to [[observe]]
# {{lb|ar|figurative}} [[domain]], [[field]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَاب|pl=أَبْوَاب|pl2=بِيبَان}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|مِنْ بَابِ أَوْلَى}}
* {{l|ar|مَقْبِض الْبَاب|t=doorknob}}
* {{l|ar|بَابَة}}
* {{l|ar|بَوَّاب}}
* {{l|ar|بَوَّابَة}}
* {{l|ar|تَبْوِيب}}
* {{l|ar|مُبَوَّب}}

