===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ب و ر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.ipass?.vn:بَوْر,بَوَار}}

# to [[perish]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=Abdullah Siraj ad-Din al-Husseini|year=1924-2002|chapter=page 6,7|text=ولكن التجارة الناجحة الرابحة التي تدر على صاحبها أضعافا مضاعفة على وجه الاستمرار بلا '''بوار''' تلك التجارة هي في الإكثار من الكلم الطيب والعمل الصالح|title=صعود الأقوال ورفع الأعمال|t=But successful and profitable trade which increases its owner multiple fold on the face of continuation without '''ruin''', this trade is through increasing in good words and righteous deeds}}
# to lie fallow, be [[uncultivated]] (land)
# to be [[futile]], [[unsuccessful]], [[unprofitable]], lead to nothing (work)
#* {{quote|ar|إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ يَتْلُونَ كِتَـٰبَ ٱللَّهِ وَأَقَامُوا۟ ٱلصَّلَوٰةَ وَأَنفَقُوا۟ مِمَّا رَزَقْنَـٰهُمْ سِرًّۭا وَعَلَانِيَةًۭ يَرْجُونَ تِجَـٰرَةًۭ لَّن تَبُورَ ٢٩|Indeed, those who recite the Book of Allāh and establish prayer and spend [in His cause] out of what We have provided them, secretly and publicly, [can] expect a transaction [i.e., profit] that will never perish -
|ref=https://quran.com/35:29
}}
# to be [[unsalable]], be dead stock (merchandise)

