Page 4039 باس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Likely from {{bor|ar|fa-cls|بوسیدن|tr=bōsīdan}}, this is an onomatopoeia common in many Indo-European languages, where the initial [[labial]] represents the protruding lips and the [[sibilant]] represents the smacking sound. Compare {{cog|en|buss}}, regional {{cog|de|Bützchen}}, {{m|de|Busserl}}, {{cog|la|basium}}, {{cog|fr|bisou}} etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَاسَ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:بَوْس}} {{tlb|ar|transitive|post-classical}}

