Via an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} dialect form equivalent {{cog|syc|ܒܠܬܐ|tr=balləṯā|t=perfume flask, ampulla}} from {{der|ar|pal|sc=Phlv|tr=pygʾl|ts=*paygāl|t=goblet, chalice, cup}}, which is in {{cog|fa|پیاله|tr=piyâla}} and thence has been reborrowed in Arabic dialects as {{m|ar|بيالة|tr=biyāla|t=cup}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَالَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَالَة|f|pl=بَالَات|pl2=بَال}}

# {{tlb|ar|obsolete|{{w|Banu al-Harith|Banū al-Ḥāriṯ}} and few other dialects}} a large [[flask]], [[flagon]], [[bottle]]
