Page 4089 بالهناء والشفاء: -------- begin text --------
{{phrasebook|ar}}

===Etymology===
From the roots {{ar-root|ه|ن|ء}} meaning "to enjoy, to go down easily, to be well-received", and {{ar-root|ش|ف|ي}} meaning "to be healthy, to be wholesome, to restore".

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ar|/bil.ha.naː.ʔi waʃ.ʃi.faːʔ/}}
<!-- not generating correct transcription: * {{ar-IPA|بِٱلْهَنَاءِ وَٱلشِّفَاء}} -->

===Interjection===
{{ar-interj|[[هناء|بِٱلْهَنَاءِ]] [[شفاء|وَٱلشِّفَاء]]|tr=bi-l-hanāʾi wa-š-šifāʾ}}

# [[bon appétit]]; "May it be with [[enjoyment]] and [[restoration]]",  "May it [[go down]] [[easily]] and [[bring]] [[health]]"
#: {{syn|ar|بِالصِّحَّة وَٱلْعَافِيَة|شَهْيَة طَيِّبَة|tr1=bi-ṣ-ṣiḥḥa wa-l-ʕāfiya|tr2=šahya ṭayyiba}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|arz|بالهنا والشفا|tr=bil-hanã wil-shifã}}

===References===
