Page 4095 بامبوزيا: -------- begin text --------
[[File:9506aSyzygium cumini Plumfvf 01.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|بامبوزيا}} – {{taxfmt|Syzygium cumini|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|كَامْبُوزَة|كَمْبُوز|زُونِيَا||unidentified Egyptian or Sudanese dialects}}
* {{alter|ar|جَمْبُول|جَمْبُولَان|جَامْبُو|جَمْبُو|جَمُّون}}

===Etymology===
From various descendants of {{der|ar|sa|जम्बुल}}. The most common form, here chosen as the title, is apparently thus extremely garbled by {{bor|ar|arz|-}} speakers owing to the plant, requiring intense tropical conditions, growing only at scattered spots of the Arabic-speaking countries – limited-use plant names tend to be distorted, compare e.g. the forms environing {{cog|ru|берескле́т|t=spindle-tree}}. Going further, it has even been argued that {{m|ar|زَنْبُوع|t=pomelo}} is derived from this wanderword.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَامْبُوزِيَا|f}}

# {{C|ar|Myrtle family plants}} [[rose apple]] ({{taxfmt|Syzygium cumini|species}})

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَامْبُوزِيَا}}

===Further reading===
* {{cite-web|work=Al-Balad|title=ar:تعرف إيه عن البامبوزيا.. فاكهة غريبة شكل الزيتون وطعم الكريز|date=2019-07-31|url=https://www.elbalad.news/3925848}}
* {{pedia|lang=ar|شجرة البامبوزيا}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=219b|entry=جُمُونٌ}}
-------- end text --------
Page 4096 باميا: -------- begin text --------

