{{ar-noun|بَامِيَا|f}}

# {{alternative form of|ar|بَامِيَة|nocap=1}}
-------- end text --------
Page 4097 بامية: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Okra fruit & flower 02.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|بَامِيَة}}|upright=1.15]][[File:09716jfFood cuisine fruits Baliuag, Bulacan Roadsfvf 31.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.15]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|بَامِيَا}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|ar}}, this plant is rarely mentioned for medieval cookery, as eating vegetables standalone and this one in particular has not been common but it has complemented stews, and additionally its mucilage made it improper for literate tables.

With respect to this, it could have been formed somewhere in the center of the {{w|Abbasid Empire}} from a dialectal form of {{af|ar|إِبْهَام|t1=thumb|ـِيَّة|pos2=used for stews with a characteristic ingredient}}, especially as the cognate {{cog|akk|𒋗𒅆|ts=ubānu|tr=ŠU.ŠI|t=finger}} also has been used for the crop, and the same consideration gave rise to {{m|ar|بَان|t=moringa|id=ben}}.

However likewise going by its outward appearance, {{bor|ar|fa-cls|بامیه|بامیا|tr=bāmiyā}} is internally analyzable as suffixed from {{m|fa|بام|tr=bâm|t=roof}}, in the fashion of {{m|fa|مومیا|tr=mumiyâ|t=mumijo; mummy}} from {{m|fa|موم|tr=mum|t=wax}}, though the Persian term later be reinforced by borrowing from Arabic.

Otherwise, in view of the geographic distribution of the species and the origin of the coordinate term {{m|ar|وَيْكَة|t=dried okra}}, a {{bor|ar|qfa-sub}} in [[Nubia]] has to be attended.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَامِيَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَامِيَة|f}}

# [[okra]], [[ladies' fingers]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَامِيَة|f}}

====Descendants====
