[[File:Grey parrot (AP4N2898 1PS) (43194627604).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|ببغاء}} – {{taxfmt|Psittacus erithacus|species}}|upright=1.5]]

===Etymology===
Perhaps of {{onomatopoeic|ar|nocap=1}} origin. In view of the bird’s range, borrowing from an unknown African or South Asian language is possible. Related to {{cog|syc|ܒܒܓܐ|ts=bbgʾ}}, {{m|syc|ܦܵܦܵܐ|tr=ppʾ|ts=pāp̄ā}}, {{cog|xcl|պապկայ}}, {{cog|fa|ببغا|tr=babğâ}}, {{m|fa|بپغا|tr=bapğâ|t=parrot}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَبَّغَاء|m|g2=f|head2=بَبْغَاء|head3=بَبَغَاء|d=بَبَّغَاوَانِ|d2=بَبْغَاوَانِ|d3=بَبَغَاوَانِ|pl=بَبَّغَاوَات|pl2=بَبْغَاوَات|pl3=بَبَغَاوَات}}

# [[parrot]]
# {{lb|ar|figurative}} one who repeats what was said
#: {{usex|ar|لَا تَكُنْ مِثْلَ الْبَبَّغَاءِ|Do not [[parrot#Verb|parrot]].}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَبَّغَاء:di|head2=بَبْغَاء:di|head3=بَبَغَاء:di|d=بَبَّغَاوَانِ|d2=بَبْغَاوَانِ|d3=بَبَغَاوَانِ|pl=بَبَّغَاوَات|pl2=بَبْغَاوَات|pl3=بَبَغَاوَات}}<!--Wehr lists first and second heads, both as diptotes; presumably third one (from Steingass) is as well -->

====Descendants====
