# to become [[rever]]ed, to become [[honour]]ed, to become [[glorify|glorified]], to become [[worship]]ped, to become [[commend]]ed, to become [[dignify|dignified]], to become [[venerate]]d
# to be in a state of [[abundance]], to [[miss]] no [[convenience]]s

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.vn:بَجَل}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[revere]], to [[honour]], to [[glorify]], to [[worship]], to [[commend]], to [[dignify]], to [[venerate]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بَجَل|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|بَجِلَ|form=I}}
# [[sufficiency]], [[enoughness]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَجَل}}

===Etymology 2===
Possibly a seafarers’ word from {{der|ar|non|bjúgr}}, {{cog|is|bjúgur}}, {{cog|sv|bjugg|lit=corn}}, their plurals ending in ''-n'', whence also the second half of the European words for {{m|en|scurvy}} – see also {{m|ar|هَيْدُورة|t=sheep-skin}} appearing of similar origin even in desert-dwellers’ dialects, and note the foreign form but with fitting vocalism in Andalusi {{m|ar|بُجُّول}}, {{m|ar|بُجُّون|t=stalk of a fig and similar fruits}}, then possibly instead figuratively petioles or nipples as in {{cog|es|pezón}} from {{der|ar|la|petiolus|peciolus}}.

{{cog|tig|በጊላ|t=festering wound on feet and legs that refuses to heal}}, {{m|tig|በጀን}}, {{m|tig|በገን|t=gonorrhoea}}, {{cog|am|በገን|t=redness of the skin of the legs when one has exposed them to the sun during the wet season}}, {{m|am|ብጒንጅ|tr=bəgʷinǧ|t=sore, furuncle}} can be Arabisms, with their usual variation of {{m|tig||ጅ}} and {{m|tig||ግ}} borrowed from {{m|ar||ج}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بَجَل|m}}

# [[bejel]], [[sibbens]], [[button scurvy]] (a [[skin]] [[disease]] transmitted through smearing of {{taxfmt|Treponema pallidum|species}})

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَجَل}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|en|bejel|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=86}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|pages=153–154}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass|page=107}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=65}}

