Page 4153 بحران: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{der|ar|arc|בחרנא|tr=bəḥrānā|t=test, turning point of disease progression, crisis}}, from {{m|arc|בְּחַר|tr=bəḥar|t=judging, testing}}; compare {{cog|he|בָּחַר|tr=bāḥar|t=to choose, appoint}}. Perhaps eventually a {{cal|ar|grc|κρίσις|nocap=1}}. The Arabic lexicographers identified the word as foreign and considered it of Greek origin.

Lane instead theorised it to be from archaic {{m|ar|البَاحُور|tr=|t=the moon|lit=expanding, widening; being at the full extent, the furthest extremities}}, from the notion of a sudden change of health being linked to the phase of the moon. Compare for this {{noncog|grc|σεληνιάζομαι|tr=|t=epilepsy; sudden drastic symptoms|lit=moonstruck}}, {{noncog|la|lunaticus}}, and {{noncog|en|lunacy}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|بُحْرَان}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بُحْرَان|m|pl=بَحَارِين}}

# {{lb|ar|now|rare}} [[crisis]], [[panic]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَزْمَة}}
# {{lb|ar|medicine}} [[crisis]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بُحْرَان|pl=بَحَارِين}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|az|böhran|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|fa-cls|بحران|tr=buḥrān|bor=1}}
* {{desc|axm|բուհրան|bor=1|alts=1}}
* {{desc|ota|بحران|tr=buhran|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|buhran}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{head|ar|noun form|tr=baḥrān}}

# {{infl of|ar|بَحْر||d}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=88}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=89}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=157}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=67}}

-------- end text --------
