===Etymology 1===
Back-formed and simplified from a [[nisba]]-[[epitheted]] name, as it has also been called {{m|ar||الْبَخْتَرِيّ}} {{m|ar||الْإِبِل الْخُرَاسَانِيَّة}}, {{m|ar||الْجَمَل الْبُخَارِيّ}} etc., various connections made to [[Bactria]], [[Balkh]] and [[Bukhara]].

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|بُخْت}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|بُخْت|sing=بُخْتِيّ|singg=m|sing2=بُخْتِيَّة|singg2=f|pl=بَخَاتِيّ}}

# a [[half-breed]] from a male [[Bactrian camel]] and a [[female]] [[dromedary]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|muslim|37|190
|passage=رُؤُوسُهُنَّ كَأَسْنِمَةِ الْبُخْتِ الْمَائِلَةِ
|translation=Their heads are inclined like the  humps of Bactrian dromedaries.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بُخْت|sing=بُخْتِيّ|pl=بَخَاتِيّ:di|d=بُخْتِيَّانِ}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|fa|بخت|tr=baxt}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|بَخْت}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بَخْت|m|pl=بُخُوت}}

# [[luck]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَخْت|pl=بُخُوت}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|arq|بخت|tr=baḵt}}
* {{desc|arz|بخت|tr=baḵt}}
* {{desc|afb|بخت|tr=baḵt}}
* {{desc|acx|بخت|tr=baḵt}}
** {{desc|sw|bahati|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ajp|بخت|tr=baḵt}} <!--Jerusalem, Jordanian Bedouin-->

