Page 4166 بختري: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَخْتَرِيّ}}

===Etymology 1===

====Adjective====
{{ar-nisba|بَخْتَرِيّ}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[sway]]ing while [[walk]]ing, of [[heavy]] [[steps]] to be [[balance]]d, [[swagger]]ing ({{m|ar||صَاحِب [[تَبَخَّتُر]]}})

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|بَخْتَرِيّ|pl=sp}}

===Etymology 2===
{{multiple images|direction=horizontal|perrow=2|
|image1=Roemeria hybrida kz03.jpg
|caption1={{lang|ar|بَختَرِيّ}} – {{taxlink|Roemeria hybrida|species}}
|image2=Teichalm, Weidenblättriges Ochsenauge.jpg
|caption2={{lang|ar|بَخْتَرِيّ}} – {{taxlink|Buphthalmum salicifolium|genus}}
}}
{{wp|lang=ar}}
Possibly from {{bor|ar|grc|βούφθαλμον}}. Interestingly, the [http://www.poesialatina.it/_ns/Greek/testi/Dioscorides/De_materia_medica_(recensiones_e_codd._Vindob.).html Dioskurides interpolations] for this plant name also rendered {{noncog|la|caltha}} {{m|grc||κάχλα}} (and {{m|grc||χάλκα}}, {{m|grc|χαλκῖτις}}, {{m|grc|χάλκανθον}}, {{m|grc|χαλκάνθεμον}}, evidently confused with native Greek stems), as it is attested instead of {{m|grc||*κάλχα}}‌—at least this is believed to be the Latin word by {{w|Classical philology|classical philologers}} rather than an {{w|Old Arabic}} or {{w|Aramaic}} version of {{m|ar|كَحْلَاء}} that comes to mind to the Semitist—, and {{w|Hesychius of Alexandria|Hesychius}} has a {{m|grc||καχίλα}} meaning {{m|grc|ἄνθη}} used by ''the Cypriots'', in either cases {{IPAchar|/tʰ/}} ~ {{IPAchar|/θ/}} going over to {{IPAchar|/x/}} and the cluster reverted, so this may be a {{bor|ar|el-cyp|-}} borrowing rather than a Bedouin distortion.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بَخْتَرِيّ|head2=بَخَتَرِيّ|m}}

# {{taxlink|Roemeria hybrida|species}}
#: {{syn|ar|مُغْزِرَة|دَيْدَحَان}}
# [[oxeye]] ({{taxfmt|Buphthalmum|genus}} spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|عَرَار|عَيْن الْبَقَر|بَهَار|رَبْد}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَخْتَرِيّ|head2=بَخَتَرِيّ}}

{{C|ar|Poppies|Composites}}
-------- end text --------
