Page 4209 بذج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Considered a word of foreign origin, which would appear [[Himyaritic]] or {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}} according to the current distribution and the reoccurring of the pattern of {{m-self|ar|بُذَج}} in triliteral root formulae, like {{m|ar|تُبَّع|t=king in ancient Yemen}} or {{m|ar|لِبَخ}} or {{m|ar|نِطَع}}, but ultimately it could have its cause in {{der|ar|ira-pro|*bujáh|t=goat}} being suffixed diminutive {{m|ira-pro|*-akah}} in later {{der|ar|ira-mid|-}}, compare {{cog|xcl|բզաք}} and {{m|xcl|բուծ|t=lamb}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَذَج|بُذَج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَذَج|head2=بُذَج|m|f=بَذَجَة|f2=بُذَجَة}}

# {{tlb|ar|now|_|southern|_|Yemeni|_|Tihama}} [[lamb]] (child of a [[sheep]] but not [[goat]])
#* {{quote-book|year=8th century|ar|url=https://www.aldiwan.net/poem71900.html|author=ar:أبو طالب المأموني|title=ar:ورب سوس من الاترج<qq:first line>|passage=ورب سوس من الاترج … متقد اللون اتقاد السرج<br/>يعوم من انائه في مزج … مجت عليه النحل أي مج<br/>فقام من رضابها في لج … بظاهر كقطع الخلنج<br/>أو العقار اعتللت بالمزج … غصت به فوهاء مثل ال'''بذج'''}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَذَج|head2=بُذَج}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:BehnstedtWoidich|WA1|pages=255–263}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=98b}}
* {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|pages=237–238}}

{{C|ar|Baby animals|Sheep}}
