Page 4219 برأ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
It is grouped at the root {{ar-root|ب ر ء}}, but borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܒܪܳܐ|tr=braʾ|t=to {{l|en|create}}}}. In Syriac the same root is more widespread, whereas in Arabic it is exotic – the verb appears in the {{l|en|Qur'an|Qurʾān}} in its finite form only in 57:22, and three times in the active participle form.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَرَأَ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.vn:بَرْء}}

# to [[create]], to bring into being
#: {{syn|ar|خَلَقَ|فَطَرَ|أَوْجَدَ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|57:22
|passage=مَا أَصَابَ مِن مُّصِيبَةٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَلَا فِي أَنْفُسِكُمْ إِلَّا فِي كِتَابٍ مِّن قَبْلِ أَن نَّبْرَأَهَا
|translation=No disaster strikes upon the earth or among yourselves except that it is in a register before we bring it into being.}}

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.vn:بَرْء}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II.vn:+,تَبْرِئَة}}

# to absolve, pardon, exonerate
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|33|69
|passage=يَا أَيُّهَا ٱلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا لَا تَكُونُوا كَٱلَّذِينَ آذَوْا مُوسَى '''فَبَرَّأَهُ''' ٱللَّهُ مِمَّا قَالُوا}}

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II.vn:+,تَبْرِئَة}}

====Related terms====
