Page 4237 براهمة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Ultimately from {{der|ar|sa|ब्राह्मण|tr=brā́hmaṇa}}. In a pseudo-etymology by Muslim scholars, it was said to come from the same root as {{m|ar|إِبْرَاهِيم}} in order to indicate an Abrahamic origin for Vedantic monotheism and to categorise Hindus as 'People of the Book'.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَرَاهِمَة}}

===Noun===
{{head|ar|noun}} {{attention|ar|added missing headword template- needs more}}

# ''a collective term for'' the [[brahmin]] caste
