===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|grc|Βαρθολομαῖος}}, from {{der|ar|arc|בר תלמי|tr=bar tolmai|gloss=son of [[Talmai]]; son of [[Ptolemy]]|pos=from {{af|arc|ברא|tr1=bra|gloss1=[[son]]|תלמי|tr2=tolmai|gloss2=[[Talmai]]; [[Ptolemy]]|nocat=1}}}}. It has long been unclear whether the Apostle's father was named after the biblical Talmai, king of Geshur, or one of the Greek Ptolemies, as the two originally unrelated names were conflated in {{w|Judeo-Aramaic languages|Jewish Aramaic}}.

