{{wp|lang=ar|بوط}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|cattail}} {{alter|ar|بُوط|بُوطَة}}
* {{sense|paper reed}} {{alter|ar|بَرْبِير}}

===Etymology===
Together with {{cog|la|buda|t=cattail}} declared a {{bor|ar|ber}} borrowing; though a connection to {{cog|xcl|պրտու|t=paper reed}} complicates this; maybe both the Armenian and Arabic have been mediated by {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, considering that the particular meaning of paper reed is distributed right in the historical Aramaic language area, and that {{cog|fa|بوری|tr=buri|id=reed}}, {{m|fa|بوریه|tr=buriya}}, {{m|fa|بوریه|tr=buriye|t=split reed, marsh reed; reed mat}} is expected from a source word ending ''-ītā'' in the [[emphatic state]]. Vollers lists the Arabic term under the “secure borrowings from Egyptian”, perhaps thinking about a semantic interference of {{sl|ar|cop|ⲃⲱ|t=bush|notext=1}} from {{der|ar|egx-dem|b|ts=*βoːʔ|t=bush}} from {{der|ar|egy|bꜣt|ts=*ˈbaːʀat|t=bush, especially paper reed}}; in Corriente’s last dictionary instead {{m|cop||[[ⲡⲓ-]][[ⲣⲱⲧ]]ⲓ ~ [[ⲣⲟϯ]]|t=overgrowths}} is suggested. But forms {{alter|ar|فَافِير|فَفِير|بَابِير|بَبِير}} employed for paper reed are secure borrowings from {{bor|ar|grc|πάπυρος}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بُرْدِيّ|بَرْدِيّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بُرْدِيّ|m|head2=بَرْدِيّ}}

# [[cattail]] ({{taxfmt|Typha|genus}} spp.)
# {{lb|ar|Egypt|Palestine}} [[paper reed]] ({{taxfmt|Cyperus papyrus|species}})
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|H|instead=1|lang=ar|page=86|passage=قد غلب عليها البربير وهو البرديُّ المعمول منه الطوامير ولم أعلم لما بمصر من هذا البربير نظيرًا بوجه الأرض إلّا ما بصقلّيَّة منه وأكثره يفتل حبالًا للمراكب وأقلُّه يعمل للسلطان منه طوامير لا تزيد على قدر كفايته|t=[And the swamplands of Palermo] were abounding in papyrus, that is paper reed, from which the scrolls where made. I know none on the face of the earth looking like that of Egypt except that of Sicily. From the bulk one plaits hawsers for the ships, and a rather small share is processed into scrolls for the ruler just as meets his demand.}}
#* {{R:ar:FAH|30|section=Nr. 973|page=87|passage=بَرْدِي: واحدة بردية، ويسمى الأباء والحَفَأ، وهو الخوص عند بعض الرواة، والخُوص أيصا هو القصب مثل البردي، […]|t=Paper reed, one is bardīya, is also called ''abāʾ'' and ''ḥafaʾ'', it is fronds amongst some pastoralists, and fronds is also a rush like the paper reed.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بُرْدِيّ|head2=بَرْدِيّ}}

