===Etymology 3===
[[File:Asphodelus tenuifolius VaraFloral 2010-7-02 LagunadelaMata.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|بَرْوَق}}|upright=1.14]]
From {{der|ar|arc|ברוק|tr=bārōq|t=yellow, pale, sickly looking}} so-called from its appearance; grayish colored leaves and yellowish flowers, which suggest the gloom of the underworld and the pallor of death. Note also {{doublet|ar|بَارُوق|notext=1|t1=white lead}} apparently from the same form.

