Page 4373 بريمة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Variant of {{m|ar|بِرِّينَة}}, see it. Later reinterpreted as {{bor|ar|arz|-}} {{ar-tool noun|lc=1}} from {{m|ar|بَرَمَ|t=to twist, to roll up etc.}}.{{ar-rootbox|ب ر م}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَرِّيمة|بِرِّيمَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَرِّيمة|f|head2=بِرِّيمَة|pl=بَرَارِيم}}

# [[drill]], [[gimlet]]
# [[corkscrew]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَرِّيمة|head2=بِرِّيمَة|pl=بَرَارِيم}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag}}
* {{R:ar:Baranov}}
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-3}}

{{C|ar|Tools|Kitchenware}}

-------- end text --------
Page 4374 برينة: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|بَرِّيمة|بَرَّانَة|بَرَّامَة}}

===Etymology===
Romanists derive from {{bor|ar|la|veruīna}}, whence {{cog|es|barrena}}, {{cog|la|barrina}}. The internal Arabic variant sound change {{m|ar||ن}} → {{m|ar||م}} is paralleled by {{m|ar|مِيجَم}}, {{m|ar|كرزن|كَرْزَم}}, {{m|ar|إِبْزِيم}}. However old {{m|ar|بَيْرَم|t=gimlet}} disallows pure Latin origin, and Classical Arabic likewise used {{m|ar|بَرَمَ}}, {{m|ar|أَبْرَمَ|t=to twist, to knot}}, hence a kind of twisted rope {{m|ar|بَرِيم}} and modern business language {{m|ar|بَرَمَ|t=to conclude, to settle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَرِّينة|بِرِّينَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَرِّينة|head2=بِرِّينَة|f|pl=بَرَارِين}}

# [[stake]], [[pale]]
#* {{RQ:Ibn al-ʿawwām|7|46|page=384 lines 2, 5 and 8|volume=1}} (we read for {{l|ar|برنية}} in this unreliable edition)
# [[drill]], [[screw]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَرِّينة|head2=بِرِّينَة|pl=بَرَارِين}}

===References===
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=135}}, with outlandish claim that “the variants with /m/ only result from ignorance or bad ear of Alcalá” – they are well known from Egyptian and Sudanese Arabic.

{{C|ar|Tools}}
-------- end text --------
Page 4375 بز: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2020|November|2}}<!--sense "garment"-->

===Etymology 1===
Cognate to {{cog|arc|בִּיזָא}}, {{m|syc|ܒܷܙܐ|tr=bizzā|t=teat}}, {{m|arc|בּוּזָא|tr=buzzā|t=teat}}, {{cog|uga|𐎁𐎑|t=teat}}. Differently {{cog|akk|𒍣𒍣𒂊|ts=zīzu|t=teat}}, {{cog|he|זִיז|tr=zīz|t=abundance, teat, protuberance}}, {{cog|he|דַּד|tr=dad|t=teat}}, {{cog|arc|דַּדָּא|tr=daddā|t=teat}}.
{{etymid|ar|mamma}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بِزّ|head2=بُزّ|m|pl=بِزَاز|pl2=أَبْزَاز}}

# {{senseid|ar|teat}}[[teat]], [[mamma]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بِزّ|head2=بُزّ|m|pl=بِزَاز|pl2=أَبْزَاز}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|بَزَّازَة|t=soother}}

===Etymology 2===
Ultimately a re-borrowing from what was originally a Semitic source ({{cog|akk|𒁍𒌋𒋗|tr=bu-u-ṣu|ts=būṣu}}); see also {{m|ar|بِزَّة|t=suit}}.
* Borrowed from {{bor|ar|xcl|բեհեզ|tr=}} or the earlier {{bor|ar|xcl||*բեեզ}}
* Alternatively, a {{clipping|ar|nocap=1}} of {{m|ar|بُزْيُون|t=a kind of silk garment}}, from {{bor|ar|gkm|βυσσίνη}}, or from {{der|ar|grc|βύσσος|t=a very fine yellowish [[flax]] and the [[linen]] woven from it}}.
{{etymid|ar|textum}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بَزّ|m|pl=بُزُوز}}

# {{senseid|ar|cloth}}{{lb|ar|now|_|regional}} [[garment]], [[raiment]], [[weed]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|tirmidhi|14|12
|passage=قَدِمَ بَزٌّ مِنَ ٱلشَّامِ لِفُلَانٍ الْيَهُودِيِّ
|translation=Some clothing arrived from the north for so-and-so, the Jew.}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|malik|31
|passage=قَالَ مَالِكٌ فِي الرَّجُلِ يَشْتَرِي الإِبِلَ أَوِ الْغَنَمَ أَوِ الْبَزَّ أَوِ الرَّقِيقَ أَوْ شَيْئًا مِنَ الْعُرُوضِ جِزَافًا إِنَّهُ لَا يَكُونُ الْجِزَافُ فِي شَىْءٍ مِمَّا يُعَدُّ عَدًّا.
|translation=Malik said about a man who bought camels and sheep and clothing and slaves and any larger good without measuring precisely that there is no wholesale acquisition of a thing that can be counted.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَزّ|pl=بُزُوز}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|بَزَّاز|t=garment salesman}}
* {{l|ar|بِزَازَة|t=garment trade}}
* {{l|ar|بَزَّ|t=to [[strip off]], to [[spoil]], to [[remove]] by [[force]]}}
* {{l|ar|اِبْتَزَّ|t=to [[strip off]], to [[spoil]], to [[remove]] by [[force]]}}

