===Etymology===
Synthetic [[quadriliteral]] verb ({{ar-form|Iq}}) derived from the consonants of the phrase {{m|ar|بِسْمِ اللّٰه|t=in the name of God}}.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|Iq}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} To say: {{m|ar||[[بسم الله|بِسْمِ الْلّٰهِ]] [[بسم الله الرحمن الرحيم|(الْرَحْمٰنِ الْرَحِيمِ)]]|tr=bismi llāhi [r-raḥmāni r-raḥīmi]|t=in the name of [[God]] [the Compassionate, the Merciful]}}.
# {{lb|ar|Christianity}} To recite the [[w:Trinitarian formula|Trinitarian formula]] ({{m|ar|بِاسْمِ الْأَبِ وَالِابْنِ وَالرُّوحِ الْقُدُسِ|tr=bi-smi l-ʔabi wa-l-ibni wa-r-rūḥi l-qudusi|gloss=In the name of the [[Father]], the [[Son]], and the [[Holy Spirit]]}})

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|Iq}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|بِسْمِ اللّٰه|gloss=in the name of [[God]]}}
* {{l|ar|بِسْمِ اللّٰهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيمِ|gloss=in the name of [[God]], the Compassionate, the Merciful}}
* {{l|ar|حَمْدَلَ|gloss=To say {{m|ar|الْحَمْدُ لِلّٰهِ}}}}
* {{l|ar|حَوْقَلَ|gloss=To say {{m|ar|لَا حَوْلَ وَلَا قُوَّةَ إِلَّا بِاللّٰهِ}}}}
* {{l|ar|كَبَّرَ|gloss=To say the [[takbir]]}}
