===Etymology===
Akin to {{cog|he|בָּצָל|tr=bāṣā́l}}, {{cog|phn|𐤁𐤑𐤋}}, {{cog|arc|בּוּצְלָא|tr=būṣlā}}, {{cog|syc|ܒܶܨܠܳܐ|tr=beṣlā}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩨𐩮𐩡}}, {{cog|gdq|béṣál|sc=Latn}}, {{cog|shv|béṣál}}, {{cog|sqt|biṣle}}. With a sound change it is also found in {{cog|akk|bisru|𒁉𒄑𒊒|tr=bisru, bišru; biṣru|t=leek, a plant or bulb covered in a skin}}, a variation influenced or conflated with {{cog|akk|biṣrum|𒁉𒄑𒀸|tr=biṣrum|t=container, pouch, wrapping}}, related also to {{cog|akk|𒁍𒊻𒍪𒊒𒌝|tr=buṣṣurum|t=to tear apart, to peel}} specifically attested about garlic (a type of onion) and {{cog|akk|biṣṣūrum|𒁉𒄑𒍪𒀸|tr=biṣṣūrum|t=vulva, labia, folds of skin}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَصَل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|بَصَل|sing=بَصَلَة}}

# [[onion]](s)
# [[bulb]](s)

