===Etymology===
In view of the {{cog|xsa|-}} {{bor|ar|sem-srb|𐩨𐩶𐩡}}, attested once from the 1<sup>st</sup> century {{CE}}, Arabic has more likely borrowed thence and not from {{cog|gez|በቅል}} as formerly claimed, but the {{cog|sem-osa}} may be an {{w|Old Arabic}} loanword as well, mule breeding only introduced not long before from the North, thus an {{unk|ar|nocap=1}}-origin borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَغْل}}

===Noun===
