===Etymology===
According to Ibn Manzor the name derives from the root {{m|ar|بكَّ|t=to be crowded, to throng, to pester}}. Popular etymology has it that it comes instead from the vb. {{m|ar|بَكَى|t=to cry}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَكَّة}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|بَكَّة|f}}

# [[Bakkah]] is a toponym mentioned in the [[Quran]] (3:96) as the ancient name of the city of Mecca
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3|96
|passage=إِنَّ أَوَّلَ بَيْتٍ وُضِعَ لِلنَّاسِ لَلَّذِي بِ'''بَكَّةَ''' مُبَارَكًا وَهُدًى لِلْعَالَمِينَ
|t=The first temple (literally, "House [of God]") established for mankind was that at Bakkah - blessed and a guidance for the worlds.
|subst=لِلنَّاسِ/لِ-نْ-نَاسِ,وَهُدًى/وَ-هُدًى,لِلْعَالَمِينَ/لِ-لْ-عَالَمِينَ,بِ'''بَكَّةَ'''/بِ-'''بَكَّةَ''',لَلَّذِي/لَ-لَّذِي
}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَكَّة:di|state=ind-def}}

===References===
* [http://lisaan.net/بكك/#335cb3a188c7674d32859c9a17efaf2a Asaas al-Balaaghah by al-Zamakhshari (d. 1143 CE)]
* [http://lisaan.net/%d8%a8%d9%83%d9%83/#d817d095a5b03ea29df297034d44abcf Al-Muhkam wal Muheet al-Aadham by Ibn Seedah al-Mursi (d. 1066 CE)]
-------- end text --------
