Page 4634 بلس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
A borrowing from probably {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, found also in {{cog|am|-}} / {{cog|ti|-}} / {{cog|tig|-}} / {{w|Gurage languages|Gurage}} / {{cog|gez|በለስ|t=fig}} which passed into {{cog|ssy|በለስ|sc=Ethi|tr=balas}} and {{cog|byn|በለሳ}} and hapax in the {{w|Book of Amos|Amos}} 7, 14 {{cog|he|בֹּולֵס|tr=bōlēs|t=nipping the unripe sycomore to further its ripening|pos=active participle}}; no further cognates are known if not {{cog|egy|nbs|t={{taxlink|Ziziphus spina-christi|species}} tree and fruit}} compared by {{w|Ludwig Köhler (Theologe)|lang=de|Koehler}}-{{w|Walter Baumgartner (Theologe)|lang=de|Baumgartner}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|بَلَس}}, dialectally also {{ar-IPA|بِلِس}} and {{ar-IPA|بُلُس}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|بَلَس|m|sing=بَلَسَة}} {{tlb|ar|Yemen}}

# {{C|ar|Mulberry family plants}} [[fig]] (tree and fruit)
# {{C|ar|Cacti}} [[Indian fig]], [[prickly pear]] (plant and fruit)

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|بَلَس}}

===Etymology 2===
Elsewhere {{m|ar|عَدَس}}, of which also {{cog|ar|عَلَس|t=emmer}} is a variant.

====Alternative forms====
