Page 4648 بلغت القلوب الحناجر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Literally ”the hearts [have] reached the throats”. [[w:Al-Qurtubi|Qurtubi]] explains that the hearts have reached the throats from fear, and if the throat were not narrow enough they would have left the bodies. [[w:Fakhr al-Din al-Razi|Razi]] exposes that due to the extremely high heart rate caused by fear the person might feel as if their heart were about to leave the body.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَلَغَتِ الْقُلُوبُ الْحَنَاجِرَ}}

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=[[بَلَغَ|بَلَغَتِ]] [[قَلْب|الْقُلُوبُ]] [[حَنْجَرَة|الْحَنَاجِرَ]]}}

# {{lb|ar|idiomatic}} felt extreme fear.
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|33:10
|passage=إِذْ جَاؤُوكُمْ مِن فَوْقِكُمْ وَمِنْ أَسْفَلَ مِنْكُمْ وَإِذْ زَاغَتِ الأَبْصَارُ وَ'''بَلَغَتِ الْقُلُوبُ الْحَنَاجِرَ''' وَتَظُنُّونَ بِاللّٰهِ الظُّنُونَا
|translation=[Remember] when they came at you from above you and from below you, and when the gazes shifted, and '''the hearts reached the throats''' and you assumed about Allah assumptions.
|subst=وَ/وَ-}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|زَاغَتِ الأَبْصَارُ}}

[[Category:Arabic terms derived from the Qur'an]]
-------- end text --------
