Page 4702 بندق: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Noisettes (CORABEL)-1-cliche Jean Weber (23379638180).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|بُنْدُق}}|upright=1.2]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|فُنْدُق|بُنْدُوق||archaic|dialectal}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|pal|pndk'||[[hazelnut]]|tr=pondik}}, from {{der|ar|grc|-}} [{{m|grc|Ποντικόν κάρυον|κάρυον|tr=-}}] {{m|grc|Ποντικόν κάρυον|Ποντικόν|[[Pontic]] [[nut]]|tr=káruon Pontikón}}, q.v. From hazelnuts, the sense spread to similarly shaped pebbles used in slings and similar projectile weapons and then to early muskets. In some dialects, the word then came to be used for the slingshots and muskets themselves.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بُنْدُق}}
** {{IPA|acw|/bun.duɡ/|[bʊn.dʊɡ]|a=Hijazi}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|بُنْدُق|sing=بُنْدُقَة|pl=بَنَادِق}}

# [[hazelnut]]
# {{lb|ar|archaic|_|or|_|historical}} [[bullet]]
#: {{ux|ar|بُنْدُق [[ال]][[رصاص|رَصَاص]]}}
# {{lb|ar|dialectal|Yemen|Oman|rural|_|Egypt}} [[gun]], [[rifle]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|بُنْدُق|sing=بُنْدُقَة|pl=بَنَادِق}}

