Page 4751 بهق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Compare {{cog|he|בֹּהַק|tr=bohaq}}, {{cog|arc|בָּהֲקָא|tr=bāhăqā}}, {{cog|gez|ዐበቅ}}, {{cog|ti|ዓብቅ}}, {{cog|am|ዓበቅ}}, {{cog|akk|𒅁𒄣|ts=epqu|t=leprosy, white marks}}, also denoting skin diseases, and {{cog|ar|عَبَاقِيَة|t=a kind of scar in the cheek}}, {{cog|gez|በክ|t=scab, wound}}. The {{cog|arc|בָּהַק|tr=bāhaq|t=to shine, to be white, to glisten}}, can be potentially connected semantically as well to {{noncog|arc|בָּהַר|tr=bāhar|t=to shine bright}}, {{cog|he|בָּהַר|tr=bāhar}}, {{noncog|arc|בַּהְרָא|tr=baherā|t=bright skin spot}}, {{noncog|he|בַּהֶרֶת|tr=bahəre|t=bright skin spot}}, found as the {{noncog|ar|بَهَرَ|tr=|t=to shine brightly}}, whereas in Ethiopia there is {{noncog|gez|በርሀ|t=to shine bright}}, {{noncog|tig|በርሃ|t=to shine bright}}, {{noncog|ti|በርሄ|t=to shine bright}}, {{noncog|am|በራ|tr=bärra|t=to shine}}. The Arabic word may be specifically from {{bor|ar|arc|בהקיתא}} / {{m|syc|ܒܗܩܝܬܐ|tr=behqīṯā}} denoting a skin disease, omitting the ending.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَهَق|m}}

# skin [[disease]] like [[vitiligo]] or [[poliosis]]
# [[lichen]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَهَق}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|أَبْهَق|t=affected by the disease termed {{l-self|ar|بَهَق}}}}
* {{l|ar|بَهَّقَ|t=to transmit the disease termed {{l-self|ar|بَهَق}} to}}
* {{l|ar|تَبَهَّقَ|t=to be affected by the disease termed {{l-self|ar|بَهَق}}}}
* {{l|ar|اِنْبَهَقَ|t=to be affected by the disease termed {{l-self|ar|بَهَق}}}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|bor=1|axm|բահաղ|պահաղ|պահակ}}
* {{desc|fa|بهق|tr=bahaq|بهک|tr2=bahak|bor=1}}

