* The sense of a pipe and the sense of a vehicle’s horn is from {{bor|ar|ota|بورو|tr=boru|t=duct, pipe, tube; horn}}. {{doublet|ar|بُرْغِيّ|t1=screw}}.
* The Egyptian Arabic name of the fish comes from {{der|ar|cop|ⲫⲟⲣⲓ|t=''[[Mugil cephalus]]''}} – so in [[Bohairic]], also {{m|cop|ϥⲟⲣⲓ}}, while in [[Sahidic]] it is {{m|cop|ⲃⲱⲣⲉ}}; the relation with {{cog|ja|鰡}} / {{m|ja|鯔|tr=bora}} denoting the same species of fish is enigmatic.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|بُورِي|m}}

# {{C|ar|Breads}}{{lb|ar|Kuwait}} a type of [[thin]] [[bread]] made with [[excessive]] amount of [[oil]]; Indian fried bread
# {{lb|ar|Iraq}} [[pipe]]
# {{C|ar|Auto parts}}{{lb|ar|Saudi Arabia}} [[motor vehicle]]'s [[horn]]
# {{C|ar|Fish}}{{lb|ar|Egypt|Morocco}} [[mullet]] (''[[Liza]]'' spp. and especially {{taxfmt|Mugil cephalus|species}})

