Page 4818 بوق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Natively derived from the root {{ar-root|ب|و|ق}}, concerning concepts related to "trumpets" or "a sudden loud blast of sound"; hence the meaning of "a sudden striking calamity" and by extension "an evil" or "wrongful conduct". Ultimately related to the root {{ar-root|ب|ق|ق}}, meaning "the buzzing of insects", "to be loud or noisy", "to be obnoxiously talkative", with likely {{psm|ar|grc|βούκινο|nocap=1}} or {{noncog|la|būcina}}, borrowed itself as {{noncog|syc|ܒܘܩ̈ܝܢܐܣ|tr=bwqynʾ|ts=būqīnā}}. Compare {{noncog|en|bugle}}, an ox or bovid horn.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بُوق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بُوق|m|pl=أَبْوَاق|pl2=بُوقَات}}

# {{lb|ar|musical instruments}} [[trumpet]], [[conch]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 965|author=w:Al-Mutanabbi|title=[http://www.adab.com/modules.php?name=Sh3er&doWhat=shqas&qid=5612 {{lang|ar|لَيَالِيَّ بَعْدَ الظَّاعِنِينَ شُكُولُ}}]|text=إِذَا كَانَ بَعْضُ النَّاسِ سَيْفًا لِدَوْلَةٍ // فَفِي النَّاسِ '''بُوقَاتٌ''' لَهَا وَطُبُولُ}}
# {{lb|ar|figuratively}} presenting [[falsities]] [[deliberately]] as true, [[lie]]; by comparison to [[embellishment]]s and [[pomp]], making a lot of [[useless]] [[noise]]
# {{lb|ar|figuratively}} one who does not [[conceal]] [[secret]]s, [[announce]]s to [[all]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بُوق|pl=أَبْوَاق|pl2=بُوقَات}}

