Page 4863 بيرم: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|بَارَم}}

===Etymology===
Possibly an artificial word from {{m|ar|بَرَمَ|t=to twist, to shape, to contort}}, unless these verbs are denominal from the instruments, compare {{m|ar|بَرَى|t=to trim, to nib}} and {{m|ar|بَرَدَ|t=to file, to pare}}, though this is also suspect of {{bor|ar|ira-mid|-}} borrowing. Arabic tradition usually claims that “{{m|ar|مُخْل}} is Greek and {{m-self|ar||بَيْرَم}} is Persian”, but Vullers in his Persian–Latin dictionary lists the Persian as from Arabic, and indeed Dihḵudā’s quote for the word is from [[w:Muhammad ibn Ahmad al-Khwarizmi|al-Ḵwarizmī]]’s originally Arabic {{m|ar||مفاتيح العلوم|tr=mafātīḥ al-ʕulūm}}, and surely at least the {{cog|syc|ܒܝܪܡܐ}} only given by {{w|Bar Bahlul}} is from Arabic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|بَيْرَم}}

===Noun===
