Page 4895 بيلسان: -------- begin text --------
<!-- ar.Wikipedia being “smart” as often by using variants of the same polysemous plant name to name the botanical articles -->
[[File:Opoponax1.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|[[راتينج|رَاتِينَج]] بلَسَان}} ({{taxlink|Commiphora guidottii|species}})|upright=1.15]]
[[File:Бузина elderberry 2.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|[[ثمر|ثَمْر]] بَيلَسَان}} ({{taxfmt|Sambucus nigra|species}})|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|بَلَسَان|بَلْسَم|بِلْسَام}}
* {{alter|ar|بَشَام}}

===Etymology===
The form {{m|ar|بَشَام}} belongs to the root {{ar-root|ب ش م}} with meanings related to indigestion, nausea, disgust. Via the idea of luxury, abundance, and indulgence; to overeat, over-indulge, to be surfeit, this compares to the contronymic significance of the root associated with {{noncog|ar|طَلْح|t=''[[Vachellia]]''}}.

Compare {{cog|he|בְּשָׂם|tr=bəśām}}, {{m|he|בָּשָׂם|tr=bāśām}}, {{m|he|בֶּשֶׂם|tr=beśem|t=sweet spice or smell}}, {{m|he|בושם|בֹּשֶׂם|tr=bṓśem|t=scent}}, {{cog|syc|ܒܣܡܐ|tr=besāmā|t=sweetness}}, {{m|syc|ܒܘܣܡܐ|tr=bussemā|t=delight, abundance}}, {{m|syc|ܒܣܡܐ|tr=besmā|t=scent}}, other {{cog|arc|בֻּשְׂםָא|tr=buśmā}} / {{m|arc|בֻּסְםָא|tr=busmā|t=sweet spice or smell}}, related to a profuse root {{m|he|ב־ס־מ}} / {{syc-root-entry|ܒ|ܣ|ܡ}} forming meanings concerning sweetness, joy, pleasure, and also feasting.

Such meanings root in a plant name, {{der|ar|ira-pro|*hampr̥sā|t=juniper}}, possibly borrowed early into {{m+|ar|بَشَام}} from {{bor|ar|he|בָּשָׂם|tr=bāśām}}, while all other forms of this Arabic plant name are from {{bor|ar|grc|βάλσαμον}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|بَيْلَسَان|m}}

# {{taxfmt|Commiphora|genus}} gen. et spp., syns. ''[[Balsamodendron]]'', {{taxlink|Balsamea|genus}}
# {{taxfmt|Impatiens|genus}} gen. et spp.
# {{taxfmt|Sambucus nigra|species}} ([[black elder]], tree and fruit)
# {{taxfmt|Myroxylon|genus}}, especially {{taxlink|Myroxylon balsamum|species}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|بَيْلَسَانٌ}}

