===Etymology===
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*(s)teg-|id=cover}}
From {{bor|ar|xpr||tr=tāg}}, attested in {{m|xpr|𐫟𐫀𐫡𐫤𐫀𐫃||ts=xārtāg|t=crown of thorns}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|ine-pro|*(s)teg-||to cover}}. Related to {{cog|ar|تَخْت||t=bed, couch...}}, also an Iranian borrowing; and to {{cog|arc|תָּגָא|tr=tāḡā}}.

Attested as {{m|ar|sc=Nbat|𐢞𐢄|tr=tj|t=crown}} {{qual|Nabatean script}} in the 4th-century {{w|Namara inscription}}.<ref name=Sayyadani>{{lang|fa|علی صیادانی، [https://rjhll.basu.ac.ir/article_973_41fcb7d848219f116e2c2d63a569f22e.pdf وام‌واژه‌های فارسی دیوان ابن هانی؛ شاعر شیعه اندلس], [https://rjhll.basu.ac.ir/ پژوهش‌های زبان‌شناسی تطبیقی]، ص ۱۵۵}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|تَاج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَاج|m|pl=تِيجَان}}

# [[crown]]
#: {{ux|ar|[[صحة|الصِّحَّةُ]] '''تَاجٌ''' [[عَلَى]] [[رأس|رُؤُوسِ]] [[صحيح|الْأَصِحَّاءِ]] [[لَا]] [[رأى|يَرَاهُ]] [[إِلَّا]] [[مريض|الْمَرْضَى]].|Health is '''a crown''' on the heads of the healthy, that only the ill can see.}}

