Page 4998 تاجر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Synchronically analyzable as {{ar-active participle|lc=1}} of {{m|ar|تَجَرَ|t=to [[trade]], to [[conduct]] [[commerce]]}} from the root {{ar-root|ت|ج|ر}}, and the original is presumably a borrowing of the noun of {{bor|ar|syc|ܬܓܪܐ|tr=taggārā}} or a dialectal form of it with different vocalization, ultimately through a ''*tangār'' from {{der|ar|akk|tamkārum|𒁮𒃼|tr=tamkārum|t=trader}} derived from the root which is in {{ar-root|م ك ر|nocat=1}} related to scheming, whereby the verb is [[denominative]], and the singular form of the Arabic noun bearing the form of an active participle has then been innovated in Arabic, other derivations under the root following suit to these new terms.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|تَاجِر}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-تاجر.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَاجِر|m|pl=تَاجِرُونَ|pl2=تُجَّار|f=تَاجِرَة}}

# [[merchant]], [[trader]], [[businessman]], [[dealer]], [[tradesman]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|تَاجِر|pl=تَاجِرُونَ|pl2=تُجَّار|f=تَاجِرَة|fpl=تَاجِرَات|fpl2=تَوَاجِرُ}}

