====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|تَبَع|m|sing=تَبَع|singg=m|sing2=تَبَعِيّ|sing2g=m|pl=أَتْبَاع}}

# [[follower]](s)

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَبَع}}

===Etymology 3===
{{unc|ar}}. {{w|Edward William Lane|Lane}} claims that it is from the root {{ar-root|ت|ب|ع}}, in reference to how when one king died, his successor would follow his policies. The unusual plural pattern suggests a borrowing from {{der|ar|sem-osa}}, but the cognate root in those languages likely has the same meaning of "follow", and is only attested in theophoric names.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|تُبَّع|m|pl=تَبَابِعَة}}

# a [[king]] in ancient [[Yemen]]; the ruler of [[Himyar]] and [[Hadramawt]]

