Page 5207 تحت: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Originally a case form of a defective noun {{m|ar|تَحْت||[[location]] that is [[below]]}}; see the usage note. From the root {{ar-root|ت ح ت}}. Related to {{cog|he|תַּחַת}}, {{cog|gez|ታሕት }}, {{cog|uga|𐎚𐎈𐎚|ts=taḥta}} and {{cog|syc|ܬܰܚܬ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|تَحْتُ}}
* {{IPA|afb|/ˈtɐħət/|a=Gulf}}

====Adverb====
{{ar-adv|تَحْتُ}}

# [[below]]

=====Usage notes=====
This originates as a case form of a defective noun {{m|ar|تَحْت||[[location]] that is [[below]]}}. It is declined normally when definite, e.g. {{m|ar||التَّحْتُ|the [[location]] that is [[below]]}}. Other forms are the adverbial accusative in the preposition {{m|ar|تَحْتَ||[[below]]}}, the genitive in the expression {{m|ar|مِنْ تَحْتِ||[[from]] [[below]], [[below]]}} (also with an attached pronoun, as in {{m|ar||مِنْ تَحْتِهَا|([[from]]) [[below]] it}}), and the irregular expression {{m|ar|مِنْ تَحْتُ||(from) [[below]]}}.

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Lane|تحت}}

===Etymology 2===
{{adverbial accusative|ar|تَحْت||[[location]] that is [[below]]}}. Related to {{cog|he|תַּחַת|tr=tákhat}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|تَحْتَ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-تحت.ogg}}

====Preposition====
{{ar-prep|تَحْتَ}}

# [[under]]
#: {{ux|ar|جَلَسْتُ '''تَحْتَ''' شَجَرَةِ ٱلزَّيْتُونِ وَٱسْتَمْتَعْتُ بِنَسِيمِ ٱلْهَوَاءِ ٱلْعَلِيلِ.|I sat under the olive tree and enjoyed the gentle breeze.}}

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|تَحْتَ}}

-------- end text --------
