Page 5465 ترف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Probably from {{bor|ar|arc|תרף}} / {{m|syc|ܬܪܦ|tr=trap̄}}. Its meanings “to sink in, to disappear; to be or become soft, to become digested or dissolved; to perish, to become ruined” are apparently from a basic meaning “to remain behind” as evidenced by {{w|South Semitic}} languages, widely used in {{cog|sem-eth|-}}, {{cog|gez|ተርፈ}}, {{m|gez|ተረፈ}} as ”to be left behind” and then from “to be left over” “to be excessive, to be superfluous”, {{cog|xsa|𐩩𐩧𐩰|t=to be left over, to remain, to be residual}}, and in the other direction {{cog|sqt|terof|t=to be in good health}}. Surely an ancient agglutination of feminine or reflexive prefix to a stem equivalent to that of {{m|ar|رَفَّ|t=to flutter; to flare}}, thence also causative {{m|ar|رَفَأَ|t=to patch, to apply something on top to fix; to leave (the ship) behind, to dock}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.nopass.vn:تَرَف}}

# to [[live]] in [[luxury]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.nopass.vn:تَرَف}}<!--cannot override active participle with تَرِف-->

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|تَرَف|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|تَرِفَ|form=I}}
# [[luxury]], [[opulence]], [[affluence]]
# [[effemination]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَرَف|m}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|تُرْفَة|تَرَافَة}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# to [[spoil]], to [[render]] [[effeminate]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|تَرِف}}

# [[luxurious]], [[opulent]], [[delicate]]
# [[effeminate]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|أَتْرَفَ|t=to live in opulence; to make opulent; to make effeminate}}
* {{l|ar|تَتَرَّفَ|t=to live in luxury}}
* {{l|ar|اِسْتَتْرَفَ|t=to behave arrogantly}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb-form|تَرِفُّ|I}}

# {{inflection of|ar|رَفَّ||2|m|s|non-past|actv|indc}}
# {{inflection of|ar|رَفَّ||3|f|s|non-past|actv|indc}}

====Verb====
