* {{l|ar|تَرَّكَ}}
* {{l|ar|اِسْتَتْرَكَ}}

===Etymology 4===
From {{m|ar|تُرْك|gloss=[[Turks]]}}, with the second triliteral conjugation implying the bestowing of a particular quality. Compare {{m|ar|عَرَّبَ|gloss=to [[Arabize]], to make [[Arab]]}}, {{m|ar|هَوَّدَ|gloss=to [[Judaize]], to make [[Jewish]]}}, {{m|ar|أَمْرَكَ|gloss=to [[Americanize]], to make [[American]]}}، {{m|ar|فَرْنَسَ|gloss=to [[gallicize|Gallicize]], to make [[French]]}}, {{m|ar|أَلْمَنَ|gloss=to [[Germanize]], to make [[German]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|تَرَّكَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[Turkify]], to make [[Turkish]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ar|تُرْكِيَّا|gloss=[[Turkey]]}}
* {{l|ar|تُرْكِيّ|gloss=[[Turk]], [[Turkish]]}}
* {{l|ar|تَتَرَّكَ|gloss=to be Turkified, to act Turkish}}

