{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|دِرْيَاق|تِرْيَاقَة}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|[[תִּירְיָיקָא]] / [[תִּרְיָיקָא]] / [[תִּירְיָאקָא]] / [[תִּרְיָאקָא]]|tr=teryāqā}}, {{m|arc|[[תִּירְיָיקִי]] / [[תִּרְיָיקִי]] / [[תִּירְיָקִי]] / [[תִּרְיָקִי]]|tr=teryāqī}} / {{m|syc|[[ܬܸܪܝܲܩܹܐ]] / [[ܬܸܪܝܲܩܹܝ]]|tr=teryaqē}}, from {{der|ar|grc|θηριακή|t=antidote}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|تِرْيَاق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تِرْيَاق|m|pl=تَرَايِيق}}

# [[antidote]], [[counter]]-[[remedy]], [[panacea]], [[antitoxin]], [[theriac]], [[treacle]]
#: {{syn|ar|شِيلْثَا|مُضَادّ}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|muslim|36|215|passage=إِنَّ فِي عَجْوَةِ العَالِيَةِ شِفَاءً أَوْ إِنَّهَا '''تِرْيَاقٌ''' أَوَّلَ البُكْرَةِ|translation=The pressed dates of Aliya contain healing effects and are an antidote in the early morning.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 1350|author=w:Ibn Qayyim al-Jawziyya|title=aṭ-ṭibb an-nabawī|trans-title=The Prophetic Medicine
|passage=بِغَمْسِ الذُّبَابِ فِي الطَّعَامِ إِذَا سَقَطَ فِيهِ لِأَجْلِ الشِّفَاءِ الَّذِي فِي جِنَاحِهِ، وَهُوَ '''كَالتِّريَاقِ''' لِلسُّمِّ
|translation=Dipping house flies in food if they fall in for the healing effects in their wings, which is like an antitoxin.
|tr=biḡamsi ḏ-ḏubābi fī ṭ-ṭaʿāmi ʾiḏā saqaṭa fīhi li-ʾajli š-šifāʾi llaḏī fī jināḥihi, wahuwa '''ka-t-tiryāqi''' li-s-summi}}
# {{lb|ar|poetic}} [[alcohol]], [[intoxicating]] [[drink]]
#: {{syn|ar|عُقَار|رَاح|نَبِيذ|خَمْر|مُدَام}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|تِرْيَاق|pl=تَرَايِيق}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|تِرْيَاق كَبِير|t=[[Venice treacle]], ''[[theriaca magna]]''}}

