Page 5653 تشريع: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Verbal noun of {{m|ar|شَرَّعَ}} From the root {{ar-root|ش|ر|ع}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَشْرِيع|m|pl=تَشْرِيعَات}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|شَرَّعَ|form=II}}
# [[legislation]] (an [[Arabic]] term used by the [[Fuqaha]], or Muslim jurists. Literally it means the process of legislation. Technically it means the establishing of [[Shari'a]] law, elucidating the rulings and canonizing the law.)
# legal [[restriction]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَشْرِيع|pl=تَشْرِيعَات}}
-------- end text --------
Page 5654 تشريعي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-etym-nisba|تَشْرِيع|t=legislation}}, from the root {{ar-root|ش|ر|ع}} meaning “a means of access to something”, “a manner or way to something”, a “way or course”, hence by extension a “way of doing things”, a “law or established custom”, a “rule or legislation”.

===Adjective===
{{ar-nisba|تَشْرِيعِيّ}}

# [[legislative]], [[lawmaking]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|تَشْرِيعِيّ|pl=sp}}
-------- end text --------
