===Etymology===
{{m|ar|تَعَدُّد||being more than one, manifoldness}} + {{m|ar|قُدَماء||old ones, eternal ones}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَعَدُّدُ الْقُدَماءِ|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam|philosophy}} “[[manifoldness]] of [[eternal]] [[entity|entities]]”: the idea that anything other than [[God]] the [[Creator]] himself is eternal without beginning; {{non-gloss definition|the term has been used by critics, such as the rationalist [[Mu'tazila]], to qualify the following [[Sunni]] dogma as contrary to [[monotheism]]: namely that God’s characteristics, such as omnipotence or omniscience, and also the [[Quran]] are not themselves God, but are nevertheless eternal and uncreated}}
