===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ت م م}}
Cognate with {{cog|he|תם|tr=tám}}.

====Pronunciation====
* Verb: {{ar-IPA|تَمَّ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.ipass?.vn:تَمّ,تِمّ,تُمّ,تَمَام,تِمَام,تُمَام,تَمَامَة,تِمَامَة}}

# to be [[fulfill]]ed, to be [[complete]]d
# {{lb|ar|proscribed}} to [[come about]], to [[happen]], to [[take place]]
# to [[persist]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<in something>}}
# to [[continue]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<something/doing something>}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Particularly in newspaper and media style, {{m|ar|تَمَّ}} is often used with a verbal noun as its subject to express the English passive:
:: {{ux|ar|تَمَّ ٱعْتِقالُ عَدَدٍ مِنَ ٱلْعَناصِرِ ٱلْإرْهابِيَّةِ فِي ٱلْقاهِرَةِ لَيْلَةَ ٱلْأَمْسِ.|t=A number of terrorist militants were arrested in Cairo last night.}}

