Page 6276 تمر: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Świeży daktyl MEDJOOL1.jpg|thumb|right|{{l-self|ar|تَمْر|tr=-}}]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{ajp-IPA|tamr<p:tæmʌr>}}
* {{audio|ajp|تمر TAHMUR tamer. Arabic word for fruit of the palm tree (edible date).wav|a=United States}}

===Etymology 1===
As a widely cultivated plant, the native distribution of the date-palm even in earlier antiquity is questionable. Particular terms relating to date culture, like {{m|ar|شِيص|t=unfecundated dates}}, {{m|ar|قَسْب|t=dried dates}}, and {{m|ar|كَافُور|id=bract|t=bract of the inflorescence of the date palm}} can be borrowed. Assuming that {{doublet|ar|ثَمَر|t1=fruits|notext=1}}, and {{cog|sem-srb|𐩻𐩣𐩧|t=fruits|ts=ṯamar}}, is the same word generalized from an original meaning “dates”, the present word {{m-self|ar|تَمْر}} and {{cog|sem-srb|𐩩𐩣𐩧|t=dates|ts=tamr}} are declared, together with {{der|ar|he|תָּמָר|tr=tāmār}}, reborrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|תמרא}} / {{m|syc|ܬܡܪܬܐ|ܬܡܪܐ|tr=tamrē|t=dates}}, in which language only {{cog|sem-pro||*ṯ}} {{IPAchar|/θ/}} becomes ''t'' {{IPAchar|/t/}}, and the vowel ''a'' is reduced to ''ə'' and then ''∅'' in such position.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|تَمْر|sing=تَمْرَة|pl=تُمُور}}

# [[date]] (fruit)

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|تَمْر|sing=تَمْرَة|pl=تُمُور|pl2=تَمَرَات}}

=====Derived terms=====
