===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|م ر د}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*marad-|t=to fortify, to set up resistance; to escape, to find a means to get away; to leave one's people, to branch off or split from a group}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|מרדנות|tr=mardanút}}, {{cog|arc|מִרְדָּא|tr=mirdā}}, {{cog|syc|ܡܪܕܐ|tr=merdā}}, {{cog|myz|tr=MYRDʾ|ࡌࡉࡓࡃࡀ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|تَمَرَّدَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|V.ipass}}

# to [[rebel]], to [[revolt]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<against someone/something>}}
#* '''10th century''', {{w|Al-Mutanabbi}}
#*: {{quote|ar|إِذَا أَنْتَ أَكْرَمْتَ الْكَرِيمَ مَلَكْتَهُ / وَإِنْ أَنْتَ أَكْرَمْتَ اللَّئِيمَ '''تَمَرَّدَا'''|t=}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=2004|translator=هادي السيد ياسين|author={{w|Ali Shari'ati|{{l|ar||عَلِيّ شَرِيعَتِي}}}}|title=النباهة والاستحمار|publisher=دار الأمير|passage=إِنَّ أَكْبَرَ قِيَمِ الإِنْسَانِ هِيَ تِلْكَ الَّتِي يَبْدَأُ مِنْهَا (بِالرَّفْضِ) وَ(عَدَمِ التَّسْلِيمِ) اللَّذَيْنِ يَتَلَخَّصَانِ بِكَلِمَةِ (لَا) وَمِنْهَا بَدَأَ آدَمٌ أَبُو البَشَرِ.. أُمِرَ أَنْ لَا يَأْكُلَ مِنْ تِلْكَ الثَّمَرَةِ، لٰكِنَّهُ اَكَلَ، فَصَارَ بَعْدَئِذٍ بَشَرًا وَهَبَطَ إِلَىٰ الأَرْضِ، وِإِلَّا لَكَانَ مَلَكًا لَا مِيزَةَ لَهُ، وَلَصَارَ غَيْرُهُ آدَمَ وَلَفُرِضَ عَلَيْهِ أَنْ يَسْجُدَ أَمَامَهُ، لَكِنَّهُ '''تَمَرَّدَ''' فَصَارَ آدَم.
|translation=For sure the biggest human value is that from which s/he begings by "refusing" and "not consenting" that are summarised in the word "no" and from it began Adam the father of humanity.. He had been ordered not to eat from that fruit, but he ate, and henceforth he became a human and landed on Earth, if he had not he would have been an angel with no distinguishing feature, and someone else would have become Adam and he would have been obliged to prostrate before him, but he '''rebelled''' and so he became Adam.}}
# to be [[arrogant]], to be [[insolent]]
# to be [[uncooperative]], to be [[disobedient]]

