Page 6407 تنوب: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Ялина європейська.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|تَنُّوب}}|upright=1.15]]
{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|ar}} origin; due to the date of its record appearance, it seems less likely to be from {{sl|ar|de|Tannenbaum|notext=1}}, although it may play a factor in its later association with Christmas. The connection to {{noncog|hit|𒄑𒋫𒈾𒀀𒌑|tr={{sup|GIŠ}}ta-na-a-ú|ts=tanau|t=fir}} also is a challenge due to the lack of intermediaries; for more see {{m|de|Tanne}}. Perhaps there is a connection to {{ar-root|ن ي ب}} in {{m|ar|نَاب}} dealing with sharp points, with Semitic glosses like “fang, tusk, pincer, honeybee, stingers, shaped like a long tooth”. This could be a reference to either the sharp and pointed pine needles, or even the general pointed cone shape of the tree.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|تَنُّوب}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَنُّوب|m}}

# [[spruce]] ({{taxfmt|Picea|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|page=165|line=11|instead=1|lang=ar}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|page=169|line=11|instead=1|lang=ar}}
#* {{RQ:Qazwiniy:1849|1|page=250}}
#* {{quote-journal|1=ar|work=AlQuds.com|url=http://www.alquds.com/articles/1543782796435438900/|title=ar:فلسطيني يصنع آلة موسيقية تقليدية عمرها 5 آلاف عام|date=2018-12-02|accessdate=3 December 2018|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20181203005440/http://www.alquds.com/articles/1543782796435438900/|archivedate=3 December 2018
|passage=وعادةً ما يتم تصنيعه باستخدام خشب شجرة التنوب أو خشب السدر المتين والذي يسمح للأداة بصوت نقي.
|translation=Usually the fabrication takes place under utilization of spruce wood or thick buckthorn wood which confers the instrument a pure resonance.}}
# [[fir]], [[conifer]], [[pine]]
## [[Christmas tree]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَنُّوب}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=201}}
* {{R:ar:Jacob-Geographen|volume=4|page=156}}

{{C|ar|Conifers}}
-------- end text --------
