Page 6483 توبة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed before Islam from {{bor|ar|arc|תְּתוּבְתָּא|tr=tǝṯūḇtā}} in the [[Judaic]] [[circle]]. Forms {{doublet|ar|nocap=1}}s of the forms under the Arabic root {{ar-root|ث و ب|nocat=1}} related to returning.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|تَوْبَة}}
** {{IPA|ar|/ˈto.bɐ/|a=Kuwait,Persian Gulf}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|تَوْبَة|f}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|تَابَ|form=I}}
# {{ar-instance noun of|تَابَ}}
#* Al-Nawawi
#*: {{quote|ar|ولو تاب عن الجميع '''توبة''' واحدة بعد جميعها صحت توبته}}
# [[repentance]]
#* Mark 1:4, {{w|lang=en|Bible translations into Arabic|Van Dyck version}}
#*: {{quote|ar|كان يوحنا يعمد في البرية ويكرز بمعمودية التوبة لمغفرة الخطايا.|John baptized in the wilderness, and preached the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|تَوْبَة}}

====Derived terms====
