Page 6557 توكل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|و ك ل}}
Compare {{m|ar|وَكَلَ||to [[trust]], to [[rely on]]}}. Appears to be related to {{cog|he|יכול|יכל|tr=yakhól|t=to be [[capable]]}}. The definitions of both roots also appear to be conceptually related as trust is a product of perceived capability. From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*wakal-}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|V.ipass}}

# to [[act]] or be [[appoint]]ed {{q|as a [[legal]] [[representative]], [[agent]], etc.}} {{+obj|ar|:فِي<in something>}}
# to [[rely on|rely]], to [[depend]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<on someone>}}
# to [[trust]], to [[have]] [[confidence]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<in someone>}}
# to be [[responsible]] for, to [[vouch]] for, to [[guarantee]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<something> + :لِ<to someone>}}
# to [[take charge]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<of something>}}
# to be [[entrust]]ed {{+obj|ar|:بِ<with something>}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|V.ipass}}

=====Descendants=====
