* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=228, 207}}, where for it and their {{m|ar||**تِيَارَة|t=effrontery; elegance}} (glossed after {{w|Pedro de Alcalá}}’s transcription into Latin which surely represents {{m|ar|طِيَارَة}}) the same general borrowing direction is recognized, only with {{m+|he|תֹּואַר|tr=tóʔar|t=form}} and a seemingly imaginative “Syriac ''tirotā'' ‘spirit, conscience’”, with root connections incompatible with Wiktionary’s previous findings (at the doublets), {{cog|akk|têrtum}}, {{cog|akk-old|tāʾertum|t=instruction, assignment}}, which they connect to {{ar-root|ر ء ي|nocat=1}} but is long known to be from {{m|akk|wârum|t=to go}}.
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=206}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=212}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-6-de|page=109}}
