Page 6598 تين: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Common Fig 01.jpg|thumb|right|{{l-self|ar|تِين|tr=-}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
While one might reconstruct a {{der|ar|sem-pro|*tiʔin-|*tiʔin-, *taʔin-}}, which may well be true given the presence of the word in {{cog|akk-old|-}}, that would have yielded a retained glottal stop in Arabic as with {{m|ar|بِئْر}} were the Arabic word inherited vocabulary, for which case also limited fig cultivation in barren Arabia must be considered. Therefore, the present term is deemed to have been borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|תינה}} / {{m|syc|ܬܝܢܐ|tr=tēnā}} – it is left open whether the singulative or collective came first. Compare {{cog|ar|بَلَس|t=fig}}, seemingly borrowed from South Semitic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|تِين}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|تِين|sing=تِينَة}}

# [[fig]] (fruit and tree)
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|95|1
|passage=وَٱلتِّينِ وَٱلزَّيْتُونِ
|translation=By the fig and the olive}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|تِين}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|tin}}
* {{desc|arz|تين|tr=tīn}}
* {{desc|ota|تین|tr=tin|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|tin|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|tini|bor=1}}

