Page 6605 ث: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Derived from {{m|ar|ت}}, and originally written as such (in {{m|en|rasm}}) by analogy with [[Nabatean]] tradition, as Nabatean cognates of Arabic words with /θ/  were indiscriminately spelled using {{m|arc|𐢞|tr=t}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/θaːʔ/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/θ/}}
* {{sense|Main dialectal variations}} {{IPA|ar|/θ/|/t/|/s/}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ث '''/''' ث‍ '''/''' ‍ث‍ '''/''' ‍ث'''|tr=ṯāʔ}}

# The fourth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. Its name is {{l|ar|ثَاء}} and is preceded by {{l|ar|ت}} and followed by {{l|ar|ج}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ث '''/''' ث‍ '''/''' ‍ث‍ '''/''' ‍ث'''|tr=ṯāʔ}}

# The twenty-third letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ت}} and followed by {{l|ar|خ}}.

