Page 6697 ثم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ar|/θum.ma/}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-ثم.ogg}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|ثُمَّ}}

# [[then]], [[afterward]], [[subsequently]]; {{non-gloss definition|used to indicate order of time, being later occurring, or even in lesser degree of impressiveness}}
# [[and]] [[again]]; {{non-gloss definition|used when repeating a word or short phrase in order to emphasize it}}
# [[and]] [[so]] or [[also]], [[likewise]], [[accordingly]], [[moreover]], [[furthermore]], [[additionally]] [[so]]; {{non-gloss definition|used to denote a speaker's order of enunciation, not indicating a sequence or delay of occurrence between two statements}}
#* {{quote|ar|أَعْجَبَنِي مَا صَنَعْتَ اليَوْمَ '''ثُمَّ''' مَا صَنَعْتَ أَمْسِ أَعْجَبُ|tr=|t=What you did today caused me to be impressed; '''accordingly''' what you did yesterday was most impressive.}}

=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|ar|ثُمَّ}} indicates that there is a certain period of time between the two actions, whereas {{m|ar|فَ}} indicates that the second action follows directly after the first action.

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|ota|ثم|tr=sümme|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{cog|he|שָׁם|tr=šām}}, {{m|he|שָׁמָּה|tr=šā́mmā}}, {{cog|arc|תַּמָּה|tr=tammā}}, {{m|arc|תַּמָּן|tr=tammān}}, {{cog|uga|𐎘𐎎}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|ar|/θam.ma/}}

