===Etymology===
Source of the root {{ar-root|ث|م|ر}}. {{doublet|ar|تَمْر|t1=date}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|ثَمَر}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|ثَمَر|sing=ثَمَرَة|pl=ثِمَار|pl2=ثُمُر|pl3=أَثْمَار}}

# {{lb|ar|collective}} the [[yield]] of [[flower]]ing [[plant]]s, [[botanical]] [[fruits]], [[crops]]
#: {{hypo|ar|خَضْرَاوَات|فَاكِهَة}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|7|141|passage=وَهُوَ الَّذِي أَنشَأَ جَنَّاتٍ مَّعْرُوشَاتٍ وَغَيْرَ مَعْرُوشَاتٍ وَالنَّخْلَ وَالزَّرْعَ مُخْتَلِفًا أُكُلُهُ وَالزَّيْتُونَ وَالرُّمَّانَ مُتَشَابِهًا وَغَيْرَ مُتَشَابِهٍ{{nbsp}}ۚ كُلُوا مِن '''ثَمَرِهِ''' إِذَا أَثْمَرَ وَآتُوا حَقَّهُ يَوْمَ حَصَادِهِ{{nbsp}}ۖ وَلَا تُسْرِفُوا{{nbsp}}ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْرِفِينَ|translation=He is the One Who produces gardens—both cultivated and wild—and palm trees, crops of different flavours, olives, and pomegranates—similar in shape, but dissimilar in taste. Eat of the '''fruit''' they bear and pay the dues at harvest, but do not waste. Surely He does not like the wasteful.}}
## {{lb|ar|collective}} the [[typical]]ly [[sweet]]- or (less commonly) [[sour]]-[[taste|tasting]] [[produce]] of [[plants]], [[fruit]], [[fruitage]]
##: {{syn|ar|فَاكِهَة}}
##: {{cot|ar|خَضْرَاوَات}}
## {{lb|ar|collective|by extension}} something or someone [[resemble|resembling]], [[liken]]ed to, or [[relate]]d to [[fruit]] (such as [[natural]] [[produce]], the [[result]] of a [[happening]] or an [[action]], [[offspring]] or [[progeny]], the [[produce]] of anything, the [[fruit]] of one's [[labor]], [[gain]], [[advantage]], [[profit]], [[possessions]], [[riches]], [[money]], and so on)
# {{lb|ar|collective|rare}} the [[knot]]s of the [[whiplash]] that [[lacerate]] the [[skin]]; the [[thong]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|ثَمَر|sing=ثَمَرَة|pl=ثِمَار|pl2=ثُمُر|pl3=أَثْمَار}}

