Page 6736 ثيتل: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|وعل نوبي|الوَعِل النّوُبِيّ أَوْ الْبَدَن|mul=ثيتل}}
[[File:PikiWiki Israel 14611 near Masada - mountain goat.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|ثَيْتَل}} – {{taxlink|Capra nubiana|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
Of the unique root {{ar-root|ث|ت|ل|nocat=1}}, natively possibly a variant of {{ar-root|ف|ت|ل|nocat=1}} meaning “to be twisted”, “to be branch-like”; in reference to the horn variation reported of the original breed identified with this term, "a mountain {{m|ar|وَعْل|tr=}} with shorter branching horns", later applied to other similar animals.

However strikingly similar to {{cog|gez|ወይጠል}}, {{cog|ti|ወይጠል}}, {{cog|tig|ቴተል}}, {{m|tig|ጦተል}}, also used to refer to some wild goat or antelope in each case and understood as native derivatives or blends of {{cog|gez|ጠሊ|t=kid, goat-child}} with {{m|gez|ውዕላ|ወዓላ|t=mountain goat}}, equalling {{cog|ar|وَعِل|t=wild goat; antelope}} commixed into {{cog|ar|طَلًا|t=young of a deer or gazelle}}.

Minding the distribution of either the Nubian ibex and the hartebeest, the Arabic term may have started as an exotism borrowed anciently from a {{bor|ar|gez|-}} form {{m|gez||*ጠይተል}} via the mediation of {{bor|ar|cus}} spoken by the {{w|Blemmyes}} north of the {{w|Aksumites}}, for the {{bor|ar|bej|-}} language now spoken there has instead of emphatics the peculiar phoneme {{IPAchar|/ʈ/}}, the {{w|voiceless retroflex plosive}}, which to an Arabic speaker sounds like the voiceless dental fricative {{IPAchar|/θ/}}. Even ancient Arabic toponyms referring to places in {{cog|sem-eth|-}}-speaking areas have been shown to have been acquired from Beja, as the name of {{w|Massawa}}, {{m|ar|بَاضِع}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|ثَيْتَل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|ثَيْتَل|m|pl=ثَيَاتِل}}

# [[Nubian ibex]] ({{taxlink|Capra nubiana|species}} syn. {{taxlink|Capra jaela|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|وَعِل نُوبِيّ|بَدَن}}
# [[hartebeest]], [[bovine]] [[antelope]], [[kongoni]] ({{taxfmt|Alcelaphus|genus}})

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|ثَيْتَل|m|pl=ثَيَاتِل}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|arz|تيتل|tr=tētal}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=211}}
* {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|page=286}}, {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|page=389}}, {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|page=439}}, {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|page=446}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=332}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=161}}
* {{R:Mammals|14200784|Capra nubiana}}
* {{R:ION|4958393|Capra jaela}}
* [https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/item/103855#page/381/mode/1up {{taxlink|Capra jaela|species}}] in {{w|Georges Cuvier}}, ''[[w:Le Règne Animal|The animal kingdom]] : arranged in conformity with its organization / The class Mammalia'' (1827)

