Page 6741 ج: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{ar-IPA|جِيم}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{ar-IPA|ج}}

* It has many standard pronunciations in [[w:Literary Arabic|Modern Standard Arabic]], which can also reflect the pronunciation in national [[w:varieties of Arabic|varieties of Arabic]]:
** {{IPA|ar|[d͡ʒ]}} in most of the Arabian Peninsula, Mesopotamia, parts of the Levant, parts of Egypt and in Central Algeria.
** {{IPA|ar|[ʒ]}} in most of the Levant and most of north Africa;
** {{IPA|ar|[ɡ]}} in most of Egypt and west Yemen and parts of Oman (e.g. Muscat dialect);
** {{IPA|ar|[ɟ]}} in Sudan (with allophones) and south Yemen, and most likely in Classical Arabic.

When reciting the [[Quran]], it is customarily pronounced as {{IPAchar|[d͡ʒ]}}.

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ج''' / '''جـ''' / '''ـجـ''' / '''ـج'''|tr=jīm}}

# The fifth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. Its name is {{l|ar|جِيم}}, and is preceded by {{l|ar|ث}} and followed by {{l|ar|ح}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ج''' / '''جـ''' / '''ـجـ''' / '''ـج'''|tr=jīm}}

# The third letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ب}} and followed by {{l|ar|د}}.

===Noun===
{{head|1=ar|2=noun|tr=-}}

# {{lb|ar|lexicography}} {{abbreviation of|ar|جَمْع|t=[[plural]]}}

