# to [[encroach]], to make [[inroads]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.ipass.vn:جَوْر}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ج ر ر}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|جَارَرَ|جَاوَرَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|III.pass.vn:+}}

# to be in the [[neighborhood]] of, to live [[nextdoor]] to
# to [[adjoin]]
# to be in the [[vicinity]], to be [[close]] to
# to [[border]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|III.pass.vn:+}}

===Etymology 3===
{{ar-rootbox|ج و ر}}If we assume a pronunciation {{IPAchar|/ɔː/}} for ''ā'' in ancient Ḥijāzi dialects of Arabic, as is also found necessary to be posited for other borrowings as {{m|ar|قَيُّوم}} and to make the {{cog|sem-eth|-}} borrowings of the present word phonologically plausible, then it is possible to conceive this word loaned from copiously attested {{bor|ar|arc|גיורא}} / {{m|syc|ܓܝܘܪܐ|tr=gīyōrā|t=alien; proselyte}}, functionally equivalent to {{cog|uga|𐎂𐎗|t=foreign resident, protected guest}} and {{cog|he|גֵּר|tr=gēr|t=alien; proselyte}} of which the feminine is {{m|he|גִיוֹרֶת|tr=giyyṓreṯ|t=proselyte}}, while the specific meaning of a “neighbour” is found developed in Palestinian {{cog|arc|מגירה}} / {{m|arc|ܡܓܝܪܐ|tr=məḡīrā}}, {{cog|sem-nwe}} derivations of {{der|ar|sem-wes-pro|*gawar-}} in the sense of ”to encroach upon the limits of, to assail, to come over” (while inheritance from {{der|ar|sem-wes-pro|-}} of the present noun per se would be difficult to construct); for the simplification of the shape of the word regard {{cog|ar|حُوت|t=fish; whale}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جَار}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَار|m|pl=جِيرَان|f=جَارة}}

# [[neighbor]]
#: {{ux|ar|جارنا الجديد هو شخص لطيف وودود.|tr=Jārnā al-ǧadīd huwa šaḫṣ laṭīf wa-wadūd.|Our new neighbor is a kind and friendly person.}}
# [[refugee]]
# [[protégé]], [[charge]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَار|pl=جِيرَان}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|arz|جار|tr=gār}}
* {{desc|afb|يار|tr=yār|جار|tr2=jār}}
