|ar
|year=a. 965
|author={{w|Al-Mutanabbi|Al-Mutanabbī}}
|title={{link|ar||جَارِيَةٌ مَا لِجِسْمِهَا رُوحُ}}
|trans-title=The Lady That Has No Soul
|url=http://www.almotanabbi.com/poemPage.do?poemId=51
|passage='''جَارِيَةٌ''' مَا لِجِسْمِهَا رُوحُ / بِالْقَلْبِ مِنْ حُبِّهَا تَبَارِيحُ<br>فِي كَفِّهَا طَاقَةٌ تُشِيرُ بِهَا / لَكُلِّ طِيبٍ مِنْ طِيبِهَا رِيحُ <br>سَأَشْرَبُ الْكَأْسَ عَنْ إِشَارَتِهَا / وَدَمْعُ عَيْنِي فِي الْخَدِّ مَسْفُوحُ
|t=A lady without a soul,<br>Yet through my love for her,<br>My heart is shivering;<br>In this hand, which she points around,<br>There is so much power;<br>Each and every fragrance<br>From her fragrance draws its scent.<br>I shall drink this glass as she points it out,<br>With tears from my eyes, on my cheek,<br>Rolling down.}}
# a [[handmaiden]]; a [[slave]]-[[woman]]
#: {{syn|ar|فَتَاة|أَمَة}}
#: {{cot|ar|غُلَام|فَتًى|عَبْد}}
# [[ship]]
