Page 6833 جامور: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ج م ر}}

===Etymology===
Due to the pattern occurring in [[Classical Arabic]] only in {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowings, for instance {{m|ar|شَاقُول}}, {{m|ar|كَابُوس}}, {{m|ar|كَابُول}}, {{m|ar|كَالُون}}, and particularly {{m|ar|كَافُور}}, it presupposes, as Fraenkel already explicitly noted, {{m|arc||*ܓܳܡܽܘܪܳܐ|tr=*gāmūrā, gāmōrā}} and {{m|arc||ܓܽܘܡܳܪܳܐ|tr=gummārā}} of similar sense, but this is [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only attested in borrowings|not attested]]. By conjecture only, it is possible to relate the senses within the Arabic and Aramaic root of “heating up” coals back to more general senses of “completion, fulfilment”, which further explains the background of the term {{m|ar|جُمَّار|t=pith of palm}}, a palm attaining maturity, perhaps by man letting it grow.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جَامُور}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَامُور|m|pl=جَوَامِير|pl2=جَامُورَات}}

# [[spire]], [[height]] of a [[tower]]
# {{C|ar|Ship parts}} a [[quadrangular]] [[piece]] of [[wood]] at the [[mast]] of a [[ship]]<!--عُوْدٌ مُرَبَّعٌ على رأْسِ الدَّقَلِ من السَّفِيْنَةِ in al-Muḥīṭ fī l-Luġa, 10th c. CE -->

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَامُور|pl=جَوَامِير|pl2=جَامُورَات}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|جَامُور|m|sing=جَامُورَة}}

# {{alternative form of|ar|جُمَّار|t=heart of palm}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|جَامُور}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=146}}
* {{R:CAL|gmr|V}}
* {{R:CAL|gmr%232|V}}
* {{R:CAL|gmr%233|V}}
-------- end text --------
