Page 6852 جاورس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|pal|tr=gʾwls|ts=gāwars|t=sorghum, giant millet}}, whence {{cog|fa|گاورس|tr=gâvars|t={{taxfmt|Setaria viridis|species}}}}, {{cog|syc|ܓܘܪܘܣ|tr=gwrws|ts=gāwarws|t=millet}}, {{cog|xcl|գաւարս}}, {{cog|sgh-ros||tr=ǰäwaws}}, {{cog|sgh-xuf||tr=jawōwc|t=millet}}, {{cog|ydg|tr=ɣawarso}}, from {{cog|ira-old|}} {{m|und|*gāwarsa-}}.<ref>{{R:xme:Asatrian:2011|page=157}}</ref><ref>{{cite-book|year=1932|page=336|last=Morgenstierne|first=Georg|authorlink=Georg Morgenstierne|chapter=The Development of Iranian ''r'' + consonant in the Shughni group|year_published=1970|title=W.B. Henning Memorial Volume|publisher=Lund Humphries|location=London}}</ref> Cognate with {{cog|kmr|garis|t={{taxfmt|Panicum miliaceum|species}}}}, {{cog|hi|ज्वार|t=greater millet}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جَاوَرْس|جَاوَرَس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَاوَرْس|head2=جَاوَرَس|m}}

# {{C|ar|Grains}} [[sorghum]], {{vern|greater millet}}, [[jawar]] ({{taxfmt|Sorghum bicolor|species}})
# {{C|ar|Grains}} [[proso millet]], [[broomcorn millet]] ({{taxfmt|Panicum miliaceum|species}})

