Page 6863 جبة: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|جبة (لباس)}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ج|ب|ب}} meaning “to cut”, “to carve a well or cistern”; from the encircling and enclosing of a well or cistern comes the secondary sense “to surround”, “to envelop”, “to en-wrap”, ultimately, from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*gbb|t=to bend, curve, cut}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جُبَّة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جُبَّة|f|pl=جُبَب|pl2=جِبَاب|pl3=جَبَائِب}}

# [[jubbah]] {{qualifier|a type of [[clothing]] worn in some Arabic lands traditionally by men}}
# a [[wrapper]], [[cloak]], [[coat]], [[outer garment]]
# {{lb|ar|archaic}} [[coat of mail]], [[defensive]] [[clothing]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جُبَّة|pl=جُبَب|pl2=جِبَاب|pl3=جَبَائِب}}

