{{ar-verb|II}}

# {{lb|ar|obsolete|Yemen}} to regard with fixed eyes

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-verb|II}}
-------- end text --------
Page 6908 جحمة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ج ح م}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَحْمَة|f}}

# [[burn]]ing [[fiercely]], being [[fiery]], [[blazing]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَحْمَة}}

===Etymology 2===
* According to the lexicographers a [[Himyaritic]] borrowing.
* Perhaps instead from the root {{ar-root|ج ح م}} “being blazing; vehement” via the idea of [[stare|staring]], as an originally coarse word, or the eyes being considered the window by which one sees the fire of the soul.
* A borrowing from a descendant of {{der|ar|ira-pro|*čášma|g=n|t=eye}}, be it via {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, can also be presumed, not requiring a particular Iranian source language, since the medial {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} would have been dissimilated in any case to resolve the homorganicity with {{IPAchar|/d͡ʒ/}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَحْمَة|f}}

# {{C|ar|Eye}}{{tlb|ar|obsolete|Yemen}} [[eye]]
#: {{syn|ar|عَيْن}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|title=unknown|section=quoted by {{w|Kitab al-'Ayn|Kitāb al-ʿAyn}} and {{w|lang=ar|تهذيب اللغة|Taḏhīb al-Luḡa}}|year=a. 750|passage=فَفَاضَتْ دُمُوعُ الْجَحْمَتَيْنِ بِعَبْرَةٍ … عَلَى الزُبِّ حَتَّى الزُبِّ فِي المَاءِ غَامِس|t=And the tears of the two eyes overflowed without sobbing … over the beard, until the beard was dipping into water|subst=فَفَاضَتْ/فَ-فَاضَتْ,بِعَبْرَةٍ/بِ-عَبْرَةٍ}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَحْمَة}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|جَحَّمَ|t=to regard with fixed eyes}}
* {{l|ar|جُحَام|t=a disease of the eyes where they are swollen}}
-------- end text --------
