# {{C|ar|Vehicles}} [[tug]], a vehicle that pulls things such as a [[tractor]] or [[tugboat]]
# {{C|ar|Arachnids}} {{lb|ar|as {{m|ar|جَرَّارَة}} or as an adjective in the masculine or feminine after {{m|ar|عَقْرَب|t=scorpion}}}} [[deathstalker]] ({{taxlink|Compsobuthus pallidus|species}} and {{taxfmt|Leiurus|genus}} (?), a scorpion which drags its prey on its tail behind itself)
#* {{RQ:Mafatih-Vloten|page=158 line 8–9|footer=<small>Commented in {{R:ar:Seidel:1915|page=19 Anm. 33}}. Identified as ''Compsobuthus pallidus'' by [https://alsirhan.com/wildlife-of-kuwait/ Wildlife of Kuwait], who on closer look also [https://alsirhan.com/compsobuthus-pallidus/ connect ''loci classici'']. But new species are continuously discovered: {{cite-journal|url=https://mds.marshall.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1328&context=euscorpius|year=2020|title=Notes on ''Compsobuthus'': redescription of ''C. arabicus'' Levy et al., 1973 from Arabia, and description of two new species from North Africa (Scorpiones: Buthidae)|work=Euscorpius – Occasional Publications in Scorpiology|issue=298|last=Kovařík|first=František|first2=Graeme|last2=Lowe|first3=Mark|last3=Stockmann|first4=František|last4=Šťáhlavský}}. The ranges of scorpions are difficult to determine too, e.g. it is unknown for the {{vern|Hebrew deathstalker}} {{taxlink|Leiurus hebraeus|species}}, so one cannot tell based on this whether the Arabic term is a {{clq|ar|arc|-|nocap=1}}.</small>|passage=الجرّارات وهي عقارب صغار تجرّ أذنابها وتكون ببلاد الخوز ويقال لها بالنبطيّة كرورا|t=''jarrārāt'' are little scorpions dragging along their tails found in Khuzistan and called in [http://cal.huc.edu/oneentry.php?lemma=grwr+N&cits=all Nabataean] ''gərōrā''.}}

