===Etymology 1===
{{ar-reduplicated}} from the root {{ar-root|ج|ر|ر}}, related to dragging; presumably borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, already in the {{w|Peshitta}} {{m|syc|ܓܪܓܪܐ|tr=gargərā}}, absolute state {{m|syc|ܓܪܓܪ|tr=gargar|t=drag, sledge}}, from the root {{syc-root|ܓ|ܪ|ܪ}} related to dragging.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَرْجَر|m}} {{tlb|ar|no plural|countable through {{l|ar|آلَة}}}}

# [[thresher]], [[threshing sledge]], an [[implement]] of [[wood]] in which there are [[revolve|revolving]] [[axle]]s [[drag]]ged along by [[beast]]s for [[crush]]ing the [[corn]]
#: {{syn|ar|نَوْرَج|طِرْبِيل|مِدْرَسَة|دَرَّاسَة}}
