Page 6966 جرجس: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Ikona sv. Georgija z Kolomenského.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|جُرْجُس}}|upright]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|ar|grc|Γεώργιος}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|جَاوْرْجِيُوس}}
* {{alter|ar|جُورْج|tr=jōrj}} {{q|especially Lebanon}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جُرْجُس}}
* {{IPA|ar|[ˈɡɪrɡɪs]|a=Egypt}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|جُرْجُس|m}}

# ([[Saint George|Saint]]) [[George]], a legendary Christian [[martyr]]
# {{given name|ar|male|from=Ancient Greek}}, [[George]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جُرْجُسُ|state=ind-def}}

===Etymology 2===
[[File:White chalky earth from Bethlehem, Palestine, 1920-1930 Wellcome L0059009.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|جِرْجِس}}]]
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|גַּרְגִּישְׁתָּא|tr=gargīštā}} / {{m|syc|ܓܰܪܓܶܫܬܴܐ|tr=gargeštā}}, of {{unknown|ar|nocap=1}} origin.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|قِرْقِس}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جِرْجِس}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جِرْجِس|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[sealing earth]], [[terra sigillata]]
# {{C|ar|Fire}} a kind of [[lunt]] or [[fuse]] from {{vern|rope grass|nopedia=1}}
#* {{quote-book|year=c. 910|ar|author=[[w:Ibn al-Faqih|Aḥmad ibn Muḥammad ibn al-Faqīh al-Hamaḏānī]]|url=https://books.rafed.net/m/?type=c_fbook&b_id=3770&page=132|title=[https://shamela.ws/book/11685/109 Kitāb al-Buldān]|passage=وَمِنْ عَجَائِبِ مِصْرَ : حَشِيشَةٌ يُقَالُ لَهَا ٱلدِّيسُ ، يُتَّخَذُ مِنْهَا حِبَالٌ لِلسُّفُنِ ، تُسَمَّى تِلْكَ ٱلْحِبَالُ ٱلْ'''قِرْقِسُ'''، يُؤْخَذُ مِنَ ٱلْ'''قِرْقِسِ''' قِطْعَةٌ فَيُشْعَلُ بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ كَٱلشَّمْعِ ، ثُمَّ يُطْفِئُ فَيَمْكُثُ سَائِرَ ٱللَّيْلِ ، فَإِذَا ٱحْتَاجُوا إِلَيْهِ أَخَذُوا طَرَفَهُ فَأَدَارُوهُ كَٱلْمِخْرَاقِ.|t=Of the wonders of Egypt, there is a grass called [[diss]], and one makes from it ropes for ships, these ropes are called '''qirqis''', one takes from the '''qirqis''' a piece and torches it like a candle between the hands, then one extinguishes and it bides the whole night; if you need to put it to use then you take its tip and twist it like a kerchief to burn.|subst=لِلسُّفُنِ//لِ-سْ-سُفُنِ}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جِرْجِس}}

===Etymology 3===
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܓܰܪܓܳܣܴܐ|tr=gargāsā|t=a type of gnats}}, ultimately probably {{onomatopoeic|ar|nocap=1}}. Compare {{cog|tmr|דגירגצא}}, {{m|arc|גירגצא}}, {{m|arc|גרגצא}}.
[[File:Конаевский округ, двупятнистый жаворонок (1).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|جِرْجِس}} – {{taxfmt|Melanocorypha bimaculata|species}}|upright=1.15]]

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|قِرْقِس}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جِرْجِس}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|جِرْجِس|sing=جِرْجِسَة}}

# {{lb|ar|Syria|obsolete}} any {{taxfmt|Nematocera|suborder}} insect: [[crane fly|crane flies]], [[gnat]]s, [[mosquitoes]]
#: {{syn|ar|بَعُوض|بَقّ|q2=Iraq|نَامُوس|بَرْغَش|خَمُوش}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{w|قيس بن الملوح|lang=ar|Qays Ibn Al-Malawwaḥ}} ?|title=quoted by {{w|Ibn Duraid}}’s ''{{w|lang=ar|جمهرة اللغة|jamhara al-luġa}}'' and {{w|lang=ar|رضي الدين الصغاني|aṣ-Ṣaġānī}}'s ''ʕubāb az-zāḫir wa-lubāb al-fāḫir''|year=660–688|passage=فَلَيْتَ ٱلْأَفَاعِي يَعْضَضْنَنَا … مَكَانَ البَرَاغِيثِ وَٱلْ'''قِرْقِسِ'''<br/>يُحَرَّمْنَ جَنْبِيَّ نَوْمَ الْفِرَاشِ … وَيُؤْذِينَ جِسْمِيَ إِنْ أَجْلَسِ|t=If only the vipers bit us … at the place of gnats and '''midges'''!<br/>They would have saved my sides for bed-sleep … and allow my chain to sit}}
# {{vern|bimaculated lark}} ({{taxfmt|Melanocorypha bimaculata|species}}), of which {{taxlink|Melanocorypha bimaculata subsp. rufescens|subspecies}} [[c:File:Melanocorypha bimaculata distribution map.png|occurs]] in summer in Arabia and Northeastern Africa and in the Northern and Western edges of Greater Syria in winter, a [[gamebird]], the other subspecies {{taxlink|Melanocorypha bimaculata subsp. bimaculata|subspecies}} East and South of the [[Caspian Sea]]) <!-- this meaning is mentioned nowhere. It took me to extract it from the photos on the web and Twitter; only here it is in a blog about bird-hunting in the KSA with the English name: https://hunting-ksa.blogspot.com/2013/12/bimaculated-lark.html. Vowels confirmed via Youtube. Fay Freak. --->

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|جِرْجِس}}

