* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=265}}
* {{R:Hommel-Säugethiere|pages=364–365}}
* {{cite-book|last=Kogan|first=Leonid|year=2006|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=RfCV3LAg0BcC&lpg=PA298&dq=nin.hur.ba.um&pg=PA282|chapter=Animal Names of Biblical Hebrew. An Etymological Survey|title=Babel und Bibel 3: Annual of Ancient Near Eastern, Old Testament, and Semitic Studies|location=Winona Lake, Indiana|publisher=Eisenbrauns in conjunction with the Russian State University for Humanities|page=282}}
* {{R:akk:Landsberger-Fauna|page=85}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=408}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=1|page=124–125 No. 84}}, seeing all the Semitic words but not the Iranian ones and providing similar {{cog|ber|-}} and {{cog|cdc|-}} words, all referring to other animals except for {{noncog|daa|gârzè}} and a word widespread in Berber but unlikely to be related, {{noncog|shi|ⴰⵖⵔⴷⴰ}}.
* {{R:fa:Monchi-Zadeh:1990|page=65 Nr. 197}}
* {{R:fa:Monchi-Zadeh:1990|pages=83–84 Nr. 251}}
