Page 6986 جريب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{wp|lang=ar}}
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*gʰrebʰ-}}
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|גְּרִיוָא|tr=gəriwā}}, {{m|arc|גְּרִיבָא|tr=gəriḇā}}, {{m|syc|ܓܪܝܻܒܳܐ|tr=gəriḇā|t=a dry measure; a measure of land}}, from {{der|ar|arc-imp|𐡂𐡓𐡉𐡅|tr=gryw}}, of {{der|ar|ira-old}} origin, {{cog|pal||tr=glyw'|ts=griw}}, {{cog|xpr||tr=gryw'|ts=griw}}, also found in {{cog|xcl|գրիւ}}, probably unrelated to the homonymous Iranian words for [[Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-Iranian/griHwáH|“neck; throat”]] but likely related to {{der|ar|iir-pro|*grabʰ|t=to grab, to seize}}, from {{der|ar|ine-pro|*gʰrebʰ-}} (compare the {{cog|sa|-}} root {{m|sa|ग्रभ्}}), if this is not the same word as treated under {{m|ar|جِرَاب}} denoting a kind of bag, see there.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جَرِيب}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَرِيب|m|pl=جُرْبَان|pl2=جَرَائِب|pl3=أَجْرِبَة|pl4=جُرُوب}}

# a [[dry measure]] for [[grain]], [[peck]]
# a division of cropland, a certain [[square measure]] varying between country and period, [[jerib]], as much as can be sown from the grain measure

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَرِيب|m|pl=جُرْبَان|pl2=جَرَائِب|pl3=أَجْرِبَة|pl4=جُرُوب}}

===Etymology 2===
{{wp|lang=ar|جريب الشعرة|mul=جريب المبيض}}
{{ar-diminutive}} of {{m|ar|جِرَاب|t={{l|la|follis}}}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جُرَيْب}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جُرَيْب|f|pl=جُرَيْبَات}}

# [[follicle]]

