===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|ar|arc|גִּישְׁרָא}} / {{m|arc|גִּשְׁרָא|tr=gišrā}} / {{m|syc|ܓܫܪܐ|tr=gešrā}}, with {{cog|he|גֶּשֶׁר|tr=géšer}} from {{der|ar|akk|𒄀𒅆𒅕𒊑|ts=gišru}}. Note the meaning “timber, beam” in Syriac – originally the Arabic word meant a wooden bridge in distinction from a stone bridge {{m|ar|قَنْطَرَة}}. The word has a derivation in {{cog|akk|-}} from {{m|akk|𒄑𒃡|tr=GIŠ.ÙR}}, {{m|akk|𒄑𒃡𒋗|tr=GIŠ.ŠU.ÙR|ts=gušūru, gašūru|t=tree-trunk; felled log, timber; beams}}, itself considered a {{der|ar|sux|-}} loanword.

