Page 7046 جعة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
A connection to the root {{ar-root|و ج ع}} (related to aches), is unlikely, as it does not conform well semantically—though theoretically alcohol causes headaches, this cannot well be imagined to be the motive. In the ''{{w|Fairuzabadi|Qāmūs}}'', it is listed under the root formula {{ar-root|ج ع و|nocat=1}}—under which other dictionaries also list an obscure {{m|ar|جَعَا|t=to collect in a heap, e.g. dung}} and an unknown colour term {{m|ar|جُعْوَة|t=bay colour of a horse’s fur; rough and dark ground}}—, and defined as a {{m|ar|نَبِيذ|t=wine}} made of barley. Given the late date of unambiguous attestation, it may well be a borrowing from {{bor|ar|ha|gíyā̀|t=beer, a cold brew of barley}}, famed as an indigenous beverage.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جِعَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جِعَة|f|pl=جِعَات}}

# [[beer]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جِعَة|pl=sfp}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=285b}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=4|page=440a}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=302a}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=2|page=1492b}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|page=150}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=186}}

{{C|ar|Zymurgy|Beer}}
