Page 7054 جعضيض: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Starr-150328-0730-Sonchus oleraceus-habit-Southwest Eastern Island-Midway Atoll (25269066615).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|جعضيض}} – {{taxfmt|Sonchus oleraceus|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
In Classical Arabic {{alter|ar|يَعْضِيض}}, from the root {{ar-root|ع ض ض}} due to its jagged appearance, altered after a scheme known from {{m|ar|جَرْبُوز}} and {{m|ar|جَرْبُوع}}, perhaps also under influence of the plant-names {{m|ar|جَعْدَة}} and {{m|ar|جُعْدَة}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جَعْضِيض}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَعْضِيض|m}}

# [[common sow thistle]] ({{taxfmt|Sonchus oleraceus|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|تِفَاف}}
# {{lb|ar|sometimes}} [[endive]] ({{taxfmt|Cichorium|genus}} gen. et spp. of the same tribe)
#: {{syn|ar|هِنْدِبَاء}}
#: {{hypo|ar|طَرَخَشْقُون}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَعْضِيض}}

===References===
* {{cite-book|ar|year=a. 1930|entryurl=https://shamela.ws/book/150964/594|entry={{lang|ar|جُعْضيضْ}}|title=ar:الألفاظ العامية المصرية|author=ar:أحمد تيمور باشا|authorlink=Ahmed Taymour}} <!--scan https://www.google.de/books/edition/Muʻjam_Taymūr_al_kabīr_fī_al_alfā/PdNEAQAAIAAJ?hl=de&gbpv=1&bsq="اليعضيض"&dq="اليعضيض"&printsec=frontcover-->

{{cln|ar|blends}}
{{C|ar|Cichorieae tribe plants}}
-------- end text --------
Page 7055 جعفر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
An augmentation of the root {{ar-root|ج|ع|ف}} meaning a to pull or uproot, to wash away, to overturn or rip from foundations, a torrent that carries things away; possibly blended with the root {{ar-root|ج|ف|ر}} denoting to be swollen, to be filled up, hence a full or flooded riverbed. The first root is potentially a dialect variant of the root {{ar-root|ج|ف|ء}} also denoting the washing away of objects from a valley full of water, to sweep off or carry away, to pull or uproot.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جَعْفَر}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَعْفَر|m|pl=جَعَافِر}}

# [[full]] [[river]]
## [[camel]] [[full]] of [[milk]]
# [[brook]], [[creek]], [[rivulet]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{l|ar||جَوَّاد عَلِي}}|title={{w|lang=ar|المفصل في تاريخ العرب قبل الإسلام|{{lang|ar|المفصل في تاريخ العرب قبل الإسلام}}}}|trans-title=The Detailed History of the Arabs before Islam|year=1960|section=1, 4
|passage=ليس في جزيرة العرب انهار كبيرة بالمعنى المعروف من لفظة نهر مثل نهر دجلة أو الفرات أو النيل، بل فيها أنهار مغيرة أو جعافر.
|translation=In the Arabian Peninsula there aren’t really rivers of river names like the river “Tigris” or the “Euphrat” or the “Nile”, but it has diverse rivers or rivulets.}}
# [[flooded]] [[wadi]], [[torrent]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَعْفَر|m|pl=جَعَافِر}}

===Proper noun===
{{head|ar|proper noun|head=جَعْفَر}}

# {{given name|ar|male}}, [[Jafar]], [[Jaafar]], [[Ja'far]]
# {{w|Ja'far al-Sadiq|Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad aṣ-Ṣādiq}}, a revered 8th-century Muslim scholar and the sixth Imam for [[Twelver]] and [[Isma'ili|ʾIsmāʿīliyy]] [[Shia]] Muslims, after whom the {{w|Jaʽfari jurisprudence|Jaʿfari}} school of [[jurisprudence]] is named.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَعْفَر:tri|state=ind-def}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|جَعْفَرِيّ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=198}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=284}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=300}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=430}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=186}}

-------- end text --------
