Page 7071 جفن: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ج ف ن}}. Cognate to {{cog|he|גֶּפֶן|tr=gép̄en|t=vine}}, {{cog|syc|ܓܦܢܬܐ|tr=gəp̄entā|t=vine}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جَفْن}}
** {{IPA|acw|/d͡ʒɪfɪn/|a=Gulf}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَفْن|m|pl=جُفُون|pl2=أَجْفَان}}

# [[eyelid]]
# {{lb|ar|archaic}} [[vat]], [[tub]]
# {{lb|ar|archaic}} [[vine]], [[grapevine]]
# {{lb|ar|archaic}} [[enceinte]], [[close]], [[building]]s of [[fortification]] [[surround]]ing an [[area]]
#* {{RQ:Ibn Batoutah|IV|page=351|lines=4–7|text=وممّا شاع من أفعال مولانا أيده الله في الجهاد إنشاؤه الأجفان بجميع السواحل واستكثاره من عُدَد البحر وهذا في زمان الصلح والمُهادنة إعْدادًا لأيّام القِرة وأخذًا بالحزم في قطع أَطْماع الكفّار.|t=One of the most notable deeds of our master (God assist him!) of struggle is his engineering of enceintes on all shores, and his manifold provisions in naval matters, in time of peace and armistice to prepare for days of war, to shortcircuit the cravings of the infidels resolutely.}}
# {{lb|ar|archaic}} a kind of [[round]] [[ship]]
#* {{RQ:Ibn Batoutah|II|page=234|line=1 a fine}}
#* {{RQ:Ibn Batoutah|IV|page=105|line=2}}
#* {{RQ:Ibn Batoutah|IV|page=271|line=3 a fine}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَفْن|pl=جُفُون|pl2=أَجْفَان}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|جَفْنَة}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|ġifen}}
* {{desc|az|cəfn|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|جفن|tr=jafn|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|ota|جفن|tr=cefn|bor=1}}
* {{desc|axm|ճփնի|bor=1|unc=1|der=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Agius|Classic|pages=338–340}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=2|page=201}}

{{C|ar|Grapevines|Eye|Watercraft}}

