Page 7073 جل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ج ل ل}}
Compare {{cog|he|גַּל|tr=gall}}.

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|جَلّ}}

# [[great]]
# [[bulky]]
# [[outstanding]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|جَلّ|f=جَلَّة|pl=جُلُول}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جُلّ|m}}

# {{lb|ar|construct}} the [[bulk]] (of), the [[majority]] (of); the [[lion's share]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَكْثَر}}
#: {{usex|ar|مَا لَا يُدْرَكُ كُلُّهُ، لَا يُتْرَكُ جُلُّهُ.|t=What is not wholly achieved is not to be largely abandoned.}}
#* {{Q|ar|year=20th century|{{lang|ar|مُصْطَفَى صادِق الرافِعي}}|[[s:ar:جل الناسِ أعداءُ|{{lang|ar|جل الناسِ أعداءُ}}]]|quote='''جل''' الناسِ أعداءُ على السرَّاءِ والضَّرَّا<br/>فلا يغرُرْكَ مبتسمٌ وإن أبدى لكَ البشرا<br/>ففي الصدر حزازاتٌ تكادُ تمزقُ الصدرا<br/>ولو كادوا النجومَ هوتْ من الخضراءِ للغبرا<br/>وما الدنيا إذا فكر تَ غير جهنمَ الصُّغرى<br/>ألستَ ترى بها أمماً وكلٌّ تلعنُ الأخرى<br/>لقد جرَّبْتُ '''جُلَّهُمُ''' فلمْ أر فيهمُ خيرا<br/>|t='''Most''' men are rabid foes, / Be they in joy or woe!<br/>Do not be fooled by smiles, / Even if seeming kind:<br/>In their breasts is hateful fury, / almost tearing their hearts apart!<br/>If men could plot against the stars, / The stars would fall into the mire.<br/>Life, if you reflect, / Is but a "lesser Hell":<br/>Do you not see in it many nations? / And each of them execrates the other!<br/>I have appraised '''most''' sorts and kinds, / And in all, I saw no goodness!}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جُلّ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.nopass?.vn:جَلَال,جَلَالَة}}

# to be [[illustrious]]
# to be [[beyond]] or [[above]]
# to be [[exalted]] or [[dignified]]
# to grow old

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.nopass?.vn:جَلَال,جَلَالَة}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|fa-cls|گل|tr=gul}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جُلّ|m}}

# {{lb|ar|uncommon}} [[jasmine]], [[rose]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جُلّ}}

===Etymology 3===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|ira}}. Compare {{cog|ckb|جِل|t=beggar’s clothes}}, {{cog|fa|جل|tr=joll|t=horse-covering, saddle-cloth}}, {{cog|bft||tr=jol|t=horse cover}}, {{cog|yai|tr=jul|t=horse-cloth}}, {{cog|hac|tr=jal, jul|t=cover, cloth}}. {{doublet|ar|شَلَّاق|جُوَالَق|جُوَال}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جُلّ|m|pl=أَجْلَال|pl2=جِلَال}} {{tlb|ar|regional}}

# [[horse]]-[[covering]], [[saddlecloth]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 869|authorlink=al-Jahiz|author=ar:الْجَاحِظ|title=ar:التَبَصُّر بِٱلتِّجَارَة|chapter=ar:باب ما يُجلب من البلدان من طرائف السلع والأمتعة والجواري والأحجار وغير ذلك<t:What one imports from strange countries in items, commodities, she-slaves, stones and else.>|url=https://www.hindawi.org/books/73505194/4/|passage=ومن السوس: الأُتْرُجُّ ودُهن البنفسج والشاه سبرم وال'''جِلال''' والبراذع.|t=From {{w|Shush, Iran|Sūs}} one gets citrons, violet-oil, basil, and '''horse-covers''' and pack-saddles.}}
#* {{RQ:Ibn Batoutah|II|page=35|line=2 a fine|passage=وقد لبسوا التلاليس و'''جِلال''' الدوابّ وجعلوا فوق رءوسهم التراب والتبن.|t=They were clothed in sacks and '''pelts''' of domestic beasts and had their heads covered with earth and straw.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جُلّ|pl=أَجْلَال|pl2=جِلَال}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|pages=103–104}}
* {{cite-journal|year=2011|volume=8|journal=Nartamongæ. The Journal of Alano-Ossetic Studies|pages=251–255 (from 236)|last=Rossi|first=Adriano Valerio|title=Ossetic and Balochi in V.I. Abaev’s SLOVAR'|url=https://www.academia.edu/36999275/Nartamonga_2011.pdf}}

{{C|ar|Horse tack}}

