Page 7075 جلابية: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly from [[Coptic]] {{m|cop|ⲕⲟⲗⲟⲃⲉⲁ|sc=Copt|tr=kolobea||robe, dress}}. The corresponding root {{ar-root|ج|ل|ب|nocat=1}} is related to taking and carrying, thus it is hard to assume a derivation from it. But see also the root {{ar-root|ج ل ب ب|nocat=1}} from which there is {{m|ar|جِلْبَاب|t={{l|en|robe}}}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَلَّابِيَّة|f|pl=جَلَّابِيَّات|pl2=جَلَالِيب}}

# {{lb|ar|Egyptian}} [[galabia]], [[djellaba]] {{gloss|a loose, shirtlike garment commonly worn by Egyptian men}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَلَّابِيَّة|pl=جَلَّابِيَّات|pl2=جَلَالِيب}}

===References===
* [http://lisaan.net/%d8%ac%d9%84%d8%a8/#59316c3e99a58ecc9bbc99ee9f8fe9a3 Al-Majmoo` al-Mugheeth fi Gharibay al-Qur'aani wal Hadeeth by Abu Musa al-Madeeni (d. 1185 CE) المجموع المغيث في غريبي القرآن والحديث لأبو موسى المديني]

