Page 7082 جلبان: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}
[[File:The Botanical Magazine, Plate 115 (Volume 4, 1791).png|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|جلبان}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, where {{cog|jpa|גילבונה|ts=*gilbɔ̄nā}}, {{m|arc|גילבונא|ts=*gilbɔ̄nā}}, {{m|arc|גלבונה|ts=*gilbɔ̄nā}}, {{m|arc|גלבונא|ts=*gilbɔ̄nā}} is {{taxlink|Lathyrus digitatus|species}} syn. {{taxlink|Lathyrus sessilifolius|species|sessilifolius}}, {{taxfmt|Lathyrus sativus|species}} and other {{taxfmt|Lathyrus|genus}} species, {{cog|tmr|גּוּלְבָּא|tr=gulbā}} and {{cog|syc|ܓܰܘܠܒܳܐ|tr=gulbā}} a kind of wheat (a {{taxfmt|Triticum|genus}} species), all derived from the root {{m|arc|ג־ל־ב|tr=g-l-b}} related to baldness, being shaven off because of the paucity of anything like hair on either plant, the smooth leaf surface compared to naked human skin.

The first witness of the term might be a Late {{cog|egy-mid|-}} text ({{w|Brooklyn Papyrus|pBrooklyn 47.218.48 & 85}} col. IV, 13–14) where it is stated that in the [[Asiatic]] language the grass-pea is called {{m|egy||tr=''gulban''}}.

The middle part can also be identified as continuing {{der|ar|akk|𒇻𒂠𒊬|tr=LU-UB<sub>2</sub>-<sup>SAR</sup>|ts=lubbu, luppu|t=[[cowpea]]}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒇻𒂠𒊬|tr=LU-UB<sub>2</sub>-<sup>SAR</sup>|ts=lub|t=[[cowpea]]}}, likely connected to the {{der|ar|sux|𒇻𒂠|tr=LU-UB<sub>2</sub>|ts=lub|t=pouch, pod, bag}} also found in {{m|ar|لُوبِيَا}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جُلُبَّان|m|head2=جُلَبَّان|head3=جُلْبَان}}

# [[grass pea|grasspea]] ({{taxfmt|Lathyrus sativus|species}}, and by extension other {{taxfmt|Lathyrus|genus}} species and the genus)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جُلُبَّان|head2=جُلَبَّان|head3=جُلْبَان}}

====Descendants====
