Page 7086 جلجلان: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{m|ar|جَلْجَلَ|t=to rattle}} for the fruits of {{taxlink|Savignya parviflora|species}}, foreboding high summer, dance and shake when ripe and dry – if the verb is not from the plant. The name for this plant also bears the forms {{m|ar|قُلْقُلَان}}, {{m|ar|قُلَيْقِلَان}}. The meaning sesame however is already found in {{cog|xsa|𐩴𐩡𐩴𐩡𐩬}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جُلْجُلان|جِلْجِلَان}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جُلْجُلان|m|head2=جِلْجِلَان}}

# {{taxlink|Savignya parviflora|species}}
# [[sesame]]
# [[achene]] (such as of a [[fig]])
#* {{R:ar:FAH|6II|page=321 Nr. 501|passage=ويقولون لطرف التِّين البُجُّول. والصّواب الذَّنبُ. ويقال لما في جَوْفِهِ الْجُلْجُلَانُ. ويقال لِلَّبَنِ الذي يسيل منه إِذا كان أخضرَ النَّسَلُ.|t=One calls a fig stalk ''bujjūl''. The right is ''ḏanab''. One says for what is in its inner ''juljulān''. And the milk which flows from it when it is green ''nasal''.}}

====Declension====
