===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|גּוּלְפָא|tr=gulp̄ā|t=empty jug, stone pitcher}}, apparently a metathesis of {{der|ar|akk|𒉺𒄖𒇻|tr=pagalu, pagulu|t=a jar used for libation}}. The term lout stemming from a drunkard, one who empties a wine jar, and their associated rowdy behavior; alternatively from the related {{der|ar|akk|𒉺𒂵𒈝|tr=pagalum|t=to be powerful, to be massive, to be bulky or cumbersome, to be brawny}}.

