Page 7239 جنوب: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{ar-root|ج|ن|ب}} with the base stem meaning “to go aside”, “to go far off in a direction”, ”to remove to a distance”, “to be remote”, “to change” or “to veer”, “to take off one's clothes” or “to lay them aside”. The direction originates as the name of a positively-viewed warm-moist southerly wind, the humid weather allowing clothes to be laid aside, whereas {{m|ar|شَمَال|t=north}} comes from a root {{ar-root|ش|م|ل|nocat=1}} with the meaning “bundling up” or “wrapping up” because that wind by contrast necessitated wrapping up clothes. Also see {{m|la|Canopus}}, and {{m|ar|سُهَيْل|t=Canopus}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جَنُوب}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-جنوب.ogg}}
** {{a|ar|Egyptian}} {{ar-IPA|tr=ganūb}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَنُوب|m}}

# [[south]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَنُوب}}

