Page 7247 جني: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Formally, {{ar-etym-nisba|جِنّ|jinns, demonkind, genies|lc=1}} though most likely borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܓܢܝ|tr=gnē|t=spirit, genie}}, or its emphatic form {{cog|arc|גניא|tr=ginnāyā}} or {{cog|syc|ܓܢܝܐ|tr=genyā}}, also meaning "a [[tutelary deity]]" or "[[Astaroth]] idols". Compare {{noncog|la|genius}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جِنِّيّ}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|جِنِّيّ|f=جِنِّيَّة|pl=جِنِّيُون}}

# [[demonic]], belonging or relative to [[genies]] or [[jinns]]

====Noun====
{{ar-sing-noun|جِنِّيّ|m|coll=جِنّ|collg=m|coll2=جِنَّة|coll2g=f|coll3=جَانّ|coll3g=mf|pl=جِنِّيُون|pl2=جَوَان|pl3=جِنَّان}}

# [[demon]], [[genie]], [[jinni]]
#: {{syn|ar|جَانّ}}
# male [[elf]], male [[fairy]], male [[pixie]], [[satyr]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-sing-noun|جِنِّيّ|coll=جِن|collg=m|coll2=جِنَّة|coll2g=f|coll3=جَانّ|coll3g=mf|pl=جِنِّيُون|pl2=جَوَان|pl3=جِنَّان}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|afb|يني|tr=yinni}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جُنِّي}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb-form|جُنِّي|I}}

