===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|syc|ܓܽܘܪܒܳܐ|tr=gurbā}}, {{cog|he|גֶּרֶב|tr=géreḇ}} and {{cog|ckb|گۆروا}}, {{l|ckb|گۆرە}}; of disputed etymology due to unknown direction of borrowings:
* Possibly {{bor|ar|fa|جوراب|tr=jôrâb|t=sock, stocking}}, with earlier forms {{der|ar|fa|گورب|tr=gôrab}}, {{m|fa|گوراب|tr=gôrâb}}, speculatively a metathesis of {{der|ar|pal||*gōrb/pāy|lit=grave of foot}} which has potential to be folk etymology.
* Alternatively the {{cog|ira|-}} was borrowed from {{der|ar|arc|[[גְּרָב]] / [[גְּרַב]]|tr=gəraḇ, gərāḇ|t=skin bottle or pouch}}, with it being unknown which language family the new specified semantic meaning as a {{l|en|sock}} developed first.

