Page 7334 جيب: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|جيب (ملابس)|جيب|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
The origin is {{unk|ar|nocap=1}}. A root {{ar-root|ج ي ب|nocat=1}} lacks otherwise except obvious derivations of this noun. Possibly from the root {{ar-root|ج ب ب}} whence also the known {{m|ar|جُبَّة}} garment. Also suggested to be from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, {{cog|syc|ܓܰܝܒ݁ܳܐ|tr=gaybā|t=temple, vaulted chamber}} with peculiar semantic evolution or from [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only witnessed by borrowings|unattested meanings]], or {{cog|arc|𐡢𐡡𐡠}} / {{m|arc|גַּבָּא}} / {{m|syc|ܓܰܒܴ݁ܐ|tr=gabbā|t=side, flank}}, if from this then {{doublet|ar|جَنْب|nocap=1}}, and {{m|ar|جَوْف|t=cavity}} is also compared.<ref name="ELA-GYB">{{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=302}}</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|جَيْب}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|جَيْب|m|pl=جُيُوب}}

# opening in a [[garment]]
## [[neckline]], [[collar]]
### {{lb|ar|metonymically}} [[breast]], [[bosom]], [[heart]]
## [[pocket]]
### [[pouch]]
# [[hole]], [[hollow]], [[cavity]], [[excavation]]

