Page 7339 جيش: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|ج ي ش}}
{{w|Central Semitic}} isogloss with {{cog|arc|גַּיָּיסָא|tr=gayyāsā}}, {{m|syc|ܓܝܣܐ|tr=gaysā|t=troop; band of raiders}},  {{cog|he|גַּיִס|tr=gáyis}}, {{m|he|גַּיָּיסָא|tr=gayyāsā|t=troop; band of invaders}},  and {{cog|xsa|𐩴𐩺𐩦}}, {{m|xsa|𐩴𐩦|t=unit, detachment}}, explained as a derivation from the base verb found in Arabic as {{m|ar|جَاشَ|t=to be excited, to be agitated, to storm, to rage}}, which means in this context to heave or rise up suddenly, hence inciting troops to action, raise military forces, to muster or rally, to incite a war or raise up arms, and can be further related to {{cog|gez|ጌሰ|t=to rise early}}, {{m|gez|ገይስ|t=departure, journey particularly at the beginning of the day}}. Can be borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|-}} into Arabic and {{cog|sem-srb|-}} if this happened in a century before the Common Era, when Proto-Semitic ''ś'' was still distinguished in {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, for which age this term must be imagined in any case.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|جَيْش}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-جيش.ogg}}
** {{IPA|arz|/ɡeːʃ/|a=Egyptian}}
** {{a|ar|Moroccan}} {{ary-IPA|jayš|jīš|gīš<q:archaic>}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|جَيْش|m|pl=جُيُوش}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|جَاشَ}}
# an [[army]], a [[military]] [[force]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|جَيْش|pl=جُيُوش}}

