Page 7351 ح ب ب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
For the swellings senses see also {{ar-root|ع ب ب|nocat=1}} and {{ar-root|غ ب ب|nocat=1}}, as well as rare {{ar-root|ء|ب|ب|nocat=1}} as in {{m|ar|أُبَاب}}.

For the love senses, see also {{cog|grc|ἀγαπάω}} and {{cog|he|אָהַב|tr=ʾaháḇ}} and {{cog|uga|𐎀𐎅𐎁|t=to love}} which developed from a different root variant, maybe there connected to the cognate of Arabic {{ar-root|ه ب ب|nocat=1}}. In the Arabic love root, the sense of a {{l|en|bulge}} seems bawdily extended to mean love, regard the explanation of {{m|ar|فَتًى|t=youngster}}. Remarkably {{cog|tig|ሐበ|tr=ḥäbbä}} apparently preserves the transitional sense “to wind oneself”, extended then in Arabic for amatory moves. (In so far as the {{cog|sem-eth|-}} root means love or friendship or the like it is borrowed from Arabic).

===Root===
{{ar-root|ح|ب|ب}}

# {{non-gloss definition|forms words relating to [[love]], [[affection]], [[focus]], [[attention]], [[captivation]] and personal preferences}}
# {{non-gloss definition|forms words relating to [[bulge]]s, [[hunch]]es, [[evanescent]] [[outgrowth]]s of [[nature]]}}

====Derived terms====
; Verbs
{{ar-verb forms|ح|ب|ب|a|I=to [[love]], to [[like]]|I-vn-head=حُبّ,مَحَبَّة
|I-pp-head=مَحْبُوب
|II=to [[evoke]] [[love]] for; to [[produce]] [[seed]]
|III=+
|IV=to [[love]]
|IV-vn-head=حُبّ،مَحَبَّة،إِحْبَاب
|IV-pp-head=مَحْبُوب،مُحَبّ
|V=to [[show]] love, to [[endear]] oneself to [[someone]]
|VI=to love [[one another]]
|X=to [[deem]] something [[recommendable]]
}}

; Nouns and adjectives
* {{l|ar|حُبّ|t=love}}
* {{l|ar|حُبِّيّ|t=related to [[love]]}}
* {{l|ar|حِبّ|t=[[beloved]]}}
* {{l|ar|حَبَاب}}, {{l|ar|حُبَاب}} and {{l|ar|حِبَاب}} of meanings dubiously distributed over the vocalizations
* {{l|ar|حَبِيب|t=[[beloved]]}}
* {{l|ar|أَحَبّ|t=elative of {{l|ar|حَبِيب|tr=-}}}}
* {{l|ar|مَحَبَّة|t=[[love]]}}
* {{l|ar|حَبّ|t=[[grain]]s; fruits}}
* {{l|ar|حَبَّة|t=[[grain]]; fruit}}
* {{l|ar|حَبَّذَا|t=how lovely}}
** {{l|ar|حَبَّذَ|t=to find lovely}}
* {{l|ar|حُبَاحِب|t=spark; glowworm; bladder-campion}}

===References===
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|pages=305–307}}, buggy explanation with {{cog|jpa|-}} and {{cog|arc-jla|חוּבָּא|tr=ḥubbā|t=bosom}}, thinking “breast” can give the meanings of “fruit”, and that the verbs are denominal to “breast”. However [http://cal.huc.edu/oneentry.php?lemma=xwb%232%20N&cits=all that word] is by attestation just a late variant of the Aramaic etymon of {{m|ar|عُبّ|t=breast-pocket}} and ideas of breast more likely did not exist for the present Arabic root.
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=330–331}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=363–365}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=495–498}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=89}}
