Page 7352 ح ب ر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The ink sense is from {{bor|ar|syc|ܚܒܪܐ|t=ink|tr=ḥeḇrā}}, and the scholar sense is from {{bor|ar|he|חָבֵר|tr=ḥaḇér|t={{l|en|comrade}}}}

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

# related to filling in various senses
# related to joy, beauty, improvement
# related to ink and variegated fabric

====Derived terms====
{{ar-verb forms|a|I=to [[fill]], to [[improve]]
|I-vn-head=حَبْر
|I2-pv=i|I2=to be [[glad]]
|I2-vn-head=حُبُور
|II=to [[ink]], to fill, to [[beautify]]
|IV=to make [[glad]], to [[cheer up]]
|V=to [[adorn]] oneself}}
* {{l|ar|حِبَار|g=m|t=trace, mark}}, also {{l|ar|حَبَار|g=m}}
* {{l|ar|حِبْر|g=m|t=[[ink]], [[mark]], [[ornament]], [[beauty]]}}
** {{l|ar|حِبْرِيّ|g=m|t=ink seller}}
* {{l|ar|مِحْبَرَة|g=f|t=[[inkpot]]}}
* {{l|ar|حَبَر|g=m|t=a type of variegated fabric}}, also {{l|ar|حَبِير|g=m}}
* {{l|ar|حَبَرَة|g=f|t=women's silk garment, shawl}}, also {{l|ar|حِبَرَة|g=f}}
* {{l|ar|حَبِير|t=soft, delicate}}
* {{l|ar|حَبْر|g=m|t=learned man, scholar, [[pontiff]]}} (borrowed from Hebrew, but influenced by the native root)
** {{l|ar|حَبْرَوِىّ|t=[[pontifical]]}}, also {{l|ar|حِبْرِىّ}}, {{l|ar|حَبْرِىّ}}
* {{l|ar|حَبْرِيَّة|g=f|t=[[chasuble]], [[robe]]}}
