===Etymology===
{{ar-active participle}} of {{m|ar|حَمَلَ|gloss=to [[carry]]}}.

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj|حَامِل|fpl=حَوَامِلُ}}

# [[pregnant]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 965 {{CE}}|author=[[w:w:en:Al-Mutanabbi|Al-Mutanabbi]]|title=ديوان أبي الطيب المتنبي بشرح أبي البقاء العكبري المسمى بالتبيان في شرح الديوان|chapter=لَكِ يَا مَنَازِلُ فِي الْقُلُوبِ مَنَازِلُ|volume=3|page=257|location=Beirut, Lebanon|publisher=Dar Al-Marefah|year_published=1978 {{CE}}|oclc=863546881|passage=لَوْ بَانَ بِٱلْكَرَمِ ٱلْجَنِينُ بَيَانَهُ / لَدَرَتْ بِهِ ذَكَرٌ أَمُ ٱنْثَى '''ٱلْحَامِلُ'''|subst=بِهِ/بِهِي}}

====Usage notes====
* Due to its semantic constraints, {{m|ar|حَامِل|gloss=pregnant}} is virtually always encountered in the feminine. As with some other gender-specific words, like {{m|ar|حائِض|t=menstruating}}, the feminine ending is usually omitted. (The form {{m|ar|حامِلة}} is a rarer variant, whence {{cog|fa|حامله|tr=hâmele}} and its descendants.)
* When used as a participle of {{m|ar|حَمَلَ}}, {{m|ar|حَامِل|gloss=carrying}} behaves like a normal participle.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|1=-|d=-|pl=-|f=حَامِل|fpl=حَوَامِل}}

