Page 7531 حبارى: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2020|August|3}}
{{swp|lang=ar|Chlamydotis|الحُبَارَى (''Chlamydotis'')}}
{{swp|lang=ar|Otis tarda|حُبَارَى عَرَبِيّ (''Otis tarda'')}}
[[File:MacQueen's bustard.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|حُبَارَى}} – {{taxfmt|Chlamydotis macqueenii|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ح ب ر}} related to delight since it is the most-prized fowl flesh. For the pattern compare {{m|ar|سُمَانَى|t=[[quail]], ''[[Coturnix coturnix]]''}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|حُبَارَى}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|حُبَارَى|f|d=حُبَارَيَانِ|pl=حُبَارَيَات}}

# [[bustard]] ({{taxfmt|Otididae|family}} bird such as {{taxfmt|Chlamydotis|genus}} spp., {{taxfmt|Otis tarda|species}}, {{taxfmt|Ardeotis arabs|species}})
#* {{RQ:Sunna|abudawud|28|62
|passage=أَكَلْتُ مَعَ رَسُولِ اللَّهِ [[صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ]] لَحْمَ '''حُبَارَى'''.
|translation=I ate with the Prophet ([[peace be upon him]]) the flesh of a '''bustard'''.
|subst=اللَّهِ/اللّٰهِ,وَسَلَّمَ/وَ-سَلَّمَ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|حُبَارَى|pl=حُبَارَيَات}}

====Derived terms====
