Page 7534 حببور: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Sabine Beckmann Anemone coronaria habitat Katharo plain 4 03.jpg|frameless|right|{{lang|ar|حَبَبَوْر}}|upright=1.5]]

===Etymology===
{{univerbation|ar|حَبّ}} and {{bor|ar|la|papāver}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|حَبَّبَوْر}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|حَبَّبَوْر|sing=حَبَّبَوْرَة}}

# {{tlb|ar|al-Andalus}} {{vern|poppy anemone}} ({{taxlink|Anemone coronaria|species}})
#* {{R:ar:FAH|6II|page=318 Nr. 482 also [https://shamela.ws/book/148096/428 online]|passage=ويقولون لنَوْرٍ أحمرَ: '''حَبَبَّوْرٌ''' . وإنَّما تقولُ له العربُ: شقائقُ النُّعْمانِ. ونُسِبَ إلى النُعْمانِ بنِ المنذِرِ لأنَّهُ حَمَاهُ. ويُقالُ له أيضًا: الشَّقِرُ، والواحدةُ: شَقِرَةٌ. ويُقالُ له أيضًا: الشُّقَارَى.|t=They say to the red flower ''ḥababbawr''. The Arabs said ''šāqāʔiq an-nuʕman''. This relates to nuʕman ibn-al-munḏir who protected it. It is also called: ''šaqir'', one ''šaqira'', and also ''šuqārā''.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|حَبَّبَوْر|sing=حَبَّبَوْرَة}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|an|ababol|babol|farabol|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ca|ababol|alts=1|bor=1}}
* {{desc|gl|papoula|bor=1|alts=1}}
* {{desc|pt|papoula|bor=1|alts=1}}
* {{desc|es|ababol|bor=1|alts=1}}

