Page 7538 حبر: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ح ب ر}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|ink}}
{{bor+|ar|syc|ܚܒܪܐ|t=ink|tr=ḥeḇrā}}, from the root {{syc-root-entry|ܚ|ܒ|ܪ}} related to darkness. Merged with the root {{ar-root|ح|ب|ر}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حِبْر}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-حبر.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حِبْر|m|pl=أَحْبَار}}

# {{senseid|ar|ink}} [[ink]]
#: {{syn|ar|مِدَاد|نِقْس}}
#: {{holo|ar|مِحْبَرَة|دَوَاة}}
# {{senseid|ar|beauty}} [[beauty]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حِبْر|pl=أَحْبَار}}

===Etymology 2===
Senses related to ink, writing, and discoloration are from Etymology 1 (see above).

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:حَبْر}} {{tlb|ar|transitive}}

# to make [[happy]]; to [[elate]]
#: {{syn|ar|Thesaurus:ar:make happy}}
#: {{hypo|ar|كَرَّمَ|نَعَّمَ|رَفَّهَ|أَرَاحَ}}
# to [[ink]], to [[fill]], [[cover]], [[smear]], [[mark]], [[write]], [[draw]], [[illustrate]], or [[outline]] with [[ink]]
## to [[write]]
##: {{syn|ar|كَتَبَ|نَمَقَ}}
# {{lb|ar|dated}} to [[improve]] the overall [[quality]] of (a text, a performance, a skill, and so on), to [[refine]], to [[polish]]; to [[perfect]]
#: {{syn|ar|حَسَّنَ}}
# {{lb|ar|dated}} to [[improve]] the [[shape]], [[form]], [[style]], [[structure]], or [[composition]] of (handwriting, voice, and so on), to [[beautify]]; to [[embellish]];  to [[pretty]]
#: {{syn|ar|جَمَّلَ}}
## to [[improve]] in [[aspect]] or [[appearance]], to make [[visual]]ly [[pleasing]], to [[deck]], to [[decorate]], to [[ornament]]
##: {{syn|ar|زَيَّنَ|نَمَّقَ|زَوَّقَ}}
## to [[pattern]] (a garment); to [[embroider]]
##: {{syn|ar|نَقَشَ|طَرَّزَ|وَشَّى}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:حَبْر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.nopass.vn:حُبُور}} {{tlb|ar|intransitive}}

# to be or become [[glad]] or [[happy]], to [[cheer up]], to [[brighten]]
#: {{syn|ar|Thesaurus:ar:become happy}}
# {{lb|ar|of teeth}} to become [[discolor]]ed (as if [[stain]]ed with [[ink]]), to become [[dark]], to [[yellow]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.nopass.vn:حُبُور}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حَبْر|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|حَبَرَ|form=I}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَبْر}}

===Etymology 3===
{{denominal verb|ar|حِبْر|t=ink|id=ink}}. Senses related to improvement, perfection, and embellishment are from or influenced by the root {{ar-root|ح|ب|ر}} (see above).

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حَبَّرَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}} {{tlb|ar|transitive}}

# to [[ink]], to [[fill]], [[cover]], [[smear]], [[mark]], [[write]], [[draw]], [[illustrate]], or [[outline]] with [[ink]]
## to [[write]] (especially in an elegant style), to [[compose]]
##: {{syn|ar|نَمَّقَ}}
# {{lb|ar|dated}} to [[better]] or [[improve]] in [[quality]], [[appearance]], etc. to [[enhance]]; to [[polish up]]; to [[perfect]]
## {{lb|ar|dated}} to [[prettify]]; to [[bedeck]], to [[adorn]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 4===
{{etymid|ar|scholar}}
{{bor+|ar|hbo|חָבֵר|tr=ḥɔḇer|t=comrade}} in a specific meaning as used for sectarian cadres. Merged with Etymology 3 by analogy with the use of ink by religious clerks and scribes, hence "a man of learning", hence "a scholarly theologian", hence "an authority in matters of religion".

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حَبْر|حِبْر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حَبْر|m|pl=أَحْبَار|head2=حِبْر}} {{tlb|ar|countable}}

# {{lb|ar|broadly}} a [[scholar]] (especially one that is [[high]]ly [[regard]]ed and [[respect]]ed by a [[certain]] [[group]] and is [[deem]]ed to be an [[authority]])
## {{q|with {{m|ar|ال|t=the}}}} the Scholar (one of the titles and designations of {{w|Ibn Abbas}}, one of companions of [[Muhammad]])
# {{lb|ar|religion|chiefly Abrahamism}} a [[well]]-[[versed]] [[religious]] [[scribe]]; a [[learned]] [[theologian]]; a [[religious]] [[authority]]
## {{lb|ar|Christianity}} a [[bishop]]
##: {{syn|ar|أُسْقُف}}
## {{lb|ar|Judaism}} a [[rabbi]]
##: {{syn|ar|حَاخَام|حَكِيم}}
## {{lb|ar|Islam}} an [[esteem]]ed [[authoritative]] [[theologian]], an [[imam]]
##: {{syn|ar|إِمَام|مَرْجَع|مُقَلَّد}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَبْر|pl=أَحْبَار|head2=حِبْر}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Ahrens-Christliches|page=20}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=247}}
* {{R:myz:Nöldeke|page=61}}
* {{R:ar:Geiger|page=48}}

{{C|ar|Liquids|Writing}}

