Page 7586 حدأة: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Black Kite (Milvus migrans), Jalpaiguri.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.55|{{l|ar|حَدَأَةٌ سَوْدَاءُ}} – ''[[Milvus migrans]]'']]

===Etymology 1===
{{unk|ar|title=Unclear}}. Compares to {{bor|ar|arc|הדיא|tr=hāḏāyā}}, {{m|arc|הודיא|tr=hōḏāyā|t=a kind of bird of prey}}, {{cog|he-mis|הֲדָיָה|tr=haḏāyā|t=a bird of the hawk species}}, for earlier {{cog|hbo|דָּאׇה|tr=dāʾā}}, {{m|he|דַּיָּה|tr=dayyā}} either of which has been assumed to mean “kite” and equated with {{cog|arc|דַּיְיתָא}}, {{m|arc|דַּיְתָא|tr=dayyəṯā}}, {{m|arc|דַּיּוּתָא|tr=dayyūṯā}}, which is found in {{cog|syc|-}} as {{m|syc|ܕܰܝܬ݂ܳܐ|tr=dayṯā|t=kite}}, {{m|syc|ܕܰܝܘܱܝ|tr=dayway|t=kite}}, even {{cog|uga|𐎄𐎛𐎊|t=a kind of bird of prey}}, and curiously poetic {{cog|ar|اِبْن دَأْيَة|t=raven}}, like the Aramaic and Hebrew bird names with ''h-'' are also preceded by {{m|arc|בַּר|tr=bar}} respectively {{m|he|בֶּן|tr=ben|t=son}}, sometimes in the latter {{m|he|בַּר|tr=bar}} which exposes the latter as an Aramaism, so perhaps the Arabic terms are too, with better-preserved consonantism as in {{m|ar|كَمَأ|t=truffle}}. Consider also the borrowing of a transferred sense in {{m|ar|دَيُّوث|t=cuckold}}. The {{cog|tig|ሕዶ|t=owl}} may be an only random correspondence.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|حِدَّايَة||colloquial}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حَدَأَة|head2=حِدْأَة|head3=حِدَأَة|head4=حِدَّأَة|f|pl=حِدْآن|pl2=حِدَأ|pl3=حِدَاء}}

# [[kite]] (bird)

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَدَأَة|f|pl=حِدْآن|pl2=حِدَأ|pl3=حِدَاء}}

=====References=====
* {{R:CAL|hwdy%232|N}}
* {{R:CAL|dyyh|N}}
* {{R:CAL|dywy|N}}
* {{R:Jastrow 1903|page=333a|entry=הֲדָיָא II, הֲדָיָה}}
* {{R:Jastrow 1903|page=299a|entry=דַּיְיתָא}}
* {{R:arc:Levy|volume=1|page=169|entry=דַּיְתָא}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=2|pages=91–92 Nr. 64}}

===Etymology 2===
From when the kite opens it wings, it looks like an axe.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حَدَأَة|f|pl=حِدَاء|pl2=حَدَأ}}

# [[pickaxe]]
#: {{syn|ar|مِعْوَل}}
# [[double-headed]] axe

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَدَأَة|f|pl=حِدَاء|pl2=حَدَأ}}

{{C|ar|Birds of prey|Tools}}
