#* {{R:ar:Geyer-Zwei Gedichte|volume=1|instead=1|lang=ar|page=102|zusatzurl=https://khatab38.blogspot.com/2010/06/blog-post_9412.html|passage=وَشِمِلَّةٍ حَرْفٍ كَأَنَّ قُتُودَهَا … جَلَّلْتُهَا ({{var}} لَبَسْتُهَا) جَوْنَ السَّرَاةِ خَفَيْدَدًا|t=Some hardy she-camel the saddle-woods of which I applied like upon a black-backed ostrich}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|حَرْف|f=حَرْف|pl=حَرْف|fpl=حَرْف|d=حَرْف:tri|fd=حَرْف:tri}}

===Etymology 1.4===
{{nonlemma}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حِرَف}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun-pl|حِرَف|p}}

# {{plural of|ar|حِرْفَة}}

===Etymology 2.1===
{{ar-verbal noun}} of the verb above, the result of turning the tongue or stylus or limb to the side. The meaning “word” is a {{semantic loan|ar|ML.|terminus|nocap=1}}, spawned in the environment of philosophy text translation (see Praetorius 1909).

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حَرْف}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-حرف.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حَرْف|m|pl=حُرُوف|pl2=أَحْرُف}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|حَرَفَ|form=I}}
# [[letter]] (of the alphabet), piece of [[type]]
#: {{ux|ar|inline=1|حَرْفًا بِحَرْفٍ|tr=ḥarfan bi-ḥarfin|t=[[word for word]]}}
# [[consonant]]
# {{lb|ar|grammar}} [[particle]]
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} [[word]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَرْف|pl=حُرُوف|pl2=أَحْرُف}}

