Page 7679 حزاء: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
In view of the hallucinogenic uses of the plant, perhaps related to {{m|ar|تَحَزَّى|t=to divine; to divine from the flights or cries of birds by driving them away}}, {{m|ar|حَزَى}}, {{m|ar|حَزَا|t=to compute by conjecture (fruits on a palm etc.)}}, a variant of {{ar-root|ح ص ي}}, {{ar-root|ح ص و}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|حَزَاء}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|حَزَاء|m|sing=حَزَاءَة}}

# {{lb|ar|rare|in post-classical Arabic only [[Bedouin]]}} [[common rue]] ({{taxfmt|Ruta graveolens|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|سُذَاب}}
#: {{hyper|ar|فَيْجَن}}
#* {{RQ:Mafatih-Vloten|pages=167 line 10 – page 168 line 1|footer=<small>commented in {{R:ar:Seidel:1915|page=25 Anm. 73}}, where held {{taxlink|Ridolfia segetum|species}}</small>|passage=الْحَزَاء بقلة تشبه الْكَرَفْس لريحها خَمْطة وهي بالفارسيّة دينارُویه|t=Rue is a vegetable similar to celery, of an acrid smell, in Persian called ''dīnārūya''.}}
#* {{RQ:Janah:2020|page=514|section=335 (fol. 31v,12–13)|passage={{ll|ar|زوفرا}}، قال الطبري: إنّه الح‹ز›اء من الحاوي، وفي موضع آخر منه: زوفرا {{ll|ar|كاشم}}.|t=Zawfarā: Aṭ-Tabarīy said: It is rue <small>[in ibn Janāḥs manuscript: {{m|ar|حنّاء|t=henna}}]</small>, from ''Al-Ḥāwī'', and elsewhere he says it is lovage.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{lang|ar|{{w|محمد بن لعبون|lang=ar}}}}|title=ar:هل الدار يا عواد إلا منازل|year=a. 1832|url=https://www.alsh3r.com/poems/view/17329|passage=وَلَا تَحْسِب اَلْجَثْجَاثَ وَٱلْرِمْثَ وَٱلْحَزَا|t=Keep away from false fleabane, saxaul and rue!}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|حَزَاء}}

{{C|ar|Rue family plants}}
