Page 7719 حسل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Freytag thought that since {{m|ar|حَسَلَ}} {{m|ar|خَسَلَ}} are tradited to mean “to repel, to propel vehemently, to cast off” just as {{m|ar|سَخَلَ}} it would be the same word as {{m|ar|سَخْل|t=offspring of a sheep or goat}}. One has to add {{m|ar|سِحْلِيَّة|t=lizard}}, which also has metathetical forms in dialects and is itself judged post-classical, lacking in the Classical Arabic dictionaries unlike {{m-self|ar|حِسْل}}. Semantic connection of it to {{m|ar|سَحَلَ|t=to scrape off}} is difficult. Perhaps this and {{cog|axm|խլէզ|t=lizard}} have to be ascribed to a colloquial {{bor|ar|arc|-}} substrate related to {{m|arc|חלד}} / {{m|syc|ܚܠܕ|tr=ḥlaḏ|t=to crawl}} whence also {{cog|arc|חוּלְדּא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܘܠܕܐ|t=mole|tr=ḥuldā}} and thence {{cog|ar|خُلْد|t=mole}} comes. In Neo-{{cog|hy|խլեզ}} is also attested as a “slug”, which permits connecting {{cog|arc|חְלָזֹונָא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܠܵܙܘܿܢܵܐ|tr=ḥəlāzōnā|t=snail, slug}} whence {{cog|ar|حَلَزُون|t=snail, slug}} is borrowed, itself formally corresponding to {{cog|arc-jla|חִילִּיז}}, {{m|arc|חִלִּיז|tr=ḥillīz}} which is translated as “cyst” and “one afflicted with an eye-disease called {{m|he|חֽלָּזֹון|tr=hillāzōn|lit=slug}}”, of dubious vowelization and perhaps identical to the Syriac alternative form of the word for “snail, slug” shaped {{m|syc|ܚܠܝܙܘܢܐ|tr=ḥəlīzōnā}}; compare {{cog|syc|ܚܰܠܳܕܺܝܬܳܐ|tr=ḥalāḏīṯā|t=gangrene}} and {{m|syc|ܚܰܠܕܘܽܕܴܐ|tr=ḥaləḏūḏā|t=jerboa}} for the root use, {{cog|arc-jla|חַלְּטָתָה}}, {{m|arc|חַלְּטָתָא|tr=ḥalləṭāṯā|t=lizard}} for the variation.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حِسْل}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حِسْل|m|pl=أَحْسَال|pl2=حُسُول|pl3=حِسْلَة|pl4=حِسْلَان}}

# [[young]] of a [[spiny-tailed lizard]], when it comes forth fresh from its egg and before it has fully [[hatch out|hatched out]]<!--ausschliefen--> (then it is called {{m|ar|غَيْدَاق}}, then {{m|ar|مُطْبِخ}}, then {{m|ar|خُضْرِم}}, and an adult is {{m|ar|ضَبّ}})

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حِسْل|pl=أَحْسَال|pl2=حُسُول|pl3=حِسْلَة|pl4=حِسْلَان}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|حُسَيْل|t=diminutive}}
* {{l|ar|أَبُو حِسْل|t=adult [[spiny-tailed lizard]]}}
* {{desc|ar|حِسَّل|t=''certain spurges''|unc=1|nolb=1|der=1}}

====Further reading====
* {{R:ar:BehnstedtWoidich|WA2|pages=361–362}} for {{m|ar|سِحْلِيَّة}}.
* {{w|Ismail ibn Hammad al-Jawhari|Jawharīy}} [http://arabiclexicon.hawramani.com/%d8%b7%d8%a8%d8%ae/#9fd863 s.v.]
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=380b}}
** via {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|page=487a|خسل}} compared from {{m|ar|سَخْل}} at {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=296a|سخل}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=569}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Lurche|page=147}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Beitr.|page=87}}

===Etymology 2===
{{unk|ar}}, possibly an alteration of the name of the spiny-tailed lizard babies since due to the yellow colour of the flowers these could be designed as such.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حِسَّل}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حِسَّل|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete|rare}}

# {{n-g|certain [[spurge]]s}}, {{taxlink|Euphorbia palustris|species}}, {{taxfmt|Euphorbia esula|species}}; {{taxlink|Euphorbia cyparissias|species}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:{{w|Ibn al-Baitar|ابن البيطار}}<tr:Ibn al-Bayṭār>|year=a. 1248|title=ar:الجامع لمفردات الأدوية والأغذية<t:{{w|lang=la|De simplicibus medicinis opus magnum (Ebenbitar)|De simplicibus medicinis opus magnum}}>|passage='''حسل''': الرازي: يسمى باليونانية حسمى وهو بقل يشبه الصعتر الطويل الورق المعروف بالبرمر إلا أنه أعظم منه وأطيب رائحة فهو لذلك أجود للمعدة. قال صاحب الفلاحة: الحسمى هو الحسل يشبه الصعتر البستاني إلا أنه أغبر وهو أطول ورقاً من الصعتر، وفيه شيء يطول حتى ينطوي بعضه على بعض، ويطبخ مع الطعام ويؤكل نيئاً وهو يصلح المعدة ويطيب الجشاء ويصلح الطعام الفاسد فيها ويسرع إحدار الطعام ويطيب النكهة وقد يشفي من لدغة العقرب ونهشه الرتيل}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حِسَّل}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|roa-oit|esula|bor=1}}
** {{desc|frm|esule|bor=1}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Glessgen:1996|page=748}}

{{C|ar|Lizards|Baby animals|Spurges}}
