Page 7759 حصرم: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2020|September|3}}
[[File:Immature grapes fruit.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|حصْرم}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology 1.1===
By surface augmented from the root {{ar-root|ح ص ر}} to [[striction]]. But compare also {{cog|he|חַרְצָן|tr=ḥarṣā́n}} now used in the sense of a [[pip]] of a grape but read preferredly<ref>{{R:he:Keil-Delitzsch|A2|page=214}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|de|last=Vilmar|first=Eduard|pages=468–469 from 438–484|title=Die symbolische Bedeutung des Naziräergelübdes|authorlink=de:Eduard Vilmar|year=1864|location=Gotha|publisher=Friedrich Andreas Perthes|volume=37|issue=3|work=Theologische Studien und Kritiken|pageurl=http://idb.ub.uni-tuebingen.de/opendigi/thstkr_1864#p=460}}</ref><ref>{{cite-journal|year=1848|title=The Produce of the Wineyard in the East|last=Homes|first=Henry|work={{w|Bibliotheca Sacra}} and Theological Review|page=286 from 283-295|location=New York and London|publisher=John Wiley; Andover: William H. Wardwell|volume=5|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=AWNPAAAAcAAJ&pg=PA286}}</ref> in the {{w|Book of Numbers}} 6:4 as referring to unripe grapes for [[verjuice]] – although that is already what {{m|he|בוסר|בֹּסֶר|tr=boser}}, the cognate of {{cog|ar|بُسْر|t=unripe dates}}, means –, connected then to the root {{ar-root|ح ر ص}} related to abrasion because of it being sharp on the tongue, as well as {{cog|he|חָרִיץ|tr=ḥārīṣ|t=cheese; slit, furrow}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حِصْرِم}}, dialectally also {{ar-IPA|حُصْرُم}} and {{ar-IPA|حَصْرَم}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|حِصْرِم|m|pl=حَصَارِم}}

# [[unripe]] [[grape]]s, [[sour grapes]], grapes [[green]] and [[acid]] due to lacking [[maturity]]
#* {{quote-web|ar|work=Aš-šarq al-ʾawsaṭ|date=2019-06-24|title=ar:باتجاه سقوط محور تركيا وإيران وقطر|author=ar:مشاري الذايدي|url=https://aawsat.com/home/article/1781221/مشاري-الذايدي/باتجاه-سقوط-محور-تركيا-وإيران-وقطر|passage=المعسكر الذي تقبع به سلطات قطر وتركيا وإيران في النازل لا الطالع، تحصد الزقوم وتتجرع العلقم وتضرس الحصرم على أسنان نخرة.|t=The camp in which the powers of Qaṭar, Turkey, and Iran trumpet is descending, not ascending; they reap the Egyptian balsam, gorge the colocynth, and chomp on sour grapes high-nosed.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|حِصْرِم|sing=-|pl=حَصَارِم}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|حِصْرِمِيَّة|t=verjuice-stew}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mt|ħesrem}}
* {{→}} Kurdish:
** {{desc|kmr|harsim}}

===Etymology 1.2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حَصْرَمَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|Iq}}

# to make [[tight]] or [[tense]], to [[constrict]] or [[straiten]]

=====Conjugation=====
