Page 7763 حصن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ح ص ن}}
{{bor+|ar|arc|חִצְנַא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܶܨܢܳܐ|tr=ḥeṣnā|t=stronghold, fortress}}, assimilating the laryngeal from earlier {{m|arc|𐡇𐡎𐡍𐡀|tr=-}} / {{m|syc|ܚܶܣܢܳܐ|tr=ḥesnā|t=stronghold, fortress}}, also {{m|arc|חוּסנַא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܽܘܣܢܳܐ|tr=ḥusnā}}, already attested in {{w|Old Aramaic}} {{m|arc|𐤇𐤎𐤍𐤀|tr=ḥsnʾ}}, deriving from a well-used root {{m|arc|ח־ס־ן}} {{syc-root-entry|ܚ|ܣ|ܢ}}, which would be cognate to the Arabic root {{ar-root|خ ش ن|nocat=1}} related to roughness, or perhaps {{ar-root|ح س ن|nocat=1}} related to goodliness, comeliness, if one relates [[pulchritude]] with [[brawn]], and fortresses with [[exalted|exaltedness]] of appearance. This ascription of Aramaic origin is corroborated by the consideration that fortresses are not to be sought in the original place of the Arabic language, and in conformity with this, most other terms for fortresses, castles, and towers are borrowed, {{m|ar|بُرْج}}, {{m|ar|قَصْر}}, {{m|ar|بَلَاط}}, {{m|ar|مِجْدَل}}, {{m|ar|صَرْح}}, {{m|ar|مِحْرَاب}}, {{m|ar|صَوْمَعَة}}, {{m|ar|سَرَاي}}, {{m|ar|إِيوَان}}, {{m|ar|قَشْلَة}}.

The root’s other formations, containing meanings related to inaccessibility, protection, strength, are {{glossary|denominal}} from the word for the fortress, {{m|ar||حِصْن}}

Though the root {{ar-root|ح|ص|ن|nocat=1}} contains {{m|ar|حِصَان|t=horse, stallion, stud}}, not even this is a strong contender for a native origin in this root, since this word for a stud or stallion, of high register, could have been invented easily in folk poetry from the idea of strength a fortress is connected to, which is supported by the fact that horses aren’t to be sought in Arabia either, and the other word {{m|ar|فَرَس}} has also been picked up.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|حِصْن}}
** {{IPA|acw|/ħi.sˤin/|[ħɪ.sˤɪn]|a=Hijazi}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حِصْن|m|pl=حُصُون|pl2=حِصَنَة|pl3=أَحْصَان}}

# {{lb|ar|also|figuratively}} [[stronghold]], [[fortress]], [[entrenchment]]
#* {{quote|ar|لَا إِلٰهَ إِلَّا اللهُ حِصْنِي فَمَنْ دَخَلَ حِصْنَي أَمِنَ مِنْ عَذَابِي|"There is no god but God" is my fortress and whomever enters my fortress is saved from my torture ([[hadith]])}}
# [[armor]] or [[weapons]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حِصْن|pl=حُصُون|pl2=حِصَنَة|pl3=أَحْصَان}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|ka|ისანი|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|ota|حصن|tr=hısn|bor=1}}
* {{desc|es|izn|bor=1}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|pages=235–236}}
* {{R:gez:Praetorius:1907|pages=616–617}}
* {{R:CAL|xcn|N}}
* {{R:CAL|xsn%232|N}}
* {{R:CAL|xsn%233|N}}
* {{R:CAL|xsn|V}}

