Page 7775 حضرتك: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{m|ar|حَضْرَة|gloss=[[presence]]}} + {{m|ar|[[كَ]]/[[كِ]]|gloss=[[your]]}}; "your presence" (i.e. "[[your grace]]"). Compare {{cog|es|usted}} (from {{m|es|vuestra merced|gloss=your mercy}}), and the cognate {{cog|pt|-}} term {{m|pt|você}}.

===Pronoun===
{{ar-pronoun|حَضْرَتُكَ|m}}

# {{lb|ar|formal}} [[you]] (''polite second-person personal pronoun'')

====Usage notes====
* {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكَ}} and {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكِ}} are used in conducting business with strangers and formal or professional acquaintances, but their use is not considered compulsory in such situations (unlike {{cog|fr|vous}}, {{cog|es|usted}}, {{cog|de|Sie}}, etc.), and Arabic does not have a true [[T-V distinction]]. Use of the simple pronouns {{m|ar|أَنْتَ}} and {{m|ar|أَنْتِ}} is generally not considered rude or disrespectful.
* Though morphologically third person, {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكَ}} and {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكِ}} display second-person agreement (thus, verbs whose subject is {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكِ}} or {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكِ}} are conjugated in the second person).
* Similarly, although {{m|ar|حَضْرَتُكَ}} is technically a form of the feminine noun {{m|ar|حَضْرَة}}, it displays masculine gender agreement.
* Although morphologically singular, the dual and plural forms display dual and plural agreement, respectively.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|حَضْرَتَك|inf_m_sg_def=حَضْرَتَك|nom_m_sg_def=حَضْرَتُكَ|gen_m_sg_def=حَضْرَتِكَ|acc_m_sg_def=حَضْرَتَكَ|inf_f_sg_def=حَضْرَتِك|nom_f_sg_def=حَضْرَتُكِ|gen_f_sg_def=حَضْرَتِكِ|acc_f_sg_def=حَضْرَتَكِ|inf_m_du_def=حَضْرَتْكُمَا|nom_m_du_def=حَضْرَتُكُمَا|gen_m_du_def=حَضْرَتِكُمَا|acc_m_du_def=حَضْرَتَكُمَا|inf_f_du_def=حَضْرَتْكُمَا|nom_f_du_def=حَضْرَتُكُمَا|gen_f_du_def=حَضْرَتِكُمَا|acc_f_du_def=حَضْرَتَكُمَا|inf_m_pl_def=حَضْرَتْكُم|nom_m_pl_def=حَضْرَتُكُم|gen_m_pl_def=حَضْرَتِكُم|acc_m_pl_def=حَضْرَتَكُم|inf_f_pl_def=حَضْرَتْكُنَّ|nom_f_pl_def=حَضْرَتُكُنَّ|gen_f_pl_def=حَضْرَتِكُنَّ|acc_f_pl_def=حَضْرَتَكُنَّ|state=def|omitarticle=yes|pos=pronoun|noirreg=yes}}

