Page 7855 حل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ح ل ل}}. Compare {{cog|he|חל}}.

The meaning of “sesame oil” may derive via a chain of calques from {{der|ar|akk|ellum|𒉌𒄑|tr=ellum}}, which is also homographic to {{m|akk|šamnum|𒉌𒄑|tr=šamnum|t=oil}}, that, to build a bridge, might suggest that {{bor|ar|arc|חָלָא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܠܐ|tr=ḥallā}} also had this meaning but has consistently been misread as more common “vinegar”, the etymon of {{m+|ar|خَلّ|t=vinegar}}, if not other homographs, due to complete merger of ''ḥ'' and ''ḫ''  more likely than in Arabic itself where it also happens due to {{glossary|tashif|taṣḥīf}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:حَلّ}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[unfasten]]; to [[untie]]; to [[unknot]]; to [[unravel]]; to [[disentangle]]; to [[loosen]]
#: {{syn|ar|فَكَّ|t=to unfasten; to unfix; to dislodge; to unscrew; to disjoint; to disintegrate; to disassemble; to unbuild; to deconstruct}}
#: {{ant|ar|عَقَدَ|رَبَطَ|سَلْسَلَ|رَكَّبَ|لَصَقَ|صَمَّغَ|t1=to tie; to knot|t2=to tie; to link|t3=to chain; to serialize|t4=to assemble; to put together; to build up; to construct|t5=to paste; to glue|t6=to glue}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|20|27|passage=وَاحْلُلْ عُقْدَةً مِّن لِّسَانِي}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[find]] an [[answer]] to or a [[solution]] for (something, such as a problem); to [[untangle]]; to [[crack]]; to [[solve]]
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[liquefy]]; to [[dissolve]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَذَابَ|سَيَّحَ|t1=to dissolve; to melt; to thaw|t2=to melt}}
#: {{cot|ar|بَخَّرَ|t1=to vaporize}}
#: {{ant|ar|صَلَّبَ|جَمَّدَ|ثَلَّجَ|t1=to harden; to solidify|t2=to solidify; to refrigerate; to freeze|t3=to refrigerate; to ice, to glaciate; to freeze}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[turn]] into a [[solution]]
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[deprive]] of [[effective]] [[legal]] or otherwise [[bind]]ing [[power]], to [[invalidate]]; to [[dissolve]]
## {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[breach]] (a contract, an agreement, an oath, and the like); to [[break]]
##: {{syn|ar|نَقَضَ|t=to break; to breach}}
# to [[settle]]; to [[approach]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=al baskari|year=713AH/1313 {{CE}}|text=فَلَأَنْتَ أَنْتَ إِذَاْ '''حَلَلْتَ''' بــ: طَيْبَةٍ|title=darul habib|t=For when you, '''approach''' goodness(طيبة) (one of the names of Madinah)}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:حَلّ}}

=====Descendants=====
