Page 7948 حناء: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|حِنَّة}}

===Etymology 1===
{{unknown|ar}} chain of etymology, but based on the era of {{noncog|arc|-}} equivalents which are taken to be Arabisms and its absence from earlier Semitic languages, the dating seems to suggest the Abbasid Era, a period with great Iranian court influence. Ultimately being derived from {{der|ar|pal|hndwtn'|ts=handūdan}}, its stem {{m|pal|hndʾd|ts=*handāy-, *hannāy-|t=to smear, to plaster, to anoint}}; a semantic cognate or calque translation with its Semitic equivalent the Qur'anic {{noncog|ar|كَافُور|tr=|t=''[[Lawsonia inermis]]''; alternatively identified as [[camphor]]}}, from {{noncog|ar|كَفَرَ|tr=|t=to cover over}}, a root connection found all across Semitic languages.

Compare {{noncog|akk|𒇒𒌓𒀀|tr=kupru|t=bitumen, pitch}}, from {{noncog|akk|𒅗𒉺𒊒|tr=kapāru|t=to smear, to daub on}}, {{noncog|he|[[כֹּפֶר]] / [[כּוֺפֶר]]|tr=kōp̱er|t=pitch, tar; henna}}, {{noncog|arc|כּוּפְרָא}}, {{noncog|syc|ܟܘܦܪܐ|tr=kūp̄rā|pos=|g=|id=||t=pitch, tar; henna}}, {{noncog|uga|𐎋𐎔𐎗|t=henna}}. For the {{noncog|ira}} compare {{cog|xmn|ʾnwdg|tr=annōdag||the anointed one, Messiah}}, and {{cog|fa|اندودن|tr=andudan|t=to besmear, to coat}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حِنَّاء|m|pl=حُنْآن}}

# [[henna]]; the plant ({{taxfmt|Lawsonia inermis|species}})
# [[henna]]; dye prepared from ({{taxfmt|Lawsonia inermis|species}})

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|حِنَّاء:tri}}

