Page 7960 حنطة: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From a common Semitic root. Compare {{cog|he|חיטה|t=wheat|חִטָּה|tr=ḥiṭṭā́}}, {{cog|uga|𐎈𐎉𐎚|t=wheat}}, {{cog|jpa|-}} and {{cog|tmr|חִיטְּתָא|tr=ḥiṭtəṯā|t=wheat}} (absolute state: {{m|arc|חִיטָּא|tr=ḥiṭṭā}}) / {{m|syc|ܚܛܬܐ|tr=ḥeṭtəṯā|t=wheat}}  (absolute state: {{m|syc|ܚܛܐ|tr=ḥeṭṭā}}), {{cog|arc-imp|𐡇𐡍𐡈𐡕𐡀|t=wheat}} (absolute state: {{m|arc|𐡇𐡍𐡈𐡀}}), {{cog|arc-pal|𐡧𐡨𐡠}} (emphatic). {{cog|gez|ኅጠት|tr=ḫəṭṭät}}, {{m|gez|ሕጠት|t=grain|tr=ḥəṭṭät}}, {{cog|sqt||ḥinṭeh|sc=Latn|t=wheat}}, {{cog|gdq||ḥeyṭ|t=wheat|sc=Latn}}, {{cog|akk|𒊺|ts=uṭṭatu, eṭṭetu|t=edible grains or kernels, especially barley or wheat}}. With some likelihood {{m|xcl|ունդ}}, {{m|xcl|հունդ|t=edible seed, grain}} is related.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|حِنْطَة}}

