Page 7975 حنيف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Of the root {{ar-root|ح ن ف}}. Probably an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} loan, borrowing first the plural of {{cog|syc|ܚܢܦܐ|tr=ḥanpā|t=pagan, impious}} and back-forming the Arabic singular, or from a [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only witnessed by borrowings|differently]] vocalized {{cog|arc-nab|-}} relative of it, the details are disputed, like the semantics were a source of disagreement from the beginning.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|حَنِيف}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj|حَنِيف|pl=حُنَفَاء}}

# [[inclining]]
## [[inclining]] from one [[religion]] to another
### belonging to the right religion, of true belief
### {{lb|ar|more often|_|obsolete}} someone connected to a wrong religion, [[impious]], [[deviatory]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|حَنِيف|pl=حُنَفَاء}}

