Page 7988 حوت: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
The source is {{unk|ar|nocap=1}}. Presumably of particularly ancient origin, which may have allowed for derivations from the roots {{ar-root|ح ي و|nocat=1}} “living”<ref name="ELA">{{R:xaa:ELA|II|pages=378–379}}</ref> or {{ar-root|ح و ي|nocat=1}} “writhing; containing”—derivations unworkable with transmitted Arabic grammar. However the {{cog|sem-nwe|-}} noun-forming suffix ''-ūt'' added to {{bor|ar|arc|𐤇𐤅𐤄|tr=ḥwh|pos=absolute state}} / {{m|arc|𐡇𐡅𐡉𐡄}} / {{m|arc|חויא|tr=ḥiwyā}} / {{m|syc|ܚܘܝܐ|tr=ḥewyā|t=snake}}, a well-known word with {{cog|ar|حَيَّة|t=snake}} from the latter root, [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only witnessed by borrowings|could have]] yielded an Arabic form {{m|ar||*حِوُوت|t=sea-snake}}, which according to the known Arabic sound law prohibiting sequences ''iwū'' and ''iyū'' in favour of ''ū'' (as in the third person plural {{g|m}} past of {{m|ar|نَسِيَ}}), would  have been contracted to {{m-self|ar|حُوت}}.

As for non-{{cog|sem|-}} provenance, {{bor|ar|egy|-}} origin has been considered, in view of fish names {{m|egy|hwn}}, {{m|egy|hwṯn}} and {{m|egy|ḥmt}},<ref name="ELA"/> without any conclusion.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|حُوت|m|pl=حِيتَان|pl2=أَحْوَات}}

# [[fish]]
#: {{syn|ar|سَمَك}}
#* {{R:ar:Lévi-Provençal:1934|page=235 (٤٣) 4}}
#* {{quote-book|year=1154|ar|author={{w|al-Idrisi|al-ʾIdrīsīy}}|title=ar:نزهة المشتاق في اختراق الآفاق|section=[[wikisource:ar:نزهة المشتاق في اختراق الآفاق/الإقليم الثالث/الجزء الثاني|{{lang|ar|الإقليم الأول - الجزء الثاني}}]]|passage=وهذه البحيرة من أعاجيب الدنيا وذلك أن بها اثني عشر نوعاً من السمك يوجد منها في كل شهر نوع واحد لا يمتزج بغيره من أصناف السمك فإذا تم الشهر لم يوجد شيء من ذلك النوع في الشهر الآتي ثم يوجد في الشهر الآتي صنف من السمك آخر غير الصنف الأول لا يمتزج بغيره هكذا لكل شهر نوع من السمك لا يمتزج بسمك غيره إلى كمال السنة هكذا في كل عام وهذه الاثنا عشر نوع من ال'''حوت''' التي ذكرناها هي البوري والقاجوج والمحل والطلنط والاشبلينيات والشلبة والقاروض واللاج والجوجة والكحلاء والطنفلو والقلا.|t=This lake is one of the wonders of the world, for it has twelve species of fish, each month one is found therein, not mixing with any other species than itself, and when the month ends, nothing of that fish is found in the coming month, then in the coming month an other kind of fish is encountered, different from the first kind and not mixing with anything other than itself, thus every month a species of fish that does not mix with other fish, up to completion of a year and so every year, and these twelve species of '''fish''' that we have related are [a list of fish follows, some of which are unidentifiable].}}
# [[whale]]
# {{lb|ar|normally with the definite article}} [[Pisces]]

