Page 8017 حي العالم: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Joubarbe d'Auvergne.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|حي العالم}} – {{taxfmt|Sempervivum tectorum|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
{{calque|ar|arc|חַיָּיא לְעָלְמָא|tr=ḥayyā lə-ʿāləmā|lit=living thing of eternity, something living for the world}}, itself together with {{cog|he|חַי הָעוֹלָם|tr=ḥay hā-ʿōlā́m}}, {{m|he|חַי לְעוֹלָם|tr=ḥay lə-ʿōlā́m}} a calque of {{der|ar|grc|ἀείζωον|t=houseleek|lit=always-living}}. Thus the meaning of perenniality got lost from Greek through Aramaic to Arabic since in Aramaic {{m|arc|עָלְמָא|tr=ʿāləmā}} means “eternity” and “world”, chosen to render Greek {{m|grc|ἀεί|t=ever}}, but the Arabic {{m|ar|عَالَم}} merely “world”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|حَيّ الْعَالَم}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|[[حَيّ]] [[الْ]][[عَالَم]]|m}}

# [[houseleek]] ({{taxfmt|Sempervivum|genus}}), [[stonecrop]] ({{taxfmt|Sedum|genus}} spp., {{taxlink|Hylotelephium|genus}} spp.), [[perennial]] [[flowering]] [[succulent]]s of the {{taxfmt|Sedoideae|subfamily}} subfamily about the taxonomy of which there is no consensus yet

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|حَيّ|mod=عَالَم|idafa=def}}

{{C|ar|Saxifragales order plants}}
-------- end text --------
