Page 8052 خ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Derived from {{m|ar|ح}}, and originally written as such (in {{m|en|rasm}}) by analogy with [[Nabatean]] tradition, as Nabatean cognates of Arabic words with /x/ were indiscriminately spelled using {{m|arc|𐢊|tr=ḥ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/xaːʔ/|/χaːʔ/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/x/|/χ/}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''خ '''/''' خ‍ '''/''' ‍خ‍ '''/''' ‍خ'''|tr=ḵāʔ}}

# The seventh letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. Its name is {{l|ar|خَاء}}, and is preceded by {{l|ar|ح}} and followed by {{l|ar|د}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''خ '''/''' خ‍ '''/''' ‍خ‍ '''/''' ‍خ'''|tr=ḵāʔ}}

# The twenty-fourth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ث}} and followed by {{l|ar|ذ}}.

===See also===
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/خ|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|خ}}]]

===References===
* {{R:ar:Diem-Orthographie|part=2|page=74}}

[[Category:Abjad numerals|3-600]]

