Page 8117 خاتم: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|خَاتَام|خَيْتَام|خَاتِيَام}}

===Etymology===
Of uncertain chain of etymology; once thought to be a borrowing from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, but deemed unlikely as had the word been borrowed from {{cog|hbo|חוֹתָם|tr=ḥōtām}} or {{cog|arc|חוֹתָמָא|tr=ḥōtāmā}} / {{m|syc|ܚܵܘܬܵܡܵܐ|tr=ḥāwtāmā|t=seal}}, it would probably have started with a /ḥ/, unless the Arabic has been borrowed from it in the incipient 1st millennium BC or earlier when Aramaic still distinguished the sounds; the initial /ḫ/ in {{noncog|ar|-}} word suggests therefore that it is derived from the same source as the latter. Ultimately suspected to be from or related to {{der|ar|egy|ḫtm|t=seal}}, however not being attested in {{noncog|akk|-}} or {{noncog|uga|-}}. The root {{ar-root|خ|ت|م}} “related to finishing, sealing” would then be derived from this borrowing; the like in every Semitic language.

Alternatively, there is a hypothetical reconstruction as {{der|ar|afa-pro|*qatam-|t=ring, signet}}, being the source of both the {{cog|sem-pro|*ḫatm-}} and {{cog|egy|ḫtm}}, as well as {{cog|mkf|katam|t=ring}} potentially a separate {{cog|cdc-wst|}} development. Compare also {{m|ar|طَابَع|t=seal, stamp}}, representing either an {{der|ar|akk|ṭepûm|𒋰|tr=ṭepûm|pos=to imprint or impress}} or an {{der|ar|egy|ḏbꜥwt|t=signet, seal}} equivalent and for more on the foreign pattern {{m|ar||فَاعَل}} see {{m|ar|عَالَم}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خَاتَم|خَاتِم}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-خاتم.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|خَاتَم|head2=خَاتِم|m|pl=خَوَاتِم}}

# [[signet]], [[seal ring]]
# [[ring]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَاتَم|pl=خَوَاتِم}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|ħatem}}
* {{desc|ary|خاتم|tr=ḵātim}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=252}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel-V|page=17}}
* {{R:ar:Jeffery-Foreign|pages=120–121}}
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|pages=267–268}}
* {{R:myz:Nöldeke|page=112}}

{{C|ar|Jewelry}}

