|passage=قَالُوا يَا أَبَانَا ٱسْتَغْفِرْ لَنَا ذُنُوبَنَا إِنَّا كُنَّا خَاطِئِينَ}}

====Usage notes====
* In standard Arabic, one would expect to find {{m|ar|خُطَّاء}} as a masculine broken plural, using the pattern {{lang|ar|فُعَّال}} (''fuʔʔāl'') also found, for example, in {{m|ar|كُتَّاب}}, {{m|ar|قُرَّاء}}, etc. The form {{m|ar|خُطَاة}} is a [[colloquialism]]<ref>{{R:ar:Wehr-4}}</ref> derived from the participle's colloquial form {{m|ar|خَاطِي}} using a pattern normally reserved for ''final-weak'' verbs (e.g. {{m|ar|قَضَى|pos=final-weak verb}} → {{m|ar|قَاضٍ|pos=active participle}} [informally {{m|ar|قَاضِي}}] → {{m|ar|قُضَاة|pos=masculine broken plural}}).

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|خَاطِئ|pl=خَاطِئُونَ|fpl=خَاطِئَات|fpl2=خَوَاطِئ}}

