====Further reading====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|خ ط ء}}

Kazimirski and Lane considered this word to be an alternative (irregular) verbal noun of the verb {{m|ar|أَخْطَأَ}}. Quoting Penrice's definition of {{m|ar|أَخْطَأَ}}: {{blockquote|{{lang|ar|خَاطِئَةٌ}} said to be a v.a. Habitual sinfulness; or it may be regarded as the fem. of {{lang|ar|خَاطِئٌ}} and agree with {{lang|ar|ٱلأَفْعَالِ}} understood, as at 69, v. 9. ''Note'': the {{lang|ar|ة}} is not unfrequently added to nouns to give intensity; [...].<ref>{{R:ar:Penrice|page=43}}</ref>}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|خَاطِئَة|f|pl=خَاطِئَات}}

# [[sin]], [[sinfulness]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|69|9|passage=وَجَاءَ فِرْعَوْنُ وَمَنْ قَبْلَهُ وَٱلْمُؤْتَفِكَاتُ '''بِٱلْخَاطِئَةِ'''}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَاطِئَةٌ|pl=sfp}}

====References====
<references/>

====Further reading====
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski}}
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:ar:Penrice}}
