Page 8184 خبز: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Often suspected a loan, presuming an [[Aksumite]] or {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}} predecessor of the {{bor|ar|gez|ኅብስት|tr=ḫəbəst|pos=formally feminine passive participle with assimilation of the last radical to the feminine suffix}}, the formations within the root {{ar-root|خ|ب|ز}} having been secondarily derived from the “loaf of bread” singulative noun {{m|ar|خُبْزَة}}. Maybe instead both hail via an {{bor|ar|arc-old|-}} term from {{der|ar|oge|ჴუეზაჲ|t=loaf of bread}}, {{cog|ka|ხვეზა}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|to bake}} {{ar-IPA|خَبَزَ}}
* {{sense|bread}} {{ar-IPA|خُبْز}}
* {{sense|baking}} {{ar-IPA|خَبْز}}

