Page 8241 خرج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
From the root {{ar-root|خ|ر|ج}}, ultimately from {{bor|ar|ira|-}}; see {{m|ar|خَرَاج|t=poll-tax}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|خَرَجَ}}
** {{a|ar|Egyptian}} {{ar-IPA|tr=ḵarag}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.ipass?.vn:خُرُوج}} {{tlb|ar|intransitive}}

# to [[move]] {{+obj|ar|:مِنْ<from inside>}} (somewhere) to [[outside]]; to [[leave]]; to [[exit]]; to [[get out]]
#: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجْتُ مَعَهَا|t=I went out with her.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجَ مِنَ الْبَيْتِ|t=He left the house.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|سِفْرُ الْخُرُوج|t=The Book of Exodus}}
# to [[go]] or [[come]] {{+obj|ar|:مِنْ<out of>}} somewhere [[physical]]ly or otherwise (depending on whether the view is from inside or outside); to [[go out]] or [[come out]]
#: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجَ مِنَ الْبَوَّابَة|t=He went out/came out through the gate.}}
## to [[go forth]] or [[come forth]]; to [[issue]]; to [[emerge]]
##: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجَ مِنَ الْيَنْبُوعِ مَاءٌ كَثِير|t=There gushed forth from the spring plenty of water.}}
##: {{uxi|ar|خُرُوجُ يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوج|t=the issuing of Gog and Magog}}
# to [[get]] {{+obj|ar|:مِنْ<out of an unwelcome or undesirable situation, a problem, and so on>}}
#: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجَ مِنَ الْمُشْكِلَةِ|t=He got out of the problem.}}
# to [[deviate]] {{+obj|ar|:عَنْ<from>}}
#: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجَ الْقِطَارُ عَنِ الْخَطِّ|t=The train ran off the rails.}}
## to [[depart]] or [[drift]] away {{+obj|ar|:عَنْ<from conventionality, orthodoxy, a religion, and so on>}}
##: {{syn|ar|خَالَفَ|شَذَّ|t=to differ; to dissent|t2=to diverge ideologically from or clash with some notional consensus}}
##: {{hypo|ar|اِرْتَدَّ|t=to switch back to a previous religion; to backslide; to leave Islam}}
# to [[march]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<against>}}, to [[take up arms]] against, to [[fight]] or [[rebel]] against
#: {{uxi|ar|خَرَجَ عَلَى الْحَاكِمِ|t=He took to open rebellion against the sovereign.}}
#: {{hyper|ar|عَصَى|t=to disobey}}
#: {{syn|ar|ثَارَ|تَمَرَّدَ|t1=to revolt|t2=to rebel}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.ipass?.vn:خُرُوج}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mt|ħareġ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}} {{tlb|ar|transitive}}

# to [[make]] [[go out]] or [[come out]] (depending on whether the view is from inside or outside)
## to [[make]] [[leave]]; to [[push out]]; to [[turn out]]; to [[force out]]
##: {{usex|ar|خَرَّجَهُ مِنْ بَيْتِهِ مُرْغَماً|t=He forcibly turned him out of his home.}}
##: {{syn|ar|طَرَدَ|t=to expel; to drive out}}
# to [[draw out]] or [[extract]] the [[essence]] or [[meaning]] of; to [[explicate]]; to [[distill]]; to [[decompose]]
# {{lb|ar|Islam}} to [[extract]] the [[chains]] of [[narrator]]s of (a tradition)
# to [[train]]
#: {{hyper|ar|عَلَّمَ|t=to instruct}}
#: {{syn|ar|دَرَّبَ}}
#: {{cot|ar|تَخَرَّجَ|t=to be trained or educated; to graduate}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

===Etymology 1.2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|خَرْج}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|خَرْج|m}}

# [[expenditure]], [[outlay]], [[expense]], [[costs]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَرْج}}

