Page 8252 خرطال: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Cadolzburg Burggarten - Hafer 2.jpg|thumb|right|360px|{{lang|ar|خَرْطَال}}]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|خَرْطَل}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*kert-}}
From the root {{ar-root|ق|ر|ط|ل}} meaning “a packsaddle”, “a basket or bag intended for provisions”, from {{der|ar|arc|קרטל|tr=qarṭāl|t=basket}} (Christian spelling {{m|syc|ܩܪܛܠܐ}}), which could be:
* from {{der|ar|hit|𒄑𒆳𒋫𒀀𒀠|tr=kurtal-, kartal-}}
* borrowed from {{der|ar|grc|κάρταλος}}, {{m|grc|κάρταλλος}} which is
** either from {{der|ar|grc|κυρτία||anything made of wicker}}; for more see {{der|ar|ine-pro|*kert-}}, found in {{cog|sa|कृणत्ति|tr=kṛṇátti|t=to twist thread, to spin}}, {{cog|sa|चृटति|tr=cṛṭáti|t=to bind, to fasten together}}, {{cog|la|crātis||wattle fence, corral}}, {{cog|en|hurdle}}.
** or borrowed from {{der|ar|arc|-}}, from {{der|ar|hit|-}}, in which case the {{der|ar|arc|-}} is not from {{der|ar|grc|-}}
* derived from {{der|ar|pal|glyw'|tr=grīw|t=a measure of grain, a peck}} + {{m|pal|-dʾl|tr=dār|t=holder, keeper, container of}}.
This must also be the name for “more than one of the highly succulent salt marsh [[chenopod]]s that are considered poor grazing for camels” like {{taxlink|Bienertia cycloptera|species}} and {{taxlink|Suaeda aegyptiaca|species}} Mandaville records from various Najdi tribes as {{m|ars|هَرْطَلَّس|tr=harṭallas}}, {{m|ars|هَطَلَّس|tr=hatạllas}}, {{m|ars|هَرْطَبِيل|tr=harṭabīl}}, {{m|ars|هُرْطُمَان|tr=hurṭumān}}, {{m|ars|طَرْطَيع|tr=ṭartēʕ}}, {{m|ars|هَطْلَس|tr=haṭlas}} but curiously describes as seemingly involving a quinqueliteral root.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خَرْطَال}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|خَرْطَال|m}}

# [[oat]] {{qualifier|{{taxfmt|Avena|genus}} gen. et spp.}}
#: {{syn|ar|شُوفَان}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَرْطَال}}

