Page 8370 خطمي: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|ختمية (نبات)|Althea|mul=خطمي|mullabel=Hibiscus}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|خِتْمِيّ|خَتْمِيّ}}

===Etymology===
Preparations from the marshmallow have been used for preparations to wash the head, so it appears to be {{ar-etym-noun-nisba|خَطْم|the nose and the mouth, snout|lc=1}}, though such a use of nisba is not common and it does not explain the variation  with {{m|ar|ت}} instead of {{m|ar|ط}}; maybe originally from {{bor|ar|arc|חלמיתא}} / {{m|syc|ܚܠܡܝܬܐ|tr=ḥlamītā}} / {{m|syc|ܚܠܡܬܐ|tr=ḥlamtā|t=[[alkanet]], {{taxlink|Anchusa officinalis|species}}}} with which there have been mutual mistranslations. Clearly now {{cog|he|חֶלְמִית|tr=ḥelmī́ṯ}} is used for [[mallow]]s, the {{taxfmt|Malva|genus}} genus and species.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خِطْمِيّ|خَطْمِيّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|خِطْمِيّ|head2=خَطْمِيّ|m|sing=خِطْمِيَّة|sing2=خَطْمِيَّة}}

# [[marshmallow]], {{taxfmt|Althaea|genus}} gen. et spp.
# the [[confectionery]] [[marshmallow]]
# [[rosemallow]], {{taxfmt|Hibiscus|genus}} gen. et spp.
#: {{syn|ar|كَرْكَدِيه}}
# [[hollyhock]], {{taxlink|Alcea|genus}} gen. et spp.
#: {{syn|ar|سِرَاج القُطْرُب}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|خِطْمِيّ|head2=خَطْمِيّ}}

