Page 8373 خطيئة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Belongs to the root {{ar-root|خ ط ء}}, from which the {{ar-form|I|verb form}} {{m|ar|خَطِئَ|gloss=to [[err]]}}. Schwally proposed that this concrete noun – and {{cog|gez|ኀጢአት|t=sin}} – is borrowed  from {{bor|ar|syc|ܚܛܝܬܐ|tr=ḥəṭīṯɑ, ḥəṭʾīṯɑ|t=sin}}. This seems likely as there must be in Geʿez a borrowing because the root there means “to lack, to be in want”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خَطِيئَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|خَطِيئَة|f|pl=خَطِيئَات|pl2=خَطَايَا}}

# {{lb|ar|countable}} [[sin]], [[offense]], [[fault]], act of [[disobedience]] for which one deserves [[punishment]]
# {{lb|ar|uncountable|especially|Christianity}} [[sin]] as a continuing [[state]]
#: {{ux|ar|يَعِيشُ فِي الخَطِيئة.|He’s living in '''sin'''.|inline=1}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَطِيئَة|pl=خَطِيئَات|pl2=خَطَايَا}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|خَطِيَّة}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|خَطِيئَة أَصْلِيَّة|tr=ḵaṭīʔa ʔaṣliyya|t=[[original sin]]}}

===References===
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|page=268}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=36}}
* {{R:ar:Schwally-Lex.|part=1|page=132}}

