# {{ar-verbal noun of|خَفَرَ|form=I|t=to watch, to protect}}: [[watch]]ing, [[guard]]ing

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَفْر}}

===Etymology 1.3===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|خَفَر|m}}

# [[guard]] [[detachment]], [[escort]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَفَر}}

===Etymology 2.1===
{{ar-rootbox|خ ف ر}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ḫapar-}}. Compare {{cog|hbo|חָפֵר|tr=ḥɔp̄er|t=to be ashamed}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|خَفِرَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.vn:خَفَر,خَفَارَة.ap:خَفِر,++,مِخْفَار}}<!-- these active participles look strange but Almaany specifically indicates them -->

# to be [[shy]]

=====Usage notes=====
* Most authorities assert that this verb is only used in relation to a woman, and it seems to be seldom, if ever, otherwise used.

=====Conjugation=====
