Page 8424 خلر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Also found with metathesis in {{cog|tmr|חורלא}} and {{cog|syc|ܚܘܪܠܐ|tr=ḥūrəlā|t=a kind of {{taxfmt|Lathyrus|genus}}}}, and {{cog|he|חרול|חָרֻל|tr=ḥārūl}}. Perhaps retaining the older order from {{der|ar|arc-imp|𐡇𐡋𐡅𐡓|ts=ḥallūr|lit=bean|t=1/40th of a shekel}}, used by the [[w:Achaemenid|Achaemenid]]s as its smallest monetary measure. From {{der|ar|akk|𒄬𒇻𒊒|ts=ḫal-lu-ru|tr=ḫallūru, ḫallāru, ḫillūru, ḫullūru|t=chickpea; 1/10 shekel}}, itself less likely to be of Semitic origin as the close pairing of {{IPAchar|/l/}} and {{IPAchar|/r/}} is not typical. Suggested ultimate {{der|ar|xhu|-|}} origin, possibly by way of {{der|ar|uga|𒄷𒌌𒇻𒊒|tr=ḫu-ul-lu-ru}}, which is attested only in syllabic form. Compare {{noncog|akk|𒄒|ts=šallūru|t=plum}}, another {{noncog|xhu|-}} loan into the Semitic family with the same pattern. Likely cognate also with {{cog|grc|ὄλῡρᾰ|t=type of harvest or grain; spelt, rice-wheat}} and with {{cog|xcl|ոլոռն|tr=|t=pea}}, dialectal {{cog|hy||քըլուր|t=a kind of corn resembling oats}}, {{m|hy||խըլօր|t=millet-sized hail; a kind of millet-sized useless grain}}, which may be derived from the same origin as the {{noncog|akk|-}} through an {{noncog|xur|-}} intermediary.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خُلَّر}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|خُلَّر|m}} {{tlb|ar|uncountable|obsolete}}

# a not further identifiable {{taxfmt|Fabeae|tribe}} tribe [[legume]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{w|Ibn Qutaybah|Ibn Quṭayba ad-Dīnawarīy}}|editor=ar:عَبْد اللّٰه الجبوري|title=ar:كتاب غريب الحديث|publisher=ar:مَطْبَعَة الْعَانِي|location=Baghdad, Iraq|year=a. 889|url=https://shamela.ws/book/7012/39#p5|edition=1st|year_published=1977|volume=1|page=185–186|passage=وَرَأى قوم على القطنية وَهِي الْحُبُوب مثل العدس والحمص والأرز والجلبان وَهُوَ '''الخلر''' والفول وَهُوَ الباقلاء وَهُوَ الجرجر أَيْضا وَأَحْسبهُ معربا والترمس وَهُوَ الجرجر الرُّومِي والدخن وَهن الجاورس واللوبياء والذرة وَأَشْبَاه ذَلِك مِمَّا يبْقى فِي أَيدي النَّاس لِلزَّكَاةِ لِأَنَّهَا حب.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|خُلَّر}}

