Page 8499 خنوص: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Piglets in Cyprus.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|خنوصان}}]]

===Etymology===
Ultimately derived from {{inh|ar|afa-pro||*ḫunʒ(-ir)-|t=pig, boar, porcupine; calf, piglet}} from whence {{cog|ar|خِنْزِير|tr=|t=pig, swine}} and {{cog|ar|خُنْس|t=gazelles, wild cows}} is also derived; inherited natively or semantically reinforced from a {{bor|ar|ber|-}} borrowing as also parallely passed into {{cog|mt|gendus}}, compare the related {{cog|kab|ⴰⴳⴻⵏⴷⵓⵣ|tr=agenduz|t=calf, young animal|sc=Tfng}}, though such a form is in Semitic only found in {{cog|syc|ܚܰܢܽܘܨܳܐ|t=piglet|tr=ḥannūṣā}} and {{cog|uga||sc=Xsux|tr=ḫe-en-ni-ṣu|ts=ḫinnīṣu, ḫannīṣu|t=piglet}}, which combined with the predominating presence of the Arabic word in the Levant and the otherwise absence of the measure save for borrowings suggests an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} substrate.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|خِنَّوْص|m|pl=خَنَانِيص|head2=خَنُّوص}}

# [[piglet]], [[young]] of a [[swine]]
# the [[young]] or [[little]] of anything

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|خِنَّوْص|pl=خَنَانِيص|head2=خَنُّوص}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|ħannus}}
* {{desc|apc|خَنُّوص|tr=ḵannūṣ}}
* {{desc|ajp|خَنُّوص|tr=ḵannūṣ}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|xnwc|N}}
* {{R:ar:BehnstedtWoidich|WA1|page=398}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=11}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=1|pages=531–532}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=2|page=149}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|pages=816–817}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=366}}

