Page 8541 خيزران: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Bambou, Parc Rochegude Albi.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|خَيْزُرَان}}]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Originally attested in Pre-Islamic poetry, like that of [[w:Al-Nabigha|an-Nābighah]] (c.535–c.604), as being abundant in the land of the [[w:Byzantine_Empire|Byzantines]]. Although of uncertain identification, it was a kind of plant with pliable twigs or roots that were deemed desirable for spear-making, later being applied to bamboo. Compare {{cog|he|חָזַר|tr=chazár|t=to return, to bounce back}}, {{cog|akk|𒄑𒋗𒌨|tr=ḫinzūru|t=apple tree, apricot tree}}, {{cog|uga|𐎈𐎏𐎗|t=apple tree}}, {{cog|akk|𒆹|tr=ḫazru|t=flooded area, swamp, reed marsh}}; perhaps ultimately derived from {{der|ar|sux|𒄑|tr=gidru|t=scepter, cane}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خَيْزُرَان}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|خَيْزُرَان|m|pl=خَيَازِر|sing=خَيْزُرَانَة|pauc=خَيْزُرَانَات}}

# [[bamboo]], [[rattan]]
# [[reed]], [[cane]]
# [[spear]], [[shaft]]
# any [[limber]] or [[pliable]] [[stick]]
# [[scepter]], a [[pointer]]
# [[oar]], a [[pole]] used to [[propel]] a [[boat]]
# [[rudder]], [[till]], [[tiller]], [[helm]] of a [[ship]]
# {{lb|ar|music}} [[reed]], [[pipes]]
# {{lb|ar|figurative}} a [[beautiful]] [[woman]]; comparably [[slender]] and [[supple]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|خَيْزُرَان|m|pl=خَيَازِر}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ca|bor=1|galzeran}}
* {{desc|ota|bor=1|هزارن}}
** {{desc|tr|bor=1|hezaren}}

