Page 8548 خيمة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Frequently thought to be a foreign word, in Jeffery’s words even “obviously not Arabic”. In this case most likely borrowed from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, from which source also {{cog|gez|ኀይመት}}, {{cog|tig|ሓይመት}}, {{cog|am|ሃይመት}}. This could be countered with {{cog|uga|𐎃𐎎𐎚|t=tent}} (attested multiple times), {{cog|uga|𐎃𐎎𐎐|t=chapel, small temple}}, {{cog|arc-imp|𐡇𐡌𐡍|t=altar, chapel|tr=ḥmn}}, {{cog|he|חַמָּן|t=altar, chapel|tr=ḥammān}} – with a small probability related to {{cog|egy|ḫꜣwt|t=altar, altar chamber}} –, {{cog|uga|𐎃𐎊𐎎|t=canopy, baldachin}} – possibly related to {{cog|akk|𒌆𒄩𒁍𒌝|tr=<sup>TUG<sub>2</sub></sup>.ḪA.BU.UM}}, {{m|akk|𒌆𒄩𒌝|tr=<sup>TUG<sub>2</sub></sup>.ḪA.UM|ts=ḫaʾum, ḫawum|t=a kind of covering cloth}}.

Compare also {{cog|kab|taxxamt}}, {{m|kab|taxyamt}}, {{m|kab|axxam}}, {{m|kab|axyam}}, this and equivalent words in other {{cog|ber|-}} languages meaning “tent” foremostly, and “cabin, chamber, room”, reconstructed for {{cog|ber-pro|-}} rather than deemed borrowed from Arabic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|خَيْمَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|خَيْمَة|f|pl=خِيَام|pl2=خِيَم}}

# [[tent]]
# [[tarpaulin]]
# [[arbor]], [[bower]]
# [[pavilion]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|خَيْمَة|pl=خِيَام|pl2=خِيَم}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|خَامَ|t=to draw back, to hold back}}
* {{l|ar|خَيَّمَ|t=to pitch one’s tent}}
** {{l|ar|مُخَيَّم|t=encampment}}
* {{l|ar|أَخَامَ|t=to construct a tent}}
* {{l|ar|تَخَيَّمَ|t=to pitch one’s tent}}

====Descendants====
