Page 8558 د ر ب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Possibly this is not even a genuine root but the meanings of “to drill”, “to train” have developed from {{m|ar|دَرْب|t=path}} from {{der|ar|grc|Δέρβη|t=[[Derbe]]}}, a border town in [[Lycaonia]] at the {{w|Cilician Gates}}, since [[Derbe]] was a town to be passed for those who were drilled for war against the Greeks. The same even applies to Spain, the [[Pyrenees]] being called {{m|ar||الدُرُوب}}, to be passed for war against the Franks.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

