Page 8577 د م س: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Compared by ''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' to the root {{ar-root|د م ث|nocat=1}} related to suavity, to {{cog|akk|𒁕𒈠𒋳|tr=da-ma-šum|ts=damāšu|t=to cover, to wipe or efface}} and to {{cog|gez|ደመሰ|t=to efface, to destroy}}, at which are also listed {{m|gez|ደመሰ|tr=dämmäsä|t=to bury, to cover, to hide}}, {{m|gez|ድሙስ}}, {{m|gez|ደሙስ|t=dark, clouded}}. Compare {{ar-root|د م ج|nocat=1}} and {{ar-root|د ب س|nocat=1}} and {{ar-root|د ه م|nocat=1}}, also of darker colour meanings. There is some interference from {{m|ar|دَيْمَاس|t=dungeon; mattamore; latibulum}}, compare the development of denominal verbs from {{m|ar|مَطْمُورَة|t=underground grain cubbyhole}} and {{m|ar|نَامُوس}}.

