Page 8584 د و س: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Likely related to {{ar-root|د ع س|nocat=1}} and {{ar-root|د ه س|nocat=1}}, either derived from them with compensatory lengthening, or they are formed from this root by inserting radicals. On the other hand, there's also {{l|ar|دَهَكَ|t=to [[crush]], to [[trample]]}}, but it's likely derived from supposedly unrelated {{l|ar|دَكَّ}} or {{l|ar|دَقَّ}} with the same ''h''-insertion.

The root {{ar-root|د ر س|nocat=1}} of {{l|ar|دَرَسَ|t=to [[thresh]], to [[flail]]}} is also related, compare {{l|ar|سَابَ|t=to [[flow]]}} and {{l|ar|سَرَبَ|t=to [[leak]]}} for derivation pattern. The verbal nouns of {{l|ar|دَرَسَ}} even share the same models with those of {{l|ar|دَاسَ}}, and there are doublets like {{l|ar|مِدرَس|t=[[flail]]}} and {{l|ar|مِدْوَس}}.

Compare {{cog|he|דָּשׁ|tr=dash|t=to [[thresh]]}}, {{cog|he|דִּשְׁדֵּשׁ|tr=dishdesh|t=to [[tread]], to [[trample]]}}, {{cog|he|דייסה|דַּיְסָה|tr=daysah|t=[[porridge]]}}, {{cog|he|דָּרַס|tr=daras|t=to [[step on]], to [[trample]]}}.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

