Page 8610 دار: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|د ر ر}}
{{ar-active participle}} of the verb {{m|ar|دَرَّ||to [[flow]] copiously}}.

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-sound|دَارّ}}

# [[flowing]] copiously
# [[productive]], [[rich]], [[lucrative]]
# [[profitable]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|دَارّ|pl=smp}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|د و ر}}
The noun originally referred to the buildings surrounding a court. Cognate with {{cog|akk|dūrum|alt=𒂦|tr=dūrum|t=city wall}} and {{cog|hbo|דּוּר|tr=dûr|t=to move in a circle}}, {{m|hbo|דָּר|tr=dār|t=to dwell}} and {{m|hbo|דּוֹר|tr=dôr|t=habitation}}.

====Pronunciation 1====
{{ar-IPA|دَار}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.ipass?.vn:دَوْر,دَوَرَان}}

