===Etymology===
{{univerbation|ar|[[دَار]] [[فِلْفِل]]}}, {{m|ar|[[دَار]] [[ال]][[فِلْفِل]]|t=house of pepper}}, originally denoting “the whole house of pepper-like spices”. The similarity to {{noncog|fa|دار|tr=dâr|t=tree}} is coincidental, and in Persian, {{m|fa|دارفلفل|tr=dârfelfel}} is used less often than the Arabic, because of the existence of other words for this item in Persian, and the sometimes mentioned form {{m|fa||دارپلپل|tr=dârpelpel}} is rare.

