Page 8692 دبوس: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|دَبُّوز|دَبُّوسَة|دَبُّوزَة}}

===Etymology===
A pre-[[mameluke|Mamluk]] {{bor|ar|trk}} borrowing, from a cognate of {{cog|ota|طوپوز|tr={{m|tr|topuz}}|t=iron mace}}. The name of a pin may have additional connection to the root {{ar-root|د ب ب}} related to crawling, pushing in, compare also {{m|ar|دَرْبَسَ|t=to shut}}, and possibly, too, the name stuck owing to {{m|ar|دِبْس|t=molasses}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَبُّوس}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-دبوس.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَبُّوس|m|pl=دَبَابِيس}}

# {{C|ar|Fasteners}} [[pin]]
# {{lb|ar|before that}}{{C|ar|Fasteners}} [[peg]], [[plug]], [[rod]], [[cudgel]], any [[oblong]] [[instrument]] [[drive|driven]] into or onto [[something]]
# {{lb|ar|figurative}} [[penis]]
#: {{syn|ar|قَضِيب|ذَكَر|زُبّ|أَيْر|آلَة}}
# {{lb|ar|originally|now|_|historical}}{{C|ar|Weapons}} [[iron]] [[mace]]
# {{lb|ar|regional}} [[government]] [[informant]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَبُّوس|pl=دَبَابِيس}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|دَبَّاسَة|t=stapler}}
* {{l|ar|دَبَّسَ|pos=verb}}
* {{l|ar|دَبُّوسِيّ|pos=adjective}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ms|dabus|bor=1}}
** {{desc|id|debus}}

===References===
