Page 8700 دجال: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|د ج ل}}

===Etymology===
Belongs to {{ar-root|د ج ل}} now, with a verb {{m|ar|دَجَلَ|t=[[dupe]], [[cheat]], [[swindle]], [[deceive]]}}, but the early religious use suggests that these meanings are a {{semantic loan|ar|syc|ܕܰܓܳܠܳܐ|tr=daggālā|nocap=1|t=liar}}, also used for the False Messiah, whereas the Arabic root prominently means “smearing things over other things”, “coating”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَجَّال}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَجَّال|m|pl=دَجَّالُون|pl2=دَجَاجِلَة|f=دَجَّالَة}}

# someone who covers, coats things
## [[gilder]], [[silverer]]
# [[swindler]], [[cheat]], [[imposter]], [[charlatan]], [[mountebank]], [[liar]]
# {{lb|ar|Islam}} the [[False Messiah]]
#: {{syn|ar|ضِدّ المَسِيح|نَقِيض المَسِيح|q1=Christianity|q2=Christianity|t1=the Antichrist|t2=the Antichrist}}

