===Etymology 2.1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|דּוֹחַן|tr=doḥan|t=millet}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒌅𒄴𒉡|ts=duḫnu; tuḫnu|t=millet}}, ultimately from a variation of {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ṭaḥan-}}/{{m|sem-pro|*ṭaḥaḥ-|t=to grind, to pound, to crush, to break down into pieces; especially of corn}}, found in {{m|ar|طَحَّ|tr=|t=to scrape, to grate, to remove an outside surface, to make flakes or powder, to break down into pieces}}. {{doublet|ar|طَحَنَ|t1=to grind, to mill}} and cognate with {{cog|syc|ܕܽܘܚܢܴܐ|tr=duḥnā|t=millet}} and {{cog|he|דֹּחַן|tr=doḥan|t=millet}}. There is no direct connection to {{m+|ine-pro|*dʰoHnéh₂}} although a distant relation has been suggested.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|دُخْن}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|دُخْن|m}}

# [[pearl millet]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|دُخْن}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|axm|տուխն|bor=1}}

{{C|ar|Grains|Grasses|Smoking}}

