Page 8732 درب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|grc|Δέρβη|t=[[Derbe]]}}, a border town in [[Lycaonia]] at the {{w|Cilician Gates}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|دَرْب|m|pl=دُرُوب}}

# [[path]], [[pass]], [[way]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَرْب|pl=دُرُوب}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|دَرْب التَّبَّانَة|gloss=[[Milky Way]]}}
* {{l|ar|دَرَّاب|t=way guardian}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|syc|ܕܰܪܒܳܐ|tr=darbā|t=way, path|bor=1}}
* {{desc|osp|adarve|adarbe|bor=1}}
** {{desc|es|adarve}}

===Etymology 2===
From the root {{ar-root|د ر ب}}. Possibly these verbs are all denominally formed from {{m-self|ar|دَرْب}}, since [[Derbe]] was a town to be passed for those who were drilled for war against the Greeks. The same even applies to Spain, the [[Pyrenees]] being called {{m|ar||الدُرُوب}}, to be passed for war against the Franks.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.ipass?.vn:دَرَب,دُرْبَة}}

# to [[accustom]] oneself, become [[familiar]] with
# {{lb|ar|construed with {{m|ar|بِ}}}} to [[practice]] in
# to be [[badly]] off

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.ipass?.vn:دَرَب,دُرْبَة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|دَرَب|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|دَرِبَ|form=I||to [[accustom]] oneself, become [[familiar]], [[practice]] in}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَرَب}}

===Etymology 3===
Causative of {{m|ar|دَرِبَ||to [[accustom]] oneself, become [[familiar]], [[practice]] in}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{audio|ar|Ar-درب.ogg}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# to [[accustom]], to [[familiarize]]
# to [[exercise]], to [[drill]]
# to [[show]] oneself [[enduring]]
# to [[guide]], to [[direct]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|pages=428–430}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=19}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=684}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|pages=866–867}}
* {{R:ar:Vollers-Beitr.|part=III|page=296–297}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|page=318}}

[[Category:Arabic causative verbs]]
{{cln|ar|denominal verbs}}

