Page 8738 دربوكة: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Darbouka de Nefta.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|دَرْبُوكَة}}|upright=0.8]]
{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|دَرَبُكَّة|دِرْبَكَّة}}

===Etymology===
An {{der|ar|ira}} borrowing, found as {{cog|syc|ܐܪܕܒܐ|tr=ʾardbā}}, {{m|syc|ܐܪܕܒܩܐ|tr=ʾardbaqqā}}, {{m|syc|ܐܪܕܒܟܐ|tr=ʾardbakkā}}, {{m|syc|ܕܥܒܒܘܩܐ|tr=daʿbukkā}}, {{m|syc|ܕܥܒܘܟܐ|tr=darbukkā}}, {{cog|tmr|דבוכא|ts=*dabbukkā}}, maybe mediated via {{bor|ar|syc|ܕܥܒܘܟܐ|tr=darbukkā, darbūkā}} specifically and ultimately the same word as {{cog|fa|تنبک|دنبک|tr=donbak}} which is the same kind of drum.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَرْبُوكَة}}
** {{a|ar|Moroccan}} {{ary-IPA|darbūka}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَرْبُوكَة|f|pl=دَرْبُوكَات}}

# [[darbuka]], a [[goblet drum]] of the Arab world and Turkey; in Iran, called a {{m|fa|تنبک|تمبک|tr=tombak}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَرْبُوكَة|pl=دَرْبُوكَات}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ota|داربوقه|tr=darbuka|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|darbuka}}

