[[File:Malta - Siggiewi - Triq il-Buskett - Buskett Gardens - Fraxinus angustifolia fem 01 ies.jpg|thumb|right|upright=1.05|{{lang|ar|دَرْدَار}} – ''[[Fraxinus angustifolia]]'']]

===Etymology===
From {{der|ar|syc|ܕܕܪܐ|tr=daddārā|t=elm, oak}}, from {{der|ar|pal|𐫅𐫀𐫡|ts=dār|t=tree, gallows; wood}}, from {{der|ar|ira-pro|*dā́ru|t=tree}}; cognate with {{cog|fa|دردار|tr=dardâr|t=elm}}.

False cognate with {{noncog|akk|𒌑𒁕𒁕𒊒|ts=daddaru|t=a thorny plant, thistle; ill tasting or smelling plant}}, {{noncog|he|דַּרְדַר|tr=dardar|t=thistle}}, {{noncog|arc|דַּרְדָּרָא|tr=dardārā|t=thistle}}, {{noncog|syc|ܕܪܕܪܐ|tr=dardərā|t=thistle}}, {{noncog|ar|دَرْدَر|t=thistle}}, {{noncog|gez|ደንደር|t=thistle}}, {{noncog|am|ደንደር|t=thistle}}, which are ultimately from {{der|ar|sem-pro|*drr|t=to give difficulty, to be too hard to handle, to be uneasy or unpleasant, to be overwhelming}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَرْدَار|head2=دِرْدَار|m}}

# [[elm]] ({{taxfmt|Ulmus|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|[[شَجَر]] [[ال]][[بَقّ]]|بُوقِيصَا|نَشَم}}
# [[ash]] ({{taxfmt|Fraxinus|genus}} spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|مُرَّان}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَرْدَار|head2=دِرْدَار}}

===References===
* {{pedia|lang=ar}}
* {{R:CAL|ddr|N}}
* {{R:CAL|drdr|N}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=432}}
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|page=136}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=3|pages=417–419}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=2|page=286}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=1|pages=404–407}}
* {{cite-book|last=Neishtadt|first=Mila|chapter=The Lexical Component in the Aramaic Substrate of Palestinian Arabic|title=Semitic Languages in Contact|series=Studies in Semitic Languages and Linguistics|seriesvolume=82|editor=Aaron Michael Butts|pages=305–309|isbn=978-90-04-30014-9|publisher=Brill|location=Leiden, Boston|year=2015}}
* {{R:sem:Růžička:1909|page=8}}, confusing the “elm” and “thistle” families however

{{C|ar|Rosales order plants|Olive family plants}}

-------- end text --------
Page 8744 دردق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|דַּרְדַּק}} / {{m|syc|ܕܪܕܩܐ|tr=dardaqā|t=small; young|pos=adjective}}, originally {{m|arc|דַּקְדַּק}} / {{m|syc|ܕܿܩܕܩܐ|tr=daqdaqā}}, from the root cognate to Arabic {{ar-root|د ق ق|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَرْدَق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|دَرْدَق|sing=دَرْدَقَة|m|pl=دَرَادِق}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete|poetic}}

# [[offspring]], [[children]] (of man or camel)
#* {{quote-book|1=ar|year=a. 846|author={{w|Ibn al-A'rabi|Ibn al-ʾAʿrābī}}|url=https://al-hakawati.net/Books/BookDetails/9779/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AC%D8%B2%D8%A1-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB--%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%84%D9%8A%D9%84%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D9%84%D8%A7%D8%AB%D9%88%D9%86|title=''unnamed title''|passage=أَعْدَدْت للجارِ وللرَّفِيقِ، – والضَّيْفِ والصاحِبِ والصَّدِيقِ<br/> ولِلْعِيالِ ال'''دَّرْدقِ''' اللُّصُوقِ – حَمْراء مِنْ نَسْلِ أَبي مَرْزُوقِ<br/> تَمْسَحُ خَدَّ الحالِبِ الرَّفِيقِ، – بِلَبنِ المَسِّ قَلِيلِ الرِّيقِ<br/> كأن صوت شخبها الفـتـيق – فحيح ضبٍ حربٍ حـنـيق<br/>في جحرٍ ضاق أشد الضيق|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20210616043057/https://al-hakawati.net/Books/BookDetails/9779/%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AC%D8%B2%D8%A1-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB--%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%84%D9%8A%D9%84%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D8%A7%D9%86%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%88%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%AB%D9%84%D8%A7%D8%AB%D9%88%D9%86|archivedate=16 June 2021}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|دَرْدَق|pl=دَرَادِق}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|drdq|A}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=111}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=22a}}
* {{R:ar:Müller:1887|page=24}}
* {{R:myz:Nöldeke|page=185}}

-------- end text --------
Page 8745 دردي: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Apple wine lees.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|دُرْدِيّ}}|upright=1.35]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|[[דּוּרְדָּא]] / [[דֻּרְדָּא]]|tr=durdā}}, its plural {{m|arc|[[דּוּרְדֵּי]] / [[דֻּרְדֵּי]]|tr=durdī}}, an {{der|ar|ira}} loanword, represented by {{cog|fa|درد|tr=dord|t=dregs}}. For this ending in Aramaisms, compare {{m|ar|نُمِّيّ}}, {{m|ar|نُوتِيّ}}, {{m|ar|سَكِّيّ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دُرْدِيّ}}
* {{a|ar|Egypt}} {{ar-IPA|دِرْدِي}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دُرْدِيّ|m}}

# [[liquid]] [[sediment]], [[lees]], [[amurca]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|nasai|51|211
|passage=سَأَلْتُ إِبْرَاهِيمَ «إِنَّا نَأْخُذُ '''دُرْدِيَّ''' الْخَمْرِ أَوِ الطِّلَاءَ فَنُنَظِّفُهُ ثُمَّ نَنْقَعُ فِيهِ الزَّبِيبَ ثَلَاثًا ثُمَّ نُصَفِّيهِ ثُمَّ نَدَعُهُ حَتَّى يَبْلُغَ فَنَشْرَبُهُ» قَالَ «يُكْرَهُ».
|translation=I asked Ibrahim: “We take the '''lees''' of the wine or thick-wine and clean it, then soak it with raisins three days, then strain, then leave it until it has become ripe, and thus we drink it.” He said: “This is vile.”}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|21|1|volume=2|page=86|passage=وينميه ويحسن نباته إن يصب دردي الزيت على الماء الذي يسقى به أو يرش رشا على أصوله ثم يسقى بالماء بعد ذلك … وإن جعل فوق دردي الزيت من هذا الزبل الذي وصفنا كان أقوى للباقلى وأنمى.|translation=What adds to growth and beauty of the plants in particular is when amurca is added to the water used for watering them or sprinkling upon their stems, after this only using the water … and if over the amurca some of this sharn is put that we have described this adds to the strength and growth of the beans.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دُرْدِيّ}}

====See also====
* {{l|ar|كُسْبَة|t=oil cake}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|dwrd)|N}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=148}}
* {{R:arz:HindsBadawi|page=284}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=2|page=290}}
* {{R:arz:Spiro-arz-en|1|page=196}}
