Page 8750 درع: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|د ر ع}}. Compare {{cog|gez|ድርዕ|t=coat of mail, harness}}, {{cog|tig|ደርዕ}}, {{cog|ti|ድርዒ}}, {{cog|am|ዲር}}, {{m|am|ድር}}, {{cog|sqt|daraḥ|t=to put on (a garment)}}. Nöldeke thinks that the Arabic is borrowed from [[Ge'ez]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|Noun}} {{ar-IPA|دِرْع}}
* {{q|Verb}} {{ar-IPA|دَرَّعَ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دِرْع|m|g2=f|pl=دُرُوع|pl2=أَدْرُع}}

# {{lb|ar|uncountable}} [[protective]] [[coverings]]
## {{lb|ar|uncountable}} protective [[war]] [[equipment]], [[armor]]
##: {{hypo|ar|خُوذَة|تُرْس}}
## {{lb|ar|countable}} a [[body]] [[armor]]
## {{lb|ar|countable}} an armor [[plate]] held in hand, a [[shield]]
##: {{syn|ar|تُرْس|مِجَنّ}}
## {{lb|ar|countable}} something that [[resemble]]s or is [[use]]d like a shield (such as [[human shield]]s)
## {{lb|ar|countable|of animals}} a protective [[shell]] or [[covering]] (as of a [[tortoise]]), [[armature]]
# {{lb|ar|by extension}} a [[garment]] worn by women

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دِرْع|c|pl=دُرُوع|pl2=أَدْرُع}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to put [[armor]] on, to [[armor]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=23}}
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|page=141}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=53}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=387}}

{{C|ar|Armor}}

