===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|pal||tr=dstk'|ts=dastag|t=bunch, bundle; handle}}, via the Neo-Persian descendant of which {{m|fa|دسته|tr=daste}} later also Arabic {{doublet|ar|دَسْتَة|notext=1}} has been acquired.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَسْتَج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَسْتَج|m|pl=دَسَاتِج}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{lb|ar|rare}} [[fagot]], [[bundle]], [[bunch]], [[truss]]
#: {{syn|ar|حُزْمَة|رِزْمَة}}
#* {{RQ:Janah:2020|year=a. 929|section=270 (fol. 26r,5–13)|page=454|passage=قَالَ ٱلخُبْزَرُزِّيُّ:<br/>فَضِلْنِي بِ'''دَسْتَجَةٍ''' عَذْبَةٍ – فَإِنِّي إِلَيْهَا مَشُوقٌ مَشُوقٌ<br/>أَصِلْكَ بِ'''دَسْتَجَةٍ''' مِثْلَهَا – مِنَ ٱلْحَلِّ تَعْلُو وَلِلْحَلِّ شُوقٌ|subst=وَلِلْحَلِّ/وَ-لِ-لْ-حَلِّ,إِلَيْهَا/إِلَيْ-هَا,بِ'''دَسْتَجَةٍ'''/بِ-'''دَسْتَجَةٍ'''|t={{w|الخبز أرزي|lang=ar|Al-Ḵubzaruzzīy}} said:<br/>Distinguish me by a dulcet '''fagot''' … by reason that to it my yearn is roused!<br/>I send you thereon an equal '''fagot''' … its unbox, like for many, puts you risen!}}
# {{lb|ar|rare}} [[handle]], [[grip]], [[helve]]
#: {{syn|ar|نِصَاب|يَد}}
# [[pestle]], [[mortar]]’s [[grip]], [[beater]]
#: {{syn|ar|مِدَقّ|يَد}}
#* {{RQ:Ibn Tilmidh:2007|page=139 Nr. 302|passage=ويحرك ب'''دستج''' الهاون نعما ويصفى في منخل ويرمى بالثفل ثم تعاود عليه التصفية […]|t=(now) stir it gently with a '''pestle''', strain it into a sieve, and throw away the sediment (that has gathered upon it); then clear it again […]}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|28|13|volume=2|page=316|passage=له ساق طويل نحو شبر شكله شكل '''دستج''' الهاون لونه إلى الفرفرية وعليه ثمر لونه لون زعفران وله أصل متوسط القدر.|translation=It [the type of dragonwort] has a leg as long as a hand’s span and is in form like a '''pestle''', its colour nears purple, its fruits have the colour of saffron, its stem is of medium size.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دَسْتَج|pl=دَسَاتِج}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Almaany}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=441b}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=29a}}

