===Etymology 4===
Suggested by Hommel as inherited from a {{inh|ar|sem-pro||*dimm-|t=wild cat}}, but presumably borrowed from {{bor|ar|gez|ድመት|tr=dəmmat}}, because this is a {{m|de|Lockwort}} rare in literary Arabic and appears in the dialects only in northwest Yemen, whereas it overspreads all {{cog|sem-eth}} as the word for the cat; the compared {{noncog|akk|𒁺𒈠𒈬|tr=du-ma-mu|ts=dumāmu, tumāmu|t=leopard}} is considered probably a foreign borrowing.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|دِمّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|دِمّ|m|f=دِمّة|pl=دِمَم}} {{tlb|ar|now|only|_|Yemen}}

# [[cat]]; [[wild cat]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|دِمّ|pl=دِمَم}}

