Page 8869 دماغ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{blend|ar|دَم|t1=blood|مُخّ|t2=brain}}, compare {{cog|ar|دَمْع|t=tears}} of the same relation with {{m|ar|عَيْن|t=eye}}. While {{m|ar|دَمْع|t=tears}} traces its formation back to [[Proto-Semitic]], the present term is only parallelled by {{cog|sem-eth|-}}, {{cog|gez|ድማሕ}}, {{m|gez|ድማኅ}}, {{m|gez|ድማህ|t=head; crown of the head; skull; summit}}, {{cog|am|ድማኅ|t=top of the head}}, {{cog|agj|ድማኅ|t=head}}, {{cog|gft|dəmʷä|t=head}}, {{cog|stv|ዱም|tr=dum}}, {{cog|wle|ዱሚ|tr=dumi|t=head; hair of head}}, {{cog|tig|ደምቀት|t=crown of the head}}, apparently back-formed from later plurals {{m|tig|ድማቅ}}, {{m|tig|ድመቅ}}, with presumable {{w|Gurage languages|Gurage}} borrowings {{cog|awn|ዱሚ|tr=dūmī|t=top}}, {{cog|om|dumi|t=head}}. While borrowing of at least a part of the terms is manifest, the preservation  of guttural fricatives unassimilated in voicedness to the second radical against Arabic points to either inheritance from {{inh|ar|sem-wes-pro|-}} or borrowing from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}} whose names of body parts use to be poorly attested.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دِمَاغ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-دماغ.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دِمَاغ|m|pl=أَدْمِغَة|pl2=دُمُغٌ}} {{tlb|ar|countable}}

# {{lb|ar|anatomy}} [[brain]] {{gl|control center of the central nervous system}}
#: {{hyper|ar|مُخّ|مُخَّيْخ|t1=the cerebrum|t2=the cerebellum}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دِمَاغ|pl=أَدْمِغَة|pl2=دُمُغٌ}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|دِمَاغِيّ|t=cerebral}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|chg|دماغ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|crh|dimağ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|axm|տիմաղ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ota|دماغ|tr=dimağ|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|dimağ|bor=1}} {{qualifier|archaic}}
* {{desctree|fa|دماغ|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=478}}
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|page=134}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=1|page=50 No. 52|entry=*dimāγ-|id=1092}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}

-------- end text --------
