===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|دُمْلُج|دُمْلَج}}

===Etymology===
{{uncertain|ar}}. {{bor|ar|gez|ድጕልማ}}, {{m|gez|ድልጕማ}} may be its origin, even in spite of or because of a {{cog|xsa|𐩵𐩴𐩡𐩣𐩩|𐩵𐩴𐩡𐩣𐩩𐩣|pos=plural}} attested in the same meaning, reported as booty from the Aethiopians; which does not exclude ultimate origin in a language of Southern Arabia. {{cog|ayn|-}} provides a verb {{m|ar|دَمْلَج|tr=damlaj|t=to roll}}, such as {{cog|arz|دحرج|tr=dahrag}}, so it might be literally something “rolled around”, as also suggested by the root {{ar-root|د م ل|nocat=1}} related to adjustion and {{ar-root|د م ج|nocat=1}} related to insertion.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دُمْلُوج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دُمْلُوج|m|pl=دَمَالِيج}}

# [[bangle]], [[armlet]], piece of [[jewelry]] [[women]] [[install]] around the [[upper arm]] for [[adornment]] [[purpose]]s
#: {{syn|ar|مِعْضَد}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=c. 800|author=ar:أبو الشيص محمد|title=[[s:ar:قُلْ للطّويلة موضع العِقْد|{{lang|ar|قُلْ للطّويلة موضع العِقْد}}]]
|passage=فنظرتِ ما يَعْملن في الخدِ<br/>لولا التمنطق والسّوار معاً<br/>والحِجْلُ والدُملوج في العضْدِ<br/>لتزايَلَتْ من كلّ ناحية<br/>لكنْ جُعِلْن لها على عَمْدِ
|translation=}}
# a kind of [[circular]] [[pastry]]

