Page 8896 دمية: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2019|September|29}}
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
* From {{ar-root|د|م|ي|t=to smear, to stain or defile, to bloody, to color or paint}} of {{m|ar|دَم|t=blood}}, deriving from the [[red ochre]] paint used to decorate idols, which is suggested by {{cog|sem-saf|𐪕𐪃𐪚|ts=damaya|t=to draw}}; alternatively, in reference to the blood sacrifices as a means to appease them. It has the appearance of {{m|ar|آدم|tr=ʔādam|t=man}}, {{cog|uga|𐎀𐎄𐎎|t=man}} etc.
* Phonologically dubiously and bare of factual basis, alleging that “it has not a spoor of derivation in Arabic”, Fraenkel claimed it being borrowed from {{noncog|syc|ܕܘܽܡܳܝܳܐ|tr=dummāyā|g=m}}, {{noncog|arc|דְּמָאִין|tr=dmāʾīn|t=likenesses, simulacra|g=m-p}}, {{m|arc|דְּמוּ|tr=dmū|g=m|t=likeness, simulacrum}}, {{m|arc|דְּמוּתָא|tr=dmūṯā|t=likeness, simulacrum|g=f}}, related to {{m|arc|דְּמָא|tr=dmaʾ|t=to be similar}}, {{m|arc|דְּמֵי|tr=dmey|t=to be similar}}, {{noncog|syc|ܕܡܳܐ|tr=dmāʾ|t=to be similar}}, apparently {{noncog|ar|دَنَا|t=to be near}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دُمْيَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دُمْيَة|f|pl=دُمًى}}

# [[statue]], [[statuette]], especially a [[painted]] [[idol]] made of [[ivory]] or [[marble]]
# an [[image]] or [[effigy]]
# a [[dummy]], [[doll]], or [[puppet]]
#* {{quote-journal|ar|work=BBC Arabic|date=2018-07-06|title=ar:دمية عملاقة على شكل "ترامب رضيع" في سماء لندن أثناء زيارة الرئيس الأمريكي|url=https://www.bbc.com/arabic/world-44739422|trans-title=[https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-london-44732754 Giant 'Trump Baby' could fly over London for president's visit]
|passage=وجمع ناشطون نحو 18 ألف جنيه استرليني لشراء دمية تنفخ بغاز الهيليوم طولها 6 أمتار، ويقولون إنها تجسد شخصية ترامب بأنه "مزاجي كالأطفال، ومغرور".
|translation=Campaigners raised almost £18,000 for the helium-filled six-metre high figure, which they said reflects Mr Trump's character as an "angry baby with a fragile ego and tiny hands".}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دُمْيَة|pl=دُمًى}}

