Page 8995 ديانة: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|د ي ن}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|ar|دِين|gloss=[[religion]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دِيَانَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دِيَانَة|f|pl=دِيَانَات}}

# [[religion]], [[confession]], [[denomination]], [[sect]]

====Usage notes====
Though {{m|ar|دِيَانَة}} and {{m|ar|دِين}} both mean "religion," they are not synonymous. {{m|ar|دِيَانَة}} generally refers to the particular religion or denomination a person adheres to (i.e., one's [[religious]] [[affiliation]]), whereas {{m|ar|دِين}} refers to "religion" in a more general or abstract sense.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|دِيَانَة|pl=دِيَانَات}}
-------- end text --------
