* {{ar-IPA|دَيْر}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|د ي ر}}
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܕܝܪܐ|tr=dayrā}} which generally means “dwelling” and specifically “cloister”, from the Syriac root {{syc-root|ܕ|ܘ|ܪ}} relating to dwelling, originally parallel to {{m|ar|دَار|t=dwelling; abode}} and {{m|ar|دَوَّارة|t=home; quarter}} from the root {{ar-root|د|و|ر|nocat=1}} bearing meanings of “circling, going about”.

====Noun====
