Page 9017 ديماس: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar|ديماس (عمارة)}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|دَيْمُوس|دَمُّوس|دَامُوس}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|דִּימוֹסָא|tr=dīmōsā}}, {{m|arc|דִּימוֹסְיָא|tr=dīmōsyā|t=public affairs; public property; fiscus; public bath}}, {{m|syc|ܕܝܡܘܣܝܘܢ|tr=dīmōsyōn|t=public affair; public bath; public building; dungeon; treasury; chancellery}}, from {{der|ar|grc|δημόσιον|t=public building; treasury; public prison; public bath}}, the neuter of {{m|grc|δημόσιος|t=public}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|دَيْمَاس|دِيمَاس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|دَيْمَاس|head2=دِيمَاس|m|pl=دَيَامِيس|pl2=دَمَامِيس}}

# any [[public]] [[building]], [[chapter]]
## [[bathhouse]], [[thermae]]
##: {{syn|ar|حَمّام}}
##* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|60|68|passage=رَأَيْتُ مُوسَى وَإِذَا رَجُلٌ ضَرْبٌ رَجِلٌ، كَأَنَّهُ مِنْ رِجَالِ شَنُوءَةَ، وَرَأَيْتُ عِيسَى، فَإِذَا هُوَ رَجُلٌ رَبْعَةٌ أَحْمَرُ كَأَنَّمَا خَرَجَ مِنْ '''دِيمَاسٍ'''|t=I saw Moses, and he was a lean man with fairly long straight hair, [and he looked] as though he were of the [towering] men of [the tribe of] Šanūʾah. And I saw Jesus, and he was a man of medium stature, [and he was] red as though he had come out of a '''bathhouse'''.}}<!--also {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|60|108}} and {{RQ:Sunna|tirmidhi|47}} “English reference: Vol. 5, Book 44, Hadith 3130, Arabic reference: Book 47, Hadith 3422”-->
# [[underground]] [[vault]], [[cavern]], [[catacomb]]
## [[dungeon]], [[calaboose]], [[can]] {{q|this first, as a prison is a public building}}
## [[souterrain]], [[mattamore]]
##: {{syn|ar|مَطْمُورة|شُونَة|عَنْبَر}}
## [[latibulum]], [[lair]] of a beast
##: {{syn|ar|نَامُوس|قُتْرَة|قُرْمُوص|زَرِيبَة|زَرْب}}
## [[water]] [[reservoir]], [[aqueduct|aquaeduct]] etc.
##: {{syn|ar|قَادُوس|قَنْطَرَة}}

