Page 9029 ذ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Derived from {{m|ar|د}}, and originally written as such (in {{m|en|rasm}}) by analogy with [[Nabatean]] tradition, as Nabatean cognates of Arabic words with /ð/ were indiscriminately spelled using {{m|arc|𐢅|tr=d}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/ðaːl/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/ð/}}
* {{sense|Main dialectal variations}} {{IPA|ar|/ð/|/d/|/z/}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ذ '''/''' ‍ذ'''|tr=ḏāl}}

# The ninth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. Its name is {{l|ar|ذَال}}, and is preceded by {{l|ar|د}} and followed by {{l|ar|ر}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ذ '''/''' ‍ذ'''|tr=ḏāl}}

# The twenty-fifth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|خ}} and followed by {{l|ar|ض}}.

