Page 9038 ذ ه ب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The senses of “going” relate to {{ar-root|ذ و ب|nocat=1}} / {{m|ar|ذَابَ|t=to melt away}} and {{ar-root|ذ ه ل|nocat=1}} / {{m|ar|ذَهِلَ|t=to become diverted, distracted, absent-minded}} and conversely {{ar-root|ذ ه ن|nocat=1}} {{m|ar|ذَهِنَ|t=to have a retentive mind; to understand}} / {{m|ar|ذِهْن|t=mind}}.

For the “gold” senses this can mean that the term references its coruscant appearance, replacing in Central Semitic, {{cog|he|זָהָב|tr=zāhāḇ}}, {{cog|syc|ܕܗܒܐ|tr=dahbā}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩹𐩠𐩨}}, the term for gold found in {{cog|hbo|חָרוּץ|tr=ḥārūṣ}}, {{cog|uga|𐎃𐎗𐎕|ts=ḫurāṣu}}, {{cog|akk|ḫurāṣum|𒆬𒄀|tr=ḫurāṣum}} but not attesting the base verb “to go” later in a language other than Arabic. Another explanation would be a reference to its economic significance from {{m|ar|ذُو}} + {{ar-root|و ه ب|nocat=1}} / {{m|ar|وَهَبَ|t=to grant, to give}}.

===Root===
{{ar-root|ذ|ه|ب}}

