Page 9073 ذرأ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|ذ ر ء}}
Dialectal variant of {{m|ar|ذَرَا}} or {{m|ar|ذَرَّ}} in all senses. How “to sow” or “to strew”, with meaning “offspring” in {{m|ar|ذُرِّيَّة}}, can mean “to create”, needs no explanation. For the coloration meaning apparently {{m-self|ar|ذَرَأ}} is the original and meant color specks figuratively strewn, ultimately becoming a [[dead metaphor]] like {{noncog|ru|сы́паться}} which is used for skin rashes and the like.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.vn:ذَرْء}}

# to [[create]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.vn:ذَرْء}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.nopass.vn:ذَرَأ,ذَرَاء,ذُرْأَة}}

# to become white, to have whiteness intermixed into the saturated colour
# {{lb|ar|al-Andalus|Morocco}} to be or become [[rusty]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.nopass.vn:ذَرَأ,ذَرَاء,ذُرْأَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|ذَرَأ|m}}

# whiteness intermixed into saturated colour
# {{lb|ar|al-Andalus|Morocco}} [[rust]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|ذَرَأ|m}}

{{C|ar|Iron|Whites|Browns}}
