Page 9126 ذو الفقار: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar|ذو_الفقار_(سيف)|ذو الفقار}}
{{wp|lang=en|Zulfiqar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ar|ذُوٱلْفَقَار|tr=ḏū-l-faqār||misspelling}}

===Etymology===
From {{compound|ar|ذُو|الـ|فَقَار|t1=possessor of, having|tr2=al-|t2=the|t3=[[vertebrae]], spine}}, variously interpreted as being a notched-sword, as “the spine-cleaver”, or as “the one having the ability to dice into pieces” like the segmentation of a vertebra.

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|standard}} {{ar-IPA|ذُو ٱلْفَقَار}}
* {{q|non-standard|but very common}} {{ar-IPA|ذُو ٱلْفِقَار}}
* {{audio|ar|LL-Q13955 (ara)-Spotless Mind1988-ذو الفقار.wav|a=nonstandard,_,pronunciation}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|ذُو الْفَقَار|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} A famous mythical weapon of {{w|Ali|Ali ibn Abi Talib}}, previously belonging to {{w|Muhammad}}.
# {{given name|ar|male}} {{n-g|enjoying greater popularity among [[Shi'a]] Muslims.}}
# {{surname|ar}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|ذ:lc|mod=فَقَار|idafa=yes|state=def}}

====Descendants====
