===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ر ب ب}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*rabb-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|رَبَّ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:رَبّ,رِبَاب}}

# to be [[master]], to be [[lord]]
# to have [[possession]], to [[gather]], to [[control]]
# to have [[authority]] over, to [[govern]]
# to [[impact]], to [[comprise]], to [[contain]]
# to [[collect]], to [[congregate]]
# to [[grow]], to [[increase]], to become greater

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:رَبّ,رِبَاب}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:رَبّ}}

# to [[bring up]], to [[raise]] (a child)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:رَبّ}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ر ب ب}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*rabb-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|رَبّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|رَبّ|m|pl=أَرْبَاب|pl2=رُبُوب|f=رَبَّة}}

# [[Lord]], an epithet of God
#: {{uxi|ar|اَللهُ رَبُّ الْعَالَمِين|God is Lord of the Worlds}}
#: {{uxi|ar|الرَّبّ|[[LORD|the LORD]]}}
# [[god]], [[deity]]
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|12|39|passage=يَاصَاحِبَيِ السِّجْنِ ءَ'''أَرْبَابٌ''' مُّتَفَرِّقُونَ خَيْرٌ أَمِ اللہُ الْوَاحِدُ الْقَهَّارُ|t=[Joseph said:] "O my two companions of the prison! Are many different '''deities''' better than God the One [Who is the Source of all things], the Overpowering?"}}
# [[master]], [[lord]], [[king]], [[sovereign]], [[potentate]]
#: {{coordinate terms|ar|عَبْد|خَادِم}}
#: {{uxi|ar|رَبُّ الدَّار|master of the house}}
#: {{uxi|ar|رَبُّ الْعَائِلَة|[[paterfamilias]]}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|12|41|passage=يَا صَاحِبَيِ السِّجْنِ أَمَّا أَحَدُكُمَا فَيَسْقِي '''رَبَّهُ''' خَمْرًا ۖ وَأَمَّا الْآخَرُ فَيُصْلَبُ فَتَأْكُلُ الطَّيْرُ مِن رَّأْسِهِ|subst=خَمْرًا ۖ/خَمْرًا|t=“O my fellow inmates! One of you will serve '''his master''' wine; while the other will be crucified, and the birds will eat from his head. Thus the matter you are inquiring about is settled.”}}
# [[leader]], [[chief]], [[head]]
#: {{uxi|ar|رَبُّ بَحْرِيّ|[[seaman]] {{gloss|naval rank}}}}
# [[owner]], [[proprietor]]
# ''(with a following genitive)'' one possessed of, one endowed with
# ''(with a following genitive)'' having to do with
# {{ar-verbal noun of|رَبَّ|form=I}}

