Page 9335 ربيثاء: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The verb {{m|ar|رَبَثَ|t=to bar someone from doing something}}, {{m|ar|رَبِيثَة}}, {{m|ar|رِبِيثَى|t=obstacle, what lies in front of something and impedes him}} seems semantically hard to be the model and is rare anyway. Apparently from the exact {{bor|ar|arc|-}} term which is attested {{cog|tmr|ריביתא}} / {{cog|syc|ܪܒܝܬܐ}} / {{cog|myz|ࡓࡁࡉࡕࡀ|tr=rəḇīṯā|t=sea, ocean}} and with further meaning in {{der|ar|myz|ࡓࡁࡉࡕࡀ|tr=rəḇīṯā|t=flood waters}}, so – perhaps supported by a connection to {{m|syc|ܐܪܒܝܬܐ|tr=ʾarbīṯā|t=shrimp, prawn}} – the dish-name originates from an understanding of fish exposed multiple times to solution; a form and meaning direction spawned in {{der|ar|myz|-}} from the form which is attested as {{cog|syc|ܪܒܝܥܬܐ|tr=rəḇīʿtā|t=mountain}}, from the root {{m|arc|ר־ב־ע}} / {{syc-root|ܪ|ܒ|ܥ}} “to lie or crouch down” cognate to the Arabic root {{ar-root|ر ب ض|nocat=1}}. From this idea of “lying or crouching down” then the same word must have acquired meanings of “a thing sitting in front of something”, something anent of man just like a herd of camels blocking the path must have been derived, thence {{m+|ar|رَبِيثَة}}, {{m|ar|رِبِيثَى|t=obstacle}}, the latter a form not native to Arabic, the verb {{m|ar|رَبَثَ|t=to bar someone from doing something}} only denominally; note also {{m|ar|تَرَبَّثَ|t=to lollygag, to rest long before gettings things done}}, {{m|ar|اِرْبَثَّ}} and {{m|ar|اِرْبَاثَّ|t=to advance slowly}} more directly related to the “crouching” meanings and using {{ar-form|IX|nocap=1}} and {{ar-form|XI|nocap=1}} in an unseen fashion, apparently in imitation of an Aramaic verb pattern. In sum no root {{ar-root|ر ب ث|nocat=1}} exists in Arabic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رُبَيْثَاء}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|رُبَيْثَاء|f}}

# {{tlb|ar|obsolete|Iraq}} a [[side dish]] from small [[fish]] in herbs and vinegar
#* {{RQ:Mafatih-Vloten|pages=169 line 1–3|passage=الرُبَيْثَاء وَال[[صَِحْنَاء]] وال[[صِير]] والسُمَيْكَات تعمل من السمك الصغار والملح والسَمَك المَمْقُور المالح الذي ينقع في الخل نحوِه.|t=''Rubayṯaʾ'' and ''ṣiḥnāʾ'' and ''ṣīr'' and ''sumaykāt'' are made from small fish and salt and marinated salty fish that has staled in vinegar and the like.}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|lang=ar|line=[https://al-maktaba.org/book/23696/132 <!--same in https://www.noorlib.ir/view/fa/book/bookview/text/4351/1/131-->6] of the apparatus of|page=131|instead=1}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|رُبَيْثَاء}}

