Page 9401 رحمن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
From the root {{ar-root|ر|ح|م}}. Compare {{bor|ar|arc|רַחְמָן}} / {{m|arc|ܪܚܡܢ|tr=raḥmān}}, {{bor|ar|he|רַחְמָן|tr=raḥmān}}. It is usual to believe the Arabic form borrowed from one of these two languages, either immediately or through the mediation of {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, due to the occurrence of the word only in this specific context of specifying the epithet of the [[monotheistic]] god {{m|ar|الرَّحْمٰن}}, as well as the fact that its [[defective]] spelling mirrors the corresponding defective spelling in the previously mentioned languages.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|رَحْمٰن}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|رَحْمٰن}}

# [[merciful]], [[compassionate]] {{qualifier|said of [[God]]}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|2|163|passage=وَإِلَٰهُكُمْ إِلَٰهٌ وَاحِدٌ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ الرَّحْمَٰنُ الرَّحِيمُ|t=And your God is one God, there is no god but He, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|رَحْمٰنُ|f=-|number=sg}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|fa-cls|رَحْمَٰن|bor=1|noalts=1}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Jeffery-Foreign|pages=140–141}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel-V|page=23}}
