Page 9405 رحيق: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|رُحَاق}}

===Etymology===
Related to {{cog|he|רֶקַח|tr=reḥāq|t=spiced; spiced wine}}, and {{cog|akk|𒋆𒈨𒌍|ts=riqqu, rīqu|t=aromatic plants, beer malt}}. Wine, at the advent of the Quranic usage, was served warm and brewed from a dehydrated paste or powder form, with spices and practices similar to modern Arabic coffee culture.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رَحِيق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|رَحِيق|m}}

# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} [[choice]]st [[wine]], [[exquisite]]ly [[treat]]ed [[wine]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|83|25-26
|passage=يُسْقَوْنَ مِن رَّحِيقٍ مَّخْتُومٍ ۝ خِتٰمُهُ مِسْكٌ
|translation=They will be given to drink of full-flavoured sealed wine ۝ and its seal is of musk.
|transliteration=yusqawna min raḥīqin maḵtūmin ۝ ḵitāmu-hū miskun}}
# [[nectar]] of [[blossom]]s

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|رَحِيق}}

