===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|إِرْضَاءُ النَّاسِ غَايَةٌ لَا تُدْرَكُ}}

===Etymology===
[[w:Ibn Abi'l-Hadid|Ibn Abī-l-Ḥadīd]] attrtibutes it to [[w:Ali|ʿAlī]] in his book [[w:ar:شرح نهج البلاغة|شرح نهج البلاغة]]. It literally means "People's acceptance is a goal that cannot be reached".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رِضَا النَّاسِ غَايَةٌ لَا تُدْرَكُ}}

===Proverb===
{{head|ar|proverb|head=[[رضا|رِضَا]] [[ناس|النَّاسِ]] [[غاية|غَايَةٌ]] [[لَا]] [[أدرك|تُدْرَكُ]]}}

# It is [[impossible]] to make a [[decision]] that is [[accept|accepted]] by every single person; [[please|pleasing]] and [[appease|appeasing]] everyone is a [[goal]] that cannot be [[reach|reached]].
