Page 9533 رعي الأيل: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|رِعْي الإِيَّل}}
* {{alter|ar|رِعْي الإِبِل||taṣḥīf}}{{cln|ar|ghost words}}

===Etymology===
{{clq|ar|syc|ܪܥܝܐ ܕܐܝܠܐ|tr=reʿyā də-ʾaylā}}, literally “meadow of deer”, “herd of deer” or “fodder of deer”—compare {{m|ar|رِعْي الْحَمَام}}—, itself calquing {{clq|ar|grc|ἐλαφοβόσκον|notext=1}}, {{m|grc|ἐλαφόβοσκον}} which in some Dioskurides manuscripts is used in [https://dioscorides.usal.es/p2.php?numero=429 the place] of {{m|grc|ἐλελίσφακος}}, {{m|grc|ἐλελίσφακον|t=sage}}, using this translation due to understanding the former Greek lexeme as {{m|grc|ἔλαφος|t=deer}} and {{m|grc|βοσκός|t=herdsman}}, the root {{syc-root|ܪ|ܥ|ܝ}} being related to senses of pasturing and herding (Arabic {{ar-root|ر ع ي|nocat=1}}). Later transformed into {{m|ar|لِسَان الْأُيَّل|lit=tongue of deer}} in reference to the leaf shape.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رِعْي الأُيَّل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|[[رِعْي]] [[ال]][[أُيَّل]]|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[sage]] ({{taxfmt|Salvia officinalis|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|مَرْيَمِيَّة|q1=now|قَصْعِين|q2=now|سَالَبِيَّة|شَالَبِيَّة|q4=al-Andalus|نَاعِمَة|q5=al-Andalus|}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|رِعْي|mod=أُيَّل|idafa=def}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=537a|entry=رعي الإبل}} (didn’t get what was used for what, relying on the reference works in his time)
* {{R:ar:Biruni|vol=IV|pages=473–474 Nr. 467}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Pflanzen|page=365 Nr. 311}}

{{C|ar|Mint family plants}}
-------- end text --------
Page 9534 رعي الحمام: -------- begin text --------
[[File:VERBENA OFFICINALIS - SANT JUST - IB-068 (Berbena).JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|رِعْي الْحَمَام}} – {{taxfmt|Verbena officinalis|species}}|upright=1.15]]
{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
A {{w|Graeco-Arabic translation movement|science translation}} {{clq|ar|syc|ܪܥܝܐ ܕܝܘܢܐ|tr=reʿyā də-yawnē|nocap=1}}, which is depending on the meaning of the first word “meadow of doves”, “kit of doves”, “food of doves”, apparently the Arabic translators took the “fodder” meaning as this is what {{cog|ar|رِعْي}} means—unless the Arabic phytonym is a [[loanblend]] even—, while the Syriac translators took the other meanings, misinterpreting {{clq|ar|grc|περῐστερεών|notext=1}}, {{m|grc|περῐστεριών}}, {{m|grc|περῐστέριον|t=vervain}} as the same word as {{m|grc|περῐστερεών|t=dovecote}}, both being from {{m|grc|περῐστερᾱ́|t=pigeon}}. Spread from the ''materia medica'' into general use, but modernly half of the time deformed as {{m|ar|رِجْل الْحَمَام}} or {{m|ar|سَاق الْحَمَام}} due to the alienness of the first word.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رِعْي الْحَمَام}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|[[رِعْي]] [[الْ]][[حَمَام]]|m}}

# [[vervain]] ({{taxfmt|Verbena|genus}} gen. et spp., especially {{taxfmt|Verbena officinalis|species}})

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|رِعْي|mod=حَمَام|idafa=def}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|r(y%234|N}}
* {{R:syc:Brockelmann 1995|page=737b}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=537a}}
* {{R:ar:Biruni|vol=IV|pages=474–475 Nr. 468}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=3|page=491}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Pflanzen|pages=365–366 Nr. 312}}

{{C|ar|Lamiales order plants}}
