Page 9543 رف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{unk|ar|Disputed etymology}}:
* Natively from the root {{ar-root|ر|ف|ف}} in the sense of an outstretched wing being symbolic of protection, a coverlet; hence originally an awning or covering; semantically becoming a story or tier of a building as each window would feature such a cloth shelf above it. Parallel semantic conception found with {{cog|he|רפפות||t=window shutters; a collection of layered thin strips}} and {{cog|amw|ܪܦ|tr=rap|t=level, story; room, chamber}}.
* Natively from the root {{ar-root|ر|ف|ف}} in the sense of stretching elbows out on a pillow or cushion, stemming from an outstretched wing; hence a place to place things, a place to spread things out on.
* {{root|ar|ine-pro|*h₁rebʰ-}}From {{der|ar|arc|-}} found in its descendant {{cog|amw|ܪܦ|tr=rap|t=level, story; room, chamber}} of uncertain etymology, but considered likely foreign or possibly even borrowed from Arabic; as for a foreign source possibly connected to {{der|ar|ine-pro|*h₁rebʰ-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|رَفّ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-رف.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|رَفّ|m|pl=رُفُوف|pl2=أَرْفُف|pl3=رِفَاف}}

# [[sill]]; [[shelf]]; [[whatnot]]
#* {{quote-text|ar|year=p. 2000|url=https://www.aldiwan.net/poem1051.html|title={{l|ar||كَرِيم مَعْتُوق}}
|passage=مَا مَرَّ شَذَاهَا بِخُطُوطِ الْوَرَقِ الْمُلْقَى عَلَى الْأَرْفُفِ
