Page 9559 رفيع: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ر ف ع}}

===Etymology===
{{m|ar||فَعِيل}}-type stative-verb {{ar-active participle|lc=1|nocat=1}} from the verb {{m|ar|رَفُعَ||to be [[high]]; to become [[thin]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رَفِيع}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj-sound|رَفِيع|el=أَرْفَع}}

# {{lb|ar|of the character, quality, or reception of a thing, such as a position, a rank, or a style}} [[elevated]]; [[high]]; [[noble]]; [[sublime]]; [[fine]]
#: {{syn|ar|عَال|سَام|شَرِيف|نَبِيل}}
#: {{ant|ar|دَنِيء|مُنْحَطّ|حَقِير|سَافِل}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|instead=1|lang=ar|page=374 ''m''–''u''|section=web [http://islamport.com/w/bld/Web/451/136.htm 1/136]|passage=وأما أرمينية فإنها كورة جليلة رسمها أرميني بن كنظر بن يافث بن نوح ومنها ترتفع الستور والزَلاليُّ ال'''رفيعة''' كثيرة الخصائص قصبتها دَبِيل ومن مدنها: بَدْلِيس، خِلَاط، أَرْجِيش، بَرْكَرِي، خُوَيُّ، سَلَمَاس، أُرْمِيَة، دَاخَرَّقَان، مَرَاغَة، أَهْرُ، مَرَنْد، سِنْجَان، قالِيقَلَا، قندرية، قَلْعَة يُونُس، نورين.|t=As for Armenia, she is a majestic expanse, originally sketched and contoured by ʾArmīnī, the son of {{w|Ashkenaz#Armenian_tradition|Ashkenaz}}, himself a descendant of {{w|Japheth}}, one of the sons of {{w|Noah}}. In Armenia, curtains, draperies, and rugs multifarious and '''fine''' hang down, the {{w|Curtain rod|rod}} being {{w|Dwin|Dabīl}}. Among her localities are {{w|Bitlis|Badlīs}} [Baghesh], {{w|Ahlat|Ḵilāṭ}} [Xlat], {{w|Erciş|ʾArjīš}} [Arjesh], [the small town of] {{w|Muradiye|Barkarī}} [east of Ḵilāṭ], {{w|Khoy|Ḵuway}} [Xoy], {{w|Salmas|Salamās}} [Salamas], {{w|Urmia|ʾUrmiyah}} [Urmia], {{w|Azarshahr|Dāḵarraqān}}, {{w|Maragheh|Marāḡah}}, {{w|Ahar|ʾAhr}}, {{w|Marand|Marand}}, Sinjān, {{w|Erzurum|Qālīqalā}}, {{w|Qandariyah|Qandariyyah}}, Qalʿat Yūnus, Nūrīn.}}
# {{lb|ar|chiefly|_|post-classical|of the thickness of an object}} [[thin]]; [[fine]]
#: {{syn|ar|رَقِيق|دَقِيق|لَطِيف}}
#: {{ant|ar|سَمِيك|ثَخِين}}
## {{lb|ar|of a person}} [[slim]]; [[lean]]
##: {{syn|ar|Thesaurus:ar:underweight}}
##: {{ant|ar|Thesaurus:ar:overweight}}
# {{lb|ar|post-classical|of someone's voice or, less commonly, any sound}} [[high-pitched]]; [[sharp]]
#: {{syn|ar|حَادّ}}
# {{lb|ar|obsolete|of someone's voice}} [[raised]]; [[loud]]
#: {{syn|ar|عَالٍ|جَهِير}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|رَفِيع|cpl=sp}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}

