Page 9620 رمان: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{uncertain|ar}} direct and ultimate source, not Semitic. Compare {{cog|he|-}} {{he-m|רימון|dwv=רִמּוֹן|tr=rimmṓn}}, {{cog|xpu|*𐤓𐤌𐤍|ts=rimmūn}} and {{cog|arc|[[רִימֹּונָא]] / [[רִמֹּונָא]]|tr=rimmōnā}} / {{m|arc|רוּמָּנָא}} / {{m|syc|ܪܘܡܢܐ|tr=rummānā}}, {{cog|gez|ሮማን}}, {{cog|akk|𒄑𒈢𒆳𒊏|ts=armannu}}.
Likely borrowed from Semitic is {{cog|egy|jnhmn|<hiero>i-n:h-mn:n-M1</hiero>|tr={{m|egy|jnhmn}}}}, which developed into {{cog|egx-dem|hrnt}}, and from this {{m|cop|ⲉⲣⲙⲁⲛ|pos=Bohairic}}, {{m|cop|ⲗⲉϩⲙⲉⲛ|pos=Akhmimic}}, {{m|cop|ϩⲉⲣⲙⲁⲛ|pos=Sahidic}}.

{{rel-top|Further potential cognates}}
{{lb|ar|With a different order of the consonants, compare also:}}
* {{cog|sux|𒉡𒌫𒈠|tr=NU-UR<sub>2</sub>-MA|ts=nurma|t=pomegranate}}
* {{cog|akk|𒉡𒌫𒈠|tr=NU-UR<sub>2</sub>-MA|ts=nurmû}}, {{cog|akk|𒇻𒆸𒌅|ts=lurmû, lurimtu, lurinnu|t=pomegranate}}, {{cog|akk|𒉡𒊑𒅎𒁺|tr=nu-ri-im-du|ts=nurimdu, nurimtu|t=pomegranate}}
* {{cog|xhu|𒉡𒊏𒀭𒋾|tr=nu-ra-an-ti|ts=nuranti|t=pomegranate}}, {{cog|uga|𐎍𐎗𐎎𐎐|t=pomegranate}}
* {{cog|hit|𒉡𒌫𒈬|ts=nurmû|t=pomegranate}}
* {{cog|fa|نار|tr=nâr}}, {{m|fa|انار|tr=anâr|t=pomegranate}}
* {{cog|zh|-}} {{och-l|榴|pomegranate}}.
{{rel-bottom}}

