Page 9624 رمث: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ر م ث}}. Apparently the root derives from the plant name {{bor|ar|qfa-sub}}, so from the picture of the plant the meaning of being in disorder, then the name for the raft apparently because of a raft consisting of complex branches, then from the building of rafts or campfires the meaning of arranging with the hand. See {{m|ar|مَرْخ|t={{taxlink|Leptadenia pyrotechnica|species}}}} for another example of a root deriving from a plant name.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.vn:رَمْث}}

# to [[arrange]] with one’s hand

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.vn:رَمْث}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.nopass.vn:رَمَث}}

# to be in [[disorder]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.nopass.vn:رَمَث}}

