===Etymology===
{{reduplication|ar}} from the root {{ar-root|ر م م}} meaning “to restore, to mend”, because leaf decoctions of the {{vern|nettle-leaved goosefoot}} ({{taxlink|Chenopodiastrum murale|species}}) as well as various {{taxfmt|Heliotropium|genus}} species were used to relieve those suffering snake bite, scorpion sting, [[animal asthma]] and the like.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رَمْرَام}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|رَمْرَام|m|sing=رَمْرَامَة}}

# {{taxfmt|Chenopodium|genus}} and {{taxlink|Chenopodiastrum|genus}}
# {{taxfmt|Heliotropium|genus}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|رَمْرَام}}

{{C|ar|Amaranths and goosefoots|Borage family plants}}
-------- end text --------
