Page 9633 رمس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Dissimilation of {{m|ar|نَامُوس}},<ref>{{R:sem:Růžička:1909|page=99}}</ref><ref>{{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=558|entry=رمس}} it is declared, as notorious for this book, an extension of a biconsonantal root, {{m|ar|رَمَّ}}, {{ar-root|ر م م|nocat=1}}, glossed there “to be heaped up”, cognate with the Hebrew and Aramaic [http://cal.huc.edu/oneentry.php?lemma=rms%20V&cits=all r-m-s] “trampling”.</ref> maybe also with influence of {{m|ar|نَاوُوس}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رَمَس}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i,u.pass.vn:رَمْس}}

# to [[bury]]
# to [[cover]], to [[wipe out]] (traces, tracks of something)

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i,u.pass.vn:رَمْس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|رَمْس|m}}

# [[grave]]; [[tomb]]; [[soil]] of a grave

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|رَمْس|pl=رُمُوس}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|رَامُوس}}

===References===
<references/>

