Page 9635 رمص: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Mostly augmented from {{m|ar|رَمَّ|t=to mend}} of the root {{ar-root|ر م م}}.

The meaning of rheum is also found in {{cog|syc|ܪܷ̈ܡܨܶܐ|tr=remṣē}} and hardly native to Arabic, even variating its consonantism to {{m|ar|رَمَسَة}} and {{m|ar|رُمُوسَة}} in al-Andalus, and {{m|ar|غَمَض}} meaning a more liquid rheum, here applying the {{m|ar||فَعَل}} pattern usual for [[excrescence]]s and {{m|ar||فُعُولَة}} for bulkier properties attached to someone or something: plausibly after a {{bor|ar|ira-mid}} borrowing equivalent to that of {{m|ar|رِمْش|t=eyelash}}, although it is also possible that with emphasis of the driedness of the rheum the term is an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} derivation of an older form of the root cognate to {{m|ar|رَمَضَ|t=to parch, to scorch}} and its root {{ar-root|ر م ض|nocat=1}}, otherwise curiously attested in {{cog|he-mis|רֶמֶץ|tr=rémeṣ|t=ember}}—the {{cog|sem-pro||*ṣ́}} phoneme gives sometimes ''ṣ'' and more prominently ''ʕ'' in Aramaic, both reflexes coexisting in Syriac, as {{m|syc|ܚܲܡܘܼܨܬܵܐ|tr=ḥammūṣtā}} and {{m|syc|ܚܲܡܘܼܥܬܵܐ|tr=ḥammūʿtā}}<!--we have to tell people as they already have been uninformed enough that thinking *ṣ́  gives ''ʕ'' they complain on Twitter about Wiktionary etymologies-->.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:رَمْص}}

# to [[compensate]], to [[mend]]
# to [[make peace]] between
# to [[dung]] {{lb|ar|supposedly|_|intransitive|_|and|_|of a [[hen]]}}

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:رَمْص}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|arc-nab|𐢛𐢓𐢙|bor=1|tr=rmṣ|t=to pacify}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.vn:رَمَص}}

# to have sticky matter in the [[corner of the eye|corners of the eyes]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.vn:رَمَص}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|رَمَص|m}}

# [[rheum]], [[sleep]] in the eye (particularly [[solid]] one)
#: {{cot|ar|غَمَص|q1=more solid one}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|رَمَص}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Baranov}}
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=558|entry=رمس}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=193a}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=1|page=924b–925a}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass|page=434b}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|page=417b}}
* {{R:CAL|rmc|V}}
* {{R:CAL|rmc%233|V}}
* {{R:CAL|rmc%232|V}} and {{R:CAL|rm(|V}}, {{R:CAL|rmw()%40dnwr)|N}} the Aramaic cognates of {{ar-root|ر م ض|nocat=1}}

{{C|ar|Bodily fluids}}
