Page 9659 رهج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|pal||tr=lhk'|ts=rahag|t=vein|sc=Phlv}}, also {{m|pal||tr=lk'|ts=rag|t=vein|sc=Phlv}} whence {{cog|fa|رگ|tr=rag|t=vein}}. It must have meant aside from a blood-vessel a “streak, haze in the air”. {{cog|fa|[[رگ]] [[ابر]]|tr=rag-i abr}} means “streak of a cloud”. Compare the transferred use in mineralogy {{m|ar|رَهْج اَلْغَار|t=realgar}}, {{m|ar|رَهَج أَصْفَر|t=[[orpiment]]}} and {{cog|xcl|երակ|t=vein or streak of a metal or mineral}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|رَهَج}} and {{ar-IPA|رَهْج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|رَهَج|head2=رَهْج|m}}

# [[dust]], [[haze]]
# {{lb|ar|meteorology}} [[stratus]]

