===Etymology 1===
{{ar-etym-iyya|رُوس|}}. Possibly imitating a foreign demonym. Compare {{der|ar|gkm|Ρωσσία}} and {{cog|ru|Росси́я||Russia}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|رُوسِيَّة|f}}

# {{lb|ar|collective|rare|historical|_|or|_|obsolete}} a [[people]] [[inhabit]]ing northeast [[Europe]] in the [[Middle Ages]] often [[presume]]d to be of [[Scandinavian]] [[stock]]

=====Usage notes=====
Very little is known about the people who are labeled thus in medieval Arabic texts, especially those whom the Islamic theologian and traveler {{w|Ibn Fadlan|Ibn Faḍlān}} reputedly encountered during his stay among the {{w|Volga Bulgars}} while propagating the Islamic religion.

