===Etymology 1===
An ancient borrowing of {{bor|ar|egy|r-pr|r(ꜣ)-pr|t=temple}}, due to agricultural properties (i.e., lands) in Egypt—which Bedouins roamed—having been administered by temples. The similarity to {{cog|akk|𒊑𒅁𒄣|tr=ri-ip-qu|ts=ripqu|t=field broken up for cultivation}} is coincidental.

