{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 5===
From the root {{ar-root|ر|ي|م}} or {{ar-root|ر|و|م}}, originally with the sense of climbing up higher, hence also away from others, to depart from, to separate oneself from, to avoid capture, to be wild or free. Related to {{der|ar|sem-pro|*rayam-|t=to be high, to be raised}}; cognates with {{cog|hbo|רְאֵם|tr=rəʾem|t=oryx, wild cows}}, {{cog|uga|𐎗𐎜𐎎|tr=rủm|t=auroch, wild buffalo}}, {{cog|akk|rīmum|𒄞𒄠|tr=rīmum|t=wild bull, wild ass}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|رِئْم}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|رِيم|m|pl=أَرْيَام}}

# [[wild]] member of the {{taxfmt|Bovidae|family}}
# [[gazelle]], [[antelope]], [[oryx]] ([[sand gazelle]] {{taxlink|Gazella leptoceros|species}} and [[goitered gazelle]] {{taxlink|Gazella subgutturosa subsp. marica|subspecies}} formerly {{taxlink|Gazella marica|species}})

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|رِيم|pl=أَرْيَام}}

===Etymology 6===

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|رِيم|f}}

# {{given name|ar|female}} (Reem)

