Page 9775 ز ه ر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Due to the restricted meaning, suspected to be loaned from the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} root {{m|arc|ז־ה־ר}} / {{syc-root|ܙ|ܗ|ܪ}}<ref>{{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=601}}</ref> which is more generally used for “to shine, to glow”, as well as in the specific meaning of “to flourish”,<ref>On the meanings: {{R:CAL|zhr%232|V}}</ref> and in {{cog|syc|ܙܗܪܐ|tr=zahrā}} both “bright light”, “splendor” and “bright or fully-bloomed flower”, as opposed to the restricted {{m+|ar|زَهْر|t=flowers}}, which was thus probably the particular term borrowed from which other meanings were back-formed, not without acquaintance with or reminiscence, that is later influence, of the general meanings in the Aramaic root. This reminds also of more specific plant names like {{m|ar|شَفَلَّح}} and {{m|ar|رَيْحَان}} being borrowed from Aramaic roots expressing ideas of things opening themselves for emission.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

