Page 9849 زجر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ز ج ر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:زَجْر}}

# to [[restrain]], to [[hinder]] especially by [[speech act]], to [[check]], to [[snub]], to [[cry out]], to [[ward off]]<!--отгонять summa-->
#: {{syn|ar|رَدَعَ}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:زَجْر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|زَجْر|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|زَجَرَ|form=I}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|زَجْر}}

===Etymology 2===
{{bor+|ar|syc|ܙܓܪܐ|tr=zaḡrā}}, absolute state {{m|syc|ܙܓܪ|tr=zaḡar}}, of unknown origin, but claimed identical to {{cog|akk|singurrum|𒉔𒄩|tr=NINDA<sub>2</sub>×DIL<sup>KU<sub>6</sub></sup>|ts=zingurru, singurru}}, {{m|akk|zingurrum|𒍣𒅔𒄥𒊒|tr=zi-in-gur-ru|ts=zingurru}}, which was borrowed into {{cog|myz|ࡎࡉࡍࡂࡅࡓࡀ|ts=singūrā}} and apparently via {{cog|xpu|-}} into {{cog|sc|tzingòrra|t=a kind of small and young eel}}

====Noun====
