Page 9857 زحل: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ز|ح|ل}} meaning "to be distant or remote", "to linger away from others"; so called as it is the furthest and has the slowest orbital period of the classical seven heavenly bodies (counting the Sun and the Moon, without the inclusion of Earth).

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|زُحَل}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|زُحَل|m}}

# [[Saturn]] {{gloss|planet}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|زُحَلُ|state=ind-def}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ar|کیوان|كَيْوَان|tr=|t=one that stays, one that lingers}}
* {{l|ar|نَكْرُ|نَكْرُه|}}, {{l|ar|[[نَكْرُ|نِكْرَة]]|tr=|t=one who seems unfamiliar, one who is foreign or estranged, distant or alien}}
* {{l|ar|نَحْس|النَحْسَانِ|tr=|t=the two misfortunes}}, paired with Mars, contrasted with Venus and Mercury, or Venus and Jupiter in another tradition
* {{l|ar|نَحْس|النَحْس الأَكْبَر|tr=|t=the greater misfortune}}, contrasted with Mars the lesser

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|fa-cls|زحل|tr=zuhal|bor=1}}

====See also====
* {{list:planets of the Solar System/ar}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.ipass.vn:زَحْل,زُحُول}}

# to [[move]] away, [[withdraw]], [[retire]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.ipass.vn:زَحْل,زُحُول}}

===Etymology 3===
Causative of {{m|ar|زَحَلَ||to [[move]] away}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# to [[remove]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

===Etymology 4===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|زَحْل|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|زَحَلَ|form=I}}

=====Declension=====
