Page 9877 زربية: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Moroccan Carpet (4803946247).jpg|thumb|right|{{l-self|ar|زُرْبِيَّة|tr=-}}|upright=0.63]]

===Etymology===
* William Hoyt Worrell considers it a genuine Arabic word. It is according to him from {{m|ar|زِرْب|t=canal}} and originally meant a “rug streaked with canals”, a “striped rug”, formed as {{m|ar|فِسْقِيَّة|t=[[fountain]]}}, {{m|ar|شَمْسِيَّة|t=[[parasol]]}}, {{m|ar|حَنَفِيَّة|t=[[faucet]], [[spigot]]}}.
* It could be borrowed from {{bor|ar|gez|ዘርቤት}} from {{m|gez|ዘረበ|t=to {{l|en|trample}}}}, which Theodor Nöldeke and Arthur Jeffery find most appealing, but Wolf Leslau and Siegmund Fraenkel assume that the Ge'ez word is from the Arabic.
* It has been suggested to be from a {{bor|ar|pal||*hcdl-pdy|ts=azēr-pay|lit=under the foot}} by {{w|lang=de|Georg Hoffmann (Orientalist)|Georg Hoffmann}}, but this is doubtful for not being attested in any Persian.
* It would rather be a {{bor|ar|pal||*DHBʾ-pay|ts=zar-pay|lit=gold-foot}}, as Jeffery corrects, but it is unsensible that this would come to mean a carpet.
* It could be a {{m|pal||*DHBʾ-ʾby|ts=zar-ābī|lit=goldeny}}, a parallel to such a formation being found in {{noncog|fa|سیمابی|tr=simâbi|t=silvery}}, to which Wilhelm Eilers and Johnny Cheung lean, and when borrowed been treated as a broken plural with the singular back-formed from the plural, but one has to assume for {{cog|fa|آب|tr=âb}} an unusual meaning “splendour, lustre” from {{der|ar|sa|आभा|t=appearance, splendour, lustre}} and the frequency of such a term is doubtful.
* It could, as Nabīl al-Waġlīsiyy reconstructs, reflect the name of the land of [[Azerbaijan]] as it is renowned yore and today for opulent rug manufacturing, being a {{doublet|ar|nocap=1|أَذَرِيّ|t1=[[Azeri]]}} of a different segmentation including {{IPAchar|/b/}} and lacking the hamzated onset.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|زِرْبِيَّة|زُرْبِيَّة|زَرْبِيَّة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|زَرْبِيَّة|f|head2=زُرْبِيَّة|head3=زِرْبِيَّة|pl=زَرَابِيّ}}

# [[carpet]], [[rug]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|88|16
|passage=وَ'''زَرَابِيُّ''' مَبْثُوثَةٌ
|translation=and carpets spread out
|subst=وَ'''زَرَابِيُّ'''/وَ-'''زَرَابِيُّ'''}}
#* {{quote-web|ar
|title="زرابي" أزلغ الأمازيغية..احتفالية قبائلية لغزل الصوف في المغرب
|work=w:Anadolu Agency
|url=https://www.aa.com.tr/ar/archive/%D8%B2%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%A8%D9%8A-%D8%A3%D8%B2%D9%84%D8%BA-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D9%85%D8%A7%D8%B2%D9%8A%D8%BA%D9%8A%D8%A9%D8%A7%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%81%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%82%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%84%D8%BA%D8%B2%D9%84-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D9%88%D9%81-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%BA%D8%B1%D8%A8/37117
|date=2015 June 12
|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20201126203912/https://www.aa.com.tr/ar/archive/%D8%B2%D8%B1%D8%A7%D8%A8%D9%8A-%D8%A3%D8%B2%D9%84%D8%BA-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%A3%D9%85%D8%A7%D8%B2%D9%8A%D8%BA%D9%8A%D8%A9%D8%A7%D8%AD%D8%AA%D9%81%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%82%D8%A8%D8%A7%D8%A6%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A9-%D9%84%D8%BA%D8%B2%D9%84-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B5%D9%88%D9%81-%D9%81%D9%8A-%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%BA%D8%B1%D8%A8/37117
|archivedate=2020 November 26
|text=أَجْمَلُ أَنْوَاعِ ٱلزَّرَابِيِّ ٱلَّتِي تَحْبِكُهَا نِسَاءُ "وَرْزَازَاتَ" فِي ٱلْأَمَاسِيِّ ٱلدَّافِئَةِ مَمْزُوجَةٌ بِأَهَازِيجِ ٱلْأَمَازِيغِ ٱلْقَدِيمَةِ، تِلْكَ ٱلْمُلَقَّبَةُ بِـ"ٱلزَّرْبِيَّةِ ٱلْوَاوْزَكِيتِيَّةِ" (نِسْبَةً لِقَبَائِلِ وَمِنْطَقَةِ زَكِيتْ قُرْبَ تَازْنَاخَتْ).
}}

