===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, there with forms as {{m|arc|עוזררא}}, {{m|arc|אנזעררתא}}, {{m|arc|זרדתא}}, {{m|arc|זרתא}}, {{m|arc|זודתא}}, {{m|arc|זירדתא}}, {{m|arc|אוזר}}, {{m|arc|חוזרר}}, {{m|arc|חזרור}}, {{m|arc|חיזרר}}, {{m|syc|ܥܙܪܪܬܐ}}. Perhaps from an {{der|ar|egy|-}} expression like {{cog|cop-sah|ⲥⲟⲩⲣⲉ ⲁⲣⲟⲟⲩⲉ|lit=needle-thistle}}, which would explain the distribution of similar {{cog|grc|μέσπιλον|t=medlar}}, {{cog|ary|مزاح|tr=mzāḥ|t=loquats, medlars}}, {{cog|ccs-pro|*sxmarṭl-|t=medlar}}, {{cog|axm|զկեռ|t=medlar}}, {{cog|fa|ازگیل|tr=azgil|t=medlar}}, {{cog|ka|ასკილი|t=dog rose, briar}}. However as the speech is of pomefruits, the form {{m|arc|חֲזְרוּרָא|tr=ḥăzrūrā}} may be most original and reduplicated from the known term {{m|syc|ܚܙܘܪܐ}} / {{m|arc|חֲזוּרָא|tr=ḥăzzūrā|t=apple}}.

