Page 9923 زفت: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Of {{unc|ar|nocap=1}} ultimate origin. Related to {{cog|jpa|-}}, {{cog|arc-jla|-}}, {{cog|tmr|זִפתָּא|tr=zip̄tā}} / {{m|arc|זִיפתָּא|tr=zip̄tā}}, {{cog|syc|ܙܦܬܐ|tr=zep̄tā}}, {{m|syc|ܙܒܬܐ|tr=zeḇtā}}, {{cog|he|זֶפֶת|tr=zéfeṯ}}, possibly Arabic-borrowed {{cog|gez|ዝፍት|tr=zəft}} and Semitic-borrowed {{cog|xcl|ձիւթ}} and {{cog|oge|ძივთი}}. {{cog|akk-nbb|𒍣𒅁𒌈|tr=zi-ib-tum|ts=ziptu, zibtu}}, once glossed “pitch” and rare enough to be {{cog|sem-wes|-}} borrowing, is more correctly<ref>{{R:gez:Kogan:2019|page=903 to 632}}</ref> glossed “a stone”.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|زِفْت|m}}

# [[pitch]], [[tar]], [[latex]], [[asphalt]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|زِفْت}}

