Page 9935 زكاة: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|زَكَوٰة|tr=zakāh||preclassical spelling}}

===Etymology===
Normalized spelling of earlier {{m|ar|زَكَوٰة|tr=zakāh}}, from {{bor|ar|arc|זכותא}} / {{m|syc|ܙܟܘܬܐ|tr=zākūṯā}} otherwise attested in the senses of “merit”, “gain; victory” from base stem {{m|arc|זכי|tr=zəḵē|t=to overcome; to triumph over; to gain}} but [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only attested in borrowings|not]] in the sense of “alms”, however in the geminate stem in {{cog|jpa|זכי|tr=zakkē}} also as “to give possession”, “to give merit” and ultimately “to give charity”. Likewise the noun is not attested but can be inferred from Arabic to have borne in Aramaic the sense of “purity or purification from guilt” as in Palestinian Aramaic the base and geminate stems meant “to be innocent” and “to judge innocent” respectively.

The Arabic root {{ar-root|ز|ك|و}} is in part from this noun.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|زَكَاة}}
** {{IPA|afb|/zəˈkaːt/|a=Gulf}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|زَكَاة|f|pl=زَكَوَات}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} [[zakat]],  [[almsgiving]] (one of the [[five pillars]] of [[Islam]])
# [[purification]] from [[excess]], to [[free]] from [[inefficiencies]], to [[dispense]] [[filth]]
# [[purifying]] (of the soul)
## {{lb|ar|adverbially}} in piety, in purity

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|زَكَاة|pl=زَكَوَات}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|صَلَاة|t=[[prayer]], [[salat]]}}
* {{l|ar|صَوْم|t=[[fast]], [[sawm]]}}
* {{l|ar|دُعَاء|t=[[supplication]], [[du'a']]}}

====Descendants====
* {{desctree|ota|زكات|tr=zekat|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|زکات|tr=zakât|bor=1}}
** {{desc|en|zakat|bor=1}}
* {{desc|es|azaque|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|zakati|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tk|zekat|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|tt|зәкәт|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Ahrens-Christliches|part=1|page=21}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel-V|page=23}}
* {{R:ar:Garosi:2022a|page=412}}
* {{R:ar:Jeffery-Foreign|page=153}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=25}}, not acquainted with the newer Aramaic attestation situation favours a native development in Muḥammad’s tongue
* {{R:ar:Rudolph|page=60}}
* {{R:ar:Torrey|JFI|page=48, 141}}
* {{R:CAL|zky|V}}, see in particular the DJPA and DCPA entries linked there
-------- end text --------
