Page 9967 زمزريق: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Tree flower dsc00981.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|زَمْزَرِيق}}|upright=1.15]]
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|ar}} etymology. While the ending might be augmented internally in Arabic, as {{m|ar|خَرْبَقَ|t=to rive}}, {{m|ar|جَوْلَق|t=gorse, broom}}, this is not credible for quinqueliterals, the more so with [[syllable weight|heavy last syllable]].

A more regular structure is afforded if one kens the {{bor|ar|ira-mid}} adjective suffix {{m|pal||-īk}}, {{der|ar|ira-pro|*-ikah}}, from {{der|ar|ine-pro|*-kos}}; such suspicion is raised by the synonyms {{m|ar|شَزْرِيق|tr=|}} and {{m|ar|خَزْرِيق}}, and {{m|ar|أَرِيج|t=fragrance}}, having no {{w|Semitic root}} derivation.

One can ween a shortening of the otherwise-known dendronym reflected in Arabic as {{m|ar|أَرْجُوَان|t=redbud}} put into an [[ezafe|izāfa]] with another word now irretrievable in Arabic, having been borrowed in an izafet-compound comparatively early and then reinterpreted multiply, owing to its being of [[cranberry morpheme|of no meaning]] to Semites.

Potential sources of contamination appear {{m|ar|زَمْهَر|t=bloodshot eyes, angry eyes}}, perhaps in reference to color; bolstered by {{m|ar|خَزِرَ|tr=|t=to squint, to contract one's eyes}} and {{m|ar|شَزَرَ|t=to give a shifty look, to glance with hatred in one's eyes}}, and {{m|ar|زَرَق|tr=|t=blindness; the color blue}} or {{der|ar|arc|זרג|tr=zāreḡ|t=eyes shining, glistening; pale red wine or amethyst color}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|زَمْزَرِيق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|زَمْزَرِيق|m}}

# [[redbud]] ({{taxfmt|Cercis|genus}})
#: {{syn|ar|أُرْجُوَان|خَزْرِيق|شَزْرِيق}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|زَمْزَرِيق|m}}

{{C|ar|Caesalpinia subfamily plants}}
-------- end text --------
