Page 9989 زنبوع: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Babloos Naranga IMG 4329.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|}}|upright=1.2]]

===Etymology===
First attested in Ibn al-ʿawwām. Originally treated as a {{bor|ar|ber|-}} borrowing, but the Berber forms have also been considered Arabisms, then correspondingly the same for the term {{m|ar|زَنْبُوج|t=olive}}. Steiger constructs a native origin arguing that the term is progressively sonorized from {{m|ar|زَنْبُوح}} and is via an intermediate {{m|ar||*زُنْحُوب}} from {{m|ar|حمبزان|حُنْزُوب|t=''[[Emex]]''}}, while the form {{m|ar|زَنْبَاع}} would be via a {{m|ar||*زِنْبَاح}} from {{m|ar|حِنْزَاب}}, also deeming the same term present in {{cog|ca|alambó}}, {{m|ca|alambor|t=bitter orange}}, ultimately explaining all as from the transparent {{m|ar|حُمَّاض}}, vulgarly {{m|ar|حَمَّاض|t=sorrel}}. Corriente and Aubaile-Sallenave derive it from the well-known term for the rose-apple via its descendant in {{bor|ar|ms|jambua}}, {{m|ms|jambuwa}}, although that wanderwort appears only very recently as {{doublet|ar|بَامْبُوزِيَا|notext=1}} and see there for other forms, and the latter author accounts for the difference in the first consonant by mentioning the variation between {{m|ar|جَدْوَار}} and {{m|ar|زَدْوَار|t=zedoary}}, although this variation probably has its root in Persian.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|زَنْبُوع}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|زَنْبُوع|head2=زُنْبُوع|m|sing=زَنْبُوعَة|sing2=زُنْبُوعَة|pl=زَنَابِيع}}

# [[pomelo]] ({{taxlink|Citrus grandis|species}} syn. {{taxfmt|Citrus maxima|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|بُومَلِي|q2=Syria|أَبُو مِيلُو}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|7|29|volume=1|page=319|passage=ويستسلف منه في الظروف علي ما تقدم وقد يكون له وللنارنج واللامون والزنبوع|translation=This borrowing process as described above fits for it as it fits oranges, lemons, and pomelos}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|زَنْبُوع|head2=زُنْبُوع|pl=زَنَابِيع}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|زَنْبَاع|t=grapefruit (''[[Citrus paradisi]]'')}}

====Descendants====
