Page 10025 زوج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*yewg-}}
From {{bor|ar|arc|זוגא|t=yoke, pair|tr=zawgā}}, from {{der|ar|grc|ζεῦγος|t=yoke}} which was used in Greek for the yoke of marriage – now it forms a root {{ar-root|ز|و|ج}}.
{{ar-rootbox|ز و ج}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|زَوْج}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-زوج.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|زَوْج|m|pl=أَزْوَاج|d=زَوْجَان}}

# one of a [[pair]]
# [[spouse]], [[mate]], [[partner]]
## [[husband]]
##: {{synonyms|ar|بَعْل}}
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|58|1
|passage=قَدْ سَمِعَ ٱللَّٰهُ قَوْلَ ٱلَّتِي تُجَادِلُكَ فِي '''زَوْجِهَا''' وَتَشْتَكِي إِلَى ٱللَّٰهِ وَٱللَّٰهُ يَسْمَعُ تَحَاوُرَكُمَا إِنَّ ٱللَّٰهَ سَمِيعٌ بَصِيرٌ
|translation=God has certainly heard the speech of her who pleads with you about her '''husband''' and complains to God. God hears the conversation between the two of you.}}
## {{lb|ar|feminine}} [[wife]]
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|20|117
|passage=فَقُلْنَا يَا آدَمُ إِنَّ هَٰذَا عَدُوٌّ لَّكَ '''وَلِزَوْجِكَ''' فَلَا يُخْرِجَنَّكُمَا مِنَ ٱلْجَنَّةِ فَتَشْقَىٰ
|translation=We said, “O Adam! This is indeed an enemy of yours and your '''mate'''’s. So do not let him expel you from paradise, or you will be miserable.”}}
##: {{synonyms|ar|زَوْجَة|اِمْرَأَة|قَرِينَة}}
# {{lb|ar|often|dual}} a pair or [[couple]]
#: {{ux|ar|هُمَا '''زَوْجَانِ'''|They two are a pair or couple.}}
# {{lb|ar|now|_|rare}} [[kind]], [[type]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|56:4-10
|passage=إِذَا رُجَّتِ الْأَرْضُ رَجًّا وَبُسَّتِ الْجِبَالُ بَسًّا فَكَانَتْ هَبَاءً مُّنْبَثًّا وَكُنتُمْ '''أَزْوَاجًا''' ثَلَاثَةً فَأَصْحَابُ الْمَيْمَنَةِ مَا أَصْحَابُ الْمَيْمَنَةِ وَأَصْحَابُ الْمَشْأَمَةِ مَا أَصْحَابُ الْمَشْأَمَةِ وَالسَّابِقُونَ السَّابِقُونَ
|translation=When the earth is shaken with convulsion / And the mountains are crushed, crumbling / And become dust dispersing / And ye become of three kinds: Then the companions of the right – what are the companions of the right? And the companions of the left – what are the companions of the left? And the forerunners, the forerunners!}}

