===Etymology 2===
{{unk|ar|Disputed}}; either:
* {{root|ar|ine-pro|*gʷeyh₃-}}{{der|ar|pal|*zyw-|tr=zīw|t=life; lifestyle, manner}}, from {{der|ar|ira-pro|*ǰíHwati}}, from {{der|ar|iir-pro|*ǰíHwati}}. Cognate with {{cog|fa|زی|tr=zi-|t=to live}}, {{cog|grc|ζω}}, and {{cog|en|zoo}}; all ultimately from {{der|ar|ine-pro|*gʷíh₃weti|*gʷíh₃woh₂}} (see also {{m|ar|زئبق|tr=ziʔbaq|t=mercury}} for the same root).
* {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*zwy-|t=to contract or pull tight, to tie on garb, to equip or supply what is needed, to outfit or furnish, to fit or fasten something on, to deck or adorn, to dress up or decorate, one's appearance or what is displayed}}. Bi-consonantal pair found in related roots like {{cog|arc|זיו|tr=ziw|t=appearance}}, {{cog|akk|𒍣𒄿𒈬|tr=zīmu, zīwu|t=appearance, looks}}, {{cog|akk|𒍝𒈾𒉡|tr=zanānu|t=to provide, to furnish, to outfit}}, {{cog|he|זִו|tr=ziv|t=a spring month; month where trees are adorned with blossoms}}, {{m|ar|زَوَى|tr=zawā|t=to wrinkle, to contract}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|زِيّ|m|pl=أَزْيَاء}}

# [[costume]], [[uniform]], [[suit]], [[dress]]
# {{lb|ar|in the plural}} [[fashion]], [[vogue]]

