Page 10067 س: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From [[Nabataean]] {{m|arc|𐢝|tr=š}}, from {{der|ar|syc|ܫ|tr=š}}, from {{der|ar|arc|ש‬|tr=š}}, from [[Imperial Aramaic]] {{m|arc|𐡔|tr=š}}, from the [[Egyptian]] {{m|arc|𓌒}}.

{{collapse|title=Further information
|content=
This letter stood for {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} in Aramaic. {{m|arc|𐢖|tr=-}} was not adopted into the Arabic alphabet because of the following considerations:

Proto-Semitic has three [[fricative]]s that became [[sibilant]]s in descendant languages: ''ś'', ''š'', ''s''. In Arabic ''ś'' gave {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}}, but ''š'' and ''s'' merged to {{IPAchar|/s/}}. In Old Aramaic all three sibilants were distinguished, and ''s'' was represented by {{m|arc|𐢖|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|ס‬|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|𐡎|tr=-}} while {{m|arc|𐢝|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|ש‬|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|𐡔|tr=-}} represented both ''ś'' and ''š''. This orthography persisted in later Aramaic even to the time of the [[Nabataean]]s, when the pronunciation of ''ś'' merged with that of ''s'' {{IPAchar|/s/}}.

So when a scribe wanted to write the Arabic sound {{IPAchar|/ʃ/}} from ''ś'', he did so by using {{m|arc|𐢝|tr=-}} / {{m-self|ar|س|tr=-}} purposefully in order to stick to a letter form that looks the same in the cognate Aramaic words. But when he wanted to write an Arabic sound /s/ from Proto-Semitic ''š'', he would defy the Aramaic spelling for this Proto-Semitic phoneme were he to represent this Arabic phoneme by the sign {{m|arc|𐢖|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|ס‬|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|𐡎|tr=-}}, whereas Arabic-Aramaic word pairs with the Proto-Semitic ''s'' are – somewhat by coincidence – rare and there was hence only negligible pressure to employ {{m|arc|𐢖|tr=-}} / {{m|syc|ܣ|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|ס|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|𐡎|tr=-}}, in total. So the impression was that {{m|arc|𐢝|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|ש‬|tr=-}} / {{m|arc|𐡔|tr=-}} / {{m-self|ar|س|tr=-}} is the most typical sign to write /s/ while the other possible sign fell out of use.
}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/siːn/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/s/}}

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|head='''س '''/''' س‍ '''/''' ‍س‍ '''/''' ‍س'''|tr=sīn}}

# The twelfth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ز}} and followed by {{l|ar|ش}}.
