Page 10156 ساجور: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܣܳܓܽܘܪܳܐ|tr=sāgūrā|t=enclosure; chain for the neck}}. The Syriac is
# either from {{m|syc|ܣܓܰܪ|tr=sgar|t=to close, to shut up}} which possibly corresponds to {{cog|ar|شَجَرَ|t=to tie up}}
# or from {{der|ar|akk|𒄑𒋛𒃻|ts=sigaru, šigaru|t=neckstock, wooden collar}} from {{der|ar|sux|𒄑𒋛𒃻|ts=sigaru|t=lock}} if the {{cog|sux|-}} is not from {{der|ar|akk|-}}, whence also the hapax {{cog|he|סוּגַר|tr=sūgar|t=neckstock}} Ezek 19:9 is said to be, which could however also be from {{cog|he|סָגַר|tr=sāgar|t=to close, to shut up}} which corresponds to {{cog|arc|סְגַר}} / {{m|syc|ܣܓܰܪ|tr=sgar|t=to close, to shut up}} and possibly {{cog|ar|شَجَرَ|t=to tie up}}. Compare {{cog|he|סָגוּר|tr=sāgūr}} Job 41:7; it is conceivable that
## only {{cog|he|סוּגַר|tr=sūgar|t=neckstock}} Ezek 19:9 is borrowed while the forms ''sāgūr'' are native Northwest Semitic or
## {{cog|he|סוּגַר|tr=sūgar|t=neckstock}} Ezek 19:9 is a misspelling of {{cog|he|סָגוּר|tr=sāgūr}} and all the Hebrew is native
## {{cog|he|סוּגַר|tr=sūgar|t=neckstock}} Ezek 19:9 is a misspelled {{m|he||*סִיגַר|tr=*sīgar}} borrowed from Akkadian and the forms ''sāgūr'' are native Northwest Semitic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَاجُور}}

===Noun===
