Page 10172 سادن: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar|سادن (اسم)}}
{{wp|lang=ar|سدانة الكعبة}}

===Etymology===
Formally {{ar-active participle|lc=1}} {{m|ar|سَدَنَ|t=to serve, to act as a chamberlain for}}, although the meaning of this verb seems denominal. Apparently cognate to {{cog|arc-hat|𐣴𐣣𐣭𐣭𐣠|tr=šdnʾ|t=overseer}}. The vowel variation in {{m|ar|سَدْن}}, {{m|ar|سِدْن}}, {{m|ar|سَدَن}}, {{m|ar|سَدَان|t=curtain, veil}} may point to an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing of a meaning of covering and unveiling, but it may also be not related to an idea of keeping something behind a veil, for {{m|ar|سَدَنَ}} also means “to let down” like {{m|ar|سَدَلَ}}, to which also {{m|ar|سِدْل}}, {{m|ar|سُدْل|t=curtain, veil}}, so that the office may be “someone who lets people go down or lets them loose”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَادِن}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَادِن|m|pl=سَدَنَة}}

# [[keeper]], [[doorholder]], [[curator]], [[chamberlain]], [[sacristan]], [[saden]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَادِن|pl=سَدَنَة}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=1335}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|page=470}}
* {{R:CAL|šdn|N}}
* {{R:sem:DNWSI|pages=1111–1112}}

{{C|ar|Occupations}}
-------- end text --------
