Page 10187 ساعة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
According to Nöldeke, {{m+|ar|سَاعَة}} and {{cog|gez|ሰዓት}}, {{m|gez|ሳዐት}} are borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|שָׁעְתָא}} / {{m|syc|ܫܳܥܬܳܐ|tr=šāʿəṯā}}. Leslau does not dispute this. Compare {{cog|he|שָׁעָה|tr=šāʿā́}} and {{cog|gdq|سات}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَاعَة}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-ساعة.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَاعَة|f|pl=سَاعَات|pl2=سَاع}}

# [[hour]] {{gloss|unit of time}}
# short [[time]], a [[while]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|34
|passage=فَإِذَا جَاءَ أَجَلُهُمْ لَا يَسْتَأْخِرُونَ سَاعَةً وَلَا يَسْتَقْدِمُونَ
|translation=There is a [preordained] time for every nation: when their time comes, they shall not defer it by a '''single hour''' nor shall they advance it.}}
# [[timepiece]], [[clock]], [[watch]]
# {{lb|ar|with the definite article|Islam}} [[judgement day]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|79|42
|passage=يَسْأَلُونَكَ عَنِ السَّاعَةِ أَيَّانَ مُرْسَاهَا
|translation=They ask you concerning the '''Hour''', “When will it set in?"}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَاعَة|pl=سَاعَات|pl2=سَاع}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|صَلَاة السَّاعَات الْكَبِيرَة}}

====Descendants====
{{top4}}
* {{desc|mt|siegħa}}
* {{desc|arz|ساعة|tr=sāʕa}}
* {{desc|ary|ساعة|tr=sāʕa}}
* {{desc|abq|сахӏат|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ab|асааҭ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ady|сыхьат|bor=1}}
* {{desc|av|сагӏат|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ce|сахьт|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ha|sa'a|bor=1}}
** {{desc|bor=1|yo|sáà|سَا}}
* {{desc|id|saat|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|kdr|саат|tr=saat}}
* {{desc|lsd|סאעא|tr=sāʕa|bor=1}}
* {{desc|lt|sahatas|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|ms|saat|ساعت}}
* {{desc|axm|սահաթ|bor=1}}
** {{desc|hy|սահաթ}}
* {{desc|os|сахат|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|fa-cls|ساعت|tr=sā'at|bor=1}}
* {{desc|so|saacad|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|sw|saa|bor=1}}
* {{desc|wo|saa|bor=1}}
{{bottom}}

