{{ar-decl-noun|سَبَطَانَة|pl=sfp}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ca|bor=1|sarabatana|sarbatana}}
* {{desc|fr|bor=1|sarbacane|alts=1}}
* {{desc|it|bor=1|cerbottana}}
* {{desc|pt|bor=1|zarabatana|alts=1}}
* {{desc|es|bor=1|cerbatana}}

===References===
* {{R:DAAL|page=257|entry=cerbatana}}, where they do not know the Malay origin and claim an influence of South Arabian variants of {{cog|sem-pro|*šabaṭ-|t=to beat}}, which is semantically and chronologically unlikely. Note that they do not have this word in the Andalusi dictionary {{R:xaa:ELA|II}}, which is another sign that this is borrowed later and from farther east.
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=223|entry=زبطانة}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=278}}
