Page 10310 سجد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|ar|arc|סְגִד|t=to bow down in respect}}, likely via or at least semantically influenced by {{bor|ar|syc|ܣܓܶܕ|tr=sg̱ed|t=}}, developing further in Arabic as the root {{ar-root|س|ج|د}}. See the cognate {{cog|he|סגד|tr=sagád}}.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:سُجُود}}

# to [[prostrate]] oneself, to [[bow down]] {{+obj|ar|:لِ<to>}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|22|18|passage=أَلَمْ تَرَ أَنَّ اللَّهَ '''يَسْجُدُ''' لَهُ مَنْ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ وَمَنْ فِي الْأَرْضِ|t=Do you not see [i.e., know] that to Allah '''prostrates''' whoever is in the heavens and whoever is on the earth [...]?}}
# to [[pay]] [[respect]], to [[honor]], to [[salute]]
# to [[bend]], to [[incline]], to [[lower]], especially a [[head]]
# {{lb|ar|dialect|[[w:Tayy|Ṭayy’]]}} to [[stand]], to [[stand]] [[tall]] or [[erect]]; possibly an extended sense, to be [[still]], to [[stand]] [[reverent]]ly, to [[stand]] [[before]] in [[homage]]

