Page 10320 سجنجل: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Palácio da Ajuda - Sala D. Luís 03.png|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|سَجَنْجَل}}]]

===Etymology===
Manfred Ullmann expounded in an analysis of the occurrences that all known poets who use this word after {{w|Imru' al-Qais}} owe it to him, and using it as “round mirror” they actually misunderstood him, who in his verse actually meant sheeny papyrus leaves, forming a {{m|ar||*سِجِلْجِل}}, {{m|ar||*سَجَلْجَل}} after the known {{m|ar|سِجِلّ|t=scroll}} which was dissimilated to {{m-self|ar|سَجَنْجَل}}; only thus far it is a {{der|ar|gkm|-}} word as it was believed in the Middle Ages to be {{m|ar|رُومِيّ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَجَنْجَل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَجَنْجَل|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete|poetic}}

# [[mirror]], [[looking-glass]]
#: {{syn|ar|مِرْآة|q1=the normal word|مَاوِيَّة|q2=poetic|مِنْظَرَة|q3=dialect|}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 965|author={{w|Al-Mutanabbi|{{l|ar||الْمُتَنَبِّي}}}}|title=[https://www.aldiwan.net/poem10111.html {{lang|ar|وَمَنزِلٍ لَيسَ لَنا بِمَنزِلِ (…)}}]
|passage=لَهُ إِذَا أَدْبَرَ لَحْظُ المُقْبِلِ / كَأَنَّمَا يَنْظُرُ مِن سَجَنْجَلِ
|translation=For it, when a look of what follows turns its back / It is as though one saw by a mirror.
|subst=لَهُ/لَ-هُو}}
# [[glossy]] [[papyrus]], [[page]]s or [[sheets]] with a [[shine]] or [[glaze]], [[glisten]]ing [[surface]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=6th century {{CE}}|author={{w|Imru' al-Qais|{{l|ar||اِمْرُؤ ٱلْقَيْس}}}}|title=Stop, Let Us Weep {{l|ar||قِفَا نَبْكِ}}
|passage=مُهَفْهَفَةٌ بَيْضَاءُ غَيْرُ مُفَاضَةٍ / تَرَائِبُهَا مَصْقُولَةٌ كَٱلسَّجَنْجَلِ
|translation=Slender, fair-colored, not obese / Her collar bone gleaming like the glossy page.}}

