===Etymology 2===
{{unk|ar}}, possible an invented word on the basis of {{m|ar|سِجْن}} and analogical to {{m|ar|عليون|عِلِّيِّين}}, compare also {{m|ar|سَجَنْجَل}}; the definition given by the Qurʔān itself as {{m|ar||كِتَابٌ مَرْقُومٌ}} may even be due to [[glossema]].

====Noun====
{{ar-proper noun|سِجِّين|m}}

# {{def-uncertain|ar}} {{ant|ar|عِلِّيُون}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|83|7-9|passage=كَلَّا إِنَّ كِتَابَ الْفُجَّارِ لَفِي '''سِجِّينٍ''' / وَمَا أَدْرَاكَ مَا '''سِجِّينٌ''' / كِتَابٌ مَّرْقُومٌ|t=
No! Indeed, the record of the wicked is in sijjeen. And what can make you know what is sijjeen? It is [their destination recorded in] a register inscribed.}}
## the [[Underworld]], a [[bottomless pit]], an infernal prison, [[Hades]], [[Sheol]], the [[abyss]], often decipted under the seven Earths.
##: {{syn|ar|هَاوِيَة|شَاؤُول|هَادِيس|الْعَالَمُ السُّفْلِيِ}}
## the [[Hell]]
##: {{syn|ar|سَعِير|لَظَىٰ|النَّار|جَهَنَّم|جَحِيم|حُطَمَة|سَقَر}}
### The lowest hellhole in the Hell
###: {{syn|ar|دَرْك}}
## the seventh Earth
## the record of the wicked
## an intensive/diminutive form of {{m|ar|سِجْن|t=prison}}

