Page 10334 سحلية: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Root consonants {{ar-root|س|ح|ل}}, but that forms meanings related to “scraping off”. Left unmentioned by Classical Arabic dictionaries. Only used in the [[Mashreq]], as opposed to {{noncog|ber|-}}-borrowed {{m|ar|زَلْمُومِيَّة}}, {{m|ar|زَرْمُومِيَّة}} ruling the [[Maghreb]], in addition to Levantine {{m|ar|حِرْذَوْن}}. Apparently traditional Arabic lizard names are just {{m|ar|ضَبّ}} and {{m|ar|عَظَاءَة}}, while {{m|ar|سِحْلِيَّة}} is another {{bor|ar|arc|-}} term terminating in ''-īṯā'', see {{m|ar|حِسْل|t=young of a spiny-tailed lizard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سِحْلِيَّة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سِحْلِيَّة|f|pl=سَحَالٍ}}

# [[lizard]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سِحْلِيَّة|pl=سَحَالٍ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:BehnstedtWoidich|WA2|pages=361–363}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|سحل}}

{{C|ar|Lizards}}

-------- end text --------
