Page 10347 سخل: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar|سخلة}}

===Etymology===
As in some Bedouin dialects also with the first consonant emphatic ({{m|ar|صَحَل}}, maybe from {{der|ar|sa|छागल}}, {{m|sa|छाग|t=goat}}, but in an original meaning of a newborn kid, with the meanings of “imperfect” dates or anything imperfect transferred, and from the brutal process of birth a denominal verb “taking or driving out by force”; though Freytag compares to {{m|ar|خَسَلَ|t=to reject, to cast out}}, {{m|ar|خُسَّل|t=debile, vile}}, which he relates further to {{m|ar|حِسْل|t=young of a spiny tailed lizard}}, {{m|ar|حَسِيل|t=bull calves; flock of cows}}, {{m|ar|حَسَلَ|t=to propel vehemently}}, which also contains a shape {{m|ar|حُسَالَة|t=rejected or filed off things; dregs}} mirroring {{m|ar|سُخَالَة|t=rejected parts of things}}, over which he leads us to well-known {{m|ar|حُثَالَة|t=dregs, refuse of any crop}}, {{cog|tmr|מַתְחֲלָא|tr=maṯḥălā|t=calyx surrounding the date in its early state, or spathe of a date-palm}}, {{cog|grc|μᾰσχᾰ́λη|t=axil, hollow at the base of a shoot; branch, young palm twig}}. In view of {{ar-root|خ ث ث|nocat=1}} there could be an original biconsonantal base.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَخْل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|سَخْل|sing=سَخْلَة|pl=سِخَال|pl2=سُخْلَان|pl3=سِخَلَة}}

# [[offspring]] of a [[sheep]] or (more widely) a [[goat]]; [[lamb]] or [[kid]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|abudawud|1|142|passage=بَيْنَا نَحْنُ مَعَ رَسُولِ ٱللّٰهِ صَلَّى ٱللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جُلُوسٌ إِذْ دَفَعَ الرَّاعِي غَنَمَهُ إِلَى الْمُرَاحِ وَمَعَهُ '''سَخْلَةٌ''' تَيْعَرُ|t=We were sitting in the company of the Messenger of God (PBUH) when we saw that a shepherd was driving a herd of sheep to their fold. He had with him a '''newly-born lamb''' that was crying.|subst=وَمَعَهُ/وَ-مَعَ-هُو}}
# {{lb|ar|Iraq|Khuzistan}} [[goat]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَخْل|pl=سِخَال|pl2=سُخْلَان|pl3=سِخَلَة}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.vn:سَخْل}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# to [[repel]], to [[drive away]], to [[banish]]
# to take by [[deceit]] or by [[seizure]]

====Conjugation====
