===Etymology 2===
[[File:Cyperus eragrostis Parque Nacional La Campana 01.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|سُعْد}}]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}
From {{bor|ar|arc|סוּעֲדָא}} / {{m|syc|ܣܘܼܥܕܵܐ|tr=suʿdā}}, {{m|syc|ܣܸܥܕܵܐ|tr=seʿdā|t=sedge (''[[Cyperus]]'')}}, a match too similar for such an unspecific grass to represent cognateship, denoting plants more native to the [[Fertile Crescent]]; compare the other borrowing of a name for {{taxfmt|Cyperus|genus}} sedges {{m|ar|كُولَان}}. A derivation from the root cognate to {{ar-root|س|ع|د}} meaning “prosperity” also with the sense of “moist soil”, “a land that is naturally watered”; sedge being a plant often associated with wetlands. From this root also in {{cog|akk|𒄑𒋆𒌋𒌋𒁺|tr=suādu|t=an aromatic plant; {{taxfmt|Cyperus|genus}}}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سُعْد}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سُعْد|m}}

# [[sedge]] ({{taxfmt|Cyperus|genus}})

