===Etymology 3.1===
Terminology of the religious sphere, borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|סִפְרָא|tr=sip̱rā|t=writing, book}} / {{m|syc|ܣܷܦܪܴܐ|tr=sep̱rā|t=writing, book}}; compare {{cog|hbo|סֵפֶר|tr=sḗp̄er|t=writing, book}}. Ultimately from {{der|ar|akk|šiprum|𒅆𒅁𒀸|tr=šiprum}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سِفْر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سِفْر|m|pl=أَسْفَار}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|سَفَرَ|form=I|t=to copy, to write}}
# [[written]] [[book]]
#: {{syn|ar|كِتَاب}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|62|5|passage=مَثَلُ الَّذِينَ حُمِّلُوا التَّوْرَاةَ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَحْمِلُوهَا كَمَثَلِ الْحِمَارِ يَحْمِلُ '''أَسْفَارًا'''|t=The example of those who were entrusted with the Torah and then did not take it on is like that of a donkey who carries '''volumes of books'''.}}
# {{lb|ar|Christianity|Judaism}} a [[book]] of the [[Bible]]
#: {{uxi|ar|سِفْرُ ٱلْمُلُوكِ ٱلْأَوَّلُ|the [[w:Books of Kings|First Book of Kings]]}}
# {{tlb|ar|archaic}} [[trace]], [[mark]], [[writing]]

