{{bor+|ar|syc|ܣܘܿܦܝܺܣܛܳܐ|tr=sōpisṭā|t=sophist}} or its [[nisba]] derivation {{m|syc|ܣܘܿܦܝܺܣܛܳܝܳܐ|tr=sōp̄isṭāyā|t=sophistic}} from {{der|ar|grc|σοφιστής}} and {{suf|ar||ـَاء|pos2=feminine ending, sometimes for Aramaic [[emphatic state]]|ـِيّ|id3=nisba|pos3=[[nisba]], expresses relation or pertinence}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَفْسَطَائِيّ}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj-sound|سَفْسَطَائِيّ}}

# [[sophist]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|سَفْسَطَائِيّ|pl=sp}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun-sound|سَفْسَطَائِيّ|m}}

# [[sophist]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|سَفْسَطَائِيّ|pl=sp}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَطِيّ|t=sophist}}
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَطَة|t=sophism, sophistic philosophers}}
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَطَ|t=to deliver a specious argument}}
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَطَائِيّة|t=sophism, sophistic philosophers}}
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَاف|t=inane speech; inane}}
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَفَة|t=loquacity, vanity, demagoguery}}
* {{l|ar|سَفْسَفَ|t=to blather}}

