Page 10504 سقنقور: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}
[[File:Scincus scincus.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|سَقَنْقُور}} – {{taxlink|Scincus scincus|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|صَقَنْقُور|إِسْقَنْقُور|إِصْقَنْقُور}}

===Etymology===
Sometimes claimed to be borrowed from {{cog|grc|-}} during the {{w|Graeco-Arabic translation movement|science translation movement}}, but a fitting form is never given, {{cog|gkm||**σκιγκούριον}}, an extension of {{m|grc|σκίγγος|σκίγκος|t=skink}}, as if containing {{m|grc|οὐρά|t=tail}}, is not found. This word is obtained in the same period as {{bor|ar|syc|ܣܩܝܢܩܘܪ|tr=sqinqūr}}, possibly evidenced by the resolution of a geminate stop, to a nasal plus a stop, common in {{cog|sem}}, but particularly {{cog|arc|-}}. It would then ultimately have relation to {{der|ar|akk|𒆲𒁯|tr=KUN.DAR|ts=šakkadirru, šakkatirru|t=skink|lit=mongoose of the forest}}, originally applied to another relatable creature, but again listed separately as a type of lizard as well.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَقَنْقُور}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَقَنْقُور|m}}

# [[skink]] ({{taxfmt|Scincus|genus}} gen. et spp.)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَقَنْقُور}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|he|סקנקור|bor=1}} {{q|Medieval}}
* {{desc|bor=1|fa|سقنقور|tr=saqanqur|اسقنقور|tr2=esqanqur}}
* {{desc|ota|سقنقور|tr=sakankur|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|sqwnqr|N}}
* {{R:TMN|volume=III|pages=258–259}}
* {{R:akk:Landsberger-Fauna|page=118}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Lurche|pages=142–144}}
* {{cite-book|last=Seetzen|authorlink=de:Ulrich Jasper Seetzen|year=1805|year_published=1855|editor={{w|lang=de|Friedrich Karl Hermann Kruse}}|first=Ulrich Jasper|location=Berlin|publisher=G. Reimer|title=Reisen durch Syrien, Palästina, Phönicien, die Transjordan-Länder, Arabia Petraea und Unter-Aegypten|volume=3|url=https://archive.org/details/ulrichjaspersee02seetgoog/page/n6/mode/2up|page=501|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/ulrichjaspersee02seetgoog/page/n519/mode/2up}}, where {{l|ar||إِسْتَنْقُور}}
