===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|سِكِّينَة}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|סכינא|tr=sakkīnā}}, from {{der|ar|akk|sikkānum|𒄑𒍣𒃶|tr=sikkānum|t=oar, steering paddle, rudder blade}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒄑𒍣𒃶|tr={{sup|g̃eš}}zi-gan|ts=zigan|t=oar, steering paddle, rudder blade}}. This is related to or possibly conflated with the Semitic {{ar-root|س|ك|ن}} meaning to stay in place, to be held at rest, and with the {{cog|akk|sikkatum|𒄑𒆕|tr=sikkatum|t=peg, nail, a lock or pin broach, cone, wedge, pyramid, pinnacle, plowshare}}, a source attested also in {{cog|ar|سَكّ|tr=|t=pin, peg, nail, stake, wedge, plowshare}}; cognate with {{cog|syc|ܣܰܟܺܝܢܳܐ|tr=sakkīnā}} and {{cog|he|סַכִּין|tr=sakkī́n}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سِكِّين}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-سكين.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سِكِّين|m|g2=f|pl=سَكَاكِين}}

# [[knife]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سِكِّين|pl=سَكَاكِين}}

