Page 10572 سلحفاة: -------- begin text --------
[[File:سلحفاة.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|سُلَحْفَاة}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
Probably derived from an [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only witnessed by borrowings|unattested]] {{bor|ar|arc|-}} form akin to {{cog|syc|ܣܠܘܦܝܬܐ|tr=sallōp̄īṯā}}, {{cog|he|שַׁלְחוּפָה|tr=šalḥūp̄ā|t=tortoise}}, from {{der|ar|akk|šeleppûm|𒃻𒅮𒈾|tr=šeleppûm|t=turtle, snake; a shell, egg, canister}}. Distortion of the Akkadian form in either Aramaic or Arabic after native roots such as {{ar-root|س ل ح|nocat=1}}, {{ar-root|س ل خ|nocat=1}}, and {{ar-root|ز ح ل|nocat=1}} is likely, as with many terms for organisms encountered only at special occasions (see exemplarily {{cog|ru|берескле́т|t=spindle tree}}); Arabic vernaculars offer forms like {{m|ar|سُحَلْفَاة}}, {{m|ar|زُلَحْفَاة}}, {{m|ar|زَحَلْفَة}} and {{m|ar|زِلَحْفَة}}. Compare the variants of {{m|ar|سَرَطَان|t=crab}} for a similar case.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سُلَحْفَاة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سُلَحْفَاة|f|pl=سَلَاحِف}}

# [[turtle]]
# {{ellipsis of|ar|سُلَحْفَاة بَرِّيَّة|t=[[tortoise]]|nocap=1}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سُلَحْفَاة|pl=سَلَاحِف}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|gdq|salefḥōt|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{pedia|lang=ar}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=2|pages=265–266 Nr. 202}}, tends towards cognateship, however deems the Syriac likely borrowed from Akkadian and the Mehri an Arabism (not considering the etymon of the Arabic just being lost, oddly also not mentioning the Hebrew form).
* {{R:ar:Siddiqi|pages=72}} interprets as {{cog|fa|سولاخ|tr=sulâx}} ~ {{m|fa|سوراخ|tr=surâx|t=hole opening}} + {{m|fa|پا|tr=pâ|t=foot}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=586}}

{{C|ar|Turtles}}

-------- end text --------
