Page 10575 سلسبيل: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=en|Salsabil (Quran)|mul=Salsabil (fountain)}}

===Etymology===
Probably an [[Elistic|elistic]] name of {{bor|ar|arc|-}} and ultimately {{der|ar|akk|-}} origin.<ref>{{R:syc:Kessler:1889|page=17|preface=1}}</ref> For metrical considerations it could still have [[tanwin|tanwīn]] in spite of being, as a proper noun, [[diptote]].<ref>{{cite-web|last=Drißner|first=Gerald|work=Arabic for Nerds|title=The Qur’an Revisited: Sura 76:18|url=https://arabic-for-nerds.com/islam/the-quran-revisited/sura-76-18/|date=20-03-2024}}</ref>

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَلْسَبِيل}}

[[File:Getty Villa - Grotto.jpg|thumb|ar|{{l|ar||سَلْسَبِيلٌ}}<small><br/>More is depicted on the Wikipedia article linked above and Volait 2021.</small><ref>A modern interpretation is depicted in {{cite-book|last=Volait|first=Mercedes|title=Antique Dealing and Creative Reuse in Cairo and Damascus 1850-1890: Intercultural Engagements with Architecture and Craft in the Age of Travel and Reform|year=2021|publisher=Brill|location=Leiden|chapter=3: Conflicted Commodification in Cairo|authorlink=fr:Mercedes Volait|url=https://www.jstor.org/stable/10.1163/j.ctv1v7zbh3.8|doi=10.1163/9789004449886_005|isbn=978-90-04-47070-5|pages=99–100, figure 69}}</ref>|upright=1.15]]
