Page 10591 سلق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|س ل ق}}
Cognate with {{cog|arc|שְׁלַק}} / {{m|syc|ܫܠܰܩ|tr=‍šlaq|t=to boil}}, whereas {{sl|ar|gez|ተሳለቀ|t=to scoff at|notext=1}} is unrelated but the source of the Qurʾānic use for verbal “bashing” and related by metathesis to the {{cog|uga|𐎖𐎍𐎕|t=to scorn}}, {{cog|he|קִלֵּס|tr=qilles|t=to mock}}, dialectal {{cog|ar|قَلَّسَ|t=to mock}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:سَلْق}}

# to [[thrust]], to [[prostrate]], to [[pierce]], to [[push]], to [[repel]]
# to [[hurt]], to [[gall]], to [[flay]], to [[lash]], to [[assault]]
## to [[hurt]] [[verbal]]ly, to [[taunt]]
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|33|19|passage=فَإِذَا جَاءَ الْخَوْفُ رَأَيْتَهُمْ يَنْظُرُونَ إِلَيْكَ تَدُورُ أَعْيُنُهُمْ كَالَّذِي يُغْشَىٰ عَلَيْهِ مِنَ الْمَوْت فَإِذَا ذَهَبَ الْخَوْفُ '''سَلَقُو'''كُم بِأَلْسِنَةٍ حِدَادٍ|t=And when fear comes, you see them looking at you, their eyes revolving of he who to whom death comes. But when fear departs, they '''lash''' you with sharp tongues}}
# to [[boil]] without [[adding]] any [[seasoning]]
# to [[remove]] animal's [[feathers]] (by [[boiling]] it)
# to [[enkindle]], to [[ignite]]
# to [[climb]] (a wall, etc)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:سَلْق}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سَلْق|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|سَلَقَ|form=I}}
#* {{RQ:Najib ad-Din Samarqandi:2017|page=166|passage=وأمّا الغَوشَنة فهي قريبة من الكمأة باردة رطبة وهي أقلّ بردًا وأصلح، وفيها بورقية وملوحة تفارقها عند ال'''سلق''' ويصلحها ال'''سلق'''. وليس له من الغلظ واللزوجة ورداءة الخلط ما الكمأة وهي تؤكل بالحموضات ولَذَّته كلَذَّة الغضاريف.|t=In what bespeaks the morel, it is near truffles, cold and wet, and in it less cold and more healthy, and it has a basicity and acidity that parts it on '''seething''', so '''seething''' betters it. And it hasn’t the coarseness and stickiness and badness for the humour which a truffle has and it is eaten with sour things and its sensory delectability is like the sensory delectability of cartilage.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَلْق}}

===Etymology 2===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܣܠܩܐ|tr=silqā, selqā}}, from {{der|ar|arc|סילקא}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|grc|Σικελικός|σικελικόν|tr=|lit=the Sicilian one}}; cognate with {{cog|akk-nbb|𒌑𒋛𒅋𒋡|ts=silqu}} itself a loan word from {{cog|arc|-}}, also a {{doublet|ar|شَلْجَم|nocap=1}} through an {{cog|ira|-}} loan.

