{{ar-decl-adj|سَلَم|f=سَلَم|pl=سَلَم|fpl=سَلَم|d=سَلَم:tri|fd=سَلَم:tri}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|arc|סוּלַם|tr=sulam}}, with influence from {{der|ar|he|סולם|סֻלָּם|tr=sullām}} – compare against {{cog|syc|ܣܒܠܬܐ|tr=sebbelṯā}} and {{cog|myz|ࡎࡅࡌࡁࡉࡋࡕࡀ|tr=sumbiltā}} – from {{der|ar|akk|simmiltum|𒄑𒄿𒇻|tr=simmiltum|t=stair; stairs; ladder}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سُلَّم}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-سلم.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سُلَّم|f|g2=m|pl=سَلَالِم}}

# [[ladder]], [[stairs]]
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|6|35|footer=<small>Translates {{w|Marmaduke Pickthall|Pickthall}}</small>|passage=وَإِن كَانَ كَبُرَ عَلَيْكَ إِعْرَاضُهُمْ فَإِنِ ٱسْتَطَعْتَ أَن تَبْتَغِيَ نَفَقًا فِي ٱلْأَرْضِ أَوْ '''سُلَّمًا''' فِي ٱلسَّمَاءِ فَتَأْتِيَهُم بِآيَةٍ|t=And if their aversion is grievous unto thee, then, if thou canst, seek a way down into the earth or a '''ladder''' unto the sky that thou mayst bring unto them a portent (to convince them all)!}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|سُلَّم|pl=سَلَالِم}}

