* {{R:CAL|swlm|N}}
* {{R:ar:Jeffery-Foreign|page=177}}
* {{R:ar:Schwally-Lex.|part=2|page=197}}
* {{cite-journal|de|authorlink=Wolfram von Soden|last=Soden|first=Wolfram von|title=Lexikalisches Archiv|journal={{w|lang=de|Zeitschrift für Assyriologie und verwandte Gebiete}}|volume=41|year=1933|pages=230–231 / Nr. 50|pageurl=https://menadoc.bibliothek.uni-halle.de/dmg/periodical/pageview/115483}}
** Addendum: {{cite-journal|de|authorlink=Benno Landsberger|last=Landsberger|first=Benno|title=Lexikalisches Archiv|journal={{w|lang=de|Zeitschrift für Assyriologie und verwandte Gebiete}}|volume=42|year=1934|page=166|pageurl=https://menadoc.bibliothek.uni-halle.de/dmg/periodical/pageview/115768}}

===Etymology 3===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.ipass.vn:سَلَامَة,سَلَام}}

# to be [[safe]], to be [[well]]
# to be [[free]] (from); to become free (from), to [[escape]] (from)
#* {{ante|965 <small>[[Appendix:Glossary#CE|C.E.]]</small>}}, Al-Mutanabbi
#*: {{quote|ar|لَا '''يَسْلَمُ''' الشَّرَفُ الرَّفِيعُ مِنَ الْأَذَى <br> حَتَّى يُرَاقَ عَلَى جَوَانِبِهِ الدَّمُ}}
#*:: High honor is not spared from harm until blood has been shed at its sides.

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.ipass.vn:سَلَامَة,سَلَام}}

===Etymology 4===
Cognates include {{cog|he|שילם|שלם}} and {{cog|arc|שלם}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[surrender]]
# to [[submit]] to, to be [[submissive]] to; to [[succumb]], to [[yield]] or to [[surrender]] to
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|4|65
|passage=فَلَا وَرَبِّكَ لَا يُؤْمِنُونَ حَتَّى يُحَكِّمُوكَ فِيمَا شَجَرَ بَيْنَهُمْ ثُمَّ لَا يَجِدُوا فِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ حَرَجًا مِمَّا قَضَيْتَ وَ'''يُسَلِّمُوا''' '''تَسْلِيمًا'''
|translation=But nay, by thy Lord, they will not believe until they make thee judge about the dispute arising between them and find between themselves no trammel from what thou rulest and '''submit with whole submission'''.
|subst=فَ/فَ-,وَ/وَ-}}
# to [[greet]] {{qualifier|with {{m|ar|عَلَى}}}}
# to make [[safe]], to keep [[safe]], to [[protect]]
#: {{ux|ar|[[الله يسلِمك|اللّٰهُ '''يُسَلِّمُكَ''']]|you're welcome; may God protect you; get well soon; goodbye (as an answer)|lit=may God '''protect''' you}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|8|43
|passage=إِذْ يُرِيكَهُمُ ٱللَّٰهُ فِي مَنَامِكَ قَلِيلًا ۖ وَلَوْ أَرَاكَهُمْ كَثِيرًا لَّفَشِلْتُمْ وَلَتَنَازَعْتُمْ فِي ٱلْأَمْرِ وَلَٰكِنَّ ٱللَّٰهَ '''سَلَّمَ''' ۗ إِنَّهُ عَلِيمٌ بِذَاتِ ٱلصُّدُورِ
|translation=When God showed them unto thee in thy dream as few, and if he had shown them to thee as many, ye would have dithered and would have made a fuss of the matter, but God '''kept''' you '''safe''' of it, for he knows how the breasts of the people go.
|subst=قَلِيلًا ۖ/قَلِيلًا&#44;,'''سَلَّمَ''' ۗ/'''سَلَّمَ'''&#44;,وَلَوْ/وَ-لَوْ,لَّفَشِلْتُمْ وَلَتَنَازَعْتُمْ/لَّ-فَشِلْتُمْ وَ-لَ-تَنَازَعْتُمْ,وَلَٰكِنَّ/وَ-لَٰكِنَّ,بِذَاتِ/بِ-ذَاتِ}}
# to [[hand over]], to [[deliver]]
#: {{ux|ar|فقالَ لِأتباعِهِ أكثَرَ مِن مَرَّةٍ إنَّهُ سيُسَلَّمُ.|He told his followers more than once that he would be handed over.}}
# to [[admit]], to [[concede]], to [[grant]] {{qualifier|with {{m|ar|ب}}}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 5===
{{ar-rootbox|س ل م}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|سَلِم|m|sing=سَلِمَة}} ''and plural of variety or alternative collective {{m|ar|سِلَام}}''

# {{senseid|ar|stones}} [[stone]]s
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 622|author=[[w:Labīd|{{lang|ar|لَبيد بن ربيعة}}]] [Labīd ibn Rabīʿa]|title=[[s:ar:معلقة لبيد بن ربيعة|{{lang|ar|معلقة}}]] [https://www.sacred-texts.com/isl/arp/arp155.htm Muʻallaqa]|section=[[s:ar:عفتِ الديارُ محلُّها فمُقامُهَا (معلقة)|line 4b]]|passage=١ عَفَتِ الدِّيارُ مَحَلُّهَا فَمُقَامُهَا * بمنًى تأبَّدَ غَوْلُها فَرِجَامُهَا<br/>٢ فمَدافعُ الرَّيَّانِ عُرِّيَ رَسْمُهَا * خَلَقًا كما ضَمِنَ الوُحِيَّ '''سِلاَمُ'''ها<br/>٣ دِمَنٌ تَجَرَّمَ بَعدَ عَهْدِ أنِيسِهَا * حِجَجٌ خَلَوْنَ حَلالُهَا وحَرَامُهَا<br/>٤ رُزِقَتْ مَرابيعَ النُّجُومِ وَصَابَهَا * وَدْقُ الرَّوَاعِدِ جَوْدُهَا فَرِهَامُها<br/>٥ مِنْ كلِّ سَارِيَةٍ وغادٍ مُدْجِنٍ * وَعَشِيَّةٍ مُتجاوبٍ إرْزَامُهَا<br/>٦ فَعَلا فُرُوعُ الأيْهُقَانِ وَأطْفَلَتْ * بالجَلهَتين ظِبَاؤهَا ونَعَامُهَا|t=Effaced are her resting-places where she stayed and settled in Mina: deserted are her camps in Ḡawl and ar-Rijām<br/>and the torrents of ar-Rayyān: the traces thereof are laid bare and are torn, as inscribed '''rocks'''.<br/>Campsites have already passed after their period of use; years of war and peace overcome.<br/>Cast off there fell upon them the rains of spring signs, and there swept sated thunder clouds and drizzling rains<br/>from every cloud of night, every full one of morn, and those of eve, answering like a hoting squawk,<br/>and there sprung shoots of arugula, and in the brinks of a valley the goats and antelopes have youngs.}}

