Page 10605 سلوقي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-etym-nisba|سَلُوق}}, a village in Yemen,<ref>on which not sole ''salūq'' Juynboll ed. ''Lexicon Geographicum'' etc. vol. II 1853 [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Lexicon_geographicum/lNUOAAAAQAAJ?hl=de&gbpv=1&dq=سلوق&pg=PA47&printsec=frontcover page 47]</ref><ref>also mentioned by [https://poetsgate.com/poet.php?pt=2456 the poet] al-Quṭāmiyy, contemporary of the Prophet, in the verse {{lang|ar|مَعَهم ضَوار من سَلوق كأنها     حُصُن تَجولٌ تُجَرَّرُ الأَرْسَانا }}.</ref> according to Arabic tradition, however there are homonymic settlement names to consider,<ref>cf. Juynboll/de Goeje ed. ''Specimen'' etc. 1860 [https://www.google.com/books/edition/Specimen_e_literis_orientalibus_exhibens/q_4XsBXGm5YC?gbpv=1&dq=%D8%B3%D9%84%D9%88%D9%82&pg=PT5&printsec=frontcover p. 26]</ref><ref>cf. {{R:ar:Goeje|M|page=245, antepenultimate line}}</ref><ref>cf. {{RQ:Ibn Batoutah|II|page=303|instead=1}}</ref> including three named {{m|ar|سَلُوقِيَّة}}, {{w|Seleucia on the Tigris}}, {{w|Seleucia in Pieria}}, {{w|Silifke|Seleucia on the Calycadnus}}.
