Page 10608 سليخة: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Gyepi.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|سَلِيخَة}}|upright=1.15]]
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|س ل خ}}; a wanderwort with potential for a native Arabian Peninsula origin, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩪𐩡𐩭𐩩}}, {{cog|akk-nbb|𒋆𒃻𒇷𒄩𒌈|ts=šalīḫātu}} (attested once as plural), {{cog|la|serichatum}} reported by {{w|Pliny the Elder|Plin.}} {{w|Natural History (Pliny)|nat. hist.}} [[s:la:Naturalis Historia/Liber XII#99|XII 99]]. {{cog|syc|ܡܫܠܚܬܐ|tr=mǝšallaḥṯā}} is apparently learnedly formed after Arabic, {{cog|syc|ܣܠܝܟܗ|tr=salīḵā}} is only found in {{w|Bar Hebraeus}} and apparently a logogram of Arabic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَلِيخَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَلِيخَة|f}}

# [[cassia]], {{taxfmt|Cinnamomum cassia|species}} syn. {{taxlink|Cinnamomum aromaticum|species}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَلِيخَة|f}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|gez|ሰሊካ|alts=1|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=339}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=2|page=114}}
* {{cite-journal|de|last=Pincus|first=Siegbert|title=Die Scholien des Barhebraeus zu Exodus|journal=Zeitschrift der Deutschen Morgenländischen Gesellschaft|volume=70|year=1916|pages=115|pageurl=https://menadoc.bibliothek.uni-halle.de/dmg/periodical/pageview/61516}}
* {{R:sem-srb:Sima:2000|pages=277–278}}
* {{R:CAL|m$lxh|N}}
* {{R:CAL|slykh|N}}

{{C|ar|Laurel family plants|Spices}}
