Page 10612 سليل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Of the root {{ar-root|س ل ل}}. The lexicographers say it means “male foetus”, “horse-foal”, ”any animal that is born with yet the fetal membrane on”; it is hence plausible that this word is an earlier borrowing of the same {{bor|ar|arc|-}} source as assumed for {{doublet|ar|شَلِيل|notext=1}}, see there.

