#* {{RQ:Qur'an|6|99|passage=وَهُوَ ٱلَّذِي أَنْزَلَ مِنَ '''ٱلسَّمَاءِ''' مَاءً فَأَخْرَجْنَا بِهِ نَبَاتَ كُلِّ شَيْءٍ|t=And it is He Who sent down rain from '''the sky'''. And with it have We brought forth germination of all things;}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|29|passage=هُوَ ٱلَّذِي خَلَقَ لَكُمْ مَّا فِي ٱلْأَرْضِ جَمِيعًا ثُمَّ ٱسْتَوَىٰ إِلَىٰ '''ٱلسَّمَاءِ''' فَسَوَّىٰهُنَّ سَبْعَ '''سَمَٰوَٰتٍ'''|t=It is He Who created for you all what is on earth. Again he directed himself towards '''the heaven''' and made thereof seven '''heavens'''.}}
## {{lb|ar|by extension}} the [[produce]] of the [[sky]] (such as [[cloud]]s, [[nimbus]]es, or [[rain]])
##: {{hypo|ar|سَحَاب|غَيْم|عَنَان|غَمَام|مُزْن|مَطَر|سَيْل|t1=clouds|t2=clouds; fog; mist|t3=clouds, the stratosphere|t4=clouds|t5=clouds, nimbi|t6=rain|t7=rain; a torrent, a shower, a hail}}
##* {{RQ:Qur’an|71|11|passage=فَقُلْتُ ٱسْتَغْفِرُوا رَبَّكُمْ إِنَّهُ كَانَ غَفَّارًا يُّرْسِلِ '''ٱلسَّمَاءَ''' عَلَيْكُمْ مِّدْرَارًا وَّيُمْدِدْكُمْ بِأَمْوَالٍ وَّبَنِينَ وَيَجْعَلْ لَّكُمْ جَنَّاتٍ وَّيَجْعَلْ لَّكُمْ أَنْهَارًا|t=So I said, "Ask your Lord for forgiveness! He surely is forgiving. He shall send unto you profusely '''the produce of the sky'''. And He shall enrich you with wealth and children and make for you gardens and make for you rivers."}}
## {{lb|ar|uncountable}}, [[outer space]] (when [[observe]]d from [[earth]]), the [[upper regions]], the [[multiverses]], the [[universe]], the [[cosmos]](es), the [[heavens]] {{lb|ar|figurative|simile}}
##: {{syn|ar|فَضَاء|t=a space, a void|فَلَك|t2=outer space, universe}}
##* {{RQ:Quran|25|61|passage=تَبَارَكَ ٱلَّذِي جَعَلَ فِي '''ٱلسَّمَاءِ''' بُرُوجًا وَّجَعَلَ فِيهَا سِرَٰجًا وَّقَمَرًا مُّنِيرًا|t=Blessed is He Who made asterisms in '''the heavens''' and [also] made therein a lamp and a luminous moon.}}
## {{lb|ar|proper noun|uncountable|figurative|simile|religion|rare|archaic|obsolete|poetic}} the [[abode]] of [[God]] traditionally conceived as beyond the sky; [[Heaven]], the [[empyrean]]
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|67|16|passage=ءَأَمِنْتُمْ مَّنْ فِي '''ٱلسَّمَاءِ''' أَنْ يَّخْسِفَ بِكُمُ ٱلْأَرْضَ فَإِذَا هِيَ تَمُورُ|t=Are you [so] certain that He Who is in '''Heaven''' will cause not the earth, when it would be swaying in tumult, to swallow you up?}}
##* {{RQ:SVD|Ezra|5|12|passage=وَلَٰكِنْ بَعْدَ أَنْ أَسْخَطَ آبَاؤُنَا إِلَٰهَ '''ٱلسَّمَاءِ''' {{...}}|t=But after our fathers made the god of '''Heaven''' angry {{...}}}}
## [[airspace]], the [[aether]]
##: {{syn|ar|أَثِير|مَجَال جَوِّيّ}}
## the [[celestial sphere]](s)
##: {{syn|ar|قُبَّة سَمَاوِيَّة|مَجَال سَمَاوِيّ}}
## the [[atmosphere]](s)
##: {{syn|ar|غِلَاف جَوِيّ}}
## the [[stratosphere]]
##: {{syn|ar|سْتْرَاتُوسْفِير}}
# {{lb|ar|countable}} a [[high]] [[covering]]; [[ceiling]], [[vault]], [[canopy]]
#: {{syn|ar|سَقْف|بِنَاء}}
#: {{uxi|ar|وَقَالَتْ '''سَمَاءُ''' الْبَيْتِ فَوْقَكَ مُخَلَّقٌ|And she said: The '''ceiling''' of the house above you is perfect in make.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|22|15|passage=مَنْ كَانَ يَظُنُّ أَنْ لَنْ يَنْصُرَهُ ٱللهُ فِي ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱلْآخِرَةِ فَلْيَمْدُدْ بِسَبَبٍ إِلَىٰ ٱل'''سَّمَاءِ''' ثُمَّ لْيَقْطَعْ فَلْيَنْظُرْ هَلْ يُذْهِبَنَّ كَيْدُهُ مَا يَغِيظُ|t=He who thinks that God will not support him in this world and the hereafter: Then let him stretch a rope upto the '''vault''' and let him strangle himself. Then let him see if his strategy makes what is enraging [him so much] go away.}}
## {{lb|ar|uncountable|figurative}} [[anything]] which resembles a [[vault]], ''particularly'' the [[sky]]; the [[firmament]], the [[vault of heaven]], the [[welkin]]
##: {{syn|ar|رَقِيع}}
##* {{RQ:Qur’an|22|65|passage=وَيُمْسِكُ '''ٱلسَّمَاءَ''' أَنْ تَقَعَ عَلَىٰ ٱلْأَرْضِ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهِ|t=And He holds up '''the firmament''' lest it fall upon the earth but by His leave.}}
# {{lb|ar|archaic|or|classical|countable}} [[Arabian horse]]’s [[back]].
#: {{syn|ar|ظَهْرُ الْفَرَسِ}}
# {{lb|ar|archaic|or|classical|countable}} [[mountaintop]], [[summit]].
#: {{syn|ar|ضَهْر}}
# {{lb|ar|archaic|or|classical|countable}} rainy [[grass]]
#: {{syn|ar|عُشْب}}

====Usage notes====
1:This word means a sky and space, although it does comprise the concept of heaven, a more specific word for Heaven is [[عليون]] according to the Ibn Kathir tafsir of the Quran. This word isn’t common as the others [[جنة]], [[فردوس]], and [[نعيم]] because it’s only mentioned twice in the Quran.<br/>
2:The plural forms سمي and أسمية are exclusive to the sense “grass”, other plural forms aren’t used with this sense.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَمَاء|d=سَمَاوَانِ|d2=سَمَاءَانِ|pl=سَمَاوَات|pl2=سَمَاءَات|pl3=أَسْمِيَة|pl4=سُمِيّ}}

