Page 10656 سمك: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|س م ك}}

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|س|م|ك}}, meaning “to be elevated or lofty”, “to be supported or held up”, “to sustain”; hence the meaning of “a source of sustenance”, “a mainstay or staple-food”. Cognate with {{cog|he|סָמַך|tr=samak|t=to lean, lay, rest, support}} attested in the Bible with the similar semantic sense “to sustain” or “to nourish”.<ref>[http://biblehub.com/text/genesis/27-37.htm Genesis 27:37]</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سَمَك}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-سمك.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|سَمَك|sing=سَمَكَة|pl=أَسْماك|pl2=سِمَاك|pl3=سُمُوك}}

# [[fish]]
#: {{ux|ar|السَّرْدِينَ عِبَارَةً عَنْ سَمَكِ زَيْتَي صَغِيرٍ يُمْكِنُ أَكْلُهُ بِالْكَامِلِ.|Sardines are small, oily fish that can be eaten whole.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|سَمَك|sing=سَمَكَة|pl=أَسْماك|pl2=سِمَاك|pl3=سُمُوك}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|afb|سمچ|tr=simič, simač}}
* {{desc|acm|سمچ|tr=simač}}
* {{desc|gez|ሰመክ|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|ota|سمك|tr=semek|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|samaki|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
From the root {{ar-root|س م ك}} in the sense of "to nourish", "to make well-fed", "to fatten up livestock".

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[thicken]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
