Page 10664 سموأل: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|سَمَوْءَل||archaic}}

===Etymology===
Pre-Islamic Arabization of {{bor|ar|hbo|שְׁמוּאֵל|tr=šəmūʾēl}}. Chiefly borne by Jews. The forms {{m|ar|سَمَوْئِيل}}, {{m|ar|سَمَوِيل}} are typically Christian, although also encountered for ethnic Jews. Later borrowed again as {{m|ar|شَمَوْئِيل}}, {{m|ar|شَمَوِيل}}, apparently supported by the {{bor|ar|syc|-}} form {{m|syc|ܫܡܘܝܠ}}, but now most popular for referring to {{cog|he-IL|-}} men. Lastly, forms like {{m|ar|صَمُوئِل}}, {{m|ar|صَمُوئِيل}}, {{m|ar|صَمْوِيل}} are from European languages including {{bor|ar|en|-}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَمَوْأَل}}

===Proper noun===
