Page 10716 سندر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Apparently from {{bor|ar|grc|σημύδα}}, a hapax attested in {{w|Theophrastus|Θεόφραστος}} often glossed as birch. Perhaps borrowed into Arabic from a manuscript variant or elsewhere with a suffix such as a {{m|grc||*σημυδάριον}} with {{m|grc|-άριον}}, or this ending is derived from popularity in Arabic, as in the example of {{m|ar|سَفَنْدَر|t={{vern|box holly}} (''[[Ruscus]]'' gen. et spp.)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَنْدَر}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَنْدَر|m}}

# [[birch]] ({{taxfmt|Betula|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|[[شَجَر]] الْ[[قضيب|قُضْبَان]]|بَتُولَا}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَنْدَر}}

