Page 10718 سندس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|xpr|-}} or {{bor|ar|pal|tr=sndws|ts=|t=a silk (or brocade) garment}}, from {{der|ar|sog|tr=sndws|ts=sandus|t=a silk wear}}, compare also {{cog|xcl|սնդուս}} an Iranian loanword. From an Anatolian source, compare {{cog|grc|σάνδυξ|t=a Lydian red fabric}}, likely ultimately descendant from {{der|ar|akk|𒉌𒌓𒍝𒄢|tr=NA<sub>4</sub>.GUG|ts=sāmtu, sāntu, sāndu|t=red stone, carnelian, cinnabar}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سُنْدُس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سُنْدُس|m}}

# a kind of [[fine]] [[silk]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|78|246
|passage=وَنَهَانَا عَنْ سَبْعٍ، عَنْ خَاتَمِ الذَّهَبِ ـ أَوْ قَالَ حَلْقَةِ الذَّهَبِ ـ وَعَنْ لُبْسِ الْحَرِيرِ، وَٱلدِّيبَاجِ، وَٱل'''سُّنْدُسِ'''، وَٱلْمَيَاثِرِ.
|translation=And he [the Prophet Muhammad] forbade us seven [things]: to wear signets of gold – or he said "[jewellery] rings of gold" –, to wear silk [thread, cloth, or garments], silk brocade, '''fine silk''' or silk saddle-pillows [and blankets, or shabraques].}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سُنْدُس}}

====Derived terms====
