Page 10719 سنديان: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Quercus faginea pedamarro.JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|سِنْدِيَان}}|upright=1.15]]
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Semantically from {{sl|ar|arc|סדיין|tr=seḏyān|t=type of oak|notext=1}}, cognates with {{cog|syc|ܣܕܝܢܐ|tr=seḏyānā}}, {{cog|akk|𒄑𒋛𒅔𒁕𒀀|tr=sindu|t=a tree}}; from the [[w:Semitic_languages|Semitic]] root {{ar-root|س|ن|د}} meaning “to stay”, “to prop up”, “to set up pieces of wood for reinforcement”. Connected to the wood’s common use in construction and sturdiness; compare {{m|arc|סדנא|tr=saddānā|t=foundation; the trunk or base of a tree}}, {{cog|he|סַד|tr=sad|t=torture stocks; a place for securing prisoners}}. Uncertain connections to {{cog|fa|سندیان|tr=sendiyân|t=type of oak}}, perhaps related to {{cog|pal||tr=cytn'|ts=cidān|t=to gather, to pile up}} as in the collecting of wood.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سِنْدِيَان|m}}

# [[oak]], [[holm oak]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سِنْدِيَان}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|sdyn|N}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=1|pages=621–630}}

