Page 10726 سنوت: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Compare {{m|ar|سَنَا|t=senna}}, denoting plants and their seeds of similar avail; the ending ''-ūt'' is an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} suffix; whereas according to G. S. Colin it seems to be a Yemenite, i. e. {{bor|ar|sem-sar|-}} word; however it is but attested in {{cog|xcl|սամիթ|t=dill}}.<!-- {{cog|omn|}} in Kjell Aartun Die minoische Schrift: Linear A-Inschriften page 89–90 is based on one encountered and two conjectured syllables apparently, and even that is not a match https://books.google.com/books?id=gsVoV63OuNYC&pg=PA90&dq=%22sinnawt%22.--> The Sunna use occurs in the same format (as a cure of every disease short of fatality) with {{m|ar|شُونِيز}}; its meaning, [[kalonji]], withal, is not ascribed to {{m-self|ar|سَنُّوت}}, and the [https://sunnah.com/muslim/39/119 tradition affirms] that the original wording was {{m|ar|حبة سوداء|الحَبّةُ السَوْدَاءُ}} and not {{m|ar|شونيز|الشُونِيزُ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سَنُّوت}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سَنُّوت|m}} {{tlb|ar|rare}}

# [[inspissate]]d [[fruit]]s, [[syrup]]
#: {{syn|ar|رُبّ}}
# [[dill]] ({{taxfmt|Anethum graveolens|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|شِبِثّ}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|ibnmajah|31
|passage=سَمِعْتُ رَسُولَ اللّٰهِ – صَلَّى اللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ – يَقُولُ «عَلَيْكُمْ بِالسَّنَى وَالسَّنُّوتِ فَإِنَّ فِيهِمَا شِفَاءً مِنْ كُلِّ دَاءٍ إِلَّا السَّامَ.» قِيلَ يَا رَسُولَ اللّٰهِ وَمَا السَّامُ قَالَ «الْمَوْتُ». قَالَ عَمْرٌو قَالَ ابْنُ أَبِي عَبْلَةَ السَّنُّوتُ الشِّبِتُّ وَقَالَ آخَرُونَ بَلْ هُوَ الْعَسَلُ الَّذِي يَكُونُ فِي زِقَاقِ السَّمْنِ وَهُوَ قَوْلُ الشَّاعِرِ «هُمُ السَّمْنُ بِالسَّنُّوتِ لَا أَلْسَ فِيهِمُ وَهُمْ يَمْنَعُونَ جَارَهُمْ أَنْ يُقَرَّدَا».
|translation=I heard the Messenger of God (PBUH) say “You should intake senna and sannūt, for it is a cure of every disease short of fatality. One said: “O Messenger of God, what is fatality?” He said ”death.” ʿAmr said that Ibn ʾAbū ʿAbla said that Sannūt is dill. But others say it is a honey kept in skins of fat and a poet says “they are fat with honey but no sour milk in them and they prevent that their neighbour gets picked on.”
|subst=بِالسَّنَى/بِ-ٱلسَّنَى,وَالسَّنُّوتِ/وَ-ٱلسَّنُّوتِ,عَمْرٌو/عَمْرٌ,الْمَوْتُ/ٱلْمَوْتُ,ابْنُ/ٱبْنُ,وَمَا/وَ-مَا,وَقَالَ/وَ-قَالَ,وَهُوَ/وَ-هُوَ,فِيهِمُ/فِي-هِمُ,وَهُمْ/وَ-هُمْ,جَارَهُمْ/جَارَ-هُمْ,عَلَيْكُمْ/عَلَيْ-كُمْ,عَلَيْهِ/عَلَيْ-هِ,فِيهِمَا/فِي-هِمَا,فَإِنَّ/فَ-إِنَّ}}
# [[fennel]] ({{taxfmt|Foeniculum vulgare|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|شَمَر}}
# [[cumin]] ({{taxfmt|Cuminum cyminum|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|كَمُّون}}

