Though [[w:de:Siegmund Fraenkel (Semitist)|Fraenkel]] assumed that the Arabic word is genuine and not a loan, likely a perhaps early loan from a byform of {{bor|ar|arc|שֵׁירָא}} / {{m|syc|ܫܶܐܪܳܐ|tr=šērā}}, see the exposure at {{ar-root|ش ج ر|nocat=1}}. Juxtapose {{m|ar|قُلْب|id=bracelet|t=bracelet}} for a Syriac loan. Compare also {{m|ar|دُمْلُوج}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|سِوَار}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|سِوَار|m|pl=أَسْوِرَة|pl2=أَسَاوِر}}

# [[bracelet]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|سِوَار|m|pl=أَسْوِرَة|pl2=أَسَاوِر}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=56}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=374}}

{{C|ar|Jewelry}}

-------- end text --------
