Page 10771 سور: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Walls of Constantinople 1.jpg|thumb|right|{{l-self|ar|سُور|tr=-}}|upright=1.35]]

===Etymology 1===
Argued to be a loan from {{bor|ar|arc|שׂוּרָא}} / {{m|syc|ܫܘܪܐ|tr=šūrā}}, but other cognates such as {{cog|xsa|𐩣𐩬𐩪𐩥𐩧𐩩|t=walls}} and {{cog|tig|ሶር|t=partition wall}} (unless that form is itself borrowed from Arabic) suggest that it may in fact be inherited.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سُور|m|pl=أَسْوَار|pl2=سِيرَان}}

# [[wall]] that encloses and protects a building

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|سُور|pl=أَسْوَار|pl2=سِيرَان}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=237}}
* {{R:sem-pro:GC|page=397}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[enclose]] with a [[wall]] or [[fences]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun-pl|سُوَر|f-p}}

# {{plural of|ar|سُورَة}}

{{C|ar|Walls and fences}}

