Page 10902 سوس: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|عرق سوس|mul=عرق السوس (حلوى)}}

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|שׁוּשָׁא}} / {{m|syc|ܫܽܘܫܳܐ|tr=šūšā|t=licorice}}, from {{der|ar|akk|šūšum|𒄑𒊺𒆕𒀀|tr=šūšum|t=licorice}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سُوس}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سُوس|m}}

# [[licorice]]
#* {{quote-web|ar|work=ʾuḥibbu Dimašq|title=ar:شراب عرق السوس|archivedate=15-08-2019|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20190612212300/http://www.lovedamascus.com/ar/syrian-cuisine/erek-el-sous-drink|date=2016-11-24|url=http://www.lovedamascus.com/ar/syrian-cuisine/erek-el-sous-drink|passage=يعتبر نبات '''السوس''' الدمشقي من أفضل الأنواع في العالم، ويسمى الشراب الذي يقطر يدويا من جذوره شراب عرق '''السوس''' وهو مفضل لدى الدمشقيين.|translation=The Damascene '''liquorice''' plant is esteemed to be of the most excellent sorts of the world, and the drink which is dropped by hand from its roots is called '''liquorice''' stem and the Damascenes are fond of it.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|سُوس}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|pt|alcaçuz|bor=1|der=1}}
* {{desc|es|alcazuz|bor=1|der=1|alts=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|سوس (قراديات)|mul=سوسية حقيقية}}
Typically declared as inherited from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*sūs-|t=moth; insect especially one that bites or chews up materials}}, from {{inh|ar|afa-pro|*suʔw-|t=a kind of insect}}, cognates with {{der|ar|akk|sāsum|𒌨𒈨|tr=sāsum|t=moth; biting insect}}, {{cog|tmr|ססא|tr=sāsā}}, {{cog|he|סָס|tr=sās}}, {{cog|syc|ܣܣܐ|tr=sāsā}}, and often also {{cog|gez|ፃፄ|t=moth, worm}}, {{m|gez|ጻጹት|t=gnat; red ant}}, akin to {{cog|am|ጭጫት}}, {{m|am|ጨጫት}}, {{m|am|ጬጫ}}, {{m|am|ጭጫን}}, {{m|am|ጬጫን|t=ant or a type of ant}}, {{cog|ti|ሺሾ|t=colony of ants or termites; large black ant with painful bite}}, {{cog|tig|ሻሽንቴ|tr=šašənte|t=ants}}.

{{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing into Arabic is at least possible if one espouses a phonologic value {{IPAchar|/ɔː/}} for ''ā'' in ancient Ḥijāzi dialects of Arabic, that later merged into {{IPAchar|/uː/}} in the standard, as assumed for {{m|ar|قَيُّوم}} and {{m|ar|جَار}}. The proposed Proto-Semitic shape, whether it be ''*sūs-'', or ''*sās-'', two identical consonants connected by a long vowel forming the noun’s stem, strains credibility, and the same authors imagine legitimate ancestry of {{m|ar|نُون|pos=unknown meaning}} and {{m|ar|تُوت|t=mulberry}}. In comparison, the moth term also appears loaned in {{cog|grc|σής}} and {{cog|xcl|ցեց}}.

====Pronunciation====
* Noun: {{ar-IPA|سُوس}}
* Verb: {{ar-IPA|سَوِسَ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|سُوس|m|sing=سُوسَة|pl=سِيسَان}}

# [[maggot]], [[moth]]-[[worm]], [[woodworm]], [[curculio]], [[weevil]]
# [[mite]]
# [[rot]], [[decay]]
#* {{RQ:Awwam|9|1|volume=1|page=508|passage=الإجاص قال غ وهو عبقر إذا أشرف وقدم فلا  يتعرض عليه بالحديد فإن دعت ضرورة لقطع أعلاه فينظر شجرته فإن ظهر فيها ال'''سوس''' فتحامى بالقطع ولا تقرب بالحديد بوجه وتنقى ما دام أملس الساق والأغصان محدثا.|translation=About the prune, that is the plum, says Ibn Ḥajjāj that when it is high and old it should not meet the iron, but if necessity calls then the top can be cut and the tree cleaned, and if '''rot''' appears on it then it can be warded off by cutting, and the iron should not approach it as long as the stem is smooth and the branches new.}}
# {{n-g|often used when referring to bacteria gnawing the teeth}}
#* {{quote-journal|ar|work=Al-Bawwāba News|date=2018-06-12|title=ar:5 أسباب وراء الاضطرار لخلع الأسنان|url=https://www.albawabhnews.com/3144723|passage=قال باسم سمير، استشاري الأسنان، أن البكتيريا النافعة المتواجدة في الفم، تعمل على تكسير مكونات الطعام وبالتالى الإسراع من هضمه، لكن إن زادت عن حدها تحولت إلى '''سوس''' يأكل في الأسنان.|translation=Bāsim Samīr, a teeth consultant, said that useful bacteria found in the mouth work towards the decomposition of food components and hence towards speeding up their digestion, but when they grow about their limit they become a '''caries''' that eats from the teeth.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|سُوس|pl=سِيسَان}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|سَوِسَ|t=to be affected by worms}}
* {{l|ar|تَسَوَّسَ|t=to be affected by worms}}
* {{l|ar|تَسَوُّس|t=mouth cavities}}

=====Descendants=====
