===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ar|water}}
A native root. Some occurrences of {{cog|hbo|שׁוֹט|tr=šōṭ}} are understood as “[[spate]]”, whose sense seems to have influenced the Arabic sense of “a punishment” otherwise belonging to the “whip” noun, as in the Qurʾān place above God {{m|ar|صَبَّ}} it, that is “poured” or “dispensed“ punishment like liquid, although Jakob Barth considered all the Arabic words and senses on this page natively developed from {{m|ar|سَطَا|t=to throw oneself upon someone or something with impetuosity; to be restive; to march with large steps; to be found in abundance {{q|said of water}}}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|سَوْط|m}}

# [[water]] that [[bide]]s in a [[pool]] or [[puddle]] or the [[place]] where there is such water
# someone's [[deal]], a [[designated]] [[deal]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|سَوْط}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[commix]] the [[liquid]]s by [[stir]]ring

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

=====Derived terms=====
