Page 10906 سوف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|סופא|סוֹף}}  / {{m|syc|ܣܘܦܐ|ܣܘܦ|tr=sōp̄|t=limit, end}},<ref>{{R:akk:Haupt:1917b|page=92}}</ref> which was used in various adverbial uses such as “after”, “in the end”. Compare the same word pervading the {{cog|he|-}} language as {{m|he|סוֹף|tr=sōp̄|t=end}} in later usage, and {{m+|he|טֶרֶם|tr=térem|t=before; not yet}} cognate to {{m|ar|طَرْمَة|t=upper lip; edge, protrusion}}.

From the Arabic particle, it was natural to form a {{ar-form|II|nocap=1}} verb “to put off in the future”, said of someone who commits to do something ({{m|ar||سَوْفَ أَفْعَلُ|t=I will do}}, and less well-known {{ar-form|I|nocap=1}} {{m|ar|سَافَ}} meaning “to endure” and “to smell” as sensory anticipation, whence ”to hunt”, and {{ar-form|III|nocap=1}} {{m|ar|سَاوِفَ|t=to smell; to say in private; to compress, to go in unto}}, and notably {{m|ar|مَسَافَة|t=distance, interval}}.

===Particle===
{{ar-particle|سَوْفَ}}

# {{n-g|added to an imperfect (present) verb form to express future tense}}: [[will]]
#: {{ux|ar|يَقْرَأُ كِتَابًا، '''سَوْفَ''' يَقْرَأُ كِتَابًا|He is reading a book, he '''will''' read a book.}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|سَـ|id=future}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|ar|لَنْ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# to [[postpone]], [[delay]], [[procrastinate]], to [[put off]] a person or thing
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[commission]] to, to [[charge]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

