Page 10957 سيراء: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|שִׁירָאָה|tr=šērāʾā}}, {{m|arc|שִּׁירָא|tr=šērā|t=silk; a kind of silk garment}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|zh|-}} {{ltc-l|絲|silk}}. In Arabic this word has been connected to the root {{ar-root|س ي ر|nocat=1}} and is thus dubiously glossed by the classical lexicographers as a kind of “striped” garment; also the vocalization {{m|ar||سِيَرَاء}} is a hyper-Arabic fabrication.

