Page 10973 سيف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Related to {{cog|grc|ξίφος}}; either a loan, or from a common original source.
The same word is probably preserved in {{cog|egy|zft}}, {{cog|cop|ⲥⲏϥⲉ}}.
Dümichen (1867) suggested an Old Semitic ''saïf'' or ''sêf'', Myres (1930) a possible Libyan or "[[Sea Peoples]]" word.
The root {{ar-root|س ي ف}} is denominal.

Compare {{cog|he|סיף|tr=sayif}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|سَيْف}}
** {{IPA|afb|/seːf/|a=Gulf}}

====Noun====
