Page 10991 ش: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{der|ar|sem-pro|*šinn-|t=tooth}}, the source of {{m|ar|سن#Etymology 3|tr=sinn|سن}}. The association of "tooth" with this letter was the result of folk etymology and based on the corresponding Phoenician letter, {{m|phn|𐤔}}, having a shape resembling a tooth. The letter originally depicted a [[composite bow]], which usually has the tips curving away from the archer when unstrung.<ref>{{R:American Heritage Dictionary|shin}}</ref><ref>Albright, W. F. (1948). "The Early Alphabetic Inscriptions from Sinai and their Decipherment". Bulletin of the American Schools of Oriental Research. 110 (110): 6–22 [p. 15].</ref>

Related to {{cog|syc|ܫ}}, {{cog|he|ש}}, {{cog|phn|𐤔}}, {{cog|arc|ܫ}}. More at [[w:Shin (letter)|Shin]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/ʃiːn/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/ʃ/}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ش '''/''' ش‍ '''/''' ‍ش‍ '''/''' ‍ش'''|tr=šīn}}

# The thirteenth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|س}} and followed by {{l|ar|ص}}.

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ش '''/''' ش‍ '''/''' ‍ش‍ '''/''' ‍ش'''|tr=šīn}}

# The twenty-first letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ر}} and followed by {{l|ar|ت}}.

===See also===
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/ش|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|ش}}]]

===References===
<references/>

