Page 10996 ش ج ر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The meanings of piercing, a fissure, forcing open, hence chin or mouth corner, are probably metathetical to {{ar-root|ش ر ج}}.

The meaning of a tree is likely generalized from the meaning of “fig tree” and via {{der|ar|arc|-}} from {{der|ar|akk|𒋗𒍀|tr=šu-guru<sub>5</sub>|ts=šugrû|t=basket; a processed form of dates}}, see the material of {{m|ar|شَيْرَة|t=threaded sparterie for the transport as well as sale of figs, pannier}}.

''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' opts for an Aramaic borrowing due the consonant correspondence with {{cog|he|שֶׁגֶר|tr=šeḡer|t=litter of animals}}, connecting via the ideas of “coming forth” of trees, ultimately seeing the root as derived from the cognate of {{ar-root|ج ر ر|nocat=1}} “to drag forth” plus causative prefix {{m|sem-pro|*ša-}}, which seems to not easily have happened, not only because that suffix is {{m|sem-wes-pro|*ha-}} since {{cog|sem-wes-pro|-}}. Some meanings “to come forth”, as “to happen”, are clearly figuratively denominal from the “trees” noun moreover. The Hebrew word can well be from the idea of a litter in a basket.

In a primitive pre-metallic time, a “bracelet”, what {{cog|arc|שֵׁירָא}} / {{m|syc|ܫܶܐܪܳܐ|tr=šērā}} and thence {{m|ar|سِوَار}} means, was also nothing else than wickerwork. About the same time one may have developed figurative meanings of “quarrels”, “brawls”, “scrimmages” and the like, people figurative becoming entangled, {{m|la|comminus}} as the Romans said.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

