Page 11031 ش ك م: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' suggests a causative, which would be {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ša-}}, attached to {{m|ar|كَمَّ|t=to muzzle}}, which would probably mean this root, and perhaps the other too, is an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing, since Proto-Semitic ''š'' regularly gives {{m+|ar|س}}, unless it had a variant {{m|sem-pro|*śa-}}. Compare also {{m|ar|شِكَال|t=hobble}}. Perhaps extended from {{m|ar|شَكَّ|t=to stick together}} then. But both {{m|ar|شِكَال|t=hobble}} and {{m|ar|شَكِيمَة|t=bit, snaffle}} are suspicious of {{bor|ar|ira-mid}} origin.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

