Page 11041 ش و ب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} root {{m|arc|שׁ־ו־ב}} / {{syc-root|ܫ|ܘ|ܒ}}, an archaic variant of the root {{m|arc|ת־ו־ב}} / {{syc-root|ܬ|ܘ|ܒ}} “to return, to turn away” passed as {{m|ar|تَابَ|t=to repent}} and cognates with {{cog|ar|ثَابَ|t=to return}} attested in meanings of “being hot; desiccating heat; (hot) blast”, which well can be connected to meanings of “blending, mixing”, both strains of meanings necessarily present in the idea of an alloy {{m|ar|أُشَابَة}} as metals only fuse when smelted by heat and beyond herbalism and alchemy trivially connected in any field kitchen, being shared by the English ideas of {{l|en|cooking}}, {{l|en|concoction}}, strains of meanings which relate to the “returning” meanings via the notions of [[draw]]ing, putting one ingredient into another or energy from one place to the other, meanings also more abstractly attested for Arabic as “to ward off” and as in the ideas of {{l|en|treason}} and {{l|en|disloyalty}} making man go off course figuratively as “to be untrustworthy”.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[draw off|drawing off]], [[deviate|deviating]], making go [[off course]]
# related to [[mixture]]
# related to [[hot]] [[temperature]]

====Derived terms====
{{ar-verb forms|a|I-vn-head=شَوْب|I=to mix; to adulterate, to vitiate, to spoil; to be untrustworthy; to ward off (from evil)|II=to ward off; to tan, to heat up at the outside|III=to be immixed|VIII=to be mixed|VIII-pp=-}}

* {{l|ar|شَوْب|t=mixture; vitiation, flaw; heat; roiling; hot wind, simoom; dreadful thirst in the desert}}
* {{l|ar|شَائِبَة|t=dirt, ordure; stain, flaw; suspicion, moment of doubt}}
* {{l|ar|شِيَاب}}, {{l|ar|شِيَابَة|t=admixture, what is blended into another thing}}
* {{l|ar|شَوْبَة|t=deceit, delusion, circumvention}}
* {{l|ar|أُشَابَة|t=alloy}}
* unclear whether {{l|ar|شُؤْبُوب|t=downpour}} from the idea of rain immixing or from {{ar-root|ش ب ب|nocat=1}} due to ideas of briskness and jumping

