{{ar-decl-adj|شَاءٍ|pl=smp}}

===Etymology 2===
Found under the root {{ar-root|ش و ه}} in Lane (see below); in Wehr (see below), listed under {{ar-root|ش و ء}}, whereas the paucal plural {{m|ar|شِوَاه}} is cross-referenced under {{ar-root|ش و ه}}. Compare {{cog|he|שֶׂה|tr=śe}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شَاء}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|شَاء|sing=شَاة|pauc=شِوَاه|pauc2=شِيَاه}}

# {{lb|ar|collective}} [[sheep]]
# [[ewes]], [[female]] [[sheep]]

=====Usage notes=====
The gender of the collective is unclear; it is also unclear if it varies depending on the meaning. The forms {{m|ar|شِوَاه}} and {{m|ar|شِيَاء}} are simply listed as plurals in Wehr, which would normally imply a plural of multiplicity or variety, but specifically noted as applying to 3-10 animals (i.e. paucal) in Lane.

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|شَاء|sing=شَاة|pauc=شِوَاه|pauc2=شِيَاه}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ar|ضَأْن}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Lane|شوه}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|شاء}}

