Page 11143 شبر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
A trade term presumably acquired by Arabic when it was employed for transactions to the north of the Peninsula in farther antiquity, from {{bor|ar|he|שֶׁבֶר|tr=šeḇer}} in a vocalization more conservative than the {{w|Tiberian vocalization|Tiberian}} one, or from {{bor|ar|sem-amm|-}} or {{bor|ar|arc-old|-}}, or even directly {{bor|ar|akk|𒆬𒉻𒁺|tr=KU₃.PAD.DU|ts=šibirtu, šabartu, šebirtu, šipirtu|t=break, fragment, lump of a stone or ore etc.}}, derivations of {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ṯabar-|t=to break in twain}}, the later {{cog|arc|-}} parallel to which also was borrowed by Arabic as {{doublet|notext=1|ar|تِبْر|t1=pure ore of gold or silver}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شِبْر|m|pl=أَشْبَار}}

# [[span]] (the [[measure]] of the [[hand]])

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شِبْر|m|pl=أَشْبَار}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|شَبَرَ|t=to mete with the span}}
* {{l|ar|شَبَّرَ|t=to magnify; to gesture}}
* {{l|ar|أَشْبَرَ|t=to beget children tall in the statures; to donate}}
* {{l|ar|تَشَبَّرَ|t=to be of a large stature}}
* {{l|ar|تَشَابَرَ|t=to approach each other in battle closely}}
* {{l|ar|أَشْبَر|t=wider in the span}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u,i.vn:شَبْر}}

# to [[mete]] with the [[span]], to [[apportion]] by the {{l-self|ar|شِبْر}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u,i.vn:شَبْر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَبْر|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|شَبَرَ|form=I}}
# [[dation]], [[gift]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَبْر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[magnify]], to [[extol]]
# to [[gesture]], to [[sign]] with the [[hand]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|la|sūber}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شُبِر|head2=شُبَر|m}}

# [[cork oak]] ({{taxfmt|Quercus suber|species}})
#* {{RQ:Awwam|34|6|volume=2|pages=721–722|passage=وقال غيره يتخذ لها الخلايا من خشب الأرز ومن طين طيب الريح وتطين الخلايا من خارجها برماد وأخثاء البقر مدقوق معجون بالماء ويتخذ لها بعض الناس الخلايا من قشور ال'''شبر''' وتسميه العامة «جناحا»|t=And another author said that for beehives cedar wood and clay of good smell is taken and the beehives are daubed from the outside with ash and cow dung powdered and kneaded with water, and some people take for beehives the barks of the '''cork oak''', generally called “wings”.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شُبِر|head2=شُبَر}}

