===Etymology===
Composed of {{compound|ar|شِبْه|t1=[[quasi-]]|جَزِيرَة|t2=[[island]]|عَرَبِيَّة|t3=[[Arab]], [[Arabian]]}}. {{m|ar|شِبْه جَزِيرَة}} by itself means "[[peninsula]]"; note, however, that {{m|ar|عَرَبِيَّة||[[Arabian]]}} modifies {{m|ar|جَزِيرَة}} rather than {{m|ar|شِبْه}}.

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|[[شبه جزيرة|شِبْه ٱلْجَزِيرَة]] [[عربي|ٱلْعَرَبِيَّة]]|f|tr=šibh al-jazīra l-ʿarabiyya}}

# [[Arabian Peninsula]]

====Declension====
In fully declined Classical Arabic, {{m|ar||شِبْهُ الجَزِيرَةِ العَرَبِيَّةِ}}. {{m|ar|شِبْه||[[quasi-]]}} is in the construct state, and both following terms are in the genitive case, with {{m|ar|عَرَبِيَّة||[[Arabian]]}} an adjectival modifier of {{m|ar|جَزِيرَة||[[island]]}}, as described above.

