Page 11171 شتان: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ش|ت|ت}}. One of a special group of words known in Arabic as {{l|ar|أَسْمَاء أَفْعَال|t=noun verbs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شَتَّانَ}}

===Verb===
{{head|ar|verb|head=شَتَّانَ}}

# {{lb|ar|defective|intransitive}} What a difference! How different they are!
#: {{ux|ar|'''شَتَّانَ''' بَيْنَ ٱلْحَقِّ وَٱلْبَاطِلِ.|'''There is a great difference''' between the right and the wrong.}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''شَتَّانَ''' ٱلْفَقْرُ وَٱلْغِنَى.|'''There is a great difference''' between poverty and richness.}}

====Usage notes====
The verb is [[defective]] and does not conjugate or receive case endings; it is used the same way with the same final vowels in all contexts.

[[Category:Arabic defective verbs]]
-------- end text --------
