Page 11286 شرك: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ش ر ك}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.pass.vn:شِرْك,شِرْكَة,شَرِكَة}}

# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to have the shoe strings broken
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[share]], to [[participate]] with (someone)
# to become a [[partner]], to be a [[participant]], to be an [[associate]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.pass.vn:شِرْك,شِرْكَة,شَرِكَة}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ش ر ك}}
The meaning of associating partners to a god or sharing allegiance across multiple gods is, according to Jeffery 1938, a {{semantic loan|ar|sem-srb|𐩦𐩧𐩫|nocap=1}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شِرْك|m|pl=أَشْرَاك}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|شَرِكَ|form=I}}
# {{lb|ar|uncountable|Islam}} [[polytheism]], [[idolatry]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|31|13
|passage=وَإِذْ قَالَ لُقْمَانُ لِٱبْنِهِ وَهُوَ يَعِظُهُ يَا بُنَيَّ لَا تُشْرِكْ بِٱللّٰهِۖ إِنَّ '''ٱلشِّرْكَ''' لَظُلْمٌ عَظِيمٌ
|translation=When Luqman said to his son, as he advised him: "O my son! Do not ascribe any partners to God. '''Polytheism''' is indeed a great injustice."
|subst=بِٱللّٰهِۖ/بِٱللّٰهِ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|35|14
|passage=إِن تَدْعُوهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُوا دُعَاءَكُمْ وَلَوْ سَمِعُوا مَا ٱسْتَجَابُوا لَكُمْۖ وَيَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَامَةِ يَكْفُرُونَ '''بِشِرْكِكُمْۚ''' وَلَا يُنَبِّئُكَ مِثْلُ خَبِيرٍ
|translation=If you invoke them they will not hear your invocation, and even if they heard they cannot respond to you, and on the Day of Resurrection they will forswear your '''polytheism''', and none can inform you like the One who is all-aware.
|subst=لَكُمْۖ/لَكُمْ,بِشِرْكِكُمْۚ/بِشِرْكِكُمْ}}
# {{lb|ar|countable}} [[share]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شِرْك|pl=أَشْرَاك}}

=====Descendants=====
