Page 11293 شرموطة: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|شَرْطُوطَة}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|ar|شَرْمَطَ||to shred}}. Most Semitists agree that it is of non-Semitic origin; perhaps from {{der|ar|pal|tr=clm|ts=čarm|t=a piece of skin, hide, or leather|sc=Phlv}} (see {{cog|fa|چرم|tr=čarm}}), perhaps conflated with {{der|ar|pal|tr=šlm|ts=šarm|t=shame|sc=Phlv}}. Compare {{cog|he|סְמַרְטוּט|tr=s'martút|t=rag}}, {{cog|arc|מַרְטוּטָא|tr=marṭūṭā}}, {{m|arc|סְמַרְטוּטָא|tr=səmarṭūṭā|t=coarse garment}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شَرْمُوطَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|شَرْمُوطَة|f|pl=شَرَامِيط}}

# {{lb|ar|now widely avoided}} [[rag]], [[shred]], [[tatter]]
#: {{syn|ar|خَلَق|خِرْقَة|رُقْعَة|كُهْنَة}}
# {{C|ar|Meats}}{{lb|ar|figurative|cooking|now widely avoided}} [[cutting]]s, [[strip]]s, [[shred]]s of a [[victual]]
#* {{RQ:In Darfur|II|page=184|section=3.3.31|passage=فيعملون اللحم قديدًا وهو المسمّى عندهم بال'''شراميط''' لأنّهم يشرمطونه أي يقطعونه سيورًا ويأكلون منه طريًّا.|t=They make the meat into jerky, which they call “'''shreds'''” because they shred it, meaning they cut it into strips. Some of it they also eat undried.}}
# {{C|ar|Prostitution|Occupations}}{{lb|ar|vulgar}} [[whore]], [[slut]]
#: {{syn|ar|عَاهِرَة|قَحْبَة}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَرْمُوطَة|pl=شَرَامِيط}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|he|שרמוטה|tr=sharmúta|bor=1}}
* {{desc|it|sciarmutta|bor=1}}
-------- end text --------
