Page 11309 شريك: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{m|ar||فَعِيل}}-type stative-verb {{ar-active participle|lc=1|nocat=1}} from the verb {{m|ar|شَرِكَ||to [[share]]}}, from the root {{ar-root|ش ر ك}}; literally, "sharer".

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شَرِيك}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|شَرِيك|m|pl=شُرَكَاء|f=شَرِيكَة}}

# {{lb|ar|countable}} a [[sharer]]
## a [[sharer]] in [[wealth]], [[profit]], or [[ownership]]; a [[business]] [[partner]]
## a [[sharer]] in [[inheritance]]; a [[coheir]]
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|4|12|passage=فَإِن كَانُوا أَكْثَرَ مِن ذَٰلِكَ فَهُمْ '''شُرَكَاءُ''' فِي ٱلثُّلُثِ|translation=If they are more than that, they are the co-heirs of the third [of the inheritance].}}
## a [[sharer]] in [[rank]], [[authority]], or [[lordship]]; a [[coordinate]]; an [[equal]]; a [[coruler|co-ruler]]
## an [[associate]], a [[partner]], a [[fellow]]; a [[companion]]
# {{C|ar|Paganism}} a [[fellow]] [[deity]], someone [[presume]]d a [[god]] other than the [[monotheistic]] [[God]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|10|35|passage=قُلْ هَلْ مِن '''شُرَكَائِكُم''' مَّن يَهْدِي إِلَى الْحَقِّ|t=Say: Is there of your partner-deities one that leads to the right? }}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|35|40|passage=قُلْ أَرَأَيْتُمْ '''شُرَكَاءَكُمُ''' الَّذِينَ تَدْعُونَ مِن دُونِ اللَّهِ أَرُونِي مَاذَا خَلَقُوا مِنَ الْأَرْضِ أَمْ لَهُمْ شِرْكٌ فِي السَّمَاوَاتِ أَمْ آتَيْنَاهُمْ كِتَابًا فَهُمْ عَلَىٰ بَيِّنَتٍ مِّنْهُ|t=Say: Have ye seen your partner-gods to whom ye pray beside Allah? Show me what they created of the earth! Or have they any share in the heavens? Or have We given them a scripture so they act on unequivocal proof therefrom?}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|شَرِيك|pl=شُرَكَاء|f=شَرِيكَة|fpl=شَرِيكَات|fpl2=شَرَائِكُ}}

