Page 11372 شق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
{{ar-rootbox|ش ق ق}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شَقَّ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:شَقّ}} {{tlb|ar|transitive}}

# to [[make]] a [[cut]] or [[gap]] in; to [[cut]] into or through; to [[tear]] through; to [[transpierce]]
#: {{syn|ar|ثَقَبَ|خَرَمَ|نَخَرَ|t1=to bore|t2=to hole|t3=to drill through}}
## to [[cut]] into or through (something [[hard]] or [[rigid]], for example, a [[skull]], a [[roof]], and so on, or a [[mass]], for example, a [[rock]]), to [[bore]] through; to [[crack]], to [[fissure]]
##: {{syn|ar|كَسَرَ|فَلَقَ|صَدَعَ|شَرَخَ|t1=to break|t2=to crack; to splinter|t3=to fissure; to fracture|t4=to hollow}}
## to [[cut]] into or through (something [[soft]] or [[pliable]], for example, [[skin]] or a [[skin]]-[[covered]] [[body]] [[part]] such as a [[finger]], a [[vein]], [[flesh]], or [[cloth]] or [[fabric]], or a [[thickness]] or [[layer]], for example, a [[paper]], a [[sheet]], or a [[leaf]]), to [[incise]], to [[slit]], to [[gash]], to [[slash]], to [[rip]]
##: {{syn|ar|قَطَعَ|قَصَّ|مَزَعَ|خَرَقَ|مَزَقَ|t1=to cut; to tear|t2=to scissor; to clip; to hack|t3=to rip; to tear|t4=to pierce, to penetrate; to hack through|t5=to tear or pull apart; to shred; to rend}}
# to [[cut]] through (something seemingly [[flat]] or [[level]], such as a [[surface]]) [[parallel]]ly;
## to [[make]] a [[recess]] in; to [[groove]]; to [[furrow]]; to [[indent]]
# to [[cut]] in [[two]] or [[asunder]], to [[tear apart]], to [[split]], to [[cleave]]
#: {{syn|ar|قَسَمَ|t=to divide; to sunder; to split}}
## to [[spread]] or [[cause]] [[disagreement]] or [[factionalism]] in or among; to [[divide]], to [[rive]]
##: {{syn|ar|قَسَّمَ|فَرَّقَ|t1=to split apart; to partition|t2=to split; to disperse; to scatter}}
# to [[move]] or [[pass]] through; to [[cut across]]; to [[traverse]], to [[cross]]

