Page 11374 شقائق النعمان: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Flowers (9058792879).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|شقائق النُعْمان}}|upright=1.15]]
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
According to Arabic tradition it is the name of King {{w|Al-Nu'man III ibn al-Mundhir|nuʕmān ibn-al-munḏir}} of {{w|al-Hira|al-Ḥīra}} who patronized the flower, but this has been recognized after Lagarde as impossible, rather {{m|ar|شَقِيقَة}} would be a [[cranberry morpheme]] from the root {{ar-root|ش ق ق}} meaning something like “gash, wound” and the second name equal the Biblical figure {{m|hbo|נַעֲמָן|tr=naʕămān|}} as a byname of [[Adonis]] like {{m|hbo|נַעֲמָה|tr=naʕămā}} of [[Astarte]], for in {{w|Book of Isaiah|Jes.}} 17, 10 {{m|he|[[נטע|נִטְעֵי]] [[נעמן|נַעֲמָנִים]]|tr=niṭʕē naʕămānīm|t=Gardens of Adonis}} were dedicated to the [[lover]] of [[Ishtar]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شَقَائِق النُّعْمَان|شَقَائِق النَّعْمَان}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|[[شقيقة|شَقَائِق]] [[نعمان|النُّعْمَان]]|sing=شَقِيقَة النُّعْمَان|sing2=شَقِيق النُّعْمَان|sing2g=m}}

# {{vern|poppy anemone}} ({{taxlink|Anemone coronaria|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|حَبَّبَوْر|شَقِر|دَيْدَحَان}}
# [[sea anemone]] (any [[polyp]] of the order {{taxfmt|Actiniaria|order}})

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|شَقَائِق|mod=نُعْمَان|idafa=def-coll|sing=شَقِيقَة|sing2=شَقِيق|pauc=شَقِيقَات}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa|شقایق|tr=šaqâyeq|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:he:Grunwald:1901|page=138}}
* {{R:he:Kerber:1897|page=55}}
* {{R:Lagarde-Semitica|volume=1|page=32}}
* {{R:grc:Langkavel|page=147}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Pflanzen|page=201}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=2|page=367}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=3|pages=118–119}}

{{C|ar|Buttercup family plants|Sea anemones}}
