===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|waterfall}}
From {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, but badly attested there, see {{m|ar|شِلَّة|t=hank, skein}} for what is attested in Aramaic; however {{cog|he-mis|-}} offers an exact {{m|he|שלולית|t=torrent, cataract etc.}}. Contaminated the root {{ar-root|ش ل ل}} with meanings of [[flow|flowing on]] or [[pour|pouring forth]] if those are not separately borrowed from other badly attested Aramaic forms for “flowing”.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|شَلَّالَة}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شَلَّال}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَلَّال|m|pl=شَلَّالَات}}

# [[waterfall]]

