Page 11433 شلة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ش|ل|ل}} meaning "to be taken away", "to pour forth or scatter", "to drive away or chasing off in groups"; applied to herds of camels and to companies of men.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شَلَّة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَلَّة|f|pl=شَلَّات}}

# [[clique]], [[squad]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَلَّة|f|pl=شَلَّات}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from a form related to {{bor|ar|syc|ܫܶܠܳܠܳܐ|tr=šəlālā|t=suture; implication, convoluted situation; stonelet (?); *skein}}, cognate with {{cog|ar|سَلِيلَة|t=oblong strips of muscles; a long slice of material;}}; see also {{m|ar|شَلِيل|t=wrap of cloth used as padding under the rear of a camel's saddle}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شِلَّة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شِلَّة|f|pl=شِلَل}}

# [[hank]], [[skein]]; [[clew]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شِلَّة|f|pl=شِلَل}}

