Page 11450 شمال: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ش م ل}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*šimāl-}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|שְׂמֹאל|t=left|tr=s'mól}}, {{cog|akk|šumēlum|𒆏|tr=šumēlum|t=left side}}, {{cog|arc|סְמָלָא|tr=səmālā}} / {{m|syc|ܣܡܠܐ|tr=semmālā|t=left side}}, {{cog|cop|ϣⲙⲟⲩⲗ}}, {{cog|uga|𐎌𐎎𐎀𐎍}}. The north sense derives from the left-hand side facing the sunrise, also attested in {{cog|xsa|𐩠𐩦𐩱𐩣𐩡|t=to be northward}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شِمَال}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شِمَال|f|pl=أَشْمُل|pl2=شَمَائِل|pl3=شُمُل}}

# [[left]] [[hand]]
# [[left]] [[side]]
# [[bad]] [[omen]]
# [[handful]] of [[ears]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شِمَال|pl=أَشْمُل|pl2=شَمَائِل|pl3=شُمُل}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ar|يَسَار}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|ar|يَمِين}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}
* “Proto-Semitic Root: *ŝimaʔl-; Number 2218” in [[w:Georgiy_Starostin|Georgiy Starostin]], [http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2fsemham%2fsemet&text_number=2218&root=config Tower of Babel], Copyright 1998-2003 by S. Starostin.

===Etymology 2===
From the root {{ar-root|ش|م|ل}} meaning “to {{l|en|bundle}}, “to {{l|en|wrap}}”, “to {{l|en|huddle}}”, “to be {{l|en|cold}}” – such senses are influenced by the cold-dry northerly wind necessitating wrapping up with clothes.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شِمَال|m|pl=شَمَائِل}}

# [[case]], [[sheath]], [[wrapping]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شِمَال|pl=شَمَائِل}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}

===Etymology 3===
From the root {{ar-root|ش|م|ل}} meaning “to be {{l|en|leftward}}” – the north direction being the left-hand side facing the sunrise; constrast with {{m|ar|اَلْيَمَن}}, originally denoting one's right-hand side, before developing the sense of "the south". Additionally it is relatable to the root meaning “to {{l|en|bundle}}” or “to {{l|en|wrap}}”, as the cold northern wind necessitated wrapping up with clothes, contrasting with {{m|ar|جَنُوب|t=south}} from the root {{ar-root|ج|ن|ب|nocat=1}} meaning “changing”, “laying aside” clothes, the warm southern wind allowing to put off clothes.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شَمَال}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-شمال.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَمَال|m}}

# [[north]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَمَال}}

=====Coordinate terms=====
* {{list:compass points/ar}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَمَال|f|pl=شَمَالَات}}

# [[north]] [[wind]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَمَال|pl=شَمَالَات}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|شمل}}

{{C|ar|Compass points|Wind}}

