# [[light]], [[agile]], [[active]], [[swift]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|شِمْر|cpl=-}}

===Etymology 2===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|شمرة (نبات)}}
From {{der|ar|arc|-}}, where attested forms include {{cog|tmr|סִמְרָא}}, {{m|arc|סִימְרָא|tr=simrā}}, absolute state {{m|arc|סְמַר|tr=smar}}, {{cog|jpa|שומרא|tr=šummārā}}, {{cog|syc|ܫܲܡܵܪܵܐ|tr=šammārā}} and {{m|syc|ܫܘܼܡܵܪܵܐ|tr=šummārā}}, all meaning fennel, deriving from {{der|ar|akk|𒌑𒄩|tr=šimru, simru|t=fennel}}, also found in {{cog|he|שומר|שֻׁמָּר|tr=šummā́r|t=fennel}} and {{m|he|tr=šāmī́r|שָׁמִיר|t=dill}}, and likely {{cog|uga|𐎘𐎎𐎗|t=likely fennel}}. Related to {{cog|xcl|շամրայ}}, {{m|xcl|շումրայ}}, a Semitic borrowing.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|شَمَار|شَمْرَة|شُمْرَة|شَوْمَر|شَوْمَار}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَمَر|m}}

# [[fennel]] {{gloss|{{taxfmt|Foeniculum|genus}} gen.}}
#: {{syn|ar|رَازِيَانَج|بَسْبَاس}}
# [[dill]] {{gloss|{{taxfmt|Anethum graveolens|species}}}}
#: {{syn|ar|رَازِيَانَج}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَمَر}}

===Etymology 3===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|شمر (قبيلة)}}
From {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}} {{m|xsa|𐩦𐩣𐩧}}, occurring already [[BCE]], in the earliest [[Middle Sabaean|Middle]] {{cog|xsa|-}} inscriptions.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|شَمَّر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|شَمَّر|m}}

