Page 11486 شن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|ش ن ن}}
{{bor|ar|ira-mid}} borrowings related to {{cog|fa|شنا|tr=šanā|t=swimming}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شَنَّ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:شَنّ}}

# to [[launch]] (war; campaign)
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[pour]], to let [[flow]], to [[toss]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى<over>}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 800|authorlink=Sa'id ibn Aws al-Ansari|author=ar:أبو زيد سعيد بن أوس الأنصاري<tr:ʔabū zayd saʕīd ibn ʔaws al-ʔanṣārīy>|title=ar:كتاب النوادر|trans-title=Buch der Seltenheiten}} {{R:ar:Fleischer-KS|volume=3|page=484}}:
#*: {{quote|ar|يَا كَرَوَانًا ضُكَّ فَأَكْبَأَنَّا <br/>فَ'''شَنَّ''' بِٱلسَلْخِ فَلَمَّا '''شَنَّا''' … بَلَّ ٱلذُنَابَى عَبَسًا مُبِنَّا|t=You thick-knee! Which when bumped will clew and '''toss''' dung and having '''hurled''' … moistens the tail with sticky soil!}}
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[don]], to [[put on]] ({{m|ar|دِرْع}})

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:شَنّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|شَنّ|m|sing=شَنَّة|pl=شِنَان}}

# [[waterskin]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|ibnmajah|30|62|passage= " إِنْ كَانَ عِنْدَكَ مَاءٌ بَاتَ فِي '''شَنٍّ''' فَٱسْقِنَا وَإِلَّا كَرَعْنَا " . قَالَ عِنْدِي مَاءٌ بَاتَ فِي '''شَنٍّ''' . فَٱنْطَلَقَ وَٱنْطَلَقْنَا مَعَهُ إِلَى ٱلْعَرِيشِ فَحَلَبَ لَهُ شَاةً عَلَى مَاءٍ بَاتَ فِي '''شَنٍّ''' فَشَرِبَ ثُمَّ فَعَلَ مِثْلَ ذَٰلِكَ بِصَاحِبِهِ ٱلَّذِي مَعَهُ .|t=‘If you have any water that has been kept overnight in a '''water skin''', then give us some to drink, otherwise we will drink by putting out mouths in the basin.’ He said: ‘I have water that has been kept in a '''water skin'''. So he went and we went with him, to the shelter, where he milked a sheep for him and (mixed it with) the water that had been kept overnight in a '''water skin'''. He drank from it, then he did likewise for his Companion who was with him.”}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|شَنّ|pl=شِنَان}}

===Derived terms===
* {{l|ar|شَنِين|t=trickling; milk to which water is added}}
* {{l|ar|شَنُون|t=pudgy: somewhat fat, somewhat meagre}}
* {{l|ar|شُنَانَة|t=dribbling water}}
* {{l|ar|أَشَنَّ|t=to launch, to send; to be used up}}
* {{l|ar|تَشَنَّنَ|t=to be old, to be used up}}
* {{l|ar|تَشَانَّنَ|t=to be mixed; to be corrugated}}
* {{l|ar|اِسْتَشَنَّ|t=to become meagre; to be old, to be used; to want to drink milk}}
* {{l|ar|شَنَان|t=raft}}
* {{l|ar|شُنَان|t=diffused, spread}}

