Page 11545 شوفان: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Avena sativa55.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|شُوفَان}}]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar|mul=شوفان (جنس)}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܫܘܦܢܐ|t=friction|tr=šūp̄ānā}}, which comes from the verb {{m|syc|ܫܳܦ|tr=šāp̄|t=to file, to scrape}} corresponding to the Arabic verb {{m|ar|شَافَ|t=to polish}}, as for the handling of the grain removing the husk by rubbing, grating, polishing is characteristic. There is also {{cog|he|שיפון|tr=šīp̄ōn|t=oat; (later) rye}}, so that formation is apparently Proto-Northwest Semitic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شُوفَان}}
* {{rhymes|ar|aːn|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|شُوفَان|m}}

# [[oat]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|شُوفَان}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=465}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=1|pages=686–690}}
* {{R:Payne Smith 1903|page=597}}

{{C|ar|Grains}}
