#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 869|authorlink=al-Jahiz|author=ar:الْجَاحِظ|title=ar:التَبَصُّر بِٱلتِّجَارَة|chapter=ar:باب ما يُعتبر من الجواهر النفيسة ومعرفتها وقيمتها<t:About how one esteems precious gems, their morphology and value>|url=https://www.hindawi.org/books/73505194/2/|passage=وخيرُ الفيروزجِ الشيربامُ الأخضر الأسمانجوني الصافي العتيق، والفيروزج حجر لا يعمل المبردُ فيه، ولا يتغير في النار والماء الحار، وغايةُ ثَمَنِ فص فيروزج إذا بلغ وزنه نصف مثقال عشرون دينارًا.|t=The best turquoise is milk-white, green with blue gleam, pure and old. It is a stone upon which the file cannot work and which cannot be altered by heat or water. The highest price for a turquoise gem when it reaches a weight of half a miṯqāl is twenty dinars.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|شِيرْبَام|f=شِيرْبَام|pl=شِيرْبَام|fpl=شِيرْبَام|d=شِيرْبَام:tri|fd=شِيرْبَام:tri}}

{{C|ar|Whites}}
-------- end text --------
Page 11571 شيرة: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|شَيْرَى|شَيْرُون}}

===Etymology===
Surely an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing, with varying reflex of the [[emphatic state]] and ''-ōn'' diminutive ending, probably a particular sense of {{m|arc|שֵׁירָא}} / {{m|syc|ܫܶܐܪܳܐ|tr=šērā}}, otherwise known as “bracelet” like {{doublet|ar|سِوَار|notext=1}} and also a kind of ring-shaped restraint around the head of a beast.

There is also {{cog|tmr|שׁוּגְרְיָא|tr=šūgrəyā|t=basket woven of palm-leaves for dates}}, derived from {{cog|akk|𒋗𒍀|tr=šu-guru<sub>5</sub>|ts=šugrû|t=basket; a processed form of dates}} and that from {{noncog|sux|𒋗𒍀|tr=šu-guru<sub>5</sub>}}, passed also into Arabic as {{m|ar|شَوْغَرَة|t=pannier of dates}}.

{{m|ar|شَجَر}}, also vocalized in a foreign fashion {{m|ar|شِجَر}} and {{m|ar|شِجَار}}, used in the meaning “fig trees” in al-Andalus and Morocco, may be a kindred borrowing, the etymon being attested as {{m|arc|שִׁיגְרָא}}, {{m|arc|שִׁגְרָא|tr=šiḡrā|t=dried or pressed dates}}. As in {{m|ar|ثَمَر|t=fruits}} against {{m|ar|تَمْر|t=dates}}, the meaning has then generalized from “figs” to “trees”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شَيْرَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|شَيْرَة|f|pl=شَيْرَات}}

# [[thread]]ed [[fillet]] of [[sparterie]] for the [[transport]] as well as [[sale]] of [[fig]]s, [[pannier]], [[two-handed]] [[frail]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|شَيْرَة|pl=شَيْرَات}}

