Page 11576 شيزى: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|شِيز}}

===Etymology===
Apparently a variant of {{bor|ar|arc|שִׁיסְקָא|tr=šīsqā|t=jujube}} / {{m|syc|שִׁיזְפָא|tr=šīzpā|t=jujube}} / {{m|syc|ܫܝܼܙܩܵܐ|tr=šīzqā|t=jujube}} / {{m|syc|ܫܵܐܙܵܐ|tr=šāzā|t=jujube}} / {{m|syc||*ܫܝܼܙܵܐ|tr=šīzā|t=jujube}}, hence {{doublet|ar|زِفْزِف|زَيْزَفُون|nocap=1|t1=jujube|t2=jujube}}, since from the wood of various {{taxfmt|Ziziphus|genus}} species crude tools were and are made and their woods turn out to be dark.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|شِيزَى}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|شِيزَى|f}}

# a kind of [[black]] [[wood]] from which bowls were made, apparently from a {{taxfmt|Ziziphus|genus}} species
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 678|author={{w|lang=ar|الحطيئة|{{l|ar||الحطيئة}}}}|title=[https://www.aldiwan.net/poem21674.html {{lang|ar|يا لَيتَ كُلَّ خَليلٍ كُنتُ آمُلُهُ (…)}}]
|passage=إِذا يَحارُ هُداةُ الناسِ لَم يَحِرِ<br/>حَتّى إِذا القَومُ كانوا في رِحالِهِمِ<br/>كانَ الجَوادُ بِذي الفاثورِ وَالغُمَرِ<br/>قَد يَملَأُ الجَفنَةَ الشيزى فَيَترِعُها
|translation=When the guides of the people return, they thirst not, until the folks are at their camps, and the horses are at their trays and bowls, then they can fill and implete the wooden stoop.}}

