#* {{quote-book|1=ar|year=a. 965|author=w:Al-Mutanabbi|title={{link|ar||ضَيْفٌ أَلَمَّ بِرَأْسِي غَيْرَ مُحْتَشِمِ}}|url=http://www.almotanabbi.com/poemPage.do?poemId=232|passage=قَبَّلْتُهَا وَدُمُوعِي مَزْجُ أَدْمُعِهَا // وَقَبَّلَتْنِي عَلَى خَوْفٍ فَمًا لِفَمِ<br/>فَذُقْتُ مَاءَ حَيَاةٍ مِنْ مُقَبَّلِهَا // لَوْ '''صَابَ''' تُرْبًا لَأَحْيَا سَالِفَ الْأُمَمِ|t=I kissed her, and my tears mixed with hers, // and she kissed me timidly, mouth to mouth.<br/>I tasted the water of life from her kiss, // which may revive the ancestors, if it '''hit''' the earth.}}
