Page 11720 صانونة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Probably an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} diminutive, form as in {{m|ar|جَامُور}}, {{m|ar|شَاقُول}} etc., from the etymon of {{m|ar|صِنّ}}, {{m|ar|صَنّ|t=a kind of basket with a lid}}, since without modern equipment it must have been some smaller [[crockware]] rather than the currently most frequent metal pans that contain the dip.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَانُونَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صَانُونَة|f}} {{tlb|ar|collective}}

# {{tlb|ar|Yemen}} [[hot sauce]], [[gravy]] or spicy [[stew]] from [[vegetable]]s usually joined with [[fish]] or [[meat]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:{{w|lang=ar|وجدي الأهدل|وَجْدِيّ الْأَهْدَل}}|title=ar:أرض المؤامرات السعيدة|year=2018|isbn=978-614-469-069-7|publisher=Nawfal / Hachette Antoine|location=Bayrūt|page=156–157|passage=أَنَا طَبَخْتُ '''صَانُونَةَ''' سَمَكٍ وَكَبْسَةَ أُرُزٍّ بِاللَّحْمِ. وَطَبَخَتْ تَاتْيَانَا بَاسْتَا بِاللَّحْمِ، وَشُورْبَةَ الْمَلْفُوفِ بِالطَّرِيقَةِ الرُوسِيّةِ {{lang|en|(Shchi)}}.|t=I prepared fish '''sanoona''' and rice [[kabsa]] with meat, and Tatyana pasta with meat, and a Russian-style cabbage soup ([[shchi]]).}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|صَانُونَة}}

{{C|ar|Sauces}}
