Page 11876 صغا: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{ar-root|ص|غ|و}}, meaning incline or lean.<ref name="Lane">“صغى and صغو” in Edward William Lane (1863), Arabic-English Lexicon, London: Williams & Norgate, pages 1692-1693, meaning to incline, bend, lean, to sway emotion or opinion, to give ear or to listen, to slant, to bend a scale or to cheat someone, to be someone relied upon, a special ally in a time of need, one leaned on.</ref>

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I.ipass?.vn:صَغْو,صُغُوّ}}

# to [[incline]], to [[bend]], to [[lean]]
# to [[incline]] one's [[ear]], to [[hearken]], to [[listen]]

