Page 11881 صف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Of the root {{ar-root|ص|ف|ف}}. Potentially an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing, {{doublet|ar|ضَفَّ|t1=to push, to throng, to jam, to collect together|nocap=1}}, the cognate of which is attested in the passive participle as {{cog|tmr|צְפִיפ|tr=ṣəp̄īp̄|t=crowded, pushed into}}, while the noun is also found as {{cog|tmr|צַפָּא|tr=ṣappā|t=row}}, a relative of which would be {{cog|jpa|צפד|tr=ṣfd|t=to weave}}, as this meaning is present in Arabic in an extended root {{cog|ar|ضَفَرَ|t=to weave, to plait}}, though the example of {{m|ar|عَصًا}} shows that rarely {{der|ar|sem-pro||*ṣ́}} inherited as {{cog|ar||ص}} is possible. Compare the suspicious term {{m|ar|صَفَد|t=fetter, shackle}}, as well as {{m|ar|رَفّ|t=shelf, a part of furniture where one rows things into}}, and {{m|ar|صُفَّة|t=bench}} is also a borrowing and possibly related to the root.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|صَفّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|صَفّ|m|pl=صُفُوف}}

# [[row]], [[line]] {{qualifier|[[sequence]] of [[people]] or [[objects]]}}
# [[battle]] [[order]] {{qualifier|[[arrangement]] of [[soldiers]] in [[battle]]}}
# [[setting]] in [[type]]
# [[year]], [[grade]], [[form]]
# [[class]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|صَفّ|pl=صُفُوف}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|az|səff|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|صف|bor=1}}
** {{desc|dv|ސަފު|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ota|صف|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|saf|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|safu|bor=1}}
* {{desc|uz|saf|bor=1}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:صَفّ}}

# to line up, align
# to compose, classify
# to [[park]] (a car)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:صَفّ}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb-form|صِفْ|I}}

# {{inflection of|ar|وَصَفَ||2|m|s|actv|impr}}

