-------- end text --------
Page 11891 صفد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
In view of the restricted meanings, exposing only denominal verbs, probably an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} borrowing, with the original form seen in {{cog|syc|ܨܦܕܐ|tr=ṣep̄dā|t=book binding; pitcher of wine}}, evidently only two fragments of a more general meaning, suggested by {{cog|jpa|צפד|tr=ṣfd|t=to weave}}. The other Arabic form {{m|ar|صِفَاد}} is secondary, a pattern popular for fasteners and instruments of a certain kind, see {{m|ar|شِكَال}}, or even back-formed in dialects from the plural as with {{m|ar|زِنَاد}} instead of {{m|ar|زَنْد}}. Probably to be traced to a biliteral root, found in {{m|syc|ܨܦܘܦܐ|tr=ṣappūp̄ā|t=fetters, clogs}}, {{cog|ar|ضَفَّ|t=to push, to throng, to jam}}, extended in {{cog|ar|ضَفَرَ|t=to weave, to plait}}, while {{m|ar|صَفَّ|t=to line}} may be an Aramaic borrowing again. {{cog|ar|كِبْل}} and {{m|ar|قَيْد}} are also Aramaisms.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَفَدَ}} (verb I)
* {{ar-IPA|صَفَّدَ}} (verb II)
* {{ar-IPA|صَفَد}} (noun)

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.vn:صَفْد,صُفُود}}

# to  [[bind]], to [[tie]], to [[shackle]], to [[fetter]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.vn:صَفْد,صُفُود}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to  [[bind]], to [[tie]], to [[shackle]], to [[fetter]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صَفَد|m|pl=أَصْفَاد}}

# [[chain]], [[shackles]]
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} [[present]], [[donation]], something [[bind|bound]] to be [[gift]]ed to someone

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|صَفَد|pl=أَصْفَاد}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|صَفَد|f}}

# {{place|ar|city|c/Israel|t1=Safed}}

