Page 11896 صفصاف: -------- begin text --------
[[File:20161026Salix matsudana tortuosa1.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|صَفْصَافَة}}|upright=1.35]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|صِرْصَاف||Al-Andalus}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ص|ف|ف}} meaning to be in rows, to grow parallel, possibly in reference to the branch shape. Alternatively, from this sense of being side by side there is also the meaning to gather together at water, as willows are prone to do. There is potentially also a connection to the {{onomatopoeic|ar|nocap=1}} sense of whistling, to rustle, perhaps semantically related to "{{m|en|weeping}}" in {{noncog|en|weeping willow}}. Cognate to {{cog|he|צַפְצָפָה|tr=ṣap̄ṣāp̄á|t=willow; vines or dangling vine-like branches}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَفْصَاف}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|صَفْصَاف|sing=صَفْصَافَة|pl=صَفَاصِف}}

# [[willow]] ({{taxfmt|Salix|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|خِلَاف|غَرَب}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|صَفْصَاف|pl=صَفَاصِف}}

