Page 11914 صقر: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|صَاقُور|زَقْر}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|ar}} with possible connections:
* The root {{ar-root|ص|ق|ر}} meaning "to rise high in elevation or temperature", "to boil or build up"; possibly derived {{onomatopoeic|ar|title=[[w:onomatopoeia|onomatopoeically]]}} from a bird-of-prey's screeching cry or the screech of steam escaping. Related to {{cog|akk|𒁲 𒊑|tr=zaqāru|lit=to build high}}; for more see {{m|en|ziggurat}}.
* Distantly related to {{cog|egy|zkr|<hiero>z:k:r-A40</hiero>|tr=zkr|t=[[w:Seker|Sakar]]}} an important hawk-headed god of [[w:Saqqara|Saqqara]], the main funerary site of the Ancient Egyptian capital [[w:Memphis,_Egypt|Memphis]]. Itself being derived from varying etymologies; perhaps ultimately from a [[w:Proto-Afroasiatic_language|Proto-Afroasiatic]] root.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ar|/sˤaqr/}}

===Noun===
