Page 11928 صلاة: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|Salah}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|صَلَوٰة|tr=ṣalāh||classical spelling}}

===Etymology===
Normalized spelling of earlier {{m|ar|صَلَوٰة|tr=ṣalāh}}, from {{bor|ar|syc|ܨܠܘܬܐ|ܨܠܘܬ|tr=ṣəlōṯ}}, whence the denominal root {{ar-root|ص|ل|و}}. It is also thought to be derived from the root {{ar-root|و|ص|ل}}. Compare {{cog|uga|𐎕𐎍𐎚}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَلَاة}}
** {{IPA|afb|/sˤə.ɫaːt/|a=Persian Gulf}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صَلَاة|f|pl=صَلَوَات}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|صَلَّى|form=II}}
# [[prayer]] in general; spontaneous prayer
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|9|103|passage=وَصَلِّ عَلَيْهِمْ إِنَّ '''صَلَاتَكَ''' سَكَنٌ لَهُمْ|subst=وَصَلِّ/وَ-صَلِّ}}
#: {{ux|ar|يُؤَدِّي اَلْمُسْلِمُونَ اَلْصَلَاةَ خَمْسَ مَرّاتٍ فِي اَلْيَوْمِ|Muslims perform the prayer five times a day.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|17|110
|passage=قُلِ ٱدْعُوا ٱللَّهَ أَوِ ٱدْعُوا ٱلرَّحْمَٰنَ أَيًّا مَا تَدْعُوا فَلَهُ ٱلْأَسْمَاءُ ٱلْحُسْنَى وَلَا تَجْهَرْ '''بِصَلَاتِكَ''' وَلَا تُخَافِتْ بِهَا وَٱبْتَغِ بَيْنَ ذَٰلِكَ سَبِيلًا
|translation=Say (to them, O Mohammed): Call upon (Him by) "God" or call upon (Him by) "''ar-Raḥmân''" ("The Merciful One"); whichever you call upon (Him by), (remember that) the most beautiful of names belong to Him; and be not very loud in '''your prayers''' nor be very quiet but follow a way in between.
|subst=فَلَهُ/فَ-لَهُ,وَلَا/وَ-لَا,بِصَلَاتِكَ/بِ-صَلَاتِكَ,وَٱبْتَغِ/وَ-ٱبْتَغِ}}
# [[place of worship]], especially of the [[Jews]], hence a [[synagogue]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|22|40|passage=وَلَوْلَا دَفْعُ ٱللهِ ٱلنَّاسَ بَعْضَهُمْ بِبَعْضٍ لَّهُدِّمَتْ صَوَامِعُ وَبِيَعٌ وَّ'''صَلَوَاتٌ''' وَّمَسٰجِدُ يُذْكَرُ فِيهَا ٱسْمُ ٱللهِ كَثِيرًا|t=And were it not that God checks some people by others there in fact would have been demolished churches and monastic cells, and '''synagogues''' and mosques wherein the name of God is oft-mentioned.}}
# {{lb|ar|Islam}} [[salat]], [[namaz]], [[prayer]]
