Page 11940 صلعم: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|peace be upon him}}

===Etymology===
From {{m|ar|صَلَّىٰ ٱللَّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ|t=may God bless him and grant him peace}}. The proper noun is re-vocalized from the initialism.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَلْعَم}}

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=صلعم|tr=ṣ.l.ʕ.m.}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam|eulogy|proscribed|[[initialism]]}} [[PBUH]] (“[[peace be upon him]]”, following mention of the prophet [[Muhammad]]).

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|صَلَّىٰ ٱللَّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ||unabbreviated}}
* {{alter|ar|ﷺ||Unicode ligature}}
* {{alter|ar|صلٓعم||typographic variant}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ba|с.ғ.с.}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|صَلْعَم|m}}

# {{lb|ar|pejorative|offensive}} [[Mahomet]] {{gloss|a [[derogatory]] term for the [[prophet]] of [[Islam]]}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|صَلْعَم|state=ind-def}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|صَلْعَمِيّ|t=[[mudslime]], [[Mahometist]]}}

{{cln|ar|expressions}}
-------- end text --------
Page 11941 صلعمي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-etym-nisba|صَلْعَم}}. From {{m|ar|صَلْعَم|pos=but rarely so pronounced}}, an acronym or alteration of {{m|ar|صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ|t=May Allah bless him and grant him peace}}, a religious [[eulogy]] that typically follows the mentioning of [[Muhammad]], the prophet of Islam, with the acronym turning into a derogatory denomination of Muhammad himself.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَلْعَمِيّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صَلْعَمِيّ|m|f=صَلْعَمِيَّة|pl=صَلاعِمة}}

# {{lb|ar|slang|religious slur}} a [[mudslime]], a [[muzzie]], a [[Mahometist]] {{gloss|a Muslim}}
#: {{syn|ar|شارِب بَوْل بَعِير|t=drinker of camel piss}}

====Usage notes====
The word is part of the slang of Arabic-speaking non-Muslims, and in particular non-theists, who have formed quite numerous and very active internet communities (particularly since the {{w|Arab Spring}} and {{w|ISIS}}). Muhammad is oftentimes called {{m|ar|صَلْعَم}} by such groups to avoid the positive significations of his name, which is the passive participle of {{m|ar|حَمَّدَ}}, thus meaning (“the Blessed”, “the Praised”).

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|صَلْعَمِيّ|pl=صَلاعِمة}}

{{C|ar|People}}
-------- end text --------
