Page 11950 صليب: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ص ل ب}}

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|צְלִיבָא}} / {{m|syc|ܨܠܻܝܒܳܐ|tr=ṣəlīḇā}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒁇|ts=ṣalāpu|t=to cross out, to pervert; to give difficulty or be crooked, not be easy or straight}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|صَلِيب|m|pl=صُلْبَان|pl2=صُلُب}}

# [[cross]] {{gloss|geometrical figure}}
#: {{ux|ar|inline=y|اَلصَّلِيب اَلْجَنُوبِيّ|t=Southern Cross}}
# {{lb|ar|also|_|Christianity}} [[cross]], [[Cross]], [[crucifix]] {{gloss|post for crucifixion}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|46|37
|passage=لَا تَقُومُ السَّاعَةُ حَتَّى يَنْزِلَ فِيكُمُ ٱبْنُ مَرْيَمَ حَكَمًا مُقْسِطًا، فَيَكْسِرَ الصَّلِيبَ، وَيَقْتُلَ الْخِنْزِيرَ، وَيَضَعَ الْجِزْيَةَ، وَيَفِيضَ الْمَالُ حَتَّى لَا يَقْبَلَهُ أَحَدٌ
|translation=The hour will not arise until the son of Mary comes down upon you as a just ruler, and he will destroy the cross, and he will kill the swine, and abolish the jizya, and fortunes will overflow so that nobody will accept them as gifts.}}

