===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|ص م غ}}
{{uncertain|ar}}. Maybe a variant of {{m|ar|سَمْع|t=ear}}, compare {{m|ar|شَمْع|t=wax}}, otherwise {{m|ar|سَمُر|t=acacia}}. A chain of comparisons also allows to assume {{bor|ar|ira|-}} borrowing: {{m|ar|سَمْعَج|t=thick sweet milk}}, {{m|ar|زَمَج|t=gum arabic; raisins}}, {{m|ar|زَاج|t=vitriol}}, {{cog|fa-cls|زمه|tr=zama|t=vitriol, alum}}, {{m|fa-cls|زنج|tr=zunj, zanj, zinj|t=resin; chin}}, {{m|fa-cls|زنخ|tr=zanax|t=chin}}, {{m|fa-cls|زاگ|tr=zāg|t=vitriol, alum}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صَمْغ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صَمْغ|m|pl=صُمُوغ|pl2=أَصْمَاغ}}

# [[resin]]
#* {{RQ:Ibn Sina:1593|liber=2|page=174|pageurl=https://www.digitale-sammlungen.de/de/view/bsb10141160?page=867|passage=قال ديسقوريدوس في كتابه ان الحلتيث صمغ الانجدان و ذكر بان يشرط اصله وساقه ثم بعد الشرط يسيل منه الحلتيث […]|t={{w|Dioscurides}} said in his book that hing is the resin of the Ferula assa-foetida and he notified that its stem and its foot is slit and then, after the slitting, the hing flows from it. […]}}
# [[glue]]

