Page 11985 صنف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|sorta}}
In the root {{ar-root|ص|ن|ف}} one also finds {{m|ar|صِنْفَة|t=border of a garment}}, which fits {{cog|gez|ጽንፍ|t=extremity, edge, border, fringe etc.}}, suspiciously enough with alternative vocalization as in Arabic {{m|gez|ጸንፍ}}. Due to the restricted semantic range and the varying vocalization one wonders about a borrowing from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}. {{cog|arc-cpa|-}} has {{m|arc-cpa|ܨܢܦܬܐ|t=border, fringe (of a garment)}} and {{cog|jpa|צנפה|tr=ṣanpā|t=border, fringe (of a garment)}} and {{m|jpa|צנף|t=to wrap or gird oneself}}, but {{cog|tmr|סנפא}}, {{m|tmr|סינפא|tr=sinpā|t=side-room}} seems also similar, via the idea of an anyhow abstract [[pigeonhole]] or {{m|ar|خَانَة}} things are fitted into, not emphatic but no doubt related because in the same isolect there is the geminate verb {{m|tmr|סנפ|t=to gird}}, which is also found in {{cog|syc|-}}, while the Syriac base stem {{m|syc|ܣܢܱܦ|tr=snap̄}} means “to introduce, to insert”; apparently a {{w|Western Aramaic}}—{{w|Eastern Aramaic}} anlaut variation. For the meaning development in to a “sort” also contrast {{m|ar|نَمَط|t=drugget, horse-rug; pattern, manner}}.

The ultimate origin is suggested by the ''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' as ultimately {{der|ar|akk||tr=ṣiliptu|t=diagonal}}, related to {{der|ar|akk||tr=ṣalāpu|t=to distort}}, well also found in {{cog|tmr|צלפ}} / {{cog|syc|ܨܠܦ|tr=ṣlap̄|t=to split, to wound}}, the geminate stem in Syriac and {{cog|arc-jla|-}} “to perforate” and “to wound”, the Syriac causative stem “to open up as to show”, with an unemphatic variant {{cog|tmr|סלף|t=to wound}}, {{cog|arc-jla|סלף|t=to wound}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[sort]], [[classify]], or [[categorize]] something
# to [[compile]] or [[compose]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
