Page 12008 صوة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ص|و|و}} or {{ar-root|ص|و|ي}}, meaning “to be rough or dry”, “to be rugged”, “rugged elevated ground”, stemming from the Bedouin practice of using rock outcroppings to determine bearings in deserts with sparse landmarks; cognate with {{cog|sem-srb|𐩮𐩥𐩺|tr=ṣwy|t=to signify, to indicate (direction)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صُوّة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صُوّة|f|pl=صُوًى|pl2=أَصْواء}}

# {{C|ar|Landforms}} an [[elevation]] of [[terrain]] marking an [[orographic]] [[transition]], a [[foothill]], [[barrow]], [[mound]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=c. 700|author=ar:أُميَّةُ بن أَبي عائِذٍ الهُذَليّ<tr:[https://almerja.com/reading.php?ida=575&id=556&idm=30879 Umayya ibn ʾabī ʿāʾiḏ] ([[w:Banu Hudhayl|al-huḏalīy]])>|title=[[w:ar:ديوان الهذليين|Dīwān Huḏalīyīn]]|trans-title=Diwan Hodsailitarum  / Hudsailian poems / Huḏaylitendiwan|page=201 verse 38 in [[w:de:Gottfried Kosegarten (Orientalist)|Kosegarten]]’s edition<!--and a recent Arabic edition https://books.google.com/books?id=B8A_AQAAIAAJ&q="طرفة"+"الآل"+"سراب"&dq="طرفة"+"الآل"+"سراب"-->|passage=وَفِي غَمْرَةِ الْآلِ خِلْتُ الصُّوَى … عُرُوكًا عَلَى رَائِس يَقْسِمُونَا|t=In the overabundance of fogs I fancied the barrows … the mariners onto the valleyhead, dividing us}}
# [[guidepost]], [[marking]] [[sign]], [[guide|guiding]] sign

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|صُوّة|pl=صُوًى|pl2=أَصْواء}}

