Page 12026 صوم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Compare with {{cog|he|צוֹם|tr=ṣōm}}, {{cog|gez|ጾም|t=fast}}, {{cog|uga|𐎑𐎎|t=fast}}. Nöldeke was convinced that the meaning “to fast” is borrowed from the {{semantic loan|ar|arc|צומא|notext=1}} / {{m|syc|ܨܰܘܡܳܐ|tr=ṣōmā, ṣawmā|t=fast}}, referring to the verb’s meaning “to stand still”, Jeffery says that the Arabic verb is “obviously denominative from {{m|ar|صَوْم}}” and notes that the term is only used in late Qurʾānic passages. Cognate with {{cog|hy|ծոմ|t=fast}} from Aramaic.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|صَوْم}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|صَوْم|m}}

