====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# {{lb|ar|ditransitive}} to [[cause]] to [[become]], to [[render]], to [[make]]
#: {{synonyms|ar|حَوَّلَ|جَعَلَ|قَلَبَ|أَحَالَ}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''صَيَّرَتِ''' الْبُرُودَةُ الْمَاءَ جَلِيدًا.|Coldness '''turned''' the water into ice.}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''صَيَّرَ''' ٱلْحُلْوَ مَرِيرًا|'''to turn''' sweet into bitter}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ar|fishpaste}}
From {{bor|ar|arc|צִיר|tr=ṣīr|t=the own juice wherein fish is conserved; fish brine}}. Also in {{cog|he|צִיר|tr=ṣīr|t=sauce, broth, gravy, brine}}. In {{cog|syc|-}} instead with unemphatic anlaut: {{m|syc|ܣܼܝܪܵܐ|tr=sīrā}} used for the sense of small dried fish in the Grecized plural {{m|syc|ܣܼܝܪ̈ܲܣ|tr=sīras}} or {{m|syc|ܣܼܝܪܸ̈ܣ|tr=sīres}}, hence apparently identical to the “strap” word found in Arabic more usually as {{doublet|ar|سَيْر|notext=1}} than as {{m-self|ar|صَيْر}}, referring to fish so small that they would only be apprehended as a “thread”.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|صِير|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[brine]]
# {{C|ar|Fish|Condiments}} {{q|perhaps various kinds of}} [[dried]] and [[fermented]] [[river]] [[fish]], [[fry]] {{gloss|main ingredient of the [[spice]] [[paste]] {{l|ar|صِحْنَاء}}}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|صِير|m}}

