Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|צִיצִיתָא|tr=ṣīṣīṯā}}, {{m|arc|צִיצְתָא|tr=ṣīṣəṯā}}, derivates of a {{m|arc|צִיצָא|tr=ṣīṣā}}, equalling {{cog|en|tzitzit}}. The closest meaning is attested in {{cog|xcl|ցից}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|صِيصِيَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|صِيصِيَة|f|pl=صَيَاصٍ|plcons=صَيَاصِي}}

# anything [[projected]] [[apt]] for [[pick]]ing or [[get hold of|getting hold of]] things, a [[pale]], [[picket]], [[palisade]], or [[horn]] or [[spur]] of a [[beast]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 620|title=ar:أرَثَّ جَدِيدُ الْحَبْلِ مِنْ أُمِّ مَعْبَدِ … بِعَاقِبَــــةٍ وَأَخْلَفَتْ كُلَّ مَوْعِدِ<qq:[https://www.diwanalarab.com/أروع-قصائد-الرثاء-العربي first line]>|url=https://www.aldiwan.net/poem24162.html|author={{w|Dorayd bin Al Soma|Durayd ibn aṣ-Ṣuma}}|passage=فجئتُ إليه والرماح تُنوشُهُ  …   كَوَقع ا'''لصياصي''' في النَسِيج المُمَدَّدِ|t=I went upon him with spears that touched him like the '''weaver’s sticks that make warp and woof even''' are positioned between the spread webs}}
#* {{RQ:Quran|33|26|passage=وَأَنزَلَ ٱلَّذِينَ ظَـٰهَرُوهُم مِّنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْكِتَـٰبِ مِن '''صَيَاصِي'''هِمْ وَقَذَفَ فِى قُلُوبِهِمُ|t=And He brought those of the People of the Scripture who backed them down from their '''strongholds''' and cast panic into their hearts.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 813|title=unknown title|author={{w|العماني الراجز|lang=ar|ar-Rājiz}}|passage=خالي لقيطٌ ({{var}} عُوَيْف) وأبو عَلِجِّ … المطعمان اللحمَ بالعَشِجِّ<br/>وبالغداةِ كِسَرَ ({{var}} فِلَق) البَرْنِجِّ … يُقْلَعُ بالوَدِّ وبال'''صِّيصجِّ'''|t=I have two uncles ʿUwayf and Abū ʿAlī … who eat meat in the vesper,<br/>And in the morn sweet shives of dates … they pluck by means of pegs and '''pales'''|footer=Translation by {{w|Gottfried Hoberg|lang=de}}:<br/>Avunculus meus est ʿUvaif et Abû ʿAlî, qui carnem vespere porrigunt<br/>et mane dactylos suaviores, qui extrahuntur paxillo et palo<br/>}}

