Page 12061 ض: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
It is hypothesized that the original pronunciation of the letter was a pharyngealised lateral fricative {{IPAchar|/ɮˤ/}}. The sound that was represented the letter ''ḍād'' in the Arabic alphabet when it was introduced is somewhat uncertain, most likely being introduced on late 7th to early 8th centuries. Early on, its sound was merged with {{m|ar|ظ}} {{IPAchar|/ðˤ/}}, a merger that is reflected in all colloquial dialects. In dialects with stopping of dental fricatives, both were then shifted further to {{IPAchar|/dˤ/}}. When the ability to produce the sound {{IPAchar|/ɮˤ/}} waned some time after its loss from actual speech, the Quran readers reassigned the stop {{IPAchar|/dˤ/}} to {{m|ar||ض}} in order to maintain its distinction from {{m|ar||ظ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/dˤaːd/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}}
** {{IPA|ar|/dˤ/}} {{q|standard}}
** {{IPA|ar|/ðˤ/}} {{q|commonly in the Arabian Peninsula, Iraq and Tunisia.}}
** {{IPA|ar|/ɮˤ/}} {{q|hypothesized pronunciation; classical Arabic}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ض '''/''' ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض'''|tr=ḍād}}

# The fifteenth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ص}} and followed by {{l|ar|ط}}.

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|لغة الضاد}}

===Symbol===
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ض '''/''' ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض‍ '''/''' ‍ض'''|tr=ḍād}}

# The twenty-sixth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ذ}} and followed by {{l|ar|ظ}}.

===See also===
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/ض|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|ض}}]]

[[Category:Abjad numerals|3-800]]

-------- end text --------
Page 12062 ض ب ب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Probably all derived from the lizard-name, from the idea that the lizard cleaves to the ground, thus a stream that hangs in its bed, a lock latch, and a fog because it locks up sight.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

# related to [[cleave|cleaving]] to the ground

====Derived terms====
{{ar-verb forms|a|I-vn-head=ضَبّ|I=to [[cleave]] to, to [[hold]] to firmly|I2-vn-head=ضَبّ,ضُبُوب،ضَبِيب|I2-pv=a|I2=to have a gently or [[scanty]] [[flow]], to [[stream]], to [[discharge]] [[sluggish]]ly|II=to clamp or strengthen, to hold or keep by putting a {{l|ar|ضَبَّة}} around|I2-pp=-|I3-pv=i|I3-vn-head=ضَبَب|I3=to be affected by the disease termed {{l|ar|ضَبّ}}|I3-pp=-|I4-pv=a|I4=to milk with five fingers|I4-vn-head=ضَبّ|IV=to keep to, to cleave to; to grasp, to take possession of; to be or become abundant, to be copiose; to abound with lizards; to be foggy; to make flow; to speak, to express, to exclaim; to be silent, to abstain from talking; to hide, to conceal, to abscond; to cover|V=to be or become so fat that the armpits are [[chapped]] and the neck is [[short]]|V-pp=-|VII=to be packed together thightly|X=+}}

