Page 12157 ضفدع: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ض|ف|د|ع}}; ultimately from {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ṣ́Vpardiʿ-}}. Cognate to {{cog|he|צְפַרְדֵּעַ|tr=tz'fardéa}}, {{cog|arc|עֻרְדְּעָנָא|tr=ˁurdəˁānā}}, {{cog|syc|ܐܘܪ̈ܕܥܐ|tr=ˀurdˁā}}, and {{cog|uga|𐎑𐎗𐎄𐎓}}. The senses of hunger and gas are {{onom|ar|nocap=1}} in origin, by comparison of croaking and ribbiting, to a stomach rumbling with hunger and to audible gas noises.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|ضِفْدِع|ضِفْدَع|ضَفْدَع|ضُفْدُع|ضُفْدَع}}
** {{IPA|arz|/dˤif.daʕ/|/dˤuf.daʕ/|a=Egyptian}}
** Gulf Arabic: {{IPA|afb|/ðˤʊf.dəʕ/|a=Kuwait}}, {{IPA|afb|/ðˤəf.daʕ/|a=Qatar}}
* {{audio|ar|ضفدع.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|ضِفْدِع|m|head2=ضِفْدَع|head3=ضَفْدَع|head4=ضُفْدُع|head5=ضُفْدَع|pl=ضَفَادِع}}

# [[frog]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|133
|passage=فَأَرْسَلْنَا عَلَيْهِمُ ٱلطُّوفَانَ وَٱلْجَرَادَ وَٱلْقُمَّلَ وَ'''ٱلضَّفَادِعَ''' وَٱلدَّمَ آيَاتٍ مُفَصَّلَاتٍ فَٱسْتَكْبَرُوا وَكَانُوا قَوْمًا مُجْرِمِينَ
|translation=We caused to be sent upon them destruction abounding, locusts, lice, '''frogs''', and the blood, as signs of proof discernibly clear, but they had considered themselves of greater importance and had been a people who caused wrongdoing to be encouraged.
|subst=وَ/وَ-,فَأَرْسَلْنَا/فَ-أَرْسَلْنَا,فَٱسْتَكْبَرُوا/فَ-ٱسْتَكْبَرُوا}}
# {{lb|ar|metaphoric|usually|in plural}} the [[source]] of [[stomach]] [[rumbling]], the [[sound]] of [[hunger]]
#* {{quote|ar|نَقَّتْ '''ضَفَادِعُ''' بَطْنِهِ|tr=|t=He was or became hungry.|lit=The '''frogs''' of his belly croaked.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|ضِفْدِع|head2=ضِفْدَع|head3=ضَفْدَع|head4=ضُفْدُع|head5=ضُفْدَع|pl=ضَفَادِع}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|Iq.nopass}}

# to [[have]] or [[abound]] with [[frog]]s
# to [[shrink]] or [[contract]]; like the movement of a frog's abdomen when vocalizing
# to [[audibly]] [[pass gas]] or [[flatulate]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|Iq.nopass}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|ضفدع}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|ضفدع|page=1795}}
* “Proto-Semitic root: {{l|sem-pro|*ṣ̂Vpardiʕ-|*ṣ̂Vpardiʕ-}}; Number 2340” in [[w:Georgiy_Starostin|Georgiy Starostin]], [http://starling.rinet.ru/cgi-bin/response.cgi?single=1&basename=%2fdata%2fsemham%2fsemet&text_number=+2527&root=config Tower of Babel], Copyright 1998-2003 by S. Starostin.

