Page 12236 طابع: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ط ب ع}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|ar|arc|טַבְעָא}} / {{m|syc|ܛܲܒܼܥܵܐ|t=stamp, seal, die, thing made sink|tr=ṭaḇəʿā}}, as well as {{cog|he|טַבַּעַת|tr=ṭaḇáʕaṯ|t=ring, seal}} from {{der|ar|akk|ṭepûm|𒋰|tr=ṭepûm|t=to attach, to append|pos=to imprint or impress said of seals}}, from {{der|ar|akk|ṭuppum|𒁾|tr=ṭuppum|t=tablet, impressed markings in clay or other materials}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|sux|𒁾|tr=dub}}.

Alternatively, from {{der|ar|egy|ḏbꜥwt|t=signet, seal}}, presumably via {{bor|ar|he|טבעת|tr=ṭaḇáʕaṯ|t=ring, seal}}, then the above {{bor|ar|arc|טַבְעָא|tr=ṭaḇəʿā}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|egy|ḏbꜥ|t=finger, digit}}, cognate to {{cog|he|אֶצְבַּע|tr=ʔeṣbáʕ}} and {{cognate|ar|إِصْبَع|t=finger}}, presumably indicating “putting one's finger” to sign or seal a royal document.

The root {{ar-root|ط ب ع}} “related to imprinting” in Arabic is merely derived from the borrowing. {{m+|arc|טְבַע}} / {{m|syc|ܛܒܲܥ|tr=ṭbaʕ}}, {{m+|he|טָבַע|tr=ṭaḇáʕ}}, {{cog|akk|ṭebû|𒋤|tr=SUD|ts=ṭebû}}, all meaning “to sink, to be dipped or drown” etc., are rather variants of {{m|arc|צְבַע}} / {{m|syc|ܨܒܱܥ|tr=ṣḇaʿ}}, {{m|he|צָבַע|tr=ṣaḇáʕ|t=to dip, to moisten; to paint, to dye}}, see them; other meanings of the Aramaic and Hebrew roots related to “coining” and “shaping” and “specifying” are derived from the seal borrowing.

Compare {{cog|ar|خَاتَم}} representing a potential {{noncog|egy|-}} equivalent. For more on the foreign pattern {{m|ar||فَاعَل|tr=}} see {{m|ar|عَالَم|tr=}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|طَابَع|m|head2=طَابِع|pl=طَوَابِع}}

# [[postage stamp]]
# [[stamp]] {{qualifier|for [[printing]], etc.}}
# [[die]] for [[branding]]
# [[impression]], [[imprint]], [[sealing]], what a [[stamp]] or [[seal]] [[leave]]s

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|طَابَع|head2=طَابِع|pl=طَوَابِع}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ط ب ع}}
{{ar-active participle}} of {{m|ar|طَبَعَ||to [[print]]}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|طَابِع|m}}

# [[printer]] {{qualifier|person who [[print]]s}}
# person who [[seal]]s
# [[stamp]], [[mark]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|طَابِع}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|Tb(|N}}
* {{R:ar:Fischer|section=§ 62 Anm. 5|page=36}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=193}}
* {{R:ar:Garosi:2022a|page=414}}
* {{R:ar:Jeffery-Foreign|pages=208–209}}
* {{R:myz:Nöldeke|page=112}}
-------- end text --------
