Page 12262 طاعون: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Of the root {{ar-root|ط ع ن}}. The pattern suggests a borrowing from {{bor|ar|syc|ܛܳܥܘܿܢܳܐ|tr=ṭāʿōnā}} from {{m|syc|ܛܥܷܢ|tr=ṭʿen|t=to carry}}, related to {{cog|ar|ظَعَنَ|t=to depart}}, though the Syriac is not known to mean a disease but “carrier”. The semantic evolution would either be via “to carry as a burden, to endure“ with the ailment understood as hardship, or via “transport” developing the meaning of transmission, the plague being transmitted quickly by [[vector]]s. Compare also the other Arabic name of the disease, {{m|ar|مُوتَان}} from another Semitic language.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|طَاعُون}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طَاعُون|m|pl=طَوَاعِين}}

# [[epidemic]] [[disease]], [[plague]], [[pestilence]], [[pest]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|طَاعُون|pl=طَوَاعِين}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|وَبَأ}}, {{l|ar|وَبَاء}}, {{l|ar|مُوتَان}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|az|taun|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|ms|taun}}
** {{desc|id|taun}}
* {{desc|bor=1|ML.|althaum|althoin}}
* {{desctree|ota|طاعون|tr=taʼun|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|طاعون|bor=1}}
**{{desc|ur|طاعُون|bor=1}}
**{{desc|gu|તાઊન|bor=1}}
* {{desc|uz|toun|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|T(wn%232|N}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=265}}
* {{R:Steiger-Voces|page=53}}

{{C|ar|Vector-borne diseases|Bacterial diseases}}

