Page 12264 طاغوت: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=de|Tāghūt}}

===Etymology===
Ordered at the root {{ar-root|ط غ و}} or {{ar-root|ط غ ي}} related to {{l|en|transgression}} and explained as a being “transgressing the law”. However it is considered a loanword:
* from {{bor|ar|gez|ጣዖት|t=idol}}, from {{der|ar|he|טָעוּת|tr=ṭaʿút|t=error}}, from {{der|ar|tmr, jpa|טעותא|tr=ṭaʿúta|t=idol, false god}}
* with Wahib Atallah from {{der|ar|egy|ḏḥwtj|t={{l|en|Thoth}}}} as a personification of superstitious practices, while he sees {{m|ar|جِبْت}} used with {{m-self|ar|طَاغُوت}} in {{l|en|hendiadys}} in Qurʾān 4:51 as reflecting [[Hijazi]] pronunciation of {{m|ar|قِبْط|t=Egyptians}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|طَاغُوت}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طَاغُوت|m|pl=طَوَاغِيت}}

# [[idol]], [[juggernaut]], [[taghut]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|256
|passage=لَا إِكْرَاهَ فِي ٱلدِّينِ قَد تَّبَيَّنَ ٱلرُّشْدُ مِنَ ٱلْغَيِّ فَمَن يَكْفُرْ '''بِٱلطَّاغُوتِ''' وَيُؤْمِن بِٱللَّهِ فَقَدِ ٱسْتَمْسَكَ بِٱلْعُرْوَةِ الْوُثْقَى لَا ٱنْفِصَامَ لَهَا وَٱللَّهُ سَمِيعٌ عَلِيمٌ
|translation=There shall be no compulsion in the religion. The right course has become clear from the wrong. So whoever disbelieves '''in false idols''' and believes in God has grasped the most trustworthy handhold with no break in it. And God is Hearing and Knowing.
|subst=وَيُؤْمِن//وَ-يُؤْمِن,بِٱللَّهِ//بِ-ٱلَّهِ,وَٱللَّهُ//وَ-ٱلَّهُ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|طَاغُوت|pl=طَوَاغِيت}}

