===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ط ر ط ر}} which means in the {{ar-form|I|verb form}} “to be elevated”, further “to be {{l|en|glorify|glorified}}”. Presumably a dialectal augment of {{ar-root|ط ر ط}}, of which {{ar-form|I|verb form}} {{m|ar|طَرِطَ|t=to be a fool; to have tiny hairs}}, adjective {{m|ar|طَرِط|t=foolish; having tiny hairs}}, related due to the hats being made of {{l|en|felt}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|طَرْطُور}}, {{ar-IPA|طُرْطُور}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طَرْطُور|head2=طُرْطُور|m|pl=طَرَاطِير}}

# [[bonnet]]
# a kind of hat worn by [[dervish]]es
# [[fool's cap]]
# {{lb|ar|informal}} [[wimp]], [[wuss]], [[weak sister]], someone who is not able to [[assert]] himself
# {{lb|ar|informal}} [[pass water|passing water]], an act of [[urination]]

====Declension====
