Page 12398 طفيل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Diminutive of {{m|ar|طِفْل|t=little child}}, though in the sense of “parasite” perhaps a backformation from the commoner adjective {{m|ar|طُفَيْلِيّ}}. Ancient Arabic lexicographers explained this sense as being derived from the name of a certain man called ''Ṭufayl'', who, among the ancient Arabs, used to [[gatecrash]] feasts. However, a derivation directly from the diminutive sense might also make sense. {{cog|he|טַפִּיל|tr=tapil|t=parasite}} is a 19th-century invention based on the Arabic word.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طُفَيْل|m}}

# {{lb|ar|biology}} [[parasite]]
# {{diminutive of|ar|طِفْل|t=little child}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|طُفَيْل}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|عِلْم الطُفَيْلِيَّات|t=[[parasitology]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل الطُفِيلِى|t=[[hyperparasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل خَارِجِيّ|t=[[ectoparasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل دَاخِلِيّ|t=[[endoparasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|ّطُفَيْل مِيكْرُوسْكُوبِي|t=[[microparasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل إِجْبَارِيّ|t=[[obligate parasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|ّطُفَيْل نَصْفِي|t=[[hemiparasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل حَيَوَانِيّ|t=[[zooparasite]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل دَمَوِيّ|t=[[hematozoon]]}}
* {{l|ar|طُفَيْل مَعَوِي|t=[[enterozoon]]}}
* {{l|ar|ّمَرَض طُفَيْلِي|t=[[parasitic disease]]}}
