Page 12400 طقس: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2017|September|25}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܛܟܣܐ|tr=ṭekkəsā}}, from {{der|ar|grc|τάξις||arrangement}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|طَقْس}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-طقس.ogg}}
** {{IPA|arz|/tˤaʔs/|a=Egyptian}}
** {{IPA|ary|/tˤaqs/|a=Moroccan}}
** {{IPA|apc|/tˤaʔs/|a=North Levantine}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طَقْس|m|pl=طُقُوس}}

# [[weather]] {{q|usually used for short period meteorological changes}}
#: {{ux|ar|أُحِبُّ الطَّقْسَ اللَّطِيفِ وَالْمَشْمِسِ فِي فَصْلِ الرَّبِيعِ.|I love the nice and sunny weather in the spring season.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|year=2003
|author=Muhammed Ibn al-Hassan al-Hajwi
|url=http://www.alwaraq.net/Core/SearchServlet/searchone?docid=2172&searchtext=2LfZgtiz&option=1&offset=1&WordForm=1&exactpage=8&totalpages=1&AllOffset=1
|title=ar:الرحلة الأوروبية 1919
|text=وَكُلُّ ذَٰلِكَ مَرْسُومٌ بِيَدِ رَسَّامٍ إِسْبَنْيُولِيٍّ كَانَ حَاضِرًا مَعَنَا يُرِينَا ذَٰلِكَ، وَٱلْمَقْصُودُ تَمْثِيلُ ٱلذَّوْقِ ٱلْإِسْبَنْيُولِيِّ فِي ٱلتَّصْوِيرِ ٱلْمُلَوَّنِ ٱلَّذِي يُطَابِقُ '''طَقْسَ''' أَرْضِهِمُ ٱلصَّافِيَةِ
|t=All this was painted by a Spanish painter who was present with us to show us that. The aim was to illustrate the Spanish taste in painting in colour, which matches '''the climate of''' their serene land}}
# {{lb|ar|usually|in the plural}} [[ritual]], [[rite]], [[religious]] [[practice]]
#* {{quote-book|ar
|year=1913
|author=Priest Ishaq Armala
|url=http://www.alwaraq.net/Core/SearchServlet/searchone?docid=2223&searchtext=2LfZgtiz&option=1&offset=1&WordForm=1&exactpage=4&totalpages=3&AllOffset=1
|title=ar:سياحة في طور عبدين
|text=وَعِنْدَمَا يُولَدُ ٱلْوَلَدُ يُعَمِّدُونَهُ بَعْدَ ثَمَانِيَةِ أَيَّامٍ أَوْ أَقَلَّ وَفِي ذَٰلِكَ يُخَالِفُونَ طَقْسَ أَجْدَادِهِمِ ٱلَّذِينَ كَانُوا قَضَوْا بِٱلْعِمَادِ فِي عِيدِ ٱلدَّنْحِ وَسَبْتِ ٱلنُّورِ فَقَطْ.
|t=When a child is born they baptise it after eight days or less and in doing so they violate '''the practice of''' their ancestors, who used to only baptise on the Epiphany or on Easter Saturday.}}
# {{lb|ar|usually|in the plural}} [[ritual]], [[rite]], any [[ceremonize]]d [[practice]]
#* {{quote-book|ar
|year=2000
|author=[[w:Fadhil Al Azzawi|ar:فاضل العزاوي]]
|title=ar:القلعة الخامسة
|publisher=ar:منشورات الجمل
|pages=136–137
|location=Cologne
|passage=لَمْ تَسْنَحْ لِي ٱلْفُرْصَةُ مِنْ قَبْلُ لِأَرَى رَجُلًا يُشْنَقُ وَسَطَ طُقُوسٍ خَاصَّةٍ كَمَا يَفْعَلُونَ ٱلْآنَ، لَٰكِنَّنِي إِذْ كُنْتُ طِفْلًا شَاهَدْتُ مَا يُشْبِهُ ٱلشَّنْقَ.
|t=I haven’t had the opportunity before to see a man being hanged according to the particular rites they do it now, but when I was a little boy I witnessed what hanging looks like.}}
# [[liturgy]], [[church]] [[constitution]]
# order of the ministry, clerical rank ''(Christianity)''
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} [[order]], [[organization]]

