Page 12409 طلح: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Acacia nilotica-4-yercaud-salem-India.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|طَلْح}}|250px]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ط|ل|ح}} originally meaning “to be [[successful]] or [[contented]]” as it was a [[fruit tree]] that [[camel|camels]] [[overindulge]] eating; negative associations from the root stem from the negative effects of [[overeating]]. Applied in a general way to all [[flourishing]] [[fruit-bearing]] trees, especially the eating of which is enjoyed.

Often times glossed as ''{{l|mul|Musa|t=[[banana]] tree}}'' in its Qurʾānic occurrence, though such an understanding is considered unlikely there; for more see [[w:Banana#Historical_cultivation|Banana]], their existence in Arabia at the eve of Islam<ref>Khair Tuwair Said Al
-Busaidi; Directorate General of Agriculture and Livestock Research, Ministry of Agriculture and Fisheries, Crop Production
Research Centre, Sultanate of Oman, 2013 [https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Khair_Said_Al_Busaidi/publication/277138739_Banana_domestication_on_the_Arabian_peninsula/links/5562f8b908ae8c0cab334604/Banana-domestication-on-the-Arabian-peninsula.pdf]</ref> and the possible connection of [[w:South Arabian|South Arabian]] trade routes as a potential source of the fruits' introduction to the African continent.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|طَلْح}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|طَلْح|sing=طَلْحَة|pl=طُلُوح}}

# {{taxfmt|Vachellia|genus}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|56:28-29
|passage=فِي سِدْرٍ مَّخْضُودٍ وَطَلْحٍ مَّنْضُودٍ
|translation=[They will be] among buckthorn trees with thorns removed and vachellia trees layered [with fruit]}}
# a [[fruit-bearing]] [[tree]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|طَلْح|pl=طُلُوح}}

===References===
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=4|page=67}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|طلح|pages=1865-1866}}
<references/>

{{C|ar|Mimosa subfamily plants}}
-------- end text --------
