===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|en|ton}} and {{bor|ar|fr|tonne|t=ton}}, from {{der|ar|la|tunna}}.{{dercat|ar|cel-gau}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|طَنّ|طُنّ}}
** {{IPA|acw|/tˤann/|a=Hijazi}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|طُنّ|m|pl=طِنَان|pl2=أَطْنَان}}

# [[tonne]], [[metric ton]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|طُنّ|pl=طِنَان|pl2=أَطْنَان}}

===Etymology 3===
The meaning of a bundle of reed is considered from {{bor|ar|arc|טוּנַּס|tr=ṭunnas|t=reed}}, which is attested once in {{cog|arc-jla|-}} and agrees with {{der|ar|grc|δόναξ|t=reed}}, otherwise compare {{m|arc|אֲטוּנָא|tr=ʔăṭūnā}}, {{m|arc|אֲטְוָנָא|tr=ʔăṭwānā|t=twisted strap}}, which occurs in {{cog|tmr|-}} sometimes without the [[aleph]] prothesis.

The meaning of a load, as which also the human body is easily understood, is from the common {{bor|ar|arc|טוּנָא|tr=ṭūna, ṭunnā}}, an assimilated form of {{m|arc|טְוּעֲנָא|tr=ṭūʕănā}}, {{m|arc|טְעוּנָא|tr=ṭəʕūnā|t=load, burden}}, which or a similar form is also the source of {{doublet|ar|طَاعُون|t1=plague|notext=1}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|طُنّ|sing=طُنَّة|m|pl=طِنَان|pl2=أَطْنَان}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# the human body
# [[load]] [[carry|carried]] on the [[camel]]'s [[back]] between the loads on both [[side]]s
# [[bundle]] of [[reed]]s used as a [[bearing]]
#: {{syn|ar|كَنْثَة}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|طُنّ|pl=طِنَان|pl2=أَطْنَان}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{desc|ar|طَنَب|der=1|unc=1|nolb=1}}

