Page 12496 طيب: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ط ي ب}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{der|ar|sem-pro|*ṭāb-|t=good, pleasant}}, with levelling to the typical Arabic adjective pattern ''CayyiC'' of hollow roots. Cognate with {{cog|akk|ṭābum|𒁕𒁍𒌝|tr=ṭābum}} and {{cog|hbo|טוֹב|tr=ṭoḇ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|طَيِّب}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|طَيِّب|pl=طَيِّبُونَ|f=طَيِّبَة|fpl=طَيِّبَات|el=أَطْيَب}}

# [[good]], [[wholesome]], [[nice]], [[fine]] (for example, [[beneficial]], [[favorable]], [[advantageous]]; [[moral]], [[pure]], [[clean]]; [[nutritious]], [[nourishing]], [[healthy]]; [[tasty]], [[delicious]], [[pleasant]], etc.)
#: {{ant|ar|خَبِيث}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|20|81
|passage=كُلُوا مِن طَيِّبَاتِ مَا رَزَقْنَاكُمْ وَلا تَطْغَوْا فِيهِ فَيَحِلَّ عَلَيْكُمْ غَضَبِي وَمَن يَحْلِلْ عَلَيْهِ غَضَبِي فَقَدْ هَوَى
|translation=ُO Children of Israel! Eat from '''the good and wholesome things''' of what We have allotted to you, and do not transgress with it, so My wrath does not come down upon you. Whomever My wrath comes down upon has lapsed.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 967 {{CE}}|author=Abu Al-Faraj Al-Asfahani|editor=Salah Al-Din Al-Munajjid|title=Adab Al-Ghurabā’|publisher=Dār Al-Kitāb Al-Jadīd|year_published=1972|edition=1st|page=26–27|passage=فمضينا ومعنا من الغناء والآلة والشراب كل شيء ظريف، وأقمنا بالعمر ثلاثة أيام، ومضت لنا به أوقات '''طيبة'''،|oclc=4771078795}}
# [[charming]], [[pleasant]], [[agreeable]]
# [[enjoyable]]
# [[tasty]], [[palatable]]

