Page 12509 طيفور: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Bol andalusí-Cerámica de Zaragoza-S XI.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|طيفور أندلسي}}|upright=1.55]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{sense|tray}} {{alter|ar|طَيْفُورِيَّة}}; in Saudi-Arabia currently {{m|ar|طُوفِرِيَّة}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ط ف ر}} related to jumping, for the bird. The origin of the name for the tray is hitherto unexplained. It may be accounted that the ship-name {{m|ar|طَيْفُورِيَّة}} is derived from the bird-name as ships are commonly likened to birds and then from the ship-name comes the tray-name {{m|ar|طَيْفُورِيَّة}} because the equating of ships with bowls was ubiquitous in the Middle Ages, and after that the form {{m-self|ar|طَيْفُور}} in the sense of a tray was back-formed{{back-formation|ar|notext=1}} from {{m|ar|طَيْفُورِيَّة}} by force of its tediousness in familiar life. However it also matches with {{cog|fa|تفور|tr=tafur|t=clay; earthenware}}, {{cog|xcl|թափուր|t=wooden tray}}, the same way that {{cog|ar|تَيْغَار|t=a large pot}} corresponds via {{bor|ar|arc|-}} to {{cog|fa|تغار|tr=tağâr|t=tub, through}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|طَيْفُور}}
** {{a|ar|Moroccan}} {{ary-IPA|ṭayfūr|ṭīfūr}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|طَيْفُور|m|pl=طَيَافِير|pl2=طَوَافِير}}

# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} a small [[jump]]ing [[bird]]
# {{lb|ar|archaic|except in Morocco and Saudi-Arabia}} a [[large]] [[round]] [[plate]] or [[tray]], such as used as a table for preparing [[harissa]] or [[eat]]ing on the [[ground]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|طَيْفُور|pl=طَيَافِير|pl2=طَوَافِير}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|es|ataifor|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:BehnstedtWoidich|WA2|page=142b}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=2|page=48}}
* {{cite-book|title=Jewish and Muslim Dialects of Moroccan Arabic|last=Heath|first=Jeffrey|authorlink=Jeffrey Heath|year=2013|location=London|publisher=Routledge|isbn=9781136126345|page=[https://books.google.com/books?id=SCstBgAAQBAJ&pg=PA111 111] and [https://books.google.com/books?id=SCstBgAAQBAJ&pg=PA303 303]}}

{{C|ar|Vessels}}
