Page 12557 ظهران: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{ar-root|ظ|ه|ر}} meaning to be in the center between two points, surrounded on each side.<ref>"ظهر" in Edward William Lane (1863), Arabic-English Lexicon, London: Williams & Norgate, pages 1926-1930, meaning the middle or main part, as though it meant that the back of one of them was before him, and that of another behind him, so that he was defended in either direction, having support or back up on all sides, to be in between or in the center of two other limits like the sun at noon.</ref>

The name of two cities in [[Saudi Arabia]], one wedged between the important port cities of [[w:Dammam|Dammam]] and [[w:Khobar|al-Khobar]]; the other was a historically important site in a mountain-pass between [[Yemen]].

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|ظَهْرَان|f}}

# {{place|ar|city|in the|p/Eastern Province|c/Saudi Arabia|a major center for the Saudi oil industry|t1=Dhahran}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|ظَهْرَان:di|state=ind-def}}

===References===
<references/>
