===Etymology===
The meaning of gulping or chugging may be just {{onomatopoeic|ar|nocap=1}}, as an alternative form {{m|ar|غَبَّ}} suggests, however the root is aptly described as the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} reflex of the Arabic root {{ar-root|ض ب ب|nocat=1}} related to sticking, density, tumorosity, see {{cog|syc|ܥܒܐ|tr=ʾāḇā|t=thicket; spiny-tailed lizard}}.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

# related to having it [[abundant]] and [[pouring]] [[forth]]

====Derived terms====
{{ar-verb forms|a|I=to gulp down, to chug|I-vn-head=عَبّ|V=to drink {{m|ar|عَبِيبَة}}|V-pp=-}}

* {{l|ar|ع ب ع ب|tr=ʕ-b-ʕ-b}}
* {{l|ar|عُبَب|t=husk tomato}}
* {{l|ar|عُبَاب|t=waves or billows of a torrent of water}}
* {{l|ar|يَعْبُوب|t=torrent}}
* {{l|ar|عَبِيبَة|t=the exudation of certain plants}}
* {{l|ar|عُبّ|t=breast pocket}}
* {{l|ar|أَعَبّ|t=of a fat nose}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=95}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|pages=1931–1933}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|page=684}}
