===Etymology===
It may be that {{m|ar|عَلَّ|t=perhaps}} is the original, in a meaning “hopefully not, lest”, so the ailment meanings are things expressed to “hopefully not” appear. That word, in turn, is<ref>{{cite-book|last=Bravmann|first=Meïr Max|series=Studies in Semitic Languages and Linguistics|title=Studies in Semitic Philology|year=1977|seriesvolume=6|publisher=E. J. Brill|location=Leiden|chapter=Syriac ''dalmā'' and related Arabic phenomena; Expressions based on the noun ''yawm-'' “day”|pages=327–328, 401|isbn=978-90-04-04743-3}}</ref> likely just {{m|ar|أَن}} joined to later shortened {{m|ar|لَا}}. In {{cog|apc|-}} this {{m|ar|لَعَلَّ}} is even found<ref>{{R:ar:Landberg|P|page=158 line 2}} and {{R:ar:Landberg|P|page=166 last line}}</ref> in the form {{m|apc|لَيِلَّ|tr=layilla}} as the conjunction following “to fear, to be afraid”, as {{m+|en|lest}} and {{noncog|la|nē}}.

===Root===
{{ar-root}}

