Page 12838 عالم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|עָלְמָא}} / {{m|syc|ܥܳܠܡܳܐ|tr=ʿāləmā}} or {{bor|ar|he|עוֹלָם|tr=ʿōlām}}, possibly from {{der|ar|akk|𒂖𒆷𒈬𒌋𒀀|ts=ellamu, illamu|t=front, before; both temporally and in location; coming before your time or being currently physically before you now}}.

{{rel-top|The pattern {{m|ar|فَاعَل|tr=}}}}
The pattern {{m|ar|فَاعَل|tr=}} is considered originally foreign to Arabic and Ethiopic, occurring only in likely loanwords such as {{m|ar|طَابَع}}, {{m|ar|خَاتَم}}, {{m|ar|فَالَج}}. It should be noted some of these loans are suspected to be early, such as {{m|ar|خَاتَم}} being present in Old Arabian Inscriptions and {{m|ar|عَالَم|tr=}} retaining the sound masculine plural ending in spite of being treated as a non-human plural; a feature that suggests it existed prior to the restriction of such a use exclusively for male humans; whereas one group renders known {{noncog|ira-mid|-}} suffixes, as in {{m|ar|طَابَق}} and {{m|ar|سَاذَج}} and {{m|ar|رَامَك}} and via {{cog|arc|-}} fricativized as in {{m|ar|كَامَخ}} the ending of which became {{noncog|fa-cls|ـه|tr=-a}} and {{m|fa|ـک|tr=-ak}}. Nautically, even {{noncog|dra|-}} borrowings with this measure like {{m|ar|طَالَم}} are possible early. Consequently due to its early appearance, the {{m|ar||فَاعَل|tr=}} pattern has since become a sparsely used coined pattern in its own right, typically however still being reserved for loanwords using the structure of these earlier loans as their basis; for example the later loan {{m|ar|طَاقَم}}.<!--note for whoever considers this section superfluous: One such text is necessary for links in other entries with this pattern explaining its implications. [[Appendix:Arabic patterns]] could be a place to move. -->
{{rel-bottom}}

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|عٰلَم}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عَالَم}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عَالَم|m|pl=عَالَمُون|pl2=عَوَالِم}}

# [[world]]
# [[universe]], [[cosmos]], [[existence]]
# {{lb|ar|chiefly|Christianity}} [[world]], [[hereunder]], [[worldly]] life
#: {{syn|ar|دُنْيَا}}
#: {{ux|ar|فِي العالَمِ يَكُونُ لَكُم ضِيقٌ، وَلٰكِن ثِقُوا: أَنَا قَد غَلَبْتُ العالَم.|t=In the '''world''' ye shall have tribulation; but be of good cheer: I have overcome the '''world'''. (''John 16:33'')}}
# [[thing]]s, [[creation]], that which [[exist]]s [[before]] you
# [[nation]], [[people]], [[group]], [[type]], or [[kind]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عَالَم|pl=عَالَمُون|pl2=عَوَالِم}}

