===Etymology 1.1===
A Central Semitic innovation, cognate with {{cog|he|עֶבֶד|tr=ʿéḇeḏ}}, {{cog|phn|𐤏𐤁𐤃}}, {{cog|uga|𐎓𐎁𐎄}}, {{cog|syc|ܥܒܕܐ|tr=ʿaḇdā}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩲𐩨𐩵|tr=ʿbd}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عَبْد}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عَبْد|m|pl=عَبِيد|pl2=عِبَاد|pl3=عُبْدَان|pl4=أَعْبُد|f={{ll|ar|أَمَة|id=slave}}}}

# a [[person]] who is under the [[ownership]] of another, a [[slave]], a [[bondservant]]
#: {{syn|ar|مَوْلَى|رَقِيق|t1=servant|q1=dated|t2=slave}}
#: {{cot|ar|مَوْلَى|رَبّ|سَيِّد|t1=overlord|q1=dated|t2=lord|t3=master}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|24|32|passage=وَأَنْكِحُوا ٱلْأَيَامَى مِنْكُمْ وَٱلصَّالِحِينَ مِنْ '''عِبَادِكُمْ''' وَإِمَائِكُمْ إِنْ يَكُونُوا فُقَرَاءَ يُغْنِهِمُ ٱللَّهُ مِنْ فَضْلِهِ وَٱللَّهُ وَاسِعٌ عَلِيمٌ|t=And marry the unmarried among you and the righteous among your male '''slaves''' and female slaves. If they should be poor, Allah will enrich them from His bounty, and Allah is all-Encompassing and Knowing}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=عَميرة بن جُعَل التَّغْلِبيّ|passage=جَمَعْتُ رُدَيْنِيًّا كَأَنَّ سِنَانَهُ / سَنَا لَهَبٍ لَمْ يَسْتَعِنْ بِدُخَانِ <br/>  لَيَالِيَ إِذْ أَنْتُمْ لِرَهْطِيَ '''أَعْبُدٌ''' / بِرَمَّانَ لَمَّا أَجْدَبَ ٱلحَرَمَانِ
|t=I held up my Rudayni spear, its teeth like splendid, smokeless flames<br/>For nights, you were '''bondsmen''' for my troop, in Ramān, when the Sanctuaries dried.}}
## someone [[resemble|resembling]], [[liken]]ed to, or [[relate]]d to a [[slave]] (as in [[status]], [[worth]], [[condition]], and so on)
##* {{quote-book|ar|author=اَلْمُتَنَبِّيّ|passage=أَكُلَّمَا ٱغْتَالَ عَبْدُ السَّوْءِ سَيِّدَهُ / أَوْ خَانَهُ فَلَهُ فِي مِصْرَ تَمْهِيدُ<br/>صَارَ الْخَصِيُّ إِمَامَ الْآبِقِينَ بِهَا / فَٱلْحُرُّ مُسْتَعْبَدٌ وَٱلْعَبْدُ مَعْبُودُ<br/>نَامَتْ نَوَاطِيرُ مِصْرٍ عَنْ ثَعَالِبِهَا / فَقَدْ بَشِمْنَ وَمَا تَفْنَى العَنَاقِيدُ<br/>الْعَبْدُ لَيْسَ لِحُرٍّ صَالِحٍ بِأَخٍ / لَوْ أَنَّهُ فِي ثِيَابِ الْحُرِّ مَوْلُودُ<br/>لَا تَشْتَرِ الْعَبْدَ إِلَّا وَٱلْعَصَا مَعَهُ / إِنَّ الْعَبِيدَ لَأَنْجَاسٌ مَنَاكِيدُ<br/>مَا كُنْتُ أَحْسَبُنِي أَحْيَا إِلَى زَمَنٍ / يُسِيءُ بِي فِيهِ كَلْبٌ وَهْوَ مَحْمُودُ
|t=Can any fiendish slave who slew or stabbed his master find in Egypt refuge, there to be advanced?<br/>The Castrate King became the Chief of Runaways! The servants are revered; the freeman is disgraced!<br/>The Egyptian shepherds, they all are now asleep, and foxes roam, and all were drowsed with endless grapes!<br/>A freeman and a slave are neither peers nor brothers, though the slave may be in freemen's clothing raised.<br/>Never pay for any slave without the stick too: a slave, to noble men, is foul, and vile, and damned!<br/>I never thought that I would live and see a dog degrading me while he himself is hailed and praised!}}
# {{lb|ar|vulgar|ethnic slur|offensive|colloquial}} term of abuse for a [[black]] [[person]], equivalent to English [[nigger]]

