Page 12919 عبعب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ع ب ع ب}} related to abundance and thickness, to be profuse or swelling, to pour forth, to gush, to gulp or guzzle, to pour uninterruptedly, to flow on swiftly, to continue moving away; likely ultimately {{onomatopoeic|ar|nocap=1}} in origin from the murmuring or bubbling sound of gushing water.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|Iq}}

# to [[flee]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|Iq}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عَبْعَب|m|pl=عَبَاعِب}}

# [[ample]] [[vestment]], [[supple]] [[tegument]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عَبْعَب|pl=عَبَاعِب}}

===Etymology 2===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}
Likely a {{sl|ar|syc|ܥܒܐ|tr=ʿāḇā|t=forest, thickets|nocap=1}}, a specification from the same root as above, thick growth or high density of plants; however the whole root may also be short of a basic meaning of gulping borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, as its cognate reflex of {{ar-root|ض ب ب|nocat=1}} related to sticking, density, tumorosity. Native Arabic {{m|ar|غَبَب}} and {{m|ar|غَبْغَب}} are also duplicated like {{m|ar|عُبَب}} and {{m|ar|عُبْعُب}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عُبْعُب|m}}

# {{taxfmt|Withania|genus}} gen. et spp.

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عُبْعُب}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=100}}

{{C|ar|Nightshades}}
