Page 12971 عجم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ع ج م}}. The word {{m|ar|عَجَم|t=non-Arabs}} is from a pre-Islamic form {{m|ar|أَعْجَم}}, from the root {{ar-root|ع ج م}}, referring to people who speak unclearly (thus reflecting the same semantic evolution as {{noncog|grc|βάρβαρος|t=barbarian}}).

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|عَجَم|sing=عَجَمِيّ|singg=m|pl=أَعْجَام}}

# non-[[Arabs]] (as [[foreigner]]s or [[barbarian]]s)
# {{lb|ar|historical}} [[Persian|Persians]].
#: {{syn|ar|فُرْس}}

====Usage notes====
* The affective value attributed to the word depends on the point of view of the user, and the historical period. For example, it had a markedly negative connotation during the Umayyad period, whereas it was often quite positive in the Abbasid period, when Iranians had much political and social influence.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|عَجَم|sing=عَجَمِيّ|pl=أَعْجَام}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|أَعْجَم}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|ar|عَرَب}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|عَجَمِيّ}}
* {{l|ar|إِعْجَام|t=dots added to letters to distinguish between them}}
* {{l|ar|مُعْجَم|t=dictionary}}
* {{l|ar|عُجْمَة|t=a confused and obscure way of speaking}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|afb|عَيَم|tr=ʕayam}}
* {{desc|az|əcəm|bor=1}}
