Page 12975 عجور: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Trái mướp.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|عَجُّور}}]]

===Etymology===
Disputed etymology largely in where it originates and the direction it was borrowed:
* From {{der|ar|pal|ʾngwl|tr=angūr|t=grape}} or alternatively {{der|ar|pal|ʾncyl|tr=anjīr|t=fig}}; applied then generically to a green produce. Cognates with {{cog|fa|غوره|tr=ğure|t=unripe, green produce; sour grapes}}, {{cog|fa|انگور|tr=angur|t=grapes}}, {{cog|arc|גורקא|tr=gūraqā|t=unripe fruit}}, {{cog|arc|גורג|tr=gūrg|t=wine made from unripe grapes}}, and more distantly {{cog|sa|अङ्कुर|t=shoot, bud, sprout}}.
* Perhaps semantically derived from {{cog|gkm|ἀγγούριον}}; compare its Slavic and Germanic descendants, {{cog|ru|огуре́ц|t=cucumber}}, {{cog|de|Gurke|t=cucumber}}; derived from {{der|ar|el|άγουρος|t=unripe, green, immature, inexperienced}}, which disputably derives from [[w:Middle Persian|Pahlavi]], [[w:Aramaic|Aramaic]], or natively from {{der|ar|grc|ἄωρος|t=immature, green, unripe|lit=[[ἀ-]]+[[ὥρα]], not season or time}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عَجُّور}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|عَجُّور|m|sing=عَجُّورَة}}

# {{vern|Egyptian cucumber}}, {{taxfmt|Luffa aegyptiaca|species}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|عَجُّور|m}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|kmr|ecûr|bor=1}}
* {{desc|om|ujuree|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=1959a}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=1|page=530–535}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=813}}
* {{R:ar:Vollers-Beitr.|part=II|page=615}}

{{C|ar|Gourd family plants|Vegetables}}
