Page 12991 عدان: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from the frequent {{bor|ar|arc|𐡏𐡃𐡍𐡀}} / {{m|arc|עִידָּנָא|tr=ʿiddānā}} / {{m|syc|ܥܷܕ݁ܳܢܳܐ|tr=ʿeddānā}}, from {{der|ar|akk|adānum|𒌓𒅗𒂵|tr=adānum}}. In {{cog|arc-hat|-}} also known as “halting place”, “station”, even used for a caravanserai. The meanings “to stay, to bide” of the Arabic root {{ar-root|ع د ن}} appear to be denominal from the spatial meaning of this lexeme. {{cog|xcl|ատեան}} is likely from Semitic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عِدّان|عَدَّان|عَدَان}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|عِدّان|m|head2=عَدَّان|head3=عَدَان}} {{tlb|ar|only used with certain bedouin tribes}}

# a [[time]], [[particular]] time something is [[set]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=w:Al-Farazdaq|year=a. 730|title=is quoted|section=by {{w|Abu Hilal al-Askari|Abū Hilāl al-ʾaskarīy}} ''Jamharat al-ʾamṯāl'' [https://maktabatalfeker.com/book.php?id=5664 1/211] and {{w|Al-Tabari|At-Ṭabarī}} ''Tārīḵ'' ed. [http://solo.bodleian.ox.ac.uk/primo_library/libweb/action/display.do?tabs=detailsTab&ct=display&fn=search&doc=oxfaleph015147832&indx=1&recIds=oxfaleph015147832 de Goeje] series 2 page 160 line 3–8 with the word at line 6
|passage=أمسكين أبكى الله عَيْنك إِنَّمَا ... جرى فِي ضلال دمعها فتحدرا<br/>بَكَيْت امْرأ من أهل ميسَان كَافِرًا ... ككسرى على عدانه أَو كقيصرا<br/>أَقُول لَهُ لما أَتَانِي نعيه ... بِهِ لَا بِظَبْيٍ بالصرائم أعفرا}}
# a place of [[remain]]ing, [[spot]] to [[bide]]
# [[bank]], [[shore]], where a [[river]] or [[sea]] [[meet]]s [[land]], the [[water]] [[end]] of a [[journey]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{w|Yazid ibn al-Sa'iq|Yazīd Ibn As-Saʾiq}}|title=quoted by {{w|Lisān al-ʿArab}}|year=a. 600|passage=جَلَبْنَ الخيلَ من تَثْلِيثَ، حتى وَرَدْنَ على أُوَارةَ فالعَدَانِ}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=[[w:Labīd|Labīd ibn Rabīʿa]]|title=ar:إن تقوى ربنا خير نفل|url=https://www.aldiwan.net/poem21191.html|year=a. 661|passage=ولقد يعلم صحبي كلهم     بعدان السيف صبري ونقل }}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عِدّان|head2=عَدَّان|head3=عَدَان}}

