Page 13007 عدن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ع د ن}}The sense “Eden” is a borrowing from {{bor|ar|hbo|עֵדֶן|tr=ʿḗden}}. The meaning “to stay, to remain” appears to be {{denominal verb|ar|عِدَّان|nocap=1|t=set time; set place of staying}}, with it of use particular to Bedouins, only the meaning “to strike” the original Arabic meaning, whence transferred “to break up the soil to manure”.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|عَدْن|m}}

# [[Eden]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|98|8|passage=جَزَاؤُهُمْ عِنْدَ رَبِّهِمْ جَنَّٰتُ '''عَدْنٍ''' تَجْرِي مِنْ تَحْتِهَا ٱلْأَنْهَٰرُ خَٰلِدِينَ فِيهَا أَبَدًا|t=Their reward is with their Lord - the gardens of '''Eden''' [with] rivers running beneath them - wherein they abide forever.}}
