Page 13075 عرناس: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2021|October|28}}
[[File:Ivory distaff Africa.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|عَرْنَاس}}|upright=1.6]]
[[File:Distaff and spindle Ar.png|thumb|right|upright=1.6]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|عِرْنَاسَة}}
* {{alter|ar|قِرْنَاس||no uses are known; but in the meaning of a [[crag]]}}

===Etymology===
Suspected to be borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc||*עַרְנָסָא|tr=*ʿarnāsā|t=[[distaff]]}}, attested as {{cog|syc|ܥܱܪܢܳܣܴܐ|tr=ʿarnāsā}} but from the 9th century and {{cog|tmr|אורנאסא|tr=ʾurnāsā}} once in the {{w|Shabbat (Talmud)|Tractate Šabbaṯ}} of the {{w|Gemara}} folio 91b(41) of uncertain meaning, lost already to the [[Geonim]], certainly not distaff, and once mentioned by {{w|Hai Gaon}} commenting {{w|Keilim|Tractate Kēlīm}} Chapter 21, 1 and referring to the previous occurrence he commented, noting it to be used at his time in Babylonia in the meaning of distaff like the Arabic, else in Neo-Aramaic lects borrowed from Arabic, so the assumed borrowing direction is met with reservation; in either language likely a foreign word, further the provenance is {{unk|ar|nocap=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عِرْنَاس|عَرْنَاس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|عِرْنَاس|head2=عَرْنَاس|m|pl=عَرَانِيس}}

# [[distaff]]
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} a kind of [[bird]] similar to a [[dove]]
#* {{RQ:Yaqut|W4|page=585 line 2<!--Ullmann gives after this “/V 162 b 3 f.“ which reference I cannot relate-->}} quoting {{quote-book|ar|year=→|author=ar:ثعلبة بن غيلان<tr:Ṯaʿlaba ibn Ġaylān>|title=nothing seems to be known of this poet|passage=إِذَا شِئْتُ غَنَّانِي ٱلْحَمَامُ بِعَيْكَةٍ<br/>وَلَيْسَ سَوَاءً صَوْتُهَا وَٱلْ'''عَرَانِس'''|t=When I want, the doves sing me in the thicket<br/>And their voices and those of the '''''ʿarānīs''''' are not on par}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عِرْنَاس|head2=عَرْنَاس|pl=عَرَانِيس}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|ar|مِغْزَل|t=[[spindle]]}}

