Page 13079 عروبة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ع ر ب}}
Derived from {{m|ar|عَرَبِيّ}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عُرُوبَة|f}}

# [[Arabness]]; [[Arabicness]]
# [[Arab]] [[nationalism]]; [[Arabism]]; [[pan-Arabism]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عُرُوبَة}}

===Etymology 2===

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj|عَرُوبَة|fpl=عُرُب}}

# {{alt form|ar|عَرُوب|t=[[concupiscent]], [[lustful]], [[bold]] in [[love]], [[lascivious]]}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|1=-|d=-|pl=-|f=عَرُوبَة|fpl=عُرُب}}

===Etymology 3===
{{bor+|ar|arc|עֲרוּבְתָּא|tr=ʿărūḇtā|t=eve; Friday}}, referring originally to the eve of Sabbath, cognate with native {{cog|ar|غُرُوب|t=sundown}}, and further {{w|Abu Mansur Mauhub al-Jawaliqi|Al-Jawālīqīy}}, in his book about Arabicized terminology, [https://www.google.de/books/edition/Mauhūb_b_Aḥmad_Ibn_al_Ǧawālīqī_s/7yo-AAAAcAAJ?gbpv=1&pg=PP111 notes] it to be in [[Nabataean]] the name of [[Athena]], seemingly confusing with [[Aphrodite]], so as with every Old Arabic weekday the name is conceived a god and planet, here [[Venus]], harmonizing with {{noncog|la|diēs Veneris}}. This is further confirmed by {{w|Ubayy ibn Ka'b|Ubayy ibn Kaʕb}}’s Qurʔān recension having {{m|ar||يَوْمِ العَرُوبَةِ الْكُبْرَى}} in [https://quran.com/62/9 62:9], where {{m|ar|الْكُبْرَى}} reflects [[Cypris]], [[Cypria]]. The name of the {{w|seven heavens|seventh heaven}} {{m|ar|عَرُوبَاء}} ~ {{m|ar|عِرْبِيَاء}} ~ {{m|ar|عَرِيبَاء}} thus must be interpreted as representing utmost love or climax, etymologically corresponding to this religious heyday of the week.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|عَرُوبَة|head2=اَلْعَرُوبَة|f}}

# {{tlb|ar|obsolete}} [[Friday]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عَرُوبَة:di|state=ind-def}}

====See also====
* {{list:days of the week/ar|sublang=Prestandard}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Fischer:1896|page=224}}
* {{R:Hommel-Chrest.|page=57}}
* {{R:ar:Rotter:1993}}
-------- end text --------
