===Etymology===
Of the root {{ar-root|ع ر ش}}, of which {{ar-form|I|verb form}} {{m|ar|عَرَشَ|t=to pull up a railing}}. Possibly originally {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, attested as {{cog|xsa|𐩲𐩧𐩺𐩦|t=shed, shack}} in the first century CE and once in the {{cog|gez|-}} {{w|Bible translations into Geʽez|Bible}} as {{m|gez|ዐሪሥ}} translating {{m|grc|σκηνή}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عَرِيش}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|عَرِيش|m|pl=عُرُش|pl2=عَرَائِش}}

# [[bower]], [[arbor]]
#: {{syn|ar|سَقِيفَة|تَكْعِيبَة}}
# [[railing]], [[guardrail]], [[espalier]], [[trellis]]
#: {{syn|ar|دَالِيَة|تَكْعِيبَة}}
# [[pole]], [[tow bar]], [[beam]]

