Page 13124 عسقلان: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{rfe|ar}}<br/><!-- What would be the direct source of the settlement name in Arabic? -->
The shallot-sense is presumably a {{sl|ar|es|escaloña|nocap=1}}, {{m|es|escalonia}}, or {{sl|ar|ML.|escalōnia|notext=1}}, going back to Classical {{der|ar|la|[[ascalōnia]] ([[cēpa]])}} the Romans called the plant after its abundant occurrence around the Palestinian town nicknamed in {{noncog|grc|Κρομμύων πολις|lit=Onion City}}, also retained in {{cog|fro|eschaloigne}} and {{cog|it|scalogno}} – while the myth persists that the cultivar spread to Western Europe only by the first {{w|Crusades}} –, otherwise Arabs had no reason to call the plant precisely like the Romans.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عَسْقَلَان}}
** {{IPA|acw|/ʕas.ɡa.laːn/|a=Hijazi}}

