Page 13194 عطارد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Ultimately unknown, without known Semitic cognates:
* Natively coined from the root {{ar-root|ط|ر|د|}} meaning, "to chase or chase away", "to race or race after", "to cause something to pick up speed", "to outstrip", "follow swiftly"; related to the planet having the shortest orbital period and its eccentric periods of velocity, an association found cross-culturally via observation. The atypical /[[ع]]/ occurs occasionally in some Arabic dialects in replacement of /[[أ]]/ due to the pharyngeal-aspect of a nearby emphatic consonant, namely /[[ط]]/.
* A variation of {{ar-root|ع|ط|د|}} meaning "to be extreme" in many senses including "to go at a very quick pace", "to be most hasty", "a very quick rate of going". Alternatively, potentially a synthesis of both roots, as such blends are a known source of etymology for some quadriliteral roots.

{{rel-top|Additional Theories and Connections}}
* A relation to {{cog|peo|𐎫𐎡𐎼𐎭𐎠𐎫|tr=t-i-r-d-a-t|ts=*tīra-dāta|t=Given by Mercury; Tiridates}}, the front portion being cognate to {{cog|fa|تیر|tr=tir|t=arrow}}, from {{cog|pal||tr=tyl|ts=tīr|t=arrow; also with the meaning Mercury, perhaps from swift moving, projectile}}. There is perhaps a layer of phono-semantic matching as the root {{ar-root|ط|ر|د|}}, with giving chase, also features terms dealing with hunting spears and arrows as well.
* As a distortion of {{noncog|grc|ὕδωρ|t=water}}, part of {{m|grc|ὑδράργῠρος|lit=liquid silver}}, as the planet and the metal have been in association since antiquity.
{{rel-bottom}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عُطَارِد}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-عطارد.ogg}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|عُطَارِد|m}}

# {{senseid|ar|Q308}}{{lb|ar|astronomy}} [[Mercury]] (planet)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عُطَارِدُ|state=ind-def}}

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|[[كُتْبَي|الكُتْبَي]]|tr=}}, {{l|ar|[[كَاتِب|الكاتِب]]|tr=|t=the scribe, the record-keeper, the accountant, the clerk, the cleric, the librarian}}
* {{l|ar|[[نبي|أَنْبَي]]|tr=|t=the caller, the informer, the announcer; the announcer of the account, informer of what really happened}}
* {{l|ar|[[نعم|مُنْعِم]]|tr=|t=the one that has been favored, the agreeable one}}, contrasted with other planets as being neutral
* {{l|ar|سَعْد|السَعْدَانِ|tr=|t=the two good fortunes}}, paired with Venus, contrasted with Mars and Saturn

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ug|ئەتتارىد|bor=1}}

===See also===
* {{list:planets of the Solar System/ar}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=176}}

{{C|ar|Planets of the Solar System}}
