Page 13240 عفص: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed into Arabic from {{bor|ar|arc|עַפְצָא|tr=ʿap̄ṣā}} / {{m|syc|ܥܱܦܨܳܐ|tr=ʿap̄ṣā}}, absolute state {{m|arc|עֲפֶץ|tr=ʿap̄eṣ}}, itself treated as a later variant of {{m|arc|אַפְצָא|tr=ʾap̄ṣā}} / {{m|syc|ܐܱܦܨܳܐ|tr=ʾap̄ṣā}}, absolute state {{m|arc|אֲפֶץ|tr=ʾap̄eṣ}}. The Arabic verbs are denominal, from the use of the idea of oakgalls being a powerful astringent, used in medicine and tanning. {{cog|ar|عَصَفَ|t=to hit on; to blow violently}} is metathetical to this denominal verb with its ideas of violence and after the inflation of an oakgall. Distantly related to the root {{ar-root|ع ص ر|nocat=1}} which also exists in Aramaic.

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|عَفْص|sing=عَفْصَة}}

# [[gallnut|gall-nut]], [[oak gall|oak-gall]]
#: {{cot|ar|تَاكُوت}}
# {{C|ar|Oaks}} [[gall oak|gall-oak]] ({{taxlink|Quercus lusitanica|species}} and other species)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|عَفْص}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|tig|አፈስ|bor=1}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.vn:عَفْص}}

# to [[tie up]], to [[wring]], to [[squish]]
# to [[defeat]] in [[battle]]
# to [[rape]], to [[sard]] [[forcefully]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.vn:عَفْص}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[tincture]] with oakgall

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj|عَفِص}}

# [[acrid]], of [[astringent]] [[taste]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|عَفِص}}

===References===
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=876}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=185a–b}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=2|pages=299b–300a}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|page=731a}}

