===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|ع ل ج}}
Connected by Jakob Barth to {{cog|gez|አድግ|t=ass}}; as a nickname originating in some ancient dialect therewith inviting to draw a parallel with {{m|ar|عَلَس|t=emmer}} vs. {{m|ar|عَدَس|t=lentil}}.

The word was quite obscure until the 2003 invasion of Iraq, when the Iraqi information minister [[w:Muhammad Saeed al-Sahhaf|Muhammad Saeed al-Sahhaf]] aka "Comical Ali" started frequently using it to refer to the invading American troops. It was a hassle for translators, and sparked debate in Arabic-language media regarding its meaning and etymology.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عِلْج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|عِلْج|m|pl=عُلُوج|pl2=أَعْلَاج|pl3=عِلَجَة}}

# [[sturdy]] man, [[bulky]] [[bloke]]
# {{lb|ar|Islam|archaic|religious slur}} [[atheist]], [[kafir]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|malik|21
|passage=إِنَّهُ بَلَغَنِي أَنَّ رِجَالاً مِنْكُمْ يَطْلُبُونَ الْعِلْجَ حَتَّى إِذَا أَسْنَدَ فِي الْجَبَلِ وَامْتَنَعَ
|translation=It has reached me that some of your men would seek and chase a non-believer till he retreats to the mountains.}}
# [[wild ass]], [[onager]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عِلْج|pl=عُلُوج|pl2=أَعْلَاج|pl3=عِلَجَة}}

