Page 13365 عمان: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
Disputed etymology with most connecting it back to {{m|ar|عُمَانَة|tr=}} considered a by-name of the city {{m|ar|[[w:Sohar|صُحَار]]|tr=}}, the most prevalent city-state at the time the name became associated with the region as a whole. Considered derived from the root {{ar-root|ع|م|ن}} meaning, "to settle or remain", "to dwell", "a place where one enters and chooses to stay", "to be abiding or a lasting settlement", "a plain or easy country".

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عُمَان}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|عُمَان|f}}

# {{tcl|ar|Oman|id=Q842}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عُمَان:di|state=ind-def}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|عُمَانِيّ}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|aii|ܥܘܼܡܵܢ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|عمان|tr='omân|bor=1}}
* {{desc|pa|عُمان|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sd|عمان|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ur|عُمان|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
Generally connected to the root {{ar-root|ع|م|م}} dealing with the concepts of "kinsmen or people", "father's brother", "to be distantly related, an extended tribe", "a very large company", "a tribe, multitude, or great band"; attested as far back as {{cog|akk|𒌷𒄠𒈠𒈾|tr=Ammān|t=City of Ammān}} likely deriving from a local power's endonym.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عَمَّان}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|عَمَّان|f}}

# {{place|ar|capital city|c/Jordan|t1=Amman}}
# {{place|ar|governorate|c/Jordan|t=Amman}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|عَمَّان:di|state=ind-def}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|عَمَّانِيّ}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|aii|ܥܲܡܵܐܢ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|عمان|tr='ammân|bor=1}}
* {{desc|pa|عَمّان|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sd|عمان|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ur|عَمّان|bor=1}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|عمان}}

===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عَمَّانِ|m-d}}

# {{inflection of|ar|عَمّ||nom|d}}

-------- end text --------
