Page 13413 عنب الثعلب: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Literally “fox's grapes”. In meaning {{m|mul|Physalis}} species, a folk etymology-motivated and perhaps also {{glossary|tashif|''taṣḥīf''}}-influenced replacement term for the old-classical {{m|ar|عُبَب الثَعْلَب|lit=fox's {{taxfmt|Withania|genus}}}} – see {{m|ar|عُبْعُب}} – and for the confusion between {{taxfmt|Solanum|genus}} and {{m|mul|Physalis}} spp.; compare {{cog|am|ኣውጥ|tr=ʾawwəṭ}}, also meaning {{taxfmt|Solanum nigrum|species}}, {{taxlink|Solanum villosum subsp. alatum|subspecies}}, and {{m|mul|Physalis}} spp., distinguished sometimes by color-adjectives, like there is English [[red nightshade]], [[yellow nightshade]], [[green nightshade]], [[black nightshade]] etc.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عِنَب الثَّعْلَب}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|[[عِنَب]] [[ثعلب|الثَّعْلَب]]|m}}

# [[gooseberry]] ({{taxfmt|Ribes uva-crispa|species}})
#: {{hyper|ar|كِشْمِش|رِيبَاس}}
#: {{cot|ar|عِنَب الذِّئْب}}
# [[blackcurrant]] ({{taxfmt|Ribes nigrum|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|كِشْمِش أَسْوَد|عِنَب الذِّئْب}}
#: {{hyper|ar|كِشْمِش|رِيبَاس}}
# {{vern|Abyssinian gooseberry}} ({{taxlink|Dovyalis abyssinica|species}})
# [[hairy nightshade]], [[woolly nightshade]], [[red nightshade]] ({{taxfmt|Solanum villosum|species}}, including {{taxlink|Solanum villosum subsp. alatum|subspecies}} seen by some as a distinct species {{taxlink|Solanum alatum|species}})
# [[black nightshade]] ({{taxfmt|Solanum nigrum|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|عِنَب الذِّئْب|مَغْد أَسْوَد}}
# [[winter cherry]], {{vern|poison gooseberry}}, [[ashwagandha]] ({{taxfmt|Withania somnifera|species}}, syn. {{taxlink|Physalis somnifera|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|عُبَب|عُبَب الثَّعْلَب}}
# [[winter cherry]], [[bladder cherry]] ({{taxfmt|Alkekengi officinarum|species}}, syn. {{taxfmt|Physalis alkekengi|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|كَاكَنْج|عُبَب|عُبَب الثَّعْلَب}}
#: {{hyper|ar|حَرَنْكَش}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عِنَب|mod=ثَعْلَب|idafa=def}}

{{C|ar|Nightshades|Willows and poplars|Saxifragales order plants}}
