Page 13478 عوسج: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Put to {{der|ar|akk|ašāgum|𒀀𒊭𒄖|tr=ašāgu}}, though CAD rather wants to connect {{m|ar|شَوْك}} glossing both – while the latter is just the usual word for “thorns” – {{taxlink|Prosopis farcta|species}}, which is known as {{m|ar|يَنْبُوت}}; the term is used at {{w|Boğazkale|Boğazköy}} in place of {{m|akk|amurdinnum|𒀀𒄯𒁷𒉡|tr=amurdinnu}} which is a thornbush noted for berries and beverage, plausibly boxthorn ''Lycium'', camelthorn bush  {{taxfmt|Alhagi|genus}}, or just bramble {{taxfmt|Rubus|genus}}, however is also found in equivalence with {{m|akk|egu|𒀀𒄖𒌋|tr=agû}}, {{m|akk|egu|𒂊𒄖𒌋|tr=egû}}, {{m|ar|حَاج|t=''Alhagi''}}: {{m|akk|egu|𒄿𒄀|tr=igi}} = {{m|akk|ašāgum|𒀀𒃻𒄖|tr=ašāgu}}. Compare also the Iranian {{m|ar|أُشَّق|t={{taxlink|Ferula marmarica|species}}, {{taxlink|Ferula aucheri|species}}, {{taxlink|Ferula ammoniacum|species}}}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عَوْسَج}}

