Page 13508 عيسى: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|عيسى بن مريم|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
The form is first unambiguously attested in the [[Qur'an]] and is of {{uncertain|ar|nocap=1}} origin. While the Christian Arabic name {{doublet|ar|يَسُوع|notext=1}} can be considered a phonetically regular equivalent of {{cog|he|יֵשׁוּעַ|tr=yēšū́aʿ}}, which is and has been believed to be Jesus's historic name, the Qur'anic {{m|ar||عِيسَى}} seems to be a phonetic modification. The common name {{cog|sem-saf|𐪒𐪊𐪚}} likely represents the same name, but cannot be securely linked to Jesus. Several theories have been brought forward to explain why the letter ''[[ayn]]'' was apparently shifted from the last to the first position. It has been noted that ''ayn'' was not pronounced in some dialects of {{der|ar|arc|-}}, including that likely spoken by Jesus himself (compare for this {{cog|he|יֵשׁוּ|tr=yēšū́}}). Moreover, there are indications that an unetymological word-initial ''ayn'' may have occurred more often in Arabic loans from Aramaic (compare {{m|ar|عَمْرُوسَة||small lamb}} from {{m|syc|ܐܷܡܪܘܿܣܬܴܐ|tr=ʾemrōstā}} or {{m|ar|عَقْر||the midst of a house}} from {{m|syc|ܐܶܩܪܶܐ|tr=ʾaqrā}} ). Dye and Kropp suggest that this may be an orthographic device borrowed from {{cog|myz|-}}, where ''ayn'' was lost in pronunciation, but used to indicate long initial /i/. For more information, see {{w|Isa (name)}} on Wikipedia.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عِيسَى}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|عِيسَى|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} [[Jesus]] ([[Isa]]), son of [[Mary]], revered as a major prophet in Islam.
#: {{syn|ar|يَسُوع|q1=Christianity}}
# {{given name|ar|male|eq=Isa}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|ar||عِيسَى}} is used almost exclusively in Islamic contexts. Arabic-speaking Christians call Jesus {{m|ar|يَسُوع}}.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عِيسَى|state=ind-def}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|ar|المَسِيح||[[Messiah]], [[Christ]]}}
* {{list:Islamic prophets/ar}}

====Derived terms====
