Page 13513 عيلة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Ultimately from the root {{ar-root|ع ي ل}}. The verb {{m|ar|عَالَ}} may be conjugated as deriving from {{ar-root|ع و ل}} (whence {{m|ar|عَوْل}} and {{m|ar|عَوِيل}}) or {{ar-root|ع ي ل}} (whence {{m|ar|عَيْل}}, {{m|ar|عِيَالَة}}, {{m|ar|عُيُول}}, and {{m|ar|مَعِيل}}). Hence, though distinct conjugations (or "roots") typically have different significations, the "needfulness" sense has been conflated.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|عَيْلَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|عَيْلَة|f}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|عَالَ|t=to be [[poor]]|form=I}}
# [[poverty]]; [[want]], [[need]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|9|28|passage=وَإِنْ خِفْتُمْ '''عَيْلَةً''' فَسَوْفَ يُغْنِيكُمُ اللَّهُ مِن فَضْلِهِ إِن شَاءَ|subst=وَإِنْ/وَ-إِنْ,فَسَوْفَ/فَ-سَوْفَ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|عَيْلَة}}

