===Etymology 1===
Morphologically from the root {{ar-root|ع|ي|ن}}, from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʕayn-}}, from {{inh|ar|afa-pro|*ʕayVn-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عَيَّنَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}} {{lb|ar|transitive}}

# to [[appoint]], to [[assign]], to [[name]], to [[nominate]]
# to [[define]]
# to [[determine]], to [[fix]], to [[identify]], to [[specify]]
# to [[allocate]], to [[allot]], to [[apportion]], to [[earmark]], to [[itemize]], to [[set aside]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ʿayn-}}, from {{inh|ar|afa-pro|*ʿayVn-}}. Synchronically from the root {{ar-root|ع|ي|ن}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|عَيْن}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|عَيْن|f|d=عَيْنَان|pl=عُيُون|pl2=أَعْيُن}}
[[File:Iris of the Human Eye.jpg|alt=|thumb|{{lang|ar|عين}}]]

# {{lb|ar|anatomy}} [[eye]] {{gloss|organ}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''عَيْنَا'''يَ|my '''two eyes'''}}'''
#: {{uxi|ar|'''عَيْنَا'''كَ|your (m/sg) '''two eyes'''}}
## (''often preceded by ''{{lang|ar|الـ}}) envy, the [[evil eye]]
## [[spy]]
##: {{syn|ar|جَاسُوس}}
# [[spring]] (of water)
#: {{syn|ar|جَدْوَل}}
# (''plural'' '''{{l|ar|أَعْيُن}}''') The thing [[itself]]
#: {{syn|ar|نَفْس|ذَات}}
# A [[revered]] person in the community.
# {{lb|ar|law}} [[money]] or whatever is the equivalent of money.
# {{lb|ar|economics}} what has monetary value except money.

=====Usage notes=====
* In most senses, the plural is either {{m|ar|عُيُون}} or {{m|ar|أَعْيُن}}. In sense 5, {{m|ar|أَعْيُن}} is the only plural.
* When referring to envy and the evil eye, {{m|ar|عَيْن}} often signifies what is regarded as the injurious and damaging supernatural effects of jealousy and envy (for example, seemingly uncurable physical or psychological ailments and a ruined social life), not envy itself, whereas {{m|ar|حَسَد}} usually refers to grudge and envy, regardless of any harmful effects believed to stem from such feelings. See the usage notes in the entry for {{m|ar|حَسَد}} for more information.

