[[File:Laurierbladeren.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|غَار}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology 3===
If it is true that the bay laurel has dispersed over the Mediterranean regions from further west, be it Asia Minor or even Western Europe, then the Arabic plant name {{m-self|ar|غَار}} has been borrowed in the earlier 1st millennium BC or before from {{bor|ar|arc|עָרָא}} / {{m|syc|ܥܳܪܳܐ|tr=ʿārā}}, also {{cog|he|עָר|tr=ʿār}}, of the same meaning, the merger of {{IPAchar|/ʁ/}} and {{IPAchar|/ʕ/}} not having happened in {{cog|sem-nwe|-}} yet—if not old enough to be ascribed to {{cog|sem-wes-pro|-}} unity.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia|غار (نبات)|mul=غار (جنس)|lang=ar}}
{{ar-coll-noun|غَار|sing=غَارَة}}

# [[bay laurel]] ({{taxfmt|Laurus nobilis|species}}); [[laurel]] (''[[Laurus]]'' gen.)
#: {{syn|ar|رَنْد|دَهْمَسْت}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|غَار}}

