|translation=So when they had passed beyond it, he said to his boy, "Bring us our '''morning meal'''. We have certainly suffered in this, our journey, much fatigue."
|subst=فَلَمَّا/فَ-لَمَّا,لِفَتَاهُ/لِ-فَتَاهُ}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 813|title=unknown title|author={{w|العماني الراجز|lang=ar|ar-Rājiz}}|passage=خالي لقيطٌ ({{var}} عُوَيْف) وأبو عَلِجِّ … المطعمان اللحمَ بالعَشِجِّ<br/>وبال'''غداةِ''' كِسَرَ ({{var}} فِلَق) البَرْنِجِّ … يُقْلَعُ بالوَدِّ وبالصِّيصجِّ|t=I have two uncles ʿUwayf and Abū ʿAlī … who eat meat in the vesper<br/>And in the '''morn''' sweet shives of dates … they pluck by means of pegs and pales|footer=Translation by {{w|Gottfried Hoberg|lang=de}}:<br/>Avunculus meus est ʿUvaif et Abû ʿAlî, qui carnem vespere porrigunt<br/>et mane dactylos suaviores, qui extrahuntur paxillo et palo<br/>}}
# [[lunch]]

