#* {{quote-book|ar|year=1946|author=w:en:Ahmed Shawqi|title=سلوا قلبي|trans-title=Ask my heart|text=سَلُوا قَلْبِي '''غَدَاةَ''' سَلَا وَثَابَا <br> لَعَلَّ عَلَى ٱلْجَمَالِ لَهُ عِتَابًا <br> وَيُسْأَلُ فِي ٱلْحَوَادِثِ ذُو صَوَابٍ <br> فَهَلْ تَرَكَ ٱلْجَمَالُ لَهُ صَوَابًا|t=Ask my heart '''the early morning''' it forgets and returns to its previous state <br> Perhaps towards the beautiful one it has some reproach <br> Only wise people are supposed to be asked <br> Did the beauty leave any wisdom to it}}
