{{ar-rootbox|غ ر ب ل}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|עַרְבָּלָא}} / {{m|syc|ܥܱܪܒܳܠܴܐ|tr=ʿarbālā}} ({{cog|tmr|-}} more commonly written {{m|arc|[[אַרְבָּאלָא]] / [[אַרְבָּלָא]]|tr=ʾarbālā}}, and also vocalized {{m|arc|עַרְכְּלָא|tr=ʿarbəlā}}, {{m|arc|אַרְכְּלָא|tr=ʾarbəlā}}). Possible a culture-word left from the {{der|ar|xhu|-}} period in {{w|Nuzi}} from which sieves have been excavated and where the Hurrian word {{m|xhu|𒂊𒅕𒁁𒀉𒋼|tr=e-ir-be-et-te|ts=erbette}} is found, said to be of uncertain meaning. Such an origin is also supported by {{cog|xcl|խարբալեմ|t=to sift}}, {{cog|axm|խարբալ|t=sieve}}. ({{cog|akk-nbb|𒌒𒁄𒆷|ts=arballu|t=sieve}} is from Aramaic.)

