* {{l|ar|تَغَاضَى|t=to contract one’s eyelids; to feign oneself unmindful}}
* {{l|ar|مُغِضّ}} and {{l|ar|غَاضٍ|t=sombre, obscure, dark}}

===Etymology 2===
From figurative uses in relation to the {{m-self|ar|غَضًا}} plant, in high demand by camels to bite off and by travels for shadow.

