===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|غ|ل|م}}. Compare {{cog|he|עֶלֶם|tr=ʿélem|t=a virgin boy}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|غُلَام|m|f=غُلَامَة|pl=غِلْمَان|pl2=غِلْمَة|pl3=أَغْلِمَة}}

# a [[young]] [[male]] [[human]], a [[boy]]-[[child]]
#: {{syn|ar|صَبِيّ|فَتًى|شَابّ}}
#: {{cot|ar|صَبِيَّة|فَتَاة|شَابَّة|جَارِيَة|q4=archaic}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|19|7|passage=يَا زَكَرِيَّا إِنَّا نُبَشِّرُكَ '''بِغُلَامٍ''' ٱسْمُهُ يَحْيَىٰ|t=Zakariyyāh, we bring you the good news of a '''boy''' whose name shall be Yaḥyāh.|inline=t}}
#* '''10th century''', [[w:en:Al-Mutanabbi|Al-Mutanabbi]]
#*: {{quote|ar|فَرُبَّ '''غُلَامٍ''' عَلَّمَ الْمَجْدَ نَفْسَهُ كَتَعْلِيمِ سَيْفِ الدَّوْلَةِ الطَّعْنَ وٱلضَّرْبَا}}
# a [[boy]]-[[servant]]; a [[slave]]-[[boy]]

====Usage notes====
The feminine of this word is now very rare, being instead replaced by {{m|ar|صَبِيَّة}} or its synonyms.

