Page 13840 غودش: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}
[[Image:Gozo.jpg|thumb|{{lang|ar|غَوْدَش}}]]

===Etymology===
Probably from a {{der|ar|phn|-}} root {{m|phn|[[𐤂]]-[[𐤅]]-[[𐤋]]}}, meaning something like “turn around”. If this derivation is correct, the Arabs must have got the name from {{der|ar|grc|Γαύδος}}, {{m|grc|Γαύλος}}, perhaps through {{der|ar|la|Gaudos}}, {{m|la|Gaulos}}. The specifics of the borrowing are related to the question of the pre-Arabic language of Malta and whether there was any population continuity after the conquest.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|غَوْدَش}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|غَوْدَش|m}}

# [[Gozo]] (the second largest island of [[Malta]])

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|غَوْدَش:di}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|Għawdex}}
-------- end text --------
