Page 14047 فتن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ف|ت|ن}}. Cognate with {{cog|gdq|tr=fetōn}}, {{cog|gez|ፈተነ|tr=fatana|t=try, test}}.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.vn:فَتْن,فِتْنَة,فُتُون}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to draw into [[temptation]], to lead [[astray]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَغْرَى|أَغْوَى|مَنَّى|أَضَلَّ|t1=to tempt; to allure, to entice; to seduce|t2=to mislead|t3=to promise, to delude with promises; to tempt|t4=to mislead, to misguide; to deceive}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|27|text=يَا بَنِي آدَمَ لَا '''يَفْتِنَنَّكُمُ''' الشَّيْطَانُ|translation=O children of Adam, let not Satan '''tempt you'''}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[enchant]], to [[captivate]], to [[charm]], to [[bewitch]]; to [[seduce]]
##: {{syn|ar|سَحَرَ}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[afflict]], to [[test]], to [[try]]
#: {{syn|ar|اِمْتَحَنَ|اِبْتَلَى|t1=to examine; to test|t2=to try, to test}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|9|126|text=أَوَلَا يَرَوْنَ أَنَّهُمْ '''يُفْتَنُونَ''' فِي كُلِّ عَامٍ مَّرَّةً أَوْ مَرَّتَيْنِ ثُمَّ لَا يَتُوبُونَ وَلَا هُمْ يَذَّكَّرُونَ|translation=Do they not see that they '''are tried''' every year once or twice but then they do not repent nor do they remember?|subst=وَلَا/وَ-لَا}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|38|34|text=وَلَقَدْ '''فَتَنَّا''' سُلَيْمَانَ وَأَلْقَيْنَا عَلَى كُرْسِيِّهِ جَسَدًا ثُمَّ أَنَابَ|translation=And We certainly '''tried''' Solomon and placed on his throne a body; then he returned.|subst=وَلَقَدْ/وَ-لَقَدْ,وَأَلْقَيْنَا/وَ-أَلْقَيْنَا}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[persecute]], to [[victimize]], to [[oppress]]; to [[torture]] (in order to forcibly convert or impose a particular ideology, for example)
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|10|83|text=فَمَا آمَنَ لِمُوسَى إِلَّا ذُرِّيَّةٌ مِّن قَوْمِهِ عَلَى خَوْفٍ مِّن فِرْعَوْنَ وَمَلَئِهِمْ أَن '''يَفْتِنَهُمْ''' وَإِنَّ فِرْعَوْنَ لَعَالٍ فِي الْأَرْضِ وَإِنَّهُ لَمِنَ الْمُسْرِفِينَ|translation=But no one believed Moses, except youths among his people, for fear of the Pharaoh and his establishment that they would '''persecute''' them. And indeed, the Pharaoh was high [and ascendant] within the land, and indeed, he was of the transgressors.|subst=فَمَا/فَ-مَا,لِمُوسَى/لِ-مُوسَى,وَإِنَّ/وَ-إِنَّ,وَإِنَّهُ/وَ-إِنَّهُ,وَمَلَئِهِمْ/وَ-مَلَئِهِمْ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|85|10|text=إِنَّ الَّذِينَ '''فَتَنُوا''' الْمُؤْمِنِينَ وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ ثُمَّ لَمْ يَتُوبُوا فَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ جَهَنَّمَ وَلَهُمْ عَذَابُ الْحَرِيقِ|translation=Indeed, those who '''have tortured''' the believing men and women and then have not repented will have the punishment of Hell, and they will have the punishment of the Burning Fire.|subst=وَالْمُؤْمِنَاتِ/وَ-ٱلْمُؤْمِنَاتِ,فَلَهُمْ/فَ-لَهُمْ,وَلَهُمْ/وَ-لَهُمْ,الَّذِينَ/ٱلَّذِينَ}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive|rare}} to [[burn]], to [[roast]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَحْرَقَ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|51|14|text=يَوْمَ هُمْ عَلَى النَّارِ '''يُفْتَنُونَ''' / ذُوقُوا '''فِتْنَتَكُمْ''' هَٰذَا الَّذِي كُنتُم بِهِ تَسْتَعْجِلُونَ}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[melt]], to [[smelt]]
##: {{syn|ar|صَهَرَ}}

====Usage notes====
* In the sense "to persecute; to torture", the word almost always refers to condemned judgment. This is because the dominant sense is that of misleading, hence "to oppress or torture in order to mislead". If the persecution is deemed rightful, justified, or deserved, other, oftentimes overtly emotive, terms are used instead, which are connotationally closer to "punish" than "persecute". Fairly neutral synonymous terms with like denotations include {{m|ar|حَاكَمَ}} and {{m|ar|قَاضَى}}.

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.vn:فَتْن,فِتْنَة,فُتُون}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun-pl|فِتَن|f-p}}

# {{plural of|ar|فِتْنَة}}
