# to [[free]] (someone) from [[captivity]] or from [[danger]] by [[pay]]ing a [[sum]] of [[money]] or by [[give away|giving away]] something to [[buy]] him [[back]]; to [[ransom]] (someone) {{+obj|ar|:بِ<for/with/through something>}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:جامع البيان في تأويل القرآن
|trans-title=The Compilation of Qur'anic Interpretations
|author=w:al-Ṭabarī
|year=9th–10th century {{CE}}
|text=
تُحَيِّي بِالسَّلَامَةِ أُمُّ عَمْرٍو * وَهَلْ لَكِ بَعْدَ رَهْطِكِ مِنْ سَلَامِ<br>ذَرِينِي أَصْطَبِحُ بِكْرًا فَإِنِّي * رَأَيْتُ الْمَوْتَ نَقَّبَ عَنْ هِشَامِ<br>وَوَدَّ بَنُو الْمُغِيرَةِ لَوْ '''فَدَوْهُ''' * بِأَلْفٍ مِنْ رِجَالٍ أَوْ سَوَامِ
|subst=عَمْرٍو/عَمْرٍ,سَلَامِ/سَلَامِي,هِشَامِ/هِشَامِي,سَوَامِ/سَوَامِي
|t=ʾUmm Amr wishes us well!<br>Have you, without your kin, ever been well?<br>Let me drink, for I have seen Death<br>Rooting about, hunting Hišām.<br>The clansmen of Muḡīrah wish<br>They could have '''ransomed him'''<br>For even a thousand head<br>Of grazers or of men.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=11th–12th century {{CE}}|author=w:en:Ibn Zuhr|title=|text=يَا غُصْنَ نَقَا مُكَلَّلًا بِٱلذَّهَبِ – '''أَفْدِي'''كَ مِنَ ٱلرَّدَى بِأُمِّي وَأَبِي|t=Oh gold-wreathed sand dune branch – I would '''ransom''' you from death with my mother and father!}}

