Page 14128 فردوس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
An {{bor|ar|ira|-}} borrowing, ultimately from {{der|ar|ira-pro|*paridayjah}}. According to Eilers, an Iranian form ''*parādēs'', which resembles the very common broken plural pattern {{m|ar||فَعَالِيق}}, was perhaps borrowed as a plural {{m|ar|فَرَادِيس}} and the singular {{m-self|ar|فِرْدَوْس}} created as a {{back-formation|ar|nocap=1}} from it.<ref>{{R:Eilers:1962|page=206}}</ref> However, the plural {{m|ar|فَرَادِيس}} could have been borrowed from {{noncog|grc|παράδεισος}} instead.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|فِرْدَوْس|m|g2=f|pl=فَرَادِيس}}

# a group of [[garden]]s, [[Elysium]], [[Eden]], [[heaven]], [[Heaven]], [[paradise]]
#: {{syn|ar|جَنَّة|نَعِيم}}
#: {{ant|ar|سَعِير|لَظَىٰ|النَّار|جَهَنَّم|جَحِيم|حُطَمَة|سَقَر|هَاوِيَة}}
## The [[Paradise]]/[[Firdaus]]; the highest place in the celestial garden.
##: {{ant|ar|دَرْك}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|فِرْدَوْس|pl=فَرَادِيس}}

