Page 14135 فرسخ: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From Northwestern {{bor|ar|ira-mid}} {{m|und||*frasax|t=parasang}}, cognate with {{cog|xcl|հրասախ}} an Iranian loanword from same source. Compare Sorthwestern Iranian form, {{cog|pal||tr=plsng|ts=frasang|sc=Phlv}} and {{cog|fa|فرسنگ|tr=farsang}}. Astronomical sense {{semantic loan|ar|en|parsec|nocap=1}}. See also {{m|ar|فَرْسَخ فَلَكِيّ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|فَرْسَخ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|فَرْسَخ|m|pl=فَرَاسِخ}}

# [[parasang]], [[farsang]]
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Egypt/Sudan until 1891}}  a [[linear measure]], 500 {{l|ar|قَصَبَة|tr=}} – about 1750 {{l|mul|m}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Saudi-Arabia until 1964}}  a [[linear measure]], {{frac|8}} of a {{l|ar|مَرْحَلَة|tr=}} – 4830 {{l|mul|m}}
# {{lb|ar|astronomy}} {{short for|ar|فَرْسَخ فَلَكِيّ||[[parsec]]|nocap=1}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|فَرْسَخ|pl=فَرَاسِخ}}

