Page 14136 فرسخ فلكي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{m|ar|فَرْسَخ}} and {{m|ar|فَلَكِيّ}}. Literally "astronomical [[parasang]]"; used to disambiguate the astronomical measure (approximately 3.26 light years) from the historical measure (roughly 2-4 miles), both of which are called {{m|ar|فَرْسَخ}} in Arabic.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|فَرْسَخ فَلَكِيّ|m|pl=فَرَاسِخ فَلَكِيَّة}}

# {{lb|ar|astronomy}} [[parsec]]

====Synonyms====
* {{l|ar|فَرْسَخ}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|ar|سَنَة ضَوْئِيَّة|tr=sana ḍawʔiyya|t=[[light year]]}}
* {{l|ar|وَحْدَة فَلَكِيَّة|tr=waḥda falakiyya|t=[[astronomical unit]]}}

{{C|ar|Units of measure}}
