Page 14143 فرصاد: -------- begin text --------
{{was fwotd|ar|2020|October|28}}
[[File:Schildau Maulbeerbaum Fruechte rot 3.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|فِرْصَاد}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
Originally {{m|ar|فِرْصِيد}}, from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, {{cog|tmr|פַּרְצֵידָא|tr=parṣīḏā|t=seed, kernel, pip}}, which is in {{cog|syc|ܦܪܨܢܬܐ|tr=parṣentā}}, collective {{m|syc|ܦܪܨܢܐ|tr=parṣennē}}, also {{cog|tmr|פּוּרְצְנֵי|tr=purṣənē|t=kernels especially of grapes}}, which was also borrowed as {{m|ar|فِرْصِن}}, {{m|ar|فِرْصِم|t=grape pips}}. This shows that the term is derived from the Aramaic root {{m|arc|פ־ר־ץ|tr=p-r-ṣ}}, cognate to the Arabic root {{ar-root|ف ر ص|nocat=1}} related to slitting and making a breach, referring to the way a kernel is obtained from a fruit. Compare {{cog|he|חַרְצָן|tr=ḥarṣā́n|t=immature and thus sour grapes}} from the root {{m|he|ח־ר־ץ}} cognate to the Arabic root {{ar-root|ح ر ص|nocat=1}} related to slitting, with such a meaning development from pips to mulberry because the mulberry is an [[aggregate fruit]]. Compare also {{cog|ar|تُوت|t=mulberry}}, again presumably an Aramaic borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|فِرْصَاد}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|فِرْصَاد|m}}

# [[mulberry]] (''[[Morus]]'' spp. plants and fruits)
#* {{RQ:Awwam|8|1|volume=1|pages=417–418|passage=شجر الفرصاد وشجرة شاه بلوط وشجر البندق وشجر الاتفاح وشجر الكمثرى كل هذه تألف بهضعا بعضا وقد يركب في لحائه دون أصله|translation=The mulberry and the chestnut and the hazelnut and the apple and the pear all join together well and they can be grafted on their bark outwith their stems.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|فِرْصَاد}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa|فرصاد|bor=1|tr=fersâd}}
* {{desc|sw|forosadi|bor=1}}

