-------- end text --------
Page 14187 فرهد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Augmented from the root {{ar-root|ف ر ح}}; some Northeastern peninsula dialects like the [[w:ar:لهجة قبيلة الشحوح|Šiḥūḥ]] have shifts of ''ḥ'' to ''h''; note also the ancient Omani tribe name {{m|ar||بَنُو فُرْهُود}}, {{m|ar||الْفَرَاهِيد}}, whence the [[nisba]] of the Oman-born [[w:Al-Khalil ibn Ahmad al-Farahidi|originator]] of the [[w:Kitab al-'Ayn|''kitāb al-ʿayn'']] derives.

