Page 14234 فشقار: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|فَشْقَر}}

===Etymology===
A {{bor|ar|roa}} borrowing. The exact meaning is found in {{cog|an|fascal|t=a heap of sheaves, a bundle of six sheaves; ''nautical'': a wisp of plaits of raw esparto from which cables are made}}; {{cog|gl|vascullo|vascallo|t=a bundle of straw}} is also close in meaning. Ultimately from a derivative of {{der|ar|cel-pro|*baskis|t=bundle}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|فَشْقَار}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|فَشْقَار|m|pl=فَشَاقِير}} {{tlb|ar|al-Andalus|Northern|_|Morocco}}

# a [[heap]] of [[sheaf|sheaves]]
#: {{syn|ar|عَرَمَة|كُدْس|شُونَة}}
#* {{R:ar:Lévi-Provençal:1934|page=196 (٤) line 13}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|فَشْقَار|pl=فَشَاقِير}}

===References===
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=968}}, where, without giving cognates, it is claimed that the word derives from “Low Latin” ''*fascalis'' and that from {{m|la|fascis}}, which is impossible due the affricatization of the last stem consonant; the Latin word is cognate to the Celtic one, hence the similarity.
* {{R:xaa:Corriente|page=399b}}, also without cognates from ''*fascalis''
* {{R:xaa:Vocabulista|page=227}}

{{C|ar|Units of measure}}
