{{wp|lang=ar|Medicago sativa|فصفص}}

===Etymology===
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*h₁eḱ-|*h₁ed-}}
{{PIE word|ar|h₁éḱwos}}
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|אַסְפַּסְתָּא|tr=ʾaspastā}} / {{m|syc|ܐܰܣܦܷܣܬܳܐ|tr=ʾaspestā|t=lucerne}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒊍𒉺𒊍𒋾|tr=aspastu|t=presumably lucerne}}, from {{der|ar|xme-old|*aspāstiš|t=lucerne}}, from {{der|ar|ira-pro|*HacwaHastiš|t=lucerne|lit=horse-food}} from {{der|ar|ira-pro|*Hácwah|t=horse}} + {{der|ar|ine-pro|-}} {{suf|ine-pro|*h₁ed-|t1=related to eating|*tis|nocat=1}}, the Assyrians having it borrowed when modelling their cavalry after the Medes and thus taking over this name for a plant serving as horsefood, passing it to the Babylonian. So the most likely chain.

