===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{ar-IPA|قَاف}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{ar-IPA|ق}}
* {{sense|Main dialectal variations}} {{ar-IPA|ء|ق|گ}}

===Etymology 1===
From the Nabataean letter {{m|arc-nab|𐢏|tr=q|t=qoph}}, derived from the {{der|ar|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤒|tr=q|t=qop}}, from an uncertain {{der|ar|egy|-}} hieroglyph ({{m|egy|𓃻}}?). See also {{m+|syc|ܩ|tr=q|t=qūp}}, {{m+|he|ק|tr=q|t=qūph}}, {{m+|grc|Φ}}, {{m+|la|Q}}.

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ق '''/''' ق‍ '''/''' ‍ق‍ '''/''' ‍ق'''|tr=qāf}}

# The twenty-first letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ف}} and followed by {{l|ar|ك}}.

====Symbol====
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ق '''/''' ق‍ '''/''' ‍ق‍ '''/''' ‍ق'''|tr=qāf}}

# The nineteenth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ص}} and followed by {{l|ar|ر}}.

=====See also=====
