===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|grc|κάδος}}. The form {{m|ar|قَدَس}}, anciently used in the Ḥijāz and thence exported to Northwestern Arabic, came via {{bor|ar|arc|-}} – {{cog|syc|ܩܱܕܣܴܐ|tr=qadsā, qaddəsā}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَادُوس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَادُوس|m|pl=قَوَادِيس}}

# {{senseid|ar|water holder}} [[skep]], [[scoop]], [[kibble]], [[bucket]], [[dipper]] (for a well or a [[mill]] or for [[irrigation]] or an [[excavator]] or whatever)
#: {{alti|ar|قَدَس}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|instead=1|lang=ar|page=208 line 8|passage=والقادوس كوز الدولاب|t=And ''bucket'' is the dipper of a water-wheel.}}
# {{senseid|ar|conduit}} [[pipe]], [[conduit]], [[duct]], for example [[such]] as [[affiliate]]d to the [[bucket]]s or [[scoop]]s of a [[waterwheel]] for [[irrigation]]
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|H|instead=1|lang=ar|page=86 line 14–15|passage=ويحيط بالبلد عيون غيرها مشهورة ينتفع بمياهها كالقادوس|t=And one finds in the environs of the town other famed springs the water of which is employed as irrigation’s wellhead.}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|15|volume=1|page=308}} with emendations {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=2|page=314}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|15|volume=1|page=656}}
