Page 14759 قت: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
For the cutting meaning, related to {{ar-root|ق د د|nocat=1}} and {{ar-root|ق ط ع}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:قَتّ}}

# to [[follow]] the [[stench]] of
# to [[calumniate]]
# to [[cut]] [[lengthwise]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:قَتّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قَتّ|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَتَّ|form=I}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَتّ}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|قَتَّات}}, {{l|ar|قَتُوت|t=calumniator}}
* {{l|ar|اِقْتَتَّ|t=to uproot}}
* {{l|ar|قَتَات}}, standardly {{l|ar|قَتَاد|t=milkvetch}}
* {{l-self|ar|قَتّ|t=lucerne}}, below
* {{l|ar|قَات|t=khat}}

===Etymology 2===
From the family above due to its being cut in dry strips, like {{m|ar|قُرْط|t=Egyptian clover}} from {{m|ar|قَرَطَ|t=to chop}}, apparently in occasional distinction from {{m|ar|رَطْبَة|t=alfalfa}} as of alfalfa in a wet ({{m|ar|رَطْب}}) state, in spite of Bos and Käs declaring the word to come apparently from {{cog|fa|قت|tr=qot}}, which is rare and listed by Vullers as itself from Arabic. Note that {{m|ar|قَتَاد|t=milkvetch}} is also a faboid.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قَتّ|m}}

# [[lucerne]] (various {{taxfmt|Medicago|genus}} spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|فِصْفِص|رَطْبَة|بِرْسِيم حِجَازِيّ}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:{{w|Avicenna|ابن سينا}}<t:Avicenna>|title=ar:القانون في الطب<t:{{w|The Canon of Medicine|Canon Medicinae}}>|year=1025|passage=قت: الماهية: هو الأسفست أي الرطبة وهو علف الدواب.<br/>آلات المفاصل: دهن القت أنفع شيء للرعشة يذهب بها.|t=Qatt: Its nature: It is alfalfa, lucerne, a fodder crop.<br/>Joints: The oil of lucerne helps a bit against shudder.}}
#* {{RQ:Ibn Janāḥ:2020|page=988|section=852 (fol. 72r,12–15)|passage=قتّ، قال أبو حنيفة: هو جفيف القضب، والقتّ هو الفصفصة، وقد ذكرنا الفصفصة في حرف الفاء وقلنا هناك إنّه يقال لها بالعجمية يربة دموله ومعناه عُشْبة البغلة.|t=Lucerne. Abū Ḥanīfa equates it with dry {{m|ar|قَضْب}}. It is {{m|ar|فِصْفِصَة}}. We have just noted {{m|ar|فصفص|فِصْفِصَة}} under the letter f. There we said that it is called in Romance yerba de mula which means she-mule herb.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَتّ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=396a}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=2|pages=670b–671a}}
* [http://www.enature.qa/ar/specie/lucerne/ Qaṭar e-Nature – {{lang|ar|قت}}] – {{taxfmt|Medicago sativa|species}}

{{C|ar|Trifolieae tribe plants|Grains}}

-------- end text --------
Page 14760 قتاد: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Astragalus onobrychis sl1.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قَتَاد}} – {{taxlink|Astragalus onobrychis|species}}|upright=1.15]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Regressively assimilated respectively progressively dissimilated in voicedness from dialectal variants {{m|ar|قَدَاد}}, {{m|ar|قَتَات}}, also {{m|ar|قَدِيد}}, {{m|ar|قَتِيت}}, from {{m|ar|قَدَّ}}, {{m|ar|قَتَّ|t=to snithe into strips, to cut lengthwise}} – the former more known, the latter however reflected in {{m|ar|قَتّ|t=lucerne}} and {{m|ar|قَات|t=qat}} –, as cutting, slitting is what one does with the [[milk-vetch]]es, whose profusion of sap was also the motive for the derivation of {{m|ar|كَثِيرَاء|t=tragacanth, gum of milk-vetches}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَتَاد}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|قَتَاد|m|sing=قَتَادَة}}

# [[milkvetch]] ({{taxfmt|Astragalus|genus}} gen. et spp.)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|قَتَاد}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=396}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Pflanzen|page=427 to 50<sub>2</sub>}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=1000}}

{{C|ar|Legumes}}
-------- end text --------
