Page 14771 قثاء: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Tirozî.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قِثَّاء}}]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
* Leonid Kogan and Jussi Aro list it as being Proto-Semitic (which already Zimmern suspected), cognate to {{cog|gez|ቍሳይ}}, {{m|gez|ቈስያ|t=cucumber}}, {{cog|akk|𒄾|tr=qiššû|t=cucumber}}, {{cog|he|קשוא|tr=qiššūʾ|t=Armenian cucumber}}, {{cog|syc|ܩܰܛܽܘܬܳܐ|tr=qaṭṭūtā|t=cucumber}} (one explains the Syriac middle consonant as having developed *{{IPAchar|/t/}} → {{IPAchar|/tˤ/}} because of {{IPAchar|/q/}}).
* It is a wanderwort found as {{cog|sux|𒄾|tr=ukuš<sub>2</sub>|t=cucumber}} {{cog|grc|σικύα|t=bottle gourd}}, {{cog|grc|σίκυος}}, {{m|grc|σικυός}}, {{m|grc|σίκυς|t=cucumber}}, {{cog|la|cucumis|t=cucumber}}, {{cog|xcl|սեխ|t=muskmelon}}, and possibly {{cog|sla-pro|*tyky|t=pumpkin, gourd}}. {{doublet|ar|كُوسَا|t1=zucchini}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قِثَّاء|قُثَّاء}}

===Noun===
