Page 14779 قد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ق د د}}
Cognate to {{cog|he|קָדַד|tr=qāḏaḏ}}, {{cog|arc|קָדַד|tr=qāḏaḏ|t=to cut out}}, {{cog|syc|ܩܰܕ|tr=qadd|t=to tear or cut away}}, {{cog|gez|ቀደ|t=to cut open, to tear apart|tr=ḳäddä}}, {{cog|gdq|ḳdd|t=to shave off, to cut off, to scalp}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قَدَّ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-قد.ogg}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:قَدّ}}

# to [[cut]] into [[strips]]
# to [[cut off]], to [[chop]] [[off]]
# to [[cut out]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:قَدّ}}

===Etymology 2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قَدّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قَدّ|m|pl=قِدَاد|pl2=قُدُود|pl3=أَقُدّ|pl4=أَقِدَّة}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَدَّ|form=I}}
# [[cutting]], [[cutting off]]
# [[size]], [[stature]], [[figure]]
# [[length]]
# [[definite]] [[measure]] or [[quantity]]
# [[equal]] of a [[person]] or [[thing]]
# [[lambskin]]
# [[strip]], [[shred]]
# [[split]]
# [[caesura]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَدّ|pl=قِدَاد|pl2=قُدُود|pl3=أَقُدّ|pl4=أَقِدَّة}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|قد}}

===Etymology 3===
From the root {{ar-root|ق|د|د}} in the sense of being a thing separated or cut apart, a thing distinct with its own measure and shape, a defined piece; extended semantically to a secure definite thing, a certainty, hence the past tense implying a thing has already been set or definitive.

The non-past tense stems from the idea of something intended, likely expected, planned to be, measured to occur, or cut out to happen.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قَدْ}}

====Particle====
{{ar-particle|قَدْ}}

# {{lb|ar|in the past tense}} {{non-gloss definition|Indicates nearness in time or recentness}}, [[recently]], [[just now]]
#: {{ux|ar|'''قَدْ''' وَصَلَ|t=he has arrived; he had arrived|inline=t}}
#: {{ux|ar|كَانَ ('''قَدْ''') وَصَلَ|t=he had arrived|inline=t}}
#: {{ux|ar|سَيَكُونُ ('''قَدْ''') وَصَلَ|t=he will have arrived|inline=t}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3|143
|passage=وَلَقَدْ كُنتُمْ تَمَنَّوْنَ الْمَوْتَ مِن قَبْلِ أَن تَلْقَوْهُ فَ'''قَدْ''' رَأَيْتُمُوهُ وَأَنتُمْ تَنظُرُونَ

|translation=You used to wish for death before you could meet it, and '''just now''', you could see it when were looking ahead.}}
# {{lb|ar|in the non-past tense}} {{non-gloss definition|Indicates nonveridicality}}, [[might]], [[could]], [[may]]
#: {{ux|ar|'''قَدْ''' يَكُونُ كَذٰلِكَ|t=It '''may''' be so.|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|ar|إِنْ سَأَلْتَهُ ٱلْمَالَ فَ'''قَدْ''' يُعْطِيكَ.|If you ask him for money, he '''may''' give you.|inline=1}}
# {{lb|ar||in the non-past tense|obsolete}} {{non-gloss definition|Expresses emphasis}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|33|18
|passage='''قَدْ''' يَعْلَمُ اللَّهُ الْمُعَوِّقِينَ مِنكُمْ وَالْقَائِلِينَ لِإِخْوَانِهِمْ هَلُمَّ إِلَيْنَا ۖ وَلَا يَأْتُونَ الْبَأْسَ إِلَّا قَلِيلًا

|translation=God '''does''' know the hinderers among you and the ones telling their brethren, "Over here!" These fight in wars only rarely.}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|لَقَدْ}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|jrb|קד|tr=qad}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|قد}}

===Etymology 4===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|en|cod}}, as the range of the fish does not overlap with typical Arabic-speaking areas; compare {{cog|he|קוד|tr=kod|t=cod}}. Compare also its other names {{m|ar|مُورَة|tr=|t=cod}} borrowed from {{noncog|fr|morue}}, and {{m|ar|غادُس|tr=|t=cod}} borrowed from {{noncog|la|gadus|t=generic term for fish; cod}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قُدّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُدّ|m}}

# [[cod]] {{gloss|the fish}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُدّ}}

===Etymology 5===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قُدْ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb-form|قُدْ|I}}

# {{inflection of|ar|قَادَ||2|m|s|actv|impr}}

====References====
* {{R:CAL|qdd|V}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=404}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=2|page=682}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=1003}}

