Page 14786 قدح: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|ق د ح}}
The base stem verb is cognate to {{cog|syc|ܩܕܰܚ|tr=qdaḥ|t=to [[bore]], to [[pierce]]; to [[light]], to [[heaten]]}}, {{cog|arc|קָדַח|tr=qādah|t=to [[bore]], to [[pierce]]}}, {{cog|gez|ቀድሐ|t=to draw water; to pierce, to drill}}. For the “cup” meaning, {{cog|gez|መቅድሕ|t=water jar; drill|tr=mäḳdəḥ}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩣𐩤𐩵𐩢|t=cup, vessel for offerings}}. Compare also {{m|ar|قَدَّ|t=to cut off}}, as that root has been confused at least by Aramaic where {{m|syc|ܩܕܰܚ|tr=qdaḥ}} also means “to shave” and {{m|arc|קְדַד|tr=qədad}} “to penetrate”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|ar|Ar-قدح.ogg}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.vn:قَدْح}}

# to [[light]], to [[ignite]], to [[spark]]
# to [[pierce]], to [[bore]], to [[drill]]
# to [[belittle]], to [[diminish]], to [[disparage]], to [[vilify]]
# to [[vilify]], to [[libel]], to [[calumniate]]
# to [[ladle]], to [[bucket]], to [[scoop]], to [[draw]]
# {{cln|ar|contranyms}} to [[pour]], to [[bucket]], to [[scoop]], to [[ladle]], to [[dole out]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.vn:قَدْح}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[attenuate]], to [[lessen]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَدْح|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَدَحَ|form=I}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَدْح}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قِدْح|m|pl=قِدَاح|pl2=أَقْدُح|pl3=أَقْدَاح|pl4=أَقَادِيح}}

# [[arrow]] [[shaft]]
#: {{syn|ar|نَضِيّ}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|61|117
|passage=يَقْرَءُونَ الْقُرْآنَ لَا يُجَاوِزُ تَرَاقِيَهُمْ، يَمْرُقُونَ مِنَ الدِّينِ كَمَا يَمْرُقُ السَّهْمُ مِنَ الرَّمِيَّةِ، يُنْظَرُ إِلَى نَصْلِهِ فَلَا يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ، ثُمَّ يُنْظَرُ إِلَى رِصَافِهِ فَمَا يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ، ثُمَّ يُنْظَرُ إِلَى '''نَضِيِّهِ ـ وَهُوَ قِدْحُهُ''' ـ فَلَا يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ، ثُمَّ يُنْظَرُ إِلَى قُذَذِهِ فَلَا يُوجَدُ فِيهِ شَيْءٌ، قَدْ سَبَقَ الْفَرْثَ وَٱلدَّمَ.
|translation=They recite the Qurʾān but it does not go beyond their clavicles and they will desert the creed as an arrow goes through a target’s body, so one would, on looking at the arrow’s blade, see nothing on it; then one would look at its sinew and see nothing, then one would look at '''its arrowshaft''' and see nothing, then one would look at its fletching and would see nothing, for the arrow, by its speed, has even obviated entrails and blood.
|subst=قُذَذِهِ/قُذَذِ-هِي,نَضِيِّهِ/نَضِيِّ-هِي,وَهُوَ/وَ-هُوَ,قِدْحُهُ/قِدْحُ-هُو,فَلَا/فَ-لَا,فِيهِ/فِي-هِ,وَٱلدَّمَ/وَ-ٱلدَّمَ,تَرَاقِيَهُمْ/تَرَاقِيَ-هُمْ,نَصْلِهِ/نَصْلِ-هِي,رِصَافِهِ/رِصَافِ-هِي,فَمَا/فَ-مَا}}
# {{lb|ar|pars pro toto}} [[arrow]]
#: {{near-syn|ar|سَهْم|نُشَّاب|حُظْوَة}}
# {{lb|ar|Yemen}} [[cheek]] (of a [[beast]] or [[human]])
#: {{near-syn|ar|خَدّ|مَلْطَم|عِذَار|عَارِض|وَجْنَة|حنك#Moroccan Arabic<alt:حَنَك><q:in dialects>}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قِدْح|m|pl=قِدَاح|pl2=أَقْدُح|pl3=أَقْدَاح|pl4=أَقَادِيح}}

[[File:Trinkglas, Tumbler-Form.jpg|thumb]]
[[File:Bucket, milk (AM 1997.72.11).jpg|thumb]]

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَدَح|m|pl=أَقْدَاح}}

# {{senseid|ar|bucket}} a [[container]] for [[carry|carrying]] or [[serve|serving]] [[liquid]]s that has a [[broad]] and [[often]] [[flat]] [[base]] and no [[spout]]s; a [[beaker]], a [[tumbler]]; a [[mug]]; a [[pail]], a [[bucket]]; a [[can]]
#: {{ux|ar|حُلِبَتِ الْبَقَرَةُ فِي '''قَدَحَيْنِ'''.|t=The cow was milked into '''two pails'''.}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|tirmidhi|14|17
|passage=رَسُولُ اللّٰهِ صَلَّى اللّٰه عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ بَاعَ حِلْسًا وَ'''قَدَحًا''' وَقَالَ ”مَنْ يَشْتَرِي هَذَا الْحِلْسَ وَالْ'''قَدَحَ'''؟“. فَقَالَ رَجُلٌ ”أَخَذْتُهُمَا بِدِرْهَمٍ“. فَقَالَ النَّبِيُّ صَلَّى اللّٰه عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ ”مَنْ يَزِيدُ عَلَى دِرْهَمٍ مَنْ يَزِيدُ عَلَى دِرْهَمٍ“ فَأَعْطَاهُ رَجُلٌ دِرْهَمَيْنِ فَبَاعَهُمَا مِنْهُ.
|translation=The Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) sold a saddle blanket and a '''drinking bowl'''. He said: “Who will buy saddle blanket and '''drinking bowl'''?”. So a man said: “I will take them for a dirham.” So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Who will give more than a dirham? Who will give more than a dirham?” A man gave him two dirhams, so he sold them to him.}}
# {{senseid|ar|drymeasure}} {{n-g|a [[dry measure]]}}
##{{lb|ar|Yemen}} about 30 kilograms and 36 [[liter]]s, exact value standardized differently by community and good (wheat, dhurra, dukhn, rice, sesame)
##{{lb|ar|obsolete|Egypt|Sudan|until 1892}} 32 {{l|ar|قِيرَاط}}, {{frac|8}} of a {{l|ar|كَيْلَة}}, {{frac|96}} of a {{l|ar|إِرْدَبّ}} – 2.062 [[liter]]s

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَدَح|pl=أَقْدَاح}}

