===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*ḳudš-|t=holy}}. Cognate with {{cog|hbo|קָדוֹשׁ|tr=qɔḏoš|t=holy}}, {{cog|he|-}} {{he-m|קודש|dwv=קֹדֶשׁ|tr=qṓḏeš}} and {{cog|sem-srb|𐩤𐩵𐩪}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/u~u.nopass.vn:قُدْس,قُدُس,قَدَاسَة}}

# to be [[pure]], to be [[immaculate]]
# to be [[holy]], to be [[sacred]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/u~u.nopass.vn:قُدْس,قُدُس,قَدَاسَة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُدُس|m|head2=قُدْس|pl=أَقْدَاس}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَدُسَ|form=I||to be [[pure]], to be [[holy]]}}
# [[purity]]
# [[sanctity]], [[holiness]]
# [[shrine]], [[sanctuary]]
# [[Paradise]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُدُس|head2=قُدْس|pl=أَقْدَاس}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|الْقُدْس||[[Jerusalem]]}}

===Etymology 2===
Causative of {{m|ar|قَدُسَ}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# to [[purify]]
# to [[sanctify]]
# to [[consecrate]] {{qualifier|something}} to [[God]]
# to [[worship]], to [[venerate]]
# {{lb|ar|Christianity}} to [[say]] or [[hear]] [[Mass]]
# {{lb|ar|Christianity}} to [[canonize]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

===Etymology 3===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قَدَس|pl=أَقْدَاس|m|pl2=قُدُوس}}

# {{alternative form of|ar|قَادُوس|nocap=1|t=scoop, dipper}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَدَس|pl=أَقْدَاس|pl2=قُدُوس}}

