Page 14859 قرظ: -------- begin text --------
[[File:28-05-2017 Gum arabic (Acacia nilotica) seedpods, Praia da Maré das Porcas (1).JPG|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قَرَظ}}|upright=1.15]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar|سنط|قَرَظ}}

===Etymology===
Inherited from {{inh|ar|sem-wes-pro|-}}, cognate to {{cog|arc|קרטא}} / {{m|syc|ܩܷܪܱܛܳܐ|tr=qerraṭṭā|t=acacia; carob}}, and {{cog|grc|κεράτιον|t=carob tree}}, matched to the Semitic. This tree is important for tanning and dying, hence the meaning of “to eulogize”.

According to Löw the Syriac word is from Arabic and the Arabic from Greek, but a borrowing of {{m|ar|ظ}} is hard (save from {{w|South Semitic}}). and the Greek gives regularly already existing {{doublet|ar|قِيرَاط|notext=1}}.

''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' considers a borrowing from {{bor|ar|egy|ꜣqrw|t=a tree the fruits of which are used officinally}}<!--Erman-Grapow I 138--> with an added second element, compare {{m|ar|نَبَق}} where the same seems to have happened.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَرَظ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|قَرَظ|sing=قَرَظَة}}

# {{taxfmt|Acacia|genus}} spp. or {{taxfmt|Vachellia|genus}} spp., especially {{taxfmt|Vachellia nilotica|species}} and {{taxlink|Acacia etbaica|species}} syn. {{taxlink|Vachellia etbaica|species}}, and especially its leaves or pods
#: {{syn|ar|طَلْح|سَنْط}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|قَرَظ}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|قُرَيْظَة|pos=diminutive}}
* {{l|ar|قَرَظِيّ}}
* {{l|ar|قَرَّظَ|t=to eulogize, to praise}}
* {{l|ar|تَقَارَظَ|t=to praise one another}}
* {{l|ar|قَرِيظ|t=eulogy}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|syc|ܩܪܕ|bor=1|tr=qrḏ}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.vn:قَرْظ}}

# to [[tan]] or [[dye]] with {{l|ar||قَرَظ}}
# to [[pluck]] the [[leaf|leave]]s or [[pod]]s {{l|ar||قَرَظ}}

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.vn:قَرْظ}}

===Verb===
