Page 14864 قرفة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Referenced as {{m|grc|κάρφεα|t=cinnamon}} in [[w:Herodotus|Herodotus's]] ''[[w:Histories_(Herodotus)|Histories]]'' in connection to Arabia by 440 BC, as well as being attested as a name in Pre-Islamic Arabia; containers with cinnamon residue have been found in the [[w:Levant|Levant]] dating to 3,000 years ago.<ref>Live Science, [https://www.livescience.com/39011-cinnamon-trade-found-in-israel.html Evidence of 3,000-Year-Old Cinnamon Trade Found in Israel]</ref> Related to {{m|ar|قِلْف|t=bark, rind}}, {{m|ar|قِلَافَة|t=bark, outer covering}}, and {{cog|syc|ܩܠܦܬܐ|tr=qlāp̄tā|t=bark, peel}}; perhaps ultimately an early [[w:Semitic languages|Semitic]] borrowing from a {{bor|ar|dra}} language such as the precursor of the {{cog|ta|கருவா|t=cinnamon or clove tree}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قِرْفَة|f}}

# [[cinnamon]]
#: {{syn|ar|دَارْصِينِيّ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قِرْفَة}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Lane|قرف|page=2987}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|قلف|page=921}}
<references/>

