Page 14885 قرنفل: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|mul=قرنفل شائع}}
[[File:Syzygium aromaticum.jpg|thumb|right|{{senseno|ar|clove}}|upright=1.15]]
[[File:Dianthus caryophyllus Γαρίφαλλο.JPG|thumb|right|{{senseno|ar|pink}}|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ar|قَرَنْفُول}}

===Etymology===
Imported from India. Compare {{cog|ta|கராம்பு}}, {{m|ta|கிராம்பு}}, {{m|ml|കരയാമ്പ്}}, {{m|ml|ഗ്രാമ്പൂ}}, {{cog|si|කරාබු}}, {{cog|tl|klabong}}, {{m|tl|klabos}}, {{m|tl|kalabumpako}},{{attention|tl|all give few hits and Tagalog Wikipedia lacks the native names}} all meaning cloves. From the same source {{cog|grc|καρυόφυλλον}}, {{cog|am|ቅርንፉድ}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَرَنْفُل|قُرَنْفُل}}
* {{rhymes|ar|ul}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَرَنْفُل|m|head2=قُرَنْفُل}}

# {{senseid|ar|clove}} [[clove]] ({{taxfmt|Syzygium aromaticum|species}})
#* {{quote-book
|ar
|year=10th century
|author=Al-Mutanabbi
|chapter=Poem #201
|title=The Works of 'Abū al-Ṭayyib al-Mutanabbī
|volume=3
|pages=201–202
|year_published=1978
|publisher=Dār Al-Ma‘rifah
|passage=وَمَنْزِلٍ لَيْسَ لَنَا بِمَنْزِلِ / وَلَا لِغَيْرِ الْغَادِيَاتِ الْهُطَّلِ<br>نَدِيِّ الْخُزَامَى ذَفِرِ '''الْقَرَنْفُلِ''' / مُحَلَّلٍ مِلْوَحْشِ لَمْ يُحَلَّلِ|t=A place, which has never been a stop for us<br>Nor anyone but the show'ring daybreak-clouds,<br>With dewy lavenders, and fragrant '''cloves''',<br>Settled by the wildlife, and no one else.}}
# {{senseid|ar|pink}} [[pink]], [[carnation]] ({{taxfmt|Dianthus caryophyllus|species}})

