Page 14895 قرية: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ق ر ي}}
[[File:Kooshk village 2 (روستای کوشک 2) - panoramio.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قَرْيَة}}|upright=1.5]]
Related to {{ar-root|ق ر ر}}. Perhaps from {{inh|ar|afa-pro|-}}. Immediate cognates are  {{cog|he|קִרְיָה|tr=qiryā́|t=complex, city}} and {{cog|he|קֶרֶת|tr=qerêt|t=city, settlement}}, {{cog|syc|ܩܪܝܬܐ|tr=qərīṯā|t=town, village}}, {{cog|uga|𐎖𐎗𐎚}}, {{m|uga|𐎖𐎗𐎊𐎚|t=city, town}}, {{cog|phn|𐤒𐤓𐤕}}, {{m|phn|𐤒𐤀𐤓𐤕|t=city}}, {{cog|obm|𐤒𐤓|tr=qr|t=wall, city}}. Further relations include {{cog|kab|iɣṛem|t=city}}, {{cog|om|goorroo|t=wall}}, {{cog|so|guri|t=dwelling, house}}, {{cog|ha|gari|t=town}}, {{cog|kr|gàrú|t=town wall}} and {{cog|kot|gaura|t=shed}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قَرْيَة}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-قرية.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قَرْيَة|f|pl=قُرًى}} {{tlb|ar|countable}}

# any [[populate]]d [[area]] or the [[community]] [[thereof]]
#: {{syn|ar|مِصْر|t=a populated locality}}
# an [[urban]] [[area]] or [[community]] (such as  a [[town]] or a [[city]])
# {{lb|ar|modern}} a [[rural]] [[area]] or [[community]] (such as a [[village]]), a [[hamlet]]
#: {{ux|ar|هٰؤُلَاءِ الْفَلَّاحُونَ هُم مِنْ تِلْكَ الْقَرْيَةِ الْمِصْرِيَّةِ الْكَبِيرَةِ.|These farmers are from that big Egyptian village.}}

