Page 14900 قريش: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Various theories exist. One theory cites the {{ar-diminutive}} form of {{m|ar|قِرْش|t=shark, any large fish that eats smaller fish}}; the name semantically is parallel to being the {{m|en|top dog}}, as sharks are {{l|en|apex predators}} at the top of their food chain. 9th-century scholar Hisham ibn al-Kalbi asserted that the name stemmed from {{m|ar|تَقَرُّش|t=coming together}} to denote the various tribes unified under Quraysh.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قُرَيْش}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|قُرَيْش|f|g2=m}}

# [[Quraysh]] ([[Arabian]] [[tribe]] or tribal confederacy)
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|106|1-3
|passage=لِإِيلَافِ '''قُرَيْشٍ''' إِيلَافِهِمْ رِحْلَةَ ٱلشِّتَاءِ وَٱلصَّيْفِ فَلْيَعْبُدُوا رَبَّ هَٰذَا ٱلْبَيْتِ {{...}}
|t=For the accustomed security of the Quraysh - their accustomed security [in] the caravan of winter and summer - Let them worship the Lord of this House {{...}}
|subst=لِإِيلَافِ/لِ-إِيلَافِ,وَٱلصَّيْفِ/وَ-ٱلصَّيْفِ,فَلْيَعْبُدُوا/فَ-لْ-يَعْبُدُوا
}}
# The 106th [[sura]] (chapter) of the [[Qur'an]].

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُرَيْش|state=ind-def}}

====Derived terms====
{{col3|ar|بَنُو قُرَيْش|قُرَيْشِيّ|قُرَشِيّ}}

{{C|ar|Qur'an}}
