====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَزْح}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-noun|قُزَح|m}}

# {{n-g|a [[god]] or [[demon]] of the [[rainstorm]] of the [[pagan]] Arabs, translatable as “[[thunder god]]” or “[[rain demon]]”. Related to a certain ritual of “standing” ({{m|ar|وُقُوف}}) performed at a hill (the hill termed {{m|ar|جَبَل قُزَح}}, now {{m|ar|جَبَل عَرَفَة|t={{w|Mount Arafat}}}}) east of [[Mecca]] at [[dawn]] where he was apparently believed to dwell, or perhaps the hill itself was [[deify|deified]].}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|tirmidhi|9|78
|passage=فَلَمَّا أَصْبَحَ أَتَى قُزَحَ فَوَقَفَ عَلَيْهِ وَقَالَ «هَذَا قُزَحُ وَهُوَ الْمَوْقِفُ وَجَمْعٌ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ»
|translation=When it became morning he went to quzaḥ and stood at him and said: “This is quzaḥ, and it is the place of standing, and all of jamʿ is a place for standing.”}}

