Page 14922 قسطاس: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|قِسْطَار|قُسْطَار|قَسْطَرِيّ|*سِقِسْطَار|سِقِنْطَار|سِنِقْطَار|سِقْطِرِيّ}}

===Etymology===
Via an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} term retained in {{cog|syc|ܣܓܘܣܛܪܐ|tr=səgosṭārā}} and other Syriac spellings from {{bor|ar|grc|ζυγοστάτης|t=weigher}}, which also passed into {{cog|la|zygostatēs}}. For the stem ending in {{m|ar||ـس}}, maybe also denoting the occupation after {{m|grc|ζυγοστασία}}, {{m|grc|ζυγοστάτησις|t=weighing}}. Influenced by {{m|ar|قِسْط|t=share}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قِسْطَاس}}, {{ar-IPA|قُسْطَاس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قُسْطَاس|m|head2=قِسْطَاس|pl=قَسَاطِيس}}

# {{C|ar|Occupations}}{{tlb|ar|obsolete}} [[weigher]], [[moneychanger]]
#: {{syn|ar|وَزَّان|صَرَّاف}}

====Usage notes====
After antiquity, when the word was no more understood, occurrences such as in the Qurʾān were frequently interpreted as “balance, scales”, and reused as such in few book titles and technical texts – e.g. the 1121 work {{m|ar||كِتَاب مِيزَان الْحِكْمَة}} of {{w|Al-Khazini|Al-Ḵāzinīy}}, surely not abiding by living language – including the particular phrasing {{m|ar||الْقِسْطَاس الْمُسْتَقِيم}} from [https://quran.com/26/182 Q 26:182].

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُسْطَاس|m|head2=قِسْطَاس|pl=قَسَاطِيس}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:EALL|volume=3|page=7|entry=Latin Loanwords|author=Shahîd, Irfan}} relates the derivation from {{bor|ar|la|cōnstāns}} as “surrounded by questions”
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=198}} about {{m|ar|قسطاس}} rejects {{w|Heinrich Leberecht Fleischer}}’s derivation from {{bor|ar|la|cōnstāns}} as semantically implausible and not supported by any Aramaic form
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|pages=279–280}} about {{m|ar|سقنطار}}, then connecting to {{noncog|la|sēcrētārius}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=187}} about {{m|ar|قسطار}}, then connecting to {{noncog|la|quaestor}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel:1892|pages=258–262}} finally connecting all; but in lack of an Aramaic form for {{m|ar||ـس}} makes a dubious {{cog|cop|-}} origin insinuation, the kind of which we nowadays distance ourselves from, as for {{m|ar|أُسْقُف}} and {{ar-root|س ج ن|nocat=1}}.
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=366b|سِنِقْطَار}}
* {{R:sem:Růžička:1909|page=6}} connects {{m|ar|سِقْطِرِيّ}} to {{noncog|la|sēcrētārius}}, and {{R:sem:Růžička:1909|page=24}} {{m|ar|سِقِنْطَار}} and {{m|ar|سِنِقْطَار}} to {{noncog|la|sēcrētārius}} after Fraenkel which Fraenkel had already dismissed.
* {{R:ota:Meninski|column=2687|entry=سنقطار}}
* {{R:ar:Wiedemann:1906|page=8}}
* {{R:CAL|skwsTr|N}}

{{cln|ar|ghost words}}
