Page 15007 قطران: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
Compare {{cog|he|קִטֵּר|tr=qiṭer}}, {{cog|he|קְטרֶת|tr=qiṭret|t=incense}}, {{cog|arc|קְטָר|tr=qəṭār|t=incense}}, {{cog|arc|עִטְרָן|tr=ʿiṭerān|t=cedar resin, pitch}}, {{cog|syc|ܥܶܛܪܳܢܳܐ|tr=ʿeṭrānā|t=cedar resin, pitch}}, {{cog|syc|ܥܰܛܪܳܢܳܐ|tr=ʿaṭrānā|t=cedar resin, pitch}}, {{cog|syc|ܥܶܛܪܳܐ|tr=ʿeṭrā|t=pitch}}, {{cog|akk|𒇒|ts=iṭṭū|t=raw bitumen}}, further also {{cog|xcl|խայտաղան}}, {{cog|axm|խայծղան|t=a kind of pitch or resin}}. The historic mutual relations are conjectural; at least secondarily both {{m|ar|قَطْر|t=syrup, drops, driblets}} and {{m|ar|عِطْر|t=essence, scented material}} seem related, with the ending {{m|ar||ـَان}} more likely added in {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, in spite of the combination of it with beginning {{m|ar||قـ}} being [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only attested in borrowings|unattested there]]; note also the {{cog|sem-eth}} shape {{m|gez|ዕጣን|t=incense}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قَطْرَان|قِطْرَان|قَطِرَان}}

====Noun====
