Page 15020 قطن: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ق ط ن}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|fabr}}
In view of {{cog|arc|כִיתָנָא}} / {{m|arc|כִיתָאנָא|tr=kittānā}} / {{m|syc|ܟܶܬܳܢܳܐ|tr=kettānā|t=flax; linen}}, source of {{m|ar|كَتّان|t=flax}}, and the derived apparel name {{cog|arc|כִּיתּוּנָא|tr=kittōnā}}, {{m|syc|ܟܝܬܘܢܐ|tr=kettōnā}}, {{m|syc|ܟܘܬܝܢܐ|tr=kuttīnā, kottīnā|t=tunic}}, noting especially its Classical Syriac byform {{m|syc|ܟܘܬܘܢܐ|tr=kuttōnā, kottōnā}}, if the semantic difference from linen to cotton is surmountable, a receival from an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} dialect with an emphaticized byform corresponding to {{cog|uga|𐎖𐎉|t=flax}} is expected in spite of lacking attestation of the needed form, given that the {{w|Western Aramaic}} dialects in the area of former {{w|Ugarit}} are generally {{unk|ar|title=unattested}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قُطْن}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|قُطْن|m|head2=قُطُن|pl=أَقْطَان|sing=قُطْنة}}

# {{C|ar|Mallow subfamily plants}} [[cotton]]
#: {{uxa|ar|هٰذَا ٱلْقَمِيصُ مَصْنُوعٌ مِنَ '''ٱلْقُطْنِ'''.|This shirt is made of '''cotton'''.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُطْن|m|head2=قُطُن|pl=أَقْطَان}}

