Page 15049 قفل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ق ف ل}}. The word for a lock is presumed to be from {{bor|ar|arc|פוּפְלָא}} / {{m|syc|ܩܘܼܦ݂ܠܵܐ|tr=qup̄lā|t=bolt; bond}} and the verbs “to lock” {{denominal verb|nocap=1|ar}}s; to be separated from genuine meanings related to drying, withering up and the returning from a journey related by the idea of retraction or folding-up (leaves as well as belongings; mind also the well-known {{m|ar|قَافِلَة|t=caravan}}), while the meanings of amassing and usuring are derived from perhaps both by the idea of locking up belongings or returning with riches. And the Aramaic is derived by Brockelmann, Asatrian, and Toll from {{der|ar|la|cōpula}}, but Diem deems this daring and CAL to be rejected, and instead related to the root {{syc-root|ܟ|ܒ|ܠ|nocat=1}} related to binding whence {{m|syc|ܟܒܠܐ|tr=kaḇlā|t=fetter}}.

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i,u.ipass.vn:قُفُول}}

# to [[return]] from a [[journey]]
# to [[carry on]] a [[usurious]] [[grain]] [[trade]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i,u.ipass.vn:قُفُول}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.pass.vn:قَفْل}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[lock]], [[lock up]]
# to [[collect]], to [[gather]], to [[amass]], to [[foredeal]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.pass.vn:قَفْل}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.ipass?.vn:قَفْل}} <br />
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.ipass?.vn:قَفْل}} <br />

# to [[dry up]], to [[wither]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.ipass?.vn:قَفْل}}
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.ipass?.vn:قَفْل}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[lock]], to [[lock up]]
#: {{usex|ar|قَفَّلَ الْأَبْوَابَ|He locked the doors thoroughly.}}

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَفْل|m}}
[[File:Medieval door lock detail (16576016123).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قُفْل}}|upright=1.0]]

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَفَلَ|form=I||to [[lock]], [[gather]], [[dry up]]}}
