Page 15054 قفير: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Probably from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}}, compare {{cog|gez|ከፈር|t=basket, canister; peck, modius}}, {{cog|ti|ከፈር|t=big basket}}, {{cog|am|ቀፎ|t=beehive}}, {{cog|xsa|𐩫𐩰𐩧|tr=kfr|t=sluice; covered cistern}}. Compare {{cog|he|כְּפוֹר|tr=kəp̄ōr|t=jar, bowl}}, {{cog|syc|ܟܳܦܱܪܬ݂ܳܐ|tr=kāp̄artā|t=a type of palm basket}}, {{cog|syc|ܟܪܴܦܬܴ݁ܐ|tr=krāp̄tā|t=household appliances}}, {{cog|akk|𒅗𒀊𒀸|tr=ka-ap-rum|ts=kapru|t=a type of sacrifice; the cup, platter, or table for it}}, {{m|akk|𒅗𒅈𒁍|tr=ka-ar-pu|ts=karpu|t=pot, jar, earthen vessel, especially of a fragile kind}}, {{m|akk|𒂁|tr=DUG|ts=karpatu|t=jar, vessel of a fragile kind}}. It may be related to the meanings of covering discussed at {{m|ar|كفر|tr=k-f-r}}, less likely it is extended from a term equaling {{noncog|akk|𒆏𒁍|ts=kappu|t=from {{noncog|sem-pro|*kapp-|t=hand}}, cupped hands; a bowl, a small serving container}} or {{m|ar|قُفَّة|t=large wicker-baskeŧ}}; see else {{m|ar|قَفِيز}} for a picture of the frequency of container names with guttural onset leading over an open vowel to a labial plosive or fricative.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَفِير}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَفِير|pl=قُفْرَان|m}}

# [[frail]], [[basket]]
# [[beehive]]
#: {{syn|ar|خَلِيَّة|جَبْح|كُوَارَة|عَسَّالَة|مَنْحَل}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَفِير|pl=قُفْرَان}}

