Page 15067 قلب: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{m|ar|قَلَبَ|t=to turn}}.{{ar-rootbox|ق ل ب}}

Alternatively, since {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*libb-}} is reconstructed to mean “heart”, the initial {{lang|ar|ق}} could be a phonological insertion to break a biconsonantal cluster and avoid *''∅alb'' or *''∅ulb'', thus *''lb'' → *''∅alb'' → ''qalb''. See also {{cog|ar|لُبّ|tr=lubb}}, "core, heart, intellect", without q- as well.

Other Semitic branches break the *lb cluster by insertion of a vowel between the consonants, not before them, see {{cog|he|לב|tr=lev}}, {{cog|syc|ܠܒܐ|tr=lebbā}}, {{cog|afa-pro|*lib-}}, {{cog|ber-pro|*ulβ}} (and {{cog|egy|jb}} which lost the initial l-), none employ q- as part of the root.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|heart}} {{ar-IPA|قَلْب}} {{audio|ar|Ar-قلب.ogg}}
* {{sense|to turn}} {{ar-IPA|قَلَبَ}}
* {{sense|to flip}} {{ar-IPA|قَلَّبَ}}
* {{sense|skillful in turning}} {{ar-IPA|قُلَّب}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قَلْب|m|pl=قُلُوب}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَلَبَ|form=I}}
# {{C|ar|Organs}}[[heart]] (organ)
# [[heart]] {{gloss|the symbolic seat of human emotion}}
#: {{ux|ar|إِنَّمَا يُمْكِنُ لِلْإِنْسَانِ أَنْ يَرَى بِصُورَةٍ صَحِيحَةٍ مِنْ خِلَالِ قَلْبِهِ؛ فَالْأُمُورَ الْجَوْهَرِيَّةِ غَيْرُ مُرَئِيَّةٍ لِلْعَيْنِ.|It is only with the heart that one can see rightly; what is essential is invisible to the eye.}}

