===Etymology 3===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|קוּלְתָא|tr=qulləṯā}}, same. From {{der|ar|akk|𒄣𒇷𒌋|tr=qulliu|t=a bowl}}, older {{der|ar|akk|𒄖𒌌𒇻|tr=gullu|t=a container}}, also {{der|ar|akk|𒄖𒌌𒆷𒌅|tr=gullatu|t=ewer}}. Also exists as {{cog|hbo|גֻלָּה|tr=gullāh}}, {{cog|uga|𐎂𐎍}}, {{cog|xeb|𒄘𒇷𒈝|tr=GÚ-LI-LUM}}. Directly from {{cog|syc|ܩܽܘܠܬܳܐ|tr=qulləṯā}}: {{cog|la|culullus|t=wine jug}}, {{cog|grc|κόλλαθον|t=a unit of liquid measure used in Syria}} (also rendered as {{cog|la|collathum}} and reborrowed as {{cog|syc|[[ܩܘܠܐܬܘܢ]] / [[ܩܘܠܬܘܢ]]}}). Also from Semitic: {{cog|grc|γαυλός|t=a kind of round [[vase]] for drinking}} and {{m|grc|γαῦλος|t=a kind of [[Punic]] [[freight]] vessel}}, from which both {{cog|la|gaulus}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|جُلَّة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُلَّة|f|pl=قِلَال}}

# [[jug]], [[jar]], [[pitcher]], [[ewer]] {{q|especially of wine}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|muslim|34|27
|passage=رَأَيْتُنَا نَغْتَرِفُ مِنْ وَقْبِ عَيْنِهِ [ٱلْعَنْبَرِ] بِٱلْقِلَالِ الدُّهْنَ وَنَقْتَطِعُ مِنْهُ الْفِدَرَ كَٱلثَّوْرِ أَوْ كَقَدْرِ الثَّوْرِ
|translation=I saw how we extracted pitcher after pitcher full of fat from the cavity of its [the sperm whale’s] eye, and cut from it pieces of meat resembling a bull or being of the measure of a bull.}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|muslim|36|6
|passage=فَإِنَّ الْخَمْرَ قَدْ حُرِّمَتْ فَقَالَ يَا أَنَسُ أَرِقْ هَذِهِ الْقِلَالَ
|translation=Verily, wine has been forbidden. O Anas, spill these pitchers!}}

