Page 15076 قلعة: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Vršačka kula posle obnove2.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قَلْعَة}}|upright=1.15]]

{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
{{unk|ar}}. Possibilities include:
* From the Arabic root {{ar-root|ق ل ع|nocat=1}}.
* From {{bor|ar|fa|کلات|tr=kalât|t=fortress}}, since a borrowing of this word regularly yields the shape {{m-self|ar||قَلْعَة}}. Akin to {{cog|mzn|کلا|tr=kalâ|t=borough}} and probably {{bor|ar|xcl|քաղաք|t=town}} (under ancient circumstances “fortress, castle” and “town” isn’t necessarily a meaning difference).
* From the name of the {{bor|ar|ms|-}} town below, after its high walls, perhaps supported by how the vocalization varies between {{m-self|ar|قَلْعَة}}, {{m-self|ar|قِلْعَة}} and {{m-self|ar|قَلَعَة}}.
* From {{der|ar|trk-pro|*kiāl-|*kiāl-mak|t=to remain}}. Compare the early Turkic borrowing for a fortification {{m|ar|خَازُوق|t=pale, stake}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|قَلْعَة}}, {{q|less common}} {{ar-IPA|قِلْعَة}}
** {{IPA|acw|[ɡal.ʕa]|[qal.ʕa]|a=Hijazi}}

