* {{l|ar|تَقَمْقَمَ}}

===Etymology 2===
[[File:Flacon van parfum N van Lucien Lelong, Bestanddeelnr 190-0880.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قُمْقُم}}|upright=1.1]]
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|קוּמְקְמָא|tr=qumqəmā|t=cooking vessel; cooling vessel}}, from {{der|ar|arc-imp|𐡒𐡅𐡒𐡌}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒂁𒆪𒆪𒁍|ts=kukkubu, quqquba|t=a smaller container used as an [[alabastron]], [[libation]] jar, or drikining flask; originally a drinking pouch made from an animal's stomach, any similar pouch with a small opening}}, considered possibly a loan or developed from {{der|ar|sux|𒂁𒃻𒋫𒆸|ts=gugguru|t=tall earthen vessel with a narrow opening}}; whence ultimately also {{cog|grc|κούκκουμα}}, diminutive {{m|grc|κουκκούμιον}}, and {{cog|la|cucuma}}, compare {{cog|syc|ܩܘܿܩܡܳܐ|t=pot|tr=qūqəmā}}, absolute state {{m|syc|ܩܘܿܩܽܡ|tr=qūqum}}. The {{cog|fa|قمقمه|tr=qomqome}}, now more popular than the Arabic word, has been borrowed from Aramaic into {{cog|pal||tr=KWKMʾ|sc=Phlv}}. <!-- the Latin must also be edited -->

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|قُمْقُمَة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُمْقُم|m|pl=قَمَاقِم}}

# [[bulbous]] [[flask]] with a [[neck]] used for [[disperse|dispersing]] [[perfume]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُمْقُم|pl=قَمَاقِم}}

