Page 15129 قميص: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ق م ص}}
{{img
|direction=vertical
|image1=White collar blue striped shirt.jpg|caption1=({{senseno|ar|shirt}})
|image2=Indian Muslim.jpg|caption2=({{senseno|ar|garment}})
|image3=A Day in the Life of a Wartime Housewife- Everyday Life in London, England, 1941 D2360.jpg|caption3=({{senseno|ar|garment}})
}}

===Etymology===
{{etymon|ar|id=shirt|bor|unc|la>camisia>shirt}}
Probably from {{bor|ar|la|camisia}}, from {{der|ar|gem-pro|*hamiþiją}}. Compare {{cog|syc|ܩܡܝܨܬܐ|tr=qamīṣtā|t=shirt; undershirt}}.

A minority of scholars think that the Latin word is indeed borrowed from Semitic. The principal witness for this theory is a {{cog|uga|-}} form /qms/, seemingly meaning “garment”. However, this word is not attested in any other old Semitic language.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَمِيص}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-قميص.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَمِيص|m|pl=قُمْصَان|pl2=أَقْمِصَة}}

# {{senseid|ar|shirt}} {{lb|ar|modern}} a [[short]] and [[usual]]ly [[form]]-[[fit]]ting [[upper]]-[[body]] [[outer]] [[garment]]; a [[sleeved]] [[top]]; a [[shirt]] (such as a [[T-shirt]] or a [[dress shirt]])
# {{senseid|ar|garment}} {{lb|ar|archaic}} any [[long]] [[non-]][[bifurcated]] [[sleeved]] [[loose]]-[[fitting]] [[garment]] (such as a [[housecoat]] or a [[nightshirt]]); a [[robe]]
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:السنن
|trans-title=The Traditions
|author={{w|Abu Dawud al-Sijistani|ʾAbū Dawūd}}
|text=
كَانَ أَحَبَّ الثِّيَابِ إِلَى النَّبِيِّ صَلَّى اللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ '''الْقَمِيصُ'''
|t=The most lovely garment to the Prophet—may Allah bless him and grant him peace—was the '''robe'''.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:الجامع الصحيح
|trans-title=The Verifiable Collection
|author={{w|al-Tirmidhi|al-Tirmiḏī}}
|text=
يَا عُثْمَانُ إِنَّهُ لَعَلَّ اللَّهَ يُقَمِّصُكَ '''قَمِيصًا'''، فَإِنْ أَرَادُوكَ عَلَى خَلْعِهِ فَلَا تَخْلَعْهُ لَهُمْ
|t=O ʾUṯmān! It may be that ʾAllāh will [one day] vest you with a '''robe''', and if they ever wish you to take it off, do not take it off for them!}}
#* {{quote-book|ar
|title=ar:السنن الصغرى
|trans-title=The Lesser Collection
|author={{w|al-Nasai|al-Nasāʾī}}
|text=
قَالَ رَسُولُ اللَّهِ صَلَّى اللهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ: «الْإِسْبَالُ فِي الْإِزَارِ، وَ'''الْقَمِيصِ'''، وَالْعِمَامَةِ مَنْ جَرَّ مِنْهَا شَيْئًا خُيَلَاءَ لَا يَنْظُرُ اللَّهُ إِلَيْهِ يَوْمَ الْقِيَامَةِ
|t=''Dangling'' is about lower garments, the '''robe''', and the headdress: whosoever trails along any of these out of self-delusion, ʾAllāh does not look at him on the Day of Resurrection.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَمِيص|pl=قُمْصَان}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|ar|قَمَّصَ|تَقَمَّصَ|قَمِيص نَوْم<t:a sleepshirt>}}

====Descendants====
