Page 15132 قن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Compare the widespread {{bor|ar|arc|ܩܸܢܵܐ}} / {{m|arc|קִנָא}} / {{m|arc|קֵינָא|tr=qennā|t=nest; animal burrow; any cluster; family of an animal}}, {{cog|he|קֵן|tr=qēn|t=nest}}, {{der|ar|akk|qinnum|𒆥𒉡|tr=qinnu|t=nest; lair; family of an animal}}. Since this term is spread chiefly in Asiatic Arabic north of Najd, it is probably a continuation of the Aramaic. It is further connected back to {{der|ar|akk|qanûm|qanû|t=to keep, to buy, to acquire}}, itself with relations to {{der|ar|akk|ganānu|𒂵𒈾𒉡|tr=ganānu|t=to confine, especially a person or living thing}}, and {{der|ar|akk|kanānum|𒅗𒈾𒉡|tr=kanānu|t=to twist or coil, to wrap up an object or possession}}, of {{der|ar|sem-pro|-}} origin denoting concepts of crafting, to acquire or make, building up, to establish or make stay.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُنّ|m|pl=قِنَان}}

# [[coop]] for domestic birds to be [[fatten]]ed, [[pen]] for [[poultry]], [[brood]]ing cage, [[henhouse]], [[pigeon]]’s home and the like
#: {{syn|ar|خُمّ|خُنّ|كِرْس|زَرِيبَة|مَدَجّ}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُنّ|pl=قِنَان}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|كُنّ||Upper Egypt}}

===Etymology 2===
Connected to {{ar-root|ق|ن|ي|}} meaning to acquire or keep; for more see above.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قِنّ|m|g2=f|pl=أَقْنَان|pl2=أَقِنَّة}}

# [[slave]], [[serf]] or a particular kind of slave or serf or enslaved possession, one that is [[kept]] or [[acquire]]d

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قِنّ|pl=أَقْنَان|pl2=أَقِنَّة}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|قُنُونَة}}, {{l|ar|قِنِّيّة|t=such slavehood}}

===Etymology 3===
{{unc|ar}} with multiple correlations suggesting doublets of a similar term. A variation of {{m|ar|قِمَّة}} denoting a heap or pile, to scrape together into a vertex. Alternatively, a variant of {{m|ar|tr=|قِنّ}}, a {{clipping|ar|قِنِّينَة|nocap=1}}; literally a bottle or flask by comparison to its narrowing as it rises. Compare also {{m|ar|قُلَّة}} which may have a similar conception as its source or alternative from its smallness at the tip, its narrowing.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُنّ|m}}

# {{alt form|ar|قُنَّة}}, summit, small mountain

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُنّ}}

