Page 15148 قنبيل: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ar|inc-apa|कमल}}, from {{der|ar|sa|कमल}}. For the consonants underlying the conservative Apabhramsa spelling compare later {{cog|sd|ڪَنَولُ}} / {{m|sd|कंवलु}}, {{cog|pa|ਕੰਵਲ}} / {{m|pa|کَن٘وَل}}, {{cog|omr|𑘎𑘪𑘯}}, {{cog|inc-ohi|कवल}}, {{cog|inc-hnd}} {{m|ur|کَن٘وَل}} / {{m|hi|कँवल}}. Or more directly from {{bor|ar|sa|काम्पिल्ल}}, {{m|sa|काम्पिल्य|t=''Mallotus philippensis''}}. Ultimately a {{der|ar|dra|-}} borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَنْبِيل}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَنْبِيل|m}}

# {{C|ar|Spurges}} [[kamala]] ({{taxfmt|Mallotus philippensis|species}} and by modern extension {{taxfmt|Mallotus|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#* {{RQ:Ibn Janāḥ:2020|page=961|section=824 (fol. 70r,10–11)|passage=قنبيل، قال ابن ماسويه: هي تربة ⟨تشبه⟩ الرمل تعلوها صفرة، من الحاوي.|t=Kamala. Ibn Māsawayh said, as stands in al-Rāzī’s ''Ḥāwī'': It is a dust resembling sand of yellowness upon it.}}
#* {{RQ:Ibn Tilmidh:2007|page=69 Nr. 73|passage=لحب القرع والديدان الكبير<br/>سرخس وبرنج و'''قنبيل''' وتربذ وترمس ومر متساوية الشربة أربعة دراهم بماء حار|t=For (the treatment of ) flukes and large worms<br/>Male fern, embelia, '''kamala''', turpeth, lupine, and myrrh (in) equal (parts). A potion (may be made by using) four dirham (of it) with hot water.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَنْبِيل}}
-------- end text --------
Page 15149 قنة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ق ن ي}} related to acquiring, for the gum acquired. But rather so formed in {{bor|ar|gez|-}} where the same root exists and a broader meaning in {{m|gez|ቀንአት|tr=ḳännəʾät}}, {{m|gez|ቅንአት|tr=ḳənnəʾät}}, {{m|gez|ቀንዓት|tr=ḳännəʿat|t=galbanum; stacta}}, which to derive vice versa from Arabic is formally dubious. Possibly a {{psm|ar|grc|κόμμι|nocap=1}} or in Ethiopia directly its {{der|ar|egy|-}} etymon or the {{der|ar|arc|-}} descendant.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قِنَّة|f}}

# [[any]] {{taxfmt|Ferula|genus}} plant, as well as the [[gum]] of such a plant ([[galbanum]])
#: {{syn|ar|بَارْزَد}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قِنَّة|f}}

====References====
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|page=434a}}, adduces Nöldeke without comment
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|pages=43–44}}, is unsure about the borrowing direction

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{m|ar|قِمَّة}}, {{m|ar|قُلَّة}}, and {{m|ar|قُنّ|t=summit, small mountain}}, and {{cog|ior|ቁኒድ|tr=qunīd|t=top, summit}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|قُنَّة|f|pl=قُنَن|pl2=قِنَان|pl3=قُنُون}}

# [[peak]], [[summit]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُنَّة|pl=قُنَن|pl2=قِنَان|pl3=قُنُون}}

