Page 15162 قنطار: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ق ن ط ر}}
{{was fwotd|ar|2020|April|11}}
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|وحدات القياس المصرية}}
{{wikipedia|Egyptian units of measurement|mul=Syrian units of measurement}}
{{wikipedia|Libyan units of measurement|mul=Tunisian units of measurement}}
{{wikipedia|Algerian units of measurement|mul=Moroccan units of measurement}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|syc|ܩܰܢܛܺܝܪܳܐ|tr=qanṭīrā}}, {{m|syc|ܩܰܢܛܺܝܢܳܪܳܐ|tr=qanṭīnārā}}, from {{der|ar|gkm|κεντηνάριον}}, from {{der|ar|la|centēnārium|t=hundredweight}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قِنْطَار}}
** {{IPA|ary|/qan.tˤaːr/|a=Moroccan}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قِنْطَار|m|pl=قَنَاطِير}}

# [[hundredweight]], [[quintal]], [[kantar]] {{qualifier|a [[weight measure]], usually the largest and dividing to 100 {{l|ar|رَطْل}}}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3:75
|passage=وَمِنْ أَهْلِ ٱلْكِتَابِ مَنْ إِنْ تَأْمَنْهُ بِ'''قِنْطَارٍ''' يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ وَمِنْهُمْ مَنْ إِنْ تَأْمَنْهُ بِدِينَارٍ لَا يُؤَدِّهِ إِلَيْكَ إِلَّا مَا دُمْتَ عَلَيْهِ قَائِمًا
|translation=And among the People of the Scripture is he who, if you entrust him with a '''qintar''', he will return it to you. And among them is he who, if you entrust him with a dinar, he will not return it to you unless you persist confronting him.
|subst=بِ'''قِنْطَارٍ'''/بِ-'''قِنْطَارٍ''',وَمِ/وَ-مِ}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Syria until 1931}}  6000 {{l|ar|وُقِيّة}} – 256.4 {{l|mul|kg}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Saudi-Arabia until 1964}} 150 {{l|ar|رَطْل}} – 67.5 {{l|mul|kg}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Egypt/Sudan until 1891}}  36 {{l|ar|أُقَّة}} – {{frac|133|1|3}} {{l|ar|وِقِيّة}} – 230,400 {{l|ar|قِيرَاط}} – 44.93 {{l|mul|kg}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Libya until 1927}}  40 {{l|ar|أُقَّة}} – 51.28 {{l|mul|kg}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Tunisia until 1895}}  2000 {{l|ar|وُقِيّة}} – 53.9 {{l|mul|kg}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Algeria until 1843}}  2400 {{l|ar|وُقِيّة}} – 81.912 {{l|mul|kg}}
## {{lb|ar|obsolete|Morocco until 1923}}  50.75 {{l|mul|kg}}
# {{lb|ar|figurative}} [[wealth]], great possessions
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3:14
|passage=زُيِّنَ لِلنَّاسِ حُبُّ ٱلشَّهَوَاتِ مِنَ ٱلنِّسَاءِ وَٱلْبَنِينَ وَٱلْ'''قَنَاطِيرِ''' ٱلْمُقَنْطَرَةِ مِنَ ٱلذَّهَبِ وَٱلْفِضَّةِ وَٱلْخَيْلِ ٱلْمُسَوَّمَةِ وَٱلْأَنْعَامِ وَٱلْحَرْثِ ذٰلِكَ مَتَاعُ ٱلْحَيَاةِ ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱللّٰهُ عِنْدَهُ حُسْنُ ٱلْمَآبِ
|translation=Beautified for men is the love of things they covet, women, children, heaped-up '''wealth''' of gold and silver, branded beautiful horses, cattle and cropland. This is the pleasure of the present world’s life, but Allah has the finest return with Him.
|subst=وَٱللّٰهُ/وَ-لّٰهُ,لِلنَّاسِ/لِ-ٱلنَّاسِ,وَٱ/وَ-ٱ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قِنْطَار|pl=قَنَاطِير}}

