Page 15169 قنفذ: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Hedgehog 1210127.jpg|thumb|right|{{l|ar|قُنْفُذ|tr=-}}]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|قُنْفُد}}

===Etymology===
Considering the spirantization of the final consonant, and the occasional variation of the second syllable with [[fatha|fatḥa]], borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|קֻפְדָּא}} / {{m|arc|קוּפְּדָּא|tr=qupdā}} / {{m|syc|ܩܽܘܦܕܳܐ|tr=quppəḏā}}, which in {{cog|myz|-}} is written out {{m|myz|ࡒࡅࡍࡐࡅࡃ|tr=qunpud}}, as also in {{cog|sam|ࠒࠍࠐࠃ}} beside {{m|sam|ࠒࠐࠃ}}, also likely the source of {{cog|he|קיפוד|קִפּוֹד|tr=qippṓḏ}}, all meaning hedgehog. Compare {{cog|ar|خنفساء|خُنْفُس|t=beetle}} as a borrowing with a similar form, where the main Aramaic dialects do not display the {{IPAchar|/n/}} insertion.

Related to meanings of the root {{m|arc|ק־פ־ד}} / {{syc-root|ܩ|ܦ|ܕ}} / {{ar-root|ق ف د}} “to be wrinkled, to be twisted up, to wind, to roll entirely round”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قُنْفُذ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قُنْفُذ|m|pl=قَنَافِذ|f=قُنْفُذَة}}

# [[hedgehog]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قُنْفُذ|pl=قَنَافِذ}}

