Page 15240 قيصر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{bor+|ar|la|Caesar}}, possibly through {{der|ar|grc|Καῖσαρ}} and/or {{der|ar|arc|קיסר|tr=qēsar}}. Uses for modern monarchs are semantic loans from {{der|ar|ru|царь}} and {{der|ar|de|Kaiser}}, themselves from the Latin.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَيْصَر}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|قَيْصَر|m}}

# [[Caesar]] {{gloss|[[Roman]] [[cognomen]], notably that of [[w:Julius Caesar|Gaius Iulius Caesar]]}}
#: {{uxi|ar|يُولْيُوس قَيْصَر|t={{w|Julius Caesar}}}}
# [[Caesar]] {{gloss|an [[epithet]] of Roman emperors, seen as a [[byname]] of the [[incumbent]]}}
#: {{ux|ar|أَعْطُوا مَا لِقَيْصَرَ لِقَيْصَرَ وَمَا لِلّٰهِ لِلّٰهِ.|t=Render unto Caesar that which is Caesar's and unto God that which is God's.}}

