Page 15242 قيصوم: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Achillea millefolium L. (s. str.) (7806922266).jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|قَيْصُوم}}|upright=1.05]]
{{slim-wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Considered a more popular variant of the likely original {{l|ar|قَيْسُوم|tr=|t=various plant types, {{l|en|southernwood}}}}, itself interrelated with the roots {{ar-root|ق|ي|س}} denoting a measure or a piece and {{ar-root|ق|س|م}} a division, compare also the native {{ar-root|ق|و|س}} a bow, a piece of flexible wood. Likely semantically a loan from or conflated with {{der|ar|arc|קיסמא|tr=qismā|t=a chip, a piece of wood, a branch}} and {{der|ar|arc|קיס|tr=qēs|t=wood}}, hence being later applied to various small trees, bushes, and shrubs. Cognates found showing similar semantic senses with {{cog|syc|ܩܝܣܘܢ|tr=qaysōn|t=small piece of wood}} and {{cog|sam|ࠒࠉࠑࠌ|tr=qīṣm|t=wood as a material, pole; used in preference to the typical {{l|he|עֵץ}} in Samaritan scripture}} even being attested with a parallel {{w|Ṣād}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَيْصُوم}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|قَيْصُوم|m}}

# [[yarrow]] (''[[Achillea]]'' gen. et spp.)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|قَيْصُوم}}

{{cln|ar|semantic loans from Aramaic}}
{{C|ar|Anthemideae tribe plants}}
-------- end text --------
Page 15243 قيطون: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed in an urban environment from  {{bor|ar|arc|קִיטֹונָא|tr=qīṭūnā}} / {{m|syc|ܩܱܝܛܘܿܢܳܐ|tr=qayṭōnā|t=bed chamber}}, absolute state {{m|arc|קִיטֹון|tr=qīṭūn}} / {{m|syc|ܩܱܝܛܘܿܢ|tr=qayṭōn}}, from {{der|ar|grc|κοιτών}}. According to Behnstedt and Woidich a genuine formation {{m|ar|قَطَن}} from the root {{ar-root|ق ط ن}} cannot be excluded to partake in some dialectal areas, whereas influence of {{noncog|fr|coton}} in the course of the French building their {{w|French colonial empire|colonial empire}}, though the meaning be in some samples “European-style tent”, is unlikely because of tents of cotton existing before.

===Pronunciation===
* {{q|literary}} {{ar-IPA|قَيْطُون}}
