Page 15245 قيقب: -------- begin text --------
{{multiple images|direction=horizontal|perrow=2|
|image1=Acer trautvetteri 5.jpg
|caption1={{lang|ar|قَيْقَب}} {{taxlink|Acer trautvetteri|species}}
|image2=Lledoner (Celtis australis) de Can Pujol.jpg
|caption2={{lang|ar|قَيْقَب}} ''[[Celtis australis]]''
|image3=Acer trautvetteri 4.jpg
|caption3={{lang|ar|قَيْقَب}} {{taxlink|Acer trautvetteri|species}}
|image4=Aldeaquemada 02.jpg
|caption4={{lang|ar|قَيْقَب}} ''[[Celtis australis]]''
}}
{{swp|lang=ar|قيقب|''Acer'' – قَيْقَب}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|ar}}, from the root {{ar-root|ق|ب|ب}}, meaning “the {{l|en|side}} of an {{l|en|animal}}”, “the {{l|en|belly}} or {{l|en|abdomen}}”, where the {{l|en|saddle}} {{l|en|rests}}; the root suggested by [[w:Edward_William_Lane|Lane]] to ultimately be {{onomatopoeic|ar|nocap=1}} in origin from the sound of a {{l|en|rumbling}} {{l|en|stomach}}. Related to {{ar-root|ق|و|ب|nocat=1}}, meaning “to {{l|en|carve}}, {{l|en|peel}}, or {{l|en|hollow out}} wood”, see {{m|ar|قَبْقَاب}}. Also relation to {{cog|syc|ܩܘܒܬܐ}} originally meaning a vaulted structure, the sense of seat being post-Arabic influence, however suggests a connection perhaps with the vaulted dome or tent like {{m|en|howdah}} design, a woman's enclosed saddle.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|قَيْقَب}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|قَيْقَب|m|sing=قَيْقَبَة}}

# [[maple]] ({{taxfmt|Acer|genus}} spp.)
# {{lb|ar|Al-Andalus}} [[nettle tree]], [[hackberry]] ({{taxfmt|Celtis australis|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|مَيْس|نَشَم أَبْيَض}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|7|38|volume=1|page=333–334|passage=فأما غراسة الميس وهو القيقب وهو ضرب من النشم وإن الذكر هو النشم الأسود وثمره حب صغار سود مدحرجة في داخلها نواة. تؤكل في أكتوبر وفيها بعض الحلاوة وخشبه جيد للسروج ولغير ذلك. وتوافقه المواضع الرطبة وكل الأرض وينجب في كل مكان إلا في الأرض السوداء الحارة.|translation=In what concerns planting of nettle trees it is the hackberry and it is a sort of elm and the male is the black elm and its fruits are small, black, rotund berries with pips in its inner. They are eaten during October and are endowed with sweetness and its wood is good for saddles and other things. Moist spots and every earth is apt for it, and it prospers on every place except on dark, hot earth.}}
#: {{rfquotek|ar|كتاب عمدة الطبيب في معرفة النبات لكل لبيب}}
#: {{rfquotek|ar|Abū al-Ḵayr al-ʾIšbīliyy}}
# [[strawberry tree]] ({{taxfmt|Arbutus unedo|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|قَيْقَبَان|قَطْلَب|جَنَاء أَحْمَر}}
#: {{rfquotek|ar|Ibn al-Bayṭār}}
# [[saddle]]-[[wood]], [[wood]] used for making [[saddles]] or [[frames]]
# [[saddle]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|قَيْقَب}}

===References===
