Page 15303 كأس: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ك ء س}}

===Etymology===
Has been envisioned as from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*kaʔs-}}. The Arabic form could be a hypercorrection after a borrowing from the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} forms listed under it however, since inheritance of {{cog|akk|kāsum|alt=𒃲|tr=kāsum}} from such a proto-form is irregular as one expects vocalism like in {{cog|akk|rēšum|alt=𒊕|tr=rēšum}} from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*raʔš-}}, so also considering the absence in {{cog|sem-eth|-}} one may conclude a post-Proto-Semitic external borrowing.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كَأْس}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-كأس.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَأْس|f|pl=كُؤُوس|pl2=أَكْؤُس|pl3=كِئَاس}}

# a [[glass]], especially a [[wine glass]] or [[arak]] glass
# a [[cup]], [[goblet]], [[tumbler]]
# a cup trophy
#: {{uxi|ar|[[كَأْس العَالَمِ]]|world '''cup'''}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَأْس|f|pl=كُؤُوس|pl2=أَكْؤُس|pl3=كِئَاس}}

====Descendants====
