Page 15324 كاد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
A root {{ar-root|ك و د|nocat=1}} hasn’t developed. The term is suggested as a borrowing from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|𐩫𐩵|t=to almost do|pos={{ar-form|I|nocap=1}}}}, related to {{m|sem-srb|𐩫𐩵|t=to treacherously endanger; to start a prosecution against|pos={{ar-form|II|nocap=1}}}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.II:و.nopass?.noimp.vn:كَوْد,مَكَاد,مَكَادَة}}

# to [[almost]] do something {{qualifier|with following non-past or with {{m|ar|أَن}} + subjunctive}}
#: {{syn|ar|أَوْشَكَ|كَرَبَ|q2=rare}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''كِدْتُ''' أَذْهَبُ|I almost went|inline=t}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|2|20|passage='''يَكَادُ''' ٱلْبَرْقُ يَخْطَفُ أَبْصَارَهُمْ|translation=It is as if the lightning almost snatched away their sight.}}
# to [[hardly]] do something {{qualifier|negated, with following non-past}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|71
|passage=فَذَبَحُوهَا وَمَا '''كَادُوا''' يَفْعَلُونَ
|translation=They slaughtered her, but they hardly brought themselves to do it.}}
# [[as soon as]] {{qualifier|negated, with following non-past}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.II:و.nopass?.noimp.vn:كَوْد,مَكَاد,مَكَادَة}}

=====References=====
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=1126}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=4|page=69a}}
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=2|page=941b}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass|كود|page=900}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|كود|page=991}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ك ي د}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.pass.vn:كَيْد,مَكِيدَة}}

# to [[plot]], to [[scheme]] {{gloss|{{l|ar|لِـ}} against}}
# to [[plan]] or [[intend]] to [[commit]] [[crime]]
# to [[deceive]], to [[fool]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.pass.vn:كَيْد,مَكِيدَة}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=4|page=73b}}
