===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ك ه ل}}, from the root's now-obsolete senses "middle age; adulthood; reliability; backing and support".

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كاهِل|m|pl=كَوَاهِل}}

# {{lb|ar|countable|anatomy}} the [[area]] between the [[shoulder]] [[joint]]s and the [[neck]]; the [[shoulder]]s and the [[upper]] [[back]]; the [[shoulder girdle]]
#: {{syn|ar|كَتِف|ظَهْر|t1=the shoulder|t2=the back}}
## {{lb|ar|countable|by extension}} something [[resemble|resembling]], [[liken]]ed to, or [[relate]]d to the [[shoulder]]s or the [[back]] (such as [[endurance]], [[energy]], [[stamina]], and so on)
## {{lb|ar|countable|by extension}} someone [[resemble|resembling]], [[liken]]ed to, or [[relate]]d to the [[shoulder]]s or the [[back]] (such as a [[friend]], a [[back]]er, a [[sponser]], a [[support]]er, a [[provide]]r, a [[chieftain]], and so on)

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَاهِل|pl=كَوَاهِل}}
