Page 15384 كاهن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-active participle}} of {{m|ar|كَهَنَ|t=to [[predict]] the [[future]]}}, from the root {{ar-root|ك ه ن}}. Compare {{cog|hbo|כוהן|alt=כֹּהֵן|tr=kōhḗn}}, {{cog|uga|𐎋𐎅𐎐}}, {{cog|arc|כָּהֲנָא|tr=kāhănā}} and {{cog|phn|𐤊𐤄𐤍}}, {{cog|gez|ካህን}}, {{cog|syc|ܟܗܢܐ}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَاهِن|m|pl=كَاهِنُونَ|pl2=كُهَّان|pl3=كَهَنَة|f=كَاهِنَة}}

# [[diviner]], [[soothsayer]], [[prognosticator]], [[fortune]]-[[teller]], [[augur]], [[forecaster]]
#: {{synonyms|ar|عَرَّاف}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|69|40-42|passage=إِنَّهُ لَقَوْلُ رَسُولٍ كَرِيمٍ &#1757; وَمَا هُوَ بِقَوْلِ شَاعِرٍ&nbsp;ۚ قَلِيلًا مَّا تُؤْمِنُونَ &#1757; وَلَا بِقَوْلِ '''كَاهِنٍ'''&nbsp;ۚ قَلِيلًا مَّا تَذَكَّرُونَ &#1757;|subst=شَاعِرٍ&nbsp;ۚ/شَاعِرٍ,'''كَاهِنٍ'''&nbsp;ۚ/'''كَاهِنٍ'''|t=40 These are the words of a noble messenger. 41 They are not the sayings of a poet. How little you believe! 42 They are not the sayings of a diviner. How seldom you remember!}}
# {{lb|ar|religion|Christianity}} [[priest]]
#: {{syn|ar|قِسِّيس}}

====Declension====
