===Etymology===
The root {{ar-root|ك ب ب}} appears to include various meanings of “rolling over”. But according to Nişanyan, borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}: compare {{cog|tmr|כבבא|tr=kbbʾ|t=roasting of meat}}, {{m|arc|כיבה|tr=kybʾ|t={{non-gloss definition|perhaps}} roasted meat}}, which are from the verb {{m|arc|כבב|tr=kbb|t=to burn, roast}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|sem-pro|*kabab-|t=to burn, to roast}}, whence also {{cog|akk|𒅗𒁀𒁍|ts=kabābu|t=to burn}}.

===Pronunciation===
