===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ك ب ر}}
{{inh+|ar|sem-pro|*kabar-}} together with {{cog|he|כָּבַר|tr=kāḇár|t=to be great, to become great; to be many, to multiply}}, {{cog|akk|kabārum|t=to be or become thick}} etc.

====Pronunciation====
* {{audio|ar|Ar-كبر.ogg|kabura}}
* {{ar-IPA|كَبُرَ}}
* {{IPA|afb|/ˈkɪbɐr/|a=Gulf Arabic}}
* {{IPA|acw|/ˈkibir/|a=Hijazi Arabic}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/u~u.ipass?.vn:كِبَر,كُبْر,كَبَارَة,كُبَارَة}} {{tlb|ar|stative}}

# to be or become [[big]]
# to [[grow]], to [[grow up]]
# to become [[famous]]
# to become too [[great]] (for something) {{+obj|ar|:عَن}}
# to be [[too]] [[proud]], to [[snub]], to [[disdain]] {{+obj|ar|:عَن}}
# to become too [[oppressive]], to appear [[intolerable]], to become too [[difficult]], to become [[troublesome]] {{+obj|ar|:عَلَى}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|6|35|footer=<small>Translates {{w|Marmaduke Pickthall|Pickthall}}</small>|passage=وَإِن كَانَ '''كَبُرَ''' عَلَيْكَ إِعْرَاضُهُمْ فَإِنِ ٱسْتَطَعْتَ أَن تَبْتَغِيَ نَفَقًا فِي ٱلْأَرْضِ أَوْ سُلَّمًا فِي ٱلسَّمَاءِ فَتَأْتِيَهُم بِآيَةٍ|t=And if their aversion '''is grievous''' unto thee, then, if thou canst, seek a way down into the earth or a ladder unto the sky that thou mayst bring unto them a portent (to convince them all)!}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/u~u.ipass?.vn:كِبَر,كُبْر,كَبَارَة,كُبَارَة}}

