===Etymology 4===
[[File:Capparis spinosa CBMen 06.jpg|thumb|right]]
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|كبر (نبات)}}
From {{der|ar|syc|ܩܦܪ|tr=qappar, qappār|t=caper-bush}} or {{der|ar|syc|ܟܦܪ|tr=kappar, kappār}}, considered from {{der|ar|grc|κάππαρις}} of uncertain likely Asian origin.<br/>For the variation ''a'' ⇌ ''ā'' in Aramaisms, compare {{m|ar|سُكَّر}}, {{m|ar|سُكَّار|t=bolt-lock}} and {{m|ar|قُنْبَر}}, {{m|ar|قُنْبَار}}, {{m|ar|كُنْبَار|t=coir}}.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|كَبَّار|قَبَّار}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كَبَر|m}}

# {{senseid|ar|caper}} [[caper]] {{gloss|{{taxfmt|Capparis|genus}} gen. and especially {{taxfmt|Capparis spinosa|species}}, as well as the edible buds from it}}
#: {{syn|ar|شَفَلَّح|عِتْر|لَصَف}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَبَر}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|axm|կապպար|bor=1}}
* {{desc|gl|alcaparra|bor=1}}
* {{desc|pt|alcaparra|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|es|alcaparra|alcaparro}}

===Etymology 5===
