===Etymology 3===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|כּוֹרָא|tr=kōrā|t=a dry measure}}, {{cog|syc|ܟܘܪܐ|tr=kōrā|t=a dry measure}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒄥|ts=kurru}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒄥|tr=gur|t=a bundle of barley; standard unit of capacity}}. Also found in {{cog|he|כור|כֹּר|tr=kōr}}, and in the meaning of a young donkey in {{cog|sem-saf|𐪋𐪇|ts=korr}} beside two asses pictured.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كُرّ|m|pl=كِرَار}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

