===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|كَرْبَلَا}}

===Etymology===
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}
Etymology {{uncertain|ar|nocap=1}}. Many theories exist, some of which are:<ref name="Al-Milani 2008">{{cite-book|last=al-Qummi|first=Ja'far ibn Qūlawayh|translator=Sayyid Mohsen al-Husaini al-Mīlāni|title=Kāmil al-Ziyārāt|year=2008|publisher=Shiabooks.ca Press|page=545}}</ref><ref>[http://arabic.irib.ir/islamic/show/item/2369 كربلاء]|archive=http://web.archive.org/web/20170204085335/http://arabic.irib.ir/islamic/show/item/2369</ref>
* {{blend|ar|كَرْب|بَلَاء|t1=distress|t2=calamity}}
* {{l|ar|كَرْبَلَة|t=flaccid, loose, soft}}, in reference to its soil.
* {{l|ar|كَرْبَل|t=[[Rumex]] plant}}, due to its existence there
* {{bor|ar|akk|𒆪𒉡𒀭|t=Near God, close to God}} ({{compound|akk|qerēbum|alt1=𒆪𒉡|ilum|alt2=𒀭|tr1=qarābu|tr2=ilu}})
* {{bor|ar|fa|[[کار]] [[بالا]]|t=Deed up risen}}
* {{compound|ar|كُوَر|بابِلِ|t1=Villages|t2=of [[Babylon]]}}, due to its proximity to them.
* {{l|ar|كَرْبَلَ|t=to purify, to clean}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|كَرْبَلَاء|f}}

# [[Karbala]], a city in [[Iraq]], holy to [[Shia]] [[Muslims]] as the site of the martyrdom of [[Wikipedia:Husayn ibn Ali|Husayn ibn Ali]]
#: {{syn|ar|الطَّف|الحائِر|النَّوَاوِيس|الغاضِرِيَّة}}

====Usage notes====
According to al-Afghani, the [[hamza]] at the end was not pronounced at first and was added later.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَرْبَلَاءُ|state=ind-def}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|en|Karbala|Karbala'}}

