Page 15512 كرز: -------- begin text --------
[[File:PikiWiki Israel 17157 Plants of Israel.jpg|thumb|right|{{l|ar|كَرَز|tr=-}}|upright=1.5]]

===Etymology 1===
See {{cog|grc|κερασός}} brought to Greece through an unidentified {{cog|ine-ana}} language; also see {{m|en|cherry}}. {{etystub|ar}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|كَرَز}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|كَرَز|sing=كَرَزَة}}

# [[cherry]], [[cherries]]
#: {{ux|ar|يُمْكِنُكَ صُنْعُ كَعْكَةِ الْكِرَزِ الْلَذِيذَةِ بِاِسْتِخْدَامِ الْكِرَزِ الْطَازِجِ.|You can make a delicious cherry cake using fresh cherries.}}
# [[cherry]] [[tree]](s)

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|كَرَز|sing=كَرَزَة}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ar|قَرَاسِيَا}}, {{l|ar|حَبّ المُلُوك}}, {{l|ar|خَوْخ الْمُلُوك}}

[[File:Michelangelo Cerquozzi - Saint John the Baptist Preaching in the Wilderness.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|يَكْرِزُ يُوحَنَّا فِي الْبَرِّيَّةِ}}|upright=1.95]]

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|كَرَزِيّ|t=cherry-related; of cherry colour}}
* {{l|ar|كُرَيْز|pos=diminutive}}
* {{l|ar|الكرز|t=[[Alcaraz]]}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|כְּרַז}} / {{m|syc|ܟܪܰܙ|tr=kraz|t=to preach}}, from {{der|ar|grc|κηρύσσω|κηρύσσειν|t=to preach}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.vn:كَرْز}}

# {{lb|ar|Christianity}} to [[preach]]
#* Mark 1:4, {{w|lang=en|Bible translations into Arabic|Van Dyck version}}
#*: {{quote|ar|كان يوحنا يعمد في البرية ويكرز بمعمودية التوبة لمغفرة الخطايا.|John baptized in the wilderness, and preached the baptism of repentance for the remission of sins.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.vn:كَرْز}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كَرْز|m|pl=كِرَازَة}}

# [[predication]], [[sermon]], {{ar-verbal noun of|كَرَزَ|form=I}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَرْز|m|pl=كِرَازَة}}

===Etymology 3===
Likely an {{der|ar|ira|-}} loanword together with {{m|ar|خُرْج|t=saddlebag}}, the plural of which is formed like of the present satchel name peculiarly {{m|ar|خِرَجَة}}, parallelled in variation by {{cog|xcl|քուրձ}} and {{m|xcl|խորգ|t=bag, sack}}; compare also {{m|ar|كُرَاز|t=a kind of jug}}, probably via {{bor|ar|arc|-}} as {{m|ar|فِلِزّ}} or {{m|ar|كَنْز}}, attested as {{cog|syc|ܟܘܪܢܐ|tr=kurzā}}, {{m|syc|ܟܘܪܓܐ|tr=kurgā}}, {{m|syc|ܟܘܪܣܐ|tr=kursā}}, {{m|syc|ܟܘܪܣܬܐ|tr=kursəṯā|t=travel bag}}. The name of a young falcon is related to {{cog|fa|کره|tr=korra|t=colt, foal}}, or compare also {{m|ar|زُرَّق|t=white falcon}}, but merged with the satchel name, so that moulting was understood as the falcon being put into the satchel. Bending could be equated with being [[bag]]ged, is however also present in {{ar-root|ك ر س|nocat=1}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كُرْز|m|pl=كِرَزَة}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{C|ar|Bags}} [[satchel]], [[herd]]’s [[sack]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كُرْز|pl=كِرَزَة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كُرَّز|m|pl=كَرَارِزَة}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{C|ar|Falconids|Baby animals}} a [[falcon]] of one or two years in age during [[moult]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كُرَّز|pl=كَرَارِزَة}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.nopass.vn:كُرُوز}} {{tlb|ar|archaic}}

# to [[lean]] [[away]], to [[flee]] by [[shape]], to [[crouch]], to [[bend]] the body to attain a lower position

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.nopass.vn:كُرُوز}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.onlypass}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{lb|ar|passive}} to [[moult]] (of a falcon)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.onlypass}}

