===Etymology===
{{cog|sem|-}} cognates include {{cog|arc|כּוּרְכְּמָא}}, {{m|syc|ܟܽܘܪܟܡܳܐ|tr=kurkmā}}, {{cog|akk|𒌑𒆪𒄀𒆸𒈾|ts=kurkanū}}, {{cog|he|[[כַּרְכֹּם]] / [[כַּרְכֹּום]]|tr=karkom}}; however because of non-philological evidence it is a preferred assumption that the Arabic word comes via India, from {{der|ar|sa|कुङ्कुम}}.

Akin to {{cog|pal|tr=kwlkwm|ts=kurkum|sc=Phlv}}, {{cog|xcl|քրքում}}, {{cog|oge|ქურქუმაჲ}}, {{cog|grc|κρόκος}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كُرْكُم}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كُرْكُم|m}}

# ''[[Curcuma]]'' and especially {{taxfmt|Curcuma longa|species}}, [[turmeric]], [[Indian saffron]]
# [[curcumin]]

