===Etymology===
From an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} cognate of {{cog|syc|ܩܪܟܕܢܐ|tr=qarkeḏnā}}, from {{der|ar|hit}}, like {{cog|he|כַּדְכֹּד|tr=kaḏkoḏ|t=an uncertain gem}}, {{cog|sa|कर्केतन|t={{l|en|chrysoberyl}}}}, {{cog|xcl|կարկեհան|t=a red gem}} (borrowed from {{cog|xpr||*karkaðan}}, to which also belong {{cog|pal||sc=Phlv|tr=karkēhanēn}} (in the {{w|Revayats|Rivāyat}} accompanying the {{w|Dadestan-i Denig|Dādestān ī Dēnīg}}), {{cog|fa|کرکهان|tr=karkahân}}, {{m|fa|کرکهن|tr=karkahan|t=amethyst}} that passed into {{cog|ar|كَرْكُهَان}}, {{doublet|notext=1|ar|كَرْكُهَن|t1=[[amethyst]]}}), {{cog|kho||tr=kirkīyaṃ}}, {{cog|grc|χαλκηδών}}, {{m|grc|χαλχηδόνιος}}, {{m|grc|χαρχηδόνιος}}.

