[[File:Vinyes del Priorat, Gratallops..jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|كَرْم}}|upright=1.75]]

===Etymology 2===
Compare {{cog|uga|𐎋𐎗𐎎|t=vineyard}}, {{cog|arc|כַּרְמָא|tr=karmā|t=vineyard}}, {{cog|he|כֶּרֶם|tr=kérem|t=vineyard}}, {{cog|akk|karānum|𒃾|tr=karānum|t=wine, vine, grapes}}, and the possible etymon {{der|ar|egy|kꜣm}}. Due to the small difference in the third consonant of the Akkadian form, the ''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' suggests a borrowing from a language of Anatolia, the same suspicion as for {{noncog|sem-wes-pro|*wayn-|t=grape}}, and additionally speculates that the homonymic root related to nobleness derived from the name of the vine plant.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|كَرْم|pl=كُرُوم|sing=كَرْمَة}}

# [[vineyard]], [[vine]]s, [[orchard]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|كَرْم|pl=كُرُوم}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|gez|ክርም|bor=1}} <!-- dixit Leslau -->
* {{desc|es|carmen|bor=1}}

