Page 15588 كسر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ك|س|ر}}, related to [[breaking]].

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.pass.vn:كَسْر}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[break]], to [[crash]], to [[smash]]
#: {{usex|ar|كَسَرا هذِهِ الوَصِيَّةَ.}}
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[defeat]], to [[rout]]
# {{lb|ar|transitive|linguistics}} to [[mark]] or [[pronounce]] {{qualifier|a [[consonant]]}} with a [[kasra]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.pass.vn:كَسْر}}

===Etymology 2===
Verbal noun of {{m|ar|كَسَرَ||to [[break]]}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كَسْر|m|pl=كُسُور|pl2=كُسُورَات}}

# {{senseid|ar|verbal noun}} {{ar-verbal noun of|كَسَرَ|form=I}}
# [[breach]], [[fracture]]
# [[breakage]]
# {{lb|ar|arithmetic}} [[fraction]]
# [[contrition]], [[affliction]]
# {{lb|ar|linguistics}} the sound of short {{IPAchar|/i/}}

=====Usage notes=====
According to Wehr, the plural {{m|ar|كُسُورَات}} is used in the sense “fractions”.

