Page 15590 كسر الصفرة: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|كَسَرَ السُفْرَة}}

===Etymology===
{{unc|ar}}. The second word may also be {{m|ar|سُفْرَة|t=leather sheet for transporting food}}. The word {{m|ar|صَفْرَة|t=yellowness}} refers to the [[bile]], bilious taste in the mouth. According to another version (possibly a folk etymology), the word means a mythical snake living in the belly and causing hunger. Lane says it means "hunger", based on the use in this expression.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كَسَرَ الصَفْرَة}}

===Verb===
{{head|ar|verb|I|head=[[كَسَرَ]] ال[[صَفْرَة]]}}

