Page 15593 كسرى: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|fa|خسرو|tr=xosrow}}.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|كِسْرَى|m}}

# [[Khosrow]] (also [[Khosrov]], [[Chosroes]], [[Osroes]]), one of several Persian monarchs

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كِسْرَى|state=ind-def}}

===Etymology 2===
From the name {{m|ar|كِسْرَى}}. Compare the expanded use of {{m|la|Caesar}} to refer to the Roman emperors in general (and the many descendants of the Latin term, including {{m|de|Kaiser}}, {{m|ru|царь}}, and {{m|ar|قَيْصَر}}).

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كِسْرَى|m|pl=أَكَاسِرَة|pl2=أَكَاسِر}}

# ''an epithet applied to [[king]]s of [[Persia]]'', [[Khosrow]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كِسْرَى|pl=أَكَاسِرَة|pl2=أَكَاسِر}}
