Page 15617 كعك: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Derived from or cognate with {{der|ar|arc|כַּעְכָּא}} / {{m|syc|ܟܥܟܐ|tr=kaʿkā|t=cake, loaf}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒈖|tr=kukku|t=cake, loaf, pastry, lump of dough}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|sux|𒈖|tr=gug|t=offering; cake}}. A widespread {{w|wanderwort}} found in many language families, {{cog|egy|ꜥkk}}, {{m|egy|ꜥq|t=a type of loaf}} and {{cog|ine-pro|*gag-}} / {{m|ine-pro|*gōg-|t=round, ball-shaped object; lump; clump}}, likely distant cognate with {{cog|en|cake}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كَعْك}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-كعك.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|كَعْك|sing=كَعْكَة}} {{tlb|ar|collective}}

# [[cake]](s)
# [[biscuits]], [[tarts]], [[buns]], [[twists]]

