===Etymology 2===
From {{bor|ar|arc|כּופְתָּא|tr=kup̄tā|t=(attested as) basket}} or another derivation of the root {{m|arc|כ־פ־ת|tr=k-p-t}} related to twisting, binding, bending, tying over, cognate to {{cog|he|כּוֹפֶשׁ|tr=kōp̄eš|t=basket}} and its root {{m|he|כ־פ־שׁ|tr=k-p-š}}, and to the {{cog|sem|-}}-borrowed {{cog|egy|kbs|ts=*kup̄ṯā|t=basket}}, and probably cognate to the Arabic root {{ar-root|ك ف ت|nocat=1}} above which in place of expected {{m|ar||*ك ف ث|tr=k-f-ṯ}} presumably got dissimilated in the manner of articulation from the second consonant and assimilated to the first for ease of pronunciation, and probably {{cog|gez|ከበሰ|t=to wrap, to tie up or around}} and {{cog|gez|ከብሶ}}, {{m|gez|ክብሶ}}, {{m|gez|ከበሳ|t=headband}} and {{cog|am|ከበሰ|tr=käbbäsä|t=to wrap around}} are also cognate, though Leslau likens them – formally possible – with {{cog|ar|كَبَسَ|t=to press}} in the sense of “to lay siege on, to surround” cognate to {{cog|arc|כ־פ־שׁ|tr=k-b-š|t=to press; to to tread on; to inlay; to overlay}}, but that one sense seems peripheral.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كِفْت|m}}

# {{senseid|ar|cooking_pot}} {{C|ar|Cookware and bakeware}} [[cooking pot]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كِفْت}}

===Etymology 3===
{{nonlemma}}

