{{ar-decl-noun|كَفْر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# {{lb|ar|religion}} to [[expiate]], do [[penance]], [[atone]]
#: {{uxi|ar|كفّر عن ذنوبه|He '''atoned for''' his sins.}}
# to [[forgive]], grant [[pardon]]
# {{lb|ar|religion}} to accuse of infidelity, charge with unbelief
# {{lb|ar|religion}} to make an [[infidel]], seduce to unbelief
# {{lb|ar|dated}} to [[cover]], [[hide]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|כַּפְרָא}} / {{m|syc|ܟܰܦܪܳܐ|tr=kap̄rā|t=village, open town, unfortified town}}, from {{der|ar|akk|kaprum|𒅗𒀊𒊒|tr=kaprum|t=farm, village; a settlement outside of a city}}, considered to represent a word particular to the non-Akkadian “{{w|Mari, Syria|Mari}} language”, that is to be formed either in the unknown {{der|ar|sem-eas}} or the unknown {{der|ar|sem-amo|-}} language spoken there. Probably originally meaning an agricultural storage-room, {{doublet|ar|غَفْر|nocap=1}}, related to the meaning of “covering” connecting the roots {{ar-root|غ ف ر|nocat=1}}, {{m|arc|כ־פ־ר|tr=k-p-r}}. Compare {{cog|he|כְּפָר|tr=kp̄ār|t=[[village]]}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كَفْر|m|pl=كُفُور}}

# [[open]], [[town]], [[village]], [[suburb]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|adab|30|42
|passage=لَا تَسْكُنِ الْكُفُورَ، فَإِنَّ سَاكِنَ الْكُفُورِ كَسَاكِنِ الْقُبُورِ
|translation=Don’t dwell in the suburbs, for he who dwells in the suburbs is like a dweller of the graves.}}

=====Usage notes=====
Not retained anymore except in place-names.

