===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|ar|kmr|gule}} – equalling {{cog|ckb|گولە}}, {{cog|fa|گوله|tr=gôla}}, {{m|fa|کله|tr=kola}}, {{m|fa|گوی|tr=gôy}}, {{m|fa|گلوله|tr=golula}}, {{cog|ur|گولی|tr=golī}} / {{cog|hi|गोली}}, all meaning more or less small balls or bullets, from the tentative {{der|ar|ine-pro|-}} root {{m|ine-pro|*gew-|t=to curve; ball}}. A word omnipresent in Syria except in the Southwest area bordering Lebanon including Damascus where one uses for the sense “marble” {{m|ar|دَحَل}}, {{m|ar|نَحَل}} and also pronounced ''gulle'', ''gull'', ''gill'', ''gille'', ''kille''.

