===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|كَمْ}}

====Adverb====
{{ar-adv|كَمْ}}

# [[how many]]?, [[how much]]? {{gloss|used with accusative noun}}
#: {{usex|ar|'''كَمْ''' كِتَابًا تُرِيدُ أَنْ تَشْتَرِيَ؟|'''How many''' books do you want to buy?}}
# [[how many]]!, [[how much]]! {{gloss|used with {{m|ar|مِنْ}}}}
#: {{usex|ar|'''كَمْ''' مِنْ كُتُبٍ هُنَا!|Oh, '''how many''' books are here!}}

===Etymology 2===
Artificial formation from the word above.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|كَمّ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كَمّ|m}}

# [[quantity]], [[multitude]]
#: {{usex|ar|اَلْعِبْرَةُ بِٱلْكَيْفِ لَا بِٱلْكَمِّ|What matters is quality, not quantity.}}
# {{lb|ar|physics}} [[quantum]]

