Page 15722 كميت: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ك م ت}}

===Etymology===
Apparently {{ar-diminutive|lc=1}} of a {{m|ar||*كَمِيت}} as a passive participle from {{m|ar|كَمَتَ|t=to cover}}, and that an extension of a form from the root {{ar-root|ك م م}} related to “covering, enveloping”, hence something “shaded” in skin-colour.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كُمَيْت}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj|كُمَيْت|cpl=كُمْت}}

# [[dark]] [[bay]] {{gloss|of [[horse]]s, then also [[wine]]}}
#* {{RQ:Sunna|abudawud|15|67|passage=عَلَيْكُمْ بِكُلِّ كُمَيْتٍ أَغَرَّ مُحَجَّلٍ، أَوْ أَشْقَرَ أَغَرَّ مُحَجَّلٍ، أَوْ أَدْهَمَ أَغَرَّ مُحَجَّلٍ|translation=Keep to every dark red horse with white on the face and on the legs, or sorrel with white on the face and on the legs, or black with white on the face and on the legs.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 625|author={{w|Al-A'sha|{{l|ar||اَلأَعْشَى}}}}|title={{lang|ar|أَجَدَّ بَتِيّاً هَجرُها وَشَتاتُها }} (first half line)|url=https://www.aldiwan.net/poem21916.html|passage=كُمَيْتٍ عَلَيْهَا حُمْرَةٌ فَوْقَ كُمْتَةٍ يُكَادُ يُفَرِّي الْمَسْكَ مِنْهَا حَمَاتُهَا|translation=A dark red wine has redness over darkness, it feels hot with touch}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 710|author={{w|Al-Akhtal al-Taghlibi|{{l|ar||الْأَخْطَل}}}}|title=[[wikisource:ar:هل عرفت الديار يابن أويس|{{lang|ar|هَلْ عَرَفْتَ الدّيارَ يابنَ أُوَيْسٍ}}]] (first half line)|passage=علِّلاني بشَرْبَة ٍ مِنْ كَميْتٍ  نعمة ُ النيم في شبا الزَّمهَريرِ|translation=Help me with a drink from a dark red wine a bliss for a frozen man in the break of bitter cold}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{w|Abu Tammam}}|text=أَوْ أَدْهَمٍ فِيهِ كُمْتَةٌ أَمَمٌ   كَأَنَّهُ قِطْعَةٌ مِنَ الغَلَسِ|subst=كَأَنَّهُ/كَأَنَّهُو|title={{lang|ar|قالَت وَعِيُّ النِساءِ كَالخَرَسِ}} (first half line)|url=https://mail.aldiwan.net/poem30489.html|year=a. 850|translation=or a black horse have dark red color, as if it is a piece of the early night.}}

====Declension====
