Page 15735 كنباث: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Equisetum arvense foliage and strobili 1.jpg|thumb|right|{{l|ar|كِنْبَاث الْحُقُول}} – {{taxfmt|Equisetum arvense|species}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
Apparently from {{m|ar|كَنْبَثَ}}, {{m|ar|كَبَّثَ|t=to be drawn together, to be shrunk, to have an inclination in such a fashion that from it things are carried into others}}, while {{m|ar|كَبِثَ|t=to be denatured}}, in relation to its [[strobilus]]. Unrelated to {{cog|sem-nwe|}} {{m|sem-pro|*būṣ-|*biṣbāṣ-, *baṣbāṣ-|t=horsetail}}, but the root reoccurs for Arabic phytonymy in {{m|ar|كَبَاث|t=fruit of the toothbrush-tree}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كِنْبَاث}} or {{ar-IPA|كِمْبَاث}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كِنْبَاث|m}}

# [[horsetail]] ({{taxfmt|Equisetum|genus}} gen. et spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|ذَنَب الْخَيْل}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كِنْبَاث}}

===References===
