Page 15745 كندوج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|pal|tr=kndwg|ts=kandūg}}, whence {{cog|fa|کندو|tr=kandu|t=a large clay-vessel wherein grain can be stored; beehive}}, {{m|fa|کندوج|tr=kanduj|t=id.}}, {{m|fa|کندوک|tr=kanduk|t=capacious jar as for grain}} for the semantic development of which compare {{cog|la|capistērium}}. Cognate to {{cog|xpr||tr=kndwg|sc=Mani|ts=kandūg}}, {{cog|os|хӕндуг}}, {{m|os|хӕндыг|t=fence-structure to dry grain}} and {{cog|syc|ܟܱܢܕܘܩܳܐ|tr=kandūqā|t=large grain-jar}}, {{cog|grc|κόνδυ|t=goblet}}, {{cog|xcl|քանդուկ|t=clayen grain bin}}, {{cog|chg|tr=kündük|t=water-jug}}, {{cog|qwm|tr=kendük|t=flour-jar}}<!--Clauson 729a-->, {{cog|ira|-}} borrowings. Apparently via extension from {{der|ar|akk|kandum|alt=𒃶𒁺|tr=kandu}}, {{der|ar|arc|כַּנְדָּא|tr=kandā}}, {{m|arc|כּדּא|tr=kaddā}}, as also in rare {{m+|ar|كَدّ|id=mortar}}, from {{der|ar|oty|𑀓𑀺𑀡𑁰𑀝𑀺}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كَنْدُوج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَنْدُوج|m|head2=كُنْدُوج|pl=كَنَادِيج}}

# a [[large]] [[vessel]] wherein [[grain]] can be [[store]]d

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَنْدُوج|head2=كُنْدُوج|pl=كَنَادِيج}}

