Page 15755 كنيس: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ك|ن|س}}, meaning to sweep together, to congregate. Compare the {{cog|he|-}} root {{m|he|כ־נ־ס|tr=k-n-s}}, hence {{cog|he|כְּנֶסֶת|tr=k'néset}}. But apparently the Arabic sense of synagogue is a {{sl|ar|arc|כְּנִישְׁתָּא|tr=kənīštā|nocap=1}}, {{m|arc|כְּנִישָׁא|tr=kənīšā}} from the root {{m|arc|כ־נ־שׁ|tr=k-n-š}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَنِيس|m}}

# [[synagogue]]
#: {{syn|ar|بِيعَة|صَلَاة}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَنِيس}}

====See also====
* {{l|ar|كنيسة|tr=kanīsa}} ([[church]])
-------- end text --------
Page 15756 كنيسة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ك|ن|س}}, referring to congregation and sweeping together. Compare the {{cog|he|-}} root {{m|he|כ־נ־ס|tr=k-n-s}}, whence {{cog|he|כְּנֶסֶת|tr=k'néset}}. Apparently, however, the sense of ''synagogue'' is a {{sl|ar|arc|כְּנִישְׁתָּא|tr=kənīštā|nocap=1}}, {{m|arc|כְּנִישָׁא|tr=kənīšā}}, from the root {{m|arc|כ־נ־שׁ|tr=k-n-š}}, to which the Christian sense was added later.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كَنِيسَة}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-كنيسة.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَنِيسَة|f|pl=كَنَائِس}}

# [[church]] {{gloss|building and organization}}
# [[synagogue]] {{gloss|building and organization}}
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} a kind of [[palanquin]] or [[litter]] in which the [[rider]] [[conceal]]s himself
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|instead=1|lang=ar|page=44 line 15}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|instead=1|lang=ar|page=134 line 3}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَنِيسَة|pl=كَنَائِس}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|church, synagogue}} {{l|ar|بِيعَة}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|كَنَسِيّ}}

====Descendants====
{{top2}}
* {{desc|arz|كنيسة|tr=kinīsa}}
* {{desc|mt|knisja}}
* {{desc|ary|كنيسية<tr:knīsiyya>|كنيسة<tr:knīsa>}}
* {{desc|ajp|كنيسة<tr:kanīse>}}
* {{desc|aeb|كنيسية<tr:knīsiyya>}}
* {{desctree|sw|kanisa|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ms|kanisah|bor=1}}
** {{desc|id|kanisah|kenisah}}
{{bottom}}

