===Etymology===
Derived from a variant of the root {{ar-root|ك|ه|ر|ب}} having in the word {{m|ar|كَهْرَبَاء}} originally the meaning “amber” and subsequently meanings related to electricity for the electric attraction properties of amber. Derived from the {{der|ar|fa|کهربا|tr=kahrobâ}}, from {{der|ar|fa|کاه|tr=kâh|t=straw}} + {{m|fa|ربا|tr=robâ|t=magnet}}, ultimately from {{der|ar|pal|khlpʾd|tr=kah-rubāy||amber}}.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَهْرَل|m|pl=كَهَارِل}}

# [[electrolyte]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَهْرَل|pl=كَهَارِل}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|كَهْرَلِيّ}}

