Page 15807 كوج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|zkh|كوچ|tr=küç|t=force, power, work, effort}}, from {{der|ar|trk-cmn|*kǖč|t=force}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كُوج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كُوج|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete|Ilkhanate}}

# [[service]], [[power]] [[offer]]ed, [[corvee]], what a [[vassal]] [[perform]]s
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=1283|chapter=[Ilkhan] {{w|Tekuder|Aḥmad Tegüder}}’s Second Letter to [Sultan] {{w|Al-Mansur Qalawun|Qalāʾūn}}|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=4D9pO_4j9-4C&pg=PA194|page=194|editor=Judith Pfeiffer|title=History and Historiography of Post-Mongol Central Asia and the Middle East. Studies in Honor of John E. Woods|year_published=2006|location=Wiesbaden|publisher=Harrassowitz|isbn=978-3-447-05278-8
|passage=وَيَتَّفِقُ الْجَمِيعُ عَلَى الْقِيَامِ بِوَاجِبِ كُوجِ قَانَ وَخِدْمَتِهِ
|translation=And all agree upon performing work and service for the Khan.
|subst=وَخِدْمَتِهِ/وَ-خِدْمَتِ-هِي,وَيَتَّفِقُ/وَ-يَتَّفِقُ,بِوَاجِبِ/بِ-وَاجِبِ}}

====Declension====
