Page 15809 كودن: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|كَوْدَنِيّ}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|כוֹדְנָא}} / {{m|syc|ܟܽܘܕܢܳܐ|tr=kōḏnā}} / {{m|arc|כוֹדַנֽיָא}} / {{m|syc|ܟܽܘܕܰܢܝܳܐ|tr=kōḏanyā|t=mule}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒀲𒆪𒁷|tr={{sup|ANŠE}}ku-din|ts=kūdunu, kūdanu, kūdannu, kūdinu}}, written many different ways, equated to {{m+|sux|𒀲𒄊𒉣|tr=anše-ĝir₂-nun|ts=anšeĝirnun|t=a type of equid}} which functions as a Sumerogram when spelled with an additional {{m|akk|𒈾|tr=-na}} in the Akkadian orthography. The exact differentiating nature of the multiple terms for donkey remains uncertain; for more see {{cog|fa|کودن}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كَوْدَن}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كَوْدَن|m|pl=كَوَادِن}}

# {{C|ar|Equids}} a [[beast of burden]], particularly a [[mule]] or [[hinny]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 1057|url=https://www.aldiwan.net/poem22453.html|author={{lang|ar|{{w|Al-Ma'arri|أبو العلاء المعري}}}} [ʾabū al-ʿalāʾ al-maʿarrī]|section=line 11|title=ar:خوى دَنُّ شَرب|passage=تَفَرَّعَتِ الْجُرْدَ الْعِرَابَ لِعِزَّةٍ / '''كَوَادِنُ''' بَيْنَ المُقَرِّفَاتِ كَوَادِي}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَوْدَن|pl=كَوَادِن}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|kwdn|N}}
* {{R:syc:Brockelmann:1897|page=659}}
* {{cite-book|last=Diem|first=Werner|title=Studien zur Semitistik und Arabistik: Festschrift für Hartmut Bobzin zum 60. Geburtstag|publisher=Otto Harrassowitz Verlag|year=2008|isbn=978-3-447-05695-3|location=Wiesbaden|page=62 from 57–72|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=7VbJVUle0rsC&pg=PA62&dq=%22kawdan%22|chapter=Schwieriger Verkauf einer Mauleselin}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=109}}
* {{R:sem:Guidi-Sede|page=24}}
* {{R:xcl:Lagarde:1866|pages=54–55 Nr. 142}}
* {{R:sem-pro:SED|volume=2|pages=169–170 No. 124}}, ignoring variants in Akkadian and the revealing variation in the Arabic which makes the long-known borrowed origin clear.
* {{R:ar:Vollers-Beitr.|part=II|page=652 Nr. 287}}, baselessly deriving from {{cog|pal||tr=kōtīna}} (while there is {{cog|fa|کودن|tr=kowdan|t=decrepit beast of burden}}), which Brockelmann corrected for a chain from Akkadian via Aramaic.
* {{R:akk:Zimmern|page=50}}
-------- end text --------
