Page 15812 كور: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
An early Semitic borrowing, ultimately derived from {{der|ar|sux|𒄥|tr=gur|gloss=to twist, to wind, to turn}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[roll]], to [[roll up]], to [[coil]], to [[wind]]
# to make [[round]]
# to [[clench]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

===Etymology 2===
Likely through {{der|ar|arc|-}} from {{der|ar|akk|𒆠𒉈|ts=kuru|t=crucible, kiln, brazier; log, thick reed; short reed mat, collection of reeds}}, likely coined from {{der|ar|sux|𒄥|tr=gur|gloss=a bundle}}, hence a place of burning bundles of firewood or tinder. The sense of a saddle originally stems from a bundle or mat rolled and placed for cushioning; a specified sense natively coined from {{der|ar|akk|𒄀𒆤𒈣|ts=kuru|t=short reed mat, collection or roll of reeds; a woven thing}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒄥|tr=gur|gloss=to twist, to wind, to turn}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كُور|m|pl=أَكْوَار|pl2=أَكْوُر|pl3=كِيرَان}}

# {{C|ar|Horse tack}} [[camel]] [[saddle]]
# [[furnace]], [[smelting]] [[furnace]], [[forge]]
# [[bellows]]
#: {{syn|ar|كِير}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كُور|pl=أَكْوَار|pl2=أَكْوُر|pl3=كِيرَان}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desctree|am|ኮር|bor=1}}
* {{desc|gez|ኮር|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|tig|ኮር|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|ti|ኮር|bor=1}}

===Etymology 3===
{{nonlemma}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun-pl|كُوَر|p}}

# {{plural of|ar|كُرَة|t=ball}}

===Etymology 4===
{{nonlemma}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun-pl|كُوَر|p}}

# {{plural of|ar|كُورَة}}

