Page 15824 كوسا: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Cucurbita pepo zucchina.jpg|thumb|right|{{l|ar|كُوسَا|tr=-}}|upright=1.5]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|ar|كُوسَى|كُوسَة}}

===Etymology===
From an urbaners’ dialect, {{doublet|ar|قُثَّاء|t1={{l|en|Armenian cucumber}}|nocap=1}}.

All plants of {{taxfmt|Cucurbita|genus}} spec., {{m|en|zucchini}} included, are New World plants only introduced to the Old World after the discovery of the Americas; the Arabic term is applied from its similar appearance to its Old World relatives in the genus {{taxfmt|Cucumis|genus}}.

Eilers derives from {{bor|ar|fa|کوسه|tr=kuse|t=man with little or no beard}}, thus literally "hairless smooth fruit". Typologically compare {{noncog|hy|սմբուկ|t=eggplant|lit=smooth one?}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|كُوسَا}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|كُوسَا|f}}

# [[zucchini]], [[courgette]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|كُوسَا}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|aii|ܟܘܼܣܵܐ|bor=1}}

===References===
* {{R:Eilers:1953|page=10, footnote 1}}

===Further reading===
* {{pedia|lang=ar}}

{{C|ar|Gourd family plants|Vegetables}}

