Page 15861 كي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*kiyā}}, a deictic particle, related to {{m|sem-pro|*ka}}.

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|كَيْ}}

# [[in order that]] {{qualifier|followed by the subjunctive}}
#: {{ux|ar|عَلَيْكَ أَنْ تَدْرُسَ '''كَيْ''' تَنْجَحَ.|You have to study '''to''' be successful}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ar|لِكَيْ|tr=li-kay}}
* {{l|ar|لِ|id=conjunction}}

====Preposition====
{{ar-prep|كَيْ}}

# {{tlb|ar|rare}} [[because of]], [[for]]
#: {{ux|ar|كَيْمَ؟|t=Why?|inline=1}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كَيّ|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|كَوَى|form=I|t=to sear; to iron; to sting}}
#* {{RQ:Awwam|33|volume=2|page=601|passage=يؤخذ طرخشقون مجفف وعدس ونورة أجزاء سواء ويسحق الجميع وينخل ويعجن بسمن بقري عتيق ثم يوضع منه على فتيلة ويدخل في الناصور نافع وربما نفع وربما نفع منه ال'''كي''' بالنار.|translation=One takes dried dandelion and lentils and lime at equal parts and grinds all and sieves and kneads with old cow butter and then one applies from it unto a wick and enters the fistula. It may be successful, however '''cauterization''' might prove more effective.}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=ar:{{w|lang=ar|وجدي الأهدل|وَجْدِيّ الْأَهْدَل}}|title=ar:أرض المؤامرات السعيدة|year=2018|isbn=978-614-469-069-7|publisher=Nawfal / Hachette Antoine|location=Bayrūt|page=182|passage=خظر ببالي أن أشكرها على غسلها و'''كيّ'''ها لملابسي،|t=It came to my mind that I thank her for washing and '''ironing''' my clothes.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كَيّ}}

===Etymology 3===
Ultimately {{der|ar|zh|-}} {{zh-l|氣}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كِي|f}}

# {{lb|ar|usually defined}} [[qi]] energy

===Etymology 4===
Compare {{cog|he|כִ֗י|tr=kī}} in {{w|Book of Job|Job 39:27}}, occurring together with {{m|he|נֶשֶׁר|tr=néšer|t=eagle; vulture}} and there sometimes, albeit dubiously, given the meaning “vulture”. {{l|he||אִם־עַל־פִּ֭יךָ יַגְבִּ֣יהַּ נָ֑שֶׁר וְ֝כִ֗י יָרִ֥ים קִנֹּֽו}}: “Is it upon your behest that the eagle and the vulture soars and makes his nest high?” Otherwise it is the well-known emphasizing particle {{m|he|כִּי|tr=kī}}: “Is it upon your behest that the eagle soars, and yea, makes his nest high?”. {{etystub|ar}}
{{rfquote|ar}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|كُي|m}}

# {{tlb|ar|obsolete}} [[ibis]] or [[pelican]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|كُي}}

