Page 15904 ل: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{sense|letter name}} {{ar-IPA|لَام}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/l/|/ɫ/}}

===Etymology 1===
From the {{der|ar|arc-nab|-}} letter {{m|arc-nab|𐢑||tr=l|lamadh}}, derived from the {{der|ar|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤋||tr=l|lāmed}}, from the {{der|ar|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓌅}}. See also {{m+|syc|ܠ|tr=l|t=lāmadh}}, {{m+|he|ל|tr=l|t=lamed}}, {{m+|grc|Λ}}, {{m+|la|L}}.

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|head='''ل '''/''' ل‍ '''/''' ‍ل‍ '''/''' ‍ل'''|tr=lām}}

# The twenty-third letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ك}} and followed by {{l|ar|م}}.

=====See also=====
* {{list:Arabic script letters/ar}}
* [[w:Arabic alphabet|Wikipedia article on the Arabic alphabet]]
* [[Special:Allpages/ل|Search for entries beginning with {{lang|ar|ل}}]]

====Symbol====
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''ل '''/''' ل‍ '''/''' ‍ل‍ '''/''' ‍ل'''|tr=lām}}

# The twelfth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ك}} and followed by {{l|ar|م}}.

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*lV-}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لِـ}}

====Preposition====
{{ar-prep|لِـ}}

# [[to]], [[for]], [[belong]]ing to.

=====Usage notes=====
When {{m|ar|لِـ}} is followed by the definite article {{m|ar|اَلْ|t=the}}, the alif of the article is dropped from the spelling, resulting in the spelling {{lang|ar|لِلْ}}. However, if this would result in three lams in a row, because the first letter following the definite article is also lam, then the lam with sukun is also dropped, resulting in a spelling starting with {{lang|ar|لِلّـ}}, with only two lams; for example, {{m|ar|لِلَّيْلَة|t=for tonight|tr=li-l-layla}}, {{m|ar|لِلّٰهِ|t=to God|tr=li-llāhi}}. The pronunciation is entirely regular in all of these cases.

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|1s=[[لِي]] / [[لِيَ]]|لِـ||لَ}}

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|لِمَا|t=for what}}
* {{l|ar|لِمَاذَا|t=why}}
* {{l|ar|لِمَ|t=why}}
* {{l|ar|لِمَنْ|t=whose}}
* {{l|ar|لِأَنَّ|t=because}}
* {{l|ar|لِأَنْ|t=for that}}
* {{l|ar|مَالِ}}

=====Descendants=====
{{q|via third-person singular masculine form {{m|ar|لَهُ}}}}:
* {{desc|az|ləh|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|له|tr=lah|bor=1}}

====Preposition====
{{ar-prep|لَـ}}

# {{non-gloss|Used to express admiration}}
#: {{usex|ar|يَا '''لَ'''لْعَجَبِ!|How wonderful!|subst='''لَ'''لْعَجَبِ//'''لَ-'''ٱلْعَجَبِ}}
#: {{ux|ar|يَا '''لَهُ''' مِنْ عَالَمٍ رَائِعٍ!|What a wonderful world!}}
# {{non-gloss|Used to call for help}}
#: {{ux|ar|يَا '''لَ'''لْأُمِّ لِلْأَطْفَالِ!|Oh '''for''' mother to the children! (Oh mother, help your children!)}}

=====Usage notes=====
It is often used in the form {{lang|ar|يَا لَهُ [مِنْ] ...}}, that is, {{lang|ar|يَا لَـ}} followed by an enclitic pronoun that does not refer to any previous noun. Rather the pronoun refers to what follows it, with an optional {{lang|ar|[[من|مِنْ]]}} in the middle.<ref>{{cite-book|fr|last=de Sacy|first=Silvestre|authorlink=Antoine Isaac Silvestre de Sacy|title=Grammaire arabe|url=https://archive.org/details/in.ernet.dli.2015.361611|year=1831|volume=1|pages=475-476}}</ref>

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|1s=[[لِي]] / [[لِيَ]]|لَـ||لَ}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|لِـ}}

# {{senseid|ar|conjunction}} [[to]], [[in order to]]: {{n-g|followed by the [[subjunctive mood]]}}
#: {{ux|ar|دَخَلْتُ ٱلْمَطْبَخَ '''لِ'''أَشْرَبَ مَاءً.|subst='''لِ'''/'''لِ-'''|t=I entered the kitchen '''to''' drink water.}}
# {{n-g|used with the verbs {{m|ar|أَرَادَ}} and {{m|ar|أَمَرَ}}}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|33|33
|passage=إِنَّمَا يُرِيدُ اللّٰهُ لِيُذُهِبَ عَنْكُمُ الرِّجْسَ}}
# [[only to]] ({{l|ar|لَامُ الْعَاقِبَة}})
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|28|8
|passage=فَالْتَقَطَهُ آلُ فِرْعَوْنَ لِيَكُونَ لَهُمْ عَدُوًّا وَحَزَنًا
|translation=And so the family of the Pharaoh picked him up, '''only to''' become an enemy and a grief.
|transliteration=fāltaqaṭahu ʾālu firʿawna '''li'''-yakūna lahum ʿaduwwan wa-ḥazanan
}}

=====Synonyms=====
* {{l|ar|لِأَنْ}}

===Etymology 3===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لِـ}}
* {{qualifier|after {{m|ar|وَ}} or {{m|ar|فَـ}}}} {{ar-IPA|لْ}}

====Particle====
{{head|ar|particle|head=لِـ}}

# {{non-gloss|Used to introduce an imperative with a jussive verb}}; [[let]]
#* {{quote-book|1=ar|year=9th century|author=Muslim ibn Al-Hajjaj|chapter=كتاب الحج|editor=|editors=|title=Sahih Muslim|url=|archiveurl=|archivedate=|edition=|location=|publisher=|date=|isbn=|oclc=|volume=|section=|sectionurl=|page=|pages=|quotee=Muhammad|pageurl=|text=لِتَأْخُذُوا مَنَاسِكَكُمْ فَإِنِّي لَا أَدْرِي لَعَلِّي لَا أَحُجُّ بَعْدَ حَجَّتِي هَذِهِ|t=|tr=}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|18|29
|passage=وَقُلِ ٱلْحَقُّ مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ فَمَنْ شَاءَ فَلْيُؤْمِنْ وَمَنْ شَاءَ فَلْيَكْفُرْ
|translation=And say, "The truth is from your Lord, so whoever wills, let him believe; and whoever wills, let him disbelieve."}}

