Page 15949 لا إله إلا الله محمد رسول الله: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|لَا إِلَاهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّاهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ ٱللَّاهِ}}
* {{audio|ar|Shahadah.ogg|text=أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّٰهُ مُحَمَّدٌ رَسُولُ ٱللَّٰهِ}}

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=[[لَا]] [[إِلَٰهَ]] [[إِلَّا]] [[ٱللَّٰهُ]] [[مُحَمَّدٌ]] [[رَسُولُ]] [[ٱللَّٰهِ]]}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} There is no [[deity]] but [[God]]; [[Muhammad]] is the [[messenger]] of God.

====Usage notes====
* This phrase, called the [[shahada]], {{m|ar|شَهَادَة}}, or [[shahadatayn]], {{m|ar|شَهَادَتَيْنِ}}, or Muslim creed, is the declaration of belief in the oneness of God and in [[Muhammad]] as His messenger. Recitation of the shahada is considered one of the [[five pillars]] of Islam by [[Sunni]] Muslims. By sincerely stating the shahada aloud before two witnesses, one is considered to have converted to Islam.
* In addition to excluding the other messengers of God, the second part of the shahada is viewed by [[Quranist]]s as unnecessary {{m|en|shirk}}, and they may instead substitute the following: {{m|ar||وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ}}.

====See also====
* {{l|ar|شَهَادَة}}
* {{l|ar|أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَا إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّٰهُ}}
* {{l|ar|أَشْهَدُ أَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا رَسُولُ ٱللَّٰهِ}}

===References===
* {{pedia|Shahadah}}

[[Category:Arabic phrasebook]]
-------- end text --------
Page 15950 لا بأس: -------- begin text --------

===Adverb===
{{ar-adv|لَا بَأْسَ}}

# {{lb|ar|with {{m|ar|بِ}}}} it is not a [[problem]], it is [[all right]], it can't [[hurt]]
#: {{ux|ar|لَا بَأْسَ بِبَعْضِ ٱلضَّحِكِ أَحْيَانًا.|t=It can’t hurt to laugh sometimes.}}
# {{lb|ar|with {{m|ar|بِ|tr=-}} + personal suffix}} a rather [[large]] (number of), [[quite a few]]
#: {{ux|ar|عَدَدٌ لَا بَأْسَ بِهِ مِنَ ٱلنَّاسِ يُعَانُونَ مِنْ مَشَاكِلَ نَفْسِيَّةٍ.|t=Quite a large number of people suffer from psychological problems.}}

===Interjection===
{{head|ar|interjection|head=لَا بَأْسَ}}

# [[no problem]]
#: {{ux|ar|هَل يُمْكِنُنِي ٱلتَّدْخِينُ؟ – لَا بَأْسَ.|May I smoke? – No problem.}}
# {{lb|ar|perhaps|_|regional}} {{ngd|Used as a wish for health and well-being.}}
#: {{ux|ar|لَا بَأْسَ عَلَيْكُمْ!|All the best to you!}}
-------- end text --------
Page 15951 لا تجعل الحبة قبة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Literally "do not make a [[grain]] into a [[dome]]", each being a metaphor for something small and something large, respectively.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|لَا تَجْعَلِ الحَبّةَ قُبّة}}

===Proverb===
{{head|ar|proverb|head=لَا تَجْعَلِ الحَبّةَ قُبّة}}

# one should not exaggerate or [[make a scene]] of trivial matters.
# one should not allow minor problems or disagreements to [[snowball]].
-------- end text --------
Page 15952 لا جرم: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Probably {{compound|ar|لَا|جُرْم}} with the last in an obsolete vocalization (not usual already in the 7<sup>th</sup> century {{CE}}) originally implying “it is no wrong [scilicet to claim]”.

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=[[لَا]] [[جرم|جَرَمَ]]}}

# [[certainly]], [[surely]], [[no doubt]], [[undoubtedly]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|16:23
|passage='''لَا جَرَمَ''' أَنَّ اللَّهَ يَعْلَمُ مَا يُسِرُّونَ وَمَا يُعْلِنُونَ ۚ إِنَّهُ لَا يُحِبُّ الْمُسْتَكْبِرِينَ
|translation='''No doubt''' that God knows what they hide and what they show, he indeed does not like the arrogant.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|16:62
|passage=وَيَجْعَلُونَ لِلَّهِ مَا يَكْرَهُونَ وَتَصِفُ أَلْسِنَتُهُمُ الْكَذِبَ أَنَّ لَهُمُ الْحُسْنَىٰ ۖ '''لَا جَرَمَ''' أَنَّ لَهُمُ النَّارَ وَأَنَّهُم مُّفْرَطُونَ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|40:43
|passage='''لا جَرَمَ''' أَنَّمَا تَدْعُونَنِي إِلَيْهِ لَيْسَ لَهُ دَعْوَةٌ فِي الدُّنْيَا وَلا فِي الآخِرَةِ وَأَنَّ مَرَدَّنَا إِلَى اللَّهِ وَأَنَّ الْمُسْرِفِينَ هُمْ أَصْحَابُ النَّارِ}}
-------- end text --------
