Page 15996 لاط: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|لَاطَ}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ل و ط}}
The sense of "anal sex" derives directly from {{m|ar|لُوط|t=Lot}}, with the meaning of "to do as Lot's people did", and was subsequently leveled to the root by analogy. For formation, compare {{noncog|en|sodomize}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:لَوْط}}

# {{lb|ar|intransitive|obsolete}} to [[stick]], to [[adhere]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<to/in something>}}
#: {{syn|ar|لَصَقَ}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive|obsolete}} to [[stick]], to [[adhere]] {{+obj|ar|acc<something> + :بِ<to something>}}
## {{lb|ar|transitive|obsolete}} to [[plaster]] (a wall)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:لَوْط}}

===Etymology 2===
The sense of "anal sex" derives directly from {{m|ar|لُوط|t=Lot}}, with the meaning of "to do as Lot's people did", and was subsequently leveled to the root by analogy. For formation, compare {{noncog|en|sodomize}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.ipass.vn:لَوْط,لِوَاط}}

# {{lb|ar|intransitive|Islam|derogatory|dated}} to have [[anal]] [[sex]] {{+obj|ar|:بِ<with a man>}}, to [[sodomize]]
#: {{hyper|ar|بَاشَر|نَاكَ|q1=largely euphemistic, archaic|q2=vulgar}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.ipass.vn:لَوْط,لِوَاط}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Because the verb derives from the name of the Islamic figure himself (unlike {{noncog|en|sodomize}}, which derives from the biblical name of the city), some have come to scruple about or even vehemently denounce the use of words thus derived to refer to homosexual intercourse, instead favoring euphemistic terms and expressions.
* All the other uses of the verb are completely obsolete, as the form has come to be associated solely with sodomy.
-------- end text --------
