Page 16039 لبلابي: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}
[[File:Lablabi photo 7 لبلابي.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|لَبْلَابِيّ}}|upright=1.15]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|لَبْلَبِيّ}}

===Etymology===
{{ar-etym-nisba|لَبْلَاب}}, that noun originally meaning [[ivy]] and then also the similarly looking [[hyacinth bean]]; perhaps by the vulgar further related to {{m|ar|لُوبِيَا}} meaning the [[cowpea]] of the same botanical tribe ({{taxfmt|Phaseoleae|tribe}}) and beans in general, and thus connected to the [[chickpea]], another [[faboid]]; the element also being found in {{m|ar|جُلُبَّان|t=[[grass pea|grasspea]]}}, another [[faboid]]; and for the word denoting a stew, influenced by {{m|ar|لُبَاب|t=pulp}} and {{m|ar|لُبّ|t=pulp}}, from which even the learned {{w|Sevan Nişanyan|Nişanyan}}<ref>{{R:tr:Nishanyan|leblebi|accessdate=2019-12-24}}</ref> wrongly derived {{m|ar|لَبْلَاب}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|لَبْلَابِيّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|لَبْلَابِيّ|m}}

# [[chickpea]]-[[stew]]

