Page 16088 لحم: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ل ح م}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*laḥm-|t=food, eatables; meat, bread}}, from {{inh|ar|afa-pro|*laḥam-||food}}. Cognate with {{cog|arc|לַחְמָא|tr=laḥmā}}, {{cog|syc|ܠܚܡܐ|tr=laḥmā}}, {{cog|he|לֶחֶם|tr=léḥem|t=[[bread]]}}, {{cog|uga|𐎍𐎈𐎎|ts=laḥmu}}, {{cog|gez|ላህም}}, all meaning “food” or “bread”. The varying semantic developments are due to the differing agriculture and diets of the {{w|Arabian Peninsula}} and the {{w|Fertile Crescent}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لَحْم}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-لحم.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|لَحْم|m|pl=لُحُوم|pl2=لِحَام|pl3=لِحْمَان|pl4=لُحْمَان|pl5=أَلْحُم}}

# [[flesh]], [[meat]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|لَحْم|pl=لُحُوم|pl2=لِحَام|pl3=لِحْمَان|pl4=لُحْمَان|pl5=أَلْحُم}}

