Page 16146 لعل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{univerbation|ar}} of {{m|ar|لَـ|t=[[truly]], [[indeed]], [[verily]]}} and {{m|ar|عَلَّ}}.
{{etymid|ar|particle}}

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لَعَلَّ}}

====Particle====
{{ar-particle|لَعَلَّ}}

# [[hopefully]]
# [[in order]], [[so that]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=|title=''The Quran''|edition=|year=7th century {{CE}}|url=https://ar.wikisource.org/wiki/القرآن_الكريم/سورة_البقرة|passage={{lang|ar|ثُمَّ بَعَثْنَاكُم مِن بَعْدِ مَوْتِكُمْ '''لَعَلَّكُمْ''' تَشْكُرُونَ}}|transliteration={{xlit|ar|ثُمَّ بَعَثْنَاكُم مِن بَعْدِ مَوْتِكُمْ '''لَعَلَّكُمْ''' تَشْكُرُونَ}}|translation=But We raised you again after you had been as dead, '''so that you''' might have cause to be grateful.}}
# [[perhaps]], [[maybe]]

=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|ar|لَعَلَّ}} functions like {{m|ar|إِنَّ}} and {{m|ar|أَنَّ}}, shifting the subject of the clause to the accusative case. The subject of the clause must immediately follow {{m|ar|لَعَلَّ}}; if it is a pronoun, it must be expressed.
* Unlike {{m|ar|لِ}}, {{m|ar|لِكَي}}, and {{m|ar|حَتَّى}}, {{m|ar|لَعَلَّ}} places its subordinate verb in the [[indicative]] mood, even when used to mean "[[in order]]," "[[so that]]."

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|لَعَلَّ}}

=====Alternative forms=====
* {{alter|ar|عَلَّ|لَعَاءَ}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:ʾinna and her sisters/ar}}

