Page 16200 لكن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{uncertain|ar}}. Bravmann proposes an origin in {{m|ar|[[إِلَّا]] [[كَانَ]]|t=except that [it/he] were}}, but does not provide a convincing explanation for the contraction of the ''ā'' or for the suspicious similarity to {{m|ar|أَنْ}} and {{m|ar|أَنَّ}} in the alternation of the ending.<ref>{{cite-book|last=Bravmann|first=Meïr Max|series=Studies in Semitic Languages and Linguistics|seriesvolume=VI|title=Studies in Semitic Philology|year=1977|publisher=E. J. Brill|location=Leiden|chapter=Arabic ''lākin(na)'' and Related Expressions|pages=338–342}}</ref>

===Etymology 1.1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لٰكِنَّ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-لكن.ogg}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|لٰكِنَّ}}

# [[but]], [[however]]

=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|ar|لٰكِنَّ}} functions like {{m|ar|إِنَّ}} and {{m|ar|أَنَّ}}, shifting the subject of the subordinate clause to the accusative case. The subject of the subordinate clause must immediately follow {{m|ar|لٰكِنَّ}}; if it is a pronoun, it must be expressed. Contrast this syntactic function and the following examples with {{m|ar|لٰكِنْ}} below.
*: {{ux|ar|'''لٰكِنَّ الرَّئِيسَ''' كَانَ أَذْكَى مِمَّا تَوَقَّعَ النَّاس|t='''but the president''' was smarter than people expected}}
*: {{ux|ar|'''لٰكِنَّهُ''' كَانَ أَذْكَى مِمَّا تَوَقَّعَ النَّاس|t='''but he''' was smarter than people expected}}

=====Inflection=====
{{ar-prep-auto|لٰكِنَّ|1s=لٰكِنَّنِي|1s2=لٰكِنِّي}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:ʾinna and her sisters/ar}}

===Etymology 1.2===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لٰكِنْ}}

====Conjunction====
{{ar-con|لٰكِنْ}}

# [[but]], [[however]]
# [[but]], [[rather]]
#: {{synonyms|ar|بَلْ}}
#: {{usex|ar|لَمْ يُسَافِرِ الطُّلَابُ '''لٰكِنْ''' وَكِيلُهُمْ|The students didn’t travel '''but''' their principal did.}}
# [[but]] [[not]], after an [[affirmative]].

=====Usage notes=====
* {{m|ar|لٰكِنْ}} acts as a simple conjunction, with the subject of the subordinate clause in the nominative; the subject may follow immediately or be delayed. If it is a pronoun, it may be omitted. Contrast this syntactic function and the following examples with {{m|ar|لٰكِنَّ}} above.
*: {{ux|ar|'''لٰكِنِ الرَّئِيسُ''' كَانَ أَذْكَى مِمَّا تَوَقَّعَ النَّاس|t='''but the president''' was smarter than people expected}}
*: {{ux|ar|'''لٰكِنْ (هُوَ)''' كَانَ أَذْكَى مِمَّا تَوَقَّعَ النَّاس|t='''but he''' was smarter than people expected}}
* {{m|ar|لٰكِنْ}} is often preceded by {{m|ar|وَـ|gloss=[[and]]}}.

=====Derived terms=====
* {{l|ar|وَلٰكِن}}

=====Descendants=====
{{top2}}
* {{desc|ajp|لاكن|tr=lāken}}
* {{desctree|fa-cls|لیکِن|bor=1|لَٰکِن|لَاکِن|noalts=1}}
* {{desc|sw|lakini|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ota|لكن|tr=lakin|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|lakin}}
{{bottom}}

