Page 16243 لو: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Compare {{cog|he|לוּ|tr=lū}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|لَوْ}}

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|لَوْ}}

# [[if]] {{lb|ar|contrary to fact}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|21|22
|passage='''لَوْ''' كَانَ فِيهِمَا آلِهَةٌ إِلَّا ٱللّٰهُ لَفَسَدَتَا
|translation='''Had''' there been within the heavens and earth gods besides Allah, they both would have been ruined.
|subst=لَفَسَدَتَا/لَ-فَسَدَتَا}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|100
|passage=أَوَلَمْ يَهْدِ لِلَّذِينَ يَرِثُونَ ٱلْأَرْضَ مِن بَعْدِ أَهْلِهَا أَن '''لَّوْ''' نَشَاءُ أَصَبْنَاهُم بِذُنُوبِهِمْ وَنَطْبَعُ عَلَى قُلُوبِهِمْ فَهُمْ لَا يَسْمَعُونَ
|translation=Has it not become clear to those who inherited the earth after its [previous] people that '''if''' We willed, We could afflict them for their sins? But We seal over their hearts so they do not hear.
|subst=لِلَّذِينَ/لِ-لَّذِينَ,بِذُنُوبِهِمْ/بِ-ذُنُوبِهِمْ,وَنَطْبَعُ/وَ-نَطْبَعُ}}
# [[that]] {{qualifier|often used with the verb {{m|ar|وَدَّ}}}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|70|11
|passage=يَوَدُّ الْمُجْرِمُ '''لَوْ''' يَفْتَدِي مِنْ عَذَابِ يَوْمِئِذٍ بِبَنِيهِ
|translation=The criminal will wish '''that''' he could be ransomed from the punishment of that Day by his children.
|subst=بِبَنِيهِ/بِ-بَنِيهِ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|15|2
|passage=رُبَمَا '''يَوَدُّ''' الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا '''لَوْ''' كَانُوا مُسْلِمِينَ
|translation=Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish '''that''' they had been Muslims.}}
# [[if only]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|167
|passage=وَقَالَ ٱلَّذِينَ ٱتَّبَعُوا '''لَوْ''' أَنَّ لَنَا كَرَّةً فَنَتَبَرَّأَ مِنْهُمْ كَمَا تَبَرَّؤُوا مِنَّا
|translation=Those who followed will say, "'''If only''' we had another turn [at worldly life] so we could disassociate ourselves from them as they have disassociated themselves from us."
|subst=وَقَالَ/وَ-قَالَ,فَنَتَبَرَّأَ/فَ-نَتَبَرَّأَ}}

====Usage notes====
* Normally used for conditions that are contrary-to-fact (unlikely to be fulfilled or incapable of being fulfilled). For possible (not contrary-to-fact) conditions, use {{m|ar|إِنْ}}.
* Used with the past tense or the present tense, in both cases with a present-tense meaning (although normally translated in English with a past tense).

====Antonyms====
* {{l|ar|لَوْلَا}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|afb|لو|tr=law}}
* {{desc|ajp|لو|tr=law}}

-------- end text --------
