Page 16273 لولا: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{af|ar|لَوْ|لَا}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|لَوْلَا}}

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|لَوْلَا}}

# [[if not for]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|34|31|passage='''لَوۡلَاۤ''' أَنتُمۡ لَكُنَّا مُؤۡمِنِينَ|subst='''لَوۡلَاۤ''' أَنتُمۡ لَكُنَّا مُؤۡمِنِينَ/'''لَوْلَا''' أَنْتُمْ لَكُنَّا مُؤْمِنِينَ|translation=If it weren't for you, we would have been believers}}

====Usage notes====
It is followed by a noun in the nominative case or a verb in the past tense. Pronouns can be either in nominative or genitive case:
* {{ux|ar|'''لَوْلَا''' ٱلنِّيلُ لَأَصْبَحَتْ  مِصْرُ صَحْرَاءَ|t='''If it weren't for''' Nile, Egypt would be a desert.}}
* {{ux|ar|'''لَوْلَا''' أَنَا / '''لَوْلَا'''يَ|t='''if not for''' me}}

-------- end text --------
