Page 16301 ليس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{uncertain|ar}}. Traditionally taken to be a contracted pronunciation of either an earlier form {{m-self|ar|لَيِسَ}}, whose ultimate origin is in turn unknown or unexplored, or of {{m|ar|لَا|t=not}} + an existential {{m|ar|أَيْس}}<ref>{{R:ar:Lane|entry=ليس|pages=1625-1627}}</ref> that has a proposed etymology in {{inh|ar|sem-pro|[[*ys]] < [[*yṯ]]}}. This existential would be a native cognate to {{cog|he|יֵשׁ|tr=yēš}}<ref>David Wilmsen (2016), page 330, ''[https://www.academia.edu/32873897/Another_Croft_cycle_in_Arabic_The_laysa_negative_existential_cycle Another Croft cycle in Arabic: The laysa negative existential cycle.]'' Advance online publication.</ref> and {{cog|akk|𒌇|ts=išu|t=to have or own; to be|pos=also used copulatively}}, although Al-Jallad (2018) expresses doubt that it is anything more than a back-formation from the negative, in other words implying that {{m|ar|لَا|t=not}} + {{m|ar|أيس|*أَيْس|pos=existential}} is just a folk etymology from which {{m|ar|أَيْس}} was created artificially. Al-Jallad proceeds to attest a form of {{m-self|ar|لَيْسَ}} in a {{w|Safaitic}} inscription dated between the first century BC and the fourth century AD, whose form, he says, invalidates the possibility of an origin in a verb {{m-self|ar|لَيِسَ}}; he thereby argues that {{m-self|ar|لَيْسَ}} may either be a loan from {{bor|ar|akk-nas|𒆷𒀸𒋗|tr=la-aš-šu|ts=laššu|t=there is not}} or from {{bor|ar|sem-tay|𐪁𐪚𐪏|tr=lys<sup>3</sup>|ts=lāʾis, lāyis|t=not existing or being}}.<ref>Ahmad Al-Jallad (2018), ''[https://www.academia.edu/34326445/Al-Jallad._2018._The_earliest_attestation_of_laysa_and_the_implications_for_its_etymology The earliest attestation of laysa and the implications for its etymology]''. Advance online publication.</ref>

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|لَيْسَ}}

====Verb====
{{head|ar|verb|head=لَيْسَ}}

# {{lb|ar|copulative|defective}} not to [[be]]
# {{lb|ar|invariably masculine singular}} [[except]]
#: {{synonyms|ar|لَا يَكُونُ}}
#: {{usex|ar|جَاءَ النَّاسُ لَيْسَ زُهَيْرًا|People came, except for Zuhayr}}
# not to [[exist]]; [[there is]] not
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|7|61
|passage=قَالَ يَٰقَوۡمِ '''لَيۡسَ''' بِي ضَلَٰلَةٞ وَلَٰكِنِّي رَسُولٞ مِّن رَّبِّ ٱلۡعَٰلَمِينَ
|translation=He said, “O my people, '''there is not''' error in me, but I am a messenger from the Lord of the worlds.”}}

=====Usage notes=====
This is a [[defective]] verb. It has only perfect indicative forms with a present-tense meaning. If there is a {{w|subject complement}}, it comes up in the accusative or (with {{m|ar|بِـ}}) the genitive.
: {{uxi|ar|لَسْتُ [[عالم|عَالِمًا]]|t=I am not learned|inline=1}}
: {{uxi|ar|لَسْتُ [[عالم|بِعَالِمٍ]]|tr=lastu bi-ʕālimin|t=I am not learned|inline=1}}
: {{uxi|ar|لَيْسَ الرَّجُلُ جَمِيلًا|t=That man is not handsome.}}

=====Conjugation=====
* Before consonantal endings, the diphthong ''-ay-'' is reduced to a short ''-a-'':
{| class="wikitable" style="text-align: center;"
!
! [[singular]]
! [[dual]]
! [[plural]]
|-
! [[first person|1st person]]
| {{m|ar|لَسْتُ}}
| colspan="2"| {{m|ar|لَسْنَا}}
|-
! [[second person|2nd person m]]
| {{m|ar|لَسْتَ}}
| rowspan="2"| {{m|ar|لَسْتُمَا}}
| {{m|ar|لَسْتُمْ}}
|-
! [[second person|2nd person f]]
| {{m|ar|لَسْتِ}}
| {{m|ar|لَسْتُنَّ}}
|-
! [[third person|3rd person m]]
