Page 16303 ليف: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|ليف (نبات)|Luffa}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|لُوف}}

===Etymology===
From the root {{ar-root|ل|ف|ف}} meaning “to fold up or roll up in”, “to wrap or envelop”, “an envelope of a plant, a [[pericarp]] or [[glume]]”.

Also suspicious of {{bor|ar|arc|-}} substrate however, as {{cog|syc|ܠܘܦܐ|tr=lawpā, lūpā}} means “[[parietary]]” and “[[arum]]” or “{{vern|edder-wort|nopedia=1}}”, deriving well from {{m|syc|ܠܴܦ|tr=lāp̄|t=to weave together, to conjoin}}, and the form {{m|ar|لُوف}} is stronger in the dialects with the additional meaning of “[[arum]]”, which is mentioned for Syriac already in the 1<sup>st</sup>-century [http://www.poesialatina.it/_ns/Greek/testi/Dioscorides/De_materia_medica_(recensiones_e_codd._Vindob.).html Dioskurides interpolations] 2:[https://dioscorides.usal.es/p2.php?numero=368 167]. Compare the Aramaic-borrowed {{m|ar|كَافُور|id=bract|t=bract of the inflorescence of the date palm}} and {{m|ar|خُوص|t=frond or leaves of the palm tree}} from similar semantic domain.

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|لِيف|m|sing=لِيفَة|pl=أَلْيَاف}}

# [[fibre]]s, [[spongy]] [[interior]] of a [[plant]]
# a handheld [[sponge]]
# {{taxfmt|Luffa|genus}} (genus and species)
# [[fibre]]s, [[tubular]] [[cell]]s of [[bodily]] [[tissue]]
#: {{uxi|ar|أَلْيَاف [[صدر|الصَّدْر]]|muscle fibres of the thorax}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|لِيف|m|pl=أَلْيَاف}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|tr|lif|bor=1}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to have much [[fibre]]
# to rub with [[fibre]] or a [[sponge]]

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|II}}

