===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|fa|لیمو|tr=lêmô, limu}} (compare {{cog|tg|лемӯ}}, {{m|tg|лимӯ}}), a loanword, probably from {{noncog|inc}} (compare {{cog|sa|निम्बू|t=lime}}). The form {{m|ar|لُومِيّ}} is a separate borrowing introduced via {{bor|ar|acx|-}} from {{bor|ar|ta|எலுமிச்சை|t=lemon, lime}}, often meaning dried lemons traded as a spice specifically.

