Page 16327 لينة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-fem|لَيِّنَة}}

# {{feminine singular of|ar|لَيِّن}}

===Etymology 2===

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-fem|لَيْنَة}}

# {{feminine singular of|ar|لَيْن}}

===Etymology 3===
{{unc|ar}}. {{w|Hisham ibn al-Kalbi}} claims he had only heard the term from [[Yathrib]] and the [[Jew]]s, therefore suggesting that the word is borrowed from {{bor|ar|he|-}}. He argues that because the Arabic root {{ar-root|ل ي ن}} is not related to the term’s meaning, he claims that the term cannot be derived from Arabic. However those Jews were monolingual Arabic speakers and no such Hebrew term is known, and some Islamic scholars contend the nativity of the word stating that the palm tree produces tender [[date]]s.

====Noun====
{{ar-sing-noun|لِينَة|coll=لِين|pl=لِينَات}}

# a kind of [[palm tree]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|59:5
|passage=مَا قَطَعْتُم مِّن '''لِّينَةٍ''' أَوْ تَرَكْتُمُوهَا قَائِمَةً عَلَىٰ أُصُولِهَا فَبِإِذْنِ اللَّهِ وَلِيُخْزِيَ الْفَاسِقِينَ
|translation=Whatever you have cut down of [their] '''palm trees''' or left standing on their trunks - it was by permission of Allah and so He would disgrace the defiantly disobedient.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-sing-noun|لِينَة|coll=لِين|
pl=لِينَات}}
-------- end text --------
