Page 16329 م: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the Nabataean letter {{m|arc-nab|𐢓|tr=m|t=mim}}, derived from the {{der|ar|phn|-}} letter {{m|phn|𐤌|tr=m|t=mem}}, from the {{der|ar|egy|-}} hieroglyph {{m|egy|𓈖}}. See also {{m+|syc|ܡ|tr=m|t=mīm}}, {{m+|he|מ|tr=m|t=mem}}, {{m+|grc|Μ}},  {{m+|la|M}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{sense|letter name}} {{IPA|ar|/miːm/}}
* {{sense|phoneme}} {{IPA|ar|/m/}}

====Letter====
{{head|ar|letter|head='''م '''/''' مـ‍ '''/''' ـ‍م‍ـ '''/''' ـ‍م'''|tr=mīm}}

# the twenty-fourth letter of the [[Arabic]] alphabet. It is preceded by {{l|ar|ل}} and followed by {{l|ar|ن}}
# [[p.m.]], after [[noon]] (abbreviation from {{l|ar|مساء}})
#: See also: {{l|ar|ص}}

====Symbol====
{{head|ar|numeral symbol|head='''م '''/''' مـ‍ '''/''' ـ‍م‍ـ '''/''' ـ‍م'''|tr=mīm}}

# the thirteenth letter in traditional [[abjad]] order, which is used in place of numerals for list numbering ([[abjad numerals]]). It is preceded by {{l|ar|ل}} and followed by {{l|ar|ن}}.

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|-}}. Sometimes thought to be derived from the pronouns present in {{cog|ar|مَا}}, {{cog|he|מה|tr=mā|t=what}}, and {{m|ar|مَن}}, {{m|he|מי|tr=mī|t=who}}, so that, for example, {{m|ar|مُدَرِّس||teacher}} is originally {{m|ar||من}} {{m|ar|يُدَرِّس|tr=man yudarris|t=he who teaches}}. Compare also {{cog|ar|مَكْتُوب}} versus {{cog|he|כתוב|tr=kāṯūḇ}}, both meaning “written”, with prefix in Arabic, but without in Hebrew.

====Prefix====
{{head|ar|prefix|tr=ma-|head=مَـ}}

# {{n-g|a prefix used to create nouns of place}}
#: {{m|ar|خَبَزَ|gloss=to [[bake]]}} → {{m|ar|مَخْبِز|gloss=[[bakery]]|lit=place of making bread}}
#: {{m|ar|دَرَسَ|gloss=to [[study]]}} → {{m|ar|مَدْرَسَة|gloss=[[school]]|lit=place of studying}}

====Prefix====
{{head|ar|prefix|tr=mi-|head=مِـ}}

# {{n-g|a prefix used to create instrument nouns}}
#: {{m|ar|فَتَحَ|gloss=to [[open]]}} → {{m|ar|مِفْتَاح|gloss=[[key]]|lit=instrument for opening}}
#: {{m|ar|وَزَنَ|gloss=to [[weigh]]}} → {{m|ar|مِيزَان|gloss=[[scales]]|lit=instrument of weighing}}

====Prefix====
{{head|ar|prefix|head=مُـ}}

# {{n-g|a prefix that forms part of the pattern for participles from {{ar-form|II|verb form}} upwards, as well as all four-root verbs, i. e. all participles that are not from {{ar-form|I|verb form}}}}
#: {{m|ar|دَرَّسَ|t=to [[teach]]}} → {{m|ar|مُدَرِّسٌ|t=teacher}}
#: {{m|ar|اِسْتَشْفَى|t=to seek a cure}} → {{m|ar|مُسْتَشْفًى|t=hospital|lit=place where cure is sought}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|ar|A.D.}}
Abbreviation of {{m|ar|مِيلَادِيّ}}.

====Adverb====
{{head|ar|adverb}}

# [[AD]]

