Page 16415 مؤنس: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ء ن س}}

===Etymology===
{{ar-active participle}} of {{m|ar|آنَسَ||}}. The weekday apparently derives from the circumstance that in antiquity it was a [[hustle and bustle]] amusement day before the main day of religion {{m|ar|عَرُوبَة}}, later {{m|ar|الْجُمْعَة}}. Compare {{m|ar|الْمُشْتَرِي|t=the supplier}} for the planet Jupiter and {{noncog|la|diēs Iovis}} naming the same day after the god Jupiter.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مُؤْنِس}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj|مُؤْنِس}}

# [[charming]], [[delighting]], [[consoling]] {{inflection of|ar|آنَسَ||active participle}}
# [[intimate]], [[congenial]], [[confiding]]

