Page 16418 مئة: -------- begin text --------
{{number box|ar|100}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|[[مائة|مِا۟ئَة]]|tr=miʔa}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*miʔat-}}.
The frequent form {{m|ar|مِائَة|مِا۟ئَة|tr=miʔa}} has a [[silent]] alif to avoid confusion with other words in [[rasm]] (else it could look identical to {{m|ar|من|مِنْهُ|t=from it, from him|tr=min-hu}}), and because it is a [[logogram]] of earlier {{obor|ar|arc|-|notext=1}} spellings.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مِئَة}}

===Numeral===
{{ar-numeral|مِئَة|f|d=مِئَتَان|pl=مِئَات|pl2=مِئُون}}

# [[hundred]]

====Usage notes====
The word {{m|ar|مِئَة}} is an inherently feminine noun. The gender is visible in constructions like [[three hundred]] (see above), where the masculine {{m|ar|ثَلَاث||[[three]]}} appears, which is used with feminine nouns (the numbers 3–10 exhibit the polarity of gender in Arabic). The plural of {{m|ar|مِئَة}} is the same as the singular when used with the numbers 3 through 9, which normally govern a noun in the genitive plural (cf. {{m|ar||ثَلَاثَةُ آلَافٍ|t=[[three thousand]]}}, with plural {{m|ar|آلَاف}}). The plural {{m|ar|مِئَات}} occurs only when used to mean ''[[hundreds]]'', i.e. an unspecified large number.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِئَة|pl=مِئَات|pl2=مِئُون|pos=numeral}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|مِئَوِيّ}}
* {{l|ar|أَرْبَعُمِئَة|t=four hundred}}
* {{l|ar|خَمْسُمِئَة|t=five hundred}}
* {{l|ar|سِتُّمِئَة|t=six hundred}}
* {{l|ar|سَبْعُمِئَة|t=seven hundred}}
* {{l|ar|ثَمَانُمِئَة|t=eight hundred}}
* {{l|ar|تِسْعُمِئَة|t=nine hundred}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|afb|امية|tr=imya}}
* {{desc|arz|مية|tr=miyya}}
* {{desc|acw|مية|tr=miyya}}
* {{desc|ajp|مية|tr=miyya, miyye}}
* {{desc|mt|mija}}
* {{desctree|ary|مية|tr=myā}}
* {{desc|sw|mia|bor=1}}

{{C|ar|Hundred}}
-------- end text --------
