Page 16424 ما: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Cognate with {{cog|he|מָה|tr=ma}} and {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎅}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَا}}

===Pronoun===
{{ar-pron|مَا|m}}

# {{lb|ar|interrogative}} [[what]]?
#: {{synonyms|ar|أَيّ شَيْءٍ|أَيْشٍ|مَاذَا}}
# {{lb|ar|indefinite}} [[some]], a [[certain]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|26
|passage=إِنَّ ٱللَّهَ لَا يَسْتَحْيِي أَنْ يَضْرِبَ مَثَلًا '''مَا''' بَعُوضَةً فَمَا فَوْقَهَا
|translation=Indeed, God is not timid to present an example: '''that of''' a mosquito or what is smaller than it.}}
# {{lb|ar|relative}} [[that]] [[which]], [[what]]
#: {{uxi|ar|اِقْرَأْ '''مَا''' كَتَبْتُ.|t=Read '''what''' I wrote.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' تَفْعَلُ تُجَازَى عَلَيْهِ|t='''Whatever''' you do, you are paid back for it.}}
#* {{quote|ar|سَتُبْدِي لَكَ الْأَيَّامُ مَا كُنْتَ جَاهِلًا}}
#* {{quote|ar
|وَلَعَلَّ '''مَا تَخْشَاهُ''' لَيْسَ بِكَائِن <br/> وَلَعَلَّ '''مَا تَرْجُوهُ''' سَوْفَ يَكُون <br/> وَلَعَلَّ '''مَا هَوَّنْتَ''' لَيْسَ بِهَيِّن <br/> وَلَعَلَّ '''مَا شَدَّدْتَ''' سَوْفَ يَهُون
|t=And maybe '''what you’re afraid of''' isn't existent<br/>And maybe '''what you desire''' is going to be<br/>And maybe '''what you deem easy''' isn’t convenient<br/>And maybe '''what you find difficult''' will be of ease
|lit=what you fear '''it''' / what you desire '''it''' / what you find easy / what you find difficult
|subst=وَلَعَلَّ/وَ-لَعَلَّ}}
# {{lb|ar|+ past or jussive}} [[whichever]]; [[whatever]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَيَّمَا|مَهْمَا}}
#: {{ux|ar|'''مَا''' تَفْعَلْ تُجَازَ عَلَيْهِ|t='''Whatever''' you do, you will be paid back for it.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|106|passage='''مَا''' نَنْسَخْ مِنْ آيَةٍ أَوْ نُنْسِهَا نَأْتِ بِخَيْرٍ مِنْهَا أَوْ مِثْلِهَا|t='''Whatever''' we abrogate that is a passage or make people forget, we come up with others that are better than or just like it.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur’an|2|197|passage=وَ'''مَا''' تَفْعَلُوا مِنْ خَيْرٍ يَعْلَمْهُ اللَّٰهُ|t='''Whatever''' you do that is good, God learns about it.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|رُبَّمَا}}, {{l|ar|رُبَمَا}}: perhaps, maybe
* {{l|ar|لِمَا}}, {{l|ar|لِمَ}}: for what, what for, why

===Particle===
{{wikipedia|Negation in Arabic}}
{{ar-particle|مَا}}

# [[not]]; [[never]]
#: {{syn|ar|إِنْ|q=archaic}}
#: {{see also|[[لا|لَا]]|[[لم|لَمْ]]|[[لن|لَنْ]]|[[ليس|لَيْسَ]]}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 1374|author=w:en:Ibn al-Khatib|title=Zaman Al-Wasl|text=وَطَرٌ '''مَا''' فِيهِ مِنْ عَيْبٍ سِوَى – أَنَّهُ مَرَّ كَلَمْحِ ٱلْبَصَرِ|t=The wish that is '''without''' a mistake except that it passed like a glance of the eye.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' كَتَبَ.|He '''never''' wrote.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' هُوَ بِمَيِّتٍ.|He '''is not''' dead.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' شَيْءٌ أَحَبَّ إِلِيَّ مِنْهُ.|There is '''no''' thing that is more lovely, to me, than that!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' أَحَدٌ مِثْلُهُ.|There is '''n'''one like him.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' مِنْ إِنْسَانٍ فِي الْبَيْتِ.|There is '''no'''body in that house.}}
#: {{uxi|ar|مَا أَرَى شَيْئًا.|I can'''not''' see a thing!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''مَا''' يَفْعَلُ ذٰلِكَ إِلَّا شُجَاعٌ.|'''No''' one would do that but the bold.}}

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|مَا}}

# [[as long as]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|9|7
|passage=فَ'''مَا''' ٱسْتَقَامُوا لَكُمْ فَٱسْتَقِيمُوا لَهُمْ
|translation=So '''as long as''' they are straight with you, be straight with them.
|subst=فَ/فَ-}}
# {{ngd|A subordinating conjunction following particles or genitival nouns in conditional statements, known as {{m|ar|مَا الزَّائِدَة}}, 'superfluous ''mā'''}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|282|passage={{...}} وَلَا يَأْبَ ٱلشُّهَدَاءُ '''إِذَا مَا''' دُعُوا {{...}}|t={{...}} And let not the witnesses refuse when they are called upon. {{...}}}}
# {{ngd|loosely translates to [[that]]; introduces a verbal complement to a preposition, standing in place of the definite verbal noun}}
#: {{syn|ar|أَنْ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|10|passage=وَلَهُمْ عَذَابٌ أَلِيمٌ بِ'''مَا''' كَانُوا يَكْذِبُونَ|subst=وَ/وَ-,بِ/بِ-|t=And they will suffer a painful punishment, '''as''' they used to lie.|lit=...for '''that''' they used to lie}}
#* {{quote-av|ar
|year=2017
|actor={{m|ar||مُهَذِّل الصُّقُور}}
|title=ar:أَتَظُنُّ أَنَّكَ عِنْدَمَا أَحْرَقْتَنِي
|url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_tS3CitSQO4
|time=0:35
|text=أَتَظُنُّ أَنَّكَ بَعْدَ '''مَا''' أَحْرَقْتَنِي وَرَقَصْتَ كَٱلشَيْطَانِ فَوْقَ رُفَاتِي|subst=وَرَقَصْتَ كَٱلشَيْطَانِ/وَ-رَقَصْتَ كَ-ٱلشَيْطَانِ
|t=Do you think that, after you set me alight, and you danced like Satan over my ashes
|lit=do you think that, you, after '''[that]''' you burned me and danced like Satan over my ashes
}}

====Derived terms====
* {{sense|as long as}} {{l|ar|مَا دَامَ}}
* {{l|ar|بَعْدَمَا}}
* {{l|ar|عِنْدَمَا}}
* {{l|ar|حِينَمَا}}
* {{l|ar|كَمَا}}

===Adverb===
{{ar-adv|مَا}}

# [[whenever]]
#: {{rfex|ar}}
# [[as far as]], to the [[extent]] that, to the [[degree]] that
#: {{rfex|ar}}
# {{lb|ar|with an [[elative]] in the accusative}} ([[oh]]) [[how]]...!
#: {{ux|ar|مَا أَجْمَلَ ٱلْحَيَاةَ!|t='''How''' beautiful life is!}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا أَلَذَّ ٱلطَّعَامَ!|'''How''' delicious the food is!}}
#: {{ux|ar|مَا أَعْظَمَكَ!|'''How''' great you are!}}

====Usage notes====
* {{sense|not}} If the negated sentence has a {{w|subject complement}}, the subject complement may occur in the '''nominative''' (like the subject), the '''accusative''' (as it would in a sentence negated instead with {{m|ar|لَيْسَ}}), or (with {{m|ar|بِ}}) '''the genitive''' (as it would in a sentence negated instead with {{m|ar|لَيْسَ}}).
* {{sense|oh how}} The above accusative construction is called {{m|ar|تَعَجُّب|t=wonderment; exclamation}} in Arabic. This pattern originated from {{m|ar|مَا}} meaning “what, something” and the accusative comparative being homophonic to a transitive verb meaning “to make...”. So the example sentence “مَا أَجْمَلَ ٱلْحَيَاةَ” “How beautiful life is!” has the origins in the meaning “Something / What made the life so beautiful?”
**There is another rarer pattern for exclamations, which uses the imperative form of the verb: {{uxi|ar|أَجْمِلْ بِهَا مِنْ حَيَاةٍ!|t=-}}

