Page 16429 ما شاء الله: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|Mashallah}}
{{phrasebook|ar}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَا شَاءَ ٱللّٰه|مَا شَاءَ ٱللّٰهُ}}

===Phrase===
{{head|ar|phrase|head=[[مَا]] [[شَاءَ]] [[ٱللّٰهُ]]}}

# [[mashallah]]:
## {{n-g|Expressing the speaker's [[gratitude]] for a [[blessing]] or their recognition of [[divine intervention]] in its occurrence.}} [[God]] [[will]]ed it.
##* {{RQ:Qur'an|18|39|passage=وَلَوْلَا إِذْ دَخَلْتَ جَنَّتَكَ قُلْتَ '''مَا شَاءَ ٱللَّهُ''' لَا قُوَّةَ إِلَّا بِٱللَّهِ إِنْ تَرَنِ أَنَا أَقَلَّ مِنْكَ مَالًا وَوَلَدًا|t=And why did you, when you entered your garden, not say, ''''What Allah willed''' [has occurred]; there is no power except in Allah '? Although you see me less than you in wealth and children|subst=وَلَوْلَا/وَ-لَوْلَا,وَ-وَلَدًا/وولدا}}
## {{n-g|Expressing the speaker's wish for a [[fortune]] to be maintained, especially against the [[evil eye]]; used in [[congratulation]].}}

