Page 16449 ماجور: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Generally believed to be of {{bor|ar|cop|-}} origin, however the exact word is omitted. One option is {{m|cop||*ⲙⲁϫⲱⲣ}} from {{m|cop|ⲙⲁ-|t=place}} + {{m|cop|ϫⲱⲣ|t=to scatter}}, another {{m|cop|ⲙⲁⲕⲣⲟ|t=trough, mortar}} to which colloquial {{bor|ar|arz|-}} could have applied the tool-pattern as in {{m|ar|كَالُون}}. However the {{w|lang=de|Liste der Mischnatraktate|Tractate}} {{w|Keilim|Kelim}} attests {{m|he-mis|מגור}} to mean a stand in which fire was held in the hearth, comparable to earlier {{cog|hbo|מְגוּרָה|tr=məḡūrā}} meaning a place of living, barn or storehouse, from the root {{m|he|ג־ו־ר|tr=g-w-r}}, the root of {{m|ar|جَار|t=neighbour}}, which itself we have charged to be an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} loanword.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَاجُور}}
* {{IPA|arz|/maɡuːr/|a=Lower Egypt}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَاجُور|m|pl=مَوَاجِير}}

# {{tlb|ar|chiefly||Egypt}} [[vat]], [[wide]]-[[belly|bellied]] [[bowl]], [[trough]] – such as for example a [[kneading trough]], or a [[pottery]] [[coffin]] for [[burial]] until the {{w|Third Dynasty of Egypt|III<sup>rd</sup> dynasty}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَاجُور|pl=مَوَاجِير}}

===References===
* {{R:arz:Bishai:1964|page=43b}}
* {{R:arc:Winter:1910|page=10}}

{{C|ar|Containers|Baking}}
-------- end text --------
