Page 16503 مال: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَالِ}}

====Adverb====
{{ar-adv|مَالِ}}

# {{obsolete spelling of|ar|مَا لِ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|61|2-3|passage=فَ'''مَالِ''' ٱلَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا۟...|t=So '''what is with''' those who disbelieve...}}

===Etymology 2===
Probably a {{univerbation|ar|nocap=1}} of {{m|ar|مَا||what}} + {{m|ar|ل|tr=l-|t=to; belonging to}}, as in {{m|ar||مَا لِي|what belongs to me}}. The root {{ar-root|م و ل}} then developed denominally. While this may seem like [[popular etymology]], similar univerbations do exist in Arabic; compare particularly the dialectal verb {{m|arz|جَاب||tr=jāb}}. Compare also {{cog|syc|ܡܵܠܵܐ|tr=mālā|t=property, wealth}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَال}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-مال.ogg}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَال|m|pl=أَمْوَال}}

# [[property]], [[possessions]], [[chattel]]s, [[goods]]
# [[wealth]], [[affluence]]
# [[fortune]], [[estate]]
# [[money]]
# [[income]], [[revenue]]
# [[assets]], [[capital]], [[stock]], [[fund]]
# {{lb|ar|Islam|law}} marketable title
# {{lb|ar|Egypt}} [[tax]], land tax

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَال|pl=أَمْوَال}}

