-------- end text --------
Page 16798 مجدل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-tool noun}} from the root {{ar-root|ج د ل}} related to things being woven strong, to be strong or compact or borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|מִגְדְּלָא|tr=migdəlā|t=tower}} / {{m|syc|ܡܰܓܕܠܳܐ|tr=magdəlā|t=tower}}, since this word has been widespread across Aramaic dialects and other Arabic terms for fortresses are borrowed too, as {{m|ar|بَلَاط}}, {{m|ar|بُرْج}}, {{m|ar|قَصْر}}, possibly also {{m|ar|حِصْن}}. There is also a native form with a similar semantic range {{l|ar|جَنْدَل|tr=|t=boulder, mass of rocks, rock outcropping; a place with strong defenses, fortress}} from the same root. Cognates are seen in {{cog|he|מִגְדָּל|t=tower|tr=migdāl}}, {{cog|obm|𐤌𐤂𐤃𐤋|t=tower}}, {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎂𐎄𐎍}} and {{m|uga|𐎎𐎄𐎂𐎍|t=tower|pos=or of uncertain meaning}}, {{cog|inm|𐩣𐩴𐩵𐩡|t=tower}}, and possibly {{cog|akk|𒈠𒀜𒂵𒆷𒌅|tr=madgaltu|t=watchtower}}. The Akkadian however appears only from {{cog|akk-mas|-}}, so a borrowing from Northwest Semitic into Akkadian too is considered, yet nothing is proven; alternatively it is from another root {{l|akk|𒅆𒅅|ts=dagālu|t=to look}} hence a place to look from, a watchtower.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مِجْدَل|pl=مَجَادِل|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[palace]], [[fortress]], [[citadel]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِجْدَل|pl=مَجَادِل}}

===References===
* {{R:CAL|mgdl|N}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel-V|page=6}}
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|pages=236–237}}
* {{R:sem-pro:GC|page=364}}
* {{R:uga:DUL-3|page=524|entry=mdgl}}
-------- end text --------
