Page 16843 مجوز: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Likely borrowed into Standard Arabic from {{bor|ar|ajp|-}} and {{bor|ar|apc||مِجْوِز، مِجْوَز|tr=mijwiz, mijwaz}}, whose other meanings include {{m|en|even|gloss=divisible by two}} and {{m|en|paired}}. Both pronunciations must descend from an {{der|ar|ar||مُجْوَز|t=paired, coupled, doubled|nocat=1}} that would have a Modern Standard Arabic cognate in {{doublet|ar|مُزْوَج|notext=1}}, {{ar-passive participle|noderived=1}} of a verb {{m|ar|أَزْوَجَ|t=to pair, to couple, to double}}. Terms of the root {{ar-root|ز|و|ج}} commonly {{glossary|metathesis|metathesized}} to {{ar-root|ج|و|ز}} in Levantine and other vernaculars.

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مِجْوِز|m|head2=مِجْوَز|pl=مَجَاوِز}}

# {{lb|ar|musical instruments}} [[mijwiz]], an Arabic double clarinet

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِجْوِز|head2=مِجْوَز|pl=مَجَاوِز}}

-------- end text --------
Page 16844 مجوس: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|Majus}}
{{ar-rootbox|م ج س}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|𐡌𐡂𐡅𐡔|tr=mgwš}}, from {{der|ar|peo|𐎶𐎦𐏁|tr=maguš}}.<ref>{{R:ar:Cheung|page=16}}</ref>

Was used by the Iraqi Baathist regime to refer to Iran during the [[w:Iran-Iraq War|Iran-Iraq War]] in the 1980s, and later  developed into a broadly anti-Shi'a slur.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَجُوس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|مَجُوس|m-p|sing=مَجُوسِيّ|singg=m}}

# {{lb|ar|collective}} [[Magian]]s, {{lb|ar|collective|historical}} [[Zoroastrian]]s
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|22:17}} (translated by [[w:Abdullah Yusuf Ali|Yusuf Ali]])
#*: {{quote|ar|إِنَّ ٱلَّذِينَ آمَنُوا وَٱلَّذِينَ هَادُوا وَٱلصَّابِئِينَ وَٱلنَّصَارَىٰ وَ''ٱلْمَجُوسَ'' وَٱلَّذِينَ أَشْرَكُوا إِنَّ اللَّهَ يَفْصِلُ بَيْنَهُمْ يَوْمَ ٱلْقِيَامَةِ إِنَّ اللَّهَ عَلَى كُلِّ شَيْءٍ شَهِيدٌ|Those who believe (in the Qur'an), those who follow the Jewish (scriptures), and the Sabians, Christians, '''Magians''', and Polytheists,- Allah will judge between them on the Day of Judgment: for Allah is witness of all things.}}
# {{lb|ar|ethnic slur}} [[Iranians]]
# {{lb|ar|religious slur}} [[Shi'a|Shi'as]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|مَجُوس|sing=مَجُوسِيّ}}

====Derived terms====
{{col-auto|ar|مَجُوسِيّ<t:Zoroastrian; of or related to Zoroastrians>|مَجَّسَ<t:to [[Zoroastrianize]]>}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|fa|مَجوس|tr=majus|bor=1}}

===References===
<references />

