Page 16904 محراب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|sem-srb|𐩣𐩢𐩧𐩨}} attested several times for a certain architectural feature of a [[palace]] or [[court]], and for a “part of a temple where {{m|sem-srb|𐩩𐩢𐩧𐩨}} oracles are obtained”, compare {{m|sem-srb|𐩩𐩢𐩧𐩨𐩩|t=votive relief}}, {{m|sem-srb|𐩩𐩢𐩧𐩨|t=to obtain a vision or an oracle}}, {{m|sem-srb|𐩢𐩧𐩨|t=to obtain an oracle}}. Possibly also related to {{cog|sem-srb|𐩣𐩫𐩧𐩨|t=sanctuary, temple}}, {{cog|gez|ምኵራብ|t=sanctuary, temple}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩫𐩧𐩨|t=to carry out instructions}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩫𐩧𐩨|t=to bless}} = {{cog|ar|بَرَّكَ|t=to bless}}, {{cog|akk|𒅗𒊏𒁍|ts=karābu|t=to pray}}, {{cog|he|כְּרוּב|tr=kerūḇ|t=[[cherub]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مِحْرَاب}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مِحْرَاب|m|pl=مَحَارِيب}}

# the [[prayer]] [[chamber]] of the [[imam]] in a [[mosque]] or instead, a [[symbolic]] [[niche]] in the wall in the direction of the [[qibla]]; [[mihrab]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=14th century {{CE}}|title={{w|al-Bidāya wa-l-Nihāya|al-Bidāya wan-Nihāya}}|trans-title=The Beginning and the End|author={{w|Ibn Kathir|ʾIbn Kaṯīr}}|text=وقد قال الشافعي رحمه الله تعالى: إن لم تكن العلماء العاقلون أولياء الله فلا أعلم لله وليا، وكان يؤم الناس للصلاة في '''محراب''' الحنابلة هو والشيخ العماد،{{...}}|t=And Ash-Shāfiʿī — ''God, He be exalted, have mercy on him'' — had said: If the prudent scholars are not the allies of God, then I know not of any ally for God; and he used to lead the people in prayer in the '''mihrab''' of the Hanbalis, along with Sheikh Al-ʿImād;{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=2008|title=Mawsūʿat Yanābīʿ al-Maʿrifa|trans-title=Encyclopedia of the Fountains of Knowledge|author=Zulaikha Amin Hussain|text=ونري ال'''محاريب''' التي شيدها المماليك في مصر والشام من أبدع ال'''محاريب''' الرخامية، حيث تنتهي تجويفة ال'''محراب''' بطاقية على شكل نصف قبـة مكسوة بأشرطة رخامية متعددة الألوان.|t=And we see the '''mihrabs''' the Mamluks erected in Egypt and Syria (the Levant) are from among the finest made marble '''mihrabs''', where the hollow of the '''mihrab''' ends with an arch in the shape of a semi-dome covered with multicoloured marble bands.}}
# the [[chief]], [[uppermost]] or most [[honorable]] [[sit]]ting place, [[throne room]], the [[high]]est [[chamber]]; [[sanctum]] of a [[king]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|34|13|passage=يَعْمَلُونَ لَهُ مَا يَشَاءُ مِنْ '''مَحَارِيبَ''' وَتَمَاثِيلَ وَجِفَانٍ كَالْجَوَابِ وَقُدُورٍ رَاسِيَاتٍ|t=They made for him what he willed of '''throne rooms''' and statues, and bowls like watering troughs and pots unwieldy.}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|38|21|passage=وَهَلْ أَتَىٰكَ نَبَئُوا ٱلْخَصْمِ إِذْ تَسَوَّرُوا ٱلْ'''مِحْرَابَ'''|t=And has news come to you of the litigants when they scaled up the '''sanctum of King''' [David]?}}
# {{lb|ar|Jewish antiquity}} [[oracle]] {{gloss|the [[sanctuary]], or most [[holy]] place in the [[temple]]}}; [[sanctum sanctorum]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3|37-39|passage={{...}}كُلَّمَا دَخَلَ عَلَيْهَا زَكَرِيَّا ٱلْ'''مِحْرَابَ''' وَجَدَ عِنْدَهَا رِزْقًا قَالَ يَٰمَرْيَمُ أَنَّىٰ لَكِ هَٰذَا{{...}}فَنَادَتْهُ ٱلْمَلَٰئِكَةُ وَهُوَ قَائِمٌ يُّصَلِّي فِي ٱلْ'''مِحْرَابِ''' أَنَّ ٱللهَ يُبَشِّرُكَ بِيَحْيَىٰ مُصَدِّقًا بِكَلِمَةٍ مِّنَ ٱللهِ{{...}}|t={{...}}Every time Zechariah entered upon her in the '''oracle''' (inner sanctuary of the Temple) he found with her provisions. [One day] he said: O Mary, whence have you this?{{...}}So the angels called out to him, and [at that time] he was standing in the '''oracle''' supplicating, [saying]: God brings you glad tidings of John, one who would verify a Word from God{{...}}}}
#* {{RQ:SVD|1 Kings|6|19|passage=وَهَيَّأَ '''مِحْرَابًا''' فِي وَسَطِ ٱلْبَيْتِ مِنْ دَاخِلْ لِّيَضَعَ هُنَاكَ تَابُوتَ عَهْدِ ٱلرَّبِّ.|t=And he prepared an '''oracle''' in the midst of the house within, to set there the ark of the covenant of the LORD.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِحْرَاب|pl=مَحَارِيب}}

====Descendants====
