# [[forbidden]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|مُحَرَّم|pl=sp}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|pt|marrão|bor=1}}
* {{desctree|es|marrano|bor=1}}
* {{desc|zh|穆哈蘭姆月|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ja|マフラム|tr=mafuramu|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{l|ar|الْمُحَرَّم|t=the forbidden}}, from {{l|ar|الشَّهْر الْمُحَرَّم}}, literally "the forbidden month", for being one of the four months in which Arabs forbade fighting, a tradition continued in Islam. The month is of special importance for [[Shia]] Muslims, for being the month in which the [[w:Battle of Karbala|Battle of Karbala]] occurred.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|مُحَرَّم|m}}

# [[Muharram]], the first of the twelve months of the Muslim lunar calendar, each beginning on a [[new moon]].
#: {{syn|ar|اَلْمُحَرَّم}}

