Page 17057 مد: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|م د د}}

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|mdd}}
Compare {{m|ar|مَتَّ}} and {{m|ar|مَطَّ}}. Cognate with {{cog|akk|madādum|𒉘|tr=madādum|t=to measure}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.pass.vn:مَدّ}} {{tlb|ar|transitive}}

# to [[extend]], to [[stretch]], to [[spread out]], to [[lay out]]
#: {{usex|ar|'''اُمْدُدْ''' يَدَكَ / '''مُدَّ''' يَدَكَ.|translation='''Extend''' your hand.}}
# to [[help]], to [[support]]
# to [[supply]], to [[provide]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.pass.vn:مَدّ}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|ar|قَصَرَ}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَدّ|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|مَدَّ|form=I}}
# [[flow]] of the sea, rising [[tide]] {{gloss|when the [[ebb]] has ceased}}
#: {{antonyms|ar|جَزْر}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَدّ}}

=====Antonyms=====
* {{l|ar|قَصْر}}

{{wp|lang=ar|مد (مكيال)}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ar|mudd}}
Probably via {{bor|ar|arc|𐡬𐡣𐡩𐡠}} / {{m|arc|מוֹדְיָא|tr=moḏyā}} / {{m|syc|ܡܘܿܕܝܳܐ|tr=moḏyā}} from {{der|ar|akk|𒉘𒈨𒌍|ts=maddattu, middattu|t=a measure of capacity for dates, water, and other things; a vessel}}, whence also {{der|ar|grc|μόδιος}} and {{der|ar|la|modius}}. Take the rarer volume measure names {{m+|ar|مُدْي|id=mudy}} and {{cog|xcl|մոդ}} into account.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مُدّ|m|pl=أَمْدَاد|pl2=مِدَاد}}

# a [[dry measure]] varying in size by several liters {{defdate|to 20<sup>th</sup> c.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مُدّ|m|pl=أَمْدَاد|pl2=مِدَاد}}

