{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|מוֹרָנָא}} / {{m|syc|*ܡܘܿܪܴܢܳܐ|tr=mōrānā}}, itself borrowed from {{der|ar|akk|murrānum|𒄑𒈠𒉡𒅊𒅊|tr=GIŠ.MA.NU.SIG₇.SIG₇|ts=murrānu}}. Equivalent to {{affix|ar|مُرّ|t1=bitter|ـَان}} from the root {{ar-root|م ر ر|nocat=1}}, for the fruits of the ash are bitter; though Fleischer related it to the root {{ar-root|م ر ن}} due to the pliable wood being used for spears, like {{cog|ang|æsċ|t=ash}}, {{cog|grc|μελία|t=ash}} and {{cog|arc|מוֹרָנִיתָא}} / {{m|syc|ܡܘܿܪܴܢܺܝܬܴܐ|tr=mōrānīṯā|lit=ash-stick}} specifically denote a spear as well—the presence of this root in the other {{cog|sem|-}} languages is not without doubt.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مُرَّان}}

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|مُرَّان|m|sing=مُرَّانَة}}

# [[ash]] ({{taxfmt|Fraxinus|genus}} spp.)
#: {{syn|ar|دَرْدَار}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|مُرَّان}}

====Descendants====
