Page 17260 مرسى الشيخ برغوت: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar|بورتسودان|مرسى الشيخ برغوت}}

===Etymology===
Superficially literally “anchorage of the shaykh of the flea”, with a name looking like the {{cog|apd|-}} form {{m|apd|بَرْغُوت|tr=barḡūt}} of {{m|ar|بُرْغُوث|t=flea}}, related to be the name of a [[faqih]] whose tomb was to the north of the original anchorage, however from {{bor|ar|bej|baarʼuut}} referring to that sea-mark, of unknown further etymology.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَرْسَى الشَّيْخ بَرْغُوت}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|مَرْسَى الشَّيْخ بَرْغُوت|m}}

# {{place|ar|the name of [[Port Sudan]], a <<city>> in <<c/Sudan>>, before its expansion in 1900–1909 from an anchorage to a port}}
#: {{syn|ar|بُورْتْسُودَان}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَرْسَى|state=ind-def|mod=شَيْخِ بَرْغُوتُ|idafa=yes|modcase=nom}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Morin:2012|page=222}}, where transcribed “''marsa šayḫ Barud'' (or ''Baġhut'') or ‘''šayḫ al-barḫat''’”. In German sources transcribed ''Marsa Scheich Barut''. All spellings that cannot be found in Arabic when reverse-transcribed, as of 2021; but no English form of the old name can be found.
