Page 17288 مرقشيتا: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Marcasite-40512.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|مرقشيتا}}|upright=1.15]]
{{swp|lang=ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|مَرْقَشِيثَا|مَارْقَشِيتَا|مَارْقَشِيثَا}}<!--مَرْكشِيثا, مَرْقَشِيطا seem corrupt. The forms with مَار should have an epenthetic vowel after this مَار according to Literary Arabic rules but I haven not seen any transcription informing me which vowel it is. -->

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|arc|מַרְקְשִׁיתָא}} / {{m|syc|ܡܰܪܩܫܺܝܬܴܐ|tr=marqəšīṯā|t=marcasite}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒉌𒌓𒍝𒄢𒈥𒄩𒅆𒌅|tr=<sup>NA<sub>4</sub>.GUG</sup>mar-ḫa-ši-tu|ts=marḫašītu|t=glass or artificial gem in the color of the ''marḫašu'' stone}}, from {{der|ar|akk|𒉌𒌓𒈥𒄩𒋗|tr=<sup>NA<sub>4</sub></sup>mar-ḫa-šu|ts=marḫašu, marḫušu, marḫaṣu|t=a kind of precious stone or gem; marcasite}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒈥𒄩𒅆𒆠|tr=mar-ḫa-ši<sup>KI</sup>|ts=marḫaši, waraḫše}}, name of the {{w|Marhasi|Mesopotamian region}} of disputed extents called in {{cog|akk|𒁀𒊏𒄴𒋢|tr=pa<sub>2</sub>-ra-aḫ-su|ts=paraḫsum, baraḫsum}}, the precious stone also being called in {{cog|xhu|𒁈𒊑 𒅖 𒄭|tr=par<sub>6</sub>ri-iš-ḫi|ts=parrišḫu, parrušḫu}}.

Encountered in {{cog|fa|-}} as {{m|fa|مرقشیشا|tr=marqašišâ}}, {{m|fa|مارقشیشا|tr=mârqašišâ|t=[[marcasite]], [[pyrite]]}}, apparently influenced by {{cog|fa|شیشه|tr=šiše|t=glass}}, and as a name of an aromatic borrowed from {{cog|ira}} into {{cog|xcl|մարդարիշար}}.

Possibly ultimately identical to {{doublet|ar|قَصْدِير|t1=tin|notext=1}}, {{cog|arc|קְסְטִירָא|tr=qəsṭīrā}}, {{m|arc|קַסִּיטְרָא|tr=qassīṭrā|t=tin}}, {{cog|grc|κασσίτερον}}, {{m|grc|κασσίτερος|t=tin}}, relating to the {{w|Kassites}} residing at the {{w|Zagros Mountains}} where one mined tin, overlapping with Marḫaši, regard the other English name of tin: {{m|en|golden marcasite}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَرْقَشِيتَا}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَرْقَشِيتَا|f}}

# [[marcasite]], [[pyrite]], and similar [[mineral]]s of [[ferrous sulfate]]
#: {{syn|ar|حَجَر النُور}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَرْقَشِيتَا}}

{{C|ar|Minerals}}
{{cln|ar|terms derived from toponyms}}
-------- end text --------
