Page 17335 مريمية: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|مَيْرَمِيَّة|مَرَمِيَّة|مَيْرَامِيَّة|مَرْمَرِيَّة||rather dialectal}}

===Etymology===
Surely contains {{m|ar|مَرْو}}, which by itself is used for sage in {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, though it is uncertain where it obtained the connection to {{m|ar|مَرْيَم|t=Mary}} in Arabic and {{cog|fa|مریم گلی|tr=maryam goli|t=sage}}, in view of which it is perhaps all the same word as {{m|ar|مَرْزَنْجُوش}}, maybe even {{m|ar|مَرْمَاخُور}}; marjoram and oregano look very similar to sage and due to greater use were likely treated as archetypical to it.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَرْيَمِيَّة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَرْيَمِيَّة|f}}

# [[sage]] (''[[Salvia]]'' and especially {{taxfmt|Salvia officinalis|species}})
#: {{syn|ar|قَصْعِين|رِعْي الأُيَّل|q2=obsolete|سَالَبِيَّة|شَالَبِيَّة|q4=al-Andalus|نَاعِمَة|q5=al-Andalus|شَاقِيَة}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَرْيَمِيَّة}}

===References===
* {{R:arc:Löw-Pflanzen|page=252}}
* {{R:arc:Löw-Flora|volume=2|page=102}}

{{C|ar|Mint family plants}}
