Page 17487 مسجد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-noun of place}} from the verb {{m|ar|سَجَدَ|t=to [[bow down]]}}, from the root {{ar-root|س|ج|د}}. Likely borrowed from a regional {{bor|ar|arc|-}} term for a place of worship, attested in {{w|Nabataean Aramaic}} {{m|arc|𐢓𐢖𐢄𐢅𐢀|tr=msgdʾ}} and in {{cog|arc-imp|𐡌𐡎𐡂𐡃𐡀}} already in the 5th century BCE, the [[emphatic state]] of which seems to underlie some of the Romance descendants.

===Pronunciation===
