===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|م س ح}}
Compare {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎌𐎈}} and {{cog|he|מָשַׁח|tr=mašáḥ|t=to [[anoint]]}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.pass.vn:مَسْح}}

# to [[stroke]] with the [[hand]] or similar, to [[wipe off]], to [[sweep]]
# to [[anoint]]
# to [[smooth]], to [[polish]]
# to [[wipe off]], to [[wipe out]], to [[cross off]], to [[erase]], to [[scrub]], to [[flush]]
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} to [[wear]], to [[fatigate]], to [[emaciate]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.pass.vn:مَسْح}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.pass.vn:مَسْح,مِسَاحَة}}

# to [[survey]], to [[scan]] for [[proportion]]s by going over, to [[clear through]], to [[peragrate]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.pass.vn:مَسْح,مِسَاحَة}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[wipe off]], to [[anoint]]
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[Christianize]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَسْح|m|pl=مُسُوح}}

# {{inflection of|ar|مَسَحَ||verbal noun}}
# a [[survey]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْح|pl=مُسُوح}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِسْح|m|pl=مُسُوح}}

# [[main]] [[route]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْح|pl=مُسُوح}}

===Etymology 2===
This could be taken as from the root {{ar-root|م س ح}} above as for a wiping rag, however the cloths denoted by this word do not seem to have been adapted for such an employment, and their property of coarseness makes the term adverse to that root’s meanings for smoothness. Therefore a connection to {{bor|ar|cop|ⲙⲟϫϩ|t=girdle of a soldier or monk}} or a related word is suggested.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِسْح|m|pl=مُسُوح}}

# {{C|ar|Fabrics}} a [[coarse]] [[cloth]], [[sackcloth]], [[gunny]], [[haircloth]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|abudawud|35|55|passage=وَأَوَّلُ مَنْ يَدْخُلُ عَلَيْهَا إِذَا قَدِمَ فَاطِمَةَ فَقَدِمَ مِنْ غَزَاةٍ لَهُ وَقَدْ عَلَّقَتْ '''مِسْحًا''' أَوْ سِتْرًا عَلَى بَابِهَا وَحَلَّتِ الْحَسَنَ وَالْحُسَيْنَ قُلْبَيْنِ مِنْ فِضَّةٍ فَقَدِمَ فَلَمْ يَدْخُلْ فَظَنَّتْ أَنَّ مَا مَنَعَهُ أَنْ يَدْخُلَ مَا رَأَى فَهَتَكَتِ السِّتْرَ وَفَكَّكَتِ الْقُلْبَيْنِ عَنِ الصَّبِيَّيْنِ وَقَطَعَتْهُ بَيْنَهُمَا|t=The first he visited on his return was Fāṭima, and he retourned from a raid and she had hung up a '''gunny''' or some drapery at her door, and bedecked al-Ḥasan and al-Ḥusayn by using silver bracelets. So, when he arrived, he entered not. And she believed he was barred from entering by what he had seen, so she tore down the drapery, unfastened the bracelets from the boys and cut them off.|subst=وَالْحُسَيْنَ/وَ-ٱلْحُسَيْنَ,فَلَمْ/فَ-لَمْ,وَأَوَّلُ/وَ-أَوَّلُ,فَقَدِمَ/فَ-قَدِمَ,وَقَدْ/وَ-قَدْ,لَهُ/لَ-هُو,مَنَعَهُ/مَنَعَ-هُو,فَظَنَّتْ/فَ-ظَنَّتْ,فَهَتَكَتِ/فَ-هَتَكَتِ,وَفَكَّكَتِ/وَ-فَكَّكَتِ,وَقَطَعَتْهُ/وَ-قَطَعَتْهُو,بَيْنَهُمَا/بَيْنَ-هُمَا,بَابِهَا/بَابِ-هَا,عَلَيْهَا/عَلَيْ-هَا,وَحَلَّتِ/وَ-حَلَّتِ}}
# {{C|ar|Clothing}} [[cilice]], [[haircloth]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَسْح|pl=مُسُوح}}

====References====
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|page=1199}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy-V|pages=405–407}}

