[[File:DjurdjuraKabylie.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|مُشْتَهَى}}|upright=0.95]]
[[File:SORBUS ARIA (Alisier blanc).jpg|frameless|right|{{lang|ar|مُشْتَهَى}}]]

===Etymology 2===
A plant not spread in the Arab world except scatteredly [[c:File:Sorbus aria range.svg|in Northwest Africa]] – a {{bor|ar|roa}} borrowing, akin to {{cog|pt|mostajeiro}}, {{cog|ast|mostayo}}, {{cog|roa-leo|[[mostellar]], [[mostayal]], [[mostayo]]}}, {{cog|es|[[mostajo]], [[mostellar]]}} (the form {{m|es|mostellar}} from Leonese), {{cog|an|[[mostayo]], [[mostajo]], [[mostachera]], [[moixera]]}}, {{cog|ca|[[mogera]], [[moixera]], [[moxera]]}}, meaning {{taxfmt|Sorbus aria|species}}, deriving from {{der|ar|VL.|-}} extensions of {{der|ar|la|mustum|t=must}}, because of the berries being stored in must or tasting of wine. {{doublet|ar|[[مُصْطَار]] / [[مُسْطَار]]|t1=must}}, an earlier borrowing of a unit of measure for must.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مُشْتَهَى|f}}

# [[common whitebeam]] ({{taxfmt|Aria edulis|species}}, syn. {{taxfmt|Sorbus aria|species}})
#* {{RQ:Awwam|30|8|volume=2|page=429|passage=وفيه ينضج الخوخ والرمان والسفرجل ويسود بعض حب الريتون ويطيب حب شجر المشتهى والبلوط والقسطل ويفصل الجوز وهو أفضل وقت جمعه وفيه يجمع الصنوبر والعناب ويظهر فيه الأسفاراج وفيه يبدئ بالحرث والزراعة بعد نزول الغيث وذلك في بعض البلاد وفيه تجمع الكراويا والكمون واللوبياء والدرونج وبزور الأحباق والكزبر والأرز وتقلع الحناء.|translation=In this ripen the peach, the pomegranate, and the quince, and some olives become black, and the common whitebeam and the oak and the chestnut become good, and the walnuts open, and it is the best time to gather them, and in it pines and jujubes are harvested, and in it asparagus appears, and one begins to till and sow after the rain in some regions, and one collects caraway and jeera and green beans and leopard’s bane and basil seeds and coriander and rice and pulls the henna.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مُشْتَهَى}}

===References===
* {{R:es:DRAE|mostellar}}
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=1|page=797}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=2|page=462}}
* {{R:ar:Simonet-Glosario|pages=381–383}}

{{C|ar|Pome fruits}}
