Page 17625 مشعل: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ش ع ل}}
The majority of Arabic dictionaries only list {{m|ar|مَشْعَل}} and its synonym {{m|ar|مَشْعَلَة}} with a [[fatḥa]] on the mīm, which gives each of these words the appearance of a {{ar-noun of place|lc=1}} instead of a {{ar-tool noun|lc=1}}. Some may have argued for them to be written with a [[kasra]], but it is not common.<ref>Quoting Lane under the entry ”{{lang|ar|مَشْعَلَةٌ}}”, “[accord. to El-Wáḥidee, it is {{lang|ar|مِشْعَلَةٌ}}; for he says that] {{lang|ar|المشعلة}} with kesr to the {{lang|ar|م}} means ''the instrument in which fire is carried'': and {{lang|ar|مَشْعلة}} [thus, with a fet-ḥah over the {{lang|ar|نار}},] means ''fire kindled; or made to burn up, burn brightly or fiercely, blaze, or flame''”.</ref> All the languages which have borrowed these two words have kept the vocalizations {{m|ar|مَشْعَل}} and {{m|ar|مَشْعَلَة}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَشْعَل}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَشْعَل|m|pl=مَشَاعِل}}

# [[torch]] {{C|ar|Light sources|Fire}}
#: {{syn|ar|مَشْعَلَة}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَشْعَل|pl=مَشَاعِل}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|hy|մաշալ|bor=1}}
* {{desc|az|məşəl|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bn|মশাল|bor=1}}
* {{desc|chg|مشعل|bor=1}}
** {{desc|ug|مەشئەل}}
** {{desc|uz|mashʼal}}
* {{→}} Hindustani:
** {{desc|hi|मशाल}}
** {{desc|ur|مشعل|tr=maś'al}}
* {{desc|ota|مشعل<alt:مَشْعَل>|tr=meş'al|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|meşal}}
* {{desc|ps|مشعل<alt:مَشْعَل>|tr=maš'ál|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fa|مشعل|tr=maš'al|bor=1}}
* {{desc|pa|مَشْعَل|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sd|مشعل<alt:مَشْعَلُ>|bor=1}}

