Page 17692 مصر: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
From a common {{der|ar|sem}} source; compare {{cog|he|מִצְרַיִם|tr=miṣráyim}}, {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎕𐎗𐎎}}, and {{cog|akk|𒈪𒄑𒊑𒄿|tr=miṣru}} or {{m|akk|𒈬𒀫|tr=muṣru}}. The ending in {{cog|he|-}} and {{cog|uga|-}} is the standard dual form, perhaps related to the ancient conceptualization of Egypt as two realms: [[Upper Egypt]] and [[Lower Egypt]]. Conflated with the root {{ar-root|م ص ر}} in some senses (see below).

The sense of [[w:Cairo|Cairo]] stems from the earlier settlement {{m|ar|مِصْرُ الفُسْطَاط|t=the Civil Center of Assembly|lit=of the large camel-hair tents, assembly halls}} that was incorporated into Cairo.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مِصْر}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-Misr2.oga}}

====Proper noun====
