Page 17727 مصوع: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|lang=ar}}
[[File:Map of Massawa.png|frameless|right|upright=1.2]]

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|tig|-}} and {{bor|ar|ti|ምጽዋዕ|tr=məṣəwwaʿ}}, {{der|ar|gez|ምጽዋዕ|tr=məṣəwwaʿ}}, attested for a body of water in front of its coast, derived by the local tradition from {{m|gez|ጸውዐ|tr=ṣäwwəʿä|t=to call}} common to all three languages, referring to the fact that the city’s historical centre lies on the outer one of the two offshore islands, being removed from either the mainland and the other island by less than a kilometre, which allowed for making oneself intelligible there by shouting into the sea.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مُصَوَّع}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|مُصَوَّع|f}}

# {{place|ar|port city|c/Eritrea|;|west of the {{w|Dahlak Archipelago}}|t=Massawa}}.
#: {{syn|ar|بَاضِع|q1=formerly}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مُصَوَّعُ|state=ind-def}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Morin:2012|pages=223–224}}
* {{R:gez:TraCES|entry=ምጽዋዕ|id=Lf08db3324e8e4994912ef6072b0f43e8}}, contains a 15<sup>th</sup> century quotation for Geʿez from {{cite-book|editor=Tedros Abraha|title=Gädlä Abunä Yonas Zä-Bur: Eritrean saint of the 15th century / Ge'ez text edited and translated|year=2015|publisher=Brepols|series={{w|Patrologia Orientalis}}|isbn=978-2-503-56548-4|seriesvolume=236 (53.2)|page=82 (378) lines 27 seqq.}} where it is named a “great sea”.
