Page 17787 مطبعة: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ط ب ع}}

===Etymology===
From {{bor|ar|ota|مطبعه|tr=matbaʾa}}, a {{ar-noun of place|lc=1}} from the root {{ar-root|ط ب ع}}. Printing did not start in the Arab world until {{w|French campaign in Egypt and Syria|Napoléon brought a printing press to Egypt}} in 1798, whereas the Ottomans had first private tries from 1726 (it did not become widescale until the next century).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَطْبَعَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَطْبَعَة|f|pl=مَطَابِع}}

# [[printery]], [[printing press]], [[print shop]], any place that prints

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَطْبَعَة|pl=مَطَابِع}}
-------- end text --------
