{{C|ar|Tools}}
-------- end text --------
Page 17814 مطمورة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ط م ر}}. Deemed by Fraenkel to reek of {{bor|ar|syc|ܡܰܛܡܽܘܪܬܳܐ|tr=maṭmūrtā|t=pit for hiding treasures}} from {{m|syc|ܛܡܰܪ|tr=ṭmar|t=to bury; to hide, to abscond}} by reason of the Arabic root missing the meaning “to store” in the old poetry, and indeed from what the web databases of Qaṣāʾid and ʾAḥādīṯ return by 2019 {{m|ar|طَمَرَ|t=to bury, to hide}} is absent. Compare against {{cog|akk|𒋼𒈨𒊒|tr=temēru, tamāru|t=to bury, to conceal}}.<!--Brockelmann gives it as ṭamāru in the Lexicon Syriacum. Should he be correct while elsewhere the Akkadian is sorted with non-emphatic plosive?-->

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَطْمُورة|f|pl=مَطَامِير|pl2=مَطْمُورَات}}

# [[underground]] [[storage]] room dug to preserve [[foodstuff]], a [[granary]], [[subterranean]] [[silo]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَطْمُورة|f|pl=مَطَامِير|pl2=مَطْمُورَات}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|mt|matmura}}
* {{desc|ca|masmorra|bor=1}}
* {{desc|fr|matamore|bor=1}}
** {{desc|en|mattamore|bor=1}}
* {{desc|gl|mazmorra|bor=1}}
* {{desc|pt|masmorra|bor=1}}
* {{desc|es|mazmorra|bor=1}}
** {{desc|en|massymore|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{nonlemma}}

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-fem|مَطْمُورة}}

# {{inflection of|ar|مَطْمُور||f}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Fraenkel|page=137}}

{{C|ar|Rooms}}
-------- end text --------
