Page 17843 معاش: -------- begin text --------

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَعَاش|m}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|عَاشَ|form=I}}
# [[livelihood]], [[subsistence]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=1377|author=w:en:Ibn Khaldun|editor=Khalīl Shaḥādah|title=[[w:en:Kitab al-ibar|{{lang|ar|تاريخ ابن خلدون}}]]|page=727|pageurl=https://shamela.ws/book/12320/725|volume=1|location=Beirut, Lebanon|publisher=Dār al-Fikr|edition=1st|year_published=1981|passage=وَأَكْثَرُ مَا يَحْمِلُ عَلَى ٱلْتِمَاسِ هٰذِهِ الصِّنَاعَةِ وَٱنْتِحَالِهَا هُوَ كَمَا قُلْنَاهُ الْعَجْزُ عَنِ الطُّرُقِ الطَّبِيعِيَّةِ '''لِلْمَعَاشِ''' وَٱبْتِغَاؤُهُ مِنْ غَيْرِ وُجُوهِهِ الطَّبِيعِيَّةِ كَٱلْفِلَاحَةِ وَٱلتِّجَارَةِ وَٱلصِّنَاعَةِ فَيَسْتَصْعِبُ الْعَاجِزُ ٱبْتِغَاءَهُ مِنْ هٰذِهِ وَيَرُومُ الْحُصُولَ عَلَى الْكَثِيرِ مِنَ الْمَالِ دُفْعَةً بِوُجُوهٍ غَيْرِ طَبِيعِيَّةٍ مِنَ الْكِيمِيَاءِ وَغَيْرِهَا.|translation=The most common cause of the desire to practice alchemy is, as we have stated; a person’s inability to make his '''living''' in a natural way and the wish to make a living in some way that, unlike agriculture, commerce, and (handi)craft, is not natural. A person without ability finds it difficult to make his living in such (legitimate occupations). He wants to get rich all at once through some (occupation) that is not natural, such as alchemy and other things.|subst=ٱلْتِمَاسِ/لْتِمَاسِ|footer=Translated by [[w:en:Franz Rosenthal|Franz Rosenthal]]}}
# {{lb|ar|post-Classical}} [[salary]]
#: {{syn|ar|رَاتِب}}

