Page 17867 معبلة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|gez|ማዕበልት|tr=maʿəbält|t=instrument, fitting, weapon, spear, arrow}} (plural {{m|gez|መዓብል|tr=mäʿabəl}}, related to {{m|gez|ዐበለ|tr=ʿäbbälä|t=to make}}, of unclear further derivation, possibly the same as {{m|ar|عَمِلَ|t=to work}}, {{cog|arc|עָמֵל|tr=ʿāmel|t=to work}}. Note that the mother of {{w|Antarah ibn Shaddad|ʿantara}} who uses this word was a captive from Aksum. At the time of the Arabic lexicographers the Arabic word had become obsolete already so they were unsure about the quality of the instrument denoted by it; the frequent characterization as “broad and long arrowhead” is interpolated by the root {{ar-root|ع ب ل|nocat=1}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مِعْبَلَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مِعْبَلَة|f|pl=مَعَابِل}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# [[arrowhead]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|author={{l|ar||{{w|Antarah ibn Shaddad|عَنْتَرَة بِن شَدَاد الْعَبْسِي}}|tr=ʕantara ibn šaddād al-ʕabsī}}|title=[[s:ar:خذوا ما أسأرتْ منها قداحى|{{lang|ar|خذوا ما أسأرت منها قداحى}}]] (first line)|year=a. 608
|passage=وَآخِرَ مِنْهُم أَجْرَرْتُ رُمْحِي <br/> وَفِي ٱلْبَجْلِيِّ مِعْبَلةٌ وَقِيعُ
|translation=And the last of them I pierced with my spear<br/>And in al-bajlī was a sharpened arrowhead}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِعْبَلَة|pl=مَعَابِل}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Dozy|volume=2|page=92}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=3|page=101}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=1942}}
* {{R:gez:Leslau-Comp.|page=54}}
* {{R:Nöldeke:Neue Beitr.|page=55}}
* {{R:ar:Schwarzlose|page=312}}

{{C|ar|Archery}}
-------- end text --------
