===Etymology===
{{ar-noun of place}} from the verb {{m|ar|قَامَ||to [[get up]]}}, from the root {{ar-root|ق|و|م}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|מָקוֹם|tr=māqōm}} and {{cog|phn|𐤌𐤒𐤌 }}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَقَام}}
** {{IPA|afb|/məˈqaːm/|a=Gulf}}
* {{rhymes|ar|aːm}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَقَام|m|pl=مَقَامَات}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|قَامَ|form=I}}
# [[place]], [[spot]]
#: {{syn|ar|مَكان}}
# [[situation]]
# [[domicile]]
# [[burial]] place
#: {{syn|ar|مَرْقَد|ضَرِيح|مَشْهَد|حَرَم|مَزار}}
# [[staying]], [[halting]], [[sojourn]], [[dwelling]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|chapter=45|title={{lang|ar|{{w|lang=ar|بحار الأنوار}}}}|trans-title={{w|Bihar al-Anwar|Biḥār al-Anwār}}|author=w:al-Majlisi|quotee=ar:بشير بن جذلم<tr:Bašīr ibn Jaḏlam>|text=يَا أَهْلَ يَثْرِبَ لَا مَقَامَ لَكُمْ بِهَا ... قُتِلَ الْحُسَيْنُ فَأَدْمُعِي مِدْرَارُ|t=O people of [[Yathrib]] (i.e. [[Medina]]) you have no staying in it ... [[Husayn]] is killed thus my tears are overflowing|year=17th century|url=https://ar.lib.eshia.ir/11008/45/147/%D9%85%D9%82%D8%A7%D9%85}}
# [[standing]], [[station]]
#: {{syn|ar|مَنْزِلَة}}
# [[office]], [[rank]], [[dignity]]
# [[esteem]], [[consideration]]
# [[court]] {{lb|ar|of a [[sovereign]]}}
# {{lb|ar|music}} [[tune]], [[song]]
# {{lb|ar|music|countable}} [[maqam]] {{gloss|Arabic musical [[scale]]}}, [[tonality]], [[mode]], [[key]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَقَام}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مُقَام|m|pl=مُقَامَات}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|أَقَامَ|form=IV}}
# {{form of|ar|[[Appendix:Arabic_nominals#Nouns_of_place|noun of place]]|أَقَامَ}}: [[residence]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مُقَام|pl=مُقَامَات}}

