Page 18117 مقدس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
ِApparently an irregular {{ar-noun of place|lc=1}} from {{m|ar|قَدُسَ|t=to be holy}}, occurring chiefly in an Arabic name for the {{w|Temple in Jerusalem}}, {{m|ar|بَيْت المَقْدِس|t=The House of the Holy Place}}, with the regular form being {{m|ar|مَقْدَس}}. Compare {{m|ar|مَطْلَع|t=rising place}} and its irregular variant, {{m|ar|مَطْلِع}}. Compare also the irregular {{m|ar|مَنْكِب|t=shoulder-joint}}, a derivation that {{w|Sibawayh|Sībawayh}}, however, suspected to be a name for this body part rather than a noun of place.

Compare with {{cog|arc|מַקְדְּשָׁא|tr=maqdəšā}}, {{cog|he|מִקְדָּשׁ|tr=miqdāsh}}, {{cog|xpu|𐤌𐤉𐤒𐤃𐤔}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَقْدِس|m}}

# a [[holy]] [[place]]; a [[sanctuary]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَقْدِس}}

===Etymology 2===
{{ar-rootbox|ق د س}}
{{ar-passive participle}} of {{m|ar|قَدَّسَ||to [[sanctify]], to make [[holy]], to [[consecrate]]}}.

====Adjective====
{{ar-adj-sound|مُقَدَّس}}

# [[sacred]], [[holy]]
# [[sanctified]]
# [[consecrated]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-adj|مُقَدَّس|pl=sp}}

