Page 18122 مقدونس إفرنجي: -------- begin text --------
[[File:20190511Anthriscus cerefolium2.jpg|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|مقدونس إفرنجي}}|upright=1.8]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|مَقْدُونِس فَرَنْجِيّ||more colloquial}}

===Etymology===
A Western European plant rarely known in Arabic lands, hence “Frankish”, which is an epithet added to any plant that is perceived as Western European, and this name has been formed already in medieval times. So also {{cog|ota|فرنك معدنوسی|tr=frenk maydanozu|t=[[garden chervil]], {{taxfmt|Anthriscus cerefolium|species}}}}, {{cog|tr|frenk maydanozu}}, and even {{cog|el|φραγκομαϊντανός}} for the same plant.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَقْدُونِس إِفْرَنْجِيّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|[[مَقْدُونِس]] [[إِفْرَنْجِيّ]]|m}}

# [[chervil]], [[garden chervil]], [[French parsley]] ({{taxfmt|Anthriscus cerefolium|species}})

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَقْدُونِس|mod=إِفْرَنْجِيّ}}

{{C|ar|Celery family plants|Spices}}
