Page 18241 ملأك: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|مَلَك}}

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|gez|መልአክ|t=messenger; angel}}, the plural of which is {{m|gez|መላእክት|tr=mälaʾəkt}}, itself a calque of {{der|ar|arc|מַלְאֲכָא}} / {{m|syc|ܡܠܐܟܐ|tr=malʾăḵā|t=angel, messenger}} and {{der|ar|he|מַלְאָךְ|tr=malʾā́ḵ|t=angel, messenger}}, closer in {{cog|ti|መልኣኽ}}, {{cog|am|መልኣክ}}, {{m|am|መላክ}} of which the plural is {{m|am|መላእክት|tr=mälaʾəkt}}. Compare the root {{ar-root|ل|ء|ك}} and {{m|ar|لَأَكَ}}, {{m|ar|أَلْأَكَ|t=to send as a [[messenger]]}}, which was regularly used as the normal word for “to send” in {{cog|gez|ለአከ}} as well as in {{cog|uga|𐎍𐎛𐎋}}, {{m|uga|𐎍𐎀𐎋}} for which the normal {{cog|ar|-}} word is {{m|ar|أَرْسَلَ}} upon which one has formed {{m|ar|رَسُول|t=messenger; apostle; angel}}, with the same pattern native {{cog|gez|ልኡክ|t=messenger; apostle; cantor}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مَلْأَك}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|مَلْأَك|m|pl=مَلَائِك|pl2=مَلَائِكَة}}

# [[angel]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَلْأَك|pl=مَلَائِك|pl2=مَلَائِكَة|pl3=مَلَائِك}}

