===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*malk-}}. The insertion of the vowel ''i'' is irregular, leading, though it could be a prop vowel as in {{m|ar|إِبِل}}, to the suggestion that it is instead borrowed from an archaic Aramaic predecessor to {{cog|arc|מַלְכָּא||king|tr=malkā}}, along with the clear borrowing {{m|ar|مَلَكُوت}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|مَلِك}}

