Page 18461 منذ: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|مُذْ}}
* {{alter|ar|مِنْذُ||obsolete|poetic}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مُنْذُ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-منذ.ogg}}

===Preposition===
{{ar-prep|مُنْذُ}} {{+obj|ar|gen/nom}}

# {{non-gloss definition|denotes the time at which an occurrence started}}
#: {{syn|ar|مِنْ}}
#: {{ux|ar|رَأَيْتُكَ '''مُنْذُ''' يَوْمُ الْخَمِيسِ|t=I have been seeing you '''since''' Thursday.}}
#: {{ux|ar|رَأَيْتُكَ '''مُنْذُ''' يَوْمُ الْخَمِيسِ إِلَى يُوْمِ الْجُمُعَةِ|t=I saw you '''from''' Thurday to Friday.}}
# {{ngd|denotes an amount of time stretching from the past}}
#: {{syn|ar|مِنْ}}
#: {{ux|ar|لَا أَزَالُ أَرَاكَ '''مُنْذُ''' يَوْمَيْنِ|t=I have been seeing you '''for''' two days.}}
# {{ngd|denotes the length of the period between a time or occurrence in the past and the present}}
#: {{syn|ar|مِن}}
#* {{quote-book
|ar
|year=a. 544 {{CE}}
|author={{w|Imru' al-Qais|Imruʾ al-Qays}}
|title={{link|ar||قِفَا نَبْكِ مِنْ ذِكْرَى حَبِيبٍ وَعِرْفَانِ}}
|trans-title=Let Us Weep
|passage=قِفَا نَبْكِ مِنْ ذِكْرَى حَبِيبٍ وَعِرْفَانِ / وَرَسْمٍ عَفَتْ آيَاتُهُ '''مُنْذُ''' أَزْمَانِ
|subst=عِرْفَانِ/عِرْفَانِي,أَزْمَانِ/أَزْمَانِي
|t=Halt! Let us weep<br>For the memory of<br>Our ladylove<br>And our memory of<br>A rubble heap,<br>Which faded away<br>So long '''ago'''.}}
#* {{quote-av
|ar
|year=21st century
|author=w:Genndy Tartakovsky
|title={{link|ar||سَامُورَاي جَاك}}
|trans-title=Samurai Jack
|text='''منذ''' زمن طويل وفي أراضٍ بعيدة، أنا آكو، المتحوّل الشرير، وسيد الظلام، أطلقت شرًا رهيبًا جدًا، لكنّ محارب ساموراي الغبيّ، يحمل سيفًا سحريًّا، تقدّم ليواجهني.
|t=Long '''ago''' in a distant land, I, Aku, the evil shape-shifter and the Master of Darkness, unleashed an unspeakable evil, but the foolish samurai warrior, who wields a magic sword, stepped forth to oppose me.}}
# {{ngd|denotes a time in the past}}
#: {{syn|ar|فِي}}
#: {{ux|ar|رَأَيْتُكَ مُنْذُ زَمَنٍ بَعِيدٍ.|t=I saw you '''back in''' a faraway time.}}
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} {{ngd|denotes a time in the present}}
#: {{syn|ar|فِي}}
#: {{ux|ar|رَأَيْتُكَ '''مُنْذُ''' الْيَوْمُ|t=I have seen you '''to'''day.}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|mindu}}

===Conjunction===
{{ar-con|مُنْذُ}}

# [[since]]
#: {{ux|ar|مَا خَرَجَ مِنَ ٱلْبَيْتِ '''مُنْذُ''' نَزَلَ ٱلْمَطَرُ.|t=He has not stepped out of the house '''since''' the rain set in.}}
#* {{quote-song|ar
|title=ar:النشيد الوطني اللبناني
|trans-title=The Lebanese National Anthem
|lyricist={{lang|ar|رشيد نخلة}} [Rashid Nakhle]
|composer={{lang|ar|وديع صبرا}} [<nowiki/>{{w|Wadih Sabra}}]
|year=1925
|text=اِسمُهُ عِزُّهُ '''مُنْذُ''' كَانَ الجُدُود
|tr=ismuhu ʿizzuhu munḏu kāna l-judūd
|t=Its name has been its glory '''since''' the time of [our] ancestors.
|lit=Its name is its glory '''since''' [our] ancestors were.
}}

====Usage notes====
* A noun that comes after {{m|ar|مُنْذُ}} or {{m|ar|مُذْ}} may occur in the nominative or in the genitive. A verb-initial clause that follows either of them may be introduced with {{m|ar|أَنْ}}, and a noun-initial clause may be introduced with {{m|ar|أَنَّ}}.
* {{m|ar|مُنْذُ}} and {{m|ar|مُذْ}} share each other's meanings and case government, but whether they are interchangeable and whether the case of the following noun alters the meaning is disputed.
* {{m|ar|مُنْذ}} and {{m|ar|مُذ}} may denote a time or an occurrence in the past or an ongoing state of affairs. This oftentimes creates ambiguity when a length of time is specified, as in this construction:
:: {{uxi|ar|رَأَيْتُكَ '''مُنْذُ''' يَوْمَانِ|t="I saw you two days '''ago'''" or "I have (or had) been seeing you '''for''' two days."}}
: Because of this, many grammarians, like {{w|Ibn Hisham al-Ansari|Ibn Hišām al-ʾAnṣārī}}, suggest that the word should govern the nominative in the first sense (ago) and that in the second sense (for) it should govern the genitive, so as to differentiate its two meanings.
* Neither {{m|ar|مُنْذُ}} nor {{m|ar|مُذْ}} is used with {{w|prepositional pronoun}}s.
* Neither {{m|ar|مُنْذُ}} nor {{m|ar|مُذْ}} occurs in the Qur'an.

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|mindu}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|منذ}}
