Page 18579 مهر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{etymid|ar|dowrystuff}}
Common {{der|ar|sem-wes|-}} term; compare {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎅𐎗|tr=}}, {{cog|sem-srb|𐩣𐩠𐩧𐩩|tr=mhrt|t=wealth, possessions, commodities, goods}}, {{cog|hbo|מָהַר|tr=mahar|t=to acquire by exchange, to barter, to purchase}}, {{cog|hbo|מֹהַר|tr=mṓhar|t=bridal payment, purchasing price}}, {{cog|syc|ܡܗܪܐ|t=bride-price}}, [[w:Nabataean|Nabataean]] {{l|arc|𐢓𐢇𐢛|tr=mohar}}. Uncertain connection to highly productive {{noncog|akk|maḫārum|𒈠𒄩𒀸|tr=maḫārum|t=to face or meet; to accept, to receive; to conduct; to do business, to shift commodities, to transact; to accept valuables, staples, or persons; to take in or collect offers, to take in women by dowries}} and {{noncog|sqt|móḥor|t=to offer}}, as the sound change complicates the semantic overlaps. Comparison to {{sl|ar|pal||mtr'|ts=mihr|t=contract, bond|notext=1}} is fundamentally coincidental.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u,a.pass.vn:مَهْر}}

# to [[settle]] a [[dowry]] for (one's [[wife]], etc.)

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u,a.pass.vn:مَهْر}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مَهْر|m|pl=مُهُور}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|مَهَرَ|form=I}}
# [[dowry]], [[dower]], [[marriage portion]]
# [[price]]
# [[contracting]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَهْر|pl=مُهُور}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|afb|مهر|tr=mahar|t=dowry}}
* {{desc|axm|մահր|bor=1}}
* {{desc|en|mahr|bor=1}}
* {{desc|sw|mahari|bor=1}}

===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|ar|sealstuff}}
