=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مَهْر|pl=مُهُور}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|مُهْرَدَار}}
* {{l|ar|مُهْرَق}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|ar|skillstuff}}
From {{der|ar|sem-pro|*mahir-|t=}}/{{m|sem-pro|*marw-|t=(young) man; still fast and physically useful}}, possibly further {{der|ar|afa-pro|*ma(hi)r-|t=servant, slave}}, potentially related to {{noncog|ar|مَرْء|}}. Compare {{cog|akk|mārum|𒌉|tr=mārum|t=young man, son; subordinate, deployable man, service man, usable worker, hireling for a service}}, {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎅𐎗|tr=|t=warrior, man, troop; skilled, expert, trained; exceptional, faster, better, or heroic}}, {{cog|xsa|𐩩𐩣𐩠𐩧𐩩|tr=tmhrt|t=contingent of Bedouin mercenaries; specialty troops, proficient at handling camels and desert warfare}}, {{cog|arc|מהר}}, {{cog|he|מָהִיר|}}, {{cog|he|מַהֵר}}, {{cog|phn|𐤌𐤄𐤓}}, {{cog|syc|ܡܗܪ|tr=|t=to instruct, to be instructed, to learn, to excel}}, {{cog|gez|ምሁረ|tr=|ts=məhur|t=trained}}.

