Page 18767 ميناء: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Joseph Vernet-Carpentras-Le Calme.jpg|thumb|right|{{l-self|ar|مِينَاء|tr=-}}|upright=1.25]]

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|مِينَاء}}

===Etymology 1===
The form is a {{m|ar||مِفْعال}} from the verb {{m|ar|أَنَى|t=to draw near}}. Nevertheless, it is predominantly considered a loanword. Perhaps from {{der|ar|egy|mjnwt|t=harbor}} or {{m|egy|mjnt|t=mooring post}}, related to {{der|ar|egy|mjnj|t=to moor}}.<ref>{{cite-book|last=Budge|first=E. A. Wallis|year=1920|entryurl=https://archive.org/details/egyptianhierogly01budguoft|title=An Egyptian Hieroglyphic Dictionary|location=London|publisher=J. Murray|page=300|entry=menȧ}}, meaning to tie a boat to land.</ref><ref>{{R:ar:Lane|page=3061}}, suggesting it is an ancient Egyptian word in origin.</ref> Alternatively from {{der|ar|grc|λιμήν|t=harbour}}, whence also {{cog|he|נמל|tr=nāmēl}}, with ''l-'' reinterpreted as the Arabic article.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|مِينَة}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِينَاء|m|pl=مَوَانِئ|pl2=مَوَانٍ}}

# [[port]], [[harbor]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِينَاء|pl=مَوَانِئ|pl2=مَوَانٍ}}

===Etymology 2===

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|مِينَاء|m|pl=مَوَانِئ}}

# {{alt form|ar|مِينَا|nocap=1}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|مِينَاء|pl=مَوَانِئ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Haywood}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|ميناء}}
<references/>

{{C|ar|Bodies of water}}

