Page 18822 ن ش ب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Derived from the {{der|ar|arc|-}} borrowing {{m|ar|نُشْبَة|t=snare}}, for which reason {{m|ar|نُشْبَة}} was retained as a verbal noun of the denominal base stem. Then from its meanings of “sticking” a figurative sense of “meddling, entangling” into an affair developed, lastly this was transferred to the current most common sense of a matter getting hot and breaking out. A side sense development rather emphasized gathering things, until {{m|ar|نَشَب}} meant “wealth, property, fortune” (rather than because one sticks to it), hence another base stem “to yield, to produce”.

{{m|ar|نُشَّاب}}, {{m|ar|نُشَاب|t=arrow}} is a separate borrowing from Aramaic, from which the {{ar-occupational noun|nocat=1|lc=1}} {{m|ar|نَشَّاب|t=archer}} was formed.

===Root===
{{ar-root|ن|ش|ب}}

