===Etymology===
The meaning of “riving” is original, reconstructible for {{inh|ar|sem-wes-pro|-}}, whence meanings of landforms have developed, then in Arabic specifically crevasses filled with water encountered by desert-dwellers. The meanings of vociferation are separate, paralleling {{m|ar|نَقَّ|t=to croak}}, {{m|ar|نَعَقَ|t=to caw, to bleat, to croak, to hoot}}, {{m|ar|قَعْقَعَ|t=to clatter}}.

