Page 18893 ناب: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ن و ب}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u.vn:نَوْب,مَنَاب,نِيَابَة}}

# to [[replace]], to [[substitute]] {{+obj|ar|:عَن}}
# to act [[on behalf of]], to [[represent]] {{+obj|ar|:عَن}}
# to [[nod]] [[assent]] to, to [[agree]] with, to [[turn]] [[towards]] {{+obj|ar|:إِلَى}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u.vn:نَوْب,مَنَاب,نِيَابَة}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{der|ar|arc|ניב|tr=nīḇ|t=fang, tusk; pincer}} unless otherwise a {{der|ar|sem-pro|-}} development, potentially an extension from {{der|ar|akk|𒉏𒋭|tr=nūbtu|t=honeybee; stringers}}, hence sharp things that pierce in and do not release like a predator's use of canine teeth. The sense "aged female camel" makes reference to the length of the female camel's permanent canine teeth, which begin to emerge around 7 years of age. It belongs morphologically to the root {{ar-root|ن ي ب}}, with connections to {{m|ar|نُوب|t=bees}}, {{cog|uga|𐎐𐎁𐎚|t=honey}}, {{cog|phn|𐤍𐤐𐤕|t=virgin honey}}, {{cog|gez|ንህብ|tr=|t=bee, drone}}, and {{cog|shv|nibbet|t=bee, wasp, stinging insect}}.

====Noun====
{{wikipedia|lang=ar|ناب خارجي|mul=ناب داخلي}}
{{ar-noun|نَاب|m|pl=أَنْيَاب|pl2=نُيُوب|pl3=أَنَايِيب|pl4=أَنْيُب}}

# [[fang]], [[tusk]]
#* '''10th century''', {{w|Al-Mutanabbi}}
#*: {{quote|ar|[[إذا|إِذَا]] [[رأى|رَأَيْتَ]] '''نُيُوبَ''' [[ليث|ٱللَّيْثِ]] [[بارز|بَارِزَةً]] <br> فَلَا [[ظن|تَظُنَّنَّ]] [[أن|أَنَّ]] [[ليث|ٱللَّيْثَ]] [[ابتسم|يَبْتَسِمُ]]|subst=فَلَا/فَ-لَا|If you see the lion’s fangs jut out,<br> you are not supposed to believe that the lion smiles!}}
# [[canine tooth]]
# [[large]] [[teeth]], [[long]] [[thick]] teeth

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَاب|m|pl=أَنْيَاب|pl2=نُيُوب|pl3=أَنَايِيب|pl4=أَنْيُب}}

