Page 18905 ناجود: -------- begin text --------
[[File:Early Byzantium, Constantinople or Syria, Byzantine period, 6th-7th Century - Chalice from the Beth Misona Treasure - 1950.379 - Cleveland Museum of Art.tif|thumb|right|{{lang|ar|نَاجُود}}|upright=1.15]]

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|syc|ܢܳܓܘܽܕܳܐ|tr=nāḡūḏā}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَاجُود}} {{q|singular}}
* {{ar-IPA|نَوَاجِيد}} {{q|plural}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَاجُود|m|pl=نَوَاجِيد}}

# a [[vessel]] for [[hold]]ing [[wine]]
#* {{ante|625}}, {{w|Al-A'sha|{{l|ar||اَلأَعْشَى}}}}
#*: {{quote|ar|وَكَأسٍ كَعَينِ الديكِ باكَرتُ حَدَّها<br/>بِفِتيانِ صِدقٍ وَالنَواقيسُ تُضرَبُ<br/>سُلافٍ كَأَنَّ الزَعفَرانَ وَعَندَما<br/>يُصَفَّقُ في ناجودِها ثُمَّ تُقطَبُ|There are stoops splendid like cock’s eyen, and I betook myself early to cross the border [into the land of the Christians]<br/>with friendly lads, where the bells are hit,<br/>where there is fore-must wine like saffron,<br/>and one clinks the '''beakers''' and then mixes the wine.|tr=wa-kaʾsin ka-ʿayni ad-dīki bākartu ḥadda-hā<br/>bi-fityāni ṣidqin wa-n-nawāqīsu tuḍrabu<br/>sulāfin ka-ʾanna az-zaʿfarāna wa-ʿindamā<br/>yuṣaffaqu fī '''nājūdi'''-hā ṯumma tuqṭabu}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|author=[[w:Abu Nuwas|Abū Nuwās]]|title=[[s:ar:طَرِبَ الشيْخُ فغنّى واصْطبحْ|{{lang|ar|طَرِبَ الشيْخُ فغنّى واصْطبحْ}}]]|year=c. 800
|passage=طَرِبَ الشيْخُ فغنّى، واصْطبحْ<br/>من عُقارٍ تُنهبُ الهمّ الفَرَحْ<br/>أخَذتْ من كلّ شيءٍ لَوْنَهــا،<br/>هي في ناجودها قوْسُ قُزَحْ<br/>شيْخُ لذّاتٍ، نقِيٌّ عِرْضُهُ،<br/>تحْسُنُ الأشعارُ فيه، والمِدَحْ.<br/>لا تراهُ الدّهْرُ إلاّ ثَمِلاً،<br/>بينَ إبْريقٍ، وزِقٍّ، وقدَحْ
|translation=The shaykh gleed and sang and craved more booze<br/>forthy delight removes the sorrow.<br/>He obtained from every thing its hues<br/>and his '''cup''' exposed a rainbow.<br/>Shaykh of bliss, no way blammed,<br/>The notes of him are merry, fele to plaud,<br/>Fate sees him not but slammed,<br/>betwixe ewer and wineskin, beaker-pawed.
|tr=ṭariba aš-šayḵu fa-ġannā, wa-iṣṭabaḥ<br/>min ʿuqārin tunhabu l-hamma l-faraḥ<br/>ʾaḵaḏat min kulli šayʾin lawna-hā<br/>hiya fī '''nājūdi'''-hā qawsu quzaḥ.<br/>šayḵu laḏḏātin, naqiyyun ʿirḍu-hū<br/>taḥsunu al-ʾašʿāru fī-hi, wa-l-midaḥ,<br/>la tarā-hu ad-dahru illā ṯamilan,<br/>bayna ʾibrīqin, wa-ziqqin, wa-qadaḥ.<br/>}}
#: {{syn|ar|بَاطِيَة}}

====Declension====
