Page 18920 نار: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
From Arabic {{ar-root|ن|و|ر}}; from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*nūr-}}. Cognate with {{cog|arc|נוּר|t=fire}}, whence the derived {{cog|he|נוּר|tr=nur|t=shining fire}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَار}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-نار.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَار|f|d=نَارَانِ|pl=نِيرَان}}

# [[fire]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|28|29|text=فَلَمَّا قَضَىٰ مُوسَى ٱلْأَجَلَ وَسَارَ بِأَهْلِهِۦۤ ءَانَسَ مِن جَانِبِ ٱلطُّورِ '''نَارࣰا''' قَالَ لِأَهْلِهِ ٱمْكُثُوۤا۟ إِنِّيۤ ءَانَسْتُ '''نَارࣰا''' لَّعَلِّيۤ ءَاتِيكُم مِّنْهَا بِخَبَرٍ أَوْ جَذْوَةࣲ مِّنَ '''ٱلنَّارِ''' لَعَلَّكُمْ تَصْطَلُونَ|tr=fa-lammā qaḍā mūsā l-ʾajala wa-sāra bi-ʾahlihī ʾānasa min jānibi ṭ-ṭūri '''nāran''' qāla li-ʾahlihi mkuṯū ʾinnī ʾānastu '''nāran''' laʿallī ʾātīkum-minhā bixabarin ʾaw jaḏwatin mina '''n-nāri''' laʿallakum taṣṯalūna|t=And when Moses had completed the term and was traveling with his family, he perceived from the direction of the mount '''a fire'''. He said to his family, "Stay here; indeed, I have perceived '''a fire'''. Perhaps I will bring you from there [some] information or burning wood from '''the fire''' that you may warm yourselves.}}
# [[conflagration]]
#* {{l|ar|النَّار}} — ''[[Hell]]''
#* {{l|ar|شَيْخ النَّار}} — ''[[Lucifer]]''
#* {{l|ar|جَبَل النَّار}} — ''[[volcano]]''
# [[gunfire]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَار|pl=نِيرَان}}

