Page 19029 نبق: -------- begin text --------
{{wikipedia|نبق|Rhamnus|mul=سدر|mullabel=Ziziphus spina-christi|lang=ar}}

===Etymology 1===
The vowel variation suggests a borrowing; it appears {{bor|ar|egy|-}} in respect of the significance of its term {{m|egy|nbs|t=Christ's thorn jujube}} and {{m|ar|سَنْط}} and {{m|ar|زَعْرُور}} being of this origin, despite the last consonant mismatch, which is perhaps caused by the addition of another Egyptian word. In {{cog|syc|-}} once {{m|syc|ܢܒܟܐ|tr=nābəḵā}} or {{m|syc|ܢܒܩܐ|tr=nābəqā}} equated by {{w|Bar Hebraeus}} with {{m|syc|ܟܢܪܐ|tr=kənārā}} and {{m|syc|ܥܙܪܪܬܐ|ܥܙܪܪܐ|tr=ʿazrārē}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|نَبَق|head2=نَبِق|head3=نَبْق|head4=نِبْق|sing=نَبَقَة|sing2=نَبِقَة|sing3=نَبْقَة|sing4=نِبْقَة}}

# ''[[Rhamnus]]'' gen. et spp.
# {{vern|Christ's thorn jujube}} ({{taxlink|Ziziphus spina-christi|species}}); its [[produce]], edible [[fruit]]s and construction [[wood]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|نَبَق|head2=نَبِق|head3=نَبْق|head4=نِبْق}}

