Page 19072 نجف: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From the root {{ar-root|ن ج ف}} originally stemming from the butting together of horns; hence the wide semantic range "to push or thrust", "to gore or stab", "to knock about", "to be pushed about".

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.vn:نَجْف}}

# to [[fashion]] a [[point]] or [[tip]]
# to [[carve]] or [[sharpen]] an [[arrow]]
# to make a [[broad]] [[spearhead]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.vn:نَجْف}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~a.vn:نِجَاف}}

# to [[bolt]] or to [[lock]] a door
# to [[barricade]], to set up a [[blockade]]
# to [[shield]] or [[block]]
# to [[push]] [[back]], to be a [[barrier]] or [[resistance]] against another thing

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~a.vn:نِجَاف}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to be [[blown]] by the [[wind]]
# to [[drift]], to be [[pushed]]
# to [[shake]], to be [[knocked about]]
# to [[push up]] into a [[heap]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|نَجَف|m|pl=نِجَاف}}

# elevated place not reached by water, [[hill]], [[dike]]
# [[embankment]], [[battlement]]
# [[dune]] especially those that [[drift]] or are [[pushed]] [[around]] or [[formed]] by the [[wind]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَجَف|pl=نِجَاف}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{m|ar|دُرّ النَجَف|tr=|t=the pearls of Najaf}}, named from the city [[w:Najaf|Najaf]], the surrounding hills of which are famed for their abundant [[quartz]] deposits.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|نَجَف|sing=نَجَفَة}}

# [[quartz]], [[crystal]]
# [[chandelier]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|نَجَف}}

