Page 19087 نحاس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{unc|ar}}; attested at least from the Amarna period in {{der|ar|sem-nwe|-}}; compare {{cog|phn|𐤍𐤇𐤔|tr=}}, {{cog|he|נחושת|נְחֹשֶׁת|tr=n'khóshet|t=copper}}, {{cog|gez|ናሕስ}}, {{cog|arc|נחשׁ|tr=|t=copper, bronze}}, and {{w|Nehushtan}}:
* From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*naḥaš-|t=snake, reptile; divination, incantations; to learn secret things}}, such a sense derived from hissing equated to whispers. The process of extracting ore and the ability to shape metal was considered connected to arcane arts in most early societies; alternatively from the use of copper, bronze, and brass bowls in commonly practiced [[hydromancy]] or in offering libations to spirits.
* From {{ar-root|ن ح س}}, connected with misfortune and difficulty, including great association with smoke, fire, and intense heat or burning; by extension the conditions of metallurgy. See also [[w:Metal fume fever|brass founders' ague, the brass shakes]] especially associated with this metal.
* Possibly from a semantic shift of {{der|ar|akk|annakum|𒀭𒈾|tr=annakum|t=tin|}}, from {{der|ar|sux|𒀭𒈾|tr=an-na|ts=anna, nagga|t=tin|}}, as most ancient languages conflate the terms for copper and bronze, bronze being an alloy of tin and copper. In this case a {{doublet|ar|آنُك|nocap=1}}.
* Possibly related to {{cog|akk|tenšu|𒋼𒂗𒋙𒌑|tr=tenšu|t=metal ornament, a metal inlay|}}, likely borrowed from {{cog|arc|-}}; less likely related to {{cog|akk|aḫuš'u|𒀀𒄭𒄊𒌋|tr=aḫuš'u|t=poetic name for copper}}, ultimately from a {{der|ar|sux|-}} loan.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نُحَاس}}
** {{IPA|ary|/nħaːs/|a=Moroccan}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نُحَاس|m}}

# {{lb|ar|uncountable}} [[copper]]
#: {{ux|ar|قِدْر نُحَاس|copper pot|inline=t}}
# [[alloy|alloys]] of [[copper]]; [[bronze]], [[brass]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نُحَاس}}

{{C|ar|Chemical elements}}

-------- end text --------
