Page 19099 نحن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*niḥnu}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|אנחנו}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|نَحْنُ}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-نحن.ogg}}

====Pronoun====
{{ar-pron|نَحْنُ|m-p|g2=f-p}} (''enclitic form'' {{m|ar|ـنَا}})

# [[we]] (''subject pronoun'')

=====Usage notes=====
As Arabic does not use dual forms in the first person, {{m|ar|نَحْنُ}} is used in cases where there are two people involved in addition to the usual three or more required for plural number.

=====See also=====
{{ar-personal pronouns}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|نحن}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb form|حنا<I.pass>|حنى<I.pass>}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Wehr-4|نحن}}

-------- end text --------
Page 19100 نحو: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ن ح و}}
The "grammar" sense, according to a report, is derived from [[w:Ali|ʿAlī]] telling [[w:Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali|ʾAbu al-ʾAswad ad-Duʾali]], who is believed to be the first Arabic grammarian: {{l|ar|«[[مَا]] [[أَحْسَنَ]] [[هٰذَا]] النَّحْوَ [[الَّذِي]] [[نحا|نَحَوْتَ]]»|t=How wonderful this direction (naḥw) that you have followed is}}<ref>[[w:ar:سير أعلام النبلاء|سير أعلام النبلاء]], Volume 4, Page 82</ref>  after he showed ʿAlī the grammar he had organized.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|نَحْو|m|pl=نُحُوّ|pl2=أَنْحَاء}}

# [[side]], [[direction]]
# [[region]], [[tract]]
# [[road]]
# [[intention]], [[purpose]], [[tendency]]
# [[kind]], [[sort]], [[manner]]
# {{lb|ar|linguistics|grammar}} [[syntax]], [[grammar]]
#* Ibn Malik, [[w:en:Alfiya|Alfiyyah]]
#*: {{quote|ar|وَأَسْتَعِينُ اللَّٰهَ فِي أَلْفِيَّةْ / مَقَاصِدُ '''النَّحْوِ''' بِهَا مَحْوِيَّةْ|subst=أَلْفِيَّةْ/أَلْفِيَّهْ,مَحْوِيَّةْ/مَحْوِيَّهْ}}

=====Declension=====
