Page 19142 نذر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ن ذ ر}}
Akin to {{sl|ar|arc|נִדְרָא|tr=niḏrā|notext=1}}, {{sl|ar|syc|ܢܕܪܐ|tr=neḏrā|notext=1}}, {{sl|ar|he|נֶדֶר|tr=néḏer|notext=1}}, {{cog|xpu|𐤍𐤃𐤓}} and {{cog|uga|𐎐𐎄𐎗}}. It is argued that the sense {{m|en|vow}} is influenced from Jewish and Christian usage in Aramaic and Hebrew, the sense of “warning” as in {{m|ar|أَنْذَرَ}} and its verbal noun {{m|ar|نُذُر}} being more particular to Arabic, so the original meaning of the base stem needs to have been “to take heed”.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~u,i.pass.vn:نَذْر,نُذُور}}

# to [[vow]], to [[pledge]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|19|26
|passage=إِنِّي نَذَرْتُ لِلرَّحْمَٰنِ صَوْمًا فَلَنْ أُكَلِّمَ الْيَوْمَ إِنسِيًّا
|translation=Lo! I have vowed a fast unto the Beneficent, and may not speak today to any mortal.}}
# to [[devote]] one's [[son]] to the [[service]] of [[God]]
# to [[place]] [[in front of]] a [[combat]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~u,i.pass.vn:نَذْر,نُذُور}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.ipass?.vn:نَذَر}}

# to [[see]] the [[danger]], to [[see]] through the [[intentions]] of an [[enemy]] and be [[on one's guard]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.ipass?.vn:نَذَر}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# to [[make]] a [[vow]] to, [[profess]] [[before]], [[profess]] a [[belief]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|نَذْر|m|pl=نُذُور|pl2=نُذُر}}

# {{ar-verbal noun of|نَذَرَ|form=I||to [[vow]], to [[warn]]}}
## [[vow]]
### anything [[consecrated]] to [[God]]
#### [[pious]] [[gift]]
##### [[present]] to [[superiors]]
##### [[mulct]] for [[wounds]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَذْر|pl=نُذُور|pl2=نُذُر}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|fa|نذر|tr=nazr|bor=1}}
