Page 19164 نزلة: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ن ز ل}}

===Etymology===
Corresponding to {{m|ar|نَزَلَ|t=to come down, to settle}} in reference to the phlegm in the course of a respiratory disease. Borrowing from unattested {{bor|ar|syc|ܢܸܙܠܬ݂ܵܐ|tr=nezləṯā|t=*catarrh, snot}}, attested in {{cog|aii|-}} in the sense of “pus” even as well as “snot”, is likely, given that {{m|arc|נזל}} / {{m|syc|ܢܙܲܠ|tr=nzal}} is a transitive verb specifically referring to flowing or shaking movements.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَزْلَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَزْلَة|f|pl=نَزَلَات}}

# {{ar-instance noun of|نَزَلَ}}, stopping, landing
# [[cold]], [[catarrh]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَزْلَة|pl=نَزَلَات}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|he|נַזֶּלֶת|tr=nazélet|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|axm|նազլայ|նուզլայ}}
* {{desctree|ota|نزله|tr=nezle|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ur|نزلہ|tr=nazla|bor=1}}

