Page 19191 نسر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ar|sem-wes-pro|*našr-}}, whence was derived the denominal root {{ar-root|ن|س|ر}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|نَسْر|m|pl=نُسُور|pl2=نُسُورَة}}

# {{lb|ar|zoology}} a [[vulture]]
# {{lb|ar|proscribed|dialectal}} an [[eagle]]
#: {{syn|ar|عُقَاب}}

=====Usage notes=====
The word is commonly used to refer to eagles, especially in the dialects. This use, however, is almost unanimously criticized by prescriptivists, who maintain that {{m|ar|عُقَاب}} should be used instead.

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَسْر|pl=نُسُور|pl2=نُسُورَة}}

