Page 19217 نشاب: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ن ش ب}}

===Etymology===
[[Appendix:Aramaic terms only attested in borrowings|Unattested]] {{bor|ar|arc|-}} term; the needed form is only attested in {{cog|syc|ܢܫܒܐ|tr=nəšāḇā}} as “blowing; storm”, however the {{w|Aramaic#Conjugations or verbal stems|ʔap̄ʕel form}} (= {{ar-form|IV|nocap=1}}) of the verb within the root means “to blow away, to let fly”. In the Middle Ages already the distinction between weapons and their projectiles became loose, hence later the meaning of a {{w|History of crossbows|crossbow}} has come to prevail in some dialects.

===Noun===
{{ar-coll-noun|نُشَّاب|head2=نَشَّاب|head3=نُشَاب|m|sing=نُشَّابَة|sing2=نَشَّابَة|sing3=نُشَابَة|pl=نَشَاشِيب}}

# [[arrow]] {{gloss|particularly of a large kind}}
# [[crossbow]], [[latch]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|نُشَّاب|head2=نَشَّاب|pl=نَشَاشِيب}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَشَّاب|m|pl=نَشَّابُون}}

# [[archer]]
#: {{syn|ar|قَوّاس}}
# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} [[arrowmaker]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَشَّاب|pl=smp}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:CAL|n%24b|V}}
* {{R:CAL|n%24b%233|N}}
* {{R:CAL|n%24b|N}}
* {{R:xaa:ELA|II|pages=1261–1262}}, where the whole root is affirmed to be loaned from Aramaic, though the explanation of this individual word not given
* {{R:ar:Huuri:1941|page=96}}, relates the interchangeability of weapon and projectile terms

{{C|ar|Archery}}

