Page 19247 نصراني: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|نَصْرَان|نَصْرِي||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
{{ar-etym-nisba-linking|[[الناصرة|نَاصِرَة]]||َان}}, based on a modified form of {{m|ar|النَّاصِرَة||[[Nazareth]]}}. Compare {{cog|he|נוֹצְרִי|tr=nots'rí}} and {{cog|syc|ܢܵܨܪܵܝܵܐ|tr=nāṣrāyā}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَصْرَانِيّ}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-nisba|نَصْرَانِيّ|pl=نَصَارَى|fpl=نَصْرَانِيَّات|fpl2=نَصَارَى}}

# [[Christian]]
#: {{syn|ar|مَسِيحِيّ}}
# {{lb|ar|rare|or|obsolete}} [[Nazarene]]
#: {{syn|ar|نَاصِرِيّ}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|نَصْرَانِيّ|cpl=نَصَارَى|fpl=sfp}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun-nisba|نَصْرَانِيّ|pl=نَصَارَى}}

#  a [[Christian]]
#: {{syn|ar|مَسِيحِيّ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|3|67|passage=مَا كَانَ إِبْرَاهِيمُ يَهُودِيًّا وَلَا '''نَصْرَانِيًّا''' وَلَٰكِنْ كَانَ حَنِيفًا مُسْلِمًا|t=Neither was Abraham a Jew nor '''a Christian''' but rather he was an upright Muslim}}
# {{lb|ar|rare|or|obsolete}} a [[Nazarene]]
#: {{syn|ar|نَاصِرِيّ}}
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=1992|author=w:Biblica|title=New Arabic Version [Kitab El Hayat] (NAV)|url=|page=|text=وَجَدْنَا هَذَا الْمُتَّهَمَ مُخَرِّباً، يُثِيرُ الْفِتْنَةَ بَيْنَ جَمِيعِ الْيَهُودِ فِي الْبِلادِ كُلِّهَا، وَهُوَ يَتَزَعَّمُ مَذْهَبَ ال'''نَّصَارَى'''|section=[[w:Acts of the Apostles|Acts]] [https://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Acts+24%3A5&version=NAV 24:5]|t=We found this accused man to be a saboteur, stirring up discord among all the Jews in the entire land. He spearheads the sect of the '''Nazarenes'''.}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-gendered-noun|نَصْرَانِيّ|cpl=نَصَارَى|fpl=sfp}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|نَصْرَانِيَّة|t=Christianity}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|نَصَّرَ|t=to [[Christianize]]}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|arz|نصراني|tr=naṣrāni}}
* {{desc|mt|Nisrani}}
* {{desc|ary|نصراني|tr=naṣrāni}}
* {{desc|ajp|نصراني|tr=naṣrāni}}
* {{desc|gur|nasaara|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ms|Nasrani|Serani|bor=1}}
** {{desc|id|Nasrani|Serani|}}
* {{desc|ml|നസ്രാണി|bor=1}}
* {{desc|mos|nasaara|bor=1}}
* {{desc|tr|Nasrani|bor=1}}

===Usage notes===
* Although the word and its nominal derivative, {{m|ar|نَصْرَانِيَّة|t=Christianity}}, are occasionally found in the works of some medieval Christian writers who composed in Classical Arabic, such as {{w|Ibn al-Tayyib|Ibn al-Ṭayyib}} and {{w|Ibn al-Khammar|Ibn al-Ḵammār}}, it is now almost never used as a self-designation by Arabic-speaking Christians and is widely considered [[politically incorrect]] or outright offensive and derogatory, at least in countries with relevant Christian populations. Since {{m|ar||نَصْرَانِيّ}} is the word used for “Christian” in the [[Quran]] and has been the primary designation for Christians in virtually all Islamic texts for centuries, it intends heavy religious connotations and thus still retains currency in Islamic religious discourse, but even there {{l|ar|مَسِيحِيّ}} may sometimes be used.

===References===
* {{R:ar:Ahrens-Christliches|page=25}}
* {{R:ar:Lane}}

{{C|ar|Christianity}}

