Page 19258 نصيري: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-etym-nisba|[[w:ar:محمد بن نصير|مُحَمَّد بِن نُصَيْر]]|[[w:Ibn Nusayr|Muhammad ibn Nusayr]]}}.

===Adjective===
{{ar-nisba|نُصَيْرِيّ}}

# {{lb|ar|obsolete}} an [[Alawite]], a member of a syncretic [[Shia]] sect concentrated in [[Latakia]] and [[Tartus]] governorates in [[Syria]]
# {{lb|ar|Islam|religious slur}} a [[Nusayri]], an [[Alawite]]

====Usage notes====
In 1920s the term {{l|ar|عَلَوِيّ}} became more common for self-identification among Alawites. Now the word "Nusayri" is used only by the critics of the sect, especially by groups like the [[w:Islamic State of Iraq and the Levant|Islamic State]] or [[w:Jabhat an-Nusra|Jabhat an-Nusra]] during the [[w:Syrian Civil war|Syrian Civil war]].

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|نُصَيْرِيّ|pl=sp}}
