Page 19313 نعش: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1.1===
Seemingly a {{bor|ar|ira-mid}} borrowing equivalent to {{cog|fa|لاش|tr=lâš}}. Prefixation to {{ar-root|ع ي ش|nocat=1}} as in {{m|ar|نَوْرَج}} is also considered. The verbs in the root {{ar-root|ن ع ش}} are denominal in any case.

====Alternative forms====
* {{alter|ar|نَعَش|نَعَاش||al-Andalus|proscribed}}, ''plurals there also {{m|ar|أَنْعَاش}} and {{m|ar|أَنْعِشَة}}''

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|نَعْش|m|pl=نُعُوش}}

# [[corpse]] (human)
# [[bier]], [[stretcher]]
#* {{R:ar:FAH|6II|page=290 Nr. 309|passage=ويقولون للّذي يُحْمَلُ عليه الميّت النَّعَاشُ. والصّواب النَّعْشُ. قال الشّاعر:<br/>أَمَحْمُولٌ عَلَى النَّعْشِ الهُمَامُ|t=Them man say for that on which one is carried dead ''naʕāš''. The right is ''naʕš''. A poet ({{w|Al-Nabigha|al-Nābiḡa aḏ-Ḏubyāni}}) [https://www.aldiwan.net/poem1968.html said]:<br/>I am carried high on the bier.}}

=====Declension=====
