Page 19335 نغمة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Together with {{m|ar|نَغْم}} of similar meaning, if this is not just the [[verbal noun]] of {{ar-form|I|nocap=1}}, borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|ܢܶܥܡܐ|tr=neʿmā}}, {{m|arc|נעמתה}} / {{m|arc|ܢܶܥܡܬ݂ܳܐ|tr=neʿmṯā}}, reinterpreted after the [http://cal.huc.edu/oneentry.php?lemma=n%28m%20V&cits=all root] cognate to the Arabic {{ar-root|ن ع م|nocat=1}} from {{der|ar|grc|νεῦμα}}, mixed with {{m|grc|πνεῦμα}}, assuming the musical meanings of the [[neume]] term aren’t a loan from {{cog|sem|-}} into Greek.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَغْمَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَغْمَة|f|pl=أَنْغَام|pl2=أَنَاغِيم|pl3=نَغَمَات}}

# [[melody]], [[tone]], [[sound]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَغْمَةٌ|pl=أَنْغَامٌ|pl2=أَنَاغِيمُ|pl3=نَغَمَات}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|نَغَمَ}} and {{l|ar|نَغِمَ|t=to hum, to recite in a modulating voice}}
* {{l|ar|نَغَّمَ|t=to recite melodiously}}
* {{l|ar|نَاغِمَ|t=to speak softly to}}
* {{l|ar|تَنَغَّمَ|t=to recite melodiously}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|az|nəğmə|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ky|наама|bor=1}}
* {{desc|ota|نغمه|tr=nağme|bor=1}}
** {{desc|tr|nağme}}
* {{desctree|fa|نغمه|bor=1|tr=nağme}}
* {{desc|tk|nagma|bor=1}}
* {{desc|uz|nagʻma|bor=1}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Almaany}}
* {{R:ar:Freytag|volume=4|page=306a–b}}
* {{R:arc:Löw:1911|page=190–193, Nr. 5}}, but there Imm. Löw and {{w|Theodor Nöldeke}} opine that the Arabic word is genuine, presumably because of skepticism about {{m+|ar|غ}} reflecting Aramaic {{m|arc|ע}} / {{m|arc|ܥ|tr=ʿ}}, but Wiktionary has not few other examples in its lists of [[:Category:Arabic terms derived from Aramaic|Aramaisms]] or [[:Category:Arabic terms derived from Classical Syriac|Syriacisms]] in Arabic, and the acquaintance with {{w|lang=de|Graeco-Arabica}} has also [[w:Graeco-Arabic translation movement|widened]].
* {{R:ar:Kazimirski|volume=2|page=1302–1303}}
* {{R:CAL|n(m%232|V}}
