Page 19423 نكح: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|ن ك ح}}

===Verb===
{{ar-verb|I/a~i,a.pass.vn:نِكَاح,نَكْح}}

# to [[marry]]
#: {{syn|ar|تَزَوَّجَ}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|230
|passage=فَإِن طَلَّقَهَا فَلَا تَحِلُّ لَهُ مِن بَعْدُ حَتَّى '''تَنْكِحَ''' زَوْجًا غَيْرَهُ ۗ فَإِن طَلَّقَهَا فَلَا جُنَاحَ عَلَيْهِمَا أَن يَتَرَاجَعَا إِن ظَنَّا أَن يُقِيمَا حُدُودَ ٱللَّهِ ۗ وَتِلْكَ حُدُودُ ٱللَّهِ يُبَيِّنُهَا لِقَوْمٍ يَعْلَمُونَ
|translation=And if he has divorced her, then she is not lawful to him afterward until she '''marries''' a husband other than him. And if the latter husband divorces her, there is no blame upon the woman and her former husband for returning to each other if they think that they can keep the limits of God. These are the limits of God, which He makes clear to a people who know.
|subst=غَيْرَهُ ۗ/غَيْرَهُ؛,ٱللَّهِ ۗ/لَّهِ؛,ٱللَّهِ/لَّهِ,فَ/فَ-,وَتِلْكَ/وَ-تِلْكَ,لِقَوْمٍ/لِ-قَوْمٍ}}
# {{lb|ar|vulgar}} to [[have sex]] with

====Usage notes====
* The sense “to marry” is standard in Islamic religious discourse and hence sometimes in legal contexts. Otherwise {{m|ar|تَزَوَّجَ}} is by far the predominant word in Modern Standard Arabic and {{m|ar||نَكَحَ}} should be used with caution because in most vernaculars it has become a vulgar word ({{m|en||to fuck}}).

====Conjugation====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i,a.pass.vn:نِكَاح,نَكْح}}

{{C|ar|Marriage|Sex}}
