Page 19447 نمط: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|נַמְטָא}} / {{m|syc|ܢܡܛܐ|tr=namṭā}}, from {{bor|ar|pal|tr=nmt'|ts=namad|t=felt, fibers}}, from {{der|ar|ira-pro|*namatā-|t=cloth made of hairs}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَمَط}} {{q|noun}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-نمط.ogg}} {{q|noun}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَمَط|m|pl=أَنْمَاط|pl2=نِمَاط|pl3=أَنْمِطَة}}

# {{lb|ar|archaic|if not dialectal}} [[drugget]], a type of [[rug]] also laid over a [[saddle]]
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 869|authorlink=al-Jahiz|author=ar:الْجَاحِظ|title=ar:التَبَصُّر بِٱلتِّجَارَة|chapter=ar:باب ما يُجلب من البلدان من طرائف السلع والأمتعة والجواري والأحجار وغير ذلك<t:What one imports from strange countries in items, commodities, she-slaves, stones and else.>|url=https://www.hindawi.org/books/73505194/4/|passage=ومن مَيْسَان: ال'''أَنْماط''' والوسائد.|t=From {{w|Maysan}} one gets '''druggets''' and cushions.}}
#* {{R:ar:Goeje|M|instead=1|lang=ar|page=380 line 8–10|section=web [http://islamport.com/w/bld/Web/451/139.htm 1/139]|passage=ولا نظير لتككهم ومحفوريَّاتهم وقرمزهم و'''أنماط'''هم وصبغهم وفاكهة تسمَّى الزُّوقال وقسبويه وسمك يقال له الطِرِّيخ ولهم تين وشاه بلُّوط في غاية الجودة.|t=There is nothing resembling their waistbands, their streaked rugs, their crimson, their '''druggets''', their dyes, and the fruit called cornel, and their dentexes, and their fish called pearl mullet. And they have figs and chestnuts of finest quality.}}
# [[pattern]], [[type]], [[style]], [[manner]], [[mode]], [[wise]]
#: {{syn|ar|شَاكِلَة}}
# [[routine]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَمَط|pl=أَنْمَاط|pl2=نِمَاط|pl3=أَنْمِطَة}}

