===Etymology 2===
From the root {{ar-root|ن و ر}} whence {{m|ar|نَار|t=fire}}, because quicklime, [[calcium oxide]], also known as {{m|en|burnt lime}}, and {{m|ar|حِجَارَة مَشْوِيَّة|tr=ḥijāra mašwiyya|lit=burnt stones}}, is produced by [[thermolysis]] of [[calcium]]-rich material.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|نُورَة|f}}

# [[quick lime]], [[plaster]], a [[substance]] used for [[mend]]ing, [[mixed]] [[lime-stone]] and [[clay]] and [[straw]] used for [[repair]]ing, [[parget]], [[plaster]] applied on the inside and outside walls of a house
#* {{RQ:Awwam|33|volume=2|page=601|passage=يؤخذ طرخشقون مجفف وعدس ونورة أجزاء سواء ويسحق الجميع وينخل ويعجن بسمن بقري عتيق ثم يوضع منه على فتيلة ويدخل في الناصور نافع وربما نفع وربما نفع منه الكي بالنار.|translation=One takes dried dandelion and lentils and lime at equal parts and grinds all and sieves and kneads with old cow butter and then one applies from it unto a wick and enters the fistula. It may be successful, however cauterization might prove more effective.}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|نُورَة}}

=====Descendants=====
* {{desc|am|ኖራ|bor=1}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|نُورَة|f}}

# {{given name|ar|female}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|نُورَة:di|state=ind-def}}

