Page 19499 نورس: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
{{unk|ar}}. Potentially borrowed from {{cog|fa|مرغ نوروزی|lit=bird of Nowruz or New Years|tr=morğ nowruzi}}, but as the apparent connection to Nowruz is unknown, the later term may itself be borrowed from Arabic.

Possibly related to {{cog|la|larus}}, derived from {{cog|grc|λάρος|t=ravenous sea bird; potentially seamew, gull}}. What complicates such an immediate identification is the lack of intermediate borrowings in other Semitic or regional languages, sources such as {{m+|syc|-}} or {{m+|pal|-}}. The initial sound change is plausible, with the occasional conflation of /l/ and /n/ in other Arabic words, especially those featuring both /l/ and /r/, which typically do not appear together in a native Arabic root; compare {{m|ar|وَرَل}}, {{m|ar|وَرَن|t=monitor lizard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|نَوْرَس}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|نَوْرَس|m|pl=نَوَارِس}}

# [[gull]], [[seagull]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|نَوْرَس|pl=نَوَارِس}}

{{C|ar|Seabirds}}

