Page 19598 ه و ي: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Cognate to the {{cog|arc|-}} root {{m|arc|ה־ו־י}} / {{syc-root-entry|ܗ|ܘ|ܝ}} meaning “to be”, “to happen”, “to come down”; {{cog|he|היה}}. Cognate with {{cog|akk|𒂊𒈬𒌑|ts=emû}}, {{cog|akk|𒋾|ts=ewû|t=to turn, to become}}, in Arabic developing as “to pitch downward”, “to turn towards a thing”, “to desire or to want to go to a thing” ({{cog|uga|𐎅𐎆𐎊|t=to want}}); “to come down or to tumble towards”, “to extend towards”, hence {{m|ar|هَوَاء}} air. Present with {{cog|sem-pro|*ša-}} causative prefix in the root {{ar-root|س و ي|nocat=1}} “related to things becoming equal”, {{m|arc|ש־ו־י}} / {{syc-root-entry|ܫ|ܘ|ܝ}}, {{cog|akk|𒍜𒉈𒅗|ts=šūmû}}, {{m|akk|𒋗𒉿𒄿|ts=šūwû|t=to make turn}}. Hence there has existed in Proto-Semitic a verb {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*haway-|t=to be, to become}} and (later elided) {{cog|sem-pro|*šahway-|t=to cause to be, to make come, to level onto}}. Sometimes proposed to be from a form such as {{inh|ar|afa-pro|*hVy/*hVw-}}, in which case it would be related to {{cog|egy|hꜣj|t=to fall, to descend}} and {{cog|irk|huu’|t=fall, drop}}.

===Root===
{{ar-root|ه و ي}}

# related to air, passion and their manifestations

====Derived terms====
''Verbs and verbal derivatives''
* '''[[Appendix:Arabic_verbs#Form_I|Form I]]''': {{l|ar|هَوِيَ|t=to be fond, to love or fall in love}}, {{l|ar|يَهْوَى}}
