Page 19599 ه ي ء: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Apparently denominal from {{m|ar|هَيْئَة}}, compare {{m|ar|طَرْز}} for an equal development. The ''Dictionnaire du faisceau dialectal arabe andalou'' suggests an {{bor|ar|sem-srb|-}} borrowing, in view of {{cog|xsa|𐩠𐩺𐩲|ts=hayaʿa|t=to flow, to run; to extend ''(boundary)''; to carry out, to implement or accomplish ''(construction)''}}, which is indeed with a voiced pharyngeal fricative instead of a voiceless glottal plosive here and in derivations, and possibly related to {{ar-root|ش ي ع|nocat=1}} related to spreading.

===Root===
{{ar-root|ه|ي|ء}}

# forms words related to [[shapes]], [[shaping]] and [[comeliness]]

====Derived terms====
; Verbs and verbal derivatives
{{ar-verb forms
|a|I=to be beautifully shaped|I-pp=-
|I2-pv=u|I2=to be beautifully shaped|I2-pp=-
|I-vn-head=هَيْئَة|I2-vn-head=هَيَاءَة
|II=to set, arrange, array|II-vn-head=تَهْيِيء,تَهْيِئَة
|III=to adapt, convene, conform
|V=to be [[ready]], to be [[possible]], to be properly dressed|V-vn=[[preparation]], [[team]]|V-pp=-
}}

; Nouns and adjectives
* {{l|ar|هَيِّئ||properly shaped, [[beautiful]]}}
** {{l|ar|هَيْئَة||[[shape]], [[aspect]], [[body]], [[organization]]}}
* {{l|ar|مُهَيَّأ||[[ready]], [[prepared]]}}

