===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|هِرْشَفَّة|هِرْشَبّة|قِرْشَبَّة|قِرْشَبّ|كِرْشَبّ}}

===Etymology===
Applying the pattern {{m|ar||فِعْلَلّ}} to multiple {{unc|ar|nocap=1|title=unclear}} words, including in some forms at least {{m|ar|كِرْش|t=paunch}} and perhaps {{m|ar|حَشَف|t=the worst kind of dates that dry up without ripening so that they have no flesh}}, with later augment ({{m|ar|إِلْحَاق}}) of {{m|ar|ر}} for dissimilation ({{m|ar|إِدْغَام}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|هِرْشَفّ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|هِرْشَفّ|m}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# a [[rag]] or [[piece]] of [[cotton]] with which water or [[ink]] is [[dry up|dried up]]
# an old, [[gross]] and [[wrinkly]] [[woman]] or [[man]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|هِرْشَفّ}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:ar:Baalbaki:2008|page=151}}; Sibawayhi’s passage in {{w|Hartwig Derenbourg|Derenbourg}}’s edition 1885 vol. 2 [https://www.google.de/books/edition/كتاب_سيبويه/dtsH8QO8SrsC?hl=de&gbpv=1&dq=%22هرشف%22&pg=RA23-PP18&printsec=frontcover page 372] line 4.
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=2514a|قِرْشَبٌّ}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=2607b|كِرْشَبٌّ}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=2892a|هِرْشَبَّةٌ}}
* {{R:ar:Lane|page=3043a|هِرْشَفَّةٌ}}

{{C|ar|Hygiene|Age}}
