Page 19853 هوتة: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The root {{ar-root|ه و ي}} forms other words meaning pits or depressions. However, the formation is irregular in Arabic terms and the ending of consonant + {{m|ar||ـْتَة}} and the vowel variation point to {{cog|syc|ܗܘܬܐ|tr=hawṯā}}, formed with the {{bor|ar|arc|-}} feminine ending from a cognate root.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|هَوْتَة|هُوتَة}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|هَوْتَة|f|head2=هُوتَة|pl=هُوَت}}

# {{lb|ar|geography}} [[depression]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|هَوْتَة|head2=هُوتَة|pl=هُوَت}}

{{C|ar|Landforms}}

-------- end text --------
Page 19854 هود: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
Uncertain. Probably from the root {{ar-root|ه و د}}, related to returning. See {{m|ar|هاد}}. Otherwise, it might be related to {{ar-root|ه د ي}}, related to guidance. See {{m|ar|هادٍ}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|هُودْ}}

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|هُود|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} [[Hud]], a prophet of Islam, sometimes identified with [[Eber]] in the Bible
# {{lb|ar|Islam}} [[Hud]], the eleventh [[sura]] of the [[Qur'an]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|هُودٌ|state=ind-def}}

=====See also=====
* {{list:Islamic prophets/ar}}

===Etymology 2===
Borrowed from a different {{bor|ar|arc|-}} dialect than from which {{m|ar|يَهُودِيّ}} was borrowed, where the anlauting ''yə'' part was weakened to ''i'' or disappeared. No singulative is attested and the form was obsolete already at the time of the Qurʾān, only used formulaically.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|هُود}}

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|هُود|p}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# {{senseid|ar|Jews}} [[Jew|Jews]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2:135
|passage=وَقَالُوا كُونُوا '''هُودًا''' أَوْ نَصَارَىٰ تَهْتَدُوا
|translation=They say, "Be '''Jews''' or Christians [so] you will be guided."}}

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|-|pl=هُود}}

=====Related terms=====
* {{l|ar|هَادَ|t=to be [[Jewish]]}}
* {{l|ar|يَهُودِيّ|t=[[Jew]], Jewish}}
* {{l|ar|تَهْوِيد|t=[[Judaizing]], [[Judaization]], the act of making something Jewish}}
* {{l|ar|تَهَوَّدَ|t=to Judaize (oneself), to be Judaized, to act Jewish}}

===Etymology 3===
{{denominal verb|ar|هُود|id=Jews}}, with the second triliteral conjugation implying the bestowing of a particular quality.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|هَوَّدَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[Judaize]], to make [[Jewish]]
#* {{RQ:Sunna|bukhari|23|137
|passage=كُلُّ مَوْلُودٍ يُولَدُ عَلَى الْفِطْرَةِ، فَأَبَوَاهُ '''يُهَوِّدَانِ'''هِ أَوْ يُنَصِّرَانِهِ أَوْ يُمَجِّسَانِهِ
|translation=Every newborn is born upon the [[fitra]] (i.e., in a state of submission to God or ''al-islām''); its parents then '''Judaize''' or [[Christianize]] or [[Zoroastrianize]] it.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

