Page 19855 هودج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{uncertain|ar}} origin, natively associated with {{ar-root|ه|د|ج}} with the senses of taking short steps, to waver when one walks, to walk like an elder person, to walk like one carrying a burden; a reference to a camel's strain.

Possibly under influence of {{psm|ar|pal||tr=kwpk'|ts=kōfag|t=saddle, the prominent parts at the front and rear of a saddle|nocap=1}}, from {{der|ar|pal||tr=kwp|ts=kōf|t=mountain, hill; hump}}; cognate to Modern and {{cog|fa-cls|کوهه|tr=kōha|t=hump; saddle; hillock}} and {{cog|fa|کوه|tr=kôh|t=mountain}}.

Compare also {{noncog|tmr|אוּכָּפָא|tr=ʾukkāp̄ā|t=packsaddle}}, {{noncog|syc|ܐܽܘܟܳܦܴܐ|tr=ʾukkāp̄ā|t=packsaddle}}, {{noncog|jpa|אכפי|ts=*ʾukkāp̄ē|t=yoke, type of load bearing device}} which form passed into {{cog|ar|أُكَّاف|t=packsaddle}} and is itself from {{noncog|akk|𒌑𒂵𒁍|tr=u<sub>2</sub>-ka<sub>3</sub>-pu|ts=ukāpu|t=saddle-cloth, pack}}, to illustrate matching and influence of saddle terms in the region.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|هَوْدَج}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|هَوْدَج|m|pl=هَوَادِج}}

# [[camel]] [[litter]], [[howdah]] {{qualifier|a [[closed]] [[compartment]] put on the back of camel, usually used for carrying brides and important women}}
# [[sedan chair]], [[litter]]

