Page 19923 و ز ن: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The original consonant order is {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*mazan-|t=to weigh}}, rare {{cog|gez|መዘነ}}, but common {{cog|am|መዘነ|tr=mäzzänä}}, which was dissimilated in Arabic to a root ''w-z-n'', and in {{cog|he|-}} {{m|he|א־ז־ן|tr=ʔ-z-n}}, {{m|he|איזן|אִזֵּן|tr=ʾizḗn}}, {{he-m|מאזניים|מֹאזְנַיִם|tr=mōzənáyim}}, but apparently kept in {{cog|uga|𐎎𐎇𐎐|t=weight}}, {{m|uga|𐎎𐎇𐎐𐎎|pos=dual|t=scales}}, and in {{cog|arc|-}} and {{cog|akk|-}} to ''z-b-n'' as borrowed in {{m|ar|زَبُون|t=customer}}, and as well in Arabic into {{ar-root|ز م ل|nocat=1}}.

