Page 19984 واسع: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
{{ar-rootbox|و س ع}}
{{ar-active participle}} of {{m|ar|وَسُعَ||to be [[wide]]}} and {{m|ar|وَسِعَ||to be [[wide]], to [[hold]], to [[contain]]}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|وَاسِع}}

===Adjective===
{{ar-adj-sound|وَاسِع|el=أَوْسَع}}

# [[large]] in [[area]], [[extensive]], [[vast]]; [[broad]]; [[wide]]; [[open]]
## [[spacious]], [[roomy]]
##: {{syn|ar|شَاسِع|فَسِيح}}
##* {{RQ:Qur’an|4|97|passage=قَالُوا أَلَمْ تَكُنْ أَرْضُ اللَّهِ '''وَاسِعَةً''' فَتُهَاجِرُوا فِيهَا}}
## {{lb|ar|of clothes}} [[loose]], [[oversized]]
## {{lb|ar|of a person's perspective, attitude, or mind}} [[open]], [[broad]]
## {{lb|ar|of a person's learning}} [[extensive]], [[deep]]
# [[expansive]]; [[comprehensive]], [[inclusive]]
# {{lb|ar|of a matter, issue, topic, or the like}} [[open]], up for [[discussion]], [[discussable]], [[undetermined]]
## {{lb|ar|when referring to issues relating to laws, rules, regulations, and the like}} [[debateable]], not [[fixed]]
# {{lb|ar|rare|approving}} not [[strict]]; not [[harsh]]; [[forgiving]]
#: {{syn|ar|سَمِح}}
# {{lb|ar|rare}} [[generous]], [[liberal]]
#: {{syn|ar|جَوَاد|مِعْطَاء}}

====Usage notes====
Strictly speaking, the word generally signifies extensiveness, vastness, and spaciousness, as well as openness, not the extent from side to side, which is denoted by {{m|ar|عَرِيض}} instead.

# {{ux|ar|اَلْغُرَفُ وَاسِعَةٌ|The rooms are large.|inline=y}}
# {{ux|ar|الأَرْضُ الْوَاسِعَةُ|the open land|inline=y}}
# {{ux|ar|سَاحَةٌ وَاسِعَةُ|an expansive area|inline=y}}

Due to the overlap between their semantic fields, however, the two are sometimes interchangeable, and there are instances where {{m|ar|وَاسِع}} is preferred and more idiomatic, especially when the wideness of the referent is convenient or desirable.

# {{ux|ar|طَرِيقٌ وَاسِعٌ|a wide road|inline=y}}
# {{ux|ar|مَمَرٌّ وَاسِعٌ|a wide corridor|inline=y}}

A like connection between narrowness and inconvenience (or frustration) is implied by its antonym {{m|ar|ضَيِّق}}. Compare {{m|en|loose}} and {{m|en|tight}}.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-adj|وَاسِع|pl=smp}}

====Antonyms====
* {{l|ar|ضَيِّق}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|mt|wiesa'}}
* {{desc|ary|واسع|tr=wāsaʕ}}

===References===
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}

-------- end text --------
