Page 20032 وتين: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Since the aorta supplies the [[cardiovascular system]] blood, perhaps a trace of {{der|ar|sem-pro|*watan-|t=to give}} put forward by a minority as the actual base verb “to give” which {{m|ar|نَتَنَ|t=to stink}} derives from. {{m|ar|وَتَنَ}} supposedly means “to be inexhaustible, to perpetual” of sources flowing without cease, parallelling like-patterned {{m|ar|وَرِيد|t=vein}} being related to {{m|ar|وِرْد|t=watering-hole}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|وَتِين}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|وَتِين|m|pl=وُتُن|pl2=أَوْتِنَة}}

# {{lb|ar|anatomy}} [[aorta]]

====Declension====
