Page 20045 وجب: -------- begin text --------
{{ar-rootbox|و ج ب}}

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-form|I}} verb from the root {{ar-root|و|ج|ب}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|وَجَبَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.nopass.vn:وُجُوب}}

# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to be [[necessary]], [[have to]] be; [[must]]: {{n-g|followed by {{m|ar|عَلَى|t=on}} or by {{m|ar|أَنْ}} and the subjunctive with a personal subject}}
#: {{ux|ar|كَمَا يَجِبُ|as it should be, as it must be}}
#: {{ux|ar|يَجِبُ أَن أَذْهَبَ|It is necessary for me to go; I must go|inline=t}}
# {{lb|ar|intransitive}} to be one's [[duty]]; to be [[incumbent]], [[imposed]], [[enjoined]]: {{n-g|followed by {{m|ar|عَلَى|t=on}}}}
#: {{ux|ar|يَجِب عَلَيْهِ أَنْ ...|t=it is his duty to, he has to, he must}}

=====Usage notes=====
In the first sense, {{m-self|ar|وَجَبَ}} is [[Appendix:Glossary#impersonal verb|impersonal]]: it does not take a personal subject. The person for whom something is necessary is given as the object of {{m|ar|عَلَى|t=on}} or as the subject of the verb in the clause introduced by the [[:Category:Arabic subjunctive particles|subjunctive particle]] {{m|ar|أَنْ}}.

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.nopass.vn:وُجُوب}}

===Etymology 2===
Causative {{ar-form|II}} verb from the root {{ar-root|و|ج|ب}}; compare {{m|ar|وَجَبَ|t=to be [[necessary]]}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{ar-IPA|وَجَّبَ}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II.pass}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive|construed with {{m|ar|عَلَى}}}} to [[impose]] {{qualifier|something}} on

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II.pass}}

=====References=====
* {{R:ar:Mace}}

-------- end text --------
