Page 20085 ود: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|و د د}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.pass.vn:وُدّ,وِدّ,وَدّ,مَوَدَّة,مَوِدَّة,وِدَاد,وَدَاد,وُدَاد,وَدَادَة,وِدَادَة,وُدَادَة}}

# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[love]], to [[like]]
# {{lb|ar|transitive}} to [[wish]], to [[like]] to [[have]], to [[love]] would it be there, to be [[comfortable]] with, to [[desire]] (+{{m|ar|لَوْ}})
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|2|96
|passage=يَوَدُّ أَحَدُهُمْ لَوْ يُعَمَّرُ أَلْفَ سَنَةً
|translation=One of them would like it were he made to live thousand years}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|15|2
|passage=رُبَمَا يَوَدُّ الَّذِينَ كَفَرُوا لَوْ كَانُوا مُسْلِمِينَ
|translation=Perhaps those who disbelieve will wish they had been Muslims.}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.pass.vn:وُدّ,وِدّ,وَدّ,مَوَدَّة,مَوِدَّة,وِدَاد,وَدَاد,وُدَاد,وَدَادَة,وِدَادَة,وُدَادَة}}

