Page 20108 ورد: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|و ر د}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*warad-}}. Cognate with {{cog|he|יָרַד|tr=yārád|t=to go down}}, {{cog|arc|ירד|tr=yreḏ|t=stream}}, {{cog|gez|ወረደ|tr=|t=fall down, go down, drain off, pour down}}, and {{cog|akk|warādum|𒉿𒊏𒁺𒌝|tr=warādum|t=to go down to lower ground, to come ashore, to go downhill or downstream}} and {{cog|uga|𐎊𐎗𐎄}}.

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/a~i.ipass?.vn:وُرُود}}

# to [[come]], to [[arrive]]
#: {{ux|ar|'''وَرَدَتْ'''نِي عُرُوضٌ مِنْ كُلِّ أَنْحَاءِ ٱلْعَالَمِ.|Offers from all over the world '''came to''' me.}}
# to [[appear]], to [[show up]]
# to be said, to be mentioned

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/a~i.ipass?.vn:وُرُود}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|II}}

# to [[import]]
#: {{ant|ar|صَدَّرَ}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|II}}

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|وِرْد|m|pl=أَوْرَاد}}

# [[watering hole]]
# {{lb|ar|religion}} ''(esp. in plural)'' specified time of day or night devoted to private [[prayer]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|وِرْد|pl=أَوْرَاد}}

===Etymology 2===
{{root|ar|ine-pro|*Hwerdʰ-}}
As {{cog|arc|וַרְדָּא|tr=wardā}}, {{m|syc|ܘܪܕܐ|tr=wardā}}, {{cog|he|וֶרֶד|tr=wéreḏ}}, and {{cog|xcl|վարդ}} and {{cog|grc|ῥόδον|ϝρόδον}}, borrowed from a reflex of {{der|ar|ira-pro|*wardah}}.

====Noun====
{{ar-coll-noun|وَرْد|sing=وَرْدَة|pl=وُرُود}}

# [[rose]]s
#: {{ux|ar|الْوَرْدُ، الَّذِي قُبِلَ بِنَدَى الصَّبَاحِ، هَمَسَ أَسْرَارَ الْحُبِّ وَالْجَمَالِ لِلْعَالَمِ، وَزُهُورُهُ الرَّقِيقَةُ شَاهِدَةٌ عَلَى هَشَاشَةِ الْحَيَاةِ.|The rose, kissed by the morning dew, whispered secrets of love and beauty to the world, its delicate petals a testament to the fragility of life.}}
# [[blossom]]s

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|وَرْد|sing=وَرْدَة|pl=وُرُود}}

