Page 20144 وزير: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
The original attested meaning is “assistant”, and the political sense only arose in the {{w|Umayyad period}}. Likely related to the verb {{l|ar|وَزَرَ|t=to carry, to shoulder}} with the root {{ar-root|و|ز|ر}}, meaning “someone who carries a burden”, but owing to the idea of assistance by handmen this may be denominal. Likely borrowed from an {{bor|ar|ira|-}} term surfacing as {{cog|pal||tr=wcyl|ts=vičīr|t=decision, judgment}}, {{cog|ae|𐬬𐬍𐬗𐬌𐬭𐬀|tr=vīcira|t=arbitrator, judge|lit=deciding, one who is taking or has made a decision}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|وَزِير}}
* {{audio|ar|Ar-وزير.ogg}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|وَزِير|m|f=وَزِيرَة|pl=وُزَرَاء}}

# [[minister]], cabinet minister
# [[vizier]]
# [[helper]], [[assistant]]
# {{lb|ar|chess}} [[queen]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|وَزِير|pl=وُزَرَاء}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|وَزِير الْخَارِجِيَّة||[[foreign minister]], [[Secretary of State]]}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ar|وِزَارَة}}
* {{l|ar|وِزَارِيّ}}

====Descendants====
{{top2}}
* {{desctree|fa-cls|وزیر|tr=wazīr|bor=1}}
* {{desc|bor=1|syc|ܘܙܝܪܐ|tr=wazzīrā}}
** {{desc|aii|ܘܲܙܝܼܪܵܐ}}
* {{desc|bor=1|en|wazir}}
* {{desc|bor=1|ms|wazir}}
** {{desc|id|wazir}}
* {{desc|bor=1|es|alguacil|alguazil|aguacil}}
** {{desc|bor=1|en|alguazil}}
** {{desc|bor=1|ca|algutzir}}
*** {{desc|bor=1|it|aguzzino}}
* {{desc|sw|waziri|bor=1}}
{{bottom}}

