Page 20155 وسق: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
Akin to {{cog|syc|ܘܰܣܩܳܐ|tr=wasqā|t=burden; captive, servant}} which shows by its onset that it is a borrowed term, since inherited {{IPAchar|/w/}} in the beginning becomes {{IPAchar|/j/}} in {{cog|sem-nwe}}. Probably to be put to {{bor|ar|sem-srb|𐩥𐩯𐩤|t=to fill}} (present: {{m|sem-srb|𐩺𐩯𐩤}}), with the derivative {{m|sem-srb|𐩯𐩤𐩩|t=pregnancy}}, compare {{cog|ar|وَاسِق|t=bearing a child (camel)}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|وَسْق}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|وَسْق|m|pl=وُسُوق|pl2=أَوْسَاق}}

# a [[measure]] of [[capacity]], about a [[camel]]’s load
#* {{quote-book|ar|year=a. 660|author={{w|Labīd}}|title=poetized the following two verses according to {{RQ:Yaqut|W2|page=266 lines 5–6|instead=1}}|passage=ويومَ أجازَتْ قُلّةَ الحَزْن منهُمُ … مواكبُ، تعلو ذَا حُسًا، وقنابلُ<br/>على الصَّرْصَرانيّات، في كل رحلة، … '''وُسُوقٌ''' عِدَالٌ، ليس فيهن مائِلُ}}
# [[freight]], [[stowage]]
# {{ar-verbal noun of|وَسَقَ|form=I}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|وَسْق|pl=وُسُوق|pl2=أَوْسَاق}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l-self|ar|وَسَقَ|t=to load}}
* {{l|ar|وَاسِق|t=pregnant (camel)}}
* {{l|ar|وَاسِقَ|t=to seek to measure oneself with}}
* {{l|ar|أَوْسَقَ|t=to load}}
* {{l|ar|اِتَّسَقَ|t=to be [[in line]] with, to be of the right measure for}}
* {{l|ar|وَسِيقَة|t=group of camels}}
* {{l|ar|اِسْتَوْسَقَ|t=to be congregated into one place}}

===Verb===
