Page 20295 ون: -------- begin text --------

===Suffix===
{{head|ar|suffix|head=ـُونَ|g=m}}

# {{n-g|Nominative-case suffix used to pluralize nouns and adjectives, generally masculine ones referring to people. The suffix changes to {{l|ar|ـِينَ}} in the genitive and accusative cases.}}
# [[-ty]]

====Usage notes====
* This suffix is mostly restricted to [[participle]]s, [[nisba]]s, and certain nouns of other building types such as the measure {{m|ar||فَعَّال}}. Only a handful of nouns not referring to people use this suffix, e.g. {{m|ar|سِنُونَ}} from {{m|ar|سَنة|t=year}}. Most other nouns have [[broken plural]]s or use the “feminine” suffix {{m|ar|ـَات}}. Note that borrowed nouns tend to use the latter even when they refer to people, e.g. {{m|ar|بَهْلَوانَات}} from {{m|ar|بَهْلَوان|t=acrobat}}.

====Derived terms====
{{rel-top|terms derived using {{lang|ar|ـُونَ}} (multiples of ten)}}
