Page 20331 يأجوج: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology===
A Qurʾānic formation later incorporated into the Arabic Islamic lexicon, apparently an alteration of {{der|ar|he|גּוֹג|tr=gōg}}, itself also the source of the Biblical form {{m|ar|جُوج}}. The addition of a syllable may have been by influence of {{bor|ar|he|מָגוֹג|tr=māgōg}}, the source of {{m|ar|مَاجُوج}} and {{m|ar|مَأْجُوج}}, and/or motivated by phonic considerations, as {{m|ar|يَأْجُوج}} is collocated with {{m|ar|مَأْجُوج}} in the two instances of the word's occurrence in the Qurʾān. For other possible phonic changes, compare with {{m|ar|عِيسَى}}, which is often conjoined or juxtaposed in the Qurʾān with such words as {{m|ar|مُوسَى}} and {{m|ar|يَحْيَى}}. Compare also with {{m|ar|قَابِيل}}, which, though not used in the Qurʾān, may have been modified by analogy with {{m|ar|هَابِيل}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|يَأْجُوج}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|يَأْجُوج|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} {{w|Gog and Magog#Islamic texts|Gog}} {{gl|an evil tribe associated with Magog}}
#: {{syn|ar|جُوج|q1=Christianity}}
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|18|94|passage=قَالُوا يَا ذَا ٱلْقَرْنَيْنِ إِنَّ '''يَأْجُوجَ وَمَأْجُوجَ''' مُفْسِدُونَ فِي ٱلْأَرْضِ فَهَلْ نَجْعَلُ لَكَ خَرْجًا عَلَى أَنْ تَجْعَلَ بَيْنَنَا وَبَيْنَهُمْ سَدًّا|t=They said, "O Dhul-Qarnayn, indeed '''Gog and Magog''' are [great] corrupters in the land. So may we assign for you an expenditure that you might make between us and them a barrier?"|subst=وَ//وَ-,فَ//فَ-}}

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|يَأْجُوجُ|state=ind-def}}
