Page 20335 يئس: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{ar-rootbox|ي ء س}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a,i.ipass?.vn:يَأْس,يَآسَة}}

# to [[give up]] [[hope]], to [[despair]], to be [[hopeless]]
#: {{syn|ar|أَيِسَ|قَنِطَ}}
#: {{ant|ar|رَجَا|أَمَلَ}}
#: {{uxi|ar|الأمل الذي يعطيه الكتاب المقدس يساعدنا أن نتحمَّل مشاكلنا ولا نيأس|The hope given by the Bible helps us to endure our problems and not despair.}}
# to [[become]] [[barren]]

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a,i.ipass?.vn:يَأْس,يَآسَة}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Lane}}
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}

===Etymology 2===
From the same root of a barren woman, to have no hope of conceiving; developing to mean just accepting that this is how things are, knowing that she cannot, to know one cannot succeed, to have no hope of anything other.

From there the sense of to stop hoping, to give up being concerned with, to abandon worrying over, to accept it to be so; a parallel semantic sense can be found in {{cog|jpa|-}}, {{cog|arc-jla|יאּש|tr=yaʾʾēš|t=to remove desperate thoughts, to stop one's mind from thinking about}}.{{rfv-etym|ar}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a,i.pass.vn:يَأْس}}

# {{lb|ar|dialect|archaic}} to [[know]], to have [[certainty]], to [[realize]] or to [[accept]], to [[come]] to a [[realization]] to [[know]] a thing to be so or [[true]]
#* {{RQ:Qur'an|13|31
|passage=أَفَلَمْ '''يَيْأَسِ''' الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا أَنْ لَوْ يَشَاءُ اللَّهُ لَهَدَى النَّاسَ جَمِيعًا
|translation=...Do not those who have trusted '''come to the realization''' that, if God caused it to be, He could certainly direct aright all people?...}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a,i.pass.vn:يَأْس}}

====References====
* {{R:ar:Steingass}}
-------- end text --------
Page 20336 يا: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ar|/jaː/}}

===Particle===
{{ar-particle|يَا}}

# [[O]]; [[hey]]; [[you]]; {{ngd|vocative particle preceding a noun used in direct address, only rarely omitted in such contexts}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' كَرِيمُ...|t=(Hey) Kareem, ...}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' حِمارُ!|t=You idiot!}}
#* {{quote-song|ar
|lyricist=w:Said Akl
|composer={{w|Rahbani Brothers|The Rahbani Brothers}}
|artist=w:Fairuz
|title={{m|ar||زَهْرَةُ المَدَائِن}}
|trans-title=The Flower of ''[All]'' Cities
|album={{m|ar||القُدْسْ فِي البَال}}
|trans-album=Jerusalem in My Heart
|year=1971
|text=يَا قُدْسُ يَا قُدْسُ يَا قُدْسُ يَا مَدِينَةَ الصَّلَاة أُصَلِّي
<!-- Manual transliteration needed for ة -->
|tr=yā qudsu yā qudsu yā qudsu yā madīnata ṣ-ṣalāh ʾuṣallī
|t=O Jerusalem, O Jerusalem, O Jerusalem, O city of prayer... I pray
}}

====Usage notes====
* If the noun following {{lang|ar|يَا}} describes a certain person and is singular, sound feminine plural or broken plural, it governs the nominative case in the construct state. If it describes a certain person and is sound dual or sound masculine plural, it governs the nominative case in the indefinite state.
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' مُحَمَّدُ!|'''O''' Muhammad!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|يَا مُحَمَّدُ!|'''O''' Muhammad!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' طَبِيبُ دَاوِنِي!|'''O''' doctor, treat me! (addressing a certain doctor)}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' مُوَظِّفُونَ!|'''O''' employees!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' نَاسُ!|'''O''' people!}}
* If the noun following {{lang|ar|يَا}} is meant in general and isn't meant to adress a certain person, it governs the accusative case in the indefinite state.
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' طَبِيبًا دَاوِنِي!|'''O''' any doctor, treat me! (calling for a doctor)}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' فَاهِمًا اِلدَّرْسَ اِشْرَحْهُ لَنَا!|tr='''yā''' fāhiman id-darsa išraḥhu lanā!|'''O''' anyone who understands the lesson, explain it to us!}}
* If the noun following {{lang|ar|يَا}} is in a genitive construction, it governs the accusative case in the construct state.
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' مُدَرِّسَ ٱلْفَصْلِ نَظِّمْ فَصْلَكَ!|'''O''' teacher of the class, organise your class!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' مُوَظِّفِي هٰذِهِ ٱلشَّرِكَةِ|'''O''' employees of this company!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' أَبَانَا!|'''O''' our father!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' حَبِيبِي!|'''O''' my dear!}}
* If we want to use the noun following {{lang|ar|يَا}} in the definite state, we must use another particle {{l|ar|أَيُّهَا}} (masculine) or {{l|ar|أَيَّتُهَا}} (feminine) together with {{lang|ar|يَا}}.
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' أَيُّهَا ٱلطَّبِيبُ دَاوِنِي!|'''O''' you doctor, treat me!}}
#: {{uxi|ar|'''يَا''' أَيُّهَا ٱلنَّاسُ!|'''O''' you people.}}
* In [[Qur'an|Qur'anic]] and to some degree [[w:Classical Arabic|Classical]] orthography, {{m|ar|يَا}} was written {{lang|ar|يَٰـ}} and joined to the following word. Compare the following verse ([http://quran.com/2/55 Surat al-Baqara 55], translation Muhammad Asad).
*: (''original orthography'') {{uxi|ar|وَإِذۡ قُلۡتُمۡ '''يَـٰمُوسَىٰ''' لَن نُّؤۡمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّىٰ نَرى ٱللَّهَ جَهۡرَةࣰ فَأَخَذَتۡكُمُ ٱلصَّـٰعِقَةُ وَأَنتُمۡ تَنظُرُونَ}}
*: (''modernized orthography'') {{uxi|ar|وَإِذْ قُلْتُمْ '''يَا مُوسَى''' لَنْ نُؤْمِنَ لَكَ حَتَّى نَرَى ٱللّٰه جَهْرَةً فَأَخَذَتْكُمُ ٱلصَّاعِقَةُ وَأَنتُمْ تَنظُرُونَ}}
*: And [remember] when you said, "'''O Moses''' indeed we shall not believe thee unto we see God face to face!" - whereupon the thunderbolt of punishment overtook you before your very eyes.

