Page 20340 ياالله: -------- begin text --------
{{phrasebook|ar}}

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|ar|يَلَّا}}

===Etymology===
Compounded from {{compound|ar|يَا|t1={{m|en|O|id=vocative}}|اللّٰه|t2=God}}. The colloquial sense derives from supplications of the sort “O God, let this and that happen!”, whence it was generalised to a particle or exclamation expressing a wish, encouragement, or command.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|يَا ٱللَّٰه}}

===Interjection===
{{ar-interj|يَاٱللَّٰه|tr=yāllāh}}

# {{lb|ar|colloquial}} [[come on]], [[c'mon|c’mon]]
# {{lb|ar|colloquial}} [[let's go|let’s go]], [[hurry up]]
# {{lb|ar|dialectal|colloquial|Levantine}} word accompanying [[bye-bye]], [[bye]]

