Page 20355 يافوخ: -------- begin text --------

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ar|يَأْفُوخ|يَافُوخَة}}

===Etymology===
Seemingly borrowed from {{bor|ar|arc|אַפְקוּתָא|tr=ʾap̄qūṯā|t=the portion of the back of neck which joins the vertebra, ''[[Genick]]'', nucha, scruff; ''also'' upper part of a date palm}}, reanalyzed from {{m|arc|אַפְרָקוּתָא|tr=ʾap̄rāqūṯā}}, {{m|arc|פְּרִיקְתָּא|tr=pərīqtā}}, {{m|arc|פִּירְקְתָא|tr=pīrəqṯā}}, {{m|arc|פּוּרְקְתָא|tr=pūrəqṯā}}, {{m|syc|ܦܴܪܱܩܬ݂ܳܐ|tr=pāraqṯā}} – obviously a much used word – after the root {{m|arc|פ־ק־ע}} cognate to the Arabic root {{ar-root|ف ق ع|nocat=1}} related to bursting in place of the root {{m|arc|פ־ר־ק}} cognate to Arabic {{ar-root|ف ر ق|nocat=1}} related to reaving, so the Arabic etymological parallel would be {{m|ar|فَقَار|t=vertebral column}} from the related {{ar-root|ف ق ر|nocat=1}}, the borrowing source being a regiolect and chronolect where the distinction of {{IPAchar|/ʔ/}}, {{IPAchar|/ʕ/}}, {{IPAchar|/ħ/}} and {{IPAchar|/j/}} was already degenerated – as the source of {{cog|xcl|յիմար}} –, resolving the gap after the stem with {{IPAchar|/x/}} as nearest consonant to {{IPAchar|/uː/}} to obtain a triconsonantal term again.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|يَافُوخ}}

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|يَافُوخ|m|pl=يَوَافِيخ}}

# {{lb|ar|anatomy}} [[crown]] (of the head), [[vertex]]
# {{lb|ar|anatomy}} [[fontanelle]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|يَافُوخ|pl=يَوَافِيخ}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|ota|یافوخ|tr=yafuh|bor=1}}
-------- end text --------
