Page 20374 يحيى: -------- begin text --------

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|يَحْيَى}}
* {{homophones|ar|يَحْيَا}}
{{rfap|ar}}

===Etymology 1===
Some scholars claim it derives from an alternative reading of the undotted ''rasm'' {{m|ar||ىحںى}} / {{m|ar||ںحںى}} (visually {{m|ar||ىحىى}}), perhaps by influence of the verb form {{m|ar|يَحْيَا|t=he is alive}}, from underlying *{{m|ar||يُحَنَّى}}, eventually from {{der|ar|he|יוֹחָנָן|tr=yōḥānān}}, but this has been disputed. Compare the Christian Arabic form {{m|ar|يُوحَنَّا}}.

====Proper noun====
{{ar-proper noun|يَحْيَى|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Islam}} [[John]] ([[John the Baptist|the Baptist]])
# {{given name|ar|male}}, [[Yahya]], [[Yehia]]

=====Usage notes=====
{{m|ar|يَحْيَى}} is used almost exclusively in Islamic and Mandaean contexts. Arabic-speaking Christians refer to John as {{m|ar|يُوحَنَّا}}.

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|يَحْيَى|state=ind-def}}

