Page 20393 يسروع: -------- begin text --------
{{wp|lang=ar}}

===Etymology===
Probably from an {{bor|ar|arc|-}} term, as well as {{m|ar|يَرَقَان|t=mildew; larvae}}, since caterpillars aren’t swift like the root {{ar-root|س ر ع|nocat=1}} means but slippery or viscous what {{m|arc|שׁ־ר־ע}} / {{syc-root-entry|ܫ|ܪ|ܥ}} means, and the prefigation of ''ya-'' is more likely in Aramaic in general, plus the vocalization variation bolsters the suspicion.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|يَسْرُوع|يُسْرُوع}}

===See also===
* [[Appendix:Aramaic terms only witnessed by borrowings]]

===Noun===
{{ar-noun|يَسْرُوع|m|head2=يُسْرُوع}} {{tlb|ar|collective or singulative; if the former then rarely forms {{m|ar|يَسْرُوعَة}} as a singulative which can also be considered as a base form with plural {{m|ar|يَسْرُوعَات}}, if the latter then forms a plural {{m|ar|يَسَارِيع}} also vocalized {{m|ar|يُسَارِيع}}}}

# [[caterpillar]], [[pupa]]

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|يَسْرُوع|head2=يُسْرُوع|pl=يَسَارِيع}}
{{ar-decl-coll-noun|يَسْرُوع|head2=يُسْرُوع}}

===Further reading===
* {{R:CAL|%24r(|V}}
* {{R:ar:Wehr-5-de|page=567|entry=س ر ع}} has {{m+|ar|يَسْرُوع}}, {{m|ar|يَسَارِيع}}

{{C|ar|Baby animals}}
