From {{bor|ar|arc|ܝܶܫܽܘܥ|tr=yešūʿ}}, from {{der|ar|hbo|יֵשׁוּעַ|tr=yešū́aʿ||Jesus}}, a {{glossary|syncope|syncopated}} form of {{m|he|יְהוֹשֻׁעַ|tr=yəhōšúaʿ||[[Joshua]]}}. {{doublet|ar|يَشُوع|t1=Joshua}} and possibly {{m|ar|عِيسَى||Jesus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{ar-IPA|يَسُوع}}

===Proper noun===
{{ar-proper noun|يَسُوع|m}}

# {{lb|ar|Christianity}} [[Jesus]] of [[Nazareth]]
#: {{syn|ar|عِيسَى|q1=Islam}}

====Usage notes====
* {{m|ar||يَسُوع}} is the name Arabic-speaking Christians call Jesus and the one generally used in secular contexts. In Islamic contexts, {{m|ar|عِيسَى}} is used instead.

====Declension====
{{ar-decl-noun|يَسُوعُ|state=ind-def}}

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|ar|المَسِيح||[[Messiah]], [[Christ]]}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|ar|يَسُوعِيّ}}

====Descendants====
* {{desc|kab|Yasuɛ|bor=1}}

{{C|ar|Biblical characters}}
