Page 20401 يعر: -------- begin text --------

===Etymology 1===
{{unk|ar|title=Unclear}}. In {{w|Psalm}} [https://biblehub.com/interlinear/psalms/29-9.htm 29:9] once plural {{m|he|יְעָ֫ר֥וֹת|tr=yəʿārōṯ}} after {{m|he|איל|אַיָּלוֹת|tr=ʾayyālōṯ|t=hinds}}, assumed by dint of comparativism a likely later misvocalized plural of a {{m|he|יַעֲרָה|t=kid|tr=yaʿărā}}—distinguished from homonymous “honeycomb”, an assumed nomen unitatis of {{m|he|יַעַר|tr=yaʿar|t=honeycombs}} found in the construct state {{m|he|יַעְרַת|tr=yaʿəraṯ}} in {{w|1 Samuel}} [https://biblehub.com/interlinear/1_samuel/14-27.htm 14:27]—, while it has thus far plausibly been translated as the plural of {{m|he|יַעַר|tr=yaʿar|t=forest}}. There is also {{cog|tig|ወርዔ|t=mountain goat}}, the consonant order of which corresponds to a word the Arabic lexicographers give as {{m|ar|يَرَع|t=youngs of wild cows, {{l|ar|[[ولد|أَوْلَادُ]] [[بَقَرِ]] الْ[[وَحْشِ]]}}}}, compare also {{m|ar|يَرَاع}} given as a synonym of {{m|ar|بَعُوض}}. If it is not instead the lost descendant of {{noncog|sem-pro|*waʕil-|t=ibex}} the Arabic term must be, as many [[:Category:ar:Baby animals|names for baby animals]], deemed a borrowing from {{bor|ar|arc|-}}, owing to the {{cog|sem-nwe|-}} ''w'' → ''y'' change.

====Noun====
{{ar-noun|يَعْر|m|pl=أَيْعَار}}

# [[offspring]] of a [[goat]], [[kid]]

=====Declension=====
{{ar-decl-noun|يَعْر|pl=أَيْعَار}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb|I/i~a.nopass.vn:يُعَر}} {{tlb|ar|obsolete}}

# to [[bleat]], to [[cry]] (of a young goat)
#* {{RQ:Sunna|abudawud|1|142|passage=بَيْنَا نَحْنُ مَعَ رَسُولِ ٱللّٰهِ صَلَّى ٱللّٰهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ جُلُوسٌ إِذْ دَفَعَ الرَّاعِي غَنَمَهُ إِلَى الْمُرَاحِ وَمَعَهُ سَخْلَة '''تَيْعَرُ'''|t=We were sitting in the company of the Messenger of God (PBUH) when we saw that a shepherd was driving a herd of sheep to their fold. He had with him a newly-born lamb '''that was crying'''.|subst=وَمَعَهُ/وَ-مَعَ-هُو}}

=====Conjugation=====
{{ar-conj|I/i~a.nopass.vn:يُعَر}}

===Etymology 2===

====Verb====
{{ar-verb-form|يُعِرْ|IV}}

# {{inflection of|ar|أَعَارَ||3|m|s|non-past|actv|jussive}}

====Verb====
{{ar-verb-form|يُعَرْ|IV}}

