# The dotless bāʾ is a letter of the Arabic alphabet that was used in ancient Arabic.  It is the common archaic form of bāʾ ‹ ب›, tāʾ ‹ ت›, ṯāʾ ‹ ث› in all forms, and of initial and medial lām ‹ ل›, nūn ‹ ن› and yāʾ ‹ ي› used in the [[رسم#Noun|rasm]] style of writing
