{{wikipedia|ألف خنجرية|lang=ar}}

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head=ـٰ}}

# '''[[superscript]] [[alif]]''', '''[[dagger]] [[alif]]''' ({{l|ar|أَلِف خَنْجَرِيَّة}}), indicates a long {{IPAchar|/aː/}} where {{l|ar|ا|tr=ʔalif}} is normally not written.

====Usage notes====
* '''ʔalif ḵanjariyya''' is a rare diacritic, is missing on standard keyboards and is sometimes replaced with a '''fatḥa''' {{m|ar|ـَ}} in a vocalised Arabic text or omitted altogether, except in the [[Qur'an]].
* '''ʔalif ḵanjariyya''' can be written with or without a [[fatḥa]], e.g. with a fatḥa {{m|ar|رَحْمَٰن}} in the Middle East or without a fatḥa {{m|ar|رَحْمٰن}} in South Asia (Pakistan, India and Bangladesh)
* The word {{m|ar|اللّٰه||Allah}} is usually produced automatically by entering "''alif + lām + lām + hāʾ''" - {{m|ar|[[ا]] [[ل]] [[ل]] [[ه]]|tr=-}} (''read from right to left''). The word consists of {{l|ar|ا|tr=ʔalif}} + [[ligature]] of doubled {{l|ar|ل|tr=lām}} with a [[shadda]] {{lang|und|sc=Arab|[[ـّ]]}} and an ʔalif ḵanjariyya above {{l|ar|ل|tr=lām}}.
* In Wiktionary we use '''ʔalif ḵanjariyya''' to generate a correct transliteration ("ā") and to indicate a long /aː/. A '''fatḥa''' alone, without '''ʔalif ḵanjariyya''' or a long alif {{l|ar|ا|tr=ʔalif}} would be transliterated as a short /a/.

===See also===
{{ar-diacritics}}
-------- end text --------
Page 20498 ٱ: -------- begin text --------

===Letter===
{{head|ar|letter|head=ٱ|tr=hamzatu l-waṣli}}

# [[alif]] carrying the waṣla sign ({{lang|ar|ٱ}}) indicates [[liaison]] with the preceding word and means that the [[hamza]] is suppressed. It is more commonly indicated by a regular alif without a hamza ({{l|ar|ا}}). It occurs, for example, in the definite article {{l|ar|ال|ٱل}}, {{l|ar|ٱسْم|tr=sm-}}, {{l|ar|ٱبْن|tr=bn-}}, imperative verbs, and the perfective aspect of verb forms VII to X, but is not pronounced following a vowel: (e.g., {{l|ar||البيت ٱلكبير}} is read al-baytu l-kabīru). It occurs only at the beginning of a word that is not initial in a word group, or the beginning of a word following a prefixed preposition or conjunction.
#: {{l|ar||هُوَ ٱبْنُ ٱلمُدَرِّسِ|gloss=He is the teacher’s son.}}
#: {{l|ar||وَٱسْمُ ٱلبِنْتِ أَنْهَارُ|gloss=And the daughter’s name is Anhar.}}

====See also====
* {{l|ar|هَمْزَةُ ٱلوَصْلِ}}
